hadiths[1151]{hadithnumber,text}:
"20668","(20662) And Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Zakariyyā informed us among others — they said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us — al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us — al-Shāfiʿī informed us — ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Muḥammad ibn Abī ʿUbayd al-Dāwarwardī narrated from Rabīʿah ibn Abī ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, from Saʿīd ibn ʿAmr ibn Sharḥabīl ibn Saʿīd ibn Saʿd ibn ʿUbādah, from his father, from his grandfather, who said: We found in the writings of Saʿd: that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ decided by the oath together with the witness. Al-Shāfiʿī, may Allah have mercy on him, said: And ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn al-Muṭṭalib narrated from Saʿīd ibn ʿAmr, from his father, who said: We found in the writings of Saʿd ibn ʿUbādah that Saʿd ibn ʿUbādah testified that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded ʿAmr ibn Ḥazm to decide by the oath together with the witness."
"20669","(20663) And Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us — they said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us — Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣaghānī narrated to us — Muʿallā ibn Manṣūr narrated to us — Sulaymān ibn Bilāl narrated from Rabīʿah, from Ismāʿīl ibn ʿAmr ibn Qays ibn Saʿd ibn ʿUbādah, from his father: that they found in the writing of Saʿd that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ decided by the oath together with the witness."
"20670","(20664) And Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan informed us — they said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us — Baḥr ibn Naṣr narrated to us — Ibn Wahb narrated to us — Ibn Lahīʿah and Nāfiʿ ibn Yazīd informed me from ʿUmārah ibn Ghazīyah al-Anṣārī, from Saʿd ibn ʿAmr ibn Sharḥabīl ibn Saʿd ibn ʿUbādah: that he found a book among the writings of his fathers: \This is what ʿAmr ibn Ḥazm and al-Mughīrah ibn Shuʿbah mentioned or recorded — they said: 'We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when two men came disputing"," one of them having a witness regarding his claim. So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ combined the oath of the claimant with his witness"," and thereby awarded him his right.'\"""""
"20671","(20665) Abū ʿAliyy al-Rūdhbārī informed us, that Muḥammad ibn Bakr informed us, that Abū Dāwūd informed us, that Aḥmad ibn ʿAbda informed us, that ʿAmmār ibn Shuʿayth ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Zubayb al-ʿAnbarī informed us, that my father informed me, he said: I heard my grandfather al-Zubayb saying: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent an army to Banū al-ʿAnbar, and they captured a caravan from a direction near al-Ṭāʾif and drove them along to the Prophet of Allah ﷺ. I rode ahead and outpaced them to the Prophet ﷺ, and I said: \Peace be upon you"," O Prophet of Allah"," and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. Your army came to us and took us"," though we had already become Muslims and had cropped the ears of the livestock.\"" When BalʿAnbar arrived"," the Prophet of Allah ﷺ said to me: \""Do you have proof that you had become Muslims before you were taken in these days?\"" I said: \""Yes.\"" He said: \""What is your proof?\"" I said: \""Samura"," a man from Banū al-ʿAnbar"," and another man whose name I mentioned for him.\"" The other man testified"," but Samura refused to testify. The Prophet of Allah ﷺ said: \""He has refused to testify for you; so take an oath along with your other witness.\"" I said: \""Yes.\"" He then demanded an oath from me"," and I swore by Allah: \""We had become Muslims on such and such a day"," and had cropped the ears of the livestock.\"" The Prophet of Allah ﷺ said: \""Go and divide their wealth into halves"," and do not touch their children. Were it not that Allah"," the Almighty and Majestic"," does not love the futility of deeds"," we would not have returned to you even a single camel.\"" Al-Zubayb said: My mother called me and said: \""This is the man who took my flock.\"" I went to the Prophet of Allah ﷺ and informed him. He said to me: \""Detain him.\"" I seized him by his collar and stood with him in our place. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ"," standing"," looked at us and said: \""What do you intend with your captive?\"" I released him from my hand. The Prophet of Allah ﷺ then stood and said to the man: \""Return to this boy's mother the flock you took from her.\"" He said: \""O Prophet of Allah"," it has gone out of my hand.\"" The Prophet of Allah ﷺ then took the man's sword and gave it to me"," and said to a man: \""Go and give him a ṣāʿ of food.\"" So he gave me a ṣāʿ of barley.\n\nHis statement \""we had cropped the ears of the livestock\"" means: we cut the tips of their ears. This was"," with regard to wealth"," a distinguishing mark between one who had become a Muslim and one who had not. Abū Sulaymān al-Khaṭṭābī"," may Allah have mercy on him"," said: In this ḥadīth there is the employment of the oath along with the witness in matters other than wealth"," except that its chain of narration is not strong. It is also possible that the oath here was intended to refer to wealth"," because Islam safeguards wealth just as it safeguards blood. [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"20672","(20666) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq informed us — and in another narration they said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us — that al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us, that al-Shāfiʿī informed us, that Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad informed us, from ʿAmr ibn Abī ʿAmr, the mawlā of al-Muṭṭalib, from Ibn al-Musayyib: that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ decided by the oath together with the witness. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"20673","(20667) And Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us — and in another narration they said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us — that al-Rabīʿ informed us, that al-Shāfiʿī informed us, that Muslim ibn Khālid informed us, from Ibn Jurayj, from ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb, that the Prophet ﷺ said regarding testimony: \If he brings a witness"," let him swear along with his witness.\"" This is a mursal ḥadīth. [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"20674","(20668) And Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, that Abū al-Naḍr al-Faqīh al-Ṭūsī informed us, that ʿUthmān ibn Saʿīd al-Dārimī informed us, that Ismāʿīl ibn ʿAbdullāh informed us, that Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Raqqī informed us, that Muṭrif ibn Māzin informed us, that Ibn Jurayj informed us, from ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb, from his father, from his grandfather, who said: The Prophet ﷺ decided by a witness and an oath regarding rights. And others also narrated it from Muṭrif similarly. [Ḍaʿīf]"
"20675","(20669) Abū al-Qāsim ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn ʿAbdullāh al-Nājī informed us, that Abū al-Qāsim Ḥamza ibn ʿUbaydullāh al-Mālikī informed us, that Abū Ḥātim al-Rāzī informed us — (ḥ) And Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, that Abū al-Naḍr al-Faqīh informed us, that ʿUthmān ibn Saʿīd al-Dārimī informed us — they both said: al-Nufaylī informed us, that Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUbayd ibn ʿUmayr al-Laythī informed us, from ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb, from his father, from his grandfather: that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ decided by the oath together with the witness. Muṭrif ibn Māzin and Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmayr are not strong (in ḥadīth), though his (Muṭrif's) corroborating narration serves as evidence for what has preceded. [Ṣaḥīḥ; it has preceded]"
"20676","(20670) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan informed us, they said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, that Baḥr ibn Naṣr informed us, that Ibn Wahb informed me, that ʿUthmān ibn al-Ḥakam informed me, that Zuhayr ibn Muḥammad informed us, from Suhayl ibn Abī Ṣāliḥ, from his father, from Zayd ibn Thābit, may Allah be pleased with him: that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ decided by an oath and a witness. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"20677","(20671) Abū Jaʿfar Kāmil ibn Aḥmad al-Mustamlī informed us, that Abū ʿAliyy al-Raffāʾ informed us, that Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbdullāh Abū Muslim informed us, that Sahl ibn Bakkār informed us, that Juwayriyyat ibn Asmāʾ informed us, from ʿAbdullāh ibn Yazīd, the mawlā al-Munbaʿith, from a man from the Egyptians, from a man who lived among the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ, whose name was Surriq, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ decided by an oath and a witness. Musaddad similarly followed him on the authority of Juwayriyyah. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"20678","(20672) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan informed us, they said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, that al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us, that al-Shāfiʿī informed us, that Mālik informed us, from Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad, from his father: that the Prophet ﷺ decided by the oath together with the witness. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"20679","(20673) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Aṣbahānī informed us, that ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, that ʿAbd al-Ṣamad ibn ʿAlī informed us, that Ibrāhīm ibn Aḥmad ibn Marwān informed us, that Shaybān informed us, that Ṭalḥah ibn Zayd informed us, that Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad informed us, from his father, from ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib, may Allah be pleased with him: that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and Abū Bakr, and ʿUmar, and ʿUthmān, may Allah be pleased with them, used to decide by the testimony of a single witness and the oath of the claimant. Jaʿfar said: \And the judges decide by that among us today.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"20680","(20674) And Abū Bakr ibn Abī Sabrah narrated it from Abū al-Zinād, from ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿĀmir, who said: I was present with Abū Bakr, ʿUmar, and ʿUthmān, may Allah be pleased with them, and they would decide by the oath together with the witness. Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith informed us, that ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar informed us, that Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Asad al-Harawī informed us, that Muḥammad ibn Ishkāb informed us, that Abū ʿĀṣim informed us, from Abū Bakr ibn Abī Sabrah, and he mentioned it. And the narration from Abū Bakr, ʿUmar, and ʿUthmān, may Allah be pleased with them, is weak, while the narration from ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib and Ubayy ibn Kaʿb, may Allah be pleased with them both, is well-known. And in what Sulaymān ibn Bilāl narrated from Rabīʿah ibn Abī ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, that ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb, may Allah be pleased with him, wrote to Sharīḥ regarding that — even though it is munqaṭiʿ (disconnected) — there is corroboration for the narration of Ibn Abī Sabrah. [Ḍaʿīf]"
"20681","(20675) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, and in the last narration they said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us, al-Shāfiʿī informed us, Muslim ibn Khālid informed us, Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad narrated to me, he said: I heard al-Ḥakam ibn ʿUtaybah asking my father, while his hand was placed upon the wall of the grave, \Did the Prophet (ﷺ) judge by the oath together with a witness?\"" He said: \""Yes"," and ʿAlī (may Allāh be pleased with him) judged by it among you.\"" [Weak]"""
"20682","(20676) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed me, Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Labbān informed us that ʿAbbād ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to them, he said: Ibrāhīm ibn Abī Yaḥyā narrated to us, from Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad, from his father: that the Messenger of Allāh (ﷺ) judged by the oath together with a witness — meaning in matters of wealth. And ʿAlī (may Allāh be pleased with him) judged by that in Kūfah. He said: And Ubayy ibn Kaʿb also judged by that during the caliphate of ʿUmar (may Allāh be pleased with them both). [Weak]"
"20683","(20677) And Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm narrated to us, al-Rabīʿ informed us, al-Shāfiʿī said: And it was mentioned from Ibrāhīm ibn Abī Ḥabībah, from Dāwūd ibn al-Ḥuṣayn, from Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī: that Ubayy ibn Kaʿb (may Allāh be pleased with him) judged by the oath together with a witness. [Sound. Mālik narrated it]"
"20684","(20678) Abū Saʿīd informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās narrated to us, al-Rabīʿ informed us, al-Shāfiʿī informed us, Mālik informed us, from Abū al-Zinād: that ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz wrote to ʿAbd al-Ḥamīd ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Zayd ibn al-Khaṭṭāb, who was his governor in Kūfah: \Judge by the oath together with a witness.\"" [Sound]"""
"20685","(20679) He said: And al-Shāfiʿī informed us, a trustworthy one from among our companions informed us, from Muḥammad ibn ʿAjlān, from Abū al-Zinād: that ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz wrote to ʿAbd al-Ḥamīd ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, who was his governor over Kūfah: \Judge by the oath together with a witness"," for it is the Sunnah.\"" Abū al-Zinād said: A man from among their elders stood and said: \""I bear witness that Shurayḥ judged by this in this mosque.\"" [Weak]"""
"20686","(20680) He said: And al-Shāfiʿī informed us, ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz al-Mājishūn mentioned, from Ruzayq ibn Ḥakīm, who said: \I wrote to ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz"," informing him that I did not find the oath together with a witness except in Madīnah.\"" He said: \""So he wrote to me: 'Judge by it"," for it is the Sunnah.'\"" [Sound]"""
"20687","(20681) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān informed us, Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar ibn al-Zibriqān informed us, Zayd ibn al-Ḥubāb informed us, ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Abī Salamah informed us: that Ruzayq ibn Ḥakīm was a governor for ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz over Aylah, and he wrote to him: \I do not find the witness and the oath except in the Ḥijāz.\"" So ʿUmar wrote to him: \""Judge by it"," for it is the Sunnah.\"" [Sound. It was narrated before]"""
"20688","(20682) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm narrated to us, al-Rabīʿ informed us, al-Shāfiʿī informed us, Marwān ibn Muʿāwiyah al-Fazārī informed us, Ḥafṣ ibn Maymūn al-Thaqafī narrated to us, he said: \I brought a dispute to al-Shaʿbī concerning a muḍiḥah wound"," and al-Qāʾis testified that it was a muḍiḥah. The wounded man said to al-Shaʿbī: 'Will you accept the testimony of a single man against me?' Al-Shaʿbī said: 'Al-Qāʾis has testified that it is a muḍiḥah"," and the wounded man shall swear an oath to that effect.'\"" He said: \""So al-Shaʿbī judged in the matter.\"" Al-Shāfiʿī (may Allāh have mercy on him) said: And it was mentioned from Hushaym"," from Mughīrah"," that al-Shaʿbī said: \""The people of Madīnah judge by the oath together with a witness.\"" [Sound]"""
"20689","(20683) And Abū Saʿīd informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās narrated to us, al-Rabīʿ informed us, al-Shāfiʿī informed us, Mālik informed us: that Sulaymān ibn Yasār and Abū Salamah ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān were asked, \Is judgment rendered by the oath together with a witness?\"" They both said: \""Yes.\""\n\nAl-Shāfiʿī (may Allāh have mercy on him) said: And Ḥammād ibn Zayd mentioned"," from Ayyūb ibn Abī Tamīmah al-Sakhtiyānī"," from Muḥammad ibn Sīrīn: that Shurayḥ judged by the oath together with a witness.\n\nHe said: And Ismāʿīl ibn ʿUlayyah mentioned"," from Ayyūb"," from Ibn Sīrīn: that ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUtbah ibn Masʿūd judged by the oath together with a witness.\n\nHe said: And Hushaym mentioned"," from Ḥuṣayn: \""I brought a dispute to ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUtbah"," and he judged by the oath together with a witness.\""\n\nAl-Shāfiʿī said: And it was mentioned from ʿImrān ibn Ḥudayr"," from Abī Mijlaz: \""Zurārah ibn Awfā judged and accepted my testimony alone.\""\n\nHe said: And Shuʿbah said"," from Abū Qays and from Abū Isḥāq: that Shurayḥ accepted the testimony of each one of them individually. [Weak]"""
"20690","(20684) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān informed us, ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us, Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān narrated to us, Ibn Numayr narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from al-Aʿmash, from Abū Isḥāq, who said: \Shurayḥ accepted my testimony alone.\"" [Good]"""
"20691","(20685) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Saʿīd al-Aḥmasī informed me; al-Ḥusayn ibn Ḥumayd narrated to us; Abū al-Walīd narrated to us; Shuʿbah narrated from Abū Qays, who said: I testified before Shurayḥ regarding a muṣḥaf, and he accepted his testimony alone. [Weak]"
"20692","(20686) Abū Ḥāzim al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-Faḍl ibn Khamīrūyah informed us; Aḥmad ibn Najdah narrated to us; Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr narrated to us; Hushaym informed us; Yūnus informed us from Ibn Sīrīn, who said: Shurayḥ used to accept the testimony of a single witness when he recognized him, along with the oath of the claimant, in matters of small value. [Authentic]"
"20693","(20687) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn Ṣāliḥ ibn Hānīʾ narrated to us; al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl narrated to us; ʿAffān ibn Muslim narrated to us; Ḥammād ibn Zayd narrated from ʿAbd al-Majīd al-ʿAtakī, that Yaḥyā ibn Yaʿmar used to judge on the basis of one witness and an oath. [Weak]"
"20694","(20688) Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us; Abū al-Aswad informed us; Ibn Lahīʿah narrated from Bukayr, that he heard Abū Salamah administering an oath to the rightful claimant along with a single witness. Bukayr said: He continued to judge by that among us. [Weak]"
"20695","(20689) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ, Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī, and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣaghānī narrated to us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf narrated to us; Kulthūm ibn Ziyād narrated: I came upon Sulaymān ibn Ḥabīb and al-Zuhri, and both of them were judging by that—that is, by one witness and an oath. Kulthūm said: Abū Thābit Sulaymān ibn Ḥabīb was the judge of the people of al-Madīnah for thirty years, judging by an oath together with a witness. [Weak]"
"20696","(20690) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr narrated to us; Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm informed us; al-Rabīʿ informed us; al-Shāfiʿī said: al-Zanjī ibn Khālid informed us from Ibn Jurayj from ʿAṭāʾ, who said: There is no revocable divorce (rajʿah) except with two witnesses, unless there is a valid excuse, in which case he brings one witness and swears an oath along with his witness.\n\nAl-Shāfiʿī, raḥimahullāh, said: ʿAṭāʾ issues fatwā on the basis of an oath together with a witness in a matter in which none of our companions holds this view.\n\nAl-Shāfiʿī, raḥimahullāh, said: An oath together with a witness does not contradict anything from the apparent meaning of the Qurʾān, for we judge by two witnesses, and by one witness and two women, and there is no oath. So when there is one witness, we judge by one witness and an oath, and this is not contrary to the apparent meaning of the Qurʾān, for He did not prohibit the acceptance of less than what He explicitly stated in His Book.\n\nAl-Shāfiʿī, raḥimahullāh, said: And the Messenger of Allah ﷺ is most knowledgeable of the meaning intended by Allah, Mighty and Sublime. And Allah, Mighty and Sublime, has commanded us to take what He has given us and to refrain from what He has forbidden us, and we ask Allah for protection and guidance. [Hasan due to supporting narrations]"
"20697","(20691) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf al-Baghdādī informed us; ʿUthmān ibn Muḥammad ibn Bishr narrated to us; Ismāʿīl al-Qāḍī narrated to us; Ibn Abī Uways and ʿĪsā ibn Mīnāʾ both said: ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī al-Zinād narrated to us from his father, from the fuqahāʾ whose opinion is relied upon among the people of al-Madīnah, that they used to say: An oath together with a witness is not valid in divorce (ṭalāq), manumission (ʿitāq), or separation (furqah), and they did not accept the testimony of women, even with a man accompanying them, except in matters that only women would witness. And they used to say: If a single witness testifies for someone regarding the killing of his slave, he swears one oath along with his witness, and the value of his slave becomes due. [Hasan due to supporting narrations]"
"20698","(20692) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Dāwūd al-Razzāz informed us; I read to him from his original in Baghdād; Abū ʿAmr ʿUthmān ibn Aḥmad al-Daqqāq narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn ʿUbayd Allāh al-Munādī narrated to us; Abū Badr narrated to us; Hāshim ibn Hāshim narrated to me; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Nisṭās, the mawlā of Kathīr ibn al-Ṣalt, informed me that Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh, raḍiya Allāhu ʿanhu, informed him that he heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: Let no one swear a sinful oath near this minbar of mine, even if it be over a green siwāk, except that he will take his seat in the Fire, or the Fire will become incumbent upon him.\n\nAnd Abū Ḍamrah Anas ibn ʿIyāḍ similarly reported it from Hāshim ibn Hāshim: \near this minbar.\"" [Authentic due to supporting narrations]"""
"20699","(20693) And Mālik ibn Anas narrated it, as Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzzakkī informed us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us; al-Shāfiʿī informed us; Mālik informed us from Hāshim ibn Hāshim ibn ʿUtbah ibn Abī Waqqāṣ from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Nisṭās from Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh, raḍiya Allāhu ʿanhu, that the Prophet ﷺ said: Whoever swears a sinful oath near this minbar of mine, he will take his seat in the Fire. [Authentic due to supporting narrations]"
"20700","(20694) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr narrated to us; Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm informed us; al-Rabīʿ informed us; al-Shāfiʿī said: al-Ḍaḥḥāk ibn ʿUthmān informed us from Nawfal ibn Musāḥiq al-ʿĀmirī from al-Muhājir ibn Abī Umayyah, who said: Abū Bakr al-Ṣiddīq, raḍiya Allāhu ʿanhu, wrote to me: \Send me Qays ibn Makshūḥ in bonds.\"" So he swore fifty oaths at the minbar of the Prophet ﷺ that he had not killed Dādhawayh. And he narrated it in the earlier version"," saying: \""Someone we trust informed us from al-Ḍaḥḥāk ibn ʿUthmān from al-Maqburī from Nawfal ibn Musāḥiq","\"" and he mentioned it with the same meaning and completed it further. [Weak]"""
"20701","(20695) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar ibn Maṭar narrated to us that Yaḥyā ibn Muḥammad narrated to us that ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Muʿādh narrated to us that my father narrated to us that Shuʿbah narrated from Manṣūr, from al-Shaʿbī, who said: A man was killed, so ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāh (may Allah be pleased with him) entered the chamber and brought in fifty men from among the defendants, and they swore: \We did not kill him"," nor do we know who the killer is.\""\n\nAnd it has been narrated to us from ʬāʾ ibn Abī Rabāḥ that a man said to his wife: \""Your rope is upon your hump\"" (i.e."," go wherever you wish)"," repeatedly. He came to ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāh (may Allah be pleased with him)"," and he made him swear between the Rukn and the Maqām: \""What did you intend by your words?\""\n\nBoth narrations are mursal"," one corroborating the other in what they agree upon regarding transferring the oath to al-Masjid al-Ḥarām. [Weak]"""
"20702","(20696) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr narrated to us that Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm narrated to us that al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān narrated to us that al-Shāfiʿī said: This is the position of the judges of Makkah and their muftīs. Among their evidences for this, along with their consensus, is that Muslim and al-Qaddāḥ informed me from Ibn Jurayj, from ʿIkrimah ibn Khālid, that ʿAbd al-Raḥman ibn ʿAwf (may Allah be pleased with him) saw people swearing between the Maqām and the House (the Kaʿbah). He said: \Is there a blood-money obligation upon me?\"" They said: \""No.\"" He said: \""Is there a great sum of wealth upon me?\"" They said: \""No.\"" He said: \""I fear that people may become too familiar with this place.\""\n\nAl-Shāfiʿī (may Allah have mercy on him) said: They held that a great sum of wealth is what you described"," namely twenty dinars and above.\n\nHe said: And Mālik said: He swears upon the minbar for a quarter of a dinar.\n\nAl-Shaykh (may Allah have mercy on him) said: His statement \""people may become too familiar\"" means they may become so accustomed to it that its reverence departs from their hearts. Abū ʿUbayd said: It is said \""baʾtu biʾl-shayʾ\"" when I become familiar with something. [Weak]"""
"20703","(20697) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq narrated to us that Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us that al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān narrated to us that al-Shāfiʿī narrated to us that Mālik ibn Anas narrated from Dāwūd ibn al-Ḥuṣayn that he heard Abū Ghaṭṭān ibn Ṭarīf al-Murrī say: Zayd ibn Thābit and Ibn Muṭīʿ disputed before Marwān ibn al-Ḥakam concerning a house. Marwān ruled that Zayd ibn Thābit should swear upon the minbar. Zayd said: \I will swear for him right here.\"" Marwān said: \""No"," by Allah"," only at the place where rights are determined.\"" So Zayd began to swear that his right was indeed a right"," but he refused to swear upon the minbar. Marwān was astonished by that.\n\nMālik said: Zayd disliked the delay of the oath. [Authentic]"""
"20704","(20698) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr narrated to us that Abū al-ʿAbbās narrated to us that al-Rabīʿ narrated to us that al-Shāfiʿī said: And it has reached me that ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāh (may Allah be pleased with him) swore upon the minbar in a dispute that was between him and a man, and that ʿUthmān (may Allah be pleased with him) had the oath returned to him upon the minbar, but he avoided it and paid expiation for it, saying: \I fear that a decree of fate may coincide with a calamity"," and it may be said: 'Because of his oath.'\"" [Weak]"""
"20705","(20699) ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us that Abū Bakr ibn Maḥmūyah al-ʿAskarī narrated to us that ʿĪsā ibn Ghaylān narrated to us that Ḥāḍir ibn Muṭahhar narrated to us that Abū ʿUbaydah Mujjāʿah narrated from Qatādah, from Jābir ibn Zayd, from Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with them both), that he was asked about a woman who testified that she had suckled a woman and her husband. He said: \Make her swear at the Maqām. If she is lying"," a year will not pass before her breasts wither.\"" So she was made to swear"," and she swore"," and a year did not pass before her breasts withered. [Weak]"""
"20706","(20700) Al-Shaykh said: We have narrated from al-Shaʿbī, from Abū Mūsā al-Ashʿarī, in the story of the bequest, who said: This was a matter that did not occur after what took place during the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him). So he made them both swear after ʿAṣr: \We did not betray.\""\n\nAbū Naṣr ibn Qatādah informed us that Abū Manṣūr al-ʿAbbās ibn al-Faḍl narrated to us that Aḥmad ibn Najdah narrated to us that Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr narrated to us that Hushaym informed us that Zakariyyā narrated from al-Shaʿbī"," and he mentioned it. [Weak]"""
"20707","(20701) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ, Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī in Naysābūr, and Abū al-Qāsim Zayd ibn Abī Hāshim al-ʿAlawī in Kūfah informed us, saying: Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī ibn Duḥaym narrated to us that Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbd Allāh informed us that Wakīʿ narrated from al-Aʿmash.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Ṣāliḥ ibn Abī Ṭāhir al-ʿAnbarī informed us that my grandfather Yaḥyā ibn Manṣūr al-Qāḍī narrated to us that Aḥmad ibn Salamah narrated to us that Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us that Jarīr narrated from al-Aʿmash, from Abī Ṣāliḥ, from Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: \Three persons whom Allah will not speak to on the Day of Resurrection"," nor will He purify them"," and for them is a painful punishment: a man who has surplus water on a path and prevents the wayfarer from it; a man who pledged allegiance to an imam for worldly gain — if he gives him what he wants"," he fulfills his pledge"," and if he does not give"," he does not fulfill it; and a man who bargains over merchandise after ʿAṣr"," swearing by Allah: 'I was given such-and-such for it","' and the other believes him.\"" The wording is that of Jarīr's hadith"," and in the hadith of Wakīʿ is not: \""a man who pledged allegiance to an imam.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Zuhayr ibn Ḥarb from Jarīr"," and from Ibn Abī Shaybah and al-Ashajj from Wakīʿ. And al-Bukhārī narrated it from ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd Allāh from Jarīr. [Authentic. Agreed upon]"""
"20708","(20702) Sumayy narrated from Abī Ṣāliḥ, from Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), as Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū Muḥammad Aḥmad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Muzanī narrated to us that ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad ibn Nājiyah narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn Yūnus al-Jammāl narrated to us that Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah narrated from ʿAmr ibn Dīnār, from Abī Ṣāliḥ, from Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Prophet (peace be upon him), who said: \Three persons whom Allah will not speak to on the Day of Resurrection"," nor will He purify them"," nor will He look at them: a man who swears an oath after the prayer of ʿAṣr to seize the property of a Muslim man; a man who swears that he was offered more for his merchandise than he was offered"," while he is lying; and a man who withholds surplus water. Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic"," says: 'I will withhold My bounty from you as you withheld surplus water that your hands did not produce.'\""\n\nBoth al-Bukhārī and Muslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from the hadith of Sufyān"," as I narrated it in the book Iḥyāʾ al-Mawāt with a higher chain. [Authentic. Agreed upon]"""
"20709","(20703) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us that Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us that al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān narrated to us that al-Shāfiʿī narrated to us that ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muʾammal narrated from Ibn Abī Mulaykah, who said: I wrote to Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with them both) from al-Ṭāʾif concerning two slave-girls, one of whom had struck the other, and there was no witness against them. He wrote back to me: \Detain them after the prayer of ʿAṣr"," then recite over them: {Indeed"," those who exchange the covenant of Allah and their oaths for a small price} [Āl ʿImrān:77].\"" I did so"," and she confessed. [Weak]"""
"20710","(20704) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr narrated to us that Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm narrated to us that al-Rabīʿ narrated to us that al-Shāfiʿī informed us that Muṭarrif ibn Māzin narrated to me with a chain I do not recall: that Ibn al-Zubayr ordered that an oath be taken upon the muṣḥaf.\n\nAl-Shāfiʿī (may Allah have mercy on him) said: And I saw Muṭarrif in Ṣanʿāʾ swearing upon the muṣḥaf. Al-Shāfiʿī (may Allah have mercy on him) said: And among the judges of the provinces were those who would administer oaths upon the muṣḥaf, and that is, in my view, good. [Weak]"
"20711","(20705) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ, Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī, and others narrated to us, they said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn ʿAffān narrated to us: Ibn Numayr narrated from al-Aʿmash, from Shaqīq, who said: ʿAbdullāh said: the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Whoever takes an oath under compulsion in order to usurp the property of a Muslim"," while he is lying therein"," he shall meet Allah and He shall be angry with him.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Agreed upon (muttafaq ʿalayh)]"""
"20712","(20706) Abū Ṣāliḥ ibn Abī Ṭāhir al-ʿAnbarī narrated to us: my grandfather Yaḥyā ibn Manṣūr al-Qāḍī narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn Salamah narrated to us: Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us: Wakīʿ narrated to us: al-Aʿmash narrated from Abī Wāʾil, who is Shaqīq ibn Salamah, from ʿAbdullāh, who is Ibn Masʿūd (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ), who said: \Whoever takes an oath under compulsion in order to usurp the property of a Muslim"," he shall meet Allah and He shall be angry with him. The confirmation of that is in the Book of Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic: {Indeed"," those who exchange the covenant of Allah and their oaths for a small price…} [Āl ʿImrān:77].\"" To the end of the verse.\n\nThen al-Ashʿath ibn Qays entered and said: \""What has Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān narrated to you?\"" He said: \""Such and such.\"" He said: \""He has spoken the truth. This was revealed concerning me. There was a dispute between me and a man regarding a piece of land in Yemen"," so we brought the dispute to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ). He said: 'Do you have proof?' I said: 'No.' He said: 'Then his oath.' I said: 'Then he will swear.' He said: 'Whoever takes an oath under compulsion in order to usurp the property of a Muslim"," he shall meet Allah and He shall be angry with him.' So Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic"," revealed: {Indeed"," those who exchange the covenant of Allah and their oaths for a small price…} [Āl ʿImrān:77] to the end of the verse.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm"," and al-Bukhārī narrated it from another route from al-Aʿmash. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Agreed upon (muttafaq ʿalayh)]"""
"20713","(20707) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq al-Faqīh narrated to us, dictating: Bishr ibn Mūsā narrated to us: al-Ḥumaydī narrated to us: Sufyān narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Malik ibn Aʿyan and Jāmiʿ ibn Abī Rāshid narrated from Abī Wāʾil, from ʿAbdullāh, who said: the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Whoever usurps the property of a Muslim by means of a false oath"," he shall meet Allah and He shall be angry with him.\""\n\nʿAbdullāh said: \""Then the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) recited to us its confirmation from the Book of Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic: {Indeed"," those who exchange the covenant of Allah and their oaths for a small price…} [Āl ʿImrān:77] — the verse.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from al-Ḥumaydī"," and Muslim narrated it from Ibn Abī ʿUmar from Sufyān. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Agreed upon (muttafaq ʿalayh)]"""
"20714","(20708) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bushrān al-ʿAdl narrated to us in Baghdad: Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Miṣrī narrated to us: Mālik ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us: Yazīd ibn Hārūn narrated to us: Jarīr ibn Ḥāzim narrated to us: ʿAdī ibn ʿAdī narrated from Rajāʾ ibn Ḥaywah and al-ʿUrs ibn ʿUmayrah, from his father ʿAdī, who said: \There was a dispute between Imruʾ al-Qays and a man from Ḥaḍramawt"," so they brought the matter to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ). He said: 'Your proof"," or else his oath.' He said: 'O Messenger of Allah"," if he swears"," he will take my land.' The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: 'Whoever takes a false oath in order to usurp the property of his brother"," he shall meet Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic"," and He shall be angry with him.' Imruʾ al-Qays said: 'O Messenger of Allah"," then what is for the one who relinquishes it while being in the right?' He said: 'Paradise.' He said: 'Then I bear witness that I have relinquished it.'\""\n\nJarīr said: \""Ayyūb added to me — and we were all together when we heard from ʿAdī — he said: ʿAdī said in the ḥadīth of al-ʿUrs ibn ʿUmayrah: 'Then this verse was revealed: {Indeed"," those who exchange the covenant of Allah and their oaths for a small price…} [Āl ʿImrān:77] to its end.' But I did not memorize it from ʿAdī.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"20715","(20709) Abū Ṣāliḥ ibn Abī Ṭāhir al-ʿAnbarī narrated to us: my grandfather Yaḥyā ibn Manṣūr al-Qāḍī narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn Salamah narrated to us: Qutaybah ibn Saʿīd al-Thaqafī narrated to us: Abū al-Aḥwaṣ narrated from Simāk, from ʿAlqamah ibn Wāʾil, from his father, who said: \A man from Ḥaḍramawt and a man from Kindah came to the Prophet (ﷺ). The Ḥaḍramī said: 'O Messenger of Allah"," this man has seized my land that belonged to my father.' The Kindī said: 'It is my land; I cultivate it in my possession. He has no right in it.' The Prophet (ﷺ) said to the Ḥaḍramī: 'Do you have proof?' He said: 'No.' He said: 'Then his oath.' He said: 'O Messenger of Allah"," the man is a transgressor; he does not care what he swears upon"," and he does not refrain from anything.' He said: 'You have nothing from him except that.' So he set out to swear for him. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said when he turned away: 'If he swears upon property in order to consume it unjustly"," he shall meet Allah and He shall be turning away from him.'\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Qutaybah ibn Saʿīd and others. In his words \""so he set out to swear for him\"" and his words \""he said when he turned away","\"" there is an indication that oaths were being transferred to the mosque in Madīnah. And Allah knows best. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim]"""
"20716","(20710) Abū Aḥmad ʿAbdullāh ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Mihrānjānī narrated to us: Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar al-Muzakkī narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Būshanjī narrated to us: Ibn Bukayr narrated to us: Mālik narrated from al-ʿAlāʾ ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, from Maʿbad ibn Kaʿb, from his brother ʿAbdullāh ibn Kaʿb, from Abī Umāmah, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Whoever usurps the right of a Muslim by means of his oath"," Allah has forbidden Paradise for him and obligated the Fire for him.\"" They said: \""Even if it is something small"," O Messenger of Allah?\"" He said: \""Even if it is a twig of a tooth-stick (siwāk).\"" He said it three times. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim]"""
"20717","(20711) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: Abū ʿAbdillāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Nuʿaym narrated to us: Qutaybah ibn Saʿīd narrated to us: Ismāʿīl ibn Jaʿfar narrated from al-ʿAlāʾ ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, and he mentioned it with its chain, similar to it, except that he did not say \he said it three times.\"" Muslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Qutaybah ibn Saʿīd. [Ṣaḥīḥ. As previously stated]"""
"20718","(20712) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: Abū al-Naḍr al-Faqīh narrated to us: Abū Salamah Muʿādh ibn Najdah al-Qurashī narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū al-Naḍr ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Qatādah narrated to us: Abū Muḥammad Aḥmad ibn Isḥāq ibn Shaybān al-Baghdādī, then al-Harawī, narrated therein: Muʿādh ibn Najdah narrated to us: Khallād ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us: Nāfiʿ ibn ʿUmar al-Makkī narrated from Ibn Abī Mulaykah, who said: \I wrote to Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with them both) regarding two women who were sewing leather in a house"," and in the room there were young girls. One of them came out with her hand dripping blood"," and she said: 'This one struck my hand","' while the other denied it.\"" He said: \""So Ibn ʿAbbās wrote to me that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) ruled that the oath is upon the one against whom the claim is made. Were people to be given based on their claims"," people would claim the bloods and properties of others. So summon her and recite to her: {Indeed"," those who exchange the covenant of Allah and their oaths for a small price — for them there will be no share in the Hereafter"," and Allah will not speak to them"," nor will He look at them on the Day of Resurrection"," nor will He purify them"," and for them is a painful punishment.} [Āl ʿImrān:77]\"" He said: \""So she confessed"," and that reached Ibn ʿAbbās"," and it pleased him.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Khallād ibn Yaḥyā"," abbreviated"," and Muslim narrated it from another route"," abbreviated"," from Nāfiʿ. And al-Bukhārī narrated it from the ḥadīth of Ibn Jurayj from Ibn Abī Mulaykah in its full length. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Agreed upon (muttafaq ʿalayh)]"""
"20719","(20713) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh al-Aṣbahānī narrated to us: ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: Ismāʿīl ibn al-ʿAbbās al-Warrāq and Aḥmad ibn al-ʿAbbās al-Baghawī narrated, they said: ʿAlī ibn Ḥarb narrated to us: Ḥumayd ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Ruʾāsī narrated from al-Ḥasan ibn Ṣāliḥ, from al-Aswad ibn Qays, from Ḥassān ibn Thumāmah, who said: \They claimed that Ḥudhayfah recognized his stolen camel and contested regarding it before the judge of the Muslims. An oath was imposed upon Ḥudhayfah in the judgment"," so he wished to buy off his oath. He was told: 'Ten dirhams for you.' He refused. He was told: 'Twenty.' He refused. He was told: 'Thirty.' He refused. He was told: 'Forty.' He refused. Ḥudhayfah said: 'I will leave my camel.' So he swore that it was his camel — he had neither sold it nor gifted it.\""\n\nIt is mentioned that Jubayr ibn Muṭʿim ransomed his oath for ten thousand dirhams.\n\nAnd it is mentioned that ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him) — in a dispute that occurred between him and Muʿādh ibn ʿAfrāʾ regarding something — said: \""So ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) took an oath"," then he said: 'Do you see that I have established my right by my oath? Go now"," for it is yours.'\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"20720","(20714) Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī narrated to us: Ḥājib ibn Aḥmad ibn Sufyān narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Ḥammād narrated to us: Abū Muʿāwiyah narrated from al-Aʿmash, from Shaqīq, from ʿAbdullāh, who said: the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Whoever takes an oath while being a transgressor therein"," in order to usurp the property of a Muslim"," he shall meet Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic"," and He shall be angry with him.\"" Al-Ashʿath said: \""By Allah"," that was the case. There was a dispute between me and a man from the Jews regarding a piece of land"," and he denied my claim. So I brought him before the Prophet (ﷺ). The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: 'Do you have proof?' I said: 'No.' He said to the Jew: 'Take an oath.' I said: 'O Messenger of Allah"," then he will swear and take my property.' So Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic"," revealed: {Indeed"," those who exchange the covenant of Allah and their oaths for a small price — for them there will be no share in the Hereafter…} [Āl ʿImrān:77] — the verse.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"20721","(20715) And Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Aḥmad ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us, that ʿAbdullāh ibn Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal narrated to me, that my father narrated to me, that Abū Muʿāwiyah narrated to me, that al-Aʿmash mentioned it with its chain of narration, similar to it.\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad from Abū Muʿāwiyah, and Muslim narrated it from Ibn Numayr from Abū Muʿāwiyah."
"20722","(20716) And Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us that Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us that Ibn Milḥān narrated to us that Yaḥyā ibn Bukayr narrated to us that al-Layth narrated from ʿUqayl from Ibn Shihāb, that he heard a man from Muzaynah — one who sought knowledge and preserved it — narrating to Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyib that Abū Hurayradh, may Allah be pleased with him, said: \While we were sitting with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ"," he mentioned the hadith concerning the Jewish man who had committed zinā after having been married. He said: 'The Prophet ﷺ set out"," leading the way to the Bayt al-Midrās"," and said to them: O assembly of Jews"," I adjure you by Allah"," Who revealed the Tawrāh to Mūsā"," what do you find in the Tawrāh regarding the punishment for one who commits zinā after having been married?'\"""""
"20723","(20717) And Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us that Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us that Aḥmad ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār narrated to us that Yūnus ibn Bukayr narrated from Ibn Isḥāq that Ḥusayn ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUbaydullāh ibn ʿAbbās narrated from ʿIkrimah from Ibn ʿAbbās, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: \The Messenger of Allah ﷺ wrote to the Jews: 'From Muḥammad"," the Messenger of Allah"," the brother of Mūsā and his companion — Allah sent him with that which He sent him. I adjure you by Allah and what was revealed to Mūsā on the day of Ṭūr Sīnāʾ"," and He split the sea for you"," and saved you"," and destroyed your enemy"," and fed you with manna and salwā"," and shaded you with clouds — do you find in your Scripture that I am the Messenger of Allah to you and to all of mankind? If that is so"," then fear Allah and submit. And if it is not with you"," then there is no compulsion upon you.'\"""""
"20724","(20718) And Abū al-Qāsim Zayd ibn Abī Hāshim al-ʿAlawī in al-Kūfah informed us that Abū Jaʿfar ibn Duḥaym narrated to us that Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbdullāh informed us that Wakīʿ narrated from Sufyān from Ayyūb from Ibn Sīrīn that Kaʿb ibn Sur brought a Jewish man into the church, placed the Tawrāh upon his head, and adjured him by Allah.\n\nAnd it is narrated from al-Ashʿarī, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: \The Jewish man is adjured in the church.\"""""
"20725","(20719) And Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us that Muḥammad ibn Bakr narrated to us that Abū Dāwūd narrated to us that Musaddad narrated to us that Abū al-Aḥwaṣ narrated to us that ʿAṭāʾ ibn al-Sāʾib narrated from Abū Yaḥyā from Ibn ʿAbbās, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to a man he had adjured: \Swear by Allah"," besides Whom there is no deity"," that he has nothing with him\"" — meaning"," regarding the claimant."""
"20726","(20720) And Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū Muḥammad al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Sakhṭawayh al-ʿAdl narrated to us that Abū Ismāʿīl Muḥammad ibn Ismāʿīl narrated to us that Abū Nuʿaym al-Faḍl ibn Dukayn narrated to us —\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us that Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd narrated to us that Tamtām narrated to us that Abū Nuʿaym narrated to us that al-Ḥārith ibn Sulaymān al-Kindī narrated to me that Kurdūs al-Thaʿlabī narrated from Ashʿath ibn Qays al-Kindī from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that a man from Kindah and a man from Ḥaḍramawt brought a dispute before the Messenger of Allah ﷺ concerning a piece of land in Yemen. The Ḥaḍramī said: \O Messenger of Allah"," this man's father seized my land.\"" He said to the Kindī: \""What do you say?\"" He said: \""I say it is it"," in my possession"," inherited from my father.\"" He said to the Ḥaḍramī: \""Do you have proof?\"" He said: \""No"," but he shall swear"," O Messenger of Allah"," by Allah"," besides Whom there is no deity"," that he does not know that it is my land which his father seized.\"" The Kindī prepared to take the oath"," but the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \""No man shall seize wealth by means of his oath except that he shall meet Allah on the Day he encounters Him"," and he shall be mutilated.\"" So the Kindī returned it.\n\nThis is the wording of the Ḥāfiẓ"," and the hadith of Ibn ʿAbdān is close to it."""
"20727","(20721) And Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Aḥmad ibn ʿUthmān al-Adamī narrated to us that Abū Qilābah narrated to us that Bishr ibn ʿUmar narrated to us that Shuʿbah narrated from al-Ḥakam from Sharīḥ regarding His statement — exalted is He — {And We gave him wisdom and decisive speech} [Ṣād 38:20]: He said: \Oaths and witnesses.\"" And Mujāhid said likewise."""
"20728","(20722) And Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī both said that Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us that al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn ʿAffān narrated to us that Abū Yaḥyā al-Ḥimṣānī narrated to us that Misʿar narrated from Abū Ḥaṣīn from Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī that the Prophet Dāwūd ﷺ was commanded to judge, and he was distressed by it. So Allah, mighty and majestic, revealed: \Adjure them by My name and ask them for the proof.\"" He said: \""That is the decisive speech.\"""""
"20729","(20723) And Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us that Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us that al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn ʿAffān narrated to us that Asbāṭ narrated from Muḥammad ibn ʿAjlān from Nāfiʿ from Ibn ʿUmar, may Allah be pleased with them both, that he heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ — a man was swearing by his father — and he said: \Do not swear by your fathers. Whoever swears by Allah"," let him speak the truth. And whoever is adjured by Allah"," let him be pleased. And whoever is adjured by Allah and is not pleased"," then he is not of Allah.\""\n\nMuḥammad ibn Ismāʿīl al-Aḥmasī followed him up from Asbāṭ."""
"20730","(20724) And Abū Naṣr ibn Qatādah informed us that Aḥmad ibn Isḥāq ibn Shaybān informed us that Muʿādh ibn Najdah narrated to us that Kāmil ibn Ṭalḥah narrated to us that Layth ibn Saʿd narrated to us that ʿUqayl narrated from Ibn Shihāb, who said: \Two men brought a dispute before the Messenger of Allah ﷺ"," and it was as though one of them was negligent in part of his proof"," not fully presenting it. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ judged in favour of the other. The one who had been negligent in his proof said: 'ḤasbiyAllāh wa niʿmal-wakīl' (Allah is sufficient for me"," and He is the best Disposer of affairs). The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'ḤasbiyAllāh wa niʿmal-wakīl","' moving his hand two or three times. He said: 'Seek your right until you are unable. And when you are unable"," then say: ḤasbiyAllāh wa niʿmal-wakīl"," for judgment between you shall be rendered based upon your proof.'\"" This is a munqaṭiʿ (disconnected) hadith."""
"20731","(20725) And Abū ʿAliyy al-Rūdhbārī informed us — that Muḥammad ibn Bakr informed us — that Abū Dāwūd informed us — that ʿAbd al-Wahhāb ibn Najdah and Mūsā ibn Marwān al-Raqqī both said — that Baqiyyat ibn al-Walīd narrated to us from Baḥīr ibn Saʿd, from Khālid ibn Maʿdān, from Sayf, from ʿAwf ibn Mālik, may Allah be pleased with him, that he narrated to them: that the Prophet ﷺ passed judgment between two men. The one against whom the judgment was given, as he turned away, said: \Allah is sufficient for me"," and He is the best Disposer of affairs\"" (ḤasbiyAllāhu wa niʿmalwakīl). The Prophet ﷺ said: \""Indeed"," Allah"," exalted is His praise"," reproaches one for incapacity; but you must adopt prudence (al-kays). When a matter overcomes you"," then say: 'Allah is sufficient for me"," and He is the best Disposer of affairs.'\"" [Ḍaʿīf (Weak)]"""
"20732","(20726) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us among others — they said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us — that al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us — that al-Shāfiʿī said: \The proof in this is that Muḥammad ibn ʿAliyy ibn Shāfiʿ informed us from ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAliyy ibn al-Sāʾib"," from Nāfiʿ ibn ʿUjayr ibn ʿAbd Yazīd"," that Rukānah ibn ʿAbd Yazīd divorced his wife"," then came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: 'I have irrevocably divorced my wife (al-battatah)"," and by Allah"," I only intended one (divorce).' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'By Allah"," did you only intend one?' Rukānah said: 'By Allah"," I only intended one.' So he (the Prophet ﷺ) restored her to him.\"" [Ḥasan (Fair) on account of other chains. Previously cited under no. 149910]"""
"20733","(20727) ʿAliyy ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us — that Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us — that Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq informed us — that al-Qaʿnabī informed us — that Nāfiʿ ibn ʿUmar al-Jumaḥī informed us from Ibn Abī Mulaykah, who said: Ibn ʿAbbās, may Allah be pleased with them both, wrote to me that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ decreed that the oath (al-yamīn) be imposed upon the defendant (al-muddaʿī ʿalayh). Al-Bukhārī and Muslim both recorded it in their Ṣaḥīḥ collections from the ḥadīth of Nāfiʿ ibn ʿUmar. This ruling applies to every defendant, unless he produces his evidence. [Ṣaḥīḥ (Authentic). Agreed upon (muttafaq ʿalayh)]"
"20734","(20728) And Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzakkī and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī both informed us — they said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us — that Baḥr ibn Naṣr informed us — that Ibn Wahb informed me — that Mālik and ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar both informed me from Nāfiʿ, from ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar, who said: \When a man gives his wife the authority over her own matter (i.e."," the option of divorce)"," then the ruling is what she decides — except that he disputes it"," saying: 'I only intended one divorce.' He shall swear an oath to that effect"," and she shall be restored to him.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ (Authentic)]"""
"20735","(20729) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr both informed us — they said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us — that Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī informed us — that Mūsā ibn Dāwūd informed us — that Sharīk informed us from ʿUbaydullāh ibn ʿUmar, from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar, who said: \If a woman claims that her husband intended divorce"," and the two parties dispute"," then the oath is upon the one who performed the act (i.e."," the husband): 'By Allah"," he did not do it.'\"" [Ḍaʿīf (Weak)]"""
"20736","(20730) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us — that Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā informed us — that Yaḥyā ibn al-Rabīʿ al-Makkī informed us — that Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah informed us from Idrīs al-Awdī, who said: Saʿīd ibn Abī Burdah brought out a document to us and said: \This is the letter of ʿUmar to Abū Mūsā"," may Allah be pleased with them both.\"" He mentioned it"," and in it (was the instruction): \""Grant the claimant (al-muddaʿī) a respite (amad) until he reaches it (i.e."," his deadline). If he produces evidence (bayyinah)"," then (act upon it); otherwise"," direct the judgment against him"," for that is more fitting to dispel the ambiguity and more effective in establishing the excuse.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ (Authentic). Previously cited under no. 20283]"""
"20737","(20731) The noble Abū al-Fatḥ Nāṣir ibn al-Ḥusayn al-ʿUmarī informed us — that ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Sharīḥ informed us — that Abū al-Qāsim al-Baghawī informed us — that ʿAlī ibn al-Jaʿd informed us — that Sharīk informed us from ʿĀṣim, from Muḥammad ibn Sīrīn, from Sharīḥ, who said: \Whoever claims against my judgment"," the burden is upon him until he brings evidence. The truth is more deserving than my judgment"," and the truth is more deserving than a false oath.\"" [Ḍaʿīf (Weak)]"""
"20738","(20732) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us among others — they said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us — that al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us — that al-Shāfiʿī informed us — that Mālik ibn Anas informed us from Abū Laylā ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Sahl, that Sahl ibn Abī Ḥathmah and several elders of his people informed him that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Ḥuwayṣah, Muḥayṣah, and ʿAbd al-Raḥmān: \Will you swear and thereby establish the right to your companion's blood?\"" They said: \""No.\"" He said: \""Then the Jews shall swear.\"" Al-Bukhārī and Muslim both recorded it in their Ṣaḥīḥ collections"," as has preceded in the Book of Qasāmah. [Ṣaḥīḥ (Authentic). Agreed upon (muttafaq ʿalayh)]"""
"20739","(20733) And Abū Saʿīd informed us — that Abū al-ʿAbbās informed us — that al-Rabīʿ informed us — that al-Shāfiʿī said — and Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah and al-Thaqafī both narrated to us from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd, from Bushayr ibn Yasār, from Sahl ibn Abī Ḥathmah, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ began with the Anṣārīs (asking them to swear); but when they did not swear, he turned the oaths over to the Jews. [Ṣaḥīḥ (Authentic). Previously cited]"
"20740","(20734) He said: And Mālik informed us from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd, from Bushayr ibn Yasār, from the Prophet ﷺ, a similar narration. The Shaykh (al-Ḥāfiẓ) said: \As for the narration of Mālik ibn Anas from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd"," it is recorded in the Muwaṭṭaʾ in this form as a mursal (disconnected) narration.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ (Authentic). Previously cited]"""
"20741","(20735) Abū Aḥmad al-Mihrānjānī informed us, Abū Bakr ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us, Ibn Bukayr narrated to us, Mālik narrated from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd, from Bishr ibn Yasār, and he mentioned the hadith, in which the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said to them: \Will you swear fifty oaths and thereby establish your right over your slain or your companion?\"" They said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," how can we do so when we neither witnessed nor were present?\"" The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \""Then the Jews shall exonerate themselves with fifty oaths.\"" As for the narration of ʿAbd al-Wahhāb ibn ʿAbd al-Majīd al-Thaqafī"," it is similar in meaning"," except that it is connected (mawṣūl). [Ṣaḥīh; narrated before it.]"""
"20742","(20736) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, Ibrāhīm ibn Abī Ṭālib narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn al-Muthannā narrated to us, ʿAbd al-Wahhāb — (ḥ) and Abū al-Faḍl ibn Ibrāhīm informed us, and the wording is his: Aḥmad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm informed us, ʿAbd al-Wahhāb al-Thaqafī narrated, saying: I heard Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd say: Bishr ibn Yasār informed me from Sahl ibn Abī Ḥathmah that ʿAbd Allāh ibn Sahl al-Anṣārī and Muḥayyiṣah ibn Masʿūd went out to Khaybar and separated for their respective needs. ʿAbd Allāh ibn Sahl was killed. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Sahl, Ḥuwayyiṣah, and Muḥayyiṣah, the two sons of Masʿūd, came to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ). ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, the brother of the slain, went forward to speak, but the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \The eldest"," the eldest.\"" So Ḥuwayyiṣah and Muḥayyiṣah spoke and mentioned to him the matter of ʿAbd Allāh ibn Sahl. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \""Will fifty of you swear so that you may establish your right over your slain or your companion?\"" They said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," we were neither present nor did we witness.\"" The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \""Then shall the Jews exonerate you with fifty oaths?\"" They said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," how can we accept the oaths of a disbelieving people?\"" He said: \""So the Prophet (ﷺ) paid the blood money (diyah) on his own behalf.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn al-Muthannā from ʿAbd al-Wahhāb.\n\nSimilarly"," al-Shāfiʿī narrated it from al-Thaqafī in another place in full"," and likewise al-Layth ibn Saʿād"," Ḥammād ibn Zayd"," Bishr ibn al-Mufaḍḍal"," and others narrated it from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd.\n\nAs for Ibn ʿUyaynah"," the narration of the group from him in this hadith is that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \""Shall the Jews exonerate you with fifty oaths"," swearing that they did not kill him?\"" They said: \""How can we be satisfied with their oaths when they are polytheists?\"" He said: \""Then will fifty of you swear that they killed him?\"" They said: \""How can we swear to what we did not see?\"" And he mentioned the hadith. [Ṣaḥīh; narrated before it.]"""
"20743","(20737) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū al-Walīd al-Faqīh narrated to us, ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad narrated to us, Isḥāq informed us, Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah narrated from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd, from Bishr ibn Yasār, that he heard him narrate from Sahl ibn Abī Ḥathmah that ʿAbd Allāh ibn Sahl al-Anṣārī was found in a well, and he mentioned the hadith.\n\nThis indicates that he began with the oaths of the Jews and then turned to the Anṣārīs, which contradicts the narration of the group, and the group is more deserving of being preserved than the single narrator. Al-Shāfiʿī (may Allah have mercy on him) reconciled the hadith of Ibn ʿUyaynah here with the hadith of al-Thaqafī, and Muslim ibn al-Ḥajjāj did likewise: he included the hadith of Ibn ʿUyaynah in his book and referred to the narration of the group without citing its full text. Al-Shāfiʿī (may Allah have mercy on him) said in the Kitāb al-Qasāmah: \Ibn ʿUyaynah was not firm on whether the Prophet (ﷺ) began with the Anṣārīs or the Jews in the oaths. It is said in the hadith that he began with the Anṣārīs"," and he says: 'It is that","' or something similar.\""\n\nThe Sheikh said: \""The statement of the one who affirmed without doubt takes precedence over the one who doubted. Those who affirmed are a number"," all of them being reliable and precise memorizers. And with Allah is the success.\"" [Ṣaḥīh; narrated before it.]"""
"20744","(20738) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr and others informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us, al-Shāfiʿī informed us, Mālik ibn Anas narrated from Ibn Shihāb, from Sulaymān ibn Yasār: A man from Banū Saʿd ibn Layth raced a horse, and it stepped on the finger of a man from Juhaynah. Blood flowed from it and he died. ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) said to those against whom the claim was made: \Will you swear fifty oaths that he did not die from it?\"" They refused and felt scruples about swearing. He said to the others: \""You swear.\"" They also refused.\n\nAbū Saʿīd added in his narration with his chain: Al-Shāfiʿī (may Allah have mercy on him) said: \""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) imposed the oath upon the Anṣārīs so they could establish their right"," but when they refused to swear"," he transferred it to the Jews to exonerate themselves with it. And ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) imposed the oath upon the Laythīs to exonerate themselves with it"," but when he refused"," he transferred it to the Juhaynīs to establish their right with it. All of this is the transfer of an oath from one context in which it was deemed appropriate to another context that differs from it. Based on this and what we have found the people of knowledge in our land relating from their muftīs and judges"," both in the past and recently"," we have spoken regarding the redirecting of oaths.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"20745","(20739) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me by way of ijāzah from what was not read to him of al-Mustadrak: Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Salamah al-ʿAnazī narrated to us, ʿUthmān ibn Saʿīd al-Dārimī narrated to us, Sulaymān ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Dimashqī narrated to us — (ḥ) and Abū Saʿīd ʿUthmān ibn ʿAbdūs ibn Maḥfūẓ al-Faqīh al-Janzarawdhī informed us: Abū Muḥammad Yaḥyā ibn Manṣūr narrated to us, Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān Muḥammad ibn al-Mundhir ibn Saʿīd al-Harawī Shukr narrated to us, Yazīd ibn ʿAbd al-Ṣamad al-Dimashqī and Sulaymān ibn Ayyūb al-Dimashqī narrated, saying: Sulaymān ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Masrūq narrated from Isḥāq ibn al-Furāt, from al-Layth ibn Saʿād, from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with them both): The Prophet (ﷺ) redirected the oath to the claimant (ṭālib al-ḥaqq).\n\nSulaymān ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Dimashqī is alone in narrating this with this chain. Reliance is placed upon what has preceded, and Allah knows best. [Ḍaʿīf]"
"20746","(20740) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū al-Walīd al-Faqīh narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Hārūn narrated from ʿUthmān ibn Saʿīd, Abū al-Walīd narrated to us, Maslamah ibn ʿAlqamah narrated from Dāwūd, from al-Shaʿbī: al-Miqdād borrowed seven thousand dirhams from ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān (may Allah be pleased with him). When he demanded repayment, he said: \They are only four thousand.\"" He took the matter to ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him). ʿUthmān said: \""I lent al-Miqdād seven thousand dirhams.\"" Al-Miqdād said: \""They are only four thousand.\"" Al-Miqdād said: \""Make him swear that they are seven thousand.\"" ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: \""He has been fair to you","\"" but he refused to swear. ʿUmar said: \""Take what he has given you.\"" And he mentioned the hadith.\n\nThis chain is sound except that it is munqaṭiʿ (disconnected). Along with what we have narrated from ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) regarding qasāmah"," each of the two narrations corroborates the other regarding what they share of ʿUmar's (may Allah be pleased with him) position on redirecting the oath to the claimant (muddaʿī). In this mursal narration there is the additional transmission of the position of ʿUthmān and al-Miqdād (may Allah be pleased with them both)"," and Allah knows best. [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"20747","(20741) Abū Naṣr ibn Qatādah informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq ibn Ayyūb al-Ṣibghī narrated to us, al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn Ziyād narrated to us, Ibn Abī Uways narrated to us, Ḥusayn ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Ḍumayrah ibn Abī Ḍumayrah narrated from his father, from his grandfather, from ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib (may Allah be pleased with him), that he said: \The oath is with the witness. If there is no proof"," then the oath is upon the one against whom the claim is made"," provided he had dealings with the claimant. If he refuses (to swear)"," then the claimant swears.\"""""
"20748","(20742) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us, Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us, Tamtām narrated to us, Abū al-Walīd narrated to us, Shuʿbah narrated from al-Aʿmash. He said: I heard Ibrāhīm narrate from ʿAlqamah, from ʿAbd Allāh, who said: When the verse {Those who believe and do not mix their belief with wrongdoing} [al-Anʿām 82] was revealed, the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Which of us does not mix his belief with wrongdoing?\"" Then the verse {Do not associate partners with Allah; indeed"," association is a great wrongdoing} was revealed.\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū al-Walīd. [Ṣaḥīh; agreed upon.]"""
"20749","(20743) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me, Abū ʿAmr — that is, Ibn Abī Jaʿfar — informed us, al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān narrated to us, Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah narrated to us, ʿAbd Allāh ibn Idrīs, Abū Muʿāwiyah, and Wakīʿ narrated from al-Aʿmash, from Ibrāhīm, from ʿAlqamah, from ʿAbd Allāh, who said: When the verse {Those who believe and do not mix their belief with wrongdoing} [al-Anʿām 82] was revealed, it weighed heavily upon the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ), and they said: \Which of us does not wrong himself?\"" The Prophet (ﷺ) said: \""It is not as you think. It is as Luqmān said to his son: {Do not associate partners with Allah; indeed"," association is a great wrongdoing} [Luqmān 13].\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah. [Ṣaḥīh; agreed upon.]"""
"20750","(20744) The Ustādh Abū Isḥāq Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm informed us, Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Shāfiʿī narrated to us, Abū Qilābah narrated to us, Abū ʀāṣim narrated to us, Zakariyyā ibn Isḥāq narrated from ʿAmr ibn Dīnār, from Ṭāwūs, from Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with them both), who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:\n\n\O Allah"," if You forgive"," forgive abundantly. And which servant of Yours is there without sin?\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīh]"""
"20751","(20745) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Sinān al-Qazzāz narrated to us: Abū ʢĀṣim informed us: Zakariyyāʾ ibn Isḥāq narrated from ʢAmr ibn Dīnār from ʢAṭāʾ from Ibn ʢAbbās regarding the verse {Those who avoid major sins and immoralities, except for minor lapses} [al-Najm 32], he said: \It is that a person commits an immoral act and then repents from it.\"" He said: And the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:\n\n\""O Allah"," if You forgive"," You forgive abundantly"," and which of Your servants has never sinned?\""\n\nAnd Rūḥ ibn ʢUbādah narrated it with the same meaning from Zakariyyāʾ ibn Isḥāq. [Ṣaḥīh. Previously referenced.]"""
"20752","(20746) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: ʢAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī informed us: Ibrāhīm ibn al-Ḥusayn narrated to us: Ādam ibn Abī Iyās narrated to us: Shuʿbah narrated to us: Manṣūr narrated from Mujāhid from Ibn ʢAbbās regarding this verse {except for minor lapses}, he said: \The one who is touched by a sin and then abandons it. Have you not heard the poet's words:\n\n'O Allah"," if You forgive"," You forgive abundantly"," and which of Your servants has never sinned?'\n\nThis is more apt.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"20753","(20747) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū ʿAbdillāh ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaydalānī narrated to us: Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm informed us: ʢAbd al-Razzāq informed us: Maʿmar narrated from Ibn Ṭāwūs from his father from Ibn ʢAbbās (may Allah be pleased with them both), who said: \I have not seen anything more apt regarding 'al-lamam' than what Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) said.\"" He said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \""Indeed"," Allah has decreed for the son of Ādam his share of adultery"," which he will inevitably attain. The adultery of the eyes is looking"," the adultery of the tongue is speech"," and the soul desires and yearns"," and the private parts either confirm it or deny it.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Maḥmūd ibn Ghaylān from ʢAbd al-Razzāq"," and Muslim narrated it from Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm. [Ṣaḥīh. Agreed upon.]"""
"20754","(20748) ʢAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʢAbdān informed us: Aḥmad ibn ʢUbayd narrated to us: Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq narrated to us: Sulaymān ibn Ḥarb narrated to us: Ḥammād ibn Salamah narrated from ʢAlī ibn Zayd from Yūsuf ibn Mihrān from Ibn ʢAbbās (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \There is no servant except that he has committed a sin or intended to commit a sin"," except Yaḥyā ibn Zakariyyā"," for he neither sinned nor intended to commit a sin.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"20755","(20749) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Isḥāq informed us: Muḥammad ibn Ghālib narrated to us: ʢAffān and Abū Salamah both said: Ḥammād ibn Salamah narrated to us from Ḥabīb ibn al-Shahīd, Yūnus ibn ʢUbayd, and Ḥumayd from al-Ḥasan from the Prophet (ﷺ).\n\nAnd ʢAlī ibn Zayd narrated from Yūsuf ibn Mihrān from Ibn ʢAbbās (may Allah be pleased with them both) from the Prophet (ﷺ), who said: \There is no human being…\"" and he mentioned its meaning.\n\nAl-Shāfiʿī (may Allah have mercy on him) said: \""If the predominant and apparent state of a person is obedience and manliness"," his testimony is accepted. And if the predominant and apparent state of a person is disobedience and contrary to manliness"," his testimony is rejected.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"20756","(20750) The Shaykh said: The explanation of this is in what Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: I heard Abū al-Walīd al-Faqīh say: I heard Abū al-ʿAbbās ibn Surayj say, when he was asked about the description of ʢadālah (integrity), he said: \He should be free"," Muslim"," of sound mind"," and sane"," not one who commits major sins"," nor one who persists upon minor sins"," and he should not abandon manliness in most customary matters.\""\n\nThe Shaykh said: As for the evidence regarding the conditions of Islam"," freedom"," puberty"," and sound mind"," these have already been established. [Ṣaḥīh]"""
"20757","(20751) The Shaykh said: As for the evidence regarding what comes after that, it is in what Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Fūrak informed us: ʢAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us: Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb narrated to us: Abū Dāwūd narrated to us: Shuʿbah narrated from ʢUbaydullāh ibn Abī Bakr from Anas: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was asked about the major sins, and he said: \Associating partners with Allah"," disobedience to parents"," killing a soul"," and false testimony.\"" Or he said: \""And false speech.\"" Both al-Bukhārī and Muslim narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from the ḥadīth of Shuʿbah. [Ṣaḥīh. Agreed upon.]"""
"20758","(20752) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: ʢAbbās ibn Muḥammad narrated to us: ʢAbbās ibn al-Faḍl al-Azraq narrated to us: Ḥarb ibn Shaddād narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Abī Kathīr narrated from ʢAbd al-Ḥamīd ibn Sinān from ʢUbayd ibn ʢUmayr — my father narrated to me, saying: \I was with the Prophet (ﷺ) during the Farewell Pilgrimage"," and I heard him say: 'Indeed"," the allies of Allah are those who pray. And indeed"," whoever performs the obligatory prayer"," considering it a right incumbent upon him by Allah"," and pays the obligatory zakah"," and fasts Ramaḍān"," and avoids the major sins' — a man said: 'O Messenger of Allah"," what are the major sins?' He said: 'The major sins are nine: the greatest of them is associating partners with Allah"," killing a believer"," consuming ribā"," consuming the wealth of the orphan"," slandering a chaste woman"," fleeing from the battlefield"," disobedience to parents"," sorcery"," and declaring the Sacred House (al-Bayt al-Ḥarām) lawful. Whoever meets Allah free from these will be with me in a Paradise whose gates are of gold.'\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"20759","(20753) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Salmān al-Faqīh narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn Ibrāhīm ibn Milḥān narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbdillāh informed me: Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar al-Muzakkī narrated to us: Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Būshanjī narrated to us. Both said: Yaḥyā ibn Bukayr narrated to us: al-Layth narrated from ʢUqayl from Ibn Shihāb from Abū Bakr ibn ʢAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Ḥārith ibn Hishām from Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \The fornicator does not fornicate while he is a believer; the one who drinks wine does not drink it while he is a believer; the thief does not steal while he is a believer; and the one does not seize a seized prize while people raise their eyes toward him during it while he is a believer.\""\n\nAnd ʢUqayl narrated from Ibn Shihāb from Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyab and Abū Salamah ibn ʢAbd al-Raḥmān from Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) from the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) a narration similar to this ḥadīth of Abū Bakr"," except for the mention of the seized prize.\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Saʿīd ibn ʢUfayr from al-Layth"," and Muslim narrated it from another chain from al-Layth. Abū Ṣāliḥ added in it from Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him): \""And repentance is still offered thereafter.\"" [Ṣaḥīh. Agreed upon.]"""
"20760","(20754) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: ʢAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Ḥasan al-Asadī informed us in Hamadhān: Ibrāhīm ibn al-Ḥusayn narrated to us: Ādam ibn Abī Iyās narrated to us: Shuʿbah narrated from al-Aʿmash from Dhakwān from Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said — and he mentioned it with its addition, except that he did not mention the seized prize. Abū ʿAbdillāh said: Al-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Ādam, and Muslim narrated it from the ḥadīth of Ibn Abī ʢAdī from Shuʿbah. [Ṣaḥīh. Agreed upon.]"
"20761","(20755) Abū al-Qāsim ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Muḥammad al-ʿAṭṭār, known as Ibn Shabbān, and Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad al-Razzāz reported to us in Baghdad, both saying: Abū ʿAmr ʿUthmān ibn Aḥmad al-Daqqāq narrated to us: Ayyūb ibn Sulaymān al-Ṣughdī narrated to us: Ādam ibn Abī Iyās narrated to us: Shuʿbah narrated to us, from Ismāʿīl ibn Abī Khālid and ʿAbd Allāh ibn Abī al-Safar, from al-Shaʿbī, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAmr ibn al-ʿĀṣ (may Allah be pleased with both of them), who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \The Muslim is the one from whose tongue and hand the Muslims are safe"," and the Muhājir (emigrant) is the one from whom Allah has forbidden [him to abstain].\""\n\nIt was narrated by al-Bukhārī in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Ādam. [Ṣaḥīḥ — agreed upon]"""
"20762","(20756) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us by dictation: Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Saʿdī informed us: Abū ʀāṣim informed us, from Ibn Jurayj: Abū al-Zubayr informed me that he heard Jābir (may Allah be pleased with him) saying: The Prophet (ﷺ) said: \The Muslim is the one from whose tongue and hand the Muslims are safe.\""\n\nIt was narrated by Muslim in his Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbd ibn Ḥumayd"," from Abū ʀāṣim. [Ṣaḥīḥ — Muslim 41]"""
"20763","(20757) Abū al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAbdān informed us: Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us: al-ʿAbbās ibn al-Faḍl and Abū Bakr al-Ṭayālisī — Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm — both said: Ibrāhīm narrated to us, they both said: Abū al-Walīd narrated to us: Isḥāq ibn Saʿīd, meaning Ibn ʿAmr ibn Saʿīd ibn al-ʿĀṣ, narrated to us: My father narrated to me, from his father, who said: I was with ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān (may Allah be pleased with him) when he called for water for ablution and said: I witnessed the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) saying: \There is no Muslim for whom a prescribed prayer is due"," and he performs its ablution well"," and its bowing and its prostration well"," except that it shall be an expiation for the sins that preceded it"," so long as he does not commit a major sin — and this applies throughout all of time.\""\n\nIt was narrated by Muslim in his Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbd ibn Ḥumayd and others"," from Abū al-Walīd. [Ṣaḥīḥ — agreed upon]"""
"20764","(20758) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: Abū Aḥmad ibn Abī al-Ḥasan informed me: Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us: ʿAlī ibn Ḥujr narrated to us: Ismāʿīl ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us, from al-ʿAlāʾ, from his father, from Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \The five prayers and one Jumuʿah to the next Jumuʿah are expiations for what is between them"," so long as the major sins are not committed.\""\n\nIt was narrated by Muslim in his Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAlī ibn Ḥujr and others. [Ṣaḥīḥ — Muslim 233]"""
"20765","(20759) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: Abū al-Walīd al-Faqīh informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān narrated to us: Hārūn ibn Saʿīd al-Aylī narrated to us: Ibn Wahb narrated to us: Abū Ṣakhr informed me that ʿUmar ibn Isḥāq, the freed slave of Zāʾidah, narrated to him, from his father, from Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) used to say: \The five prayers"," and one Jumuʿah to the next Jumuʿah"," and one Ramaḍān to the next Ramaḍān are expiations for what is between them"," provided the major sins are avoided.\""\n\nIt was narrated by Muslim in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Hārūn ibn Saʿīd and others. [Ṣaḥīḥ — as previously mentioned]"""
"20766","(20760) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥakam informed us: Ibn Wahb informed us: ʿAmr ibn al-Ḥārith informed me that Ibn Abī Hilāl narrated to him that Nuʿaym ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Mujmir narrated to him that Ṣuhayb, the freed slave of the ʿUṭwāriyyīn, narrated to him that he heard Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī and Abū Hurayrah narrating from the Prophet (ﷺ) that he ascended the pulpit and then said: \By the One in Whose Hand is my soul\"" — three times. Then he fell silent"," and every one of us began to weep out of distress over the oath of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ). Then he said: \""There is no servant who performs the five prayers"," fasts Ramaḍān"," and avoids the seven major sins"," except that the gates of Paradise shall be opened for him on the Day of Resurrection"," until they shall [open wide] with a clapping sound.\"" Then he recited: {If you avoid the major sins which you are forbidden"," We will expiate from you your misdeeds} [al-Nisāʾ 31]. In these reports and those similar to them regarding the severity concerning major sins and the expiation of minor sins"," there is confirmation for the position of those who differentiate between the two by rejecting the testimony of one who commits a major sin"," as opposed to one who commits a minor sin.\n\nAnd among the reports that indicate that when minor sins accumulate"," they bring their perpetrator to the level of one who commits a major sin — in terms of the rejection of testimony and otherwise — is what follows. [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"20767","(20761) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to me: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad ibn Mūsā al-Ṣaydalānī narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Ayyūb informed us: Abū al-Walīd narrated to us: Mahdī ibn Maymūn narrated to us: Ghaylān narrated from Anas, who said: \You are indeed performing deeds that are finer in your eyes than hair"," yet in the time of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) we would count them among the destructive sins.\""\n\nIt was narrated by al-Bukhārī in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū al-Walīd. [Ṣaḥīḥ — al-Bukhārī 6492]"""
"20768","(20762) Abū Bakr ibn Fūrak informed us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us: Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb narrated to us: Abū Dāwūd al-Ṭayālisī narrated to us: ʿImrān al-Qaṭṭān narrated to us, from Qatādah, from ʿAbd Rabbih, from Abī ʿIyāḍ, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Masʿūd (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Beware of the belittled sins"," for they accumulate upon a man until they destroy him.\"" And indeed"," the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) struck a parable for them"," like the parable of a people who encamped in a barren land. The people's feast was prepared"," and so a man would come with a twig"," and a man would come with a small stick"," until they gathered a great heap of it. Then they kindled a fire"," and it consumed everything that was thrown into it.\n\nAnd something similar has been narrated from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Yazīd"," from Ibn Masʿūd (may Allah be pleased with him)"," as his own statement"," not raised [to the Prophet]. [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"20769","(20763) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Bakkār ibn Qutaybah, the judge in Egypt, narrated to us: Ṣafwān ibn ʿĪsā informed us: Muḥammad ibn ʿAjlān narrated to us, from al-Qaʿqāʿ ibn Ḥakīm, from Abī Ṣāliḥ, from Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \When a believer commits a sin"," a black spot appears on his heart. If he repents"," desists"," and seeks forgiveness"," his heart is polished clean of it. But if it returns"," it spreads until his heart is sealed with it. And that is what Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic"," mentioned in His Book: {No! Rather"," rust has covered their hearts because of what they used to earn} [al-Muṭaffifīn 14].\""\n\nThe Shaykh said: It is as though these reports and those similar to them regarding severity and stern warning apply to one who persists in sins without seeking forgiveness from them"," and without resolving to abandon them. [Ḥasan]"""
"20770","(20764) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-Naḍr al-Faqīh narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Ayyūb informed us: Abū al-Walīd al-Ṭayālisī narrated to us: Hammām ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us. He said: I heard Isḥāq ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Abī Ṭalḥah saying: I heard ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī ʿAmrah saying: I heard Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) saying: \A servant committed a sin and said: 'O Lord"," I have committed a sin"," so forgive me.' His Lord said: 'My servant knows that he has a Lord who forgives sins and takes [punishment] for them.' So He forgave him. Then he remained for as long as Allah willed"," then he committed another sin — and perhaps he said: 'another sin' — and said: 'O Lord"," I have committed another sin"," so forgive me.' His Lord said: 'My servant knows that he has a Lord who forgives sins and takes [punishment] for them.' So He forgave him. Then he remained for as long as Allah willed"," then he committed another sin — and perhaps he said: 'another sin' — and said: 'O Lord"," I have committed another sin"," so forgive me.' His Lord said: 'My servant knows that he has a Lord who forgives sins and takes [punishment] for them.' Then His Lord said: 'I have forgiven My servant"," so let him do as he wishes.'\""\n\nIt was narrated by al-Bukhārī in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Rajāʾ"," from Hammām"," and it was narrated by Muslim from ʿAbd ibn Ḥumayd"," from Abū al-Walīd. [Ṣaḥīḥ — agreed upon]"""
"20771","(20765) Abū ʿAliyy al-Rūdhbārī informed us that Ibn Dāsah narrated to us that Abū Dāwūd narrated to us that al-Nufaylī narrated to us that Makhlad ibn Yazīd narrated to us that ʿUthmān ibn Wāqid al-ʿUmariyy narrated from Abū Nuṣayrah, from a freedman of the family of Abū Bakr al-Ṣiddīq, may Allah be pleased with him, from Abū Bakr al-Ṣiddīq, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: \He does not persist (in sin) who seeks forgiveness"," even if he returns to it seventy times in a day.\""\n\n[Weak]"""
"20772","(20766) Abū Bakr ibn Fūrak informed us that ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us that Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb narrated to us that Abū Dāwūd narrated to us that Shuʿbah narrated from ʿAmr ibn Murrah, who heard Abū ʿUbaydah narrating from Abū Mūsā al-Ashʿarī, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: \Indeed"," Allah extends His Hand by night so that the sinner of the day may repent"," and He extends His Hand by day so that the sinner of the night may repent"," until the sun rises from its place of setting.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Bundār"," from Abū Dāwūd. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 2759]"""
"20773","(20767) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us that Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us that al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn ʿAffān al-ʿĀmiriyy narrated to us that Abū Usāmah narrated from al-Aʿmash, from ʿUmārah ibn ʿUmayr, who said: I heard al-Ḥārith ibn Suwayd say: We came to ʿAbdullāh, meaning Ibn Masʿūd, and he narrated to us two hadiths — one from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, and the other from himself. He said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: \Allah rejoices more at the repentance of His believing servant than a man who is in a desolate"," barren"," and perilous land"," with his mount carrying his food and drink. He dismounted there and fell asleep"," with his mount beside his head. He awoke and found it gone. He went in search of it but could not find it"," until thirst overcame him. He said: 'By Allah"," I shall return to where my mount was and die there.' So he returned"," fell asleep"," and then awoke to find his mount beside his head"," with his food and drink upon it.\"" Then ʿAbdullāh said: \""Indeed"," the believer sees his sins as though he is sitting at the base of a mountain"," fearing it will collapse upon him. And the sinner sees his sins as though a fly passed over his nose"," and he waved his hand over his nose and it went away.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Isḥāq ibn Manṣūr"," from Abū Usāmah.\n\nThe Sheikh said: The \""rejoicing\"" attributed to Allah"," Mighty and Majestic"," in this hadith carries the meaning of pleasure and acceptance"," as in His Most High's words: \""Every party rejoices in what it has\"" (al-Mu'minūn 53)"," meaning they are pleased. This was stated by some of the people of knowledge"," and it is a sound interpretation. There are many narrations regarding repentance from sin"," but this is not the place for them.\n\nAs for the one who departs from the abode of this world having been tainted by sins and transgressions"," he is under the will of Allah"," the Most High. If He wills"," He forgives his sins — both minor and major — by His grace. And if He wills"," He punishes him for his sins by His justice"," and then removes him from his punishment into His Paradise by His mercy"," or by the intercession of the intercessors"," by His permission in that. There are many narrations concerning this"," but we point here only to what clarifies the matter"," by the facilitation of Allah"," the Most High."""
"20774","(20768) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us that Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn Ṣāliḥ ibn Hānī' narrated to us that al-Saryy ibn Khuzaymah narrated to us that ʿUmar ibn Ḥafṣ ibn Ghiyāth narrated to us that my father narrated to us that al-Aʿmash narrated to us that Zayd ibn Wahb narrated — and by Allah — that Abū Dharr narrated at al-Rabadhah, saying: I was walking with the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, in the rocky tract of Madīnah at nightfall, when Mount Uḥud came before us. He said: \O Abū Dharr"," I would not love that this Uḥud be turned into gold for me"," with a night passing over me while I have any dinars of it remaining — except a dinar I set aside for a debt — unless I were to say with it regarding the servants of Allah: 'such and such","' and he gestured with his hand.\"" Then he said: \""O Abū Dharr.\"" I said: \""At your service and at your command"," O Messenger of Allah.\"" He said: \""Indeed"," the most abundant in wealth are the least in reward — except one who says 'such and such' and 'such and such.'\"" Then he said to me: \""Stay where you are"," O Abū Dharr"," and do not move until I return to you.\"" He departed until he disappeared from me. I heard a voice and feared that something had befallen the Messenger of Allah"," peace and blessings be upon him. I wanted to go to him"," but then I remembered his words: 'Do not move.' So I stayed. The Prophet"," peace and blessings be upon him"," said: \""That was Jibrīl. He came to me and informed me that whoever of my Ummah dies without associating anything with Allah shall enter Paradise.\"" I said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," even if he committed adultery and even if he stole?\"" He said: \""Even if he committed adultery and even if he stole.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿUmar ibn Ḥafṣ ibn Ghiyāth"," and he also narrated it through other chains from al-Aʿmash. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Agreed upon]"""
"20775","(20769) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn Ṣāliḥ narrated to us that al-Saryy ibn Khuzaymah narrated to us that ʿUmar ibn Ḥafṣ narrated to us that my father narrated to us that al-Aʿmash narrated to me that Abū Ṣāliḥ narrated from Abū al-Dardā', similarly.\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿUmar ibn Ḥafṣ. Al-Bukhārī said: The hadith of Abū Ṣāliḥ from Abū al-Dardā' is mursal, and the ṣaḥīḥ narration is the hadith of Abū Dharr.\n\nAl-Bukhārī said: And al-Naḍr ibn Shumayl said, and he mentioned what (follows)."
"20776","(20770) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥusayn ibn ʿAbdillāh ibn Muḥammad al-Sadīriyy al-Bayhaqī informed us that Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-Khusrawjirdiyy narrated to us that Dāwūd ibn al-Ḥusayn al-Bayhaqī narrated to us that Ḥumayd ibn Zanjawayh narrated to us that al-Naḍr ibn Shumayl informed us that Shuʿbah narrated to us that Ḥabīb ibn Abī Thābit, Sulaymān al-Aʿmash, and ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Rufayʿ narrated. They said: We heard Zayd ibn Wahb narrating from Abū Dharr, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: \Indeed"," Jibrīl came to me and gave me glad tidings that whoever of my Ummah dies without associating anything with Allah shall enter Paradise.\"" He said: \""I said: 'Even if he committed adultery and even if he stole?'\"" He said: \""Even if he committed adultery and even if he stole.\""\n\nSulaymān said"," meaning to Zayd ibn Wahb: \""This hadith is only narrated from Abū al-Dardā'.\"" He said: \""As for me"," I heard it from Abū Dharr.\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Preceded above]"""
"20777","(20771) Abū Ṣāliḥ ibn Abī Ṭāhir al-ʿAnbariyy informed us that my grandfather Yaḥyā ibn Manṣūr al-Qāḍī narrated to us that Aḥmad ibn Salamah narrated to us that Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm informed us that Jarīr narrated from ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Rufayʿ, from Zayd ibn Wahb, from Abū Dharr, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: \I went out one night and there was the Messenger of Allah"," peace and blessings be upon him"," walking with no one with him.\"" He mentioned the hadith. He said: \""When he came"," I could not restrain myself and said: 'O Prophet of Allah"," may Allah make me your ransom"," who were you speaking to on the side of the rocky tract? I did not hear anyone replying to you anything.'\"" He said: \""That was Jibrīl. He appeared to me on the side of the rocky tract and said: 'Give glad tidings to your Ummah that whoever dies without associating anything with Allah shall enter Paradise.' I said: 'O Jibrīl"," even if he stole and even if he committed adultery?' He said: 'Yes"," even if he stole and even if he committed adultery.' I said: 'Even if he stole and even if he committed adultery?' He said: 'Even if he stole"," committed adultery"," and drank wine.'\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Qutaybah"," from Jarīr. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Preceded above]"""
"20778","(20772) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us that Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us that al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn ʿAffān al-ʿĀmiriyy narrated to us that ʿAbdullāh ibn Numayr narrated from al-Aʿmash, from al-Maʿrūr ibn Suwayd, from Abū Dharr, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: \Indeed"," I know the last of the people of Paradise to enter Paradise and the last of the people of the Fire to emerge from it. A man will be brought on the Day of Resurrection and it will be said: 'Present to him his minor sins and conceal his major sins.' So his minor sins will be presented to him"," and it will be said: 'On such-and-such a day you did such-and-such"," and on such-and-such a day you did such-and-such.' He will say: 'Yes","' and he will not be able to deny it"," while he fears that his major sins will be presented. Then it will be said to him: 'For every evil deed you shall have a good deed.' He will say: 'My Lord"," I have done things that I do not see here.'\"" He said: \""And I saw the Messenger of Allah"," peace and blessings be upon him"," laugh until his back teeth were visible.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh ibn Numayr"," from his father. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 190]"""
"20779","(20773) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me that Abū Bakr ibn ʿAbdillāh narrated to us that al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān narrated to us that Ḥarmalah ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us that Ibn Wahb narrated to me that Yūnus informed me from Ibn Shihāb that ʿAmr ibn Abī Sufyān narrated to him that Abū Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, said to Kaʿb al-Aḥbār: \The Messenger of Allah"," peace and blessings be upon him"," said: 'Every prophet has a supplication that is answered"," and every prophet hastened in his supplication. But I have withheld my supplication as intercession for my Ummah until the Day of Resurrection. It shall reach"," if Allah wills"," whoever of my Ummah dies without associating anything with Allah.'\"" Kaʿb said to Abū Hurayrah: \""Did you hear this from the Messenger of Allah"," peace and blessings be upon him?\"" Abū Hurayrah said: \""Yes.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Ḥarmalah ibn Yaḥyā"," and with this wording he also narrated it from the hadith of Abū Ṣāliḥ"," from Abū Hurayrah. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Agreed upon]"""
"20780","(20774) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq al-Faqīh informed us that Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq al-Qāḍī and Abū al-Muthannā al-ʿAnbariyy both said: Sulaymān ibn Ḥarb narrated to us that Bisṭām ibn Ḥurayth narrated from Ashʿath al-Ḥuddānī, from Anas, from the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, who said: \My intercession is for the people of major sins among my Ummah.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Agreed upon]"""
"20781","(20775) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣaghānī narrated to us: Rūḥ ibn ʿUbādah narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Muḥammad ʿAbdullāh ibn Yūsuf al-Aṣbahānī informed us: Abū Saʿīd ibn al-Aʿrābī narrated to us: al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad al-Zaʿfarānī narrated to us: Rūḥ ibn ʿUbādah narrated to us: Shuʿbah narrated from Qatādah, from Anas (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Every prophet had a supplication which he made for his nation"," and I have kept my supplication as intercession for my nation on the Day of Resurrection.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Zuhayr ibn Ḥarb and others"," from Rūḥ. [Ṣaḥīḥ — agreed upon.]"""
"20782","(20776) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr both informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣaghānī narrated to us: Rūḥ ibn ʿUbādah narrated to us: Ibn Jurayj narrated to me: Abū al-Zubayr informed me that he heard Jābir ibn ʿAbdillāh (may Allah be pleased with him) saying: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said — and he mentioned it with the same meaning.\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Abī Khalaf, from Rūḥ. [Ṣaḥīḥ — Muslim 201.]"
"20783","(20777) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbdullāh ibn Yūsuf al-Aṣbahānī narrated to us by dictation: Abū Saʿīd ibn al-Aʿrābī informed us: Saʿdān ibn Naṣr al-Mukharramī informed us: Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah narrated, saying: ʿAmr heard Jābir ibn ʿAbdillāh (may Allah be pleased with him) saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) with these two ears of mine saying: \Indeed"," Allah"," the Most High"," will bring forth a people from the Fire and admit them into Paradise.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah"," from Sufyān. [Ṣaḥīḥ — Muslim 191.]"""
"20784","(20778) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us: Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us: Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq narrated to us: ʿĀrim ibn al-Faḍl narrated to us: Ḥammād ibn Zayd narrated from ʿAmr ibn Dīnār, from Jābir ibn ʿAbdillāh, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \A people will be brought out of the Fire through intercession"," and they will grow as cucumbers grow.\""\n\nIt was said to ʿAmr: \""And what are al-thaʿārīr?\"" He said: \""Al-daghābīs (cucumbers).\"" Ḥammād said: \""And ʿAmr's mouth had fallen.\"" Ḥammād said: \""So I said to ʿAmr: 'O Abū Muḥammad"," did you hear Jābir ibn ʿAbdillāh say: I heard the Prophet (ﷺ) say: Indeed"," Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic"," will bring forth a people from the Fire through intercession?'\"" He said: \""Yes.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿĀrim. And Muslim narrated it from Abū al-Rabīʿ"," from Ḥammād. He also narrated it from the ḥadīth of Yazīd al-Faqīr"," from Jābir. And Jābir cited as evidence the words of Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic: {Perhaps your Lord will raise you to a station of praise and glory} [al-Isrāʾ 79]"," and said: \""It is the station of praise of Muḥammad"," by which Allah will bring forth whom He wills.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ — agreed upon.]"""
"20785","(20779) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us: Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Ghālib narrated to us: Mūsā ibn Ismāʿīl Abū Salamah narrated to us: Wuhaib ibn Khālid narrated from ʿAmr ibn Yaḥyā, from his father, from Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \When the people of Paradise enter Paradise and the people of the Fire enter the Fire"," Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic"," will say: 'Whoever has in his heart the weight of a mustard seed of good"," bring him out.' So they will be brought out"," having been reduced to cinders and turned to charcoal. They will be cast into a river called the River of Life (Nahr al-Ḥayāh). They will grow therein as a seed grows in the flood debris.\"" The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \""Do you not see that it grows yellow and twisted?\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Mūsā ibn Ismāʿīl. And both he and Muslim narrated it from the ḥadīth of Mālik and others"," from ʿAmr.\n\nThe Shaykh said: \""And in this are many reports"," and what we have mentioned"," along with the text of the Book regarding the forgiveness of all sins besides shirk for whom He wills"," is sufficient. And upon Allah is the reliance.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ — agreed upon.]"""
"20786","(20780) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbdullāh ibn Yūsuf al-Aṣbahānī narrated to us: Abū Saʿīd ibn al-Aʿrābī narrated to us: al-Ramādī, i.e. Aḥmad ibn Manṣūr, narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us: Maʿmar narrated from Abū Ḥāzim, from Ṭalḥah ibn Karīz al-Khuzāʿī, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Indeed"," Allah"," the Most High"," is Noble (Karīm); He loves the nobility of character and despises its baseness.\""\n\nThis is a mursal ḥadīth. And likewise al-Thawrī narrated it from Abū Ḥāzim. [Ṣaḥīḥ in other chains.]"""
"20787","(20781) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān informed us in Baghdād: Abū al-Ḥusayn Aḥmad ibn ʿUthmān ibn Yaḥyā al-Adamī narrated to us: ʿĪsā ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Ṭayālisī narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn Yūnus narrated to us: Fuḍayl ibn ʿIyāḍ narrated from Muḥammad ibn Thawr, from Maʿmar, from Abū Ḥāzim, from Sahl ibn Saʿd, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Indeed"," Allah is Noble (Karīm); He loves nobility and the loftiness of character"," and He despises its baseness.\""\n\nAnd likewise it was narrated from Abū Ghassān"," from Abū Ḥāzim. [Ṣaḥīḥ.]"""
"20788","(20782) Abū Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf al-Aṣbahānī informed us: Abū Saʿīd ibn al-Aʿrābī narrated to us: Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn ʿUbayd al-Marwarūdhī narrated to us: Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr narrated to us: ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Muḥammad narrated to me: Muḥammad ibn ʿAjlān narrated from al-Qaʿqāʿ ibn Ḥakīm, from Abū Ṣāliḥ, from Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \I was only sent to perfect the noble character traits.\""\n\nThus it was narrated from al-Dārawardī. [Ḥasan.]"""
"20789","(20783) Abū Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf informed us: Abū Saʿīd ibn al-Aʿrābī informed us: Abū Yaʿqūb Isḥāq ibn Jābir al-Qaṭṭān — reciting to him — narrated to you: Saʿīd ibn Abī Maryam narrated to us: Yaḥyā, i.e. Ibn Ayyūb, narrated to me: Ibn ʿAjlān informed me that al-Qaʿqāʿ ibn Ḥakīm informed him, from Abū Ṣāliḥ, from Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \The most complete of the believers in faith is the one among them with the best character.\""\n\nIbn ʿAjlān said: \""And the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: 'I was sent to perfect righteous character.'\"" [Ḥasan.]"""
"20790","(20784) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn ʿAffān narrated to us: ʿAbdullāh ibn Numayr narrated from al-Aʿmash, from Shaqīq, from Masrūq, who said: I heard ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr (may Allah be pleased with him) saying: \The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was not obscene (fāḥish) nor did he seek to be obscene (mutafahḥish). And he used to say: 'The best of you (akhyārakum) are those among you with the finest character.'\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh ibn Numayr"," from his father. And al-Bukhārī and Muslim both narrated it from other routes from al-Aʿmash. And some of them said in the ḥadīth: \""The best of you (khiyārakum).\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ — agreed upon.]"""
"20791","(20785) Abū al-Qāsim ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿUbayd Allāh al-Ḥurfī and Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Abī Ṭāhir al-Daqqāq in Baghdād narrated to us, saying: ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Zubayr al-Qurashī al-Kūfī narrated to us: al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn ʿAffān narrated to us: Zayd ibn al-Ḥubāb narrated to us from Muʿāwiya ibn Ṣāliḥ: ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Jubayr ibn Nufayr ibn Mālik al-Ḥaḍramī narrated to me from his father, from al-Nawwās ibn Samʿān al-Anṣārī, who said: \I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about righteousness (al-birr) and sin (al-ithm)"," and he said: 'Righteousness is good character (ḥusn al-khuluq)"," and sin is that which wavers in your soul and you dislike that people should become aware of it.'\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from the ḥadīth of ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Mahdī from Muʿāwiya ibn Ṣāliḥ.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 2553]"""
"20792","(20786) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Hārūn ibn Sulaymān al-Aṣbahānī narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Mahdī narrated to us from Shuʿba, from Qatāda, who said: \I heard ʿAbd Allāh ibn Abī ʿUtba say: I heard Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī (may Allah be pleased with him) say: 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was more bashful than a virgin in her seclusion. When he disliked something"," we would recognize it in his face.'\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Bundār from Ibn Mahdī. And Muslim narrated it from Zuhayr ibn Ḥarb and others from Ibn Mahdī.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Muttafaq ʿalayh]"""
"20793","(20787) Abū ʿAlī al-Ḥusayn ibn Muḥammad al-Rūdhabārī narrated to us: Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Maḥmawya narrated to us: Jaʿfar al-Qalānisī narrated to us: Ādam ibn Abī Iyās narrated to us: Shuʿba narrated to us from Manṣūr, who said: \I heard Ribʿī ibn Ḥirāsh narrate from Abū Masʿūd"," who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Indeed"," among the words of prophethood that people have attained is: If you feel no shame"," then do as you wish.'\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Ādam.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Al-Bukhārī 6120]"""
"20794","(20788) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: Abū al-Faḍl ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn Salama narrated to us: Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm and Hannād ibn al-Sarī both narrated to us: Abū Muʿāwiya narrated to us from Hishām ibn ʿUrwa, from his father, from ʿĀʾisha (may Allah be pleased with her), who said: \I never saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ strike a servant"," nor did he ever strike anything with his hand"," except when he fought in the cause of Allah. Nor was anything done to him that he would avenge for himself against the one who did it"," unless it was a matter pertaining to Allah's rights — then he would take vengeance for it. And he was never given a choice between two matters except that he would take the easier of the two"," so long as it was not a sin. If it was a sin"," he was the furthest of people from it.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū Kurayb from Abū Muʿāwiya.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 2328]"""
"20795","(20789) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān in Baghdād narrated to us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar ibn Durustawayh narrated to us: Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān narrated to us: Aṣbagh ibn Faraj and Yaḥyā ibn Sulaymān both narrated to us: Ibn Wahb narrated to us from ʿAmr ibn al-Ḥārith: Abū al-Naḍr narrated to me from Sulaymān ibn Yasār, from ʿĀʾisha (may Allah be pleased with her), who said: \I never saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ laugh fully so that I could see his uvula (lahawātih); he would only smile.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Yaḥyā ibn Sulaymān"," and Muslim narrated it from Hārūn ibn Maʿrūf and others from Ibn Wahb.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Muttafaq ʿalayh]"""
"20796","(20790) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl narrated to us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us: Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān narrated to us: Abū Nuʿaym narrated to us: ʿImrān ibn Zayd, Abū Yaḥyā al-Mulāʾī narrated to me: Zayd al-ʿAmmī narrated to me from Anas ibn Mālik, who said: \When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ shook hands with a man"," or a man shook hands with him"," he would not withdraw his hand until the man withdrew his. And when he turned his face toward someone"," he would not turn away from him until the man turned away. And he was never seen extending his knees before anyone sitting with him.\""\n\n[Ḍaʿīf]"""
"20797","(20791) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad al-Kaʿbī narrated to me: Muḥammad ibn Ayyūb narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Sinān narrated to us: Fulayḥ narrated to us: Hilāl, meaning Ibn ʿAlī, narrated to us from Anas, who said: \The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was not obscene"," nor did he speak obscenities deliberately"," nor was he one who cursed frequently or reviled others. He would say to one of us when reproaching him: 'What is the matter with him? May his forehead be dusted (taribat jabīnuh)!'\"" \n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn Sinān."""
"20798","(20792) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bushrān al-ʿAdl in Baghdād narrated to us: Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn Manṣūr al-Ramādī narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Razzāq narrated to us: Maʿmar narrated to us from Zayd ibn Aslam, who said: \ʿAbd al-Malik ibn Marwān used to send Umm al-Dardāʾ to his wives so that she would spend the night with them and they would ask her about things. One night he got up and called his servant"," but she was slow in coming"," so he cursed her. She said: 'Do not curse"," for Abū al-Dardāʾ narrated to me that he heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \""Indeed"," those who frequently curse will not be intercessors (shufaʿāʾ) nor witnesses (shuhadāʾ) on the Day of Resurrection.\""'\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Isḥāq ibn Rāhawayh from ʿAbd al-Razzāq.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 2598]"""
"20799","(20793) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf al-Aṣbahānī narrated among others, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān narrated to us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Wahb narrated to us: Sulaymān ibn Bilāl narrated to us from al-ʿAlāʾ ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, from his father, from Abū Hurayra (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \It is not befitting for a truthful person (ṣiddīq) to be one who frequently curses.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Hārūn al-Aylī from Ibn Wahb.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 2597]"""
"20800","(20794) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Ayyūb narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn Yūnus narrated to us.\n\n(And in another chain:) Abū Manṣūr Aḥmad ibn ʿAlī al-Dāmghānī, then al-Bayhaqī, narrated to us: Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī narrated to us: Abū Isḥāq Ibrāhīm ibn Sharīk narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūnus narrated to us: Abū Bakr ibn ʿAyyāsh narrated to us from al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAmr al-Fuqaymī, from Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Yazīd, from his father, from ʿAbd Allāh, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \The believer is not one who frequently defames (ṭaʿʿān)"," nor one who frequently curses (laʿʿān)"," nor one who speaks obscenities (fāḥish)"," nor one who utters vulgarities (badhīʾ).\""\n\nA similar narration has been reported from ʿAlqama from ʿAbd Allāh from the Prophet ﷺ.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"20801","(20795) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us that Aḥmad ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār narrated to us that Abū Muʿāwiya narrated from al-Aʿmash from Tamīm ibn Salamah from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Hilāl from Jarīr ibn ʿAbdillāh, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \Whoever is deprived of gentleness (rifq) is deprived of all good.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū Kurayb from Abū Muʿāwiya. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 2592]"""
"20802","(20796) Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Fūrak informed us that ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar al-Aṣbahānī narrated to us that Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb narrated to us that Abū Dāwūd narrated to us that Shuʿbah narrated from al-Miqdām ibn Shurayḥ from his father from ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her): She was upon a camel and began striking it, so the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \O ʿĀʾishah"," adopt gentleness"," for it is never present in anything except that it adorns it"," and it is never removed from anything except that it disfigures it.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ through two other chains from Shuʿbah. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muttafaq ʿalayh]"""
"20803","(20797) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us that al-ʿAbbās ibn Muḥammad al-Dūrī narrated to us that Hārūn ibn Maʿrūf narrated to us that ʿAbdullāh ibn Wahb narrated to me that Ḥaywah narrated to me that Ibn al-Hād narrated to me from Abū Bakr ibn ʿAmr ibn Ḥazm from ʿAmrah bint ʿAbd al-Raḥmān from ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her), the wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \O ʿĀʾishah"," indeed Allah is Gentle (Raʿīf) and He loves gentleness. He grants through gentleness what He does not grant through harshness"," and what He does not grant through anything else.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Ḥarmalah from Ibn Wahb. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muttafaq ʿalayh]"""
"20804","(20798) ʿAbdullāh ibn Yūsuf narrated to us that Abū Saʿīd ibn al-Aʿrābī narrated to us that Saʿdān ibn Naṣr narrated to us that Sufyān narrated from ʿAmr ibn Dīnār from Ibn Abī Mulaykah from Yaʿlā ibn Mamlak from Umm al-Dardāʾ, who narrated it from Abū al-Dardāʾ from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), who said: \Whoever is given his share of gentleness has been given his share of good"," and whoever is deprived of his share of gentleness has been deprived of his share of good.\"" And he said: \""The heaviest thing in the scale of the believer is good character. Indeed"," Allah detests the obscene and foul-mouthed.\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Muttafaq ʿalayh]"""
"20805","(20799) Abū Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf al-Aṣbahānī informed us that Abū Saʿīd ibn al-Aʿrābī narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Malik al-Daqīqī narrated to us that Yazīd ibn Hārūn informed us that Dāwūd ibn Abī Hind narrated from Makḥūl from Abū Thaʿlabah al-Khushanī that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \Indeed"," the most beloved of you to me and the closest of you to me are those with the best character. And indeed"," the most hated of you to me and the farthest of you from me are those with the worst character — the tharthārūn (those who talk excessively)"," the mutashaddiqūn (those who speak with affected eloquence)"," and the mutafayhiqūn (those who speak with pompous exaggeration).\""\n\n[Ḍaʿīf]"""
"20806","(20800) And Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us that Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Faḥḥām narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us that Abū Nuʿaym narrated to us that al-Barāʾ ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Qāṣṣ narrated to me that ʿAbdullāh ibn Shaqīq al-ʿUqaylī narrated from Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), who attributed it to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): \Shall I not inform you of the worst of this ummah? The tharthārūn (those who talk excessively)"," the mutashaddiqūn (those who speak with affected eloquence)"," and the mutafayhiqūn (those who speak with pompous exaggeration). Or shall I not inform you of the best of them? Those with the finest character.\""\n\n[Ḍaʿīf]"""
"20807","(20801) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bushrān al-ʿAdl in Baghdad informed us that Daʿlaj ibn Aḥmad narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr ibn al-Naḍr narrated to us that Aḥmad ibn Yūnus narrated to us that Zuhayr narrated to us that Qābūs ibn Abī Ẓabyān narrated from his father from Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with them both) from the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), who said: \Righteous guidance"," a righteous demeanor"," and moderation are one part of twenty-five parts of prophethood.\""\n\n[Ḍaʿīf]"""
"20808","(20802) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me that Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Jawharī narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn Bashshār and Muḥammad ibn al-Muthannā both said: Muḥammad ibn Abī ʿAdī narrated to us from Saʿīd from Qatādah, who informed me that more than one person who had met the delegation — and he mentioned Abū Naḍrah — narrated from Abū Saʿīd, who mentioned the story of the delegation of ʿAbd al-Qays. He said: The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) was brought the chief of ʿAbd al-Qays, and he said: \Indeed"," there are two qualities in you that Allah and His Messenger love: forbearance (ḥilm) and deliberateness (anāh).\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn al-Muthannā and Muḥammad ibn Bashshār. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 18]"""
"20809","(20803) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq al-Faqīh informed us that Muḥammad ibn Ghālib ibn Ḥarb narrated to us that ʿAffān ibn Muslim narrated to us that ʿAbd al-Wāḥid ibn Ziyād narrated to us that al-Aʿmash narrated from Mālik ibn al-Ḥārith from Muṣʿab ibn Saʿd from his father. Al-Aʿmash said: \And I do not know it except from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him)","\"" who said: \""Deliberateness (tuʾadah) in all things is good"," except in the deeds of the Hereafter.\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"20810","(20804) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh and Abū Muḥammad ʿAbdullāh ibn Yūsuf al-Aṣbahānī both said: Abū Bakr al-Qaṭṭān informed us that Aḥmad ibn Yūsuf al-Sulamī narrated to us that ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us that ʿAbdullāh ibn Saʿīd ibn Abī Hind narrated from his father from Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \Indeed"," Allah detests every obstinate tyrant"," one who raises his voice in the markets"," a corpse by night (i.e."," one who sleeps through the night)"," a donkey by day (i.e."," one engrossed in worldly affairs)"," knowledgeable of the world but ignorant of the Hereafter.\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"20811","(20805) Al-Ustādh Abū Bakr ibn Furak informed us that ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar informed us that Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb narrated to us that Abū Dāwūd narrated to us that Shuʿbah narrated from Maʿbad ibn Khālid from Ḥārithah ibn Wahb, who heard the Prophet (peace be upon him) say: \Shall I not inform you of the people of Paradise? Every weak one who is regarded as weak; if he were to swear an oath by Allah"," He would fulfil it.\"" And he said: \""The people of the Fire are every tyrant"," arrogant one who is insolent and conceited.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī and Muslim narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from the ḥadīth of Shuʿbah. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"20812","(20806) Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-ʿAlawī (may Allah have mercy on him) informed us that ʿUbaydullāh ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn al-Sharqī informed us that Abū al-Azhar narrated to us that Muḥāḍir narrated to us that Saʿd ibn Saʿīd al-Anṣārī narrated to me that ʿAmr ibn Abī ʿAmr narrated from Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) from the Prophet (peace be upon him) that he said: \Whoever is gentle"," easy-going"," and lenient"," Allah has forbidden him the Fire.\""\n\nIt was narrated by Sahl ibn ʿAmmār from Muḥāḍir"," and he said in it: from al-Muṭṭalib from Abū Hurayrah. [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"20813","(20807) ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us that Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd narrated to us that Ibn Abī Qumāsh narrated to us that Saʿdawayh narrated from Abī ʿUqayl from Ismāʿīl ibn Rāfiʿ from a son of Umm Salamah al-Makhzūmī from Umm Salamah, the wife of the Prophet (peace be upon him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: \The first thing my Lord"," the Mighty and Majestic"," forbade me of and enjoined upon me after the worship of idols and the drinking of wine was slandering and backbiting among men.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"20814","(20808) Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī in Naysābūr and Abū Manṣūr Aḥmad ibn ʿAlī al-Dāmaghānī in Bayhaq informed us, both saying: Abū Aḥmad ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAdī al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us that Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm ibn Ismāʿīl, Abū ʿImrān al-Ghazī in Ghazzah, in the year three hundred, narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn Abī al-Sarī al-ʿAsqalānī narrated to us that Bakr ibn Bishr al-Sulamī narrated to us that ʿAbd al-Ḥamīd ibn Sawwār narrated from Iyās ibn Muʿāwiyah ibn Qurrah al-Muzanī, who said: We were in the presence of ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz when modesty (ḥayāʾ) was mentioned before him, and they said: \Modesty is part of the religion.\"" ʿUmar said: \""Rather"," it is the entire religion.\"" Iyās said: My father narrated to me from my grandfather Qurrah"," who said: We were in the presence of the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) when modesty was mentioned before him"," and they said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," modesty is part of the religion.\"" The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: \""Rather"," it is the entire religion.\"" Then the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: \""Indeed"," modesty"," chasteness"," and the inability of the tongue—not of the heart—and righteous action are part of faith. They increase one's portion in the Hereafter and decrease it in this worldly life"," and their increase in the Hereafter is greater than their increase in this worldly life.\""\n\nIyās ibn Muʿāwiyah said: ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz commanded me"," so I dictated it to him"," and he wrote it down in his own hand. Then he led us in the Ẓuhr and ʿAṣr prayers while it was still in his sleeve"," and he did not put it down"," out of admiration for it. [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"20815","(20809) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbdullāh ibn Yūsuf informed us that Abū Saʿīd ibn al-Aʿrābī narrated to us that al-ʿAbbās al-Dūrī narrated to us that Abū Dāwūd Sulaymān ibn Muḥammad al-Mubārakī narrated to us that Abū Shihāb narrated from Sufyān al-Thawrī from al-Ḥajjāj ibn Farāfiṣah from Yaḥyā ibn Abī Kathīr from Abī Salamah ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān from Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: \The believer is noble and generous"," and the wicked person is treacherous and despicable.\""\n\nIt was likewise narrated from ʿĪsā ibn Yūnus from Sufyān"," and it was said: from Sufyān from al-Ḥajjāj from a man from Abī Salamah from Abū Hurayrah.\n\nIt was also narrated by Bishr ibn Rāfiʿ from Yaḥyā ibn Abī Kathīr from Abī Salamah ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān from Abū Hurayrah"," likewise"," as a marfūʿ narration. [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"20816","(20810) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Bakr al-Qāḍī both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās, al-Aṣamm, narrated to us that al-ʿAbbās ibn Muḥammad al-Dūrī narrated to us that Yūnus ibn Muḥammad al-Muʾaddib narrated to us that Muslim ibn Khālid al-Zanjī narrated from al-ʿAlāʾ ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān from his father from Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: \The nobility of a person is his religion"," his manliness (murūʾah) is his intellect"," and his lineage (ḥasab) is his character.\""\n\nThis is known through Muslim ibn Khālid al-Zanjī"," and it has been narrated from two other weak chains from Abū Hurayrah. [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"20817","(20811) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Ṣādiq Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad al-ʿAṭṭār both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us that Mūsā ibn Dāwūd narrated to us that Shuʿbah narrated from ʿAbdullāh ibn Abī al-Safar, who said: I heard al-Shaʿbī say: I heard Ziyād ibn Ḥudayr say: I heard ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him) say: \The lineage (ḥasab) of a person is his religion"," his manliness (murūʾah) is his character"," and his origin is his intellect.\""\n\nThis mawqūf narration has a sound (ṣaḥīḥ) chain of transmission. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"20818","(20812) Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī informed us, saying: I heard Abū Manṣūr Muḥammad ibn al-Qāsim ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān say: I heard Ibrāhīm ibn Maḥmūd say: I heard al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān say: I heard al-Shāfiʿī say: \Manliness (murūʾah) consists of four pillars: good character"," generosity"," humility"," and devotion to worship.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ — from al-Shāfiʿī]"""
"20819","(20813) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū Bakr ibn Dāwūd al-Zāhid narrated to us that al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān narrated to me that al-Muntajiʿ ibn Muṣʿab narrated to us that Ghundar narrated from Shuʿbah from Ḥabīb al-Tamīmī that Muʿāwiyah asked a man from ʿAbd al-Qays: \What do you consider manliness (murūʾah) to be among you?\"" He said: \""Skill in earning a livelihood and chasteness (ʿiffah).\""\n\nAnd it has been narrated from Abī Sawwār"," who said: It was said to Muʿāwiyah: \""What is manliness (murūʾah)?\"" He said: \""Chasteness in religion and setting right one's livelihood.\"" [Ḥasan]"""
"20820","(20814) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, saying: I heard Abū Bakr ibn al-Muʾammal say: I heard Abū ʿAbdullāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb al-Fārisī say: I read in some books that Yazīd ibn Muʿāwiyah asked al-Aḥnaf ibn Qays about manliness (murūʾah), and al-Aḥnaf said: \Manliness is piety (taqwā) and forbearance.\"" Then al-Aḥnaf was silent for a while and then said:\n\n\""And if the one of beautiful countenance does not act beautifully","\nThen his beauty is of no benefit.\nThe goodness of a young man's character\nIs nothing but his piety and his forbearance.\""\n\nYazīd said: \""You have spoken well"," O Abū Baḥr! The well has met its match.\"" Al-Aḥnaf said: \""Why did you not say: 'The meaning has met its explanation'?\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"20821","(20815) Abū Muḥammad al-Mu'ammalī informed us; Abū ʿUthmān al-Baṣrī narrated to us; Abū Aḥmad al-Farrāʾ narrated to us; ʿAlī ibn ʿUthmān narrated from al-Aʿmash, who said: Salm ibn Qutaybah said: \By al-Dunyā is meant well-being; by al-Shabāb is meant health; and by al-Murūʾah is patience with men.\"" He (the narrator) said: \""I asked: 'What is patience with men?' He described it as al-Mudārah (gentleness and forbearance).\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"20822","(20816) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān informed us in Baghdād; Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār narrated to us; Mushrif ibn Saʿīd narrated to us; Isḥāq ibn Muḥammad narrated to us; Sufyān ibn Ḥusayn said: \I said to Iyās ibn Muʿāwiyah: 'What is al-Murūʾah?' He said: 'In your town"," where you are known"," it is al-Taqwā (God-consciousness); but where you are not known"," it is clothing (al-Libās).'\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"20823","(20817) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn ʿAffān narrated to us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Numayr narrated from al-Aʿmash, from Shaqīq, who said: ʿAbd Allāh, meaning Ibn Masʿūd (raḍiya Allāhu ʿanhu), said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Upon you is truthfulness"," for truthfulness leads to al-Birr (righteousness)"," and al-Birr leads to Paradise. A man continues to speak the truth until he is recorded in the presence of Allah as a Ṣiddīq (truthful one). And beware of lying"," for lying leads to al-Fujūr (wickedness)"," and al-Fujūr leads to the Fire. A man continues to lie until he is recorded in the presence of Allah as a Kadh-dhāb (liar).\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muttafaq ʿalayh]"""
"20824","(20818) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us; Abū Muʿāwiyah narrated from al-Aʿmash, and he mentioned it with his isnād, except that he said: \A man continues to speak the truth and to seek the truth until he is recorded in the presence of Allah as a Ṣiddīq.\"" And he said at its end: \""A man continues to lie and to seek falsehood until he is recorded in the presence of Allah as a Kadh-dhāb.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā"," and both he and al-Bukhārī reported it from the ḥadīth of Manṣūr from Abū Wāʾil Shaqīq. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"20825","(20819) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us by dictation; Muḥammad ibn Nuʿaym narrated to us; Qutaybah ibn Saʿīd narrated to us; Ismāʿīl ibn Jaʿfar narrated from Abū Suhayl Nāfiʿ ibn Mālik ibn Abī ʿĀmir, from his father, from Abū Hurayrah (raḍiya Allāhu ʿanhu), that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \The signs of the munāfiq (hypocrite) are three: when he speaks"," he lies; when he makes a promise"," he breaks it; and when he is entrusted with something"," he betrays it.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī and Muslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Qutaybah. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muttafaq ʿalayh]"""
"20826","(20820) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; ʿAlī ibn ʿĪsā narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr al-Ḥarashī and Mūsā ibn Muḥammad al-Dhuhlī narrated; they said: Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us. He said: I read to Mālik from Abū al-Zinād, from al-Aʿraj, from Abū Hurayrah (raḍiya Allāhu ʿanhu), that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Indeed"," among the worst of people is the dhū al-wajhayn (the two-faced one)"," who comes to these people with one face and to those people with another face.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā"," and al-Bukhārī reported it from the ḥadīth of Abū Ṣāliḥ from Abū Hurayrah (raḍiya Allāhu ʿanhu). [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muttafaq ʿalayh]"""
"20827","(20821) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Burshān al-ʿAdl informed us in Baghdād; Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn Manṣūr al-Ramādī narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Razzāq narrated to us; Maʿmar narrated from Ayyūb, from Ibn Abī Mulaykah, that ʿĀʾishah (raḍiya Allāhu ʿanhā) said: \There was no character more hateful to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) than lying. A man would lie in the presence of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"," and it would remain in his (the Prophet's) heart against him until he came to know that the man had repented for it.\""\n\nAbū Bakr said: \""In our copy from ʿAbd al-Razzāq"," this ḥadīth was from Ibn Abī Mulaykah or someone else.\"" Then ʿAbd al-Razzāq narrated to us without doubt"," and he said: \""From Ibn Abī Mulaykah","\"" and he did not mention \""or someone else.\""\n\nThe Shaykh said: \""It has a shāhid (corroborating witness) from Ibn Abī Mulaykah.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"20828","(20822) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Bakr al-Qāḍī informed us; they said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Abū Zurʿah al-Dimashqī narrated to us; Maḥmūd ibn Khālid narrated to us; Marwān narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Muslim narrated to us; Ayyūb al-Sakhtiyānī narrated from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Abī Mulaykah, from ʿĀʾishah (raḍiya Allāhu ʿanhā), who said: \There was nothing more hateful to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) than lying. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) never experienced lying from anyone and then turned back to him until he knew from him (that he had offered) repentance.\""\n\nOur Shaykh also reported it in what was not dictated from al-Mustadrak from al-Aṣamm"," from Ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥakam"," from Ibn Wahb"," from Muḥammad ibn Muslim"," from Ayyūb al-Sakhtiyānī"," from Muḥammad ibn Sīrīn"," from ʿĀʾishah (raḍiya Allāhu ʿanhā).\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Preceded before it]"""
"20829","(20823) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Burshān informed us; Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn Manṣūr narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Razzāq narrated to us; Maʿmar narrated from Mūsā ibn Abī Shaybah: \The Prophet (ﷺ) invalidated the testimony of a man due to a lie he told.\"" Thus it is in my copy: Mūsā ibn Abī Shaybah. [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"20830","(20824) Abū Saʿd al-Mālinī informed us; Abū Aḥmad ibn ʿAdī narrated to us; Hamzah al-Kātib narrated to us; Nuʿaym ibn Ḥammād narrated to us; Ibn al-Mubārak narrated from Maʿmar, from Mūsā ibn Shaybah: \The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) impugned the testimony of a man due to a lie he told.\"" And this is more correct"," and it is mursal. [Ḍaʿīf. Preceded before it]"""
"20831","(20825) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us that al-ʿAbbās ibn Muḥammad al-Dūrī narrated to us that Abū ʾĀṣim informed us that Bahz ibn Ḥakīm narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us that Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-Qaṭṭān narrated to us that Aḥmad ibn Yūsuf al-Sulamī narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf said: Sufyān mentioned from Bahz ibn Ḥakīm, from his father, from his grandfather, from the Prophet ﷺ, who said: \Woe to the one who speaks and lies in order to make people laugh. Woe to him! Woe to him!\"" [Ḥasan]"""
"20832","(20826) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzakkī informed us that Abū ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Wahhāb informed us that Jaʿfar ibn ʿAwn informed us that Ismāʿīl — he is Ibn Abī Khālid — narrated from Qays ibn Abī Ḥāzim, who said: I heard Abū Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) say: \Beware of lying"," for lying is entirely incompatible with faith.\""\n\nThis is a mawqūf narration"," and it is authentic"," and it has also been narrated as marfūʿ. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"20833","(20827) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Muqriʾ informed us that al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us that Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb al-Qāḍī narrated to us that ʿAmr ibn Marzūq narrated to us that Shuʿbah narrated from Salamah ibn Kuhayl from Muṣʿab ibn Saʿd, from his father, who said: \A Muslim may be disposed to every trait except treachery and lying.\""\n\nThis is a mawqūf narration"," and it is authentic"," and it has also been narrated as marfūʿ. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"20834","(20828) Abū Saʿd al-Mālinī informed us that Abū Aḥmad ibn ʿAdī al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us that ʿAbd Allāh ibn Ḥafṣ al-Wakīl narrated to us that Dāwūd ibn Rushayd narrated to us that ʿAlī ibn Hāshim narrated from al-Aʿmash, from Abī Isḥāq, from Muṣʿab ibn Saʿd, from his father, from the Prophet ﷺ, who said: \The believer may be disposed to everything except treachery and lying.\"" [Munkar]"""
"20835","(20829) Abū ʿAmr al-Adīb informed us that Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī narrated to us that Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb al-Qāḍī narrated to us that ʿAmr ibn Marzūq informed us that Shuʿbah narrated from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Abī Bakr ibn Anas, from Anas (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Prophet ﷺ, who said: \The greatest of major sins are: associating partners with Allah"," taking a life unjustly"," disobedience to parents"," and false speech\"" — or he said"," \""false testimony.\""\n\nBoth al-Bukhārī and Muslim recorded it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from the ḥadīth of Shuʿbah"," and al-Bukhārī narrated it from ʿAmr ibn Marzūq. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"20836","(20830) Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith both informed us that ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us that Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn Sulaymān al-Nuʿmānī narrated to us that ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAbd al-Ṣamad ibn Abī Khidāsh narrated to us that ʿĪsā ibn Yūnus narrated to us that ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Abī Ḥumayd narrated from Abī al-Malīḥ al-Hudhalī, who said: ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb wrote to Abū Mūsā al-Ashʿarī (may Allah be pleased with them both), and he mentioned the ḥadīth, in which he said: \The Muslims are upright witnesses against one another"," except one who has been flogged in a prescribed punishment"," or one who has been tested in giving false testimony"," or one who is suspected due to loyalty or kinship.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Previously cited under no. 20283]"""
"20837","(20831) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān al-ʿAdl in Baghdad informed us that Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār narrated to us that Aḥmad ibn Manṣūr narrated to us that ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us that Maʿmar narrated from al-Zuhrī, from Ḥumayd ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, from his mother Umm Kulthum bint ʿUqbah — and she was among the first female Emigrants (al-Muhājirāt al-Ūlā) — who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \He is not a liar who reconciles between people and speaks good or conveys good.\""\n\nMuslim recorded it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from the ḥadīth of Ibn ʿUlayyah from Maʿmar. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Agreed upon]"""
"20838","(20832) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Aḥmad ibn Jaʿfar al-Qaṭīʿī narrated to us that ʿAbd Allāh ibn Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal narrated to me that my father narrated to us that Yaʿqūb ibn Ibrāhīm ibn Saʿd narrated to us that my father narrated from Ṣāliḥ ibn Kaysān narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn Muslim ibn ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Shihāb informed us that Ḥumayd ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAwf informed him that his mother, Umm Kulthum bint ʿUqbah, informed him that she heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \He is not a liar who reconciles between people"," conveying good or speaking good.\""\n\nAnd she said: \""I did not hear him permit anything of what people say except in three cases: in war"," in reconciling between people"," and in a man's speaking to his wife and a woman's speaking to her husband.\"" She said: Umm Kulthum bint ʿUqbah was among the female Emigrants who gave their pledge of allegiance to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn ʿAbd Allāh from Ibrāhīm ibn Saʿd in an abridged form"," and Muslim narrated it from ʿAmr al-Nāqid from Yaʿqūb in its entirety. And he recorded it from the ḥadīth of Yūnus from Ibn Shihāb up to his words: \""and conveys good.\"" Then he attributed the remainder to the words of Ibn Shihāb. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Previously cited]"""
"20839","(20833) ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us that Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us that Ibn Milḥān narrated to us that Yaḥyā ibn Bukayr narrated to us that al-Layth narrated from Ibn al-Hād, from ʿAbd al-Wahhāb, from Ibn Shihāb, from Ḥumayd ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, from his mother Umm Kulthum bint ʿUqbah, who said: \I did not hear the Messenger of Allah ﷺ permit anything of lying except in three cases. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say: 'I do not regard him as a liar: a man who reconciles between people"," speaking words intending nothing but reconciliation; a man who speaks words during war; and a man who speaks to his wife"," and a woman who speaks to her husband.'\""\n\nAnd similarly Nāfiʿ ibn Yazīd and others narrated it from Ibn al-Hād"," from ʿAbd al-Wahhāb"," from Abī Bakr. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Previously cited]"""
"20840","(20834) Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-ʿAlawī informed orally that Abū Ḥāmid ibn al-Sharqī narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn ʿUqayl and Aḥmad ibn Ḥafṣ both narrated to us that Ḥafṣ ibn ʿAbd Allāh narrated to me that Ibrāhīm ibn Ṭahmān narrated from Mūsā ibn ʿUqbah. Abū al-Zinād informed me from al-Aʿraj, from Abū Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Indeed"," Ibrāhīm"," the Khalīl of al-Raḥmān"," never lied except in three instances: his statement regarding their gods: 'Rather"," their great one did this' (Q 21:63); his statement when they invited him to argue about their gods: 'Indeed"," I am sick' (Q 37:89); and his statement to Sārah: 'She is my sister.'\""\n\nThis is a well-established ḥadīth. Both al-Bukhārī and Muslim recorded it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from the ḥadīth of Ibn Sīrīn from Abū Hurayrah.\n\nHis statement \""Rather"," their great one did this\"" was uttered by way of explanation and clarification"," meaning that their gods are incapable of any action. His statement \""Indeed"," I am sick\"" carries the meaning that he would soon fall ill. And his statement to Sārah \""She is my sister\"" was in the sense of the bond of faith (ukhuwwat al-Islām). And Allah knows best. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Previously cited]"""
"20841","(20835) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿUmar al-Muqriʾ ibn al-Ḥammāmī informed us in Baghdad — may Allah have mercy on him — that Aḥmad ibn Salmān informed us, that Ibrāhīm ibn Isḥāq narrated to us, that Muḥammad ibn Sinān al-ʿAwqī narrated to us, that Ibrāhīm ibn Ṭahmān narrated from Budayl, from ʿAbd al-Karīm, from ʿAbdullāh ibn Shaqīq, from his father, from ʿAbdullāh ibn Abī al-Ḥamsāʾ, who said: \I made a transaction with the Prophet ﷺ"," and there remained a balance due upon me. I promised him that I would bring it to him at that place. I forgot that day and the following day. Then I came to him on the third day"," and he was at that place. He said to me: 'O young man"," you have indeed caused me hardship. I have been waiting here for three days for you.'\""\n\nThus he narrated it from ʿAbdullāh ibn Shaqīq from his father. [Weak]"""
"20842","(20836) And Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ, and Abū Bakr al-Qāḍī, and Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, that Abū Umayyah narrated to us, that Muḥammad ibn Sinān al-Baṣrī narrated to us, that Ibrāhīm ibn Ṭahmān narrated from Budayl ibn Mayṣarah, from ʿAbd al-Karīm, from ʿAbdullāh ibn Shaqīq, from his father, from ʿAbdullāh ibn Abī al-Ḥamsāʾ, who said: \I transacted with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with a sale before he was sent as a Prophet.\"" Then he mentioned this hadith with its meaning. [Weak. Previously cited.]"""
"20843","(20837) And Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us, that Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us, that Abū Dāwūd narrated to us, that Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā al-Naysābūrī narrated to us, that Muḥammad ibn Sinān narrated to us, and he mentioned this hadith.\n\nAbū Dāwūd said: Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā said: \According to us"," this is from ʿAbd al-Karīm ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn Shaqīq.\""\n\nThe Shaykh Aḥmad — may Allah have mercy on him — said: Ibrāhīm ibn Hānʾ narrated it from Muḥammad ibn Sinān"," and he said: \""from ʿAbdullāh ibn Abī al-Ḥamsāʾ\"" or \""al-Ḥamsāʾ\"" with doubt. And Muʿādh ibn Hānʾ narrated it from Ibrāhīm ibn Ṭahmān"," and he did not express doubt regarding ʿAbdullāh ibn Abī al-Ḥamsāʾ. [Weak]"""
"20844","(20838) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us, that Muḥammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, that Abū Dāwūd narrated to us, that Ibn al-Muthannā narrated to us, that Abū ʿĀmir narrated to us, that Ibrāhīm ibn Ṭahmān narrated from ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd al-Aʿlā, from Abī al-Nuʿmān, from Abī Waqqāṣ, from Zayd ibn Arqam, from the Prophet ﷺ, who said: \When a man promises his brother something and intends to fulfill it but does not fulfill it and does not come at the appointed time"," there is no sin upon him.\"" [Weak]"""
"20845","(20839) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad informed us, that Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us, that ʿAbbās al-Asfaṭī narrated to us, that Abū al-Walīd narrated to us, that Layth ibn Saʿd narrated from Muḥammad ibn ʿAjlān, from a freed slave of ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿĀmir, from ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿĀmir, who said: \The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to our house while I was a small boy. I went off to play. My mother said to me: 'O ʿAbdullāh"," come"," I will give you something.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'What did you intend to give him?' She said: 'I intended to give him dates.' He said: 'If you had not done so"," a lie would have been recorded against you.'\"" [Weak]"""
"20846","(20840) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān informed us, that ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us, that Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān narrated to us, that Saʿīd ibn Abī Maryam informed us, that Yaḥyā ibn Ayyūb informed me, that Muḥammad ibn ʿAjlān narrated from Ziyād, the freed slave of ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿĀmir ibn Rabīʿah, from ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿĀmir ibn Rabīʿah, who heard him say: \The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to my mother while I was a boy. I turned to go outside"," and my mother called out to me: 'O ʿAbdullāh"," come here!' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to her: 'What will you give him?' She said: 'I will give him dates.' He said: 'If you had not done so"," a lie would have been recorded against you.'\"" [Weak. Previously cited.]"""
"20847","(20841) ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn Bishrān informed us, that Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār narrated to us, that Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Malik narrated to us, that Yazīd — meaning Ibn Hārūn — informed us, that Sulaymān — meaning al-Taymī — narrated from Abī ʿUthmān, that ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb — may Allah be pleased with him — said: \In equivocal speech (al-maʿārīḍ) there is that which suffices a man in place of lying.\"" [Sound]"""
"20848","(20842) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, that Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, that Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib informed us, that ʿAbd al-Wahhāb ibn ʿAṭāʾ informed us, that Saʿīd — meaning Ibn Abī ʿArūbah — narrated from Qatādah, from Muṭarrif, from ʿImrān ibn al-Ḥuṣayn, that he said: \Indeed"," in equivocal speech (al-maʿārīḍ) there is a means of keeping away from lying.\""\n\nThis is the sound version"," as a mawqūf narration. [Sound]"""
"20849","(20843) And Abū al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAbdān informed us, that Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd narrated to us, that Muḥammad ibn al-Faḍl ibn Jābir narrated to us, that Abū Ibrāhīm narrated to us, that Dāwūd ibn al-Zibriqān narrated from Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿArūbah, from Qatādah, from Zurārah ibn Awfā, from ʿImrān ibn Ḥuṣayn — may Allah be pleased with him — who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Indeed"," in equivocal speech (al-maʿārīḍ) there is a means of keeping away from lying.\"" [Denounced (Munkar)]"""
"20850","(20844) And Abū Saʿd al-Mālinī informed us, that Abū Aḥmad ibn ʿAdī al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, that Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn al-Jaʿd al-Washshāʾ narrated to us, that Abū Ibrāhīm al-Tarjumānī narrated to us, and he mentioned it with its chain, the same. Dāwūd ibn al-Zibriqān is alone in raising it (as a marfūʿ narration).\n\nAnd it has been narrated through another weak chain from ʿAlī — may Allah be pleased with him — as a marfūʿ narration. [Denounced (Munkar)]"
"20851","(20845) Abū ʿAbd al-Rahmān al-Sulamī informed us that Abū al-Hasan al-Kārizī informed us that ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz said that Abū ʿUbayd said: \Al-Maʿārīd (equivocation/tawriyah) is that a man intends to speak words which"," if stated explicitly"," would be a lie"," so he employs equivocation through other words that agree with those words in wording but differ in meaning"," such that the listener supposes he intended the former. His statement 'mandūhah' means 'broadly' and 'with ample scope.'\""\n\nThe Sheikh said: \""This is only permissible when it is used to repel harm and does not cause harm to another. As for that which harms another"," it is not permissible.\""\n\n[Sound]"""
"20852","(20846) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us that Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us that Abū Dāwūd narrated to us that Haywah ibn Shurayh al-Hadramī narrated to us that Baqiyyah ibn al-Walīd narrated to us from Ḍubārah ibn Mālik al-Hadramī from his father, from ʿAbd al-Rahmān ibn Jubayr ibn Nufayr, from his father, from Sufyān ibn Usayd al-Hadramī, who said: \I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: 'It is a great betrayal that you speak to your brother words in which he believes you to be truthful"," while you are lying to him.'\""\n\n[Weak]"""
"20853","(20847) ʿAlī ibn Ahmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us that Ahmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Saffār informed us that ʿUbayd ibn Sharīk narrated to us that ʿAbd al-Wahhāb, namely Ibn Najdah, narrated to us that Baqiyyah ibn al-Walīd narrated to me that Abū Sharīh Ḍubārah ibn Mālik al-Hadramī informed him that he heard his father narrate from ʿAbd al-Rahmān ibn Jubayr ibn Nufayr that his father narrated to him from Sufyān ibn Usayd al-Hadramī that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say — and he mentioned it.\n\n[Weak. Previously mentioned]"
"20854","(20848) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us that Abū Bakr Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Mahmūyah narrated to us that Jaʿfar ibn Muhammad al-Qalānisī narrated to us that Ādam ibn Abī Iyās narrated to us that Shuʿbah narrated to us that Thābit al-Bunānī narrated to us from Anas ibn Mālik, who said: \The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) was on a journey"," and his wives were in front of him"," and there was a camel-driver or a herdsman. In another version"," it is said: 'So the camel-driver sang a song"," and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \""Be gentle"," O Anjashah! Take care with the fragile vessels.\""'\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in the Sahīh from Ādam"," and Muslim narrated it from another chain.\n\n[Sound. Agreed upon]"""
"20855","(20849) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Hāfiz narrated to us that Abū al-ʿAbbās Muhammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us that Jaʿfar ibn Muhammad ibn Shākir narrated to us that Husayn ibn Muhammad al-Marwarrūdhī narrated to us that Jarīr narrated to us from Muhammad from Anas, who said: \The people were alarmed"," so the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) rode a slow horse belonging to Abū Talhah. Then he went out galloping alone"," and the people rode galloping behind him. He said: 'You have nothing to fear; it is indeed a sea (i.e."," a horse of great endurance).'\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in the Sahīh from al-Fadl ibn Sahl from Husayn ibn Muhammad.\n\n[Sound. Agreed upon]"""
"20856","(20850) Ibn Fūrak informed us that ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us that Yūnus ibn Habīb narrated to us that Abū Dāwūd narrated to us that Shuʿbah narrated from Qatādah, who said: \Anas narrated to us"," saying: 'There was an alarm in Madīnah"," so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) rode a horse belonging to Abū Talhah called Mandūb. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: 'If there was any alarm"," we found it to be a sea (i.e."," a horse of great endurance).'\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī and Muslim narrated it in the Sahīh from the hadith of Shuʿbah.\n\n[Sound. Agreed upon]"""
"20857","(20851) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Hāfiz and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr both narrated to us, saying: \Abū al-ʿAbbās Muhammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us that al-Hasan ibn ʿAlī ibn ʿAffān narrated to us that Husayn ibn ʿAlī narrated to us from Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah from ʿAmr from Jābir"," who said: 'The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \""Let us go to al-Basīr who is among Banī Wāqif to visit him.\""' He was a blind man"," thus he said.\""\n\n[Munkar]"""
"20858","(20852) Abū al-Husayn ibn al-Fadl al-Qattān informed us in Baghdad that Abū Sahl ibn Ziyād al-Qattān narrated to us that Zakariyyā ibn Yahyā Abū Yahyā al-Nāqid narrated to us that Muhammad ibn Yūnus al-Hammāl narrated to us that Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah narrated from ʿAmr ibn Dīnār from Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mutʿim from his father, who said: \The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) used to say to his companions: 'Come with us to Banī Wāqif to visit al-Basīr.'\""\n\nSufyān said: \""They were a clan of the Ansār"," and he was blind.\"" Thus he narrated it as a connected narration. The correct version from Sufyān is from ʿAmr from Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mutʿim from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) as a mursal (disconnected) narration.\n\n[Munkar]"""
"20859","(20853) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Hāfiz informed us that ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muhammad ibn al-Nuʿmān al-Mihrajānī narrated to us that Yahyā ibn Muhammad al-Bakhtarī narrated to us that Muhammad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ghubarī narrated to us that Abū ʿAwwānah narrated from al-Jaʿd from Anas, who said: \The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said to me: 'O my little son!'\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in the Sahīh from Muhammad ibn ʿUbayd.\n\n[Sound. Muslim 2151]"""
"20860","(20854) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Hāfiz and Abū Sādiq Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Attār both narrated to us, saying: \Abū al-ʿAbbās Muhammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us that al-Hasan ibn Mukram narrated to us that Abū al-Nadr Muhammad ibn Rāshid narrated to us from Sulaymān ibn Mūsā from ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb from his father from his grandfather that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) rejected the testimony of the treacherous man"," the treacherous woman"," the one who harbors rancor against his brother"," and the testimony of the dependent (al-qāniʿ) for the people of the household — meaning the subordinate — but permitted it against others.\""\n\n[Hasan]"""
"20861","(20855) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us: Muḥammad ibn Bakr informed us: Abū Dāwūd narrated to us: Ḥafṣ ibn ʿUmar narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Rāshid narrated it with its chain of narration, identical to it, except that he said: \And he permitted it for others","\"" and he did not say \""meaning the Tābiʿī.\"" [Hasan. It was mentioned before it.]"""
"20862","(20856) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī both informed us, saying: Abū ʿAlī al-Ḥusayn ibn ʿAlī al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn al-Muʿāfā al-Ṣaydāwī narrated to us in Ṣaydā: Yaḥyā ibn ʿUthmān al-Ḥaḍramī narrated to us: Zayd ibn Yaḥyā ibn ʿUbayd narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us: Muḥammad ibn Bakr informed us: Abū Dāwūd narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Khalaf ibn Ṭāriq narrated to us: Zayd ibn Yaḥyā ibn ʿUbayd al-Khuzāʿī narrated to us: Saʿīd ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz narrated from Sulaymān ibn Mūsā with his chain of narration, saying: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \The testimony of a treacherous man"," a treacherous woman"," a fornicator man"," a fornicator woman"," and one who harbors rancor against his brother shall not be accepted.\""\n\nAbū ʿAbdillāh added in his narration: \""In Islam.\"" [Hasan]"""
"20863","(20857) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Muḥammad ibn Abī Ḥāmid al-Muqriʾ both informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn ʿAffān narrated to us: ʿUbaydullāh ibn Mūsā narrated from al-Zinjī ibn Khālid, who said: I heard al-ʿAlāʾ ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān narrating from his father, from Abū Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet ﷺ, who said: \The testimony of one who is a close companion"," one who is insane"," and one who harbors rancor born of enmity shall not be accepted.\"" Thus he said. [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"20864","(20858) ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us: Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd informed us: Tamtām narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Ṣamad narrated to us: Muslim ibn Khālid narrated to us: al-ʿAlāʾ ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān narrated from his father, from Abū Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \The testimony of one who harbors rancor and one who harbors suspicion shall not be accepted.\"" Al-Ẓinnah is more accurately preserved than al-Khullah. [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"20865","(20859) The most authentic narration in this chapter, even though it is mursal, is what Abū Ṣāliḥ ibn Abī Ṭāhir al-ʿAnbarī informed us: My grandfather, Abū Muḥammad Yaḥyā ibn Manṣūr al-Qāḍī, narrated to us: Abū ʿAlī Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr narrated to us: al-Qaʿnabī narrated to us: Ibn Abī Dhiʾb narrated from al-Ḥakam ibn Muslim, from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān — al-Aʿraj informed us — who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \The testimony of one who harbors suspicion"," one who is insane"," and one who harbors rancor shall not be accepted.\""\n\nAl-Jinnah means insanity"," and al-Ḥinnah refers to one between whom and another there is enmity. I do not know from which of these narrators this explanation originates. It has also been narrated through another route as a mursal narration concerning the disputing party and the one suspected. [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"20866","(20860) Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī informed us: Abū al-Ḥasan al-Kārizī informed us: ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz informed us from Abī ʿUbayd: Ḥafṣ ibn Ghiyāth narrated to us from Muḥammad ibn Zayd ibn Muhājir, from Ṭalḥah ibn ʿAbdillāh ibn ʿAwf, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent a caller until he reached the Thaniyyah, proclaiming: \The testimony of a disputing party and one who is suspected shall not be accepted"," and the oath is upon the one against whom the claim is made.\""\n\nAbū Dāwūd recorded it along with the ḥadīth of al-Aʿraj among the mursal narrations. [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"20867","(20861) Abū Aḥmad al-Mihrajānī informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Jaʿfar al-Muzakkī informed us: Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us: Ibn Bukayr narrated to us: Mālik informed us, having heard that ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb, may Allah be pleased with him, said: \The testimony of a disputing party and one who is suspected shall not be accepted.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"20868","(20862) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq informed us: Isḥāq ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Maymūn narrated to us: Abū al-Walīd al-Ṭayālisī narrated to us: Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah narrated from ʿAmr ibn Dīnār, from Ibn Abī Mulaykah, from al-Miswar ibn Makhramah, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Fāṭimah is a part of me; whoever harms her has harmed me.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī recorded it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Abī al-Walīd"," and Muslim recorded it from Abī Maʿmar from Sufyān. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Agreed upon.]"""
"20869","(20863) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbdullāh ibn Yūsuf al-Aṣbahānī informed us: Abū Saʿīd ibn al-Aʿrābī informed us: Saʿdān ibn Naṣr narrated to us: Sufyān narrated from Ibrāhīm ibn Mayṣarah, from Ibn Abī Suwayd, from ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz, who said: The righteous woman, Khawlah bint Ḥakīm, the wife of ʿUthmān ibn Maẓʿūn, claimed that the Prophet ﷺ came out while he was embracing one of his daughter's two sons, saying: \By Allah"," you are indeed ignorant"," cowardly"," and miserly"," and you are indeed among the fragrant flowers of Allah.\""\n\nAnd Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: ʤAlī ibn Ḥamshādh al-ʿAdl narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī ibn Buṭḥā narrated to us: ʿAffān narrated to us: Wahb narrated to us: ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUthmān ibn Khuthaym narrated from Saʿīd ibn Abī Rāshid"," from Yaʿlā ibn Munayyah al-Thaqafī"," who said: al-Ḥasan and al-Ḥusayn came running to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ"," so he embraced them both and then said: \""Indeed"," the child is a cause of miserliness"," cowardice"," and grief.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"20870","(20864) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū ʿUthmān Saʿīd ibn Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdān al-Naysābūrī both informed us, saying: Abū ʿAbdillāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad al-Ribāṭī narrated in Rajab of the year 263 AH, saying: It was recited to Abī ʿUbayd.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī informed us: Abū al-Ḥasan al-Kārizī informed us: ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz informed us from Abī ʿUbayd: Marwān al-Fazārī narrated to us from a scholar from the people of al-Jazīrah whose name was Yazīd ibn Abī Ziyād, from al-Zuhrī, from ʿUrwah, from ʿĀʾishah, may Allah be pleased with her, from the Prophet ﷺ, that he said: \The testimony of a treacherous man"," a treacherous woman"," one who harbors rancor against his brother"," one who is suspected in matters of allegiance or kinship"," and one who is a dependent of a household on their behalf shall not be accepted.\""\n\nThis is the wording of ʿAlī's narration. In the narration of al-Ribāṭī it reads: \""and one who is suspected"," and one accused of kinship","\"" and the former is more authentic. This Yazīd is weak. [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"20871","(20865) It was also narrated by 'Uqayl from al-Zuhrī that he said: \The established practice (sunnah) is that the testimony of an adversary and one whose reliability is not confirmed is not acceptable.\"" Abū 'Abdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us"," Abū al-Walīd narrated to us"," Ibrāhīm narrated to us"," from al-Ḥasan b. 'Īsā"," from Ibn al-Mubārak"," from Yaḥyā b. Ayyūb"," from 'Uqayl"," from Ibn Shihāb"," and he mentioned it. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"20872","(20866) Abū 'Abdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū al-Walīd informed us, Muḥammad b. Hārūn narrated to us, 'Uthmān b. Sa'īd narrated to us, 'Abdullāh b. Ṣāliḥ narrated to us, from al-Layth, from 'Uqayl, who said: \I asked Ibn Shihāb about a man who is the guardian of an orphan—is his testimony acceptable?\"" Ibn Shihāb said: \""The established practice (sunnah) in Islam is that the testimony of an adversary"," one whose reliability is not confirmed"," and the testimony of an adversary against the one with whom he is in dispute"," are not acceptable.\""\n\nThe Shaykh said: \""This wording regarding kinship is only narrated in the document that 'Umar wrote to Abū Mūsā al-Ash'arī"," may Allah be pleased with both of him"," and it has been transmitted with its chain.\n\nAnd we have narrated the rejection of the testimony of one whose reliability is not confirmed (al-ẓanīn) absolutely"," from two mursal narrations from the Prophet ﷺ"," and from another perspective as a mawsūl narration"," though it contains weakness. It is strengthened by the two mursal narrations alongside it. And Allah knows best.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"20873","(20867) Abū Ḥāzim al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū al-Faḍl b. Khamīruwayh informed us, Aḥmad b. Najdah narrated to us, Sa'īd b. Manṣūr narrated to us, Hushaym informed us, al-Shaybānī informed us, from al-Sha'bī, that Shurayḥ used to accept the testimony of a brother in favor of his brother, provided he was upright ('adl). [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"20874","(20868) He said: And Sa'īd narrated to us, Khālid b. 'Abdullāh narrated to us, from Muḥammad b. 'Amr b. 'Alqamah, from 'Umar b. 'Abd al-'Azīz, that he accepted the testimony of a brother in favor of his brother.\n\nAnd we have narrated from Abū Yaḥyā al-Sājī that he narrated it from Ibn al-Zubayr, Shurayḥ, al-Ḥasan, al-Sha'bī, and 'Umar b. 'Abd al-'Azīz. He said: And al-Ḥasan and al-Zuhrī said: \The testimony of a husband and wife is acceptable.\"" [Ḍa'īf]"""
"20875","(20869) Abū 'Abdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū Bakr Aḥmad b. Sulmān b. al-Ḥasan al-Faqīh narrated to us, dictating in the Jāmi' al-Manṣūr, Abū Dāwūd Sulaymān b. al-Ash'ath narrated to us, Mūsā b. Ismā'īl narrated to us, 'Abd al-'Azīz b. Abī Ḥāzim narrated to us, from his father, from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet ﷺ, who said: \The Qadariyyah are the Magians (majūs) of this Ummah. If they fall ill"," do not visit them"," and if they die"," do not attend their funeral prayers.\""\n\nAbū Dāwūd recorded it in the Kitāb al-Sunan thus. [Ḍa'īf]"""
"20876","(20870) Abū al-Ḥasan 'Alī b. Aḥmad b. 'Abdān informed us, Abū al-Qāsim Sulaymān b. Aḥmad al-Ṭabarānī informed us, 'Alī b. 'Abd al-'Azīz narrated to us, Abū Nu'aym narrated to us, Sufyān narrated to us, from 'Umar b. Muḥammad, from 'Umar, the freedman of Ghufrah, from a man among the Anṣār, from Ḥudhayfah, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Every Ummah has its Magians"," and the Magians of this Ummah are those who say there is no predestination (qadar). If any of them falls ill"," do not visit him"," and if any of them dies"," do not attend his funeral. They are the party of the Dajjāl"," and it is a right upon Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic"," to join them with him.\""\n\nAbū Dāwūd recorded it in the Kitāb al-Sunan from Muḥammad b. Kathīr"," from Sufyān. And what has been narrated from Ibn 'Umar and Ḥudhayfah regarding the explicit takfīr of the Qadariyyah is established textually and by clear indication in the authentic ḥadīth from Ibn 'Umar from his father from the Prophet ﷺ concerning Īmān"," along with Ibn 'Umar's dissociation from those who denied qadar. [Ḍa'īf]"""
"20877","(20871) Abū al-Ḥusayn 'Alī b. Muḥammad b. 'Abdullāh b. Bishrān al-'Adl in Baghdād informed us, Abū Ja'far Muḥammad b. 'Amr al-Razzāz informed us, 'Īsā b. 'Abdullāh al-Ṭayālisī informed us, Abū 'Abd al-Raḥmān al-Muqrī' informed us, Kahmas b. al-Ḥasan said: I heard 'Abdullāh b. Buraydah narrate that Yaḥyā b. Ya'mar said: \The first person to speak about qadar in Baṣrah was Ma'bad al-Juhanī. So we set out for Ḥajj"," I and Ḥumayd b. 'Abd al-Raḥmān"," and when we arrived we said: 'If we could meet one of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and ask him about what these people are saying regarding qadar.' He said: We came upon 'Abdullāh b. 'Umar in the mosque"," and I and my companion surrounded him"," one of us on his right and the other on his left. Yaḥyā said: I thought my companion had delegated the speech to me"," so I said: 'O Abū 'Abd al-Raḥmān"," people have appeared among us who recite the Qur'ān and claim knowledge"," yet they assert that there is no qadar and that the matter is entirely uncreated (unf).' 'Abdullāh said: 'When you meet those people"," inform them that I am free of them and they are free of me. And by Him by whom 'Abdullāh b. 'Umar swears"," if any of them had gold equal to Mount Uḥud and spent it"," Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic"," would not accept it from him until he believes in all of qadar—its good and its evil.' Then he said: 'My father"," 'Umar b. al-Khaṭṭāb"," may Allah be pleased with him"," narrated to me"," saying: \""One day we were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when suddenly a man appeared"," intensely white in clothing"," intensely black in hair"," upon whom no trace of travel was visible"," and none of us recognized him"," until he sat before the Messenger of Allah ﷺ"," placed his knees against his knees"," and put his palms upon his thighs. Then he said: 'O Muḥammad"," tell me about Islam—what is Islam?' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Islam is that you bear witness that there is no god but Allah and that Muḥammad is His slave and His Messenger"," that you establish the Ṣalāh"," pay the Zakāh"," fast Ramaḍān"," and perform Ḥajj to the House if you are able to make the journey.' The man said: 'You have spoken truly.' 'Umar said: 'We were amazed at him—he asked him and then confirmed him.' Then he said: 'O Muḥammad"," tell me about Īmān—what is Īmān?' He said: 'Īmān is that you believe in Allah"," His angels"," His books"," His messengers"," the Last Day"," and all of qadar—its good and its evil.' He said: 'You have spoken truly.' He said: 'Tell me about Iḥsān.' He said: 'Iḥsān is that you worship Allah as though you see Him"," and if you do not see Him"," then indeed He sees you.' He said: 'Tell me about the Hour—when is the Hour?' He said: 'The one asked about it is no more knowledgeable than the one asking.' He said: 'Tell me about its signs.' He said: 'That the slave-girl gives birth to her mistress"," and that you see the barefoot"," naked"," destitute shepherds competing in the construction of tall buildings.' Then he departed. 'Umar"," may Allah be pleased with him"," said: 'I remained for three days"," then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: 'O 'Umar"," do you know who the questioner was?' I said: 'Allah and His Messenger know best.' He said: 'That was Jibrīl"," peace be upon him—he came to you to teach you your religion.'\""'\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muttafaq 'alayh]"""
"20878","(20872) Abū al-Ḥusayn informed us, Abū Ja'far informed us, Muḥammad b. 'Ubaydullāh b. Yazīd narrated to us, 'Abd al-Wahhāb b. Aṭā' informed us, Kahmas narrated to us, from 'Abdullāh b. Buraydah, and he mentioned its meaning. Muslim b. al-Ḥajjāj recorded it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from the ḥadīth of Kahmas and others.\n\nAnd al-Bukhārī and Muslim recorded it from the ḥadīth of Abū Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet ﷺ, and its corroborating narrations are many, from the ḥadīth of 'Alī, Abū Dharr, and others, from the Prophet ﷺ. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Previously cited]"
"20879","(20873) Abū 'Abdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū Aḥmad informed us, Bakr b. Muḥammad al-Ṣayrafī in Marw narrated to us, 'Abd al-Ṣamad b. al-Faḍl al-Balkhī narrated to us, 'Abdullāh b. Yazīd al-Muqrī' narrated to us, Sa'īd b. Abī Ayyūb narrated to us, 'Aṭā' b. Dīnār narrated to us, Ḥakīm b. Sharīk al-Hudhalī narrated to us, from Yaḥyā b. Maymūn al-Ḥaḍramī, from Rābi'ah al-Jurashī, from Abū Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, from 'Umar b. al-Khaṭṭāb, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet ﷺ, who said: \Do not sit with the people of qadar"," and do not engage them in legal disputes.\""\n\nAbū Dāwūd recorded it in the Kitāb al-Sunan from Aḥmad b. Ḥanbal"," from al-Muqrī'. [Ḍa'īf]"""
"20880","(20874) Abū al-Ḥusayn b. Bishrān al-'Adl in Baghdād informed us, Abū 'Alī Ismā'īl b. Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār informed us, al-Ḥasan b. Mukram informed us, Isḥāq b. Sulaymān informed us, Abū Sinān Sa'īd b. Sinān al-Shaybānī said: I heard Wahb b. Khālid al-Ḥimṣī narrate to us from Ibn al-Daylamī, who said: \Something concerning qadar occurred to my mind"," so I went to Ubayy b. Ka'b and said: 'O Abū al-Mundhir"," something concerning qadar has occurred to me"," and I fear it may bring about the destruction of my religion and my affair.' He said: 'O my nephew"," if Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic"," were to punish the inhabitants of His heavens and the inhabitants of His earth"," He would punish them while being unjust to none of them"," and if He were to have mercy on them"," His mercy would be better for them than their deeds. If you had gold equal to Mount Uḥud and spent it in the cause of Allah"," Allah would not accept it from you until you believe in qadar and know that what has befallen you was not to miss you"," and what has missed you was not to befall you. And if you die upon anything other than this"," you will enter the Fire. And there is no harm in you going to my brother 'Abdullāh b. Mas'ūd and asking him.'\""\n\n\""So I went to 'Abdullāh b. Mas'ūd and asked him"," and he said the same thing.\""\n\nIsḥāq said: \""He narrated the entire story as he said"," though I have abridged it. And he said to me: 'There is no harm in you going to Ḥudhayfah b. al-Yamān and asking him.'\""\n\n\""So I went to Ḥudhayfah b. al-Yamān and asked him"," and he said the same thing to me. And he said: 'Go to Zayd b. Thābit and ask him.'\""\n\n\""So I went to Zayd b. Thābit and asked him"," and he said: 'I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \""If Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic"," were to punish the inhabitants of His heavens and the inhabitants of His earth"," He would punish them while being unjust to none of them"," and if He were to have mercy on them"," His mercy would be better for them than their deeds. If you had gold equal to Mount Uḥud and spent it in the cause of Allah"," Allah would not accept it from you until you believe in qadar and know that what has befallen you was not to miss you"," and what has missed you was not to befall you. And if one dies upon anything other than this"," he will enter the Fire.\""'\""\n\nAbū Dāwūd recorded it in the Kitāb al-Sunan from Muḥammad b. Kathīr"," from Sufyān al-Thawrī"," from Abū Sinān. And we have narrated something to that effect from 'Alī b. Abī Ṭālib"," 'Ubādah b. al-Ṣāmit"," Salmān al-Fārisī"," and others"," may Allah be pleased with them all. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"20881","(20875) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us in the book of Sunan: Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Bakr narrated to us: Abū Dāwūd narrated to us: Jaʿfar ibn Musāfir al-Hudhalī narrated to us: Yaḥyī ibn Ḥassān narrated to us: al-Walīd ibn Rabāḥ narrated from Ibrāhīm ibn Abī ʿAblah from Abī Ḥafṣah, who said: ʿUbadah ibn al-Ṣāmit said to his son: \O my dear son"," you will never taste the true essence of faith until you know that whatever has befallen you was not destined to miss you"," and whatever has missed you was not destined to befall you. I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: 'Indeed"," the first thing Allah created was the Pen"," and He said to it: \""Write.\"" It said: \""O my Lord"," what shall I write?\"" He said: \""Write the decrees of everything until the Hour is established.\""'\""\n\nO my dear son"," I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: \""Whoever dies upon anything other than this is not from me.\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Aḥmad 22197]"""
"20882","(20876) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq al-Faqīh informed us: Bishr ibn Mūsā narrated to us: Abū Nuʿaym narrated to us: Sufyān narrated from Abū Isḥāq from Abī al-Ḥajjāj al-Azdī from Salmān, that he was asked about faith in al-Qadar (divine decree). He said: \Know that whatever has befallen you was not destined to miss you"," and whatever has missed you was not destined to befall you.\""\n\n[Ḍaʿīf]"""
"20883","(20877) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq informed us: Bishr ibn Mūsā informed us: Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Muqriʾ narrated to us: Abū Ḥanīfah narrated from al-Haytham from al-Shaʿbī from ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him), that he addressed the people from the pulpit of Kūfah and said: \He is not from us who does not believe in al-Qadar"," its good and its evil.\""\n\n[Ḍaʿīf]"""
"20884","(20878) Abū ʿAbdillāh informed us: Abū Bakr informed us: Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad ibn Ḥayyān al-Anṣārī narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Kathīr informed us: Shuʿbah narrated from Abū Isḥāq from al-Ḥārith from ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: \A servant will never taste the sweetness of faith until he believes in al-Qadar.\""\n\n[Ḍaʿīf]"""
"20885","(20879) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq informed us: Mūsā ibn al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAbbād narrated to us: Ḥajjāj ibn Minhāl narrated to us: Ḥammād narrated from Sulaymān al-Taymī from Mujāhid, who said: \I came to Ibn ʿAbbās with a man and said: 'O Ibn ʿAbbās"," this man wishes to speak to you about al-Qadar.' He said: 'Bring him close to me.' I said: 'Here he is. Do you intend to kill him?' He said: 'Yes"," by the One in Whose Hand is my soul"," had you brought him close to me"," I would have placed my hand on his neck and not released it until I crushed it.'\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"20886","(20880) Abū ʿUbaydillāh ibn Burhān, Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān, and Abū Muḥammad al-Sukkarī in Baghdād said: Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn ʿArafah narrated to us: Marwān ibn Shuʿāj al-Jazarī narrated from ʿAbd al-Malik ibn Jurayj from ʬāʾ ibn Abī Rabāḥ, who said: \I came to Ibn ʿAbbās while he was drawing water from Zamzam"," the lower part of his garments being soaked. I said to him: 'People have spoken about al-Qadar.' He said: 'Have they indeed done so?' I said: 'Yes.' He said: 'By Allah"," this verse was revealed only concerning them: \""Taste the touch of Saqar! Indeed"," everything We created with measure (Qadar).\"" [Al-Qamar 48–49] They are the worst of this Ummah. Do not visit their sick and do not pray over their dead. If I were to see any one of them"," I would gouge out my eyes with these two fingers of mine.'\""\n\n[Ḥasan]"""
"20887","(20881) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn Ṣāliḥ ibn Hānīʾ narrated to us: al-Sarī ibn Khuzaymah narrated to us: Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ʿAbdullāh ibn Yazīd al-Muqriʾ narrated to us: Saʿīd ibn Abī Ayyūb narrated to me: Abū Ṣakhr narrated from Nāfiʿ, who said: \Ibn ʿUmar had a friend from the people of Shām who used to correspond with him. ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar wrote to him: 'It has reached me that you have spoken about something concerning al-Qadar. Beware that you do not write to me"," for I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: \""There will be people in my Ummah who will deny al-Qadar.\""'\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"20888","(20882) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me: Abū al-Naḍr al-Faqīh narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Naṣr al-Imām narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Aʿlā ibn Ḥammād al-Narsī narrated to us. He said: \I read to Mālik ibn Anas from Ziyād ibn Saʿd from ʿAmr ibn Muslim from Ṭāwūs al-Yamānī"," who said: 'I met a number of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) who used to say: \""Everything is by Qadar (divine decree).\""' Ṭāwūs said: 'And I heard ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \""Everything is by Qadar"," even incapacity (al-ʿajz) and intelligence (al-kays)"," or intelligence and incapacity.\""'\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbd al-Aʿlā ibn Ḥammād. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 2655]"""
"20889","(20883) Abū Naṣr ibn Qatādah informed us: Abū ʿAmr ibn Najayd narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Bukayr narrated to us: Mālik narrated from his uncle Abū Suhayl ibn Mālik, who said: \I was walking with ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz (may Allah be pleased with him) and he said: 'What is your opinion about these Qadariyyah?' I said: 'I think you should ask them to repent. If they accept"," [well and good]; otherwise"," you should put them to the sword.' ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz said: 'That is my opinion as well.'\""\n\nMālik said: \""And that is also my opinion.\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Mālik 1665]"""
"20890","(20884) Abū al-Qāsim ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿUbaydillāh al-Ḥurfī in Baghdād informed us: Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Salmān al-Faqīh narrated to us: ʿAbdullāh ibn Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal narrated to me: My father narrated to us: Anas ibn ʿIyāḍ narrated to me: Nāfiʿ ibn Mālik, Abū Suhayl, narrated that ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz said to him: \What do you think about those who say there is no Qadar?\"" He said: \""I think they should be asked to repent. If they repent"," [well and good]; otherwise"," their necks should be struck.\"" ʿUmar said: \""That is the correct opinion regarding them. Were it not for anything other than this one verse"," it would suffice: 'And you"," and what you worship besides Allah"," are not temptations over Him"," except he who is destined for the Hellfire.' [Al-Ṣāffāt 161–163]\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Aḥmad]"""
"20891","(20885) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū Bakr ibn Dārim al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us that Abū ʿAbdillāh Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Qammāṭ narrated to us that Abū Saʿīd al-Ashajj narrated to us that al-Ḥakam ibn Sulaymān al-Kindī said: I heard al-Awzāʿī being asked about the Qadariyyah, and he said: \Do not sit with them.\"" [Weak]"""
"20892","(20886) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū Muḥammad al-Ḥasan ibn Ḥalīm narrated to us that Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq ibn Rāhawayh al-Qāḍī in Marw said: My father was asked — and I was listening — about the Qurʾān, and he said: \The Qurʾān is the Speech of Allah"," His knowledge"," and His revelation; it is not created.\"" And Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah narrated from ʿAmr ibn Dīnār"," who said: \""I found our elders"," for seventy years"," saying…\""\n\n(Chain) And Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq informed us that Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdūs narrated to us"," saying: I heard ʿUthmān ibn Saʿīd al-Dārimī say: I heard Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm al-Ḥanẓalī say: Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah said"," from ʿAmr ibn Dīnār"," who said: \""I found the people"," for seventy years"," saying: 'Allah is the Creator"," and everything besides Him is created"," and the Qurʾān is the Speech of Allah"," exalted is He.'\""\n\nAbū al-Ḥasan said: My father said: \""And ʿAmr ibn Dīnār met the most eminent Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) among the Badrīs"," the Muhājirūn"," and the Anṣār — such as Jābir ibn ʿAbdillāh"," Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī"," ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar"," ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbbās"," and ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Zubayr — and the most eminent of the Tābiʿūn. And upon this the early generation of this Ummah proceeded.\"" [Authentic]"""
"20893","(20887) Abū Naṣr ibn Qatādah informed us that Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbdah narrated to us that Abū ʿAbdillāh Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Būshanjī narrated to us that Abū Rajāʾ Qutaybah ibn Saʿīd narrated to us that al-Qāsim ibn Muḥammad narrated to us — he was a Baghdādī, trustworthy — that ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, meaning Ibn Muḥammad ibn Ḥabīb ibn Abī Ḥabīb, narrated from his father, from his grandfather, who said: I witnessed Khālid ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Qasrī delivering a sermon to them on the Day of Sacrifice in Wāsiṭ. He said: \Go back"," O people"," and offer your sacrifice"," may Allah accept it from you"," for I am offering the sacrifice of al-Jaʿd ibn Dirham"," for he claimed that Allah did not take Ibrāhīm as a Khalīl and did not speak to Mūsā directly. Glorified and exalted is He above what al-Jaʿd ibn Dirham says.\"" Then he descended and slaughtered him.\n\nAbū Rajāʾ said: \""And al-Jahm took this speech from al-Jaʿd ibn Dirham.\"" [Weak]"""
"20894","(20888) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū ʿUthmān Saʿīd ibn Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdān both informed us that Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us that Ḥusnūn al-Bannāʾ al-Kūfī narrated to us that ʿUmar ibn Ibrāhīm ibn Khālid narrated to us that Qays ibn al-Rabīʿ said: I asked Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad about the Qurʾān, and he said: \It is the Speech of Allah.\"" I said: \""Is it created?\"" He said: \""No.\"" I said: \""What do you say about one who claims it is created?\"" He said: \""He is to be killed"," and no repentance is to be sought from him.\"" [Weak]"""
"20895","(20889) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī both informed us that Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us that Abū Umayyah al-Ṭarsūsī narrated to us that Yaḥyā ibn Khalaf al-Muqrīʾ said: I was with Mālik ibn Anas when a man came to him and said: \What do you say about one who says the Qurʾān is created?\"" He said: \""In my view"," he is a disbeliever; kill him.\""\n\nYaḥyā ibn Khalaf said: \""And I asked Layth ibn Saʿd and Ibn Lahīʿah about one who says the Qurʾān is created"," and both of them said: 'He is a disbeliever.'\"" [Weak]"""
"20896","(20890) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, saying: I heard Abū Zakariyyā Yaḥyā ibn Muḥammad al-ʿAnbarī say: I heard ʿImrān ibn Mūsā al-Jurjānī in Naysābūr say: I heard Suwayd ibn Saʿīd say: I heard Mālik ibn Anas, Ḥammād ibn Zayd, Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah, al-Fuḍayl ibn ʿIyāḍ, Sharīk ibn ʿAbdillāh, Yaḥyā ibn Sulaym, Muslim ibn Khālid, Hishām ibn Sulaymān al-Makhzūmī, Jarīr ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥamīd, ʿAlī ibn Mushhir, ʿAbdah, ʿAbdullāh ibn Idrīs, Ḥafṣ ibn Ghiyāth, Wakīʿ, Muḥammad ibn Fuḍayl, ʿAbd al-Raḥīm ibn Sulaymān, ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Abī Ḥāzim, al-Dārawardī, Ismāʿīl ibn Jaʿfar, Ḥātim ibn Ismāʿīl, ʿAbdullāh ibn Yazīd al-Muqrīʾ, and all those from whom I transmitted knowledge, saying: \Īmān is statement and action"," it increases and decreases; and the Qurʾān is the Speech of Allah"," from the attribute of His Essence"," not created; and whoever says it is created is a disbeliever in Allah the Magnificent.\""\n\nAnd we have narrated it from ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Mubārak"," Yazīd ibn Hārūn"," ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Mahdī"," Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā"," Muḥammad ibn Ismāʿīl al-Bukhārī"," Muslim ibn al-Ḥajjāj"," Abū ʿUbayd al-Qāsim ibn Sallām"," and others of our Imams — may Allah have mercy upon them. [Weak]"""
"20897","(20891) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr both informed us that Abū al-ʿAbbās, al-Aṣamm, narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣaghānī narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn Ashkīb narrated to us, saying: I heard my father say: I heard Abū Yūsuf in Khurāsān say: \There are two groups on the earth that are more hateful to me than any others: the Muqātiliyyah and the Jahmiyyah.\"" [Weak]"""
"20898","(20892) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, saying: I heard Abū Ḥabīb Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Mūsā al-Maṣāḥifī say: I heard my father say: I heard Ayyūb ibn al-Ḥasan al-Faqīh say: \Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan did not permit the testimony of the Jahmiyyah.\"" [Weak]"""
"20899","(20893) Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-Sulamī informed us, saying: I heard ʿAbdullāh ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī ibn Ziyād say: I heard Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq ibn Khuzaymah say: I heard al-Rabīʿ say: \When al-Shāfiʿī spoke to Ḥafṣ al-Fard"," and Ḥafṣ said: 'The Qurʾān is created","' al-Shāfiʿī said to him: 'You have disbelieved in Allah the Magnificent.'\"" [Authentic]"""
"20900","(20894) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me that Abū al-Faḍl ibn Abī Naṣr al-ʿAdl narrated to me that Ḥaml ibn ʿAmr al-ʿAdl narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn Fawrash narrated from ʿAlī ibn Sahl al-Ramlī that he said: I asked al-Shāfiʿī about the Qurʾān, and he said to me: \It is the Speech of Allah"," not created.\"" I said: \""Then what about one who says it is created — what is he in your view?\"" He said: \""A disbeliever.\"" So I said to al-Shāfiʿī — may Allah have mercy on him: \""Whom did you meet among your teachers who said what you said?\"" He said: \""I did not meet any one of them except that he said: 'Whoever says the Qurʾān is created is a disbeliever in their view.'\"" [Authentic — al-Shāfiʿī]"""
"20901","(20895) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad ibn Ḥayyān al-Qāḍī narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Ziyād informed us, Abū Yaḥyā al-Sājī — or, in what he authorized to me orally — narrated to us: al-Rabīʿ said, \I heard al-Shāfiʿī say: 'That a servant meets Allah with every sin except shirk (associating partners) with Allah is better than that he meet Him with any of these [innovated] whims.' And that is because he saw a people disputing about al-qadar (divine decree) before him. Al-Shāfiʿī said: 'The will (al-mashīʾah) belongs to Allah alone"," to the exclusion of His creation"," and the will is the irādah (intention/desire) of Allah. Allah"," Mighty and Majestic"," says: {And you do not will except that Allah wills} [al-Insān: 30]. Thus He informed His creation that the will belongs to Him.' And he (al-Shāfiʿī) used to affirm al-qadar (divine decree).\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ — from al-Shāfiʿī]"""
"20902","(20896) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, al-Zubayr ibn ʿAbd al-Wāḥid al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to me, Ḥamzah ibn ʿAlī al-ʿAṭṭār in Egypt narrated to us, al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān said: \Al-Shāfiʿī was asked about al-qadar (divine decree)"," and he began to recite:\n\nWhatever You will comes to pass"," even if I do not will it;\nAnd whatever I will does not come to pass"," unless You will it.\n\nYou created the servants according to what You knew","\nAnd in Your knowledge the young and the old proceed.\n\nUpon this one You bestow favor"," and this one You forsake;\nThis one You aid"," and that one You do not aid.\n\nAmong them are the wretched and among them are the fortunate","\nAnd among them are the ugly and among them are the beautiful.\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ — from al-Shāfiʿī]"""
"20903","(20897) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ said: I heard Abū Aḥmad al-Ḥusayn ibn ʿAlī say: I heard Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq say: I heard al-Rabīʿ say: I heard al-Buwayṭī say: \Whoever says the Qurʾān is created (makhlūq) is a disbeliever. Allah"," Mighty and Majestic"," says: {Our command for a thing"," when We intend it"," is only that We say to it 'Be","' and it is} [al-Naḥl: 40]. Thus Allah informed that He creates creation by [the word] 'Be' (kun). So whoever claims that 'kun' is created has claimed that Allah creates creation by means of a creation.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ — from al-Buwayṭī]"""
"20904","(20898) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī informed us, both saying: We heard Abū Muḥammad Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥārith say: I heard Abū Zakariyyā Yaḥyā ibn Zakariyyā say: I heard al-Muzanī say: \The Qurʾān is the Speech of Allah"," not created.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ — from al-Muzanī]"""
"20905","(20899) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, Abū Muḥammad al-Muzanī said: I heard Yūsuf ibn Mūsā al-Marwazī in the year 295 AH say: \We were in Egypt in the company of Abū Ibrāhīm al-Muzanī"," a group of us from the people of Khurāsān. We used to gather with him at night"," and we would present questions among ourselves. He would stand for Ṣalāh"," and when he completed it"," he would turn to us and say: 'What do you think — if it were said to you such-and-such"," how would you respond to them?' Then he would return to his Ṣalāh. One night we rose"," and I and some companions of mine went to him and said: 'We are a people from Khurāsān"," and among us there has arisen a people who say the Qurʾān is created (makhlūq). We are not among those who delve into kalām (speculative theology)"," and we do not seek a fatwā from you regarding this matter except for our own religion and for those among us"," so that we may inform them of what you answer us.' He said: 'The Qurʾān is the Speech of Allah"," not created. And whoever says the Qurʾān is created is a disbeliever.'\""\n\nThe Shaykh (may Allah have mercy on him) said: \""This is the madhhab of our Imams (may Allah have mercy on them) regarding these innovators who were deprived of tawfīq (divine guidance) and abandoned the apparent meaning of the Book and the Sunnah in favor of their embellished opinions and their reprehensible interpretations.\""\n\nAnd I heard Abū Ḥāzim ʿUmar ibn Aḥmad al-ʿAbdawī al-Ḥāfiẓ say: I heard Zāhir ibn Aḥmad al-Sarakhsī say: \""When the appointed time of Abū al-Ḥasan al-Ashʿarī (may Allah have mercy on him) drew near in my house in Baghdad"," he called me and said: 'Bear witness that I do not declare any one of the people of this qiblah to be a disbeliever"," for all of them point to one God"," and this is merely a difference of expressions.'\""\n\nThe Shaykh (may Allah have mercy on him) said: \""Whoever holds this view claims that this is also the madhhab of al-Shāfiʿī (may Allah have mercy on him). Do you not see that he said in the book Adab al-Qāḍī: 'The people went — those who interpreted the Qurʾān"," the aḥādīth"," and qiyās (analogical reasoning)"," or those among them who went to matters concerning which they differed and in which they diverged severely"," and some of them deemed lawful regarding one another some of what would take long to recount — and all of that was from him (the Prophet ﷺ) in the era of the Salaf and after them until this day. We do not know anyone among the Salaf of this Ummah who is to be followed"," nor among the Tābiʿūn after them"," who rejected the testimony of anyone on the basis of an interpretation (taʾwīl)"," even if he considered him to be in error and misguided.' Then he continued speaking until he said: 'And the testimony of one who considers lying to be shirk with Allah or a sin for which the Fire is obligatory is more deserving that one's soul be at ease with it than the testimony of one who lightens the sin in it.' They said: 'And what has been narrated to us from al-Shāfiʿī and other Imams regarding the takfīr (declaring to be a disbeliever) of these innovators — they only intended by it kufr (disbelief) that does not constitute absolute kufr"," as Allah"," Mighty and Majestic"," says: {And whoever does not judge by what Allah has revealed — it is they who are the disbelievers} [al-Māʾidah: 44]. Ibn ʿAbbās said: 'It is not the kufr that you go to; it is not a kufr that removes one from the religion (millah)"," but rather it is a kufr lesser than kufr.'\"" The Shaykh (may Allah have mercy on him) said: \""It is as though they intended by their takfīr what they went to in terms of negating these attributes that Allah"," Exalted"," has affirmed for Himself and their denial of them through a far-fetched interpretation"," while their belief was in affirmation of what Allah"," Exalted"," has affirmed. So they deviated from the apparent meaning through an interpretation"," and by it they did not exit the religion"," even though the interpretation was erroneous — just as one who denied the inclusion of al-Muʿawwidhatayn in the muṣāḥif (copies of the Qurʾān) alongside the other sūrahs did not exit the religion on account of the doubt that he went to"," even though it was erroneous according to others. And what has been narrated to us from the Prophet ﷺ in his saying: 'The Qadarīyah are the Magians (Majūs) of this Ummah' — he only called them Magians because of the resemblance of some of what they hold to the doctrines of the Magians in their doctrine of the two origins"," namely light and darkness. They claim that good is from the action of light and that evil is from the action of darkness"," so they became dualists. Likewise"," the Qadarīyah attribute good to Allah and evil to other than Him. Allah"," Exalted"," is the Creator of good and evil"," both being attributed to Him in terms of creation and bringing into existence"," and to the doers among His servants in terms of action and acquisition.\"" This is the statement of Abū Sulaymān al-Khaṭṭābī (may Allah have mercy on him) regarding the good.\n\nAnd Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣibghī said in what…"""
"20906","(20900) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us regarding the evidence that the Qadarīyah are the Magians of this Ummah: \The Magians said that Allah created some of these attributes (aʿrāḍ) but not others — He created light but did not create darkness. And the Qadarīyah said that Allah created some of these attributes but not others — He created the sound of thunder but did not create the sound of the flint. And the Magians said that Allah did not create ignorance (jahl) or forgetfulness (nisyān). And the Qadarīyah said that Allah did not create memory (ḥifẓ)"," knowledge (ʿilm)"," or action (ʿamal). And the Magians said that Allah does not misguide anyone. And the Qadarīyah said the same. Yet Allah"," Mighty and Majestic"," says: {He misguides whom He wills} [al-Raʿd: 27]"," and He says: {He intends to mislead you} [Hūd: 34].\"" The Shaykh (may Allah have mercy on him) said: \""He only called them Magians on account of these meanings"," or some of them"," and he attributed them along with that to the Ummah.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"20907","(20901) Abū ʿAlī al-Ḥusayn ibn Muḥammad al-Rūdhabārī informed us in the book of the Sunan that Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Bakr informed us, Abū Dāwūd narrated to us, Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated to us, from Khālid, from Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr, from Abū Salamah, from Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \The Jews split into seventy-one or seventy-two sects"," and the Christians split into seventy-one or seventy-two sects"," and my Ummah will split into seventy-three sects.\""\n\nAbū Sulaymān al-Khaṭṭābī (may Allah have mercy on him) said"," according to what reached me from him"," regarding his (the Prophet's ﷺ) statement: \""My Ummah will split into seventy-three sects\"" — \""In this is evidence that all of these sects are not outside the religion"," since the Prophet ﷺ made them all part of his Ummah. And in it is evidence that one who interprets (mutaʾawwil) does not exit the religion"," even if he errs in his interpretation.\"" The Shaykh (may Allah have mercy on him) said: \""Whoever declares a Muslim to be a disbeliever absolutely on the basis of an interpretation does not"," by his takfīr of him through that interpretation"," exit the religion. This has already been discussed in the book of Ṣalāh in the ḥadīth of Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh regarding the story of the man who left the Ṣalāh of Muʿādh ibn Jabal. That reached Muʿādh"," and he said: 'A hypocrite!' Then the man mentioned that to the Prophet ﷺ"," and the Prophet ﷺ did not add to commanding Muʿādh to shorten the Ṣalāh and said: 'Are you a fitnah-monger"," O Muʿādh"," by lengthening the Ṣalāh?'\""\n\n\""And we have narrated in the story of Ḥāṭib ibn Abī Baltaʿah"," when he wrote to Quraysh about the march of the Prophet ﷺ to them during the year of the Conquest"," that ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: 'O Messenger of Allah"," let me strike the neck of this hypocrite.' The Prophet ﷺ said: 'He witnessed Badr.' And the Prophet ﷺ did not censure ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) for calling him that"," since what he did was an apparent sign of hypocrisy. And it is only the one who declares a Muslim to be a disbeliever without an interpretation (taʾwīl) who becomes a disbeliever.\"" [Ḥasan for other than him]"""
"20908","(20902) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Aḥmad ibn Salmān narrated to us, Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq narrated to us, al-Qaʿnabī narrated to us, from Mālik, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Dīnār, from Ibn ʿUmar, that the Prophet ﷺ said: \Any man who says to his brother"," 'O disbeliever!' — it will return to one of them.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Ismāʿīl from Mālik"," and Muslim narrated it from the ḥadīth of Ismāʿīl ibn Jaʿfar from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Dīnār. Upon this methodology"," the testimony of the people of whims (ahl al-ahwāʾ) — when they have an interpretation (taʾwīl) — is accepted. [Ṣaḥīḥ — agreed upon]"""
"20909","(20903) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ said: I heard Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn Ṣāliḥ ibn Hānīʾ say: I heard Abū ʿAmr al-Mustamlī say: I heard al-Ḥusayn ibn Manṣūr say: I heard ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Mahdī say: \Knowledge is recorded from the people of whims (ahl al-ahwāʾ)"," and their testimonies are accepted"," so long as they do not call to it (their innovation). But if they call to it"," then nothing is recorded from them and their testimonies are not accepted.\"" By \""recording knowledge\"" he means the narration of reports (akhbār). [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"20910","(20904) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ said in what he authorized me to narrate from him: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, al-Rabīʿ informed us, and said: Al-Shāfiʿī said in the book Adab al-Qāḍī: \…Except that among them there may be one who is known to deem lawful the giving of false testimony against a man because he considers his blood lawful or his wealth lawful — so his testimony is rejected on account of falsehood. Or among them there may be one who deems lawful or sees that one may testify for a man if he trusts him"," so he swears an oath for him regarding his right and testifies for him categorically"," though he was not present and did not hear it — so his testimony is rejected on account of his deeming false testimony lawful. Or among them there may be one who opposes a man who differs from him with the opposition of enmity towards him — so his testimony is rejected on account of enmity.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"20911","(20905) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, he said: I heard Abū Turāb saying: I heard Muḥammad ibn al-Mundhir saying: I heard Abū Ḥātim al-Rāzī saying: I heard Ḥarmalah saying: I heard al-Shāfiʿī saying: \I have not seen anyone more ready to bear false witness than the Rāfiḍah.\"" Others besides Ḥarmalah also narrated it. [Weak]"""
"20912","(20906) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥusayn ibn Muḥammad ibn Finjawayh al-Dīnawarī informed us at Dāmaghān, ʿAbdullāh ibn Muḥammad ibn Shanbah narrated to us, Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Karābīsī narrated to us, Abū Ḥātim al-Rāzī said: I heard Yūnus ibn ʿAbd al-Aʿlá saying: I heard al-Shāfiʿī saying: \The testimony of all the people of whims is accepted except that of the Rāfiḍah"," for they bear witness for one another.\"" The Shaykh"," may Allah have mercy on him"," said: \""Likewise"," the testimony of anyone among them who is known to revile the Companions — who are the lanterns of this Ummah and its vanguard — shall not be accepted so long as his reviling of them is out of partisanship or ignorance"," and not on the basis of an interpretation or a doubt.\"" [Authentic]"""
"20913","(20907) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh ibn ʿAttāb al-ʿAbdī in Baghdād, Abū al-Faḍl al-Ḥasan ibn Yaʿqūb al-ʿAdl in Naysābūr, and Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī al-Shaybānī in Kūfah informed us, all saying: Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbdillāh al-ʿAbsī narrated to us, Wakīʿ narrated from al-Aʿmash from Abū Ṣāliḥ from Abū Saʿīd, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Do not revile my Companions. By the One in Whose Hand is my soul"," if any one of you were to spend the mountain of Uḥud in gold"," it would not equal a mudd spent by one of them"," nor even half of it.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū Kurayb and others from Wakīʿ. [Authentic — Agreed Upon]"""
"20914","(20908) ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us, Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us, Abū Muslim narrated to us, Sulaymān — i.e., ibn Ḥarb — narrated to us, Shuʿbah narrated from Manṣūr, who said: I heard Abū Wāʾil narrating from ʿAbdullāh from the Prophet ﷺ, who said: \Reviling a Muslim is sinful disobedience (fusūq)"," and fighting him is disbelief (kufr).\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Sulaymān ibn Ḥarb"," and Muslim narrated it through another chain from Shuʿbah. [Authentic — Agreed Upon]"""
"20915","(20909) Abū Saʿd al-Mālinī informed us, Abū Aḥmad ibn ʿAdī al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAlī ibn al-Jārūd narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Būshanjī narrated to us, Yaʿqūb ibn Isḥāq narrated to us, ʿAbdullāh ibn Sawwār al-ʿAnbarī said: \A man came to my father to give testimony"," and he rejected his testimony. The man later came back and said: 'You rejected my testimony?' He said: 'Yes.' The man said: 'Why?' He said: 'Because it has reached me that you speak ill of or harbour hatred towards the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ.' The man said: 'I only speak ill of ʿAmr ibn al-ʿĀṣ.' He said: 'Indeed"," I shall add to your imprisonment until you repent.'\"" [Weak]"""
"20916","(20910) Abū ʿAmr Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Bisṭāmī informed us, Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī informed us, Abū Yaʿlá narrated to us, Abū al-Rabīʿ narrated to us, Ḥammād narrated to us, Thābit narrated — (ḥ) and Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī informed us, Abū Bakr al-Marwazī informed us, Khalaf ibn Hishām narrated to us, Ḥammād narrated from Thābit from Anas: \A funeral procession passed by the Prophet ﷺ and the deceased was praised with good words. The Prophet ﷺ said: 'It has become obligatory (i.e."," Paradise).' Then another funeral procession passed by and the deceased was praised with bad words. The Prophet ﷺ said: 'It has become obligatory.' It was said: 'O Messenger of Allah"," you said \""It has become obligatory\"" for that one and you said \""It has become obligatory\"" for this one.' He said: 'The testimony of the people — the believers are the witnesses of Allah upon the earth.'\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū al-Rabīʿ"," and al-Bukhārī narrated it from Sulaymān ibn Ḥarb from Ḥammād ibn Zayd. We have also narrated from the Prophet ﷺ that he said: \""The religion is sincerity (naṣīḥah).\"" [Authentic — Agreed Upon]"""
"20917","(20911) Abū Saʿd al-Mālinī informed us, Abū Aḥmad ibn ʿAdī al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, ʿAbdullāh ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz narrated to us, Abū al-Rabīʿ al-Zahrānī narrated to us, Ḥammād ibn Zayd narrated from Baqiyyah ibn al-Walīd from Muʿādh ibn Rifāʿah from Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-ʿAdhrī, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \This knowledge will be inherited by the upright among every generation; they will ward off from it the misinterpretations of the ignorant"," the fabrications of the falsifiers"," and the distortions of the extremists.\"" [Weak]"""
"20918","(20912) Abū Saʿd al-Mālinī informed us, Abū Aḥmad ibn ʿAdī informed us, al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān narrated to us, Ibrāhīm — meaning ibn Ayyūb al-Dimashqī — narrated to us, al-Walīd — meaning ibn Muslim — narrated to us, Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān narrated to us, a trustworthy one among our shaykhs said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said something similar to it. [Weak — preceded before it]"
"20919","(20913) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Muqriʾ informed us, al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq informed us, Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb al-Qāḍī narrated to us, Sulaymān ibn Ḥarb narrated to us, Ḥammād ibn Zayd narrated from Ayyūb from Muḥammad from ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUtbah: \Subayʿah bint al-Ḥārith gave birth fifteen days after the death of her husband. Abū al-Sanābil passed by her and said: 'It seems as though you wish to remarry.' She said: 'Yes","' or as she said. He said: 'Not until four months and ten days have passed.' She came to the Prophet ﷺ and mentioned that to him. He said: 'Abū al-Sanābil has erred. When someone suitable comes to you"," inform me.'\""\n\nThis is a good mursal hadith"," and it has corroborating narrations. We have narrated from a number of the Companions and the Tābiʿīn clarification regarding the condition of one from whom something necessitating the rejection of his report is found"," though this is not the place for it. However"," al-Shāfiʿī"," may Allah have mercy on him"," included this issue within the discussion of the testimony of the people of whims"," so we have pointed to some of its evidences. And success is through Allah. [Authentic — Aḥmad 4261]"""
"20920","(20914) As for the hadith: Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū ʿAbdillāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū al-Ṭayyib Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Shaʿīrī both said: Abū Shujaʿ Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaydalānī narrated to us, al-Jārūd ibn Yazīd narrated from Bahz ibn Ḥakīm from his father from his grandfather, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Do you refrain from mentioning the wicked person? Mention him for what he is"," so that the people may know him and beware of him.\""\n\nThis hadith is known through al-Jārūd ibn Yazīd al-Naysābūrī"," and the scholars of hadith rejected it. I heard Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ say: I heard Abū ʿAbdillāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb al-Ḥāfiẓ say more than once: \""Abū Bakr al-Jārūdī"," when he would pass by the grave of his grandfather in the cemetery of al-Ḥusayn ibn Muʿādh"," would say: 'O father"," had you not narrated the hadith of Bahz ibn Ḥakīm"," I would have visited you.'\"" The Shaykh said: \""A group of weak narrators stole it from him and narrated it from Bahz ibn Ḥakīm"," and nothing authentic has been established regarding it.\"" [Weak]"""
"20921","(20915) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yaḥyā ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār al-Sukkārī informed us in Baghdad, he said: it was read to Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad ibn Ismāʿīl al-Ṣaffār while I was listening, he said: ʿAbbās ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Tarqafī narrated to us, he said: Dāwūd ibn al-Jarrāḥ, Abū ʿIṣām al-ʿAsqalānī narrated to us, he said: Abū Saʿd al-Sāʿidī narrated to us from Anas ibn Mālik, he said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Whoever casts off the garment of modesty"," there is no backbiting against him.\"" And this narration is not strong. And Allah knows best."""
"20922","(20916) Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī informed us, he said: Abū Sahl ibn Ziyād al-Qaṭṭān narrated to us, he said: ʿAbd al-Karīm ibn al-Haytham narrated to us, he said: Abū al-Yamān narrated to us — (ḥ) And Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān informed us, he said: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿf ibn Durustawayh narrated to us, he said: Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān narrated to us, he said: Abū al-Yamān informed me, from Shuʿayb, from al-Zuhrī — (ḥ) he said: and Ḥajjāj, meaning Ibn Abī Manīʿ, narrated to us, he said: my grandfather narrated to us from al-Zuhrī, he said: Abū Idrīs, ʿĀʾidh Allāh ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Khawlānī informed him, that Yazīd ibn ʿAmīrah, a companion of Muʿādh, informed him: that Muʿādh, may Allah be pleased with him, used to say whenever he sat in a gathering of remembrance of Allah — \A just judge\"" — and Abū al-Yamān said: \""Qusṭ — blessed is His name — the doubters perish.\"" Then Muʿādh ibn Jabal said one day in a gathering he sat in: \""Behind you are tribulations in which wealth shall abound and the Qurʾān shall be recited"," until the believer and the hypocrite"," the free and the slave"," the man and the woman"," the old and the young all take their share. Soon someone will say: 'Why do not the people follow me"," when I have recite the Qurʾān?' By Allah"," they shall not follow me until I innovate something else for them. Beware of what is innovated"," for what is innovated is misguidance. And beware the deviation of the wise"," for verily the Satan may utter a word of misguidance on the lips of the wise"," and the hypocrite may utter a word of truth.\"" He (the narrator) said: I said to him: \""What would make me know"," may Allah have mercy on you"," that the wise man utters a word of misguidance and the hypocrite utters a word of truth?\"" He said: \""Avoid the ambiguous speech of the wise man when he says: 'What is this?' And let not that divert you from him"," for perhaps he will retract and speak the truth when he hears it"," for upon the truth there is light.\"" And in the narration of al-Qāḍī: \""and let not that divert you from him.\""\n\nAnd ʿUqayl narrated it from al-Zuhrī"," and said in the hadith: \""and let not that divert you from him.\""\n\nMuʿādh ibn Jabal informed that the deviation of the wise man does not necessitate turning away from him; rather"," that which has no light is abandoned from his speech — for upon the truth there is light — meaning"," and Allah knows best"," evidence from a Book"," or a Sunnah"," or consensus (ijmāʿ)"," or analogy (qiyāṣ) upon some of this. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"20923","(20917) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us, he said: Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us, he said: Tamtām narrated to us, he said: Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Musayyibī narrated to us, he said: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Nāfiʿ narrated to us from Kathīr ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAmr ibn ʿAwf, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Beware of the slip of the scholar and await his return.\""\n\nAnd likewise Maʿn ibn ʿĪsā narrated it from Kathīr. [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"20924","(20918) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us in a similar manner, he said: I heard Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb saying: I heard al-ʿAbbās ibn al-Walīd saying: I heard Muḥammad ibn Shuʿayb ibn Shābūr saying: I heard al-Awzāʿī saying: \Whoever takes hold of the anomalous opinions of the scholars has departed from Islam.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ from al-Awzāʿī]"""
"20925","(20919) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū ʿAbd Allāh Isḥāq ibn Muḥammad al-Sūsī both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, he said: Aḥmad ibn ʿĪsā al-Tinnīsī narrated to us, he said: ʿAmr ibn Abī Salamah said: I heard al-Awzāʿī saying: \That which is abandoned from the people of Makkah is temporary marriage (mutʿah) and currency exchange (ṣarf); from the people of Madīnah: listening to musical instruments (samāʿ) and approaching women from their behinds; from the people of Shām: predestination (jabr) and obedience (ṭāʿah); and from the people of Kūfah: nabīdh and suḥūr.\"" [Ḥasan li-ghayrihi]"""
"20926","(20920) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Bakr al-Qāḍī both informed us, they said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, he said: al-ʿAbbās ibn al-Walīd ibn Mazīd al-Bayrūtī narrated to me, he said: Abū ʿAbd Allāh Minbaj Ḥawrān narrated to me, he said: I heard al-Awzāʿī, may Allah have mercy on him, saying: \We avoid — or we abandon — five things from the people of Iraq and five from the people of the Ḥijāz. From the people of Iraq: drinking intoxicants"," eating at the time of dawn in Ramaḍān"," the Jumuʿah prayer being held only in seven cities"," delaying the ʿAṣr prayer until the shadow of every thing is four times its length"," and fleeing on the day of battle (yawm al-zaḥf). And from the people of the Ḥijāz: listening to musical entertainment (malāhī)"," combining two prayers without a valid excuse"," temporary marriage with women"," one dirhams for two dirhams and one dīnār for two dīnārs hand to hand"," and approaching women from their behinds.\"" [Ḥasan li-ghayrihi]"""
"20927","(20921) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, he said: I heard Abū al-Walīd saying: I heard Abū al-ʿAbbās ibn Surayj saying: I heard Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq al-Qāḍī saying: I entered upon al-Muʿtaḍid and he handed me a book which I examined. It had been compiled for him as concessions (rukhaṣ) from the slips of the scholars, and the arguments each of them used to justify themselves. I said to him: \O Commander of the Faithful"," the compiler of this book is a heretic (zindīq).\"" He said: \""These hadiths are not authentic.\"" I said: \""The hadiths are as they have been reported"," but whoever permits intoxicants does not permit temporary marriage"," and whoever permits temporary marriage does not permit singing and intoxicants. And there is no scholar but that he has a slip. Whoever gathers the slips of the scholars and then takes them as his own"," his religion is lost.\"" Then al-Muʿtaḍid ordered"," and that book was burned. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"20928","(20922) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, he said: I heard Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb saying: I heard al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān saying: I heard al-Shāfiʿī saying: \Saʿīd ibn Jubayr used to play chess from behind his back"," saying: 'With what did he push such-and-such? He said such-and-such. Push with such-and-such.'\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"20929","(20923) Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī informed us, he said: al-Ḥasan ibn Rashīq narrated to us by way of authorization (ijāzah), he said: Muḥammad ibn al-Rabīʿ narrated to us, he said: Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥakam informed us, he said: al-Shāfiʿī said: \Muḥammad ibn Sīrīn and Hishām ibn ʿUrwah used to play chess in concealment (istidbāran).\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"20930","(20924) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bushrān informed us in Baghdad, he said: Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār narrated to us, he said: Aḥmad ibn Manṣūr narrated to us, he said: ʿAbd al-Razzāq said: Maʿmar informed me, he said: \Al-Shaʿbī used to play chess"," wear a woman's wrap (milḥafah)"," and let his hair hang loose"," and that was because he was concealing himself from al-Ḥajjāj.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"20931","(20925) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq informed us that Abū Muslim informed us that Maʿqil ibn Mālik al-Bāhilī said: I came out of the congregational mosque, and suddenly a man had a mount brought before him. A man asked him: \What did al-Ḥasan say about chess?\"" He replied: \""He used to see no harm in it"," but he used to dislike backgammon.\"" I asked: \""Who is this?\"" They said: \""Ibn ʿAwn.\"" He used to have his teeth overlaid with gold. [Ḥasan]"""
"20932","(20926) Abū Saʿd al-Mālinī informed us that Abū Aḥmad ibn ʿAdī informed us that Muḥammad ibn Ismāʿīl al-ʿAṭṭār informed us that al-Qāsim ibn Muḥammad al-Salāmānī informed us that Yaḥyā ibn Sulaymān al-Juʿfī informed us that Aḥmad ibn Bashīr said: I went to Baṣra in search of hadith, and I came to Bahz ibn Ḥakīm. I found him among a group of people who were playing chess. [Ḍaʿīf]"
"20933","(20927) Abū Saʿd informed us that Abū Aḥmad informed us that Zakariyyā al-Sājī informed me that Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad informed us that al-Ramādī said: I heard Sufyān say: \I saw Ibrāhīm al-Hajarī"," and he used to play chess.\""\n\nAl-Shāfiʿī"," may Allah have mercy on him"," considered playing chess to be among the disputed matters"," in that it does not necessitate the rejection of testimony. As for the dislike of playing it"," he explicitly stated that in what we have previously mentioned"," and that is more consistent and more appropriate to his madhhab. Those who disliked it are more numerous"," and with them are those whose statements constitute evidence. And with Allah lies success. [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"20934","(20928) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us that al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān narrated to us that Ibn Wahb narrated to us that Sulaymān ibn Bilāl narrated to us from Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad from his father from ʿAlī, may Allah be pleased with him, that he used to say: \Chess is the gambling of the non-Arabs (al-aʿājim).\""\n\nThis is a mursal narration"," but it has corroborating chains. [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"20935","(20929) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bushrān informed us in Baghdād that Abū ʿAlī al-Ḥusayn ibn Ṣafwān narrated to us that ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad ibn Abī al-Dunyā narrated to us that Ziyād ibn Ayyūb narrated that Shabābah ibn Sawwār narrated from Fuḍayl ibn Marzūq from Maysarah ibn Ḥabīb who said: ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib, may Allah be pleased with him, passed by a group of people who were playing chess, and he said: \What are these images to which you are devoted?\"" (Sūrat al-Anbiyāʾ"," 52). [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"20936","(20930) Abū al-Ḥusayn informed us that al-Ḥusayn narrated to us that ʿAbd Allāh narrated to us that ʿAlī ibn al-Jaʿd narrated to us that Abū Muʿāwiyah narrated to us that Saʿd ibn Ṭarīf narrated from al-Aṣbagh ibn Nubātah from ʿAlī, may Allah be pleased with him, that he passed by a group of people playing chess and said: \What are these images to which you are devoted?\"" (Sūrat al-Anbiyāʾ"," 52). \""That one should touch burning coals until they extinguish is better for him than that he should touch it.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"20937","(20931) He said: And ʿAlī ibn al-Jaʿd narrated to us that Sharīk narrated to us from Ibn Abī Laylā from al-Ḥakam who said: ʿAlī, may Allah be pleased with him, said: \The chess player is the most lying of people; one of them says"," 'I killed","' when he has not killed.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"20938","(20932) Abū al-Ḥusayn informed us that al-Ḥusayn narrated to us that ʿAbd Allāh narrated to us that Ibrāhīm ibn Rāshid, Abū Isḥāq, narrated to us that al-Qaʿnabī narrated to us that Marwān ibn Muʿāwiyah narrated from Muḥammad ibn Abī Zakariyyā from ʿAmmār ibn Abī ʿAmmār who said: ʿAlī, may Allah be pleased with him, passed by an assembly of the Banū Taym Allāh while they were playing chess. He stopped before them and said: \By Allah"," you were not created for anything other than this! By Allah"," were it not that it might become a Sunnah"," I would strike your faces with it.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"20939","(20933) Abū al-Ḥusayn informed us that al-Ḥusayn narrated to us that ʿAbd Allāh narrated to us that Isḥāq ibn al-Buhlūl narrated to us. He said: I heard Maʿn ibn ʿĪsā say: Mālik said: \Chess is a form of backgammon. It has reached us that Ibn ʿAbbās"," when he was appointed guardian of an orphan's property"," burned it.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"20940","(20934) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Muḥammad ibn Ṣāliḥ narrated to us that Aḥmad ibn Salamah narrated to me that Jaʿfar ibn Munīr al-Qaṭṭān al-Madāʾinī, the righteous man, narrated to us that Abū Badr Shujaʿ ibn al-Walīd narrated to us that ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿUmar narrated from Nāfiʿ from Ibn ʿUmar that he was asked about chess, and he said: \It is worse than backgammon.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"20941","(20935) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq narrated to us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Baḥr ibn Naṣr narrated to us: Ibn Wahb narrated to us: Yūnus ibn Yazīd informed me, from Ibn Shihāb, that Abū Mūsā al-Ashʿarī said: \None plays chess except a sinner.\"" [Weak]"""
"20942","(20936) And Abū Zakariyyā narrated to us: Abū al-ʿAbbās narrated to us: Baḥr narrated to us: Ibn Wahb narrated to us: Layth ibn Saʿd informed me, from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Abī Jaʿfar, who said: ʿĀʾishah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, used to dislike backgammon (al-kubl), even if no wager was placed upon it; and Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī used to dislike chess being played. [Weak]"
"20943","(20937) And Abū Zakariyyā narrated to us: Abū al-ʿAbbās narrated to us: Baḥr narrated to us: Ibn Wahb narrated to me: ʿAbd al-Jabbār ibn ʿUmar informed me, from Ṣāliḥ ibn Abī Yazīd, who said: I asked Ibn al-Musayyab about chess, and he said: \It is falsehood (bāṭil)"," and Allah does not love falsehood.\"" [Weak]"""
"20944","(20938) And Abū Zakariyyā narrated to us: Abū al-ʿAbbās narrated to us: Baḥr narrated to us: Ibn Wahb narrated to me: Yaḥyā ibn Ayyūb informed me, from ʿUqayl, from Ibn Shihāb, that he was asked about the playing of chess, and he said: \It is of falsehood"," and I do not love it.\"" [Sound]"""
"20945","(20939) And through its chain of narration: Ibn Wahb narrated to us: Muʿāwiyah ibn Ṣāliḥ informed me, from Ibrāhīm ibn Isḥāq, that he asked Ibn Shihāb about chess, and he said: \It is of falsehood"," and Allah does not love falsehood.\"" [Sound]"""
"20946","(20940) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān informed us: Ḥusayn ibn Ṣafwān narrated to us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad ibn Abī al-Dunyā narrated to us: Khalaf ibn Hishām narrated to us: Abū Shihāb narrated to us, from Ismāʿīl, who said: Abū Jaʿfar was asked about chess, and he said: \Leave us away from this Magian practice (al-majūsiyyah).\""\n\nAnd reports have been transmitted regarding the dislike of playing it from Yazīd Abī ibn Ḥabīb"," Muḥammad ibn Sīrīn"," Ibrāhīm al-Nakhaʿī"," and Mālik ibn Anas. [Weak]"""
"20947","(20941) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us: Muḥammad ibn Bakr narrated to us: Abū Dāwūd narrated to us: Mūsā ibn Ismāʿīl narrated to us: Ḥammād narrated to us, from Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr, from Abū Salamah, from Abū Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw a man following a pigeon and said: \A devil following a she-devil.\"" [Weak]"""
"20948","(20942) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us: Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār narrated to us: Saʿdān ibn Naṣr narrated to us: Rūḥ ibn ʿĀbidah informed us, from Usāmah ibn Zayd, who said: I witnessed ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ordering that racing pigeons be slaughtered, while the clipped ones be left alone. [Sound]"
"20949","(20943) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān informed us in Baghdad: Ḥamzah ibn Muḥammad ibn al-ʿAbbās narrated to us: Ibrāhīm ibn Danūqā narrated to us: Zakariyyā ibn Abī ʿAdī narrated to us: ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿAmr narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us: Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad al-Sawṭī and ʿAbbās al-Faḍl both said: Jandal ibn Wāliq narrated to us: ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿAmr al-Raqqī narrated to us, from ʿAbd al-Karīm, from Qays ibn Ḥabṭar, from Ibn ʿAbbās, may Allah be pleased with both of them, from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, who said: \Indeed"," Allah has forbidden you wine (khamr)"," gambling (maysir)"," and the kūbah.\"" And he said: \""Every intoxicant is forbidden (ḥarām).\"" [Sound. Al-Sijistānī narrated it as 3692]"""
"20950","(20944) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzakkī narrated to us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Baḥr ibn Naṣr narrated to us: Ibn Wahb narrated to me: Yaʿqūb ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān and ʿIyāḍ ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Fihrī informed me, from Mūsā ibn ʿUqbah, from Nāfiʿ, that Ibn ʿUmar used to say: \Al-Maysir is gambling (qimār).\"" [Weak]"""
"20951","(20945) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī narrated to us, that Ibrāhīm ibn al-Ḥusayn narrated to us, that Ādam narrated to us, that Warqāʾ narrated from Ibn Abī Najīḥ, from Mujāhid, regarding His (Exalted is He) words, \al-maysir\"" — he said: \""It is the dice of the Persians"," the arrows of the Arabs"," and all forms of gambling.\"" [Weak]"""
"20952","(20946) And Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bushrān informed us that Ismāʿīl al-Ṣaffār narrated to us, that Aḥmad ibn Manṣūr narrated to us, that ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us, that Maʿmar narrated from Layth, from Mujāhid, who said: \Al-maysir refers to all forms of gambling"," even the walnut-shell with which children play.\"" [Weak]"""
"20953","(20947) Abū al-Fatḥ Hilāl ibn Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar al-Ḥaffār informed us that al-Ḥusayn ibn Yaḥyā ibn ʿAyyāsh al-Qaṭṭān narrated to us, that Yaḥyā ibn al-Sarī narrated to us, that Jarīr narrated from Misʿar, from Abī ʿAwn, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Shaddād, who said: Ibn ʿAbbās said: \Wine (al-khamr) is forbidden in its entirety — its small quantity and its large quantity — and intoxication (al-sakr) is present in every intoxicating drink. From this and what resembles it arose the doubt of the one who permitted the small quantity of other beverages. As for us"," we do not permit any of it when its large quantity causes intoxication"," because of what we have narrated from Saʿd ibn Abī Waqqāṣ"," Ibn ʿUmar"," and others"," from the Prophet ﷺ: 'I forbid you from that whose large quantity intoxicates"," even in small quantity.' And he said: 'That whose large quantity intoxicates"," its small quantity is unlawful.' And he said: 'Every intoxicant is wine (khamr)"," and every intoxicant is unlawful.'\""\n\nAnd we have narrated in this ḥadīth of Ibn ʿAbbās that he said: \""And the intoxicant (muskir) is present in every drink.\"" [Authentic]"""
"20954","(20948) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān informed us in Baghdād that Abū Sahl ibn Ziyād al-Qaṭṭān narrated to us, that Isḥāq ibn al-Ḥasan al-Ḥarbī narrated to us, that ʿAffān narrated to us, that Ḥammād ibn Salamah narrated to us, that Simāk ibn Ḥarb narrated from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Shaddād ibn al-Hād, from Ibn ʿUmar, who said: \I was with ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāx (may Allah be pleased with him) during a Ḥajj or an ʿUmrah"," and we were riding when we saw a rider. ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: 'I think he is seeking us.' The man came and began to weep. ʿUmar said: 'What is the matter with you? If you are in debt"," we will assist you; if you are afraid"," we will grant you safety — unless you have committed a murder"," in which case you will be executed for it; or if you dislike the neighbourhood of a people"," we will relocate you from among them.' The man said: 'I have drunk wine"," and I am one of Banū Taym. Abū Mūsā flogged me"," shaved my head"," blackened my face"," paraded me among the people"," and said: \""Do not sit with him and do not eat with him.\"" So I considered three courses of action: either to take a sword and strike Abū Mūsā with it; or to come to you so that you might relocate me to Shām"," for they do not know me there; or to join the enemy and eat and drink with them.' ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) wept and said: 'It does not please me that you did that"," and indeed ʿUmar had such-and-such [to his credit]. I used to serve people with wine in the Jāhiliyyah"," and it is not like zinā (fornication).' And he wrote to Abū Mūsā: 'Peace be upon you. To proceed: So-and-so ibn so-and-so al-Taymī has informed me of such-and such. By Allah"," if you repeat this"," I shall blacken your face and parade you among the people. If you wish to know the truth of what I say to you"," then command the people to sit with him and eat with him. If he repents"," accept his testimony"," and give him two hundred dirhams.'\""\n\nʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) reported that the testimony of the one who drinks wine is invalidated"," and that if he repents"," his testimony is then accepted.\n\nAl-Shāfiʿī (may Allah have mercy upon him) said: \""The seller of wine has his testimony rejected"," because there is no disagreement among any of the Muslims that its sale is forbidden.\""\n\nAl-Shaykh said: \""The evidence for the prohibition of its sale"," along with the consensus (ijmāʿ)"," has been presented in the Book of Sales.\"" [Weak]"""
"20955","(20949) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf al-Aṣbahānī informed us that Abū Saʿīd ibn al-Aʿrābī narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī and Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bushrān informed us, saying: Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār narrated to us, saying: Saʿdān ibn Naṣr narrated to us, that Isḥāq ibn Yūsuf narrated to us, that Sufyān al-Thawrī narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bushrān informed us that al-Ḥusayn ibn Ṣafwān informed us that Ibn Abī al-Dunyā narrated to us that Abū Khaythamah narrated to us that ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Mahdī narrated from Sufyān, from ʿAlqamah ibn Murthad, from Sulaymān ibn Buraydah, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Whoever plays nardashīr (backgammon) is like one who plunges his hand into the flesh and blood of a pig.\""\n\nThe wording of the ḥadīth is that of Isḥāq. And in the narration of ʿAbd al-Raḥmān: \""The Prophet ﷺ said: 'Whoever plays nardashīr is as if he has dyed his hand in the flesh of a pig and its blood.'\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū Khaythamah Zuhayr ibn Ḥarb. [Authentic. Muslim 2660]"""
"20956","(20950) Abū Aḥmad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Mihrajānī informed us that Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar al-Muzakkī narrated to us, that Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-ʿAbdī narrated to us, that Ibn Bukayr narrated to us, that Mālik narrated from Mūsā ibn Maysarah, from Saʿīd ibn Abī Hind, from Abū Mūsā al-Ashʿarī, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Whoever plays nard (dice/backgammon) has disobeyed Allah and His Messenger.\""\n\nAnd likewise Yazīd ibn al-Hād and Usāmah ibn Zayd narrated it from Saʿīd ibn Abī Hind. [Weak]"""
"20957","(20951) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Muḥammad ibn Abī Ḥāmid al-Muqrīʾ narrated to us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, that al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn ʿAffān narrated to us, that Muḥammad ibn ʿUbayd narrated from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿUmar, from Nāfiʿ, from Saʿīd ibn Abī Hind, from Abū Mūsā al-Ashʿarī, who said: The Prophet ﷺ said: \Whoever plays nard (dice/backgammon) has disobeyed Allah and His Messenger.\""\n\nAnd likewise Yaḥyā al-Qaṭṭān narrated it from ʿUbayd Allāh"," and Ayyūb al-Sakhtiyānī narrated it from Nāfiʿ"," from Saʿīd"," from Abū Mūsā"," as his own statement (mawqūf)"," not raised (to the Prophet). And there was disagreement regarding it from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Saʿīd ibn Abī Hind. It was narrated from him"," from his father"," from a man"," from Abū Mūsā"," from the Prophet ﷺ"," concerning al-kʿāb (dice). And it was also narrated from him"," from Abū Mūsā"," in a manner similar to the narration of the majority"," and this is more appropriate. [Weak. Preceded before it.]"""
"20958","(20952) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bushrān informed us in Baghdād that al-Ḥusayn ibn Ṣafwān narrated to us that ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad ibn Abī al-Dunyā narrated to us, that Abū Khaythamah narrated to us, that Makkī ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us, that al-Juʿayd narrated from Yazīd ibn Khuṣayfah, from Ḥumayd ibn Bashīr, from Muḥammad ibn Kaʿb, who said: Abū Mūsā al-Ashʿarī (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated to me that he heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \No one turns over its cubes waiting for what they will bring except that he has disobeyed Allah and His Messenger.\"" [Weak]"""
"20959","(20953) Abū al-Fatḥ Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Abī al-Fawāris al-Ḥāfiẓ (may Allah have mercy upon him) informed us in Baghdād that Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Ismāʿīlī narrated to us, that Ibrāhīm ibn Zuhayr al-Ḥulwānī narrated to us, that Makkī ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us, that al-Juʿayd ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān narrated from Mūsā ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, meaning al-Khaṭmī, that he heard Muḥammad ibn Kaʿb, while he was asking ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, say: \Tell me what you heard your father say from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\"" ʿAbd al-Raḥmān said: \""I heard my father say: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'The likeness of the one who plays nard (backgammon) and then stands to pray is like the one who performs wuḍūʾ with pus and the blood of a pig"," and then stands to pray.'\"" [Weak]"""
"20960","(20954) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bushrān informed us that al-Ḥusayn ibn Ṣafwān narrated to us that Ibn Abī al-Dunyā narrated to us, that Ziyād ibn Ayyūb narrated to us, that Ziyād ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Bakkāʾī narrated to us, that Ibrāhīm ibn Muslim narrated from Abī al-Aḥwaṣ, from ʿAbd Allāh, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Beware of these two marked dice (al-kʿabatayn) which are cast with a rattling sound"," for they are from the maysir (gambling) of the non-Arabs (ʿajam).\""\n\nAl-Bakkāʾī raised it from Ibrāhīm"," and Sawayd narrated from Abī Muʿāwiyah"," from Ibrāhīm. [Weak]"""
"20961","(20955) The preserved narration is a mawqūf report. Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq informed us that Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Shaybānī informed us that Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Wahhāb informed us that Jaʿfar ibn ʿAwn informed us that Ibrāhīm al-Hajarī informed us from Abū al-Aḥwaṣ from ʿAbd Allāh who said: \Beware of these two marked types of nard (backgammon) which are only rebuked with a stern rebuke"," for indeed they are the gambling of the non-Arabs (ʿajam).\""\n\nAnd likewise ʿAbd al-Malik ibn ʿUmayr and others narrated it from Abū al-Aḥwaṣ from Ibn Masʿūd as a mawqūf report. [Weak. Referred to previously.]"""
"20962","(20956) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us, both saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān narrated to us, ʿAbd Allāh ibn Wahb informed us, Sulaymān ibn Bilāl informed us, al-Juʿayd narrated to me from Mūsā from Abū Suhayl from Zuyayd ibn al-Ṣalt that he heard ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān (may Allah be pleased with him) saying while upon the minbar: \O people"," beware of al-maysir","\"" meaning nard (backgammon). \""It has been mentioned to me that it is in the houses of some among you. So whoever has it in his house"," let him burn it or break it.\"" ʿUthmān (may Allah be pleased with him) said another time while upon the minbar: \""O people"," I have already spoken to you about this nard"," yet I do not see that you have removed it. I have resolved to order bundles of firewood to be gathered and then sent to the houses of those in whose houses it is"," and to burn it upon them.\"" [Weak]"""
"20963","(20957) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq narrated to us, Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, Baḥr ibn Naṣr narrated to us, Ibn Wahb informed us, Muʿāwiya ibn Ṣāliḥ informed me from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd from Nāfiʿ that ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar used to say: \Nard (backgammon) is al-maysir (gambling).\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"20964","(20958) Abū Zakariyyā narrated to us, Abū al-ʿAbbās narrated to us, Baḥr narrated to us, Ibn Wahb informed me, Yūnus ibn Yazīd informed me from Nāfiʿ that Ibn ʿUmar, whenever he found it (nard) with any member of his household, he ordered it to be broken and struck the person. Then he ordered it to be burned with fire. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"20965","(20959) Abū Aḥmad al-Mihrajānī informed us, Abū Bakr ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us, Ibn Bukayr narrated to us, Mālik informed us from Nāfiʿ from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar that whenever he found any member of his household playing with nard (backgammon), he would strike him and break it. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"20966","(20960) And with his chain of narration, Mālik narrated from ʿAlqama ibn Abī ʿAlqama from his mother from ʿĀʾishah, the wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), that it reached her that the people of a house in her dwelling, who were tenants therein, had nard (backgammon). So she sent to them: \If you do not remove it"," I will surely expel you from my house.\"" And she denounced that upon them. [Ḥasan]"""
"20967","(20961) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān informed us, al-Ḥusayn ibn Ṣafwān narrated to us, Ibn Abī al-Dunyā narrated to us, ʿAlī ibn al-Jaʿd narrated to us, Salām ibn Miskīn narrated to us, Qatādah narrated from Abū Ayyūb from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAmr who said: \The one who plays nard (backgammon) with gambling is like the one who eats the flesh of swine"," and the one who plays it without gambling is like the one who anoints himself with the fat of swine.\""\n\nAnd it was also narrated by ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb from his father from his grandfather as a mawqūf report. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"20968","(20962) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us, Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ṣaffār narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Ghālib narrated to us, Muslim ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us, Rabīʿah ibn Kulthūm narrated to me, my father said: \Ibn al-Zubayr addressed us in Makkah and said: 'O people of Makkah"," it has reached me that men among the Quraysh play a game called Nardashīr (backgammon). Indeed"," Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic"," says in His Book: {O you who believe"," indeed wine"," gambling (al-maysir)"," stone altars (al-anṣāb)"," and divining arrows (al-azlām) are but abomination from the work of Satan"," so avoid them} [al-Māʾidah 90] — the entire verse. And I swear by Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic"," that no man who plays this game shall be brought to me except that I shall punish him upon his hair and his skin"," and I shall give his spoils to whoever brings him to me.'\"" [Ḥasan]"""
"20969","(20963) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān informed us, al-Ḥusayn ibn Ṣafwān narrated to us, Ibn Abī al-Dunyā narrated to us, Bishr ibn Muʿādh al-ʿAqadī informed us, ʿĀmir ibn Yassāf informed us from Yaḥyā ibn Abī Kathīr who said: \The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) passed by a people who were playing nard (backgammon) and said: 'Hearts that are heedless"," hands that are active"," and tongues that are engaged in idle talk.'\"" This is a mursal narration. [Weak]"""
"20970","(20964) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Maḥbūb the merchant in Marw narrated to us, Saʿīd ibn Masʿūd narrated to us, al-Naḍr ibn Shumayl informed us, Shuʿbah informed us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn al-Muthannā narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us, Shuʿbah narrated from ʿAbd al-Malik ibn ʿUmayr from Abū Salamah from Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \The truest verse spoken by the poets is: 'Indeed"," everything besides Allah is falsehood.'\"" This is the wording of al-Naḍr's narration. And in the narration of Ghundar"," it is from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him). Al-Bukhārī and Muslim narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn al-Muthannā. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Agreed upon.]"""
"20971","(20965) Abū al-Qāsim Zayd ibn Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad al-ʿAlawī informed us in Kūfah from the original of his hearing, that Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī ibn Duḥaym narrated to us, that Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn Abī al-Ḥunayn narrated to us, that Ibn al-Madīnī narrated to us, that Yaḥyā ibn Muḥammad ibn Qays from the people of Madīnah narrated, he said: I heard ʿAmr ibn Abī ʿAmr say: I heard Anas ibn Mālik say: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \I am not of falsehood"," falsehood is not of me.\"" ʿAlī ibn al-Madīnī said: I asked Abū ʿUbaydah"," the scholar of the Arabic language"," about this"," and he said: He means"," \""I am not of falsehood and falsehood is not of me.\""\n\nThe Shaykh said: And Abū ʿUbayd al-Qāsim ibn Sallām said: al-Dad means play and amusement.\n\nAnd it was narrated from ʿAmr"," from al-Muṭṭalib"," from Muʿāwiyah"," and that was reported in the ḥadīth of Abī al-Zubayr from Jābir. [Weak]"""
"20972","(20966) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq informed us, that Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, that Baḥr ibn Naṣr narrated to us, that Ibn Wahb narrated to us, that Yaḥyā ibn Ayyūb narrated to us, that Abū Qabīl narrated from ʿUqbah ibn ʿĀmir, who said: That I should worship an idol that was worshipped in the Jāhiliyyah is more beloved to me than that I should play with dhū al-maysir—or he said, al-qinnīn. He said: These are sticks with which one played on the ground. And I saw him in another place with dhū al-ʿasharah. [Good]"
"20973","(20967) He said: And Ibn Wahb narrated to us, that Ibn Lahīʿah informed me, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Hubayrah, from Ḥanash ibn ʿAbd Allāh, from Faḍālah ibn ʿUbayd, who said: It is all the same to me whether I play with al-kabl or perform wuḍūʾ with the blood of a pig and then stand for prayer. [Weak]"
"20974","(20968) He said: And Ibn Wahb narrated to us, that ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar informed me, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Dīnār, that Ibn ʿUmar passed by some boys playing with al-kujjah, which were holes containing wood with which they played. So Ibn ʿUmar filled them in and forbade them from it. He said: They were not reopened except after some time. [Weak]"
"20975","(20969) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān informed us, that al-Ḥusayn ibn Ṣafwān narrated to us, that ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad ibn Abī al-Dunyā narrated to us, that ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿUmar narrated to us, that Ḥammād ibn Zayd narrated from Ayyūb, from Nāfiʿ, from Ṣafiyyah, that Ibn ʿUmar entered upon some of his family while they were playing with this shahārdah, so he broke it. He said: And I heard Ḥammād once say: He broke it over his head. [Authentic]"
"20976","(20970) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān informed us, that Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār narrated to us, that Saʿdān ibn Naṣr narrated to us, that Isḥāq al-Azraq narrated, from Bassām ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ṣayrafī, who said: I asked Abū Jaʿfar about al-nardashīr (backgammon), and he disapproved of it and said: ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥusayn used to play with his family with al-shahārdah.\n\nImām al-Shāfiʿī (raḥimahullāh) said: Whoever plays with any of this while considering it permissible, his testimony is not rejected.\n\nThe Shaykh (raḥimahullāh) said: And this is due to the difference of opinion regarding it, or regarding some of it. [Authentic]"
"20977","(20971) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us, that Muḥammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, that Abū Dāwūd narrated to us, that al-Qaʿnabī narrated from Mālik, from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd, from Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā ibn Ḥabbān, from Ibn Muḥayrīz, that a man from Banī Kinānah called al-Makhdajī heard a man in Shām called Abū Muḥammad saying: \Indeed"," al-Witr is obligatory.\"" So al-Makhdajī set out to ʿUbadah ibn al-Ṣāmit and informed him. ʿUbadah said: \""Abū Muḥammad has lied. I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say: 'Five prayers has Allah ordained upon the servants. Whoever comes with them"," not neglecting anything of them out of disdain for their right"," he has with Allah a promise that He will admit him into Paradise. And whoever does not come with them"," he has no promise from Allah"," Mighty and Glorious—if He wills"," He will punish him"," and if He wills"," He will admit him into Paradise.'\"" [Weak]"""
"20978","(20972) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq informed us, that Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, that Baḥr ibn Naṣr narrated to us, that Ibn Wahb narrated to us, that Yaḥyā ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Sālim informed me, from Abī Salamah, who said: I asked al-Qāsim ibn Muḥammad: \What is al-maysir?\"" He said: \""Everything that distracts from the remembrance of Allah and from prayer—that is al-maysir.\"" [Authentic]"""
"20979","(20973) Yaḥyā said: And ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿUmar informed me that he heard ʿUmar ibn ʿUbayd Allāh saying to al-Qāsim ibn Muḥammad: \This nard (dice) is maysir. What is your opinion about al-shiṭranj (chess)—is it maysir?\"" Al-Qāsim said: \""Everything that distracts from the remembrance of Allah and from prayer—that is al-maysir.\"" [Authentic]"""
"20980","(20974) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān informed us, that al-Ḥusayn ibn Ṣafwān narrated to us, that ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad ibn Abī al-Dunyā narrated to us, that ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿUmar narrated to us, that Ḥammād ibn Zayd narrated from Ayyūb, from Nāfiʿ, from Ṣafiyyah, that Ibn ʿUmar entered upon some of his family while they were playing with this shahārdah, so he broke it. He said: And I heard Ḥammād once say: He broke it over his head.\n\nImām al-Shāfiʿī (raḥimahullāh) said: If one is so engrossed in it that he misses the prayer, repeatedly, until the time elapses, and then returns to it until the time elapses again, we reject his testimony on account of his belittling the appointed times of prayer. [Weak]"
"20981","(20975) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, al-ʿAbbās ibn al-Walīd, i.e. ibn Mazīd, informed me, my father narrated to us, Ibn Jābir narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān informed us in Baghdād, ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us, Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān narrated to us, ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUthmān and Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr both said: ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Mubārak narrated to us, ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Yazīd ibn Jābir narrated to me, Abū Salām narrated to me, Khālid ibn Zayd narrated: I was a man skilled in archery, and ʿUqbah ibn ʀmir would call me and say, \Come out"," O Khālid"," so that we may shoot.\"" One day I was slow in coming to him"," so he said"," \""Come"," I shall narrate to you what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ narrated to me","\"" or he said"," \""I shall tell you what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me.\"" He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \""Indeed"," Allah"," Mighty and Majestic"," will admit three persons into Paradise by virtue of a single arrow: its maker who intends goodness in its manufacture"," the one who shoots it"," and the one who hands it over. So shoot and ride"," and shooting is more beloved to me than riding. There is no pastime except three: a man training his horse"," his play with his wife"," and his shooting with his bow and arrows. And whoever abandons archery after having learned it"," out of aversion to it"," then it is a blessing he has shown ingratitude for.\""\n\nThe wording is from the ḥadīth of al-Walīd ibn Mazīd. [Weak]"""
"20982","(20976) Abū ʿAbdillāh the Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib informed us, ʿAbd al-Wahhāb ibn ʿAṭāʾ informed us, Hishām al-Dastuwāʾī narrated from Yaḥyā ibn Abī Kathīr, from Abū Salām, from ʿAbdullāh ibn Yazīd al-Zuraqī, that ʿUqbah ibn ʀmir al-Juhanī said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said — and he mentioned the ḥadīth with its meaning, saying: \Everything with which a man occupies himself in play is vain"," except a man's shooting with his bow"," his training of his horse"," and his play with his wife"," for they are of the truth. And whoever abandons archery after having learned it has shown ingratitude for that which he was taught.\""\n\nThe Shaykh"," may Allah have mercy on him"," said: Thus it is in my book"," \""ʿAbdullāh ibn Yazīd","\"" but others narrated from Hishām"," saying \""ʿAbdullāh ibn Zayd al-Azraq.\"" [Weak]"""
"20983","(20977) Abū ʿAmr Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Adīb informed us, Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī informed me, al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān narrated to us, Aḥmad ibn ʿĪsā narrated to us, Ibn Wahb informed us, ʿAmr informed us that Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān narrated to him from ʿUrwah, from ʿĀʾishah, may Allah be pleased with her, that she said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to me while I with two young girls who were singing the songs of Buʿāth. He lay down on the bed and turned his face away. Abū Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, came in and rebuked me, saying, \The instrument of Shayṭān in the presence of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ!\"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ turned toward him and said"," \""Leave them.\"" When he was distracted"," I gave them a subtle signal and they left. She said: It was the day of ʿĪd"," and the Abyssinians were playing with shields and spears. Either I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ"," or he said"," \""Would you like to watch?\"" I said"," \""Yes.\"" She said: He stood me behind him"," my cheek upon his cheek"," and he was saying"," \""Carry on"," O Banū Arfidah!\"" until I grew tired. He said"," \""Enough?\"" I said"," \""Yes.\"" He said"," \""Go.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Aḥmad"," and Muslim narrated it from Hārūn ibn Saʿīd and Yūnus ibn ʿAbd al-Aʿlā"," all of them from Ibn Wahb. [Sound — agreed upon]"""
"20984","(20978) Abū Naṣr ibn Qatādah informed us, ʿAbdullāh ibn Aḥmad ibn Saʿd the Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, Abū ʿAbdillāh Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Būshanjī narrated to us, Yūsuf ibn ʿAdī narrated to us, Sharīk ibn ʿAbdillāh narrated from al-Mughīrah, from ʀmir al-Shaʿbī, from ʿIyāḍ al-Ashʿarī, that he witnessed an ʿĪd in al-Anbār and said: \What is the matter with you that you do not engage in taqlīs"," as they used to do in the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?\"" Yūsuf ibn ʿAdī said: Al-Taqlīs is that the young girls and boys sit at the roadsides playing with the drum and other such things.\n\nThe Shaykh"," may Allah have mercy on him"," said: Hushaym narrated it from al-Mughīrah"," except that he said: \""For it is of the Sunnah on the two ʿĪds","\"" meaning the beating of the duff upon departing. Yazīd ibn Hārūn narrated it from Sharīk"," and he said: Ziyād ibn ʿIyāḍ al-Ashʿarī. [Weak]"""
"20985","(20979) And Abū ʿAbdillāh the Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥīm al-Harawī in Sāfiriyyah narrated to us, Ādam ibn Abī Iyās narrated to us, Shaybān and Isrāʾīl narrated from Jābir, from ʀmir, from Qays ibn Saʿd, who said: There was nothing done in the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that I did not see being practiced after him, except one thing — taqlīs was performed for him on the day of Fiṭr.\n\nʿAmr ibn Muḥammad narrated it from Isrāʾīl, who said: \Taqlīs was performed for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the day of ʿĪd","\"" and al-taqlīs means play."""
"20986","(20980) Abū ʿAbdillāh the Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, Abū Isḥāq Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā al-Muzzī narrated to us by dictation, Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn ʿUthmān ibn Karāmah narrated to us, Khālid ibn Makhlad narrated to us, from Sulaymān ibn Bilāl, Sharīk ibn ʿAbdillāh ibn Abī Nimr informed me, from ʿAṭāʾ, from Abū Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Allah"," Mighty and Majestic"," said: 'Whoever shows enmity to a walī (friend) of Mine"," I declare war against him. My servant does not draw near to Me with anything more beloved to Me than what I have made obligatory upon him. My servant continues to draw near to Me with voluntary acts until I love him. When I love him"," I become his hearing with which he hears"," his sight with which he sees"," his hand with which he strikes"," and his foot with which he walks. Were he to ask of Me"," I would surely give him. Were he to seek refuge in Me"," I would surely grant him refuge. I do not hesitate about anything as I hesitate about taking the soul of the believing servant — he hates death"," and I hate to harm him.'\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn ʿUthmān ibn Karāmah. [Sound — Bukhārī 6502]"""
"20987","(20981) Abū ʿAbdillāh the Ḥāfiẓ, and Abū Ṭāhir the Faqīh, and Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq, and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥakam informed us, Anas ibn ʿIyāḍ narrated from Hishām ibn ʿUrwah, from his father, from ʿĀʾishah, may Allah be pleased with her, that she said: I used to play with dolls in the presence of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and my friends would come to me, but they would withdraw from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. She said: The Prophet ﷺ would send them back to me, and they would play with me. Anas said: \They would withdraw\"" means they would flee.\n\nAl-Bukhārī and Muslim narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ through various routes from Hishām ibn ʿUrwah. [Sound — agreed upon]"""
"20988","(20982) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzzī informed us, Abū al-Ḥasan Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdūs narrated to us, ʿUthmān ibn Saʿīd al-Dārimī narrated to us, Saʿīd ibn Abī Maryam informed us, Yaḥyā ibn Ayyūb narrated to me, ʿUmārah ibn Ghaziyyah informed me that Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Taymī narrated to him from Abū Salamah ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, from ʿĀʾishah, may Allah be pleased with her, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ returned from the expedition of Tabūk, and I had hung a curtain over the door of my room, and there was an Armenian curtain across the width of my house. He entered the house, and when he saw it, said: \What is this for me"," O ʿĀʾishah? And the world!\"" So he tore the curtain until it fell to the ground. In its niche was a curtain"," and a breeze blew and exposed a corner of the curtain"," revealing ʿĀʾishah's dolls. He said: \""What is this"," O ʿĀʾishah?\"" She said: \""My dolls.\"" She said: He saw among them a horse with two wings made of patches. He said: \""What is this that I see in the middle of them?\"" She said: \""A horse.\"" He said: \""What is this on it?\"" She said: \""Two wings.\"" He said: \""A horse with two wings?\"" She said: \""Have you not heard that Sulaymān ibn Dāwūd had horses with wings?\"" She said: He laughed until his molars became visible.\n\nAbū Dāwūd narrated it in the Sunan from Muḥammad ibn ʿAwf"," from Saʿīd ibn Abī Maryam"," and he said in the ḥadīth: \""From the expedition of Tabūk or Khaybar.\"" The prohibition of images and statues has been established from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ through many routes. It is possible that the preserved narration in the report of Abū Salamah from ʿĀʾishah refers to his return from the expedition of Khaybar"," and that this was before the prohibition of images and statues. The prohibition then came after that. Among those who narrated the prohibition from the Prophet ﷺ is Abū Hurayrah"," and his acceptance of Islam was at the time of Khaybar"," so his hearing would have been after that. In the ḥadīth of Jābir: the Prophet ﷺ commanded ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb"," may Allah be pleased with him"," at the time of the Conquest"," while he was in al-Baṭḥāʾ"," to go to the Kaʿbah and erase every image in it. The Prophet ﷺ did not enter the Kaʿbah until every image in it had been erased.\n\nThe Shaykh said: The time of the Conquest was after Khaybar. Furthermore"," she was young at the time when she was married to the Prophet ﷺ"," and she had dolls with her — this is established. [Good]"""
"20989","(20983) From al-Zuhrī, from ʿUrwah, from ʿĀʾishah: The Prophet ﷺ married her when she was seven years old, and she was brought to him when she was nine years old, and her dolls were with him, and he passed away when she was eighteen years old. Abū ʿAbdillāh the Ḥāfiẓ informed me, Abū ʿAmr ibn Abī Jaʿfar informed us, al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān narrated to us, Fayyāḍ ibn Zuhayr narrated to us, ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us, Maʿmar narrated from al-Zuhrī, and he mentioned it.\n\nMuslim narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbd ibn Ḥumayd, from ʿAbd al-Razzāq. (Q) In none of the narrations is it stated that she had reached the age of women by other than years at the time of her marriage being consummated. It is possible that her occupation with her dolls and the Prophet's ﷺ approval of her in that continued until the time of her reaching maturity, and Allah knows best. Abū ʿUbayd interpreted it thus, saying: The reason for this is only that it is amusement for young girls. If it were for grown women, it would be disliked. Al-Ḥalīmī mentioned that if something is made of wood, stone, brass, or copper in the likeness of a complete human being with full limbs, like an idol, it must be broken and it is not permissible to keep it. But if one of them takes a piece of cloth, wraps it, and shapes it in the form of a young girl, and calls it a daughter or a mother, and plays with it, she is not to be prevented from it, and he mentioned what is in it of the expansion of her heart, the goodness of her upbringing, and her practice in caring for children. [Sound — agreed upon]"
"20990","(20984) Abū ʿAbdillāh the Ḥāfiẓ narrated to me, al-Ḥusayn ibn ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā al-Dārimī narrated to me from the original of his book, Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us — he dictated it to us — Abū Kurayb narrated to us, Abū Usāmah narrated from Hishām ibn ʿUrwah, from his father, from ʿĀʾishah, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ married me when I was six years old, and he consummated the marriage with me when I was nine years old. She said: I came to Madīnah and was feverish for a month, and my hair grew down to my shoulders. Umm Rūmān came to me while I was on a swing, with my friends. She called out to me, and I came to her, not knowing what was wanted of me. She took my hand and stood me at the door. I said, \Hādhihi"," hādhihi","\"" until my breath settled. She took me into a room where there were women of the Anṣār"," who said"," \""For goodness and blessing"," and upon the best of omens.\"" They handed me over to them"," and they washed my head and prepared me. Nothing alarmed me except the Messenger of Allah ﷺ"," and they handed me over to him.\n\nMuslim narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū Kurayb"," and al-Bukhārī narrated it through another route from Hishām. [Sound — agreed upon]"""
"20991","(20985) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Dāwūd al-Razzāz reported to us in Baghdād: Abū Sahl ibn Ziyād al-Qaṭṭān narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār narrated to us: ʿAbdullāh ibn Idrīs al-Awdī narrated from Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr from Yaḥyā ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Ḥāṭib, who said: ʿĀ'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her, said: \The Prophet ﷺ married me when I was six years old. When we arrived in Madīnah"," we alighted at al-Sunḥ in the territory of Banī al-Ḥārith ibn al-Khazraj. I was swinging between two palm branches"," and I was a girl of nine. Then my mother came and took me down. She walked with me until she brought me to the door"," and I was exhausted. She wiped my face with some water"," parted my hair which I had"," and brought me in to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. In the house there were men and women. She said: 'These are your family. May Allah bless you in them and bless them in you.' Then the men and women stood up and left"," and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ consummated the marriage with me.\"""""
"20992","(20986) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bushrān reported to us in Baghdād: al-Ḥusayn ibn Ṣaffwān informed us: Abū Bakr ʿAbdullāh ibn Muḥammad ibn Abī al-Dunyā narrated to me: my father informed us: Hushaym narrated from Ziyād ibn Abī ʿUmar from Ṣāliḥ Abī al-Khalīl that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered the cutting down of the swings (al-marājīḥ). This is a munaqaṭiʿ narration, and it has been reported through another weak chain as a mawṣūl narration, but it is not of significance. Abū Burdah and Ṭalḥah ibn Muṣarrif used to dislike them."
"20993","(20987) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr both reported to us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: ʿAbbās al-Dūrī narrated to us: Abū Ghassān Mālik ibn Ismāʿīl al-Nahdī narrated from Manṣūr ibn Abī al-Aswad from ʿAṭā' ibn al-Sā'ib from Saʿīd ibn Jubayr from Ibn ʿAbbās regarding this verse: \And of the people is he who buys the amusement of speech\"" [Luqmān 6]. He said: \""It was revealed concerning singing and the like thereof.\"""""
"20994","(20988) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ reported to me: Abū Bakr ibn ʿAbdullāh informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān narrated to us: Hishām ibn ʿAmmār narrated to us: Ṣadaqah ibn Khālid narrated to us: Ibn Jābir narrated from ʿAṭiyyah ibn Qays al-Kilābī from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Ghanm al-Ashʿarī, who said: \Abū ʿĀmir"," or Abū Mālik—and by Allah"," he did not lie to me—narrated that he heard the Prophet ﷺ say: 'There will certainly be among my Ummah people who will deem lawful silk"," wine"," and musical instruments (al-maʿāzif). And there will be people who will encamp beside a mountain"," and their flocks will return to them in the evening. Then a man will come to them with a need"," and they will say: \""Come back to us tomorrow.\"" But Allah will destroy them during the night"," causing the mountain to collapse upon them"," and He will transform others among them into apes and swine until the Day of Resurrection.'\"" Al-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ"," saying: \""And Hishām ibn ʿAmmār said…\"""""
"20995","(20989) ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān reported to us: Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us: Abū Ismāʿīl al-Tirmidhī narrated to us: Abū Ṣāliḥ narrated to us: Muʿāwiyah ibn Ṣāliḥ narrated from Ḥātim ibn Ḥurayth from Mālik ibn Abī Maryam, who said: \ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Ghanm al-Ashʿarī came to Damascus as a delegate"," and a group of us gathered around him. We mentioned al-ṭalā' (a type of oil/unguent)"," and among us were those who permitted it and those who disliked it. He said: 'I heard Abū Mālik al-Ashʿarī"," the Companion of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ"," narrate from the Prophet ﷺ that he said: \""People from my Ummah will drink wine"," calling it by other than its name"," and musical instruments and female singers will be played over their heads. Allah will cause the earth to swallow them and will make among them apes and swine.\""'\"" And there are corroborating narrations for this from the ḥadīth of ʿAlī"," ʿImrān ibn Ḥuṣayn"," ʿAbdullāh ibn Busr"," Sahl ibn Saʿd"," Anas ibn Mālik"," and ʿĀ'ishah"," may Allah be pleased with them all"," from the Prophet ﷺ."""
"20996","(20990) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bushrān informed us: al-Ḥusayn ibn Ṣaffwān narrated to us: ʿAbdullāh ibn Muḥammad ibn Abī al-Dunyā narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Yūsuf al-Zammī narrated to us: ʿUbaydullāh ibn ʿAmr narrated from ʿAbd al-Karīm, who is al-Jazarī, from Qays ibn Ḥabṭar from Ibn ʿAbbās from the Prophet ﷺ, who said: \Indeed"," Allah"," the Blessed and Most High"," has forbidden you wine"," gambling"," and the kūbah—and it is the drum—and He said: 'Every intoxicant is unlawful (ḥarām).'\"""""
"20997","(20991) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Muqri' informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us: Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Abī Bakr narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh al-Zubayrī narrated to us: Sufyān narrated from ʿAlī ibn Bādhimah from Qays ibn Ḥabṭar, who said: \I asked Ibn ʿAbbās about the jar"," and he mentioned the story of ʿAbd al-Qays. Then he said—meaning the Prophet ﷺ: 'Indeed"," Allah has forbidden me—or has forbidden—wine"," gambling"," and the kūbah"," and He said: \""Every intoxicant is unlawful.\""'\"" Sufyān said: \""I asked ʿAlī: 'What is the kūbah?' He said: 'The drum (al-ṭabl).'\"" Abū Dāwūd narrated it in the Sunan from Muḥammad ibn Bashshār from Abī Aḥmad al-Zubayrī."""
"20998","(20992) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān reported to us in Baghdād: ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar informed us: Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān narrated to us: al-Ḥajjāj ibn Minhāl narrated to us: Ḥammād narrated from Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq from Yazīd ibn Abī Ḥabīb from al-Walīd ibn ʿAbdah from ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade wine, gambling, the kūbah, and the ghubyarā', and he said: \Every intoxicant is unlawful.\"" ʿAbd al-Ḥamīd ibn Jaʿfar contradicted him regarding the name of the person from whom Yazīd ibn Abī Ḥabīb narrated."""
"20999","(20993) Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn Abī al-Maʿrūf al-Faqīh al-Isfarāyīnī reported to us in Iṣfahān: Abū ʿAmr Ismāʿīl ibn Najayd al-Sulamī informed us: Abū Muslim Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbdullāh narrated to us: Abū ʿĀṣim narrated from ʿAbd al-Ḥamīd ibn Jaʿfar from Yazīd ibn Abī Ḥabīb from ʿAmr ibn al-Walīd from ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Whoever lies about me deliberately"," let him take his seat in the Fire.\"" Then he said: \""Indeed"," Allah and His Messenger have forbidden wine"," gambling"," the kūbah"," and the ghubyarā'.\"" Others narrated from ʿAbd al-Ḥamīd from Yazīd from ʿAmr ibn al-Walīd ibn ʿAbdah."""
"21000","(20994) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzakkī and Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī both reported to us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥakam informed us: Ibn Wahb informed me: Ibn Lahīʿah narrated from ʿAbdullāh ibn Hubayrah from Abī Hurayrah or Hubayrah al-ʿAjlānī from a mawlā of ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr from ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr ibn al-ʿĀṣ that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out to them one day while they were in the mosque and said: \Indeed"," my Lord has forbidden me wine"," gambling"," the kūbah"," and the qinnīn.\"" And the kūbah is the drum."""
"21001","(20995) He said: Ibn Wahb informed us, narrating to me al-Layth ibn Sa'd and Ibn Lahī'ah from Yazīd ibn Abī Ḥabīb from 'Amr ibn al-Walīd from Qays ibn Sa'd — who was the bearer of the Prophet's ﷺ standard — that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \That is so. And al-Ghubayrā' and every intoxicant is ḥarām.\"" 'Amr ibn al-Walīd said: \""And it reached me from 'Abdullāh ibn 'Amr ibn al-'Āṣ something similar"," and al-Layth did not mention al-Qinnīn.\"" [Weak. Referred to previously.]"""
"21002","(20996) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān informed us, al-Ḥusayn ibn Ṣafwān informed us, 'Abdullāh ibn Muḥammad ibn Abī al-Dunyā narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Yaḥyā ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣāliḥīnī narrated to us from Yaḥyā ibn Ayyūb from 'Ubaydullāh ibn Zaḥr from Bakr ibn Sawādah from Qays ibn Sa'd ibn 'Ubādah that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Indeed"," my Lord has forbidden upon me wine (al-khamr)"," gambling (al-maysir)"," al-qinnīn"," and al-kūbah.\"" Abū Zakariyyā said: \""Al-qinnīn is al-'ūd (a type of wood).\"" [Weak.]"""
"21003","(20997) Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī informed us, Abū al-'Abbās al-Aṣamm informed us, Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us, Abū Mushir narrated to us, Sa'īd ibn 'Abd al-'Azīz narrated to us. (Ḥ) And Abū 'Alī al-Rūdhbārī informed us — and the wording is his — Muḥammad ibn Bakr informed us, Abū Dāwūd narrated to us, Aḥmad ibn 'Ubaydullāh al-Ghudānī narrated to us, al-Walīd ibn Muslim narrated to us, Sa'īd ibn 'Abd al-'Azīz narrated to us from Sulaymān ibn Mūsā from Nāfi', who said: \Ibn 'Umar heard a mizmār (flute)"," so he placed his fingers in his ears and turned away from the road. He said to me: 'O Nāfi'"," do you hear anything?' I said: 'No.' He then removed his fingers from his ears and said: 'I was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when he heard something like this"," and he did the same.'\"" In the narration of al-Qāḍī"," he said: \""I was walking with Ibn 'Umar when he heard the sound of a shepherd's pipe. He left the road and kept saying: 'Do you hear?' I said: 'No.' Then he returned to the road and said: 'Thus I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ do.'\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ.]"""
"21004","(20998) Abū 'Alī informed us, Muḥammad ibn Bakr informed us, Abū Dāwūd narrated to us, Maḥmūd ibn Khālid narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Muṭ'im ibn al-Miqdām narrated to us, Nāfi' narrated, who said: \I was riding behind Ibn 'Umar when a shepherd passed by playing a pipe"," and he mentioned something similar to it.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Referred to previously.]"""
"21005","(20999) And Abū 'Alī informed us, Muḥammad ibn Bakr informed us, Abū Dāwūd narrated to us, Aḥmad ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us, 'Abdullāh ibn Ja'far al-Raqqī narrated to us, Abū al-Malīḥ narrated to us from Maymūn from Nāfi', who said: \We were with Ibn 'Umar when I heard the sound of a mizmār"," and he mentioned something similar to it.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ.]"""
"21006","(21000) Abū Naṣr ibn Qatādah informed us, Abū Manṣūr al-'Abbās ibn al-Faḍl al-Naḍrawī informed us, Aḥmad ibn Najdah informed us, Sa'īd ibn Manṣūr informed us, Abū 'Awanah narrated to us from 'Abd al-Karīm al-Jazarī from Abī Hāshim al-Kūfī from Ibn 'Abbās, who said: \The duff (hand-drum) is ḥarām"," the ma'āzif (musical instruments) are ḥarām"," the kūbah is ḥarām"," and the mizmār (flute) is ḥarām.\"" [Weak.]"""
"21007","(21001) 'Alī ibn Aḥmad ibn 'Abdān informed us, Aḥmad ibn 'Ubayd informed us, Hishām ibn 'Alī narrated to us, 'Abdullāh ibn Rajā' narrated to us, 'Abd al-'Azīz narrated to us. (Ḥ) And Abū 'Abd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī informed us, Abū al-Ḥasan al-Kārizī informed us, 'Alī ibn 'Abd al-'Azīz informed us from Abī 'Ubayd, Abū al-Naḍr narrated to us from 'Abd al-'Azīz ibn 'Abdullāh ibn Abī Salamah from Hilāl ibn Abī Hilāl from 'Aṭā' ibn Yasār from 'Abdullāh ibn 'Amr, who said regarding this verse in the Qur'an: {O you who believe, indeed wine, gambling, idols, and divination arrows are an abomination of Satan's handiwork, so avoid them that you may be successful} [al-Mā'idah 90]: \It is in the Torah: 'Indeed"," Allah sent down the truth to nullify falsehood and to invalidate through it play (al-la'b)"," dancing (al-zafn)"," flutes (al-zimmārāt)"," stringed instruments (al-mazāhir)"," and al-kinnārāt.'\"" Ibn Rajā' added in his narration: \""And images (al-taṣāwīr)"," poetry (al-shi'r)"," and wine (al-khamr). Whoever tastes them"," my Lord has sworn by His Might: whoever drinks it after I have forbidden it"," I shall make him thirsty on the Day of Resurrection; and whoever abandons it after I have forbidden it"," I shall give him to drink from the Pure Pond (Ḥaḍīrat al-Quds).\"" Abū 'Ubayd said: \""Al-mazāhir is the plural of mizhar"," which is the 'ūd (lute) that is played. As for al-kinnārāt"," it is said they are the 'īdān (reeds)"," and it is also said they are the duffūf (drums). As for al-kūbah mentioned in another marfū' report"," Muḥammad ibn Kathīr informed me that al-kūbah is al-nard (backgammon) in the speech of the people of Yemen"," and others said it is the ṭabl (drum).\"" The Sheikh said: [Ṣaḥīḥ.]"""
"21008","(21002) It was also narrated by Zayd ibn al-Ḥubāb from Abī Mawdūd al-Madanī from 'Aṭā' ibn Yasār from Ka'b, who said: \Indeed"," in what Allah"," Mighty and Majestic"," revealed to Mūsā: 'We sent down the truth to nullify falsehood and to invalidate through it play"," stringed instruments (al-mazāmīr)"," al-kinnārāt"," poetry"," and wine.' My Lord"," Mighty and Majestic"," swore: 'No servant abandons them out of fear of Me except that I shall give him to drink from the Pools of Purity (Ḥiyāḍ al-Quds).'\"" Zayd ibn al-Ḥubāb said: \""I asked Abī Mawdūd: 'What are al-mazāmīr?' He said: 'Square duffūf (drums).' I said: 'What are al-kinnārāt?' He said: 'The ṭanābīr (stringed instruments).'\"" Abū 'Abdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us"," Abū Isḥāq Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us"," Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us"," Abū Aḥmad Sha'tham ibn Uṣayl al-'Ijlī narrated to us by dictation in Jankarūdh"," Zayd ibn al-Ḥubāb narrated to us"," Abī Mawdūd al-Madanī narrated to us"," and he mentioned it along with the explanation. [Ṣaḥīḥ.]"""
"21009","(21003) Abū 'Abdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū al-'Abbās Muḥammad ibn Ya'qūb informed us, Bakkār ibn Qutaybah al-Qāḍī informed us, Ṣafwān ibn 'Īsā al-Qāḍī informed us, Ḥumayd al-Kharrāṭ narrated to us from 'Ammār al-Duhnī from Sa'īd ibn Jubayr from Abī al-Ṣahbā' from Ibn Mas'ūd, who said regarding the verse: {And of the people is he who purchases idle talk (lahw al-ḥadīth) to mislead from the path of Allah} [Luqmān 6]: \By Allah"," it is singing (al-ghinā').\"" [Ḥasan.]"""
"21010","(21004) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān informed us, al-Ḥusayn ibn Ṣafwān informed us, 'Abdullāh ibn Muḥammad ibn Abī al-Dunyā informed us, Zuhayr ibn Ḥarb narrated to us, Jarīr narrated to us from 'Aṭā' ibn al-Sā'ib from Sa'īd ibn Jubayr from Ibn 'Abbās regarding the verse: {And of the people is he who purchases idle talk (lahw al-ḥadīth)}: \It is singing (al-ghinā') and the like.\"" And it has been narrated to us from Mujāhid"," 'Ikrimah"," and Ibrāhīm al-Nakha'ī. [Weak.]"""
"21011","(21005) ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn Bishrān informed us that al-Ḥusayn ibn Ṣafwān narrated to us that Ibn Abī al-Dunyā narrated to us that ʿUbaydullāh ibn ʿUmar narrated to us that Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd narrated from Sufyān, from his father, from ʿIkrimah, from Ibn ʿAbbās, regarding the verse: {while you are indulging in idle amusement} [an-Najm 61], he said: It refers to singing in the Ḥimyarī fashion — \Sing for us"," entertain us with song.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"21012","(21006) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān informed us that al-Ḥusayn ibn Ṣafwān narrated to us that ʿAbdullāh ibn Muḥammad ibn Abī al-Dunyā narrated to us that Abū Khaythamah and ʿUbaydullāh ibn ʿUmar both said: Ghundar narrated to us from Shuʿbah, from al-Ḥakam, from Ḥammād, from Ibrāhīm, who said: ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd said: \Singing produces hypocrisy in the heart.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"21013","(21007) And Ibn Bishrān informed us that al-Ḥusayn ibn Ṣafwān narrated to us that Ibn Abī al-Dunyā narrated to us that ʿAlī ibn al-Jaʿd informed us that Muḥammad ibn Ṭalḥah narrated from Saʿīd ibn Kaʿb al-Murādī, from Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Yazīd, from Ibn Masʿūd, who said: \Singing produces hypocrisy in the heart"," just as water produces crops; and the remembrance of Allah (dhikr) produces faith in the heart"," just as water produces crops.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"21014","(21008) Ibn Bishrān informed us that al-Ḥusayn ibn Ṣafwān narrated to us that Ibn Abī al-Dunyā narrated to us that ʿIṣmah ibn al-Faḍl narrated to us that Ḥaramī ibn ʿUmarah narrated to us that Sallām ibn Miskīn narrated to us that a shaykh narrated from Abū Wāʾil, from ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Singing produces hypocrisy in the heart"," just as water produces herbage.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"21015","(21009) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān informed us that al-Ḥusayn ibn Ṣafwān narrated to us that Ibn Abī al-Dunyā narrated to us that Abū Khaythamah narrated to us that Bishr ibn al-Sarī narrated from ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz al-Mājishūn, from ʿAbdullāh ibn Dīnār, who said: Ibn ʿUmar passed by a young girl who was singing, and he said: \Were Satan to leave anyone alone"," he would have left this one.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"21016","(21010) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq narrated to us that Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm informed us that Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥakam informed us that Ibn Wahb informed us from ʿAmr ibn al-Ḥārith that Bukayr ibn al-Ashajj narrated to him that Umm ʿAlqamah, the freed slave of ʿĀʾishah, informed him that the daughters of ʿĀʾishah's brother (may Allah be pleased with her) had been circumcised and were distressed by it. So it was said to ʿĀʾishah: \O Mother of the Believers"," shall we not summon someone to entertain them?\"" She said: \""Yes.\"" She said: So a certain singer was sent for and came to them. ʿĿʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her) passed by him in the house and saw him singing and moving his head in rapture"," and he had abundant hair. ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her) said: \""Uff! A devil! Expel him! Expel him!\"" So they expelled him. [Ḥasan]"""
"21017","(21011) And Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān informed us that al-Ḥusayn ibn Ṣafwān narrated to us that Ibn Abī al-Dunyā narrated to us that ʿUbaydullāh ibn ʿUmar and Abū Khaythamah both said: Yaḥyā ibn Sulaym narrated to us from ʿUbaydullāh ibn ʿUmar, who said: A man asked al-Qāsim ibn Muḥammad about singing, and he said: \I forbid you from it and I detest it.\"" He said: \""Is it ḥarām?\"" He said: \""Look"," O son of my brother"," when Allah distinguishes truth from falsehood"," in which category will He place singing?\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"21018","(21012) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿUmar both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us that Aḥmad ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥamīd al-Ḥārithī narrated to us that Abū Usāmah narrated from Hishām ibn ʿUrwah, from his father, from ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her), who said: Abū Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) came to me while I had two girls from among the girls of the Anṣār who were singing what the Anṣār used to recite on the day of Buʿāth or Bughāth — al-Ḥārithī was uncertain — and they were not professional singers. Abū Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) said: \The flute of Satan in the house of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ!\"" And that was the day of ʿĪd. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \""O Abū Bakr"," every people has a festival"," and this is our festival.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿUbayd ibn Ismāʿīl"," and Muslim narrated it from Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah"," both from Abū Usāmah"," and they both said \""the day of Buʿāth\"" without uncertainty. [Ṣaḥīḥ — Muttafaq ʿalayh]"""
"21019","(21013) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us that Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us that ʿUbayd ibn Sharīk narrated to us that Yaḥyā narrated to us that al-Layth narrated from ʿUqayl, from Ibn Shihāb, from ʿUrwah ibn al-Zubayr, from ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her), who said: Abū Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) came to her while she had two girls during the days of Minā who were singing and playing the tambourine (daff), and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was wrapped in his garment. Abū Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) rebuked them, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ uncovered his face and said: \Leave them"," O Abū Bakr"," for these are the days of ʿĪd"," and those are the days of Minā.\"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was in Madīnah. ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her) said: \""I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ screening me with his garment while I was watching the Ethiopians playing in the mosque"," and I was a young girl.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Yaḥyā ibn Bukayr"," and Muslim narrated it through another chain from Ibn Shihāb. [Ṣaḥīḥ — Muttafaq ʿalayh]"""
"21020","(21014) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn Khālid al-Ḥimṣī narrated to us that Bishr ibn Shuʿayb ibn Abī Ḥamzah narrated from his father, from al-Zuhrī, who said: al-Sāʾib ibn Yazīd said: We were with ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAwf on the road to Ḥajj, heading towards Makkah, when ʿAbd al-Raḥmān (may Allah be pleased with him) withdrew from the road and said to Rabbāh ibn al-Mughṭarif: \Sing for us"," O Abū Ḥassān","\"" and he was skilled in reciting naṣb (a form of Bedouin song resembling camel-driving chants). While Rabbāh was singing for them"," ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him) came upon them during his caliphate and said: \""What is this?\"" ʿAbd al-Raḥmān said: \""There is no harm in this; we are passing the time and shortening our journey.\"" ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: \""If you must do so"," then recite the poetry of Ḍirrār ibn al-Khaṭṭāb — and Ḍirrār was a man from Banū Muḥārib ibn Fihr.\""\n\nThe Shaykh said: \""Al-naṣb is a type of Bedouin singing resembling camel-driving chants (ḥudāʾ).\"" Abū ʿUbayd al-Harawī said so.\n\nAnd we have narrated another account regarding this from Khawwāt ibn Jubayr concerning ʿUmar"," ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAwf"," and Abū ʿUbaydah ibn al-Jarrāḥ (may Allah be pleased with them all) in the Book of Ḥajj"," in which Khawwāt said: \""I continued singing for them until it was the time of dawn.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"21021","(21015) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān informed us in Baghdād that Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār narrated to us, Aḥmad ibn Manṣūr narrated to us, ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us, Maʿmar narrated on the authority of al-Zuhrī, from ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Ḥārith ibn Nawfal, who said: I saw Usāmah ibn Zayd (may Allah be pleased with him) sitting in the assembly, placing one of his legs upon the other, raising his voice. I think he said: He was singing poetry (al-naṣb). [Weak]"
"21022","(21016) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Bakr al-Qāḍī both informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās, al-Aṣamm, narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Khālid narrated to us, Bishr ibn Shuʿayb narrated on the authority of his father, on the authority of al-Zuhrī, who informed me: ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz informed him that Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Nawfal informed him: He saw Usāmah ibn Zayd in the Mosque of the Messenger (peace and blessings be upon him), lying down, placing one of his legs upon the other, singing poetry (al-naṣb). And thus did Yūnus ibn Yazīd and others narrate it on the authority of al-Zuhrī.\n\nMuslim ibn al-Ḥajjāj said: The hadith is as the people said, other than Maʿmar. [Weak]"
"21023","(21017) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Bakr informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Khālid narrated to us, Bishr narrated on the authority of his father, on the authority of al-Zuhrī, who said: Sulaymān informed me that one in whom there is no suspicion informed him that he heard Abū Masʿud ʿUqbah ibn ʿAmr al-Anṣārī — who had witnessed Badr and who was the grandfather of Zayd ibn Ḥasan, the father of his mother — narrating. Sulaymān said: The one who heard him while he was upon his mount and he was the commander of the army, raising his voice, singing poetry (al-naṣb).\n\nAnd on the authority of al-Zuhrī, who said: ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUtbah informed me that his father informed him that he heard ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Arqam raising his voice, singing. ʿAbd Allāh said: By Allah, I have never seen any man among those whom I have seen and known whom I consider more fearful of Allah than ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Arqam. [Weak]"
"21024","(21018) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān informed us that Ismāʿīl al-Ṣaffār narrated to us, Aḥmad ibn Manṣūr narrated to us, ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us, Maʿmar narrated on the authority of Hishām ibn ʿUrwah, on the authority of Wahb ibn Kaysān, who said: ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Zubayr — and he was reclining — said: Bilāl was singing. A man said to him: He is singing? So he sat upright and then said: Which man among the Muhājirūn have I not heard singing poetry (al-naṣb)? [Authentic]"
"21025","(21019) Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī informed us, al-Ḥusayn ibn ʿAlī al-Tamīmī narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Sulaymān ibn Fāris narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Rajāʾ al-Sulamī narrated to us, Abū Dāwūd narrated to us, Abū ʿĀṣim narrated on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, who said: I asked ʿAṭāʾ about singing poetry, and he said: I see no harm in it so long as it is not obscene. [Authentic]"
"21026","(21020) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī narrated to us, Ibrāhīm ibn al-Ḥusayn narrated to us, Ādam narrated to us, Warqāʾ narrated on the authority of Ibn Abī Najīḥ, on the authority of Mujāhid, regarding His statement {And of the people is he who purchases idle talk} [Luqmān 6], he said: It refers to the purchasing of a male singer and a female singer with abundant wealth, and listening to them and to the like of that which is falsehood. [Authentic]"
"21027","(21021) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū ʿAbd Allāh Isḥāq ibn Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf al-Sūsī both informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn ʿAffān al-ʿĀmirī narrated to us, ʿAbd Allāh ibn Numayr narrated on the authority of al-Aʿmash, on the authority of Shaqīq, who said: ʿAbd Allāh, meaning Ibn Masʿūd (may Allah be pleased with him), said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: There is none more jealous than Allah, and for this reason He has forbidden indecencies. And there is none to whom praise is more beloved than Allah, the Mighty and Majestic.\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ on the authority of Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Numayr, and al-Bukhārī narrated it through another chain from al-Aʿmash. [Authentic — Agreed Upon]"
"21028","(21022) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us that Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us, Tamtām narrated to us, Mūsā ibn Ismāʿīl narrated to us, Hammām narrated on the authority of Yaḥyā ibn Abī Kathīr that Abū Salamah informed him that Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) informed him that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Bakr ibn Fūrak informed us that ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar al-Aṣbahānī narrated to us, Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb narrated to us, Abū Dāwūd narrated to us, Ḥarb ibn Shaddād narrated on the authority of Yaḥyā, on the authority of Abū Salamah, on the authority of Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Verily Allah, the Blessed and Most High, is jealous, and the believer is jealous. And the jealousy of Allah is that the believer should commit that which has been forbidden upon him.\n\nIn the narration of Hammām: And from the jealousy of Allah is that the believer should commit the indecency which Allah has forbidden upon him.\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Mūsā ibn Ismāʿīl, and Muslim narrated it from Abū Mūsā, from Abū Dāwūd. [Authentic]"
"21029","(21023) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān al-ʿAdl informed us in Baghdād that Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār narrated to us, Aḥmad ibn Manṣūr narrated to us, ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us, Maʿmar narrated on the authority of Zayd ibn Aslam, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Verily jealousy (al-ghayrah) is from faith, and the dayyūth (the cuckold, one devoid of jealousy) is from hypocrisy. And the dayyūth is the one who is devoid of jealousy. [Weak]"
"21030","(21024) Abū ʿUbayd al-Qāsim ibn Sallām narrated it on the authority of more than one, on the authority of Dāwūd ibn Qays, on the authority of Zayd ibn Aslam, thus as a mursal narration, without his statement \and the dayyūth is the one who is devoid of jealousy.\"" Abū ʿUbayd said: The word mithyāʾ (cuckoldice) is derived from al-madhy"," meaning that he gathers men and women together and then leaves them to engage in mutual indecency — that is cuckoldice (mithyāʾ).\n\nAbū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī informed us that Abū al-Ḥasan al-Kārizī narrated to us"," ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz narrated to us"," on the authority of Abū ʿUbayd"," who said: More than one narrated it to us on the authority of Dāwūd ibn Qays"," and he mentioned it.\n\nThe Shaykh said: Others besides the two of them narrated it on the authority of Zayd ibn Aslam"," on the authority of ʿAṭāʾ ibn Yasār"," on the authority of Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī"," on the authority of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him)"," as a connected (mawṣūl) narration. [Authentic]"""
"21031","(21025) Abū al-Qāsim ʿAbd al-Khāliq ibn ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd al-Khāliq al-Naysābūrī informed us that Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Khanb Abū Bakr narrated to us. (Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Mukram ibn Aḥmad al-Qāḍī in Baghdād narrated to us, both saying that Abū Ismāʿīl Muḥammad ibn Ismāʿīl al-Tirmidhī narrated to us that Ayyūb ibn Sulaymān ibn Bilāl narrated to us that Abū Bakr ibn Abī Uways narrated to me from Sulaymān ibn Bilāl from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yasār al-Aʿraj that he heard Sālim ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar narrating from his father from the Prophet ﷺ that he said: \Three shall not enter Paradise: the one who is disobedient to his parents"," the cuckold (dayyūth)"," and the effeminate man among women.\"" (T) ʿUmar ibn Muḥammad followed him"," narrating from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yasār. [Weak]"""
"21032","(21026) Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī informed us that Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us that Aḥmad ibn Hishām ibn Bahrām al-Madāʾinī narrated to us that Hishām ibn Lāḥiq narrated from ʿĀṣim that a man came to al-Ḥasan and said to him, \O Abū Saʿīd"," I have a slave-girl with a beautiful voice; if I were to teach her singing"," perhaps I could earn money from these people through her.\"" Al-Ḥasan said"," \""Indeed"," Ismāʿīl used to command his family with prayer and zakah"," and he was well-pleasing to his Lord.\"" The man repeated his statement three times"," and each time al-Ḥasan replied"," \""Indeed"," Ismāʿīl used to command his family with prayer and zakah.\"" [Weak]"""
"21033","(21027) Abū al-Ḥusayn Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī ibn Khashīsh al-Muqriʾ in Kūfah informed us that Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī ibn Duḥaym al-Shaybānī narrated to us that Aḥmad ibn Ḥāzim ibn Abī Ghazrah narrated to us that ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Mūsā narrated to us that Isrāʾīl narrated from Abī Isḥāq from Hānīʾ ibn Hānīʾ from ʿAlī (may Allāh be pleased with him) who said: \We came to the Messenger of Allāh ﷺ—myself"," Jaʿfar"," and Zayd. He said to Zayd"," 'You are our brother and our mawlā.' So Zayd hopped (raised one foot and jumped on the other out of joy). Then he said to Jaʿfar"," 'You resemble my character and my disposition.' So Jaʿfar hopped after Zayd's hop. Then he said to me"," 'You are from me and I am from you.' So I hopped after Jaʿfar's hop.\"" The Shaykh said: \""Hānīʾ ibn Hānīʾ is not well-known. In this"," if it is authentic"," there is an indication of the permissibility of hopping—that is"," raising one foot and jumping on the other out of joy. Dancing that is of a similar nature would likewise be permissible in the same manner. And Allāh knows best.\"" [Weak]"""
"21034","(21028) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us that al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us that al-Shāfiʿī informed us that Sufyān narrated from Ibrāhīm ibn Maisarah from ʿAmr ibn al-Sharīd from his father who said: \The Messenger of Allāh ﷺ mounted me behind him and said"," 'Do you have any poetry of Umayyah ibn Abī al-Ṣalt with you?' I said"," 'Yes.' He said"," 'Go on.' So I recited a verse"," and he said"," 'Go on.' I continued until I reached one hundred verses.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 2255]"""
"21035","(21029) Abū ʿAbd Allāh informed me that Abū al-Walīd narrated to us that Ibrāhīm ibn Abī Ṭālib narrated to us that Ibn Abī ʿUmar narrated to us that Sufyān narrated it with its chain, similar to it. Muslim narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Ibn Abī ʿUmar. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Preceded before it]"
"21036","(21030) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī both informed us that Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us that Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib informed us that Abū Aḥmad al-Zubayrī narrated to us that ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Thaqafī narrated from ʿAmr ibn al-Sharīd from his father who said: \I recited to the Prophet ﷺ one hundred verses (qāfiyahs) from the poetry of Umayyah ibn Abī al-Ṣalt"," and throughout all of that he kept saying"," 'Go on"," go on.' Then he said"," 'He nearly became a Muslim in his poetry.'\"" Muslim narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from the ḥadīth of al-Muʿtamir ibn Sulaymān and ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Mahdī from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān. Al-Shāfiʿī (may Allāh have mercy on him) said: \""The Messenger of Allāh ﷺ listened to camel-driving songs (ḥudāʾ) and rajaz poetry.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Preceded before it]"""
"21037","(21031) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us that Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us that Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq al-Qāḍī narrated to us that Sulaymān ibn Ḥarb narrated to us that Ḥammād ibn Zayd narrated from Thābit from Anas, and Ayyūb from Abī Qilābah from Anas (may Allāh be pleased with him) who said: \The Messenger of Allāh ﷺ was on a journey"," and there was a young boy called Anjashah who was driving the camels for them and urging them on. The Messenger of Allāh ﷺ said to him"," 'Woe to you"," O Anjashah! Gently—your driving of the fragile vessels (al-qawārīr).'\"" Ayyūb said from Abī Qilābah"," meaning the women. Al-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Sulaymān ibn Ḥarb"," and Muslim narrated it from Abī al-Rabīʿ and others from Ḥammād. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Agreed upon]"""
"21038","(21032) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣaghānī narrated to us that ʿAffān narrated to us that Hammām narrated to us that Qatādah narrated from Anas (may Allāh be pleased with him) that the Prophet ﷺ had a camel-driver called Anjashah who had a beautiful voice. The Prophet ﷺ said, \Take it easy"," O Anjashah! Do not break the fragile vessels (al-qawārīr).\"" Both narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from the ḥadīth of Hammām. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Agreed upon]"""
"21039","(21033) Abū Bakr ibn Fūrak informed us that ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us that Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb narrated to us that Abū Dāwūd narrated to us that Ḥammād ibn Salamah narrated from Thābit from Anas (may Allāh be pleased with him) who said: \Anjashah used to drive the camels for the women"," and al-Barāʾ ibn Mālik used to drive the camels for the men. Anjashah had a beautiful voice; when he sang"," the camels would hasten. The Messenger of Allāh ﷺ said"," 'Woe to you"," O Anjashah! Take it easy—your driving of the fragile vessels (al-qawārīr).'\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"21040","(21034) Abū ʿAmr Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Adīb informed us that Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī narrated to us that Abū Yaʿlā narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn ʿAbbād narrated to us that Ḥātim ibn Ismāʿīl narrated from Yazīd ibn Abī ʿUbayd, the mawlā of Salamah, from Salamah ibn al-Akwaʿ who said: \We went out with the Messenger of Allāh ﷺ to Khaybar. We travelled by night"," and a man from the people said to ʿĀmir ibn al-Akwaʿ"," 'Will you not recite some of your little verses for us?' ʿĀmir was a poet. So he dismounted and began driving the camels for the people"," reciting:\n\n'O Allāh"," were it not for You"," we would not have been guided","\nNor would we have given charity"," nor prayed.\nSo forgive us"," as a ransom for You"," what we have followed","\nAnd make our feet firm if we meet the enemy","\nAnd cast tranquillity upon us.\nIndeed"," when we are called out"," we come","\nAnd with the shouting they have cried out upon us.'\""\n\nThe Messenger of Allāh ﷺ said"," \""Who is this driver?\"" They said"," \""ʿĀmir ibn al-Akwaʿ.\"" He said"," \""May Allāh have mercy on him.\"" And he mentioned the rest of the ḥadīth. Muslim narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn ʿAbbād"," and al-Bukhārī and Muslim narrated it from Qutaybah from Ḥātim. Al-Shāfiʿī (may Allāh have mercy on him) said: \""He commanded Ibn Rawāḥah during a journey and said"," 'Stir the people (into action).' So he began reciting rajaz verses.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Agreed upon]"""
"21041","(21035) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū ʿAbdillāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūh al-Shaybānī narrated to us: Abū ʿAmr Aḥmad ibn Naṣr narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn ʿUbaydillāh al-Warrāq narrated to us: ʿUmar ibn ʿAlī narrated to us, from Ismāʿīl ibn Abī Khālid, from Qays ibn Abī Ḥāzim, from ʿAbdullāh ibn Rawāḥah (may Allah be pleased with him), that he was with the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) on a journey. He said to him: \O Ibn Rawāḥah"," dismount and urge the mounts on.\"" He said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," I have left that.\"" ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) said to him: \""Listen and obey.\"" He said: He glared at me and then said:\n\n\""By Allah"," were it not for You"," we would not have been guided","\nNor would we have given charity"," nor prayed.\nSo send down tranquility upon us","\nAnd make our feet firm if we meet [the enemy].\""\n\n[Rejected (Munkar)]"""
"21042","(21036) Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn Dāwūd al-ʿAlawī (may Allah have mercy on him) informed us: Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-Qaṭṭān narrated to us: Abū al-Azhar al-Salīṭī narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us: Maʿmar narrated, from al-Zuhrī, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) entered Makkah while Ibn Rawāḥah was holding the stirrup of his mount, reciting:\n\n\Clear the way"," O sons of the disbelievers"," from his path!\nToday we shall strike you upon its revelation—\nA strike that shall sever heads from their resting places","\nAnd render the companion oblivious of his companion.\nO Lord"," I am a believer in his word.\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīh]"""
"21043","(21037) And Abū ʿUmar Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-Qāḍī informed us: Sulaymān ibn Aḥmad ibn Ayyūb, Abū al-Qāsim al-Lakhmī, in Iṣbahān, narrated to us: Ibrāhīm ibn Abī Suwayd al-Shibāmī narrated to us, in the year two hundred and seventy-eight, in the city of Shibām: ʿAbd al-Razzāq narrated to us, from Maʿmar, from al-Zuhrī, from Anas, who said: When the Prophet (peace be upon him) entered Makkah during the ʿUmrah of Qaḍāʾ, ʿAbdullāh ibn Rawāḥah walked before him, reciting:\n\n\Clear the way"," O sons of the disbelievers"," from his path!\nThe Most Merciful has sent down in His revelation:\nIndeed"," the best of slain are those killed in His path.\nWe fought you over its interpretation","\nJust as we fought you over its revelation.\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīh. It has been mentioned before.]"""
"21044","(21038) And Abū Saʿd al-Mālinī informed us: Abū Aḥmad ibn ʿAdī al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū Yaʿlā narrated to us: Quṭn ibn Nasīr informed us: Jaʿfar ibn Sulaymān narrated to us: Thābit narrated—Quṭn said: I think he said—from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) entered Makkah, and its people stood in two rows, looking at the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) and his Companions. Ibn Rawāḥah was walking before the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him), and Ibn Rawāḥah said:\n\n\Clear the way"," O sons of the disbelievers"," from his path!\nToday we shall strike you upon its revelation—\nA strike that shall sever heads from their resting places","\nAnd render the companion oblivious of his companion.\nO Lord"," I am a believer in his word.\""\n\nʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: \""O Ibn Rawāḥah! In the Sanctuary of Allah and before the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him)"," you recite poetry?\"" The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: \""Leave him"," O ʿUmar! By the One in whose Hand is my soul"," his words are more severe upon them than the falling of arrows.\""\n\nAl-Shāfiʿī (may Allah have mercy on him) said: \""The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) came upon a rider from Banī Tamīm"," and they had a camel-driver with them.\"" He then mentioned the meaning of the story.\n\n[Ṣaḥīh. It has been mentioned before.]"""
"21045","(21039) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbdullāh ibn Yūsuf informed us: Abū Saʿīd ibn al-Aʿrābī informed us. And Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān informed us: Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr al-Razzāz informed us. Both said: Saʿdān ibn Naṣr narrated to us: Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah narrated to us, from ʿAmr, from ʿIkrimah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) was travelling towards al-Shām when he heard a camel-driver during the night. He said: \Hasten us towards this camel-driver.\"" He said: \""So they hastened until they caught up with him"," and he greeted them. He said: 'Who are the people?' They said: 'Muḍar.' The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: 'And we are from Muḍar.'\"" He said: \""That night"," in relation to Muḍar"," a man said: 'O Messenger of Allah"," indeed we were the first to drive camels in the Jāhiliyyah.' He said: 'How was that?' He said: 'A man from among us raided some camels and drove them away. He began telling his servant or his hired hand: \""Gather them!\"" But he refused. So the camels began to scatter. He struck him and broke his hand. The boy began saying: \""Woe to my hand! Woe to my hand!\"" And the camels began to gather. He was saying: \""Say such and such.\""' The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) began to laugh.\""\n\nSufyān said: \""Al-ʿAlāʾ ibn ʿAbd al-Karīm added in it"," from Mujāhid"," that the Prophet (peace be upon him) said: 'Indeed"," our camel-drivers were sluggish.'\""\n\n[Weak (Ḍaʿīf)]"""
"21046","(21040) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us: Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us: ʿAbbās ibn al-Faḍl narrated to us: Ibrāhīm—meaning ibn Ḥamzah—narrated to us: Ibn Abī Ḥāzim narrated to us, from Yazīd—meaning ibn al-Hād—from Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm, from Abū Salamah, from Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), who heard the Prophet (peace be upon him) say: \Allah has not permitted anything as He has permitted a Prophet with a beautiful voice to recite the Qurʾān aloud.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Ibrāhīm ibn Ḥamzah"," and Muslim narrated it from another route from Yazīd ibn al-Hād.\n\n[Ṣaḥīh. Agreed upon (Muttafaq ʿalayh).]"""
"21047","(21041) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us: Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us: ʿUbayd ibn Sharīk narrated to us: Yaḥyā narrated to us: Al-Layth narrated to us, from ʿUqayl, from Ibn Shihāb, that Abū Salamah ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān informed him, from Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), that he used to say: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: \Allah has not permitted anything as He has permitted a Prophet to chant the Qurʾān.\"" A companion of his added: \""To recite it aloud.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Yaḥyā ibn Bukayr"," and Muslim narrated it from another route from Ibn Shihāb.\n\n[Ṣaḥīh. Agreed upon (Muttafaq ʿalayh).]"""
"21048","(21042) Yūnus ibn Yazīd said in his narration from Ibn Shihāb: \Allah has not permitted anything like His permission for a Prophet to chant the Qurʾān.\"" Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Ismāʿīl ibn Aḥmad al-Jurjānī informed us: Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Qutaybah narrated to us: Ḥarmalah ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us: Ibn Wahb informed us: Yūnus ibn Yazīd informed me"," from Ibn Shihāb"," that Abū Salamah ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān informed him"," from Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him)"," who said: \""I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) say\""—and he mentioned it.\n\nMuslim narrated it from Ḥarmalah. The preserved wording in this narration is \""like His permission\"" (ka-adhnihi)"," and some of them say \""as His permission\"" (kaʾidhnihi).\n\nAbū ʿUbayd said regarding his statement \""ka-adhnihi\"": It means that Allah has not listened to anything as He listens to a Prophet who chants the Qurʾān. He did not approve the narration of those who said \""kaʾidhnihi.\"" He said: \""His statement 'to chant the Qurʾān' (yataghannā biʾl-Qurʾān)—its meaning"," according to us"," is the beautification of the recitation.\"" He said: \""And from that is his other hadith.\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīh. It has been mentioned before.]"""
"21049","(21043) That is, Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Ibrāhīm ibn Marzūq narrated to us: Wahb ibn Jarīr narrated to us: Shuʿbah narrated to us, from Abū Iyās Muʿāwiyah ibn Qurrah, from ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Mughaffal, who said: \I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) on the day of the Conquest of Makkah reciting Sūrat al-Faṭḥ and making tarjīʿ (repetition with melodic modulation).\"" He said: \""ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Mughaffal recited and made tarjīʿ.\"" He said: \""And Abū Iyās recited"," and he said: 'Were it not that I fear the people would gather around me"," I would recite with that melody with which the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) recited.'\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī and Muslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from the ḥadīth of Shuʿbah.\n\nAbū ʿUbayd said: \""And it is the interpretation of his statement: 'Adorn the Qurʾān with your voices.'\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīh. Agreed upon (Muttafaq ʿalayh).]"""
"21050","(21044) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān informed us in Baghdād: Abū Jaʿfar al-Razzāz narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn al-Faraj al-Jushamī narrated to us: ʿAbdullāh ibn Numayr informed us: Sulaymān al-Aʿmash narrated to us, from Ṭalḥah ibn Muṣarrif, from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAwsajah, from al-Barāʾ ibn ʿĀzib, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: \Adorn the Qurʾān with your voices.\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīh]"""
"21051","(21045) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Muqriʾ informed us that al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq informed us, that Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, that Abū al-Rabīʿ narrated to us, that Jarīr narrated from Manṣūr, from Ṭalḥah ibn Muṣarrif, from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAwsajah, from al-Barāʾ ibn ʿĀzib, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) used to say: \Indeed"," Allah and His angels send blessings upon the first row.\"" He (the narrator) said: \""And I think he said: 'And adorn the Qurʾān with your voices.'\""\n\nThis is a long ḥadīth which a group narrated from Ṭalḥah ibn Muṣarrif"," except that ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAwsajah used to have doubt regarding this wording.\n\nAnd he said in the narration of Shuʿbah from Ṭalḥah ibn Muṣarrif from him: \""I had forgotten this word until al-Ḍaḥḥāk ibn Muzāḥim reminded me of it.\"" And Allah knows best. [Ṣaḥīḥ; see before it]"""
"21052","(21046) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzakkī informed us that Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAbd al-Bāqī ibn Qāniʿ al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, that Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā ibn al-Mundhir narrated to us, that Abū ʿĀṣim narrated from Ibn Jurayj, from al-Zuhrī, from Abū Salamah, from Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \He is not from us who does not recite the Qurʾān with a beautiful voice (yataghannā).\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Isḥāq from Abū ʿĀṣim with this wording.\n\nAnd the group from al-Zuhrī only narrated it with the wording that we transmitted at the beginning of this chapter"," and with that wording Yaḥyā ibn Abī Kathīr and Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Taymī and Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr narrated it from Abū Salamah. This wording is only known from the ḥadīth of Saʿd ibn Abī Waqqāṣ (may Allah be pleased with him) and others"," except that the one who narrated it from al-Zuhrī with this wording is a ḥāfiẓ and imām"," so it is possible that both are preserved. And Allah knows best. [Ṣaḥīḥ; Bukhārī 7527]"""
"21053","(21047) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us that Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us, that ʿAbbās ibn al-Faḍl and al-Faḍl ibn ʿAmr both said: Ḥaddathanā Abū al-Walīd narrated to us, that Layth narrated to us, that ʿAbdullāh ibn Abī Mulkah narrated from ʿUbaydullāh ibn Abī Nahīk, from Saʿd ibn Abī Waqqāṣ (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \He is not from us who does not recite the Qurʾān with a beautiful voice (yataghannā).\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"21054","(21048) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq al-Faqīh and ʿAlī ibn Ḥamshādh both said: Bishr ibn Mūsā informed us, that al-Ḥumaydī narrated to us, that Sufyān narrated to us, that ʿAmr ibn Dīnār narrated from Ibn Abī Mulkah, from ʿUbaydullāh ibn Abī Nahīk, from Saʿd, who said: \I came to him and he asked me: 'Who are you?' So I informed him of my occupation.\"" Saʿd said: \""A merchant by trade. I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say: 'He is not from us who does not recite the Qurʾān with a beautiful voice (yataghannā).'\"" Sufyān said: \""Meaning"," he seeks sufficiency through it.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ; see before it]"""
"21055","(21049) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, he said: I heard Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb say: I heard al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān say: I heard al-Shāfiʿī say: \He is not from us who does not recite the Qurʾān with a beautiful voice (yataghannā).\"" A man said to him: \""Meaning"," he seeks sufficiency through it.\"" He said: \""No"," this is not its meaning. Its meaning is: he recites it with measured intonation and in a sorrowful voice.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"21056","(21050) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Muqriʾ informed us that al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq informed us, that Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, that ʿAbd al-Aʿlā ibn Ḥammād narrated to us, that ʿAbd al-Jabbār ibn Ward narrated to us, he said: I heard Ibn Abī Mulkah say: ʿUbaydullāh ibn Abī Yazīd said: I heard Abū Lubābah say: I heard the Prophet (ﷺ) say: \He is not from us who does not recite the Qurʾān with a beautiful voice (yataghannā).\"" I said to Ibn Abī Mulkah: \""O Abū Muḥammad"," what if one does not have a beautiful voice?\"" He said: \""He should beautify it as much as he is able.\""\n\nThis ḥadīth differs in its isnād from Ibn Abī Mulkah; it has been narrated from him through these two routes"," and it has been said from him from Ibn ʿAbbās"," and it has been said from him from ʿĀʾishah"," and it has been said from him other than that. The statement of Ibn Abī Mulkah in this ḥadīth confirms the correctness of the interpretation of al-Shāfiʿī (may Allah have mercy on him). [Munkar]"""
"21057","(21051) Abū ʿAbdillāh Isḥāq ibn Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf al-Sūsī and Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī and others said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, that al-ʿAbbās ibn al-Walīd ibn Yazīd informed us, that my father informed me, that al-Awzāʿī narrated to us, that Ismāʿīl ibn ʿUbaydullāh ibn Abī al-Muhājir narrated from Faḍālah ibn ʿUbayd al-Anṣārī, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Allah is more attentive to a man with a beautiful voice reciting the Qurʾān than an owner of a singing girl is to his singing girl.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"21058","(21052) Al-Walīd ibn Muslim narrated it from al-Awzāʿī, from Ismāʿīl, from Mayṣarah, the mawlā of Faḍālah, from Faḍālah, who said: I heard the Prophet (ﷺ) say: \Allah is more attentive to a beautiful voice reciting the Qurʾān than an owner of a singing girl is to his singing girl.\""\n\nAbū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī informed us that Aḥmad ibn Isḥāq ibn Ayyūb al-Faqīh informed us"," that Muḥammad ibn Ayyūb informed us"," that Muḥammad ibn ʿUqbah ibn Kathīr al-Sadūsī narrated to us"," that al-Walīd ibn Muslim narrated to us"," that al-Awzāʿī narrated"," and he mentioned it.\n\nAl-Shāfiʿī (may Allah have mercy on him) said: \""And indeed he (ﷺ) heard ʿAbdullāh ibn Qays—meaning Abū Mūsā—reciting"," and he said: 'Indeed this one has been given from the flutes of the family of Dāwūd.'\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"21059","(21053) Abū al-Qāsim ʿAbd al-Khāliq ibn ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd al-Khāliq informed us that Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Khanb narrated to us, that Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib informed us, that Zayd ibn al-Ḥubāb narrated to us, that Mālik ibn Mighwal narrated from ʿAbdullāh ibn Buraydah ibn Ḥuṣayb, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said to Abū Mūsā al-Ashʿarī while he was reciting in a corner of the mosque: \Indeed this one has been given a flute from the flutes of the family of Dāwūd.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from another route from Mālik ibn Mighwal. [Ṣaḥīḥ; agreed upon]"""
"21060","(21054) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū ʿAbdillāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, that Ḥusayn ibn Muḥammad al-Qabbānī and ʿImrān ibn Mūsā both said: Dāwūd ibn Rushayd narrated to us, he said: Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd al-Umawī narrated to us, that Ṭalḥah ibn Yaḥyā narrated from Abū Burdah, from Abū Mūsā, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said to me: \If you had seen me while I was listening to your recitation last night"," you would have known that you have been given a flute from the flutes of the family of Dāwūd.\"" He said: \""Had I known"," I would have adorned it for you with the utmost beauty.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Dāwūd ibn Rushayd"," and al-Bukhārī narrated it from another route from Abū Burdah in an abridged form. [Ṣaḥīḥ; see before it]"""
"21061","(21055) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbdullāh ibn Yaḥyā ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār al-Sukkarī informed us in Baghdād: Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn Manṣūr narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us: Maʿmar narrated from al-Zuhrī, from Abū Salamah, who said: Whenever ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) sat in the presence of Abū Mūsā, he would say to him: \Remind me"," O Abū Mūsā","\"" and he would recite [the Qur'an]. [Weak]"""
"21062","(21056) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ, Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī, and Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Abū Umayyah narrated to us: Abū ʿĀṣim narrated to us: Ṣāliḥ al-Nājī narrated from Ibn Jurayj, from Ibn Shihāb, regarding His statement {He increases in creation what He wills} [Fāṭir 1], he said: \A beautiful voice.\"" [Weak]"""
"21063","(21057) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī ibn Maymūn al-Raqqī narrated to us: al-Firyābī narrated to us: Sufyān narrated from al-Aʿmash, from Ibrāhīm, from ʿUbaydah, from ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \Recite to me.\"" I said: \""Shall I recite to you"," when it was revealed to you?\"" He said: So I began reciting Sūrat al-Nisā'. When I reached the verse {And how [will it be] when We bring from every nation a witness and We bring you"," [O Muḥammad]"," against these as a witness} [al-Nisā' 41]"," he said: \""That is sufficient for you.\"" I turned and saw that his eyes were flowing with tears.\n\nIt was narrated by al-Bukhārī in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from al-Firyābī"," and both al-Bukhārī and Muslim narrated it through other chains from al-Aʿmash. [Authentic — Agreed upon]"""
"21064","(21058) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn Ziyād narrated to us: Ibrāhīm ibn Mūsā narrated to us: al-Walīd ibn Muslim narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī informed us: Abū ʿAmr ibn Ḥamdān and Abū Bakr ibn Quraysh informed us, saying: al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān narrated to us: ʿAbdullāh ibn Muḥammad ibn Sālim and Ṣafwān ibn Ṣāliḥ narrated to us, saying: al-Walīd ibn Muslim narrated from Ismāʿīl ibn Rāfiʿ, who narrated to me: Ibn Abī Mulaykah narrated from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Sā'ib, who said: Saʿd ibn Mālik came to us, and I went to him to greet him. He asked me about my lineage, and I told him. He said: \Welcome"," nephew! I have been told that you have a beautiful voice in reciting the Qur'an. I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: 'Indeed"," this Qur'an was sent down with sorrow"," so when you recite it"," weep. And if you cannot weep"," then feign weeping.'\""\n\nThe wording is that of al-Sulamī. In the narration of Abū ʿAbdillāh"," he said: Saʿd ibn Abī Waqqāṣ came to us"," his sight having been lost"," and I went to him to greet him. He said: \""Who are you?\"" I informed him"," and he said: \""O nephew","\"" and he mentioned the hadith"," adding at the end: \""And beautify [your voices] with it (the Qur'an). And whoever does not beautify [his voice] with it is not of us.\"" [Weak]"""
"21065","(21059) Abū ʿAlī al-Ḥusayn ibn Muḥammad al-Rūdhabārī informed us: Abū ʿAlī Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad ibn Ismāʿīl al-Ṣaffār narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Malik al-Daqīqī narrated to us: Rūḥ ibn ʿUbadah narrated to us: Mālik narrated.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me: Abū al-Naḍr al-Faqīh narrated to us: Hārūn ibn Mūsā narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā narrated, saying: I read to Mālik, from Abū al-Zinād, from al-Aʿraj, from Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \Beware of suspicion"," for suspicion is the most false of speech. Do not spy on one another"," do not search for one another's faults"," do not compete with one another in worldly matters"," do not envy one another"," do not hate one another"," and do not turn your backs on one another. And be"," O servants of Allah"," brothers.\""\n\nIt was narrated by al-Bukhārī in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbdullāh ibn Yūsuf from Mālik"," and Muslim narrated it from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā. [Authentic — Agreed upon]"""
"21066","(21060) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: al-ʿAbbās ibn Muḥammad al-Dawrī narrated to us: Wahb ibn Jarīr narrated to us: Shuʿbah narrated from al-Aʿmash, from Abū Ṣāliḥ, from Abū Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \Do not sever ties with one another"," do not turn your backs on one another"," do not hate one another"," and do not envy one another. And be"," servants of Allah"," brothers"," as Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic"," has commanded you.\""\n\nIt was narrated by Muslim in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī al-Ḥulwānī and others from Wahb ibn Jarīr. [Authentic — Agreed upon]"""
"21067","(21061) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me: Abū Muḥammad Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdullāh al-Muzanī and Abū ʿAlī Ḥāmid ibn Muḥammad al-Harwī informed us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū al-Qāsim ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Muḥammad al-Sirāj informed us: Abū ʿAlī Ḥāmid ibn Muḥammad al-Harwī informed us, saying: ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿĪsā narrated to us: Abū al-Yamān informed us: Shuʿayb informed us from al-Zuhrī, who said: Anas ibn Mālik informed me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \Do not hate one another"," do not envy one another"," and do not turn your backs on one another. And be"," servants of Allah"," brothers. It is not permissible for a Muslim to forsake his brother for more than three nights — the two meet and each turns away from the other. The best of the two is the one who initiates the greeting of peace.\""\n\nIt was narrated by al-Bukhārī in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū al-Yamān"," and Muslim narrated it through another chain from al-Zuhrī.\n\nAl-Shāfiʿī (may Allah have mercy on him) said: \""Allah has united the people through Islam and attributed them to it"," and it is the most noble of their lineages. So if a person loves"," let him love for its sake.\"" [Authentic — Agreed upon]"""
"21068","(21062) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us: Abū Ṭāhir Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Muḥammadbādhī narrated to us: Abū Qilābah narrated to us: Ḥusayn ibn Ḥafṣ narrated to us: Hishām ibn Saʿd narrated from Saʿīd al-Maqburī, from Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \Indeed"," Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic"," has removed from you the arrogance of the Days of Ignorance and boasting about one's forefathers. [Know that] a person is either a believing"," God-fearing [soul] or a wretched"," sinful one. All people are the children of Ādam"," and Ādam was created from dust. Let people cease boasting about their forefathers in the manner of the Days of Ignorance"," or they will become"," in the sight of Allah"," more contemptible than the dung beetle that pushes filth away with its nose.\"" [Weak]"""
"21069","(21063) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-Qāsim ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Ḥasan al-Asadī narrated to us orally: Abū Isḥāq Ibrāhīm ibn Ḥusayn ibn Dayzīl narrated to us: Ādam ibn Abī Iyās narrated to us: Shuʿbah narrated from Qatādah, from Anas (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \None of you will find the sweetness of faith until he loves a person only for the sake of Allah; until it is more beloved to him to be thrown into the Fire than to return to disbelief after Allah has saved him from it; and until Allah and His Messenger are more beloved to him than anything else.\""\n\nIt was narrated by al-Bukhārī in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Ādam"," and Muslim narrated it through another chain from Shuʿbah. [Authentic — Agreed upon]"""
"21070","(21064) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us: Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn ʿUmar ibn Ḥafṣ al-Zāhid informed us: Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbdullāh al-ʿAbsī informed us: Wakīʿ narrated from al-Aʿmash, from Abū Ṣāliḥ, from Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \By the One in whose Hand is my soul"," you will not enter Paradise until you believe"," and you will not truly believe until you love one another. Shall I not direct you to something which"," if you do it"," you will love one another? Spread the greeting of peace (salām) among yourselves.\""\n\nIt was narrated by Muslim in al-Ṣaḥīḥ through another chain from al-Aʿmash. [Authentic — Muslim 542]"""
"21071","(21065) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbdullāh ibn Yūsuf al-Aṣbahānī informed us: Abū Saʿīd ibn al-Aʿrābī narrated to us: al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad al-Zaʿfarānī narrated to us: Yazīd ibn Hārūn informed us: Hishām al-Dastuwāʾī informed us, from Yaḥyā ibn Abī Kathīr, from Yaʿīsh ibn al-Walīd, from al-Zubayr ibn al-ʿAwwām (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \The disease of the nations before you has crept upon you: envy and hatred. It is the shaver — the shaver of the religion"," not the shaver of hair. By the One in whose hand is the soul of Muḥammad"," you shall not believe until you love one another. Shall I not inform you of a thing which"," if you do it"," you will love one another? Spread salām amongst you.\"" [Weak]"""
"21072","(21066) It is also narrated from Sulaymān al-Taymī, from Yaḥyā, from Yaʿīsh, from a freed slave of al-Zubayr, from al-Zubayr, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said — Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhabārī informed us: Ismāʿīl al-Ṣaffār narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Ghālib narrated to us: ʿUbayd ibn ʿUbaydah narrated to us: Muʿtamir ibn Sulaymān narrated to us, from his father, and he mentioned it with the same meaning."
"21073","(21067) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū ʿAbdullāh ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Nuʿaym narrated to us: Qutaybah ibn Saʿīd narrated, from Mālik, from ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Maʿmar, from Saʿīd ibn Yasār, from Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Indeed"," Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic"," will say on the Day of Resurrection: 'Where are those who love one another for My glory? Today I shall shade them in My shade"," on a day when there is no shade except My shade.'\"" Muslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Qutaybah. [Ṣaḥīḥ — Muslim 2566]"""
"21074","(21068) Abū Bakr ibn Fūrak informed us: ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us: Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb narrated to us: Abū Dāwūd narrated to us: Shuʿbah narrated to us: Yaʿlā ibn ʿAṭāʾ narrated, from al-Walīd ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, from Abū Idrīs al-ʿĀidhī, who said: I came to ʿUbadah ibn al-Ṣāmit, and he said: \I shall narrate to you only what I heard from the tongue of Muḥammad (ﷺ): 'My love is obligatory for those who love one another for My sake"," My love is obligatory for those who maintain ties of kinship for My sake"," and My love is obligatory for those who show sincere affection for My sake' — or he said"," 'My love is obligatory for those who sacrifice for My sake.'\"" [Ḥasan]"""
"21075","(21069) Abū Bakr ibn Fūrak informed us: ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us: Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb narrated to us: Abū Dāwūd narrated to us: al-Ṣaʿq ibn Ḥazn narrated, from ʿAqīl al-Jaʿdī, from Abū Isḥāq, from Suwayd ibn Ghafalah, from ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \O ʿAbdullāh"," which bond of Islam is the strongest?\"" He said: \""I said: 'Allah and His Messenger know best.' He said: 'Loyalty for the sake of Allah"," love for the sake of Allah"," and hatred for the sake of Allah.'\"" That is also narrated in the ḥadīth of al-Barāʾ"," Ibn ʿAbbās"," and ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with them). Al-Shāfiʿī (may Allah have mercy on him) said: \""If a man singles out his people with love without directing towards others what is not permissible for him"," then this is a bond of kinship and not tribalism. Rarely is a person found without that which is beloved and that which is disliked in him.\"" [Weak]"""
"21076","(21070) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me: Abū al-Naḍr al-Faqīh narrated to us: Abū ʿAbdullāh Muḥammad ibn Naṣr al-Imām narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us: Khālid ibn ʿAbdullāh narrated, from Khālid, from Abū ʿUthmān, who said: ʿAmr ibn al-ʿĀṣ informed me that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) sent him with the army of Dhāt al-Salāsil. [Ṣaḥīḥ — Agreed upon]"
"21077","(21071) Abū ʿAbdillāh informed me: Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh al-Jawharī narrated to us: Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us: Abū Bishr al-Wāsiṭī narrated to us: Khālid narrated, from Khālid, from Abū ʿUthmān, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) sent ʿAmr ibn al-ʿĀṣ with the army of Dhāt al-Salāsil. He said: \So I came to him and said: 'Who among the people is most beloved to you?' In the ḥadīth of Yaḥyā"," I said: 'O Messenger of Allah"," who among the people is most beloved to you?' He said: 'ʿĀʾishah.' I said: 'Among the men?' He said: 'Her father.' I said: 'Then who?' He said: 'Then ʿUmar","' and he enumerated several men.\"" Al-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū Bishr al-Wāsiṭī"," who is Isḥāq ibn Shāhīn"," and Muslim narrated it from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā. [Ṣaḥīḥ — Previously mentioned]"""
"21078","(21072) Abū al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAbdān informed us: Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us: Abū Muslim narrated to us: al-Ḥajjāj ibn Minhāl narrated to us: Shuʿbah ibn al-Ḥajjāj narrated to us: ʿAdīy ibn Thābit narrated, and he said: I heard al-Barāʾ say: \I saw the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) with al-Ḥasan on his shoulder"," and he was saying: 'O Allah"," I love him"," so love him.'\"" Al-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Ḥajjāj"," and Muslim narrated it through another chain from Shuʿbah. [Ṣaḥīḥ — Agreed upon]"""
"21079","(21073) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us: Abū Ḥāmid ibn Bilāl narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn al-Rabīʿ al-Makkī narrated to us: Sufyān narrated, from ʿUbaydullāh ibn Abī Yazīd.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Aḥmad ibn Jaʿfar al-Qaṭīʿī narrated to us: ʿAbdullāh ibn Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal narrated to me: My father narrated to me: Sufyān narrated to me: ʿUbaydullāh ibn Abī Yazīd narrated, from Nāfiʿ ibn Jubayr, from Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Prophet (ﷺ), that he said to al-Ḥasan (may Allah be pleased with him): \O Allah"," I love him"," so love him"," and love those who love him.\"" Muslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal. [Ṣaḥīḥ — Agreed upon]"""
"21080","(21074) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān informed us in Baghdād: Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār narrated to us: al-Ḥasan ibn Mukram and Aḥmad ibn Mulāʿib both said: Hawdhalah ibn Khalīfah narrated to us: Sulaymān al-Taymī narrated, from Abū ʿUthmān al-Nahdī, from Usāmah ibn Zayd, who said: \The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) would take me and al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī and say: 'O Allah"," I love them both"," so love them both.'\"" Al-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from the ḥadīth of Muʿtamir ibn Sulaymān"," from his father. Al-Shāfiʿī (may Allah have mercy on him) said: \""What is disliked in a man's love for one of his people is that he direct towards others what Allah has forbidden — such as transgression"," defamation of lineage"," tribalism"," and hatred based on lineage — not hatred for the sake of Allah's disobedience or for a crime committed by the one who is hated. Rather"," one says: 'I hate him because he is the son of so-and-so.' This is pure tribalism"," by which testimony is rejected.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ — Bukhārī 3747]"""
"21081","(21075) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-Walīd informed me; Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār narrated to us; ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿUmar al-Qawārīrī narrated to us; Ḥammād ibn Zayd narrated from Ayyūb, from Ghaylān ibn Jarīr, from Ziyād ibn Rabbāḥ, from Abū Hurayrah (raḍiya Allāhu ʿanhu), from the Prophet (ﷺ), who said: \Whoever departs from obedience and separates from the jamāʿah and dies"," dies a death of jāhiliyyah. And whoever is killed under a blind banner"," raging for ʿaṣabiyyah and supporting ʿaṣabiyyah and calling to ʿaṣabiyyah"," and is killed"," his killing is a killing of jāhiliyyah. And whoever rises against my Ummah"," striking its righteous and its wicked alike"," not refraining from its believers and not fulfilling the covenant of those under covenant — he is not of my Ummah.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from al-Qawārīrī. [Ṣaḥīḥ — Muslim 1848]"""
"21082","(21076) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us; Muḥammad ibn Bakr informed us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; Maḥmūd ibn Khālid al-Dimashqī narrated to us; al-Firyābī narrated to us; Salamah ibn Bashr al-Dimashqī narrated from the daughter of Wāthilah ibn al-Asqaʿ that she heard her father say: I said, \O Messenger of Allāh"," what is ʿaṣabiyyah?\"" He said: \""That you aid your people in wrongdoing.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"21083","(21077) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq informed us; Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Isḥāq ibn Ayyūb al-Faqīh informed us; Muḥammad ibn Sulaymān ibn al-Ḥārith narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh narrated to us; Ḥumayd al-Ṭawīl narrated from Anas ibn Mālik, who said: A man came to the Prophet (ﷺ) and said, \O Messenger of Allāh"," is it ʿaṣabiyyah that a man support his people upon the truth?\"" He said: \""No.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"21084","(21078) Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Fūrak informed us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us; Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb narrated to us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; Shuʿbah and ʿAmr ibn Thābit narrated from Simāk ibn Ḥarb. He said: I heard ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAbd Allāh narrate from his father, who said: \The likeness of the one who aids his people upon other than the truth is like a camel that has fallen into a well and is being pulled out by its tail.\""\n\nAbū Dāwūd said: ʿAmr ibn Thābit raised it (as a marfūʿ hadith)"," but Shuʿbah did not raise it.\n\nThe Shaykh (raḥimahu Allāh) said: It has also been narrated from Sufyān and Isrāʾīl as marfūʿ. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"21085","(21079) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us; Muḥammad ibn Bakr informed us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; Ibn Bashshār narrated to us; Abū ʿĀmir narrated to us; Sufyān narrated from Simāk ibn Ḥarb, from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Masʿūd, from his father, who said: \I came to the Prophet (ﷺ) while he was in a tent of leather.\"" Then he mentioned something similar to it. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"21086","(21080) Abū Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf narrated to us; Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us; Abū Yaḥyā ibn Abī Masarrat narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Qazaʿah narrated to us; Isrāʾīl narrated from Simāk ibn Ḥarb, from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Masʿūd, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allāh (ﷺ) said: \Whoever aids in wrongdoing is like a camel that has fallen into a well and is being pulled out by its tail.\""\n\nAnd Zuhayr ibn Muʿāwiyah narrated it from Simāk as mawqūf. [Ṣaḥīḥ — as preceded above]"""
"21087","(21081) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān al-ʿAdl in Baghdād informed us; Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār narrated to us; Saʿdān ibn Naṣr narrated to us; Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah narrated from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Abī Yazīd, who heard Ibn ʿAbbās say: \Among the traits of jāhiliyyah are: defaming lineages"," wailing (over the dead)"," and he forgot the third.\"" Sufyān said: \""They say it is seeking rain through the stars (al-istisqāʾ biʾl-anwāʾ).\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAlī from Sufyān. And something to that effect has preceded as marfūʿ from the hadith of Abū Mālik al-Ashʿarī and Abū Hurayrah (raḍiya Allāhu ʿanhumā). [Ṣaḥīḥ — Bukhārī 3850]"""
"21088","(21082) Al-Sayyid Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn Dāwūd al-ʿAlawī informed us by dictation; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Rāmjārī informed us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Hāshim narrated to us; Wakīʿ narrated to us; ʿUyaynah ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Ghaṭafānī narrated from his father, from Abū Bakrah, who said: The Messenger of Allāh (ﷺ) said: \There is no sin more deserving that Allāh hasten its punishment for its companion in this world"," in addition to what He stores for him in the Hereafter"," than baghy (transgression/oppression) and severing the ties of kinship.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"21089","(21083) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-Faḍl ibn Ibrāhīm informed us; Aḥmad ibn Salamah narrated to us; Abū ʿAmmār al-Ḥusayn ibn Ḥurayth narrated to us; al-Faḍl ibn Mūsā narrated from al-Ḥusayn ibn Wāqid, from Maṭar; Qatādah narrated to me; Muṭarrif ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Shikhkhīr narrated from ʿIyāḍ ibn Ḥimār, who said: The Messenger of Allāh (ﷺ) stood among us and mentioned the hadith. In it he said: \And indeed"," Allāh revealed to me that you should be humble"," so that no one takes pride over another.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū ʿAmmār. [Ṣaḥīḥ — Muslim 2865]"""
"21090","(21084) And Abū Manṣūr Muḥammad ibn ʿĪsā al-Hamadhānī informed us there; Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Qaṭṭān in Aṣbahān narrated to us; Abū ʿAlī al-Ḥusayn ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Dārakī narrated to us; Abū ʿAmmār al-Ḥusayn ibn Ḥurayth al-Marwazī narrated to us, and he mentioned it with his isnād that the Prophet (ﷺ) said in his khutbah, adding: \And let no one commit baghy (transgression) against another.\""\n\nAnd al-Ḥajjāj ibn al-Ḥajjāj narrated it from Qatādah"," from Yazīd ibn ʿAbd Allāh"," from ʿIyāḍ"," from the Prophet (ﷺ)"," and he also added in it: \""So that no one commits baghy against another.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ — as preceded above]"""
"21091","(21085) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān al-ʿAdl informed us in Baghdād that Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār narrated to us that Aḥmad ibn Manṣūr narrated to us that ʿAbd al-Razzāq narrated to us that Maʿmar narrated from al-Zuhrī from Ḥumayd ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān from Abū Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \The strong man is not the one who can wrestle others to the ground.\"" They said: \""Then who is the strong man"," O Messenger of Allah?\"" He said: \""The one who controls himself at the time of anger.\"""""
"21092","(21086) Abū Ṣāliḥ ibn Abī Ṭāhir al-ʿAnbarī informed us that Yaḥyā ibn Manṣūr, my grandfather, narrated to us that Aḥmad ibn Salamah narrated to us that Qutaybah ibn Saʿīd al-Thaqafī narrated to us that al-Layth narrated from Ibn al-Hād from Saʿd ibn Ibrāhīm from Ḥumayd ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAmr ibn al-ʿĀṣ that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Among the major sins is a man's cursing his parents.\"" They said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," does a man curse his parents?\"" He said: \""Yes. He curses a man's father"," so the man curses his father"," and he curses a man's mother"," so the man curses his mother.\"""""
"21093","(21087) Abū Bakr ibn Fūrak informed us that ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us that Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb narrated to us that Abū Dāwūd narrated to us that ʿImrān al-Qaṭṭān and Hammām narrated from Qatādah. Hammām said: from Yazīd ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Shikhkhīr, and ʿImrān said: from Muṭarrif ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Shikhkhīr, from ʿIyāḍ ibn Ḥimār, who said: I said: \O Messenger of Allah"," a man from my people insults me while he is beneath me in status.\"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \""The two who curse each other are two devils who hurl lies and falsehood at one another. What they say is upon the one who initiated it"," until the oppressed one transgresses.\"""""
"21094","(21088) ʿAmr ibn Marzūq narrated from ʿImrān from Qatādah from Yazīd, and Ibn Abī ʿArūbah narrated from Qatādah from Muṭarrif up to his words \and they hurl lies at one another.\"" And Shaybān narrated from Qatādah"," who said: Muṭarrif ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Shikhkhīr narrated from ʿIyāḍ ibn Ḥimār that he asked the Prophet ﷺ and said: \""O Prophet of Allah"," what do you say about a man who insults me while he is of lesser lineage than me?\"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \""The two who curse each other are two devils who hurl lies and falsehood at one another.\"" And it used to be said"," and he mentioned the meaning of what follows it. Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us that Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Abī Dāwūd al-Munādī narrated to us that Yūnus ibn Muḥammad narrated to us that Shaybān narrated from Qatādah"," and he mentioned it.\n\nAnd that wording has been established from the ḥadīth of Abū Hurayrah without what precedes it."""
"21095","(21089) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn Nuʿaym narrated to us that Qutaybah ibn Saʿīd narrated to us that Ismāʿīl ibn Jaʿfar narrated from al-ʿAlāʾ from his father from Abū Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \The two who curse each other — what they say is upon the one who initiated it"," unless the oppressed one transgresses.\""\n\nAnd that has been narrated in the ḥadīth of Anas ibn Mālik. And in it is evidence of the permissibility of retaliating without transgressing or uttering obscenity. And the ḥadīth of ʿĀʾishah regarding the story of Zaynab bint Jaḥsh"," may Allah be pleased with them both"," is evidence of the permissibility of retaliation"," for she said: Zaynab bint Jaḥsh did not cease until she came to know that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not dislike one's retaliating. And forgiveness and forgoing retaliation is more preferable."""
"21096","(21090) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Muqriʾ informed us that al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us that Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us that Abū al-Rabīʿ narrated to us that Ismāʿīl ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us that al-ʿAlāʾ ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān narrated from his father from Abū Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet ﷺ said: \Charity does not decrease wealth"," and Allah increases not the one who forgives except in honour"," and no one shows humility for the sake of Allah except that Allah raises him.\"""""
"21097","(21091) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥām al-Muzakkī informed us that Abū Bakr ibn Abī Dārim al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us in Kūfah that Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Ayyūb al-Makhramī narrated to us that Saʿīd ibn Muḥammad al-Jarmī narrated to us that Yaʿqūb ibn Abī al-Mutaʾyid narrated from Abū Isḥāq from al-Ḥārith from ʿAlī, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Shall I not direct you to the most noble of character traits in this world and the Hereafter?\"" He then said: \""You forgive the one who wrongs you"," you give the one who deprives you"," and you maintain ties with the one who severs them from you.\"""""
"21098","(21092) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us that Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Bālawayh narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn Shādhān al-Jawharī narrated to us that Saʿīd ibn Sulaymān narrated to us that Sulaymān ibn Dāwūd al-Yamāmī narrated from Yaḥyā ibn Abī Kathīr from Abū Salamah from Abū Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \There are three qualities; whoever possesses them"," Allah will grant him an easy reckoning and admit him into Paradise by His Mercy.\"" They said: \""Who are they"," O Messenger of Allah?\"" He said: \""You give the one who deprives you"," you forgive the one who wrongs you"," and you maintain ties with the one who severs them from you.\"" He said: \""If I do that"," what is my reward"," O Messenger of Allah?\"" He said: \""That you be given an easy reckoning and that Allah admit you into Paradise by His Mercy.\"""""
"21099","(21093) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us that Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us that Abū Dāwūd narrated to us that Musaddad narrated to us that Yaḥyā narrated from Abī Ghifār who narrated to us that Abū Tamīmah al-Hujaymī narrated to us — and Abū Tamīmah's name is Ṭarīf ibn Mujālid — from Abū Jurry Jābir ibn Sulaym, who said: I saw a man from whom the people would take guidance in their opinions; he would say nothing but that they would follow it. I said: \Who is this?\"" They said: \""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\"" I said: \""Upon you be peace"," O Messenger of Allah","\"" twice. He said: \""Do not say 'Upon you be peace","' for 'Upon you be peace' is the greeting of the dead. Say: 'Peace be upon you.'\"" He said: I said: \""Are you the Messenger of Allah?\"" He said: \""I am the Messenger of Allah"," the One whom"," if harm befalls you and you call upon Him"," He removes it from you; and if a year of drought afflicts you and you call upon Him"," He causes it to grow for you; and if you are in a barren land or desert and your mount goes astray and you call upon Him"," He returns it to you.\"" He said: I said: \""Give me a counsel.\"" He said: \""Never curse anyone.\"" He said: \""After that I never cursed a free man"," nor a slave"," nor a camel"," nor a sheep.\"" He said: \""And do not belittle any act of goodness"," even if it is that you speak to your brother while your face is cheerful toward him"," for that is from among acts of goodness. And raise your lower garment to the middle of the shin; if you refuse"," then to the ankles. And beware of letting the lower garment trail"," for that is from arrogance"," and Allah does not love arrogance. And if a man insults you and reproaches you with what he knows about you"," do not reproach him with what you know about him"," for the burden of that is upon him.\"""""
"21100","(21094) Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad ibn Ḥamm al-Isfarāʾinī narrated to us there that Abū ʿAmr Ismāʿīl ibn Najayd al-Sulamī informed us that Abū Muslim Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbd Allāh narrated to us that Abū ʿĀṣim narrated from Yazīd ibn Abī ʿUbayd from Salamah ibn al-Akwʿ, who said: I set out intending al-Ghābah when I heard a slave of ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAwf saying: \The milch camels of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ have been seized.\"" He said: I said: \""Who seized them?\"" He said: \""Ghatafān and Fazārah.\"" He said: I ascended the ridge and cried out: \""Yā ṣabāḥāh! Yā ṣabāḥāh!\"" Then I set out running in their tracks until I recovered them from them. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came with a group of his Companions. I said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," the people are thirsty; we hastened before they could water their flocks.\"" He said: \""O son of al-Akwʿ"," you have gained the upper hand"," so be generous"," for the people of Ghatafān are hospitable.\"""""
"21101","(21095) Abu al-Hasan 'Ali ibn Ahmad ibn 'Abdān narrated to us — Ahmad ibn 'Ubayd al-Saffār narrated to us — al-Hasan ibn 'Ali al-Ma'marī narrated to us — Hishām ibn 'Ammār narrated to us — Sadaqah ibn Khālid narrated to us — Zayd ibn Wāqid narrated from Busr ibn 'Ubayd Allah — from 'Ā'idh Allah, Abū Idrīs al-Khawlānī — from Abū al-Dardā', who said:\n\nI was sitting with the Prophet ﷺ when Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, came forward, holding the edge of his garment, such that his knees became exposed. He said: \As for this companion of yours"," he has taken a risk.\"" He offered salām and said: \""There was something between me and 'Umar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb"," and I acted hastily"," then he left. I asked him to forgive me"," but he refused me and withdrew into his house. So I have come to you.\"" He [the Prophet ﷺ] said: \""May Allah forgive you"," O Abu Bakr\"" — three times. Then 'Umar"," may Allah be pleased with him"," felt remorse and came to the house of Abu Bakr"," may Allah be pleased with him"," and asked: 'Is Abu Bakr present?' They said: 'No.' So he came to the Prophet ﷺ"," and the face of the Prophet ﷺ began to change [in expression]"," until Abu Bakr became concerned. He knelt upon his knees and said: 'O Messenger of Allah"," by Allah"," I was the wrongdoer — twice.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'O people"," indeed Allah"," glorified and exalted is He"," sent me to you"," and you said: \""He has lied","\"" and Abu Bakr said: \""He has spoken the truth","\"" and he consoled me with himself and his wealth. Will you not leave my companion to me?' He said this twice. And he was not harmed after that."""
"21102","(21096) Abu al-Hasan 'Ali ibn Muḥammad al-Muqri' narrated to us — al-Hasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us — Yūsuf ibn Ya'qūb narrated to us — Muḥammad ibn Abī Bakr narrated to us — Yaḥyā ibn Sa'īd narrated to us — from Ibn 'Ajlān — Sa'īd ibn Abī Sa'īd narrated to me — from Abū Hurayrah, who said:\n\nA man was reviling Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was sitting [there]. He [the Prophet ﷺ] was amazed and smiling. When the man persisted in this, Abu Bakr responded to him with some of his words. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ became angry and stood up. Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, followed him and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, he was reviling me while you were sitting. When I responded to him with some of his words, you became angry and stood up.' He said: 'There was with you one who was defending you. When you responded to him, Satan seated himself, and I cannot sit with Satan.' Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'O Abu Bakr, there is no servant who is wronged with an injustice and then forgives it for the sake of Allah, Mighty and Majestic, except that Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will strengthen his support through it.'"
"21103","(21097) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh narrated to us — Abu al-Hasan al-Ṭarā'ifī narrated to us — 'Uthmān ibn Sa'īd narrated to us — Hārūn ibn Ma'rūf al-Baghdādī narrated to us — 'Abd Allāh ibn Wahb narrated to us — Abū Ṣakhr narrated from Abū Ḥāzim — from Abū Ṣāliḥ — from Abū Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, who said:\n\nThe Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \The believer is one who is befriended"," and there is no good in one who is not befriended nor who befriends others.\"""""
"21104","(21098) Abū Bakr ibn Fūrak narrated to us — 'Abd Allāh ibn Ja'far narrated to us — Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb narrated to us — Abū Dāwūd narrated to us — Ibrāhīm ibn Sa'd narrated from al-Zuhrī.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq narrated to us — Abu al-'Abbās al-Aṣamm narrated to us — al-Rabī' narrated to us — al-Shāfi'ī narrated to us — Ibrāhīm ibn Sa'd ibn Ibrāhīm narrated from Ibn Shihāb — from Abū Bakr ibn 'Abd al-Raḥmān — from Marwān ibn al-Ḥakam — from 'Abd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Aswad ibn 'Abd Yaghūth that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Indeed"," there is wisdom in some poetry.\""\n\nThe wording is that of the ḥadīth of al-Shāfi'ī. And in the narration of Abū Dāwūd"," he said: from Ubayy ibn Ka'b"," from the Prophet ﷺ"," who said: \""Indeed"," there is wisdom in some poetry.\"""""
"21105","(21099) And Abū Naṣr ibn Qatādah narrated to us — Abū Muḥammad Aḥmad ibn Isḥāq al-Harawī narrated to us — 'Ali ibn Muḥammad ibn 'Īsā narrated to us — Abu al-Yamān narrated to us — Shu'ayb narrated from al-Zuhrī — Abu al-Yamān informed me that Abū Bakr ibn 'Abd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Ḥārith ibn Hishām informed him that Marwān ibn al-Ḥakam informed him that 'Abd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Aswad informed him that Ubayy ibn Ka'b al-Anṣārī informed him that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Indeed"," there is wisdom in some poetry.\"""""
"21106","(21100) Abu al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn Dāwūd al-'Alawī, may Allah have mercy on him, narrated to us dictating — Abū Ḥāmid ibn al-Sharqī narrated to us — 'Ali ibn Sa'īd al-Nasawī narrated to us — Bakr ibn Bakkār narrated to us — Shu'bah narrated to us — Simāk ibn Ḥarb narrated to us — from 'Ikrimah — from Ibn 'Abbās, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said:\n\nThe Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Indeed"," there is wisdom in some poetry.\"""""
"21107","(21101) Abu 'Abd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us — Abu 'Abd Allāh Muḥammad ibn 'Abd Allāh al-Saffār narrated to us — Aḥmad ibn 'Iṣām narrated to us — Rūḥ narrated to us — Shu'bah said: I heard 'Abd al-Malik ibn 'Umayr say: I heard Abū Salamah ibn 'Abd al-Raḥmān narrate from Abū Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, that he said:\n\nThe Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \The truest verse of poetry that the Arabs have spoken is: 'Everything"," save Allah"," is falsehood.'\"""""
"21108","(21102) Abu al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān in Baghdad narrated to us — Ismā'īl ibn Muḥammad al-Saffār narrated to us — Aḥmad ibn Manṣūr narrated to us — 'Abd al-Razzāq narrated to us — Ma'mar narrated from al-Zuhrī — from Ibn al-Musayyib that Ḥassān ibn Thābit said — addressing a group among whom was Abū Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him:\n\n\I adjure you by Allah"," did you hear the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'Answer on my behalf — may Allah support you with the Holy Spirit (Rūḥ al-Qudus)?'\"" He said: \""O Allah"," yes.\"""""
"21109","(21103) Abu 'Abd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us — Abu al-Ḥasan Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn 'Ubdūs narrated to us — 'Uthmān ibn Sa'īd al-Dārimī said: I read to Abu al-Yamān that Shu'ayb ibn Abī Ḥamzah informed him from al-Zuhrī, who said: Abū Salamah ibn 'Abd al-Raḥmān informed me that he heard Ḥassān ibn Thābit al-Anṣārī seeking testimony from Abū Hurayrah: \I adjure you by Allah"," have you heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'O Ḥassān"," answer on behalf of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ — O Allah"," support him with the Holy Spirit (Rūḥ al-Qudus)?'\"" Abū Hurayrah"," may Allah be pleased with him"," said: \""Yes.\"""""
"21110","(21104) Abu 'Ali al-Rūdhbārī narrated to us — Abū Muḥammad ibn Shawdhb al-Muqri' al-Wāṣiṭī therein narrated to us — Aḥmad ibn Sinān narrated to us — Wahb ibn Jarīr narrated to us — Shu'bah narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abu 'Abd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to me — Abu al-Naḍr al-Faqīh narrated to us — 'Uthmān ibn Sa'īd al-Dārimī narrated to us — Sulaymān ibn Ḥarb narrated to us — Shu'bah narrated from 'Adī ibn Thābit — from al-Barā' ibn 'Āzib that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Ḥassān: \Satirize them"," and Jibrīl is with you.\"" This is the wording of the ḥadīth of Wahb. And in the narration of Sulaymān: \""Satirize them\"" — or he said: \""Revile them\"" — \""and Jibrīl is with you.\"""""
"21111","(21105) Abu 'Abd Allah, the hafiz, informed us: Abu al-Hasan Ahmad ibn Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Saydalani al-'Adl, by dictation, narrated to us: Isma'il ibn Qutaybah narrated to us: Yahya ibn Yahya informed us: Yahya ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, from Hisham ibn 'Urwah, from his father, from 'A'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her, she said: Hassan said: \O Messenger of Allah"," grant me permission regarding Abu Sufyan.\"" He said: \""Then what about my kinship with him?\"" He said: \""By the One Who honoured you"," I will surely extract you from them as a hair is extracted from dough.\"" Then Hassan recited:\n\nIndeed"," the pinnacle of glory belongs to the family of Hashim","\nThe daughter of Makhzum — and your father is a slave.\n\n[It was] reported by Muslim in al-Sahih from Yahya ibn Yahya"," and both [al-Bukhari and Muslim] reported it without the poetry from the hadith of 'Abadah from Hisham.\n[Authentic. Agreed upon.]"""
"21112","(21106) Abu al-Hasan 'Ali ibn Ahmad ibn 'Abdana informed us: Ahmad ibn 'Ubayd al-Saffar narrated to us: Ibn Milhan narrated to us: Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated to us: al-Layth narrated to us, from Khalid, that is, ibn Yazid, from Sa'id ibn Abi Hilal, from 'Umarah ibn Ghaziyyah, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, from Abu Salamah ibn 'Abd al-Rahman, from 'A'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her, that the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: \Satirize the Quraysh"," for it is more severe upon them than the striking of arrows.\"" So he sent to Ibn Rawahah and said: \""Satirize them.\"" So he satirized them"," but it did not satisfy [him]. Then he sent to Ka'b ibn Malik. Then he sent to Hassan ibn Thabit. When he entered upon him"," Hassan said: \""The time has come for you to send to this lion that strikes with its tail.\"" Then he stuck out his tongue and began to move it"," and said: \""By the One Who sent you with the Truth"," I will surely tear them apart with my tongue as hides are torn apart.\"" The Messenger of Allah"," peace be upon him"," said: \""Do not be hasty"," for Abu Bakr is the most knowledgeable of the Quraysh regarding their lineages"," and I have a lineage among them"," so that my lineage may be clarified for you.\"" So Hassan came to [Abu Bakr] and then returned and said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," he has clarified for me your lineage. By the One Who sent you with the Truth"," I will surely extract you from them as a hair is extracted from dough.\"" 'A'ishah"," may Allah be pleased with her"," said: \""I heard the Messenger of Allah"," peace be upon him"," saying to Hassan: 'The Spirit of Holiness (Ruh al-Qudus) will continue to support you as long as you defend the Messenger of Allah.'\"" And she said: \""I heard the Messenger of Allah"," peace be upon him"," saying: 'Hassan satirized them and brought relief and satisfaction.'\"" Then Hassan recited:\n\n(1) You satirized Muhammad"," so I answered on his behalf","\nAnd with Allah is the reward for that.\n\n(2) You satirized Muhammad — righteous and upright","\nThe Messenger of Allah"," whose noble trait is fidelity.\n\n(3) For my father"," his father"," and my honour","\nAre a shield for the honour of Muhammad against you.\n\n(4) May I lose my daughters if you do not see her","\nRaising the dust on both sides at her appointed time.\n\n(5) They clash with their lances"," unsheathed","\nUpon their shoulders — thirsty"," bloodthirsty spears.\n\n(6) Our steeds will come charging","\nTheir mouths wiped by women with their veils.\n\n(7) If you turn away from us"," we shall perform 'Umrah","\nAnd the victory will come and the veil will be lifted.\n\n(8) Otherwise"," await the battle of a day","\nOn which Allah will whomever He wills honour.\n\n(9) Allah has said: \""I have sent a servant","\nWho speaks the truth — there is no concealment in it.\""\n\n(10) Allah has said: \""I have sent an army —\nThey are the Ansar"," whose resolve is to meet [the enemy].\""\n\n(11) We have"," every day"," from Ma'add","\nEither captivity"," or battle"," or satire.\n\n(12) Whoever among you satirizes the Messenger of Allah","\nOr praises him or supports him — they are all equal.\n\n(13) And Gabriel is the Messenger of Allah's envoy among us","\nAnd the Spirit of Holiness — there is no equal to Him.\n\n[It was] reported by Muslim in al-Sahih from 'Abd al-Malik ibn Shu'ayb ibn al-Layth"," from his father"," from his grandfather.\n[Authentic.]"""
"21113","(21107) Abu 'Abd Allah, the hafiz, informed us: Abu 'Abd Allah Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Salamah and 'Abd Allah ibn Muhammad said: Bishr ibn Khalid narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Sulayman, from Abu al-Duha, from Masruq, he said: \I entered upon 'A'ishah"," may Allah be pleased with her"," and with her was Hassan ibn Thabit"," reciting poetry to her"," embellishing with verses of his"," saying:\n\nChaste and dignified — never suspected of any blame","\nAnd she goes hungry for the flesh of heedless women.\n\n'A'ishah"," may Allah be pleased with her"," said: 'But you are not like that.'\"" Masruq said: \""I said to her: 'Why do you permit him to enter upon you"," when Allah"," exalted is He"," has said: (And the one who took upon himself the greater sin among them — for him is a great punishment)?' She said: 'And what punishment is more severe than blindness?' And she said: 'Indeed"," he used to defend — or satirize on behalf of — the Messenger of Allah"," peace be upon him.'\""\n\n[It was] reported by al-Bukhari and Muslim in al-Sahih from Bishr ibn Khalid.\n[Authentic. Agreed upon.]"""
"21114","(21108) Abu al-Husayn ibn Bishran in Baghdad informed us: Isma'il ibn Muhammad al-Saffar narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Mansur narrated to us: 'Abd al-Razzaq informed us: Ma'mar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Ka'b ibn Malik, from his father, that he said to the Prophet, peace be upon him: \Indeed"," Allah"," exalted is He"," has revealed regarding poetry what He has revealed.\"" He said: \""Indeed"," the believer strives with his sword and his tongue. By the One in Whose Hand is my soul"," it is as if you were striking them with volleys of arrows.\"" — Thus he said.\n[Authentic. Reported by 'Abd al-Razzaq.]"""
"21115","(21109) And Abu Bakr ibn al-Hasan al-Qadi informed us: Abu Sahl ibn Ziyad al-Qattan narrated to us: 'Abd al-Karim ibn al-Haytham narrated to us: Abu al-Yaman informed me: Shu'ayb informed me, from al-Zuhri, who informed me: 'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Abd Allah ibn Ka'b ibn Malik informed me that Ka'b ibn Malik, when Allah revealed regarding poetry what He revealed, came to the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, and said to him: \Indeed"," Allah has revealed regarding poetry what you know. So what is your view on it?\"" The Messenger of Allah"," peace be upon him"," said: \""Indeed"," the believer strives with his sword and his tongue.\""\n[Authentic. Previously cited.]"""
"21116","(21110) And Abu Bakr ibn al-Hasan al-Qadi informed us: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us: Abu al-Yaman al-Hakam ibn Nafi' informed us: Shu'ayb informed us, from al-Zuhri, who said: And Bashir ibn Ka'b ibn Malik used to narrate that Ka'b ibn Malik used to narrate that the Prophet, peace be upon him, said: \By the One in Whose Hand is my soul"," it is as if you were striking them with arrows in what you say to them of poetry.\""\n[Authentic. Previously cited.]"""
"21117","(21111) Abu 'Ali al-Rudhbari informed us: Abu Bakr ibn Dasah narrated to us: Abu Dawud narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Marwazi narrated to me: 'Ali ibn Husayn narrated to me, from his father, from Yazid al-Nahwi, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas, he said: Regarding the verse (And the poets — the deviators follow them) [al-Shu'ara' 224], this was abrogated and an exception was made: (Except those who believe and do righteous deeds and remember Allah much) [al-Shu'ara' 227].\n[Weak.]"
"21118","(21112) Abu al-Husayn ibn al-Fadl al-Qattan in Baghdad informed us: 'Abd Allah ibn Ja'far ibn Durustawayh narrated to us: Ya'qub ibn Sufyan narrated to us: Abu Salih and Ibn Bukayr said: al-Layth narrated to us: Yunus narrated to me, from Ibn Shihab, who informed me: al-Haytham ibn Abi Sinan informed me that he heard Abu Hurayrah, while he was relating stories, mentioning the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, saying: \You have a brother who does not speak obscenities.\"" He meant by that 'Abd Allah ibn Rawahah. He recited:\n\n(1) Among us is the Messenger of Allah"," reciting His Book","\nWhen the dawn of goodness breaks forth"," radiant.\n\n(2) He showed us guidance after blindness"," and our hearts\nAre certain of it — that what which he said will come to pass.\n\n(3) He spends the night with his side removed from his bed","\nWhen the couches grow heavy upon the disbelievers.\n\n[It was] reported by al-Bukhari in al-Sahih from Yahya ibn Bukayr.\n[Authentic. Al-Bukhari 1155"," 6151.]"""
"21119","(21113) Abu 'Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami informed us: Abu 'Amr ibn Hamdan informed us: Abu Ya'la narrated to us: 'Abbad ibn Musa narrated to us: 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Thabit narrated to us, from Hisham ibn 'Urwah, from his father, from 'A'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her, she said: \The Messenger of Allah"," peace be upon him"," was asked about poetry"," and he said: 'It is speech — its good is good and its ugly is ugly.'\""\n\nA group [of narrators] connected it"," and the authentic version from the Prophet"," peace be upon him"," is mursal.\n[Hasan.]"""
"21120","(21114) Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn al-Hasan informed us: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us: al-Hasan ibn 'Ali ibn 'Affan narrated to us: Abu Usamah narrated to us: 'Abd al-Malik narrated to us: Simak ibn Harb narrated to us, from 'Ikrimah, he said: \'A'ishah"," may Allah be pleased with her"," was asked: 'Did the Messenger of Allah"," peace by upon him"," ever recite any poetry?' She said: 'Sometimes he would enter saying: \""You will come with news from one who has not provided you with provisions.\""'\""\n[Weak.]"""
"21121","(21115) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us: Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb al-Karābīsī narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Abī Bakr narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Naṣr ibn Qatādah and Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Fārisī informed us — they both came to us in Bayhaq, and both of their hearings are sound — they said: Abū ʿAmr ibn Maṭar narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Ayyūb narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Abī Bakr al-Muqaddamī narrated to us: Abū Maʿshar al-Baṣrī, i.e., al-Barāʾ, narrated to me: Ṣadaqah ibn Ṭaysalah narrated to me: Maʿn ibn Thaʿlabah al-Māzinī narrated to me: al-Aʿshā al-Māzinī said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and recited to him:\n\n(1) \O Master of mankind and Sovereign of the Arabs","\n\n(2) I have encountered a sharp-tongued one of the sharp-tongued.\n\n(3) I went out seeking her sustenance in Rajab.\""\n\nAnd in the narration of al-Karābīsī:\n\n\""I went out seeking her"," but she pursued me with spears and conflict; she broke the covenant and wallowed in sin. And they are the worst of those who overcome"," for those whom they overcome.\""\n\nHe said: So the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) began to repeat it"," saying: \""And they are the worst of those who overcome"," for those whom they overcome.\"" [Weak]"""
"21122","(21116) And ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us: Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd informed us: Aḥmad ibn Yaḥyā al-Ḥulwānī narrated to us: Ibrāhīm ibn ʿArʿarah narrated to us: Yūsuf ibn Yazīd narrated to us: Abū Maʿshar al-Barāʾ informed us: Ṭaysalah ibn Nubātah al-Māzinī narrated to me: my father and the tribe narrated to me from al-Aʿshā ibn Māʿiz, who said: I came to the Prophet (ﷺ) and recited to him, and he mentioned it, except that he said: \I married a sharp-tongued woman","\"" and he said: \""I went seeking her","\"" and he said: \""She opposed me with spears and fled.\"" He did not mention the fifth verse. And others narrated from Ibrāhīm: Ṭaysalah ibn Ṣadaqah. [Weak. Previously mentioned.]"""
"21123","(21117) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān informed us in Baghdād: Abū ʿAmr ibn al-Sammāk narrated to us: Ḥanbal ibn Isḥāq narrated to us: ʿĀṣim ibn ʿAlī narrated to us: Qays ibn al-Rabīʿ narrated to me: Simāk narrated to me from Jābir ibn Samurah, who said: I said to him: \Did you see the Prophet (ﷺ)?\"" He said: \""Yes.\"" He was long in silence"," and his Companions would recite poetry to him and mention matters of the Jāhiliyyah"," and they would laugh"," and he would smile along with them when they laughed. [Weak]"""
"21124","(21118) And Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān informed us: ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us: Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥamīd narrated to us: Sharīk narrated to us from Simāk, who said: I said to Jābir ibn Samurah: \Did you sit in the company of the Prophet (ﷺ)?\"" He said: \""Yes.\"" He was long in silent"," and he laughed little. The Companions of the Prophet (ﷺ) would recite poetry"," and the Prophet (ﷺ) would smile. [Weak]"""
"21125","(21119) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān informed us: Abū ʿAmr ibn al-Sammāk narrated to us: Ḥanbal ibn Isḥāq narrated to us: Ibrāhīm ibn Naṣr narrated to us: Abū Ismāʿīl narrated to us from Abī al-Bilād from al-Shaʿbī, who said: I saw some of the Companions of the Prophet (ﷺ) reciting poetry near the House or around the House — I do not know except that he said they were in iḥrām. Ibrāhīm expressed doubt. [Weak]"
"21126","(21120) He said: And Ḥanbal ibn Isḥāq narrated to us: ʿUthmān ibn Abī Shaybah narrated to us: Ismāʿīl ibn ʿUlayyah narrated to us from Ayyūb from Muḥammad ibn Kathīb ibn Aflaḥ, who said: The last session in which we sat with Zayd ibn Thābit was a session in which we recited poetry. [Weak]"
"21127","(21121) Abū al-Qāsim ibn Abī Hāshim al-ʿAlawī informed us in al-Kūfah: Abū Jaʿfar ibn Duḥaym narrated to us: Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbdullāh narrated to us: Wakīʿ narrated to us from al-Aʿmash: Abū Khālid al-Wālibī narrated to us, who said: We used to sit in the company of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ), and they would recite poetry and recall their days in the Jāhiliyyah. [Sound]"
"21128","(21122) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān informed us: Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn Manṣūr narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us: Maʿmar informed us from Maṭar al-Warrāq from Muṭarrif ibn ʿAbdullāh, who said: I accompanied ʿImrān ibn Ḥuṣayn from al-Baṣrah to Makkah, and he would recite poetry to me every day. Then he said to me: \Poetry is speech"," and among speech there is truth and falsehood.\"" [Weak]"""
"21129","(21123) Abū ʿAbdullālāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Hārūn ibn Sulaymān narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Mahdī narrated to us from Saʿīd ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān from Muḥammad ibn Sīrīn, who said: The poets among the Companions of Muḥammad (ﷺ) were ʿAbdullāh ibn Rawāḥah, Ḥassān ibn Thābit, and Kaʿb ibn Mālik. [Good]"
"21130","(21124) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr said: Abū al-ʿAbbās narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār narrated to us: Wakīʿ narrated to us from Usāmah ibn Zayd from ʿIkrimah from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: \When one of you recites something from the Qurʾān and does not know its interpretation"," let him seek it in poetry"," for it is the dīwān (literary treasury) of the Arabs.\""\n\nThis is the correct version"," as a mawqūf narration. [Good through other chains.]"""
"21131","(21125) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿUqbah al-Shaybānī in Kūfah narrated to us, Aḥmad ibn Mūsā al-Ḥimār narrated to us, al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī narrated to us, Yaḥyā ibn Ādam narrated to us, Isrāʾīl narrated from Simāk, from ʿIkrimah, from Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with them both), who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Indeed"," there is wisdom in some poetry"," and when anything of the Qurʾān becomes obscure to you"," seek it in poetry"," for it is Arabic.\""\n\nThe first wording was narrated by other than Isrāʾīl from Simāk. As for the second wording"," it may be from the statement of Ibn ʿAbbās and was incorporated into the hadith. [Weak]"""
"21132","(21126) Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn Dāwūd al-ʿAlawī narrated to us by dictation, ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn al-Sharqī narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā al-Dhuhlī narrated to us, ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Mahdī narrated from Mālik ibn Anas, from al-Zuhrī, from Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyab, from Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Prophet (ﷺ), who said: \The strong man is not the one who can wrestle"," but rather the strong man is the one who controls himself at the time of anger.\""\n\nIt was recorded in the Ṣaḥīḥ from the hadith of Mālik. [Sound — Agreed Upon]"""
"21133","(21127) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān informed us in Baghdad, ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us, Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān narrated to us, Abū al-Yamān informed us, Shuʿayb ibn Abī Ḥamzah narrated from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Abī Ḥusayn, Nawfal ibn Musāḥiq narrated to me, from Saʿīd ibn Zayd, from the Prophet (ﷺ), that he said: \Among the gravest forms of usury is the unjust violation of a Muslim's honour.\"" [Sound]"""
"21134","(21128) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bushrān informed us, Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad narrated to us, Aḥmad ibn Manṣūr narrated to us, ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us, Maʿmar narrated from Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAmr ibn ʿUthmān, who reported it, saying: The Prophet (ﷺ) said: \Indeed"," among the forms of usury is the defamation of honour"," and the severest form of defamation is satirical invective.\"" The narration is that of one of the two defamers.\n\nThis is a mursal narration"," and it corroborates what preceded it.\n\nIt was also narrated by ʿImrān ibn Anas al-Makkī from Ibn Abī Mulaykah"," from ʿĀʾishah"," from the Prophet (ﷺ)"," as a musnad narration with the first wording.\n\nAl-Bukhārī said: He was not corroborated in it. [Weak]"""
"21135","(21129) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzakkī, Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī, and Abū Ṣādiq ibn Abī al-Fawāriṣ al-ʿAṭṭār informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, al-ʿAbbās ibn al-Walīd ibn Mazīd al-Bayrūtī informed us, Muḥammad ibn Shuʿayb ibn Shābūr informed us, Shaybān ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān narrated from Sulaymān al-Aʿmash, who informed them, from ʿAmr ibn Murrah, from Yūsuf ibn Māḥik, from ʿUbayd ibn ʿUmayr, from ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her), who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Indeed"," the greatest of people in falsehood is a man who satirises another man and thereby satirises his entire tribe"," and a man who disowns his father and commits adultery with his mother.\"" [Sound]"""
"21136","(21130) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf informed us, Abū Saʿīd ibn al-Aʿrābī informed us, al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad al-Zaʿfarānī narrated to us, Sufyān narrated from ʿAmr ibn Dīnār, from ʿIkrimah: that a poet came to the Prophet (ﷺ), and the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \O Bilāl"," silence his tongue for me.\"" So he was given forty dirhams and a garment. He said: \""You have silenced my tongue — by Allah"," you have silenced my tongue.\""\n\nThis is a munqaṭiʿ narration. It was narrated from Muḥammad ibn Muslim from ʿAmr as a musnad narration mentioning Ibn ʿAbbās"," but it is not preserved. [Weak]"""
"21137","(21131) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās — al-Aṣamm — narrated to us, Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib narrated to us, Abū Dāwūd al-Ṭayālisī narrated to us, Yaʿqūb al-Ṭāʾifī narrated to me, my father narrated from Najīd ibn ʿImrān ibn Ḥuṣayn, from his father, that he gave a gift to a poet. It was said to him: \O Abū Najīd"," do you give to a poet?\"" He said: \""Indeed"," I ransom my honour from him.\"" [Weak]"""
"21138","(21132) ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us, Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us, Aḥmad ibn Yaḥyā al-Ḥulwānī narrated to us, Ibn Bakkār narrated to us, ʿAbd al-Ḥamīd ibn al-Ḥasan al-Hilālī narrated from Muḥammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Jābir (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Every act of kindness is charity. Whatever a man spends on himself and his family is recorded as charity for him. Whatever he spends to protect his honour is recorded as charity for him. Whatever he spends in expenditure"," Allah shall replace it for him"," except what is spent in building or in disobedience.\""\n\nI said to Muḥammad ibn al-Munkadir: \""What does 'protect his honour' mean?\"" He said: \""He gives to the poet and the sharp-tongued person.\"" [Weak]"""
"21139","(21133) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us, Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī narrated to us, Saʿīd ibn Sulaymān narrated to us, Miswar ibn al-Ṣalt narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn al-Munkadir narrated from Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh, mentioning something similar to it as a marfūʿ narration, except that he said: Muḥammad said: \We said to Jābir: 'What does \""protecting a man's honour\"" mean?'\"" He said: \""He means the poet and the sharp-tongued person — as though he is saying: the one whose tongue is to be guarded against.\""\n\nIt was narrated by other than Miswar in a manner similar to the hadith of al-Hilālī. This hadith is known through both of them"," though neither is strong. And Allah knows best. [Weak]"""
"21140","(21134) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us, Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Maḥmawayh al-ʿAskarī narrated to us, Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad al-Qalānisī narrated to us, Ādam ibn Abī Iyās narrated to us, Shuʿbah narrated from Khālid al-Ḥadhāʾ, from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Bakrah, from his father: that a man was mentioned in the presence of the Prophet (ﷺ), and a man praised him with good words. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Woe to you! You have cut the neck of your companion.\"" He repeated it several times: \""If one of you must praise his brother"," let him say"," 'I think such and such","' if he believes that to be the case. His reckoning is with Allah"," and let no one vouch for anyone before Allah.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Ādam. [Sound — Agreed Upon]"""
"21141","(21135) Our Shaikh and Imam Abu al-Tayyib Sahl ibn Muhammad ibn Sulayman, may Allah have mercy upon him, narrated to us by dictation: Abu Sahl Bishr ibn Abi Yahya al-Mihrajani narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn Ali al-Dhuhli narrated to us: Yahya ibn Yahya narrated to us: Yazid ibn Zurai' narrated from Khalid al-Hadha' from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakrah from his father, who said: A man praised another man in the presence of the Prophet ﷺ, so he said: \Woe to you! You have cut the neck of your companion.\"" Repeatedly"," he said: \""When one of you must praise his companion"," let him say: 'I think so-and-so is such-and-such"," and Allah is his Reckoner"," and I do not vouch for anyone before Allah.' I think him to be such-and-such"," if he knows that about him.\"" Muslim narrated it in his Sahih from Yahya ibn Yahya."""
"21142","(21136) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us: Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Sakani al-Bukhari narrated to us: Salih ibn Muhammad al-Hafiz narrated to us: Muhammad ibn al-Sabbah narrated to us: Isma'il ibn Zakariyya narrated to us: Yazid ibn 'Abd Allah narrated from Abu Burdah from Abu Musa, who said: The Prophet ﷺ heard a man praising another man and lavishing praise upon him, so he said: \You have destroyed"," or you have broken the back of the man.\"" Al-Bukhari and Muslim narrated it in their two Sahihs from Muhammad ibn al-Sabbah."""
"21143","(21137) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us: Ahmad ibn Ja'far narrated to us: 'Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us: My father narrated to us: 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated from Sufyan from Habib ibn Abi Thabit from Mujahid from Abu Ma'mar, who said: A man stood and praised one of the commanders, so al-Miqdad began throwing dust in his face and said: \The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded us to throw dust in the faces of those who lavish praise.\"" Muslim narrated it in his Sahih from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah and others from 'Abd al-Rahman. [Sahih. Muslim 3552]"""
"21144","(21138) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us: Abu Bakr al-Isma'ili informed us: Abu Ya'la narrated to us: Abu Khaythamah narrated to us. And Abu Bakr informed us: 'Imran ibn Musa narrated to us: 'Uthman narrated to us. Both said: Jarir narrated from Mansur from Abu Wa'il from 'Abd Allah, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Truthfulness leads to righteousness"," and righteousness leads to Paradise. A man continues to speak the truth until he is recorded with Allah as a truthful one. Falsehood leads to wickedness"," and wickedness leads to the Fire. A man continues to lie until he is recorded with Allah as a liar.\"" Al-Bukhari narrated it in his Sahih from 'Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah"," and Muslim narrated it from Abu Khaythamah and 'Uthman. [Sahih. Agreed upon]"""
"21145","(21139) Abu Bakr ibn Furak informed us: 'Abd Allah ibn Ja'far narrated to us: Yunus ibn Habib narrated to us: Abu Dawud narrated to us: Shu'bah and al-Mas'udi narrated from 'Amr ibn Murrah. He said: I heard 'Abd Allah ibn al-Harith narrating from Abu Kathir al-Zubaydi from 'Abd Allah ibn 'Amr ibn al-'As, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Beware of injustice"," for injustice will be darknesses on the Day of Resurrection. And beware of obscenity"," for Allah does not love obscenity or its proliferation. And bevere of miserliness"," for it destroyed those before you. It commanded them to sever ties of kinship"," so they severed them; it commanded them to be miserly"," so they were miserly; and it commanded them to be wicked"," so they were wicked.\"" Then a man stood and said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," which Islam is best?\"" Shu'bah said in his hadith: \""The one from whose tongue and hand the Muslims are safe.\"" And al-Mas'udi said: \""That the Muslims be safe from his tongue and his hand.\"" Then that man or another stood and said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," which emigration is best?\"" He said: \""That you abandon what your Lord dislikes.\"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \""Emigration is of two types: the emigration of the city-dweller and the emigration of the bedouin. As for the bedouin"," he responds when he is called and obeys when he is commanded. As for the city-dweller"," his trial is greater and his reward is greater.\"" Al-Mas'udi said: A man called out to him and said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," which martyr is best?\"" He said: \""That your steed be hamstrung and your blood be shed.\"" [Sahih. Al-Tayalisi 2386]"""
"21146","(21140) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us: Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Ishaq al-Faqih informed us: Muhammad ibn Ghalib ibn Harb narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Sabiq narrated to us: Isra'il ibn Yunus narrated from al-A'mash from Ibrahim from 'Alqamah from 'Abd Allah, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \The believer is not one who faults others"," nor one who curses"," nor one who is obscene and foul-mouthed.\"" [Hasan]"""
"21147","(21141) Abu al-Husayn ibn Bishran informed us: Abu 'Amr ibn al-Sammak narrated to us: Hanbal ibn Ishaq narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn Nasr narrated to us: Abu Isma'il narrated from al-Mujalid from al-Sha'bi, who said: We were reciting poetry to one another near the Ka'bah when Ibn al-Zubayr came toward us and said: \In the Sanctuary of Allah and near the House of Allah"," you recite poetry?\"" A man from the Ansar who was with us"," a Companion of the Prophet ﷺ"," said: \""O Ibn al-Zubayr"," there is no harm upon you if you do not corrupt yourself. The Prophet of Allah ﷺ only forbade poetry in which women were mentioned and wealth was squandered.\"" [Da'if]"""
"21148","(21142) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us: Abu al-Qasim 'Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Hasan al-Asadi in Hamadhan informed us: Ibrahim ibn al-Husayn narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir al-Hizami narrated to us: al-Hajjaj ibn Dhi al-Raqibah ibn 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Ka'b ibn Zuhayr ibn Abi Salma al-Muzani narrated from his father from his grandfather, who said: Ka'b and Bujayr, the two sons of Zuhayr, set out. Then he mentioned the hadith concerning the Islam of Bujayr, what Ka'b composed of poetry regarding him, and then Ka'b's arrival before the Prophet ﷺ, his acceptance of Islam, and his recitation of his qasidah, the beginning of which is:\n\n(1) Su'ad has departed, and my heart today is lovesick, enslaved by her, not freed from its bondage.\n\n(2) And Su'ad, on the morning of the farewell when they departed, is but a melodious-voiced one with downcast, kohl-lined eyes.\n\n(3) She reveals the flash of her teeth when she smiles, as though it were a spring overflowing from a cup.\n\nHe mentioned the entire qasidah at length, which consists of forty-eight verses, and among its verses are:\n\n(1) I was told that the Messenger of Allah has threatened me, yet forgiveness from the Messenger of Allah is hoped for.\n\n(2) Gently, O Messenger, the One who granted you the supererogatory gift of the Furqan, in which are admonitions and detailed exposition.\n\n(3) Do not take the words of slanderers, for I have not committed a crime, even though accusations against me have multiplied.\n\n(4) Indeed, the Messenger is a light by which illumination is sought, and a drawn sword from the swords of Allah.\n\n(5) Among a band of Qurayshi youths, their spokesman said: \In the valley of Makkah"," when they embraced Islam"," they caused it to tremble.\""\n\nHe said: And Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir narrated to me: Muhammad ibn Fulayh narrated to me from Musa ibn 'Uqbah"," who said: Ka'b ibn Zuhayr recited \""Banat Su'ad\"" before the Prophet ﷺ in his mosque in Madinah. When he reached his verse:\n\n(1) Indeed"," the Messenger is a sword by which illumination is sought"," a drawn Indian blade from the swords of Allah.\n\n(2) Among a band of Qurayshi youths"," their spokesman said: \""In the valley of Makkah"," when they embraced Islam"," they caused it to tremble.\""\n\nThe Messenger of Allah ﷺ gestured with his sleeve toward the people so that they would come and listen to it. [Da'if]"""
"21149","(21143) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us: Abu 'Abd Allah al-Husayn ibn al-Hasan ibn Ayyub al-Tusi informed us: Abu Hatim al-Razi narrated to us: 'Ubayd Allah ibn Musa narrated to us: Hanzalah ibn Abi Sufyan al-Jumahi al-Makki narrated from Salim from Ibn 'Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \That the belly of one of you be filled with pus is better for him than that it be filled with poetry.\"" Al-Bukhari narrated it in his Sahih from 'Ubayd Allah ibn Musa. [Sahih. Bukhari 6154]"""
"21150","(21148) Abu Tahir al-Faqih informed us: Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn 'Umar ibn Hafs al-Zahid narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn 'Abd Allah al-'Absi informed us: Waki' narrated from al-A'mash from Abu Salih from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \That the belly of a man be filled with pus that he can see is better for him than that it be filled with poetry.\"" Al-Bukhari narrated it in his Sahih through another chain from al-A'mash. Muslim narrated it from Abu Sa'id al-Ashajj from Waki'. He also narrated it as a marfu' hadith from the narration of Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas"," may Allah be pleased with him. [Sahih. Agreed upon]"""
"21151","(21145) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, that Muḥammad ibn Shādhān and Aḥmad ibn Salamah both said: Qutaybah ibn Saʿīd narrated to us, that al-Layth narrated from Ibn al-Hād, from Yuḥannas, the freed slave of Muṣʿab ibn al-Zubayr, from Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī, who said: \While we were travelling with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at al-ʿArj"," a poet appeared reciting poetry. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Seize the Shayṭān' or 'Hold back the Shayṭān"," for it is better for a man's belly to be filled with pus than to be filled with poetry.'\""\n\nIt was narrated by Muslim in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Qutaybah. [Ṣaḥīḥ — agreed upon]"""
"21152","(21146) Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī informed us that Abū al-Ḥasan al-Kārizī narrated to us, that ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz narrated from Abī ʿUbayd, who said: al-Aṣmaʿī said regarding His word \ḥattā yariyahu\"": it is from al-wary"," meaning that his belly becomes inflamed. Abū ʿUbayd said: and I heard Yazīd ibn Hārūn narrate from al-Sharqī ibn al-Quṭāmī from Mujāld from al-Shaʿbī that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \""For the belly of any one of you to be filled with pus until it inflames is better for him than for it to be filled with poetry\"" — meaning poetry by which the Prophet ﷺ was satirized.\n\nAbū ʿUbayd said: and what I hold regarding this hadith is other than this view"," for that by which the Prophet ﷺ was satirized"," even if it were half a verse"," would constitute disbelief. However"," its meaning in my view is that his heart becomes so filled with poetry that it overwhelms him"," distracting him from the Qurʾān and from the remembrance of Allah"," so that poetry becomes dominant over him"," regardless of what poetry it may be. [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"21153","(21147) Abū Bakr ibn Fūrak informed us that ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us, that Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb narrated to us, that Abū Dāwūd narrated to us, that al-Aswad ibn Shaybān narrated to us, that Abū Nawfal ibn Abī ʿAqrab said: It was said to ʿĀʾishah, may Allah be pleased with her: \Was poetry recited in the presence of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?\"" She said: \""It was the most hateful of speech to him.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"21154","(21148) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us that Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us, that Tamtām narrated to us, that Yaḥyā ibn Yūsuf al-Zammī narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me that Abū Bakr ibn ʿAbd Allāh informed us that al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān narrated to us, that Muslim ibn Salām narrated to us. Both said: Abū Bakr ibn ʿAyyāsh narrated from Abī Ḥuṣayn from Abī Ṣāliḥ from Abī Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet ﷺ, who said: \May the slave of the dīnār"," the dirham"," the qaṭīfah"," and the khameeṣah perish. If he is given"," he is pleased"," and if he is not given"," he does not fulfil [his duty].\""\n\nIt was narrated by al-Bukhārī in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Yaḥyā ibn Yūsuf"," and Muslim narrated it from Muslim ibn Salām. [Ṣaḥīḥ — agreed upon]"""
"21155","(21149) Abū al-Ḥasan ibn Abī ʿAlī al-Saqqāʾ and Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Muqriʾ both informed us that al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us, that Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, that ʿAmr ibn Marzūq informed us that ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Dīnār narrated from his father from Abī Ṣāliḥ from Abī Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet ﷺ, who said: \May the slave of the dīnār"," the slave of the dirham"," and the slave of the khameeṣah perish. If he is given"," he is pleased"," and if he is withheld from"," he is angered. May he perish and be overturned. And if he is pricked by a thorn"," he cannot extract it.\"" And he mentioned the hadith.\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ"," saying: \""And ʿAmr mentioned it.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ — agreed upon]"""
"21156","(21150) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān in Baghdād informed us that Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār narrated to us that Zakariyyā ibn Yaḥyā al-Marwazī narrated to us, that Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah narrated from Ibn al-Munkadir that he heard ʿUrwah ibn al-Zubayr say: ʿĀʾishah, may Allah be pleased with her, narrated to us that a man sought permission to enter upon the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: \Grant him permission. What a wretched man of the tribe\"" or \""What a wretched member of the tribe.\"" When he entered"," he spoke gently to him. ʿĀʾishah said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," you said what you said about him"," yet when he entered"," you spoke gently to him.\"" He said: \""O ʿĀʾishah"," the worst of people in station on the Day of Resurrection is the one whom people abandon or leave alone out of fear of his obscenity.\""\n\nIt was narrated by al-Bukhārī and Muslim in their Ṣaḥīḥs from Qutaybah and others from Sufyān. [Ṣaḥīḥ — agreed upon]"""
"21157","(21151) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to me that Muḥammad ibn Nuʿaym narrated to me that Ismāʿīl ibn Sālim informed us that Hushaym informed us that Khālid narrated from Abī Qilābah from Abī al-Ashʿath al-Ṣanʿānī from ʿUbadah ibn al-Ṣāmit, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: \The Messenger of Allah ﷺ took a pledge from us"," as he took from the women"," that we would not associate anything with Allah"," nor steal"," nor commit adultery"," nor kill our children"," nor that any of us would slander another. Whoever among you fulfils it"," his reward is upon Allah. And whoever among you commits a sin and the prescribed punishment is carried out upon him"," it is his expiation. And whoever is concealed by Allah"," his affair is with Allah: if He wills"," He will punish him"," and if He wills"," He will forgive him.\""\n\nIt was narrated by Muslim in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Ismāʿīl ibn Sālim. [Ṣaḥīḥ — agreed upon]"""
"21158","(21152) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us that Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us that Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbd Allāh informed us that Muḥammad ibn ʿUbayd narrated to us that al-Aʿmash narrated from Abī Ṣāliḥ from Abī Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Two things among the people constitute disbelief (kufr): wailing over the dead and defaming lineage.\""\n\nIt was narrated by Muslim in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Numayr from his father and Muḥammad ibn ʿUbayd. [Ṣaḥīḥ — Muslim 67]"""
"21159","(21153) Abū al-Ḥusayn ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Bishrān in Baghdād informed us that Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār narrated to us that Saʿdān ibn Naṣr narrated to us that Sufyān narrated from Ziyād ibn ʿIlaqah, who heard Usāmah ibn Sharīk say: \I witnessed the Bedouins asking the Prophet ﷺ: 'Is there any sin upon us regarding such and such?' He said: 'Servants of Allah"," Allah has removed hardship (ḥaraj) from you"," except for one who takes something from the honour of his brother — that is the one upon whom hardship falls.' They said: 'O Messenger of Allah"," what is the best thing that a servant can be given?' He said: 'Good character (khuluq ḥasan).'\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"21160","(21154) Abū Bakr ibn Fūrak informed us that ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us that Abū Masʿūd Aḥmad ibn al-Furāt narrated to us that Yaʿlā ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṭanāfisī narrated to us that al-Aʿmash narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us that Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us that al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn ʿAffān narrated to us that Ibn Numayr narrated from al-Aʿmash from Abī Ṣāliḥ from Abī Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \You will find the worst of people on the Day of Resurrection to be the one with two faces (dhū al-wajhayn)"," who comes to these people with the speech of these people and comes to those people with the speech of those people.\""\n\nAnd in the narration of al-Ṭanāfisī: \""You will find among the worst of people the one with two faces.\"" Al-Aʿmash said: \""He is the one who comes to these people with one face and to those people with another face.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ — agreed upon]"""
"21161","(21155) Abū ʿAmr al-Adīb informed us — Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī informed us — al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān narrated to us — Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah narrated to us — Ḥafṣ and Abū Muʿāwiyah narrated from al-Aʿmash, with his chain of narration, the same as the one preceding it: \Among the worst of Allah's creation is the possessor of two faces"," who comes to these people with one face and to those people with another face.\""\n\nal-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿUmar ibn Ḥafṣ"," from his father"," from al-Aʿmash"," with the first wording. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"21162","(21156) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq and Abū ʿAbdullāh Isḥāq ibn Muḥammad ibn Yūsūs al-Sūsī both said — Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us — Abū Umayyah al-Ṭarsūsī narrated to us — Manṣūr ibn Salamah narrated to us — Sulaymān ibn Bilāl narrated from Muḥammad ibn ʿAjlān, from ʿUbaydullāh ibn Sulaymān, from his father, from Abū Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \It is not befitting for the possessor of two faces to be a trustee (amīn).\""\n\n[Ḥasan]"""
"21163","(21157) ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us — Aḥmad ibn ʔUbayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us — Tamtām narrated to us — Abū Nuʿaym al-Faḍl ibn Dukayn narrated to us — Sharīk narrated from al-Rukayn ibn al-Rabīʿ, from Nuʿaym ibn Ḥanẓalah, from ʿAmmār ibn Yāṣir, from the Prophet ﷺ, that he said: \Whoever is a possessor of two faces in this world will have two tongues of fire on the Day of Resurrection.\""\n\n[Ḍaʿīf]"""
"21164","(21158) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me — ʿAbdullāh ibn Saʿd narrated to us — Ibrāhīm ibn Abī Ṭālib narrated to us — Muḥammad ibn al-Muthannā and Muḥammad ibn Bashshār both said — Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us — Shuʿbah said: I heard Abū Isḥāq narrating — he said: I heard Abū al-Aḥwaṣ narrating from ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: Indeed, Muḥammad ﷺ said: \Shall I not inform you what al-ʿAḍhah is? It is al-namīmah — tale-carrying that causes discord between people.\"" And indeed"," Muḥammad ﷺ said: \""A man may continue to speak the truth until he is recorded with Allah as a ṣiddīq (truthful one)"," and a man may continue to lie until he is recorded with Allah as a kadhdhāb (liar).\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn al-Muthannā and Muḥammad ibn Bashshār. [Ṣaḥīḥ — Muttafaq ʿalayh]"""
"21165","(21159) Anas ibn Mālik, may Allah be pleased with him, narrated from the Prophet ﷺ that he said: \Do you know what al-ʿAḍhah is?\"" They said: \""Allah and His Messenger know best.\"" He said: \""It is carrying tales between people in such a way that it causes enmity between them.\""\n\n[Ḍaʿīf]"""
"21166","(21160) Hammām ibn al-Ḥārith, may Allah be pleased with him, said: We were sitting with Ḥudhayfah, may Allah be pleased with him, when he mentioned a marfūʿ hadith. Ḥudhayfah said: I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: \The tale-carrier (al-ghībah eater) shall not enter Paradise.\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"21167","(21161) Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh, may Allah be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \When a man speaks while looking this way and that"," that conversation becomes a trust (amānah).\""\n\n[Ḥasan]"""
"21168","(21162) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us — Muḥammad ibn Bakr narrated to us — Abū Dāwūd narrated to us — Aḥmad ibn Ṣāliḥ said: I recited to ʿAbdullāh ibn Nāfiʿ, who said: Ibn Abī Dhiʾb informed me from the brother of Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh, from Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Gatherings are to be held in confidence (amānah)"," except three gatherings: the shedding of unlawful blood"," the commission of unlawful sexual intercourse"," or the seizure of wealth without right.\""\n\n[Ḍaʿīf]"""
"21169","(21163) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Muqriʾ informed us — al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us — Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us — Abū al-Rabīʿ informed us — Ismāʿīl ibn Jaʿfar narrated —\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me — Abū ʿAmr ibn Ḥamdān informed us — Abū Yaʿlā narrated to us — Yaḥyā ibn Ayyūb narrated to us — Ismāʿīl ibn Jaʿfar, from al-ʿAlāʾ, from his father, from Abū Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Do you know what al-ghībah (backbiting) is?\"" They said: \""Allah and His Messenger know best.\"" He said: \""It is mentioning your brother with that which he dislikes.\"" It was said: \""What if what I say about my brother is true?\"" He said: \""If it is as you say"," then you have backbited him; and if it is not as you say"," then you have slandered him (buhtān).\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Yaḥyā ibn Ayyūb and others. [Ṣaḥīḥ — Muslim 2589]"""
"21170","(21164) ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us — Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us — al-Asfāṭī narrated to us — Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn Yūnus narrated to us — Abū Bakr ibn ʿAyyāsh narrated from al-Aʿmash, from Saʿīd ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn Jurayj, from Abū Barzah, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \O you who have believed with your tongues but faith has not entered your hearts — do not backbit the Muslims"," and do not seek out their faults. For whoever seeks out the faults of his Muslim brother"," Allah will expose his faults and disgrace him even within the confines of his own home.\""\n\n[Ḍaʿīf]"""
"21171","(21165) Abū Ḥāmid Aḥmad ibn ʿAlī al-Muqriʾ al-Khusrūjirdī, may Allah have mercy upon him, informed us: Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Ismāʿīl al-Warrāq narrated to us in Baghdād: Abū al-Qāsim ʿAbdullāh ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz narrated to us: ʿAlī ibn al-Jaʿd narrated to us: Sufyān al-Thawrī narrated from ʿAlī ibn al-Aqmar, from Abī Ḥudhayfah, from ʿĀʾishah, may Allah be pleased with her, who said: \I imitated a person"," so the Prophet ﷺ said to me: 'I would not like to imitate a person"," even if I were given such and such.'\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"21172","(21166) Abū ʿAbdullāh Isḥāq ibn Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf al-Sūsī informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: al-ʿAbbās ibn al-Walīd ibn Mazīd narrated to us: My father narrated to me, he said: I heard al-Awzāʿī say: Yaḥyā ibn Abī Kathīr narrated to me: Abū Qilābah al-Jarmī narrated to me, he said: Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Jarmī said to Abū Masʿūd: \How did you hear the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say regarding 'they claim' (zaʿamū)?\"" He said: \""I heard him say: 'What a wretched mount of a man it is (biʾsa maṭiyyat al-rajul).'\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"21173","(21167) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us: Abū al-Faḍl ʿAbdūs ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn Manṣūr al-Naysābūrī narrated to us: Abū Ḥātim al-Rāzī narrated to us: al-Anṣārī narrated to me: Ḥumayd narrated from Anas: \The son of Umm Sulaym"," who was called Abū ʿUmayr"," used to be playfully engaged by the Prophet ﷺ when he came. One day he came and the Prophet ﷺ engaged him playfully but found him distressed. He said: 'Why do I see Abū ʿUmayr distressed?' They said: 'O Messenger of Allah"," his little finch (nughayr) with which he used to play has died.' So the Prophet ﷺ began calling out: 'O Abū ʿUmayr"," what did the little finch do (mā faʿala al-nughayr)?'\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"21174","(21168) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us: Khalaf ibn Hishām narrated to us: Khālid ibn ʿAbdullāh narrated from Ḥumayd, from Anas: \A man asked the Prophet ﷺ for a mount. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'We will mount you on a young camel (walad nāqah).' He said: 'O Messenger of Allah"," what shall I do with a young camel?' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Do camels give birth except to young ones (nāqāt)?'\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"21175","(21169) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us: Muḥammad ibn Bakr narrated to us: Abū Dāwūd narrated to us: Ibrāhīm ibn Mahdī narrated to us: Sharīk narrated from ʿĀṣim, from Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: \The Prophet ﷺ said to me: 'O Dhā al-Udhunayn (the one with two ears).'\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"21176","(21170) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me: Abū Aḥmad al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: Abū al-Ḥusayn Aḥmad ibn ʿUmayr narrated to us: Mūsā ibn ʿĀmir narrated to us: al-Walīd ibn Muslim narrated to me: ʿAbdullāh ibn al-ʿAlāʾ ibn Zabr narrated to me that he heard Busr ibn ʿUbaydullāh al-Ḥaḍramī, from Abī Idrīs al-Khawlānī, from ʿAwf ibn Mālik al-Ashjaʿī, who said: \I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ during the expedition of Tabūk while he was in a leather tent. I sat in the courtyard of the tent and greeted him"," and he returned the greeting and said: 'Enter"," O ʿAwf.' I said: 'All of me or part of me?' He said: 'All of you.' So I entered.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"21177","(21171) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us: Abū Dāwūd narrated to us: Ṣafwān ibn Ṣāliḥ narrated to us: al-Walīd narrated to us: ʿUthmān ibn Abī al-ʿĀtikah said: \He only said 'all of me' on account of the small size of the tent.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"21178","(21172) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān informed us in Baghdād: Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn Manṣūr narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us: Maʿmar narrated from Thābit, from Anas: \A man from the desert-dwellers whose name was Zāhir ibn Ḥizām or Ḥarām — the Prophet ﷺ loved him"," and he was of dark complexion. The Prophet ﷺ came to him one day while he was selling his goods. He embraced him from behind while the man could not see him. The man said: 'Let me go! Who is this?' He turned around and recognized the Prophet ﷺ"," and he did not cease pressing his back against the chest of the Prophet ﷺ once he recognized him. The Prophet ﷺ began saying: 'Who will buy this slave?' The man said: 'O Messenger of Allah"," then you will find me worthless (kāsid).' The Prophet ﷺ said: 'But with Allah you are not worthless","' or he said: 'But with Allah you are precious (ghālī).'\"" Our shaykh did not confirm it"," and there is a discrepancy regarding the name: it is said Ḥizām and it is said Ḥarām. ʿAbd al-Ghanī al-Ḥāfiẓ said: \""Ḥarām with a rāʾ is more correct.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"21179","(21173) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Muḥammad ibn Abī Ḥāmid al-Muqriʾ both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: al-ʿAbbās ibn Muḥammad al-Dūrī narrated to us: ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥasan narrated to us: ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Mubārak narrated from Usāmah ibn Zayd, from Saʿīd al-Maqburī, from Abī Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: \It was said: 'O Messenger of Allah"," you joke with us.' He said: 'I only speak the truth.'\"" [Ḥasan]"""
"21180","(21174) And ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us: Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd narrated to us: ʿUbayd ibn Sharīk narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Bukayr narrated to us: al-Layth narrated from Ibn ʿAjlān, from Saʿīd al-Maqburī, from Abī Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that he said: \I only speak the truth.\"" One of his companions said: \""You joke"," O Messenger of Allah.\"" He said: \""I only speak the truth.\"" One of his companions said: \""You joke"," O Messenger of Allah.\"" He said: \""I only speak the truth.\"" And ʿIkrimah narrated from the Prophet ﷺ in a mursal narration that he possessed a sense of humour (duʿābah). [Ḥasan]"""
"21181","(21175) Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī informed us that Abū al-Ḥasan al-Kārizī informed us; ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz narrated from Abū ʿUbayd, who said: Ibn ʿUlayyah narrated to me from Khālid al-Ḥadhāʾ from ʿIkrimah, who attributed it (marfūʿan). Abū ʿUbayd said: His statement \al-duʿābah\"" means joking (al-mizāḥ).\n[Weak]"""
"21182","(21176) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān informed us in Baghdād that Abū ʿAlī Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār narrated to us; Sulaymān ibn al-Ashʿath al-Sijistānī — that is, Abū Dāwūd — narrated to us.\n(Ḥ) And Abū al-Rūdhbārī informed us that Muḥammad ibn Bakr narrated to us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn ʿUthmān al-Dimashqī narrated to us; Abū Kaʿb Ayyūb ibn Muḥammad al-Saʿdī narrated to me; Sulaymān ibn Ḥabīb al-Muḥāribī narrated from Abū Umāmah, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \I guarantee a house on the outskirts of Paradise for the one who abandons disputing even if he is in the right; a house in the middle of Paradise for the one who abandons lying even if he is joking; and a house in the highest part of Paradise for the one who has good character.\""\n[Ḥasan]"""
"21183","(21177) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us that Muḥammad ibn Bakr narrated to us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Sulaymān al-Anbārī narrated to us; Ibn Numayr narrated from al-Aʿmash from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yasār from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Laylā, who said: The Companions of Muḥammad ﷺ narrated to us that they were traveling with the Prophet ﷺ when a man among them fell asleep. Some of them went to a rope he had with him and took it, frightening him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \It is not permissible for a Muslim to frighten another Muslim.\""\n[Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"21184","(21178) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū al-Walīd narrated to us; al-Sirāj narrated to us; Ziyād ibn Ayyūb narrated from Hushaym from Yūnus from al-Ḥasan regarding the child of zinā (illegitimate child), he said: \The child of lawful wedlock is not preferred over him except by piety.\""\n[Weak]"""
"21185","(21179) Abū Saʿd al-Mālinī informed us that Abū Aḥmad ibn ʿAdī informed us; Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Ayyūb al-Makhrāmī narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Mūsā al-Balkhī narrated to us. He said: I asked Abū ʿUbayd al-Qāsim ibn Sallām about the explanation of this (hadith), and he said: \As for the dyer (al-ṣabbāgh)"," he is the one who adds words to a hadith to adorn it with them. As for the goldsmith (al-ṣāʾigh)"," he is the one who fabricates a hadith that has no basis.\""\nThe Shaykh"," may Allah have mercy on him"," said: This is what has been narrated from him"," and it is possible that what is meant is the one who works with his hands"," and this is explicit in what has been narrated from Abū Saʿid. It has been attributed to lying — and Allah knows best — due to the frequency of his false promises despite his knowledge that he does not fulfill them. There is some question regarding the authenticity of this hadith.\nImām al-Shāfiʿī"," may Allah have mercy on him"," mentioned the testimony of one who takes compensation for good deeds"," and the evidence for its permissibility has been discussed in the Book of Hire and the Book of the Division of the Fayʾ and Spoils"," and elsewhere. He also mentioned the testimony of beggars"," and the evidence regarding who is permitted to beg and who is not has been discussed in the Book of the Division of Charitable Offerings. He also mentioned the testimony of one who attends a feast without being invited"," and the report concerning this has been discussed in the Book of the Wedding Feast"," so there is no point in repeating it. And regarding everyone whose testimony is rejected due to something he is upon"," Imām al-Shāfiʿī"," may Allah have mercy on him"," said: \""His testimony is only rejected as long as he remains upon that; but if he desists and repents"," his testimony is accepted.\"" The Shaykh said: The reports concerning this have been discussed in the Chapter on the Testimony of the Slanderer.\n[Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"21186","(21180) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū al-Walīd narrated to us; al-Sirāj narrated to us; Ziyād ibn Ayyūb narrated from Hushaym from Yūnus from al-Ḥasan regarding the child of zinā, he said: \The child of lawful wedlock is not preferred over him except by piety.\""\n[Weak]"""
"21187","(21181) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf al-Raffāʾ al-Baghdādī informed us that ʿUthmān ibn Muḥammad ibn Bishr narrated to us; Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq narrated to us; Ibn Abī Uways narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī al-Zinād narrated from his father from the jurists whose opinions are relied upon among the people of Madīnah, who used to say regarding the child of zinā: \His origin is an evil origin"," but if his conduct and character are good"," his testimony is valid"," and they used to consider freeing him to be commendable.\""\n[Weak]"""
"21188","(21182) ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us that Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd narrated to us; ʿUbayd ibn Sharīk narrated to us; Ibn Abī Maryam narrated to us; Nāfiʿ ibn Yazīd narrated to us.\n(Ḥ) And Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq informed us that Abū Muḥammad Daʿlaj ibn Aḥmad al-Sijzī narrated to us; Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Būshanjī narrated to us; Rūḥ ibn Ṣalāḥ narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Ayyūb and Nāfiʿ ibn Yazīd ibn al-Hād narrated from Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr ibn ʿAṭāʾ from ʿAṭāʾ ibn Yasār from Abū Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, that he heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \The testimony of a bedouin against a settled person is not valid.\"" And it is possible that this was stated regarding testimony that is subject to consideration"," and in matters where the witness is required to possess hidden expertise. The Shaykh Abū Sulaymān al-Khaṭṭābī"," may Allah have mercy on him"," said — as it has reached me — that the reason the testimony of the bedouins was disliked is due to their harshness in religion and their ignorance of the rulings of the Sharīʿah"," for they generally do not give testimony properly nor establish it correctly"," owing to their deficient knowledge of what alters it and changes its nature. And Allah knows best.\n[Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"21189","(21183) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū al-Walīd al-Faqīh narrated to us; al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān narrated to us; Abū Bakr — that is, Ibn Abī Shaybah — narrated to us; Muʿādh ibn Hishām narrated from al-Ashʿath from al-Ḥasan that he used to say regarding a slave and a dhimmī when they testify: \Their testimony is rejected; then if this one is freed and this one accepts Islam"," their testimony becomes valid.\""\n[Weak]"""
"21190","(21184) He said: And Abū Bakr narrated to us; Ibn Mahdī narrated from Ḥammād ibn Salamah from ʿAbd al-Karīm from ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb and ʿAṭāʾ that ʿUmar, may Allah be pleased with him, said: \Their testimony is valid.\"" And he mentioned the hadith."""
"21191","(21185) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Muḥammad ibn Ṣāliḥ ibn Hānī narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Nuʿaym narrated to us: Qutaybah ibn Saʿīd narrated to us: Jarīr narrated from al-Aʿmash, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAbd Allāh, from Saʿīd ibn Jubayr, from Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with them both), who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \You are heard"," and from you it is heard"," and from those who hear from you it is heard.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"21192","(21186) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-Walīd al-Faqīh informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān narrated to us: Abū Bakr narrated to us: Wakīʿ narrated from Isrāʾīl, from Jābir, from Masrūq and Shurayḥ, that they both said: \Testimony upon testimony is not accepted in a ḥadd"," and no surety is accepted in a ḥadd.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"21193","(21187) He said: And al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān narrated to us: Abū Bakr narrated to us: Ḥumayd ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān narrated from Ḥasan, from Layth, from ʬāʾ and Ṭāwūs, who said: \Testimony upon testimony is not accepted in a ḥadd.\"" And it has been narrated to us from al-Shaʿbī and Ibrāhīm"," and the reports on this have preceded under the chapter of averting the ḥudūd by means of doubts in the Book of Ḥudūd. [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"21194","(21188) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān informed us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us: Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān narrated to us: al-Ḥumaydī narrated to us: Sufyān narrated from al-Aswad ibn Qays, from Kulthūm ibn al-Aqmar, from Shurayḥ, who said: \I do not permit the testimony of one who conceals himself.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ in other than this chain]"""
"21195","(21189) He said: And Sufyān narrated to us, saying: Ruqyah narrated it to me from Bayān, from al-Shaʿbī: \He used not to permit the testimony of one who conceals himself.\"" He said: Then I heard it from Bayān. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"21196","(21190) Abū Ḥāzim al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-Faḍl ibn Khamīrūyah informed us: Aḥmad ibn Najdah narrated to us: Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr narrated to us: Hushaym informed us: al-Shaybānī informed us from Muḥammad ibn ʿUbayd Allāh al-Thaqafī: that ʿAmr ibn Ḥurayth used to permit his testimony and would say: \Thus is done with the treacherous one and the immoral one.\"" The Shaykh (may Allah have mercy on him) said: \""And this is what we hold.\"" Al-Shāfiʿī (may Allah have mercy on him) said"," as was narrated from him: \""Because ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) permitted the testimony of those who lay in wait for a man who was committing zinā"," but they did not complete four [witnesses].\"" He said: \""And this is the more likely of the two opinions.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"21197","(21191) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-Walīd al-Faqīh narrated to us: al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān narrated to us: Abū Bakr narrated to us. (Ḥ) And Abū al-Walīd informed us: Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Zuhayr narrated to us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Hāshim said: Wakīʿ narrated from Ismāʿīl al-Azraq, from al-Shaʿbī, who said: \The testimony of a witness upon a witness is not valid until they are two [i.e."," two direct witnesses].\"" The Shaykh (may Allah have mercy on him) said: \""Al-Shāfiʿī (may Allah have mercy on him) repeated here the chapter of testimony regarding the ḥudūd"," and we have mentioned the reports and narrations on this in the Book of Ḥudūd and the Book of Theft.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"21198","(21192) Abū Saʿīd al-Ṣayrafī narrated to us: Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm narrated to us: al-Rabīʿ said: al-Shāfiʿī said, from Sufyān. (Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-Walīd al-Faqīh narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us: ʿAlī ibn Ḥujr narrated to us: Hushaym narrated—all of them—from Muṭarrif, from al-Shaʿbī: \That two men testified before ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) against a man regarding theft"," so ʿAlī cut off his hand. Then they came with another man and said: 'This is the thief"," not the first one.' So ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) made the two witnesses liable for the blood-money of the hand of the first one who was cut"," and he said: 'Had I known that you did it deliberately"," I would have cut off your hands.' And he did not cut the second one.\"" The wording is that of Ḥushaym. And in the narration of Sufyān from Muṭarrif"," they said: \""And we were mistaken regarding the first one.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"21199","(21193) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-Walīd informed us: Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad narrated from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā, from Hushaym, from Manṣūr, from al-Ḥasan, who said: \If two witnesses testify regarding a killing"," then the killer is killed"," then one of the two witnesses retracts"," he is killed.\"" The Shaykh said: \""This is in the case where he said: 'I deliberately testified against him so that he would be killed","' while the first [killing] was a mistake.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"21200","(21194) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-Walīd informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān narrated to us: Ḥabbān narrated from Ibn al-Mubārak, from Sufyān, from Abī Ḥuṣayn, from Shurayḥ: \That a man testified before him with a testimony"," and Shurayḥ rendered judgment based upon it. Then the man retracted afterwards"," so he did not accept his word—meaning he did not annul the first [judgment]—and he did not accept his word regarding the retraction. Then the liability for compensation is in that which constitutes destruction of what has already passed.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"21201","(21195) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, that al-ʿAbbās al-Dūrī narrated to us, that Muḥammad ibn Muṣʿab narrated to us, that al-Awzāʿī said: I asked al-Zuhrī about a man who testified before the imām, and the imām recorded his testimony, but then he was called back and he changed it. Is his first testimony accepted, or the latter one? He said: He has no testimony in the first nor in the latter.\n\nThe Shaykh said: This pertains to retraction before the enforcement of the ruling based on the first testimony."
"21202","(21196) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us that Muḥammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, that Abū Dāwūd narrated to us, that Muḥammad ibn al-Ṣabbāḥ narrated to us, that Ibrāhīm ibn Saʿd narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Muḥammad ibn ʿĪsā narrated to us that ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar al-Makhramī and Ibrāhīm ibn Saʿd narrated, from Saʿd ibn Ibrāhīm, from al-Qāsim ibn Muḥammad, from ʿĀʾishah, may Allah be pleased with her, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Whoever introduces into our affair that which is not from it"," it is rejected.\"" Ibn ʿĪsā said: The Prophet ﷺ said: \""Whoever does a deed not in accordance with our affair"," it is rejected.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn al-Ṣabbāḥ"," and al-Bukhārī and Muslim both narrated it from the ḥadīth of Ibrāhīm and ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muttafaq ʿalayh]"""
"21203","(21197) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿid ibn Abī ʿAmr both informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, that Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib narrated to us, that ʿAbd al-Wahhāb ibn ʬAṭāʾ informed us, that Ibn Jurayj reported to us, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Abī Mulaykah, from Ibn ʿAbbās, may Allah be pleased with them both, from the Prophet ﷺ, who said: \Were people to be granted according to their claims"," men would claim the blood and wealth of other people. Rather"," the oath is upon the one against whom the claim is made.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muttafaq ʿalayh]"""
"21204","(21198) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū ʿAmr ibn Abī Jaʿfar reported to me, that ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf narrated to us, that Abū Ṭāhir narrated to us, that Ibn Wahb informed me, that Ibn Jurayj reported it with its chain, similarly.\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Abī al-Ṭāhir, from Ibn Wahb. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Preceded before it]"
"21205","(21199) Abū ʿAmr Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Adīb informed us that Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī informed me that ʿImrān ibn Mūsā narrated to us, that Naṣr ibn ʿAlī al-Jahḍamī narrated to us, that ʿAbd Allāh ibn Dāwūd informed us, that Ibn Jurayj reported from Ibn Abī Mulaykah that two women were engaged in leather-working in a house. One of them came out with an awl having pierced through her palm. The matter was brought to Ibn ʿAbbās, and Ibn ʿAbbās, may Allah be pleased with them both, said: Indeed, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Were people to be granted according to their claims"," men would claim the blood and wealth of other people. Remind her of Allah and recite over her: {Indeed"," those who exchange the covenant of Allah and their oaths for a small price…} [Āl ʿImrān:77].\"" So they reminded her"," and she confessed.\n\nIbn ʿAbbās said: The Prophet ﷺ said: \""The oath is upon the one against whom the claim is made.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Naṣr ibn ʿAlī. This is the narration of the majority from Ibn Jurayj. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"21206","(21200) Abū ʿAmr al-Adīb informed us that Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī informed me that al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān narrated to us, that Ṣafwān ibn Ṣāliḥ narrated to us, that al-Walīd — who is Ibn Muslim — narrated to us, that Ibn Jurayj narrated from Ibn Abī Mulaykah, who said: A woman was brought to me claiming that her companion had injured her with an awl until it appeared through her palm. She asked Ibn ʿAbbās, and he said: Indeed, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Were people to be granted according to their claims"," men would claim the blood and wealth of other people. Rather"," the proof is upon the claimant"," and the oath is upon the one from whom the claim is sought.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"21207","(21201) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us that Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us, that Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad al-Firyābī narrated to us, that al-Ḥasan ibn Sahl narrated to us, that ʿAbd Allāh ibn Idrīs narrated to us, that Ibn Jurayj and ʿUthmān ibn al-Aswad narrated from Ibn Abī Mulaykah, who said: I was a judge for Ibn al-Zubayr over al-Ṭāʾif. He mentioned the story of the two women. He said: I wrote to Ibn ʿAbbās, and Ibn ʿAbbās, may Allah be pleased with them both, wrote: Indeed, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Were people to be granted according to their claims"," men would claim the wealth and blood of a people. Rather"," the proof is upon the claimant"," and the oath is upon the one who denies.\"" And he mentioned the ḥadīth. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muttafaq ʿalayh]"""
"21208","(21202) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAbdūs informed us, that ʿUthmān ibn Saʿid al-Dārimī narrated to us, that al-Qaʿnabī narrated to us, that Nāfiʿ ibn ʿUmar narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us — and the wording is his — that Ismāʿīl ibn Qutaybah narrated to us, that Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah narrated to us, that Muḥammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, from Nāfiʿ ibn ʿUmar, from Ibn Abī Mulaykah, from Ibn ʿAbbās, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ruled that the oath is upon the one against whom the claim is made.\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Abī Nuʿaym and Khallād, from Nāfiʿ ibn ʿUmar, and Muslim narrated it from Abī Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah. It has already been mentioned in full in the Book of Testimonies. This is the narration of the majority from Nāfiʿ ibn ʿUmar al-Jumaḥī. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muttafaq ʿalayh]"
"21209","(21203) ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us that Abū al-Qāsim Sulaymān ibn Aḥmad al-Lakhmī informed us that Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm ibn Kathīr al-Ṣūrī informed us in his book to us, that al-Firyābī narrated to us, that Sufyān narrated, from Nāfiʿ ibn ʿUmar, from Ibn Abī Mulaykah, from Ibn ʿAbbās, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Prophet ﷺ said: \The proof is upon the claimant"," and the oath is upon the one against whom the claim is made.\""\n\nAbū al-Qāsim said: None narrated it from Sufyān except al-Firyābī. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muttafaq ʿalayh]"""
"21210","(21204) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muazzakī informed us that Abū al-Ḥasan Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdūs informed us, that ʿUthmān ibn Saʿid al-Dārimī narrated to us, that Mūsā ibn Ismāʿīl narrated to us, that Abū ʿAwanah narrated, from al-Aʿmash, from Abī Wāʾil, from ʿAbd Allāh, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Whoever swears a compelled oath by which he seizes the property of a Muslim"," he will meet Allah while He is angry with him.\"" So Allah"," the Blessed and Most High"," revealed the confirmation of that: {Indeed"," those who exchange the covenant of Allah and their oaths for a small price…} to the end of the verse. Then al-Ashʿath ibn Qays entered and said: What has Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān narrated to you? They said: Such and such. He said: This verse was revealed concerning me. I had a well on the land of a paternal cousin of mine. I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ"," and he said: \""Your proof"," or his oath.\"" I said: Then he will swear for it"," O Messenger of Allah. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \""Whoever swears a compelled oath while being sinful in it"," thereby seeking to seize the property of a Muslim"," he will meet Allah while He is angry with him.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Mūsā ibn Ismāʿīl"," and both al-Bukhārī and Muslim narrated it through other chains from al-Aʿmash. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muttafaq ʿalayh]"""
"21211","(21205) Abū Ṣāliḥ ibn Abī Ṭāhir al-Anbarī informed us that my grandfather Yaḥyā ibn Manṣūr al-Qāḍī narrated to us, Aḥmad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm informed us that Jarīr informed us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAmr al-Adīb informed us that Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī narrated to us, ʿImrān ibn Mūsā narrated to us, ʿUthmān narrated to us that Jarīr narrated from Manṣūr, from Abū Wāʾil, from ʿAbdullāh who said: \Whoever takes an oath through which he seeks to claim another's wealth while being false therein"," he shall meet Allah while He is angry with him.\"" And the confirmation of that is in the Book of Allah: {Indeed"," those who exchange the covenant of Allah and their oaths for a small price — they will have no share in the Hereafter} [Āl ʿImrān:77]. He said: Then al-Ashʿath ibn Qays came out to us and said: \""What is Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān narrating to you?\"" So we narrated to him what he had said. He said: \""He spoke the truth. This verse was revealed concerning me. There was a dispute between me and a man over a well"," so we brought our dispute to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him). He said: 'Your two witnesses or his oath.' I said: 'Then he will swear and not care.' The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: 'Whoever takes an oath through which he seeks to claim wealth while being false therein"," he shall meet Allah while He is angry with him.' Then Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic"," revealed the confirmation of that"," then He recited this verse: {Indeed"," those who exchange the covenant of Allah and their oaths for a small price} [Āl ʿImrān:77].\"" This is the wording of the ḥadīth of Isḥāq.\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿUthmān ibn Abī Shaybah"," and Muslim narrated it from Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Muttafaq ʿalayh]"""
"21212","(21206) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū al-Walīd al-Faqīh narrated to us, ʿAbdullāh ibn Muḥammad narrated to us, Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm informed us that Rūḥ narrated from al-Ḥajjāj ibn Abī ʿUthmān, from Ḥumayd ibn Hilāl, from Zayd ibn Thābit, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) who said: \If the claimant has no proof"," then the oath is upon the one who is claimed against.\""\n\nWe have narrated the ḥadīth of \""the proof is upon the claimant and the oath is upon the one who denies\"" from other routes"," all of them weak"," and what we have mentioned is sufficient. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"21213","(21207) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us that Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us, Yaḥyā ibn al-Rabīʿ al-Makkī narrated to us, Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah narrated from Idrīs al-Awdī who said: Saʿīd ibn Abī Burdah brought out a document to us and said: \This is the letter of ʿUmar to Abū Mūsā al-Ashʿarī (may Allah be pleased with both of them).\"" He mentioned it"," and in it was: \""The proof is upon the claimant and the oath is upon the one who denies.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"21214","(21208) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ, Abū Bakr al-Qāḍī, and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib informed us, ʿAbd al-Wahhāb ibn ʿAṭāʾ informed us that Saʿīd narrated from Qatādah regarding His statement {And We gave him wisdom and decisive speech}: \The proof is upon the claimant and the oath is upon the one who is claimed against.\""\n\nAnd it has been narrated to us previously from Sharīḥ that he said regarding this verse: \""Oaths and witnesses.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"21215","(21209) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us in the aḥādīth of Mālik: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us that al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us that al-Shāfiʿī informed us that Mālik narrated from Jamīl ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Muʾadhdhin that he used to attend ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz when he was governor over Madīnah and he would judge between the people. When a man came claiming a right against another man, he would look: if there was between them any dealing or association, he would make the one against whom the claim was made take an oath; and if there was nothing of that, he would not make him take an oath.\n\nThe Shaykh (may Allah have mercy on him) said: \This is something he went to on the basis of personal preference (istiḥsān)"," and likewise what has been narrated to us from al-Qāsim ibn Muḥammad that he said: 'When a wicked man claims against a righteous man something that the people see he is lying about and there was no transaction between them"," he would not be made to take an oath.' And the aḥādīth that we have mentioned contradict him.\""\n\nAl-Shāfiʿī (may Allah have mercy on him) said in the book of Claims: \""The oath is upon the one who is claimed against"," whether there was any dealing between them or not.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"21216","(21210) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us that Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us, ʿUthmān ibn ʿUmar al-Dabbī narrated to us, Musaddad narrated us, Abū al-Aḥwaṣ narrated to us, Simāk ibn Ḥarb narrated from ʿAlqamah ibn Wāʾil ibn Ḥujr, from his father, who said: \A man from Ḥaḍramawt and a man from Kindah came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him). The Ḥaḍramī said: 'O Messenger of Allah"," this man has seized a piece of land that belonged to me.' The Kindī said: 'It is my land; in my possession"," I cultivate it; he has no right in it.' The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said to the Ḥaḍramī: 'Do you have proof?' He said: 'No.' He said: 'Then his oath.' He said: 'O Messenger of Allah"," he is a wicked man; he does not care what he swears upon; he abstains from nothing.' The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said to him: 'You have nothing from him except that.' He set off to take the oath. When the man turned away"," the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: 'Indeed"," if he swears upon wealth to consume it unjustly"," he shall meet Allah while He is turning away from him.'\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Qutaybah and a group"," from Abī al-Aḥwaṣ. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 139]"""
"21217","(21211) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq and Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, Baḥr ibn Naṣr narrated to us, Ibn Wahb informed me that Sulaymān ibn Bilāl informed him that Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd narrated to him that Abū al-Zubayr informed him from ʿAdī ibn ʿAdī, from his father, who said: \Two men came disputing to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) over a piece of land. One of them said: 'It is mine.' The other said: 'It is mine; I have seized it and taken possession of it.' He said: 'The oath is upon the one in whose hand the land is.' When he was about to take the oath"," the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: 'Indeed"," whoever swears upon a Muslim's wealth"," he shall meet Allah while He is angry with him.' He said: 'So who abandons it?' He said: 'For him is Paradise.'\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Previously narrated under no. 20708]"""
"21218","(21212) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr narrated to us that Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn ʿAffān narrated to us, Abū Usāmah narrated from Jarīr, who is Ibn Ḥāzim, who said: I heard ʿAdī ibn ʿAdī al-Kindī narrating in a gathering in Minā. He said: Rijāʾ ibn Ḥaywah and al-ʿUrs ibn ʿAmīrah narrated to me from ʿAdī ibn ʿAmīrah al-Kindī that Imruʾ al-Qays ibn ʿĀbis al-Kindī brought a dispute to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) against a man from Ḥaḍramawt over a piece of land. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) asked the Ḥaḍramī for proof, but he had no proof, so he ruled against Imruʾ al-Qays with the oath. The Ḥaḍramī said: 'You have given him the means of the oath, O Messenger of Allah; by Allah, he will take my land!' The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: 'Whoever takes a false oath to seize his brother's wealth, he shall meet Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, on the day he meets Him while He is angry with him.' A man said — and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) recited: {Indeed, those who exchange the covenant of Allah and their oaths for a small price} [Āl ʿImrān:77] to the end of the verse. Imruʾ al-Qays said: 'O Messenger of Allah, then what is for the one who abandons it?' He said: 'For him is Paradise.' He said: 'Then I bear witness that I have abandoned it.'\ [Ṣaḥīḥ. Previously narrated]"""
"21219","(21213) Abū Naṣr Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Ismāʿīl al-Bazzāz narrated to us in Ṭabarān that ʿAbdullāh ibn Aḥmad ibn Manṣūr al-Ṭūsī narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Ismāʿīl al-Ṣāʾigh narrated to us, Rūḥ ibn ʿĀbidah narrated to us, Saʿīd narrated.\n\n(Ḥ) And ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us that Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Yūnus narrated to us, Saʿīd ibn ʿĀmir narrated to us, Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿArūbah narrated from Qatādah, from Saʿīd ibn Abī Burdah, from his father, from Abū Mūsā, who said: \Two men brought a dispute to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) over something\"" — and Rūḥ said: \""over a camel\"" — \""and neither of them had proof"," so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) judged it between them equally"," half and half.\"" Likewise Yazīd ibn Zurayʿ"," ʿAbd al-Raḥīm ibn Sulaymān"," and Muḥammad ibn Bakr narrated it from Ibn Abī ʿArūbah"," and likewise it was narrated from Saʿīd ibn Bashīr from Qatādah. [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"21220","(21214) And Shuʿbah narrated from Qatādah and sent it as a mursal narration. Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Aḥmad ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us, ʿAbdullāh ibn Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal narrated to me, my father narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us, Shuʿbah narrated from Qatādah, from Saʿīd ibn Abī Burdah, from his father, that two men brought a dispute to the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) over a beast, and neither of them had proof, so he made it between them half and half.\n\n[Ḍaʿīf. Previously narrated]"
"21221","(21215) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us that Muḥammad ibn Bakr narrated to us that Abū Dāwūd al-Sijistānī narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn al-Minhāl narrated to us that Yazīd ibn Zuraiʿ narrated to us that Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿArūbah narrated from Qatādah, from Khilās, from Abū Rāfiʿ, from Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) that two men brought a dispute regarding some merchandise to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), and neither of them had any proof. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \Cast lots for the oath"," whether they like it or not.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Ibn Abī Shaybah 6/318]"""
"21222","(21216) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us that Muḥammad ibn Bakr narrated to us that Abū Dāwūd narrated to us that Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah narrated to us that Khālid ibn al-Ḥārith narrated to us from Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿArūbah, with his chain of narration, a similar report. He said: it was concerning a riding animal, and neither of them had any proof. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) commanded them to cast lots for the oath.\n\nThe Sheikh said: It is possible that this ruling is a continuation of the first ruling in the ḥadīth of Abū Burdah, as though he (peace and blessings be upon him) had divided it between them into two halves by the rule of possession, and each one of them sought the oath of his companion regarding the half that had fallen to him. So he placed the obligation of the oath upon both of them. Then they disputed at the beginning over which of them should take the oath first, so he commanded them to cast lots for the oath. And Allah knows best.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Preceded before it]"
"21223","(21217) In a similar vein, Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū al-Faḍl Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us that Aḥmad ibn Salamah narrated to us that Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm and ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Bishr narrated — Isḥāq said \informed us\"" and ʿAbd al-Raḥmān said \""narrated to us\"" — that ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us that Maʿmar narrated from Hammām ibn Munabbih"," who said: This is what Abū Hurayrah narrated to us"," and he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) proposed the oath to a people"," and they hastened to it. So he commanded that lots be cast among them for the oath — as to which of them should swear.\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Isḥāq ibn Naṣr from ʿAbd al-Razzāq with this wording. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 2674]"""
"21224","(21218) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us that Abū Bakr al-Qaṭṭān narrated to us that Aḥmad ibn Yūsuf narrated to us that ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us that Maʿmar narrated from Hammām ibn Munabbih, from Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \If two persons are compelled to take the oath and they accept it"," then cast lots between them.\"" And with this wording"," Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal and a group narrated it from ʿAbd al-Razzāq"," except that in the narration of Aḥmad it reads: \""If two persons are compelled to take the oath and they accept it"," then let them cast lots for it\"" — meaning"," and Allah knows best"," whether they like it or dislike it"," in both cases lots should be cast between them.\n\nAnd Abū Bakr ibn Yaḥyā ibn al-Naḍr narrated it from his father"," from Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him)"," from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): \""If two persons dislike the oath or accept it"," let them cast lots for it.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"21225","(21219) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū al-Faḍl ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us that Aḥmad ibn Salamah narrated to us that Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm informed us that Wakīʿ narrated to us that al-Aʿmash narrated from Abū Wāʾil, from al-Ashʿath ibn Qays, who said: There was a dispute between me and a man concerning a piece of land. We brought our dispute to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him). He said: \Do you have any proof?\"" I said: \""No.\"" He said: \""Then his oath.\""\n\nBoth al-Bukhārī and Muslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ as has preceded. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muttafaq ʿalayh]"""
"21226","(21220) We have also received in the ḥadīth of ʿAlqamah ibn Wāʾil ibn Ḥujr al-Ḥaḍramī from his father, in the story of the Ḥaḍramī and the Kindī: the Ḥaḍramī said: \O Messenger of Allah"," this man has seized a piece of land that belonged to my father.\"" The Kindī said: \""It is my land; in my possession"," I cultivate it. He has no right to it.\"" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said to the Ḥaḍramī: \""Do you have any proof?\"" He said: \""No.\"" He said: \""Then you have his oath.\"" Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us of it"," narrating that Muḥammad ibn Bakr narrated to us that Abū Dāwūd narrated to us that Hannād ibn Surayy narrated to us that Abū al-Aḥwaṣ narrated from Simāk"," from ʿAlqamah ibn Wāʾil ibn Ḥujr al-Ḥaḍramī"," from his father"," who said: A man from Ḥaḍramawt and a man from Kindah came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)"," and he mentioned it.\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Hannād. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 139]"""
"21227","(21221) Abū ʿAbd Allāh Isḥāq ibn Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf al-Sūsī narrated to us that Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm narrated to us that Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad ibn Hishām al-Aḥmarī narrated to us that Ibrāhīm ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣīnī narrated to us that ʿAbd al-Raḥīm ibn Sulaymān narrated from al-Ḥajjāj ibn Arṭāh, from ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb, from his father, from his grandfather, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say on the day of the conquest of Makkah: \The defendant is more entitled to the oath"," unless proof is established against him.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"21228","(21222) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū al-Walīd narrated to us that Jaʿfar ibn Aḥmad narrated to us that ʿAlī ibn Ḥujr narrated to us that Ismāʿīl ibn ʿAyyāsh narrated from al-Muthannā ibn al-Ṣabbāḥ, from ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \The defendant is more entitled to the oath than one for whom no proof has been established.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"21229","(21223) He mentioned the ḥadīth that Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī narrated to us that Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us that al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us that al-Shāfiʿī informed us that Ibn Abī Yaḥyā narrated from Isḥāq ibn Abī Farwah, from ʿUmar ibn al-Ḥakam, from Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh that two men contested a claim regarding a riding animal, and each of them produced proof that it was his own she-camel that he had bred. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) judged it in favour of the one in whose possession it was. [Ḍaʿīf]"
"21230","(21224) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Aṣbahānī al-Faqīh informed us that ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us that al-Ḥusayn ibn Ismāʿīl, Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar al-Maṭīrī, and Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn ʿĪsā al-Khawwāṣ said: Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Manṣūr, Abū Ismāʿīl al-Faqīh, narrated to us that Zayd ibn Nuʿaym narrated in Baghdād that Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan narrated to us that Abū Ḥanīfah narrated from Haytham al-Ṣayrafī, from al-Shaʿbī, from Jābir, that two men brought a dispute to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) regarding a she-camel. Each one of them said: \This she-camel was born in my custody","\"" and each produced proof. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) judged it in favour of the one in whose possession it was. [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"21231","(21225) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū al-Walīd al-Faqīh informed us that al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn ʿUbayd narrated to us that Ḥammād ibn Zayd narrated from Ayyūb from Muḥammad: that two men brought a dispute before Shurayḥ regarding a beast, and each of them produced evidence that it belonged to him and that he had bred it. Shurayḥ said: \It belongs to the one in whose hand the offspring is; the one who bred it has greater right than the one who merely recognizes it.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"21232","(21226) Abū ʿAbd Allāh informed us that Abū al-Walīd informed us that ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad narrated to us that ʿAmr ibn Zurārah informed us that Hushaym narrated from Yūnus, Ibn ʿAwn, and Hishām from Muḥammad ibn Sīrīn from Shurayḥ: that two men laid claim to a beast, and one of them produced evidence while it was in his hand that he had bred it, and the other produced evidence that it was his beast which he recognized. Shurayḥ said: \The one who bred it has greater right than the one who merely recognizes it.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Previously cited.]"""
"21233","(21227) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū al-Walīd al-Faqīh informed us that Jaʿfar ibn Aḥmad narrated to us that ʿAlī ibn Ḥujr narrated to us that Hushaym narrated from Dāwūd from al-Shaʿbī, who said: ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Udhaynah wrote to Shurayḥ concerning a group of the Azd who had made a claim against a group of Banī Asad, and he said: \If these people come with evidence in the morning"," those others will come with more than them.\"" So he wrote back to him: \""I am not one to be swayed by mutual contradiction and numerical preponderance in any matter. The beast belongs to those in whose hands it is"," provided they produce evidence.\"" And it has been narrated to us from Ḥanash from ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) that he said: \""No preference is given on account of greater numbers.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"21234","(21228) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us that Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us that Tamtām, i.e. Muḥammad ibn Ghālib, narrated to me that Hudbah narrated to us that Hammām narrated to us that Qatādah narrated from Saʿīd ibn Abī Burdah from his father from Abū Mūsā: that two men laid claim to a camel, and each of them produced two witnesses, so the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) divided it between them. And likewise Ḥajjāj ibn Minhāl narrated it from Hammām, and it is preserved in the wording of Ḥammām ibn Yaḥyā from Qatādah with this wording. [Ḍaʿīf. Previously cited under no. 21213.]"
"21235","(21229) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us that Abū Ṭāhir Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Muḥammadābādhī narrated to us that Abū Qilābah narrated to us that Saʿid ibn ʿĀmir narrated to us that Shuʿbah narrated from Qatādah from Saʿīd ibn Abī Burdah from his father from his grandfather: that two men brought a dispute to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ), and each of them produced two witnesses, so the Prophet (ﷺ) judged that it be divided between them into two equal parts — thus said the narration from Shuʿbah. And we have previously narrated it from Ibn Abī ʿArūbah from Qatādah as a connected (mawṣūl) narration, and from Shuʿbah from Qatādah as a disconnected (mursal) narration, both of which contradict Hammām. This narration from Shuʿbah differs in its wording, for they (the narrators from Shuʿbah) said: \Neither of them had evidence","\"" whereas in the narration of Hammām and this narration from Shuʿbah: \""Each of them produced two witnesses.\"" It is remotely possible that these are two separate cases"," or it may be one and the same incident"," and when the two sets of evidence contradicted each other"," they were both set aside"," so it was said that neither of them had evidence"," and the thing was divided between them into two equal parts by virtue of possession (al-yad). And Allah knows best. The hadith is considered defective (maʿlūl) among the scholars of hadith due to the disagreement in its chain of narration from Qatādah. [Ḍaʿīf. Previously cited.]"""
"21236","(21230) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū al-Walīd al-Faqīh informed us that Yaḥyā ibn Muḥammad ibn Ṣāʿid narrated to us that ʿAmr ibn Ayyūb al-Ṭāʾī, the grandson of Abī al-Mughīrah, narrated to me that my grandfather Abū al-Mughīrah narrated from al-Ḍaḥḥāk ibn Ḥamzah from Qatādah that Abā Mijlaz informed him from Abī Burdah from Abū Mūsā: that two men brought a dispute to the Prophet (ﷺ) regarding a camel, both of them claiming it, each asserting that it was his, and each of them came with two witnesses that the camel was his. So the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) judged that it be divided between them into two equal parts. [Ḍaʿīf. Previously cited.]"
"21237","(21231) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū al-Walīd informed us that ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad ibn Shīrūyah narrated to us that Isḥāq informed us that ʿAbd al-Ṣamad ibn ʿAbd al-Wārith narrated to us that Ḥammād ibn Salamah narrated from Qatādah from al-Naḍr ibn Anas from Bashīr ibn Nahīk from Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him): that two men laid claim to a beast, and each of them produced two witnesses, so the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) made it divided between them into two equal parts. Thus I found it in my book in two places, and I have seen it in the Musnad of Isḥāq thus, except that he later struck out the name of Bashīr ibn Nahīk. I wrote it in an old handwriting. [Ḍaʿīf. Previously cited.]"
"21238","(21232) And ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us that Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd narrated to us that Hishām ibn ʿAlī narrated to us that Abū ʿUmar al-Ḍarīr, Ḥafṣ ibn ʿUmar, narrated to us that Ḥammād ibn Salamah narrated from Qatādah that they were informed by al-Naḍr ibn Anas from Abī Burdah from Abū Mūsā: that two men brought a dispute to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) regarding a camel, and each of them produced evidence that it was his, so the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) made it divided between them into two equal parts. And likewise Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm narrated it, as far as I know, from al-Naḍr ibn Shumayl from Ḥammād as a connected narration, so the hadith reverts to the hadith of Abī Burdah, except that the narration from Qatādah from al-Naḍr ibn Anas is rare (gharīb). And Abū al-Walīd narrated it from Ḥammād but sent it as a mursal narration, saying: from Qatādah from al-Naḍr ibn Anas from Abī Burdah that two men laid claim to a beast and found it in the possession of a man — and this is what Ibn Khuzaymah mentioned from Abū Mūsā from Abū al-Walīd. [Ḍaʿīf. Previously cited.]"
"21239","(21233) Abū Ḥāzim al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū al-Faḍl ibn Khamīruwayh informed us that Aḥmad ibn Najdah narrated to us that Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr narrated to us that Abū ʿAwānah narrated from Simāk ibn Ḥarb from Tamīm ibn Ṭarfah, who said: I was informed that two men brought a dispute to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) regarding a camel, and each of them produced two witnesses, so he divided it between them. And likewise Sufyān al-Thawrī narrated it from Simāk. [Ḍaʿīf. Previously cited.]"
"21240","(21234) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū al-Walīd informed us that ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad narrated to us, and he said: Abū ʿAbd Allāh, i.e. Muḥammad ibn Naṣr, informed us that Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā informed us that Muḥammad ibn Jābir narrated from Simāk from Tamīm ibn Ṭarfah, who said: Two men brought a dispute to the Prophet (ﷺ) regarding a camel, each of them holding its reins, and each of them produced two witnesses, so he divided it between them into two equal parts. This is a mursal narration. And it has reached me from Abū ʿĪsā al-Tirmidhī that he asked Muḥammad ibn Ismāʿīl al-Bukhārī about the hadith of Saʿīd ibn Abī Burdah from his father in this chapter, and he said: \This hadith reverts to the hadith of Simāk ibn Ḥarb from Tamīm ibn Ṭarfah.\"" Al-Bukhārī said: \""And Ḥammād ibn Salamah narrated"," saying: Simāk ibn Ḥarb said: 'I myself narrated this hadith to Abī Burdah.'\"" The Sheikh said: And the mursal narration of Shuʿbah of this hadith from Qatādah from Saʿīd ibn Abī Burdah from his father in the narration of Ghundar from him is indicative of that. And Allah knows best. [Ḍaʿīf. Previously cited.]"""
"21241","As for the hadith of Ibn al-Musayyab: Abū ʿAbd Allāh the Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū al-Walīd the Faqīh informed us that ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us that Ibn Abī Maryam narrated to us that al-Layth narrated from Bukayr ibn ʿAbd Allāh that he heard Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyab say: Two men came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) disputing over a matter. Each of them brought witnesses of equal number and equal standing. So the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) drew lots between them and said: \O Allah"," it is You who shall judge between them.\"" Then he gave the ruling in favor of the one whose lot came out. Abū Dāwūd narrated it in *al-Marāsīl* from Qutaybah from al-Layth"," and there is a corroborating narration from another chain. [Weak]"""
"21242","Abū ʿAbd Allāh the Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū al-Walīd informed us that ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad narrated to me — Abū ʿAbd Allāh said: I think he was Muḥammad ibn Naṣr — that al-Ṣaghānī narrated from Abū al-Aswad from Ibn Lahīʿah from Abū al-Aswad from ʿUrwah and Sulaymān ibn Yasār: Two men came to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) disputing, and each of them brought witnesses, and they were equal in number. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) drew lots between them.\n\nAs for the narration from ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib (may Allah be pleased with him) regarding this matter, it is in what follows. [Weak]"
"21243","Abū ʿAbd Allāh the Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū al-Walīd informed us that al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān narrated to us that Abū Kāmil narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) Abū al-Walīd said, and ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad narrated to us, saying: Abū ʿAbd Allāh said: Abū Kāmil and Ḥāmid ibn ʿUmar narrated to us — and this is the hadith of the latter — both saying: Abū ʿĀwānah narrated from Simāk from Ḥanash, who said: ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) was brought a mule that was being sold in the market. A man said: \This is my mule; I neither sold it nor gave it away","\"" and he produced five witnesses to support his claim. Then another man came"," also claiming it"," asserting that it was his mule"," and he brought two witnesses. ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) said: \""There is in this matter both a judgment and a settlement. As for the settlement: the mule shall be sold and divided into seven shares — five for the one who brought five witnesses and two for the other. But if you insist on a judgment based on the right"," then one of the two parties must swear that it is his mule and that he neither sold it nor gave it away. If you dispute over which of you should swear"," I shall draw lots between you regarding the oath; whichever of you the lot falls upon shall swear.\"" And he judged accordingly"," and I was a witness.\n\nAnd it has been narrated in this regard from Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) that he attributed it (as a marfūʿ narration)"," but it is as follows. [Weak]"""
"21244","ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us that Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn Ghālib narrated to us that Mūsā ibn Ismāʿīl narrated to us that Abān narrated to us that Qatādah narrated from Khilās from Abū Rāfiʿ from Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: \When each of them brings a witness"," lots shall be drawn between them\"" — from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him). He said \""a witness\"" (in the singular).\n\nIt is possible that what is meant by it is witnesses in general (i.e."," the category of witnesses). There has already passed"," in the narration of Ibn Abī ʿArūbah from Qatādah from Khilās from Abū Rāfiʿ from Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him)"," from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him)"," regarding two men who came to him disputing over merchandise"," neither of whom had proof (bayyinah)"," and the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \""Draw lots regarding the oath.\""\n\nAl-Shāfiʿī (may Allah have mercy on him) said: The other opinion is that he should judge between them by dividing it equally"," because the evidence of each of them is the same.\n\n[Sound. It was previously cited under no. 21215.]"""
"21245","Abū ʿAbd Allāh the Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū al-Walīd informed us that al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān narrated to us that Hudbah narrated to us that Hammād narrated from Qatādah from Saʿīd ibn Abī Burdah from his father from Abū Mūsā: Two men both claimed a camel. Each of them brought two witnesses. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) divided it between them. The discussion of the defect (ʿillah) of this hadith has already passed, as well as what occurred regarding disagreement in its chain of narration (isnād), its connection (waṣl), and its text (matn). And it is not stated in it that the camel was not in the possession of either of them. [Weak]"
"21246","Abū ʿAbd Allāh the Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū al-Walīd informed us that Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf narrated to us that Qutaybah narrated to us that Abū ʿĀwānah narrated from Simāk from Tamīm ibn Ṭarfah: Two men came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) disputing over a camel. Each of them brought two witnesses. So he judged between them by dividing it equally.\n\nAbū al-Walīd said, and Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAlī narrated to us that Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā informed us that Abū ʿĀwānah narrated something similar in its entirety.\n\nThe Shaykh (may Allah have mercy on him) said: This is munqaṭiʿ (disconnected). And there has already passed, in the narration of Muḥammad ibn Jābir from Simāk, evidence indicating that the camel was in the possession of both of them.\n\nAl-Shāfiʿī (may Allah have mercy on him) said in *al-Qadīm*: Tamīm is an unknown man (majhūl), and the narration of an unknown person, if no one contradicts it, is not a proof. And Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyab narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) what we have described. And Saʿīd is trustworthy. And we have stated that when two hadiths differ, the proof lies in the more sound of the two. And I do not know any scholar upon whom it would be unclear that our hadith is more sound, and that Saʿīd is among the most sound of people in mursal narrations, and that he is more in accordance with the established Sunnah regarding drawing lots.\n\nThe Shaykh said: Tamīm ibn Ṭarfah al-Ṭāʾī was a Kūfan who narrated from ʿAdī ibn Ḥātim and Jābir ibn Samurah. He was among the later generation of the Successors (tābiʿīn), and he does not reach the rank of Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyab. [Weak. It was previously cited.]"
"21247","Abū ʿAbd Allāh the Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū al-Walīd the Faqīh informed us that al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn ʿUbayd narrated to us that Ḥammād ibn Zayd narrated from ʿAṭāʾ ibn al-Sāʾib from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Laylā, who said: I was present with Abū al-Dardāʾ when a group of people came to him disputing over a horse. Each of them brought proof (bayyinah) that it was his mount, born in his possession. So he judged between them. [Good]"
"21248","He said: And Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Aṣbahānī informed us that Abū Naṣr al-ʿIrāqī narrated to us that Sufyān ibn Muḥammad al-Jawharī narrated to us that ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥasan narrated to us that ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Walīd narrated to us that Sufyān narrated from ʿAlqamah ibn Murthad from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Laylā, who said: Two men came to Abū al-Dardāʾ disputing over a horse. Each of them brought proof (bayyinah) that it was born in his possession and that he had neither sold it nor given it away. The other party came with the same claim. Abū al-Dardāʾ said: \One of you is lying.\"" Then he divided it equally between them. [Good. It was previously cited.]\n\nAnd it has been narrated in this story that they disputed over a horse and found it with a man. [Good. It was previously cited.]"""
"21249","Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad al-Aṣbahānī informed us that Abū Muḥammad ibn Ḥayyān informed us that ʿAbd Allāh ibn Bundār informed me that Ibrāhīm al-Ḍabbī narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn al-Mughīrah narrated to us that al-Nuʿmān ibn ʿAbd al-Salām narrated from Qays ibn al-Rabīʿ from ʿAlqamah ibn Murthad and ʿAṭāʾ ibn al-Sāʾib from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Laylā, who said: I was sitting with Abū al-Dardāʾ, and he mentioned its meaning, and he said it was regarding a horse they found with a man.\n\nAl-Shāfiʿī (may Allah have mercy on him) said regarding a case like this, after mentioning the horse: \This is a matter in which I seek guidance from Allah"," and I am hesitant regarding it.\"" Then he said: \""Neither of them shall be given anything"," and it shall be held in abeyance until they reach a settlement.\""\n\nThe Shaykh (may Allah have mercy on him) said: The foundational principle in such matters is what follows. [Good. It was previously cited.]"""
"21250","Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzakkī informed us that Abū ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yaʿqūb al-Shaybānī informed us that Abū Aḥmad Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Wahhāb informed us that Jaʿfar ibn ʿAwn informed us that Usāmah ibn Zayd narrated from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Rāfiʿ from Umm Salamah (may Allah be pleased with her), who said: Two men from the Anṣār came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) disputing over inheritances whose traces had faded and those who knew of them had passed away. He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \I am only a human being. I judge in matters in which nothing has been revealed to me according to my own opinion. So if I were to decree anything for anyone at the expense of his brother's right"," I would merely be cutting out a piece of fire for him.\"" The two men wept"," and each of them said: \""My right belongs to him"," O Messenger of Allah!\"" He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \""Go"," divide it between you"," seek what is right"," then draw lots"," and then let each of you absolve his companion.\"" [Weak]"""
"21251","(21245) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū al-Walīd al-Faqīh narrated to us that al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān narrated to us that Ḥibbān ibn Mūsā narrated to us, from Ibn al-Mubārak, from ʿAbd al-Malik ibn Abī Sulaymān, who said: It was said to ʿAṭāʾ: \Do you judge by the principle of original ownership regarding houses?\"" He said: \""Yes"," when evidence is established that it is his house and that he neither sold nor gifted it.\""\n\nAnd it has been narrated from ʿAṭāʾ that he said: \""I found the people judging by the principle of original ownership regarding houses.\"" And from Shurayḥ and ʿĀmir al-Shaʿbī that they both used to judge by the principle of original ownership regarding houses. [Weak]"""
"21252","(21246) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū ʿAbdillāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us that Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad and Aḥmad ibn Salamah both said: Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm informed us that Jarīr narrated to us, from Manṣūr, from Abī Wāʾil, from ʿAbdillāh, who said: \Whoever swears an oath to claim wealth through it while being false therein"," he shall meet Allah while He is angry with him.\"" Then Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic"," revealed the confirmation of that: {Indeed"," those who exchange the covenant of Allah and their oaths for a small price…} [Āl ʿImrān: 77] to the end of the verse.\n\nThen al-Ashʿath ibn Qays came out to us and said: \""What is Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān narrating to you?\"" So we narrated to him what he had said. He said: \""He has spoken the truth. This verse was revealed concerning me. There was a dispute between me and a man over something"," so we brought the matter before the Prophet ﷺ. He said: 'Your two witnesses"," or his oath.' I said: 'Then he will swear and not care.' The Prophet ﷺ said: 'Whoever swears an oath to claim wealth through it while being false therein"," he shall meet Allah while He is angry with him.' Then Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic"," revealed the confirmation of that"," and then he recited this verse.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿUthmān and Qutaybah"," from Jarīr; and Muslim narrated it from Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm. [Authentic. Agreed upon]"""
"21253","(21247) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzakkī informed us that Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Salamah narrated to us that ʿUthmān ibn Saʿīd Abū Saʿīd narrated to us that Abū al-Walīd al-Ṭayālisī narrated to us that Abū ʿAwnah narrated to us, from ʿAbd al-Malik ibn ʿUmayr, from ʿAlqamah ibn Wāʾil, from his father, who said: \I was with the Prophet ﷺ when two disputing parties came to him. One of them said: 'O Messenger of Allah"," this man seized my land during the Jāhiliyyah.' He was Imruʾ al-Qays ibn ʿĀbis al-Kindī"," and his opponent was Rabīʿah. He said: 'It is my land; I cultivate it.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Do you have proof?' He said: 'No.' He said: 'Then his oath.' He said: 'Then he will take it"," for he does not care what he swears upon.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'You have nothing from him except that.' When he went to take the oath"," the Prophet ﷺ said: 'Indeed"," if he swipes his wealth unjustly by his oath"," he shall meet Allah while He is angry with him.'\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Zuhayr and Isḥāq"," from Abū al-Walīd. [Authentic. Bukhārī 139]"""
"21254","(21248) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us that Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us that al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān said: al-Shāfiʿī said: Ḥafṣ ibn Ghiyāth narrated to us, from Ibn Abī Laylā, from al-Ḥakam, from Ḥanash, that ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) used to consider the oath alongside the evidence.\n\nAnd Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Laylā narrated it thus.\n\nAnd it has been narrated previously through another chain from Ḥanash, from ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him), that he only held this view when the two pieces of evidence were in conflict. And Allah knows best. [Weak]"
"21255","(21249) Abū Ḥāzim al-ʿAbdawī al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū al-Faḍl ibn Khamīruwayh informed us that Aḥmad ibn Najdah narrated to us that Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr narrated to us that Hushaym narrated to us that Hishām and Manṣūr narrated to us, from Ibn Sīrīn, that a man claimed a right against another and presented evidence against him. Shurayḥ asked the defendant to take an oath, but he seemed reluctant to take the oath. So Shurayḥ said: \What a poor testimony you have given your witnesses!\"" [Authentic]"""
"21256","(21250) Abū Ḥāzim informed us that Abū al-Faḍl informed us that Aḥmad narrated to us that Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr narrated to us that Hushaym informed us that Abū Mālik al-Ashjaʿī said: \I was present with Shurayḥ when two men came to him disputing. One of them claimed an animal from the other"," asserting that it was his animal that had given birth to it. Shurayḥ asked him for evidence"," so he brought a group of eight men who testified on his behalf. The one who had the animal in his possession said: 'Ask him to take an oath.' So Shurayḥ said: 'Take an oath.' The claimant said: 'I have established my case with eight witnesses.' Shurayḥ said: 'Even if you had established it with such-and-such number of witnesses"," I would not rule in your favor until you take an oath.'\"" [Authentic]"""
"21257","(21251) Abū Ḥāzim informed us that Abū al-Faḍl informed us that Aḥmad informed us that Saʿīd narrated to us that Hushaym informed us that al-Ashʿath ibn Sawwār narrated to us, from ʿAwn ibn ʿAbdillāh ibn ʿUtbah, from his father, that he asked a man to take an oath along with the evidence, but the man refused to swear. So ʿAbdillāh ibn ʿUtbah said to him: \I will not rule for you regarding wealth upon which you will not take an oath.\"" [Weak]"""
"21258","(21252) Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn Abī al-Maʿrūf al-Faqīh informed us that Bishr ibn Aḥmad al-Isfarāʾinī informed us that Abū Jaʿfar Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-Ḥaddāʾ narrated to us that ʿAlī ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Madanī narrated to us that Yaḥyā ibn Zakariyyā ibn Abī Zāʾidah informed me that Dāwūd ibn Abī Hind informed me, from ʿĀmir, from Shurayḥ, who said: \The evidence of the claimant is upon his original right"," and the declaration of the heirs of the deceased that their companion had fulfilled the right of the claimant — the oath of the claimant by Allah"," besides whom there is no deity"," that he died while this right was upon him — and we hold this view in claims when evidence is established against a deceased person"," or an absent person"," a child"," or an insane person.\"" [Authentic]"""
"21259","(21253) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū al-Walīd al-Faqīh said: I heard Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq ibn Khuzaymah say: al-Muzanī said: al-Shāfiʿī (may Allah have mercy on him) said: Sufyān informed us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū Naṣr Aḥmad ibn Sahl al-Faqīh in Bukhārī narrated to us that Qays ibn Unayf narrated to us that Qutaybah ibn Saʿīd narrated to us that Sufyān narrated to us, from al-Zuhrī, from ʿUrwah, from ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her), who said: \The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon me one day while he was cheerful"," the lines of his face radiant. He said: 'Have you not seen that Mujazziz al-Mudlajī entered upon me and saw Usāmah ibn Zayd and Zayd ibn Ḥārihah wrapped in a cloth"," their heads covered but their feet exposed"," and he said: \""Indeed"," these feet are from one another.\""'\""\n\nThe wording is that of the ḥadīth of Qutaybah. Al-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Qutaybah ibn Saʿīd"," and Muslim narrated it from Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah and others"," from Sufyān. [Authentic. Agreed upon]"""
"21260","(21254) Abū al-Ḥusayn ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh ibn Bushrān and Abū Muḥammad ʿAbdillāh ibn Yaḥyā ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār al-Sukkarī in Baghdad both informed us that Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār narrated to us that Aḥmad ibn Manṣūr al-Ramādī narrated to us that ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us that Ibn Jurayj informed me that Ibn Shihāb informed me, from ʿUrwah, from ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her), that the Prophet ﷺ entered upon her while he was cheerful, the lines of his face radiant, and he said: \Have you not heard what Mujazziz al-Mudlajī said when he saw Usāmah and Zayd sleeping"," their feet exposed"," and he said: 'Indeed"," these feet are from one another.'\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Yaḥyā"," and Muslim narrated it from ʿAbd ibn Ḥumayd"," both from ʿAbd al-Razzāq. And they both narrated it through the ḥadīth of Layth ibn Saʿd from al-Zuḥrī as well. [Authentic. Agreed upon]"""
"21261","(21255) Abū Bakr ibn Fūrak informed us: ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us: Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb narrated to us: Abū Dāwūd narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAmr Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh al-Adīb informed us: Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī informed us: al-Ḥasan, that is, ibn Sufyān, and Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ṣūfī informed us — both saying: Manṣūr ibn Abī Muzāḥim narrated to us — both saying: Ibrāhīm ibn Saʿd narrated from al-Zuhrī, from ʿUrwah, from ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her), who said: A qāʾif (physiognomist) came while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) was present, and Usāmah ibn Zayd and Zayd ibn Ḥārihah were lying down. He said: \Indeed"," these feet are from one another [i.e."," they share a common lineage].\"" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) was delighted by that and was pleased"," and he informed ʿĀʾishah of it. This is the wording of the ḥadīth of Manṣūr ibn Abī Muzāḥim.\n\nal-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Yaḥyā ibn Qazaʿah from Ibrāhīm"," and Muslim narrated it from Manṣūr ibn Abī Muzāḥim.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Muttafaq ʿalayh.]"""
"21262","(21256) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh al-Aṣbahānī informed us: ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: Abū Bakr al-Naysābūrī narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Wahb narrated to us: My uncle narrated to us: Ibrāhīm ibn Saʿīd narrated, mentioning the ḥadīth with its like, and added: Ibrāhīm ibn Saʿd said: \And Zayd was ruddy-complexioned"," fair-skinned"," and white"," while Usāmah was like the night [i.e."," dark-skinned].\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Muttafaq ʿalayh.]"""
"21263","(21257) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū ʿAmr, that is, ibn Ḥamdān, informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān narrated to us: Ḥarmalah ibn Yaḥyā informed us: Ibn Wahb informed us: Yūnus informed me, from Ibn Shihāb, from ʿUrwah ibn al-Zubayr, from ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) came to me joyful and happy because of what Mujazziz al-Mudlijī had said. He looked at Usāmah ibn Zayd lying down with his father and said: \These feet are from one another.\"" And Mujazziz was a qāʾif (physiognomist).\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Ḥarmalah.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Muttafaq ʿalayh.]"""
"21264","(21258) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzzakī and Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī both informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us: al-Shāfiʿī informed us: Anas ibn ʿIyāḍ narrated from Hishām ibn ʿUrwah, from his father, from Yaḥyā ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Ḥāṭib: \That two men disputed over a child"," so ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) called the qāʾifah (physiognomists)"," and they said: 'Indeed"," both of them share in him [i.e."," both have a claim].' So ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) said to the child: 'Attach yourself to whichever of them you wish.'\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ.]"""
"21265","(21259) He said: And al-Shāfiʿī informed us: Mālik informed us, from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd, from Sulaymān ibn Yasār, from ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him), with the same meaning.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Previously mentioned.]"
"21266","(21260) He said: And al-Shāfiʿī informed us: Muṭarrif ibn Māzin informed us, from Maʿmar, from al-Zuhrī, from ʿUrwah, from ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him), with the same meaning.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Previously mentioned.]"
"21267","(21261) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-Walīd al-Faqīh informed us: ʿAbdullāh ibn Ibrāhīm al-Akfānī narrated to us: Baḥr ibn Naṣr narrated to us: Ibn Wahb narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī al-Zinād narrated to me, from Hishām ibn ʿUrwah, from his father, from Yaḥyā ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Ḥāṭib, from his father, who said: \Two men came to ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him)"," disputing over a boy from the children of the Jāhiliyyah. This one saying: 'He is my son","' and this one saying: 'He is my son.' So ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) called a qāʾif from Banī al-Muṣṭaliq and asked him about the boy. The Muṣṭaliqī looked at him"," looked again"," and then said to ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him): 'Indeed"," both of them share in him entirely.' So ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) stood up to him with the dirrah (whip) and struck him with it.\"" He said"," and he mentioned the ḥadīth. He said: \""Then ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) said to the boy: 'Attach yourself to whichever of you he wishes.' So the boy stood up and followed one of them.\"" ʿAbd al-Raḥmān said: \""It is as though I can see him"," following one of them"," going away.\"" And ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: \""May Allah destroy the brother of Banī al-Muṣṭaliq!\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ for other than it.]"""
"21268","(21262) And Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-Walīd informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān narrated to us: Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah narrated to us: Abū Usāmah narrated to us, from Hishām ibn ʿUrwah, from his father, from Yaḥyā ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Ḥāṭib, from his father: \That ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him) judged between two men who both claimed a man without it being known which of them was his father. So ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) said to the man: 'Follow whichever of them you wish.'\""\n\nThis is a ṣaḥīḥ"," connected isnād.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Ibn Abī Shaybah.]"""
"21269","(21263) Abū Naṣr ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Qatādah informed us: Abū ʿAmr ibn Najayd informed us: Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-ʿAbdī narrated to us: Ibn Bukayr narrated to us: Mālik narrated, from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd, from Sulaymān ibn Yasār: \That ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him) used to attach the children of the Jāhiliyyah to whoever claimed them in Islam.\"" Sulaymān said: \""Two men came"," each of them claiming the child of a woman. So ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him) called a qāʾif"," and he looked at them. The qāʾif said: 'Indeed"," both of them share in him.' So ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) struck him with the dirrah (whip). Then he said to the woman: 'Tell me your story.' She said: 'This one of the two men used to come to me while I was among the camels of her family"," and he would not leave her until he thought that pregnancy had taken hold of her. Then he departed from her"," and she bled [i.e."," had a miscarriage or bleeding]. Then this other one came after him"," and I do not know from which of them it is.' The qāʾif exclaimed 'Allāhu Akbar!' So ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him) said to the boy: 'Attach yourself to whichever of them you wish.'\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ for other than it.]"""
"21270","(21264) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-Walīd informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān narrated to us: Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah narrated to us: Abū Bakr ibn ʿAyyāsh narrated to us, from Aslam al-Minqarī, from ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUbayd ibn ʿUmayr, who said: \ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAwf (may Allah be pleased with him) sold a slave-girl with whom he had had intercourse before observing the ʿiddah of istibrāʾ (waiting period to confirm absence of pregnancy). Pregnancy then became apparent when she was with the buyer. They brought their dispute to ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him). He said: So ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) called the qāʾifah (physiognomists)"," and they looked at the child and attached him to ʿAbd al-Raḥmān.\"" He said: \""And in another place [in the narration] it is mentioned that ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: 'Did you used to have intercourse with her?' He said: 'Yes.' He said: 'Then did you sell her before observing the istibrāʾ?' He said: 'Yes.' He said: 'You were not fit [to do so].'\"" He said: \""Then ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) called the qāʾifah"," and he mentioned it.\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ.]"""
"21271","(21265) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr narrated to us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib narrated to us: Yazīd ibn Hārūn informed us: Hammām ibn Yaḥyā narrated from Qatāda from Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyib: that two men had intercourse with a woman in the same period of purity, and she bore a child. They brought the matter to ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭābb, may Allah be pleased with him. He called for three experts in physiognomy (qāfa). They requested some soil, and the two men and the boy walked upon it. Then he said to one of them, \Look.\"" So he looked"," facing"," examining from the side"," and from behind. Then he said"," \""Shall I disclose or conceal?\"" He said"," \""Rather"," conceal.\"" He said"," \""He has indeed taken resemblance from both of them"," and I do not know which of them he belongs to.\"" So he seated him. Then he said to the other"," \""Look.\"" So he looked"," facing"," examining from the side"," and from behind. Then he said"," \""Shall I disclose or conceal?\"" He said"," \""Rather"," conceal.\"" He said"," \""He has indeed taken resemblance from both of them"," and I do not know which of them he belongs to.\"" So he seated him. Then he said to the third"," \""Look.\"" So he looked"," facing"," examining from the side"," and from behind. Then he said"," \""Shall I disclose or conceal?\"" He said"," \""Rather"," disclose.\"" He said"," \""The resemblance has indeed been taken from both of them"," and I do not know which of them he belongs to.\"" ʿUmar"," may Allah be pleased with him"," said: \""We trace the resemblances three times\""—and ʿUmar"," may Allah be pleased with him"," was himself an expert in physiognomy. So he assigned the child to both of them; they would inherit from him and he would inherit from them. Saʿīd said"," \""Do you know who his ʿaṣaba (residuary heirs) are?\"" I said"," \""No.\"" He said"," \""The last of the two to die.\"" [Ḥasan]"""
"21272","(21266) Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn ʿAlī al-Aṣbahānī informed us: Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Aṣbahānī informed us: Ismāʿīl ibn Ibrāhīm al-Qaṭṭān narrated to us: al-Ḥasan ibn ʿĪsā informed us: Ibn al-Mubārak informed us: Shuʿba narrated from Qatāda from Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyib, who said: ʿUmar, may Allah be pleased with him, called the experts in physiognomy (qāfa) regarding two men who had intercourse with a woman, each one of the two claiming the child. They said, \They share in him.\"" So ʿUmar"," may Allah be pleased with him"," divided him between the two of them. Saʿīd said"," \""Do you know who inherits from him?\"" He said"," \""The last of the two to die inherits from him.\"" [Ḥasan]"""
"21273","(21267) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd narrated to us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās narrated to us: Yaḥyā narrated to us: Yazīd narrated from Mubārak ibn Faḍāla from al-Ḥasan from ʿUmar, may Allah be pleased with him, regarding two men who had intercourse with a slave woman in a single period of purity, and she bore a boy. They brought the matter to ʿUmar, may Allah be pleased with him, and he called for three experts in physiognomy (qāfa). They agreed that he had taken resemblance from both of them. ʿUmar, may Allah be pleased with him, was himself an expert in physiognomy who traced resemblances. He said: \The bitch is mounted by the black dog"," the yellow dog"," and the tawny dog"," and she produces offspring resembling each dog. I had not seen this among people until I saw this.\"" So ʿUmar"," may Allah be pleased with him"," assigned the child to both of them; they would inherit from him and he would inherit from them"," and he would belong to the last of the two to die.\n\nThe Shaykh"," may Allah have mercy on him"," said: These two narrations are the narration of the Baṣrans from Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyib from ʿUmar"," and their narration from al-Ḥasan from ʿUmar"," may Allah be pleased with him; both of them are munqaṭiʿ (disconnected). In them"," if they are authentic"," there is evidence"," along with what has preceded"," for ruling by resemblance and"," in cases of uncertainty"," referring to the statement of the experts in physiognomy (qāfa). As for attributing the child to both of them in the absence of the qāfa"," the Baṣrans are alone in this from ʿUmar"," may Allah be pleased with him. The narration of the Ḥijāzīs from ʿUmar"," may Allah be pleased with him"," is as has been mentioned previously"," and the narration of the Ḥijāzīs from him is more deserving of authenticity. The narration of Yaḥyā ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Ḥāṭib from his father from ʿUmar"," may Allah be pleased with him"," is mawṣūl (connected)"," and the narration of Sulaymān ibn Yasār has corroborating witnesses. Both of them confirm the statement of ʿUmar"," may Allah be pleased with him"," \""Whichever of them you wish","\"" and ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Ḥāṭib says in his narration: \""It is as though I see him following whichever of them he goes.\"" And Allah knows best. [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"21274","(21268) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq narrated to us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān narrated to us: al-Shāfiʿī narrated to us: Ibn ʿUlayya narrated from Ḥumayd from Anas: that he had doubts regarding a son of his, so he called the experts in physiognomy (qāfa) for him. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"21275","(21269) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-Walīd al-Faqīh narrated to us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Aʿlā narrated to us: al-Muʿtamir narrated to us. He said: I heard Ḥumayd narrating from one of the sons of Anas ibn Mālik: that Anas fell ill with an illness and had doubts regarding the pregnancy of his slave woman. He said: \If I die"," then call the experts in physiognomy (qāfa) for him.\"" He said: \""Then he recovered.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"21276","(21270) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn Ḥamshādh narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Ismāʿīl, Abū Ismāʿīl, narrated to us: Ibn Abī Maryam narrated to me: Yaḥyā ibn Ayyūb narrated to me: Ḥumayd informed me that Mūsā ibn Anas ibn Mālik narrated to him from Anas ibn Mālik: that he made a will during his illness and had doubts regarding the pregnancy of his slave woman. He said: \See to it that you call the experts in physiognomy (qāfa) for her child.\"" He said: \""Then he recovered from that illness.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ; see above]"""
"21277","(21271) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-Walīd narrated to us: Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā informed us: Ḥammād ibn Zayd narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn ʿUbayd narrated to us: Ḥammād ibn Zayd narrated from one who informed him from Muḥammad ibn Sīrīn: that Abū Mūsā, may Allah be pleased with him, ruled by the experts in physiognomy (qāfa). And it is narrated from Ibn ʿAbbās that which indicates that he acted upon the statement of the experts in physiognomy (qāfa)."
"21278","(21272) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq informed us: Ismāʿīl ibn Qutayba narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā informed us: al-Layth ibn Saʿd narrated from Ibn Shihāb from ʿUrwa from ʿĀʾisha, may Allah be pleased with her, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, came to me in a state of delight, the lines of his face gleaming, and said: \Have you not seen that Mujazziz just now looked at Zayd ibn Ḥāritha and Usāma ibn Zayd and said"," 'Some of these feet are from some of the others'?\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ; agreed upon]"""
"21279","(21273) He said: And Abū al-Faḍl ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn Salama narrated to us: Qutayba ibn Saʿīd narrated to us: al-Layth narrated it with its chain, similar to it.\n\nIt was narrated by al-Bukhārī and Muslim in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Qutayba, and Muslim narrated it from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā. [Ṣaḥīḥ; agreed upon]\n\n(21274) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Abū ʿAmr al-Mustamlī narrated to us: Qutayba ibn Saʿīd narrated to us: Ibn Abī Zāʾida narrated from his father from Muṣʿab ibn Shayba from Musāfiʿ ibn ʿAbd Allāh from ʿUrwa ibn al-Zubayr from ʿĀʾisha, may Allah be pleased with her, in the story of a woman's nocturnal emission. She said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: \Resemblance only comes from that direction: when her fluid prevails over the man's fluid"," the child resembles his maternal uncles; and when the man's fluid prevails over her fluid"," the child resembles his paternal uncles.\""\n\nIt was narrated by Muslim in the Ṣaḥīḥ from the ḥadīth of Yaḥyā ibn Zakariyyā ibn Abī Zāʾida. [Ṣaḥīḥ; agreed upon]"""
"21280","(21275) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān in Baghdād informed us: Abū Sahl ibn Ziyād al-Qaṭṭān narrated to us: Ismāʿīl al-Qāḍī narrated to us: Ismāʿīl ibn Abī Uways narrated to us: Mālik narrated from Ibn Shihāb from Saʿīd from Abū Hurayra, may Allah be pleased with him: that a Bedouin man came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, and said: \O Messenger of Allah"," my wife has given birth to a black boy.\"" The Prophet"," peace and blessings be upon him"," said to him: \""Do you have camels?\"" He said"," \""Yes.\"" He said"," \""What are their colors?\"" He said"," \""Red.\"" He said"," \""Is there among them a grey one (awraq)?\"" He said"," \""Yes.\"" He said"," \""How is that?\"" He said"," \""I think it is a vein (ʿirq) that has pulled it.\"" The Messenger of Allah"," peace and blessings be upon him"," said: \""Perhaps your son is one whose vein has pulled him.\""\n\nIt was narrated by al-Bukhārī in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Ismāʿīl ibn Abī Uways"," and Muslim narrated it from another route from al-Zuhrī. [Ṣaḥīḥ; see above]"""
"21281","(21275) Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: A Bedouin came and said, \My wife has given birth to a black child.\"" The Prophet (peace be upon him) asked"," \""Do you have camels?\"" He replied"," \""Yes.\"" The Prophet (peace be upon him) asked"," \""What is their colour?\"" He said"," \""Red.\"" The Prophet (peace be upon him) asked"," \""Is there any grey among them?\"" He said"," \""Yes.\"" The Prophet (peace be upon him) asked"," \""Where did that come from?\"" He said"," \""Perhaps a vein drew it out.\"" The Prophet (peace be upon him) said"," \""Perhaps your son was likewise drawn out by a vein.\"""""
"21282","(21276) Anas ibn Malik (may Allah be pleased with him), regarding the story of li'an (mutual cursing), narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: \Observe her. If she gives birth to him white"," with straight hair and sunken eyes"," then he is the son of Hilal ibn Umayyah. And if she gives birth to him black"," with curly hair and thin shins"," then he is the son of Sharik ibn Sahma'.\"" The narrator said: \""I was informed that she gave birth to him black"," with curly hair and thin shins.\"""""
"21283","(21277) Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that Hilal ibn Umayyah accused his wife of adultery with Sharik ibn Sahma' in the presence of the Prophet (peace be upon him). He mentioned the story of li'an. The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: \Observe her. If she gives birth to him with dark"," deep-set eyes"," full buttocks"," and thin shins"," then he is the son of Sharik ibn Sahma'.\"" She gave birth to him thus. The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: \""Were it not for what has already passed of the decree of Allah"," there would have been for me and her a matter.\"""""
"21284","(21278) A'ishah (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas and Abd ibn Zam'ah disputed over a boy. Sa'd said, \O Messenger of Allah"," this is the son of my brother Utbah ibn Abi Waqqas. He entrusted him to me. Look at his resemblance.\"" And Abd ibn Zam'ah said"," \""This is my brother"," O Messenger of Allah. He was born on my father's bed from his slave-girl.\"" The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) looked at the resemblance and saw a clear resemblance to Utbah. He said"," \""He is yours"," O Abd. The child belongs to the bed"," and the adulterer receives the stones.\"" And he said"," \""O Sawdah bint Zam'ah"," veil yourself from him.\"" So she never saw him."""
"21285","(21279) Muhammad ibn Sirin narrates: Abu al-Walid performed Hajj with us, and we were seven children of Sirin. We passed through Madinah and he took us to Zayd ibn Thabit. He said to him, \These are the children of Sirin.\"" Zayd said"," \""These two are from one mother"," and these two are from one mother"," and these two are from one mother"," and this one is from a mother.\"" He did not err"," for Yahya ibn Sirin was the brother of Muhammad from his mother."""
"21286","(21280) Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him)—the truthful and the one told the truth—said: \Indeed"," the creation of each one of you is gathered in the womb of his mother for forty days"," then he becomes a clot for the same period"," then he becomes a lump of flesh for the same period. Then Allah sends an angel to him"," who breathes the spirit into him"," and he is commanded with four words: Write his provision"," his deeds"," his lifespan"," and whether he is wretched or blessed. By Allah"," besides whom there is no deity"," indeed one of you may perform the deeds of the people of the Fire until there is only an arm's length between him and it"," and the decree overtakes him"," and he is sealed with the deeds of the people of Paradise"," so he enters it. And indeed one of you may perform the deeds of the people of Paradise until there is only an arm's length between him and it"," and the decree overtakes him"," and he is sealed with the deeds of the people of the Fire"," so he enters it.\"""""
"21287","(21281) Zayd ibn Arqam (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) was in Yemen when three men came to him who had all been intimate with one woman during a single period of purity. He asked two of them, \Do you acknowledge this child?\"" They said"," \""No.\"" Then he asked another two"," \""Do you acknowledge this child?\"" They said"," \""No.\"" Then he asked another two"," \""Do you acknowledge this child?\"" They said"," \""No.\"" He said: \""Every time I asked two of them"," 'Do you acknowledge this child?' they said"," 'No.' So he cast lots among them and attributed the child to the one upon whom the lot fell"," and placed upon him two-thirds of the blood-money.\"" He mentioned this to the Prophet (peace be upon him)"," and he laughed until his molars became visible."""
"21288","(21282) Zayd ibn Arqam (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: I was sitting with the Prophet (peace be upon him) when a man from the people of Yemen came and said, \A group of three men from the people of Yemen came to Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) disputing over a child"," and they had all been intimate with one woman during a single period of purity. He said to two of them"," 'Consent to this child for this one","' but they refused. Then he said to another two"," 'Consent to this child for this one","' but they refused. He said"," 'You are contentious partners. I shall cast lots among you. The one upon whom the lot falls shall have the child"," and upon him shall be two-thirds of the blood-money for his two companions.' So he cast lots among them and assigned it to the one upon whom the lot fell.\"" The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) laughed until his molars—or he said"," his wisdom teeth—became visible."""
"21289","(21283) Abu Sa'id al-Malini narrated to us, Abu Ahmad ibn Adi al-Hafiz narrated to us, he said: I heard Ibn Hammad say: Al-Bukhari said: \Abdullah ibn al-Khudhrami narrated from Zayd ibn Arqam from the Prophet (peace be upon him) regarding the casting of lots—he was not followed up on it.\"" The Sheikh said: Al-Bukhari mentioned the hadith of Abd al-Razzaq"," where he said it was narrated from Abd Khayr"," as though he did not consider it preserved. And the hadith of Ibn Khalil was likewise narrated by a group from al-Ajlah. It was also narrated from him from Amir al-Sha'bi from Abi al-Khalil from Zayd. And it was said from him from al-Sha'bi from Abdullah ibn al-Khudhrami from Ali (may Allah be pleased with him). And it was said from him from al-Sha'bi from Ali (may Allah be pleased with him)."""
"21290","(21284) Abu Muhammad Abdullah ibn Yusuf al-Isbahani narrated to us, Abu Sa'id ibn al-A'rabi narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Muhammad al-Za'farani narrated to us, Shababah narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated from Salamah ibn Kuhayl from al-Sha'bi from Abi al-Khalil or Ibn al-Khalil from Ali (may Allah be pleased with him): \Three men shared in the intimacy of one woman during a single period of purity"," and they all claimed the child. Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) ordered a man to cast lots among them"," and he ordered the one upon whom the lot fell to give the other two two-thirds of the blood-money"," and the child would be his.\"" This is a mawquf narration"," and Ibn al-Khalil is alone in it"," and Allah knows best. Al-Shafi'i (may Allah be pleased with him) mentioned this hadith in the old compilation and in the book of Ali and Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with them both)"," and he said: \""If it were established from the Prophet (peace be upon him)"," we would follow it"," and the proof would be in it.\"""""
"21291","(21285) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū al-Walīd narrated to us, ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad said: Abū ʿAbd Allāh — meaning Muḥammad ibn Naṣr — said: Abū Thawr said: Abū ʿAbd Allāh — meaning al-Shāfiʿī, may Allah have mercy upon him — said: \When there is no expert in physiognomy (qāfah) and the one who would provide clarification is absent"," then lots shall be drawn between them.\"" The Shaykh"," may Allah have mercy upon him"," said: It has been narrated through another chain from ʿAlī"," may Allah be pleased with him"," in a marfūʿ (elevated) narration. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"21292","(21286) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr al-Ṣayrafī both informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn ʿAffān narrated to us, ʿUbayd Allāh — he is the son of Mūsā — informed us, Dāwūd al-Awdī narrated from al-Shaʿbī, from Abū Juḥayfah al-Suwāʾī, who said: \When ʿAlī"," may Allah be pleased with him"," was in Yemen"," three men came to him disputing over a boy — or he said: contesting over a boy. Each one of them said: 'He is my son.' So ʿAlī"," may Allah be pleased with him"," drew lots among them. He assigned the child to the one upon whom the lot fell"," and imposed upon him two-thirds of the blood-money for the other two men.\"" He said: \""This reached the Messenger of Allah ﷺ"," and he laughed until his back teeth were visible"," on account of ʿAlī's judgment"," may Allah be pleased with him.\"" Dāwūd ibn Yazīd al-Awdī is not used as a ḥujjah (authoritative proof). [Ḥasan]"""
"21293","(21287) Another judgment has been narrated from ʿAlī, may Allah be pleased with him, in this matter, in a different story. Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn ʿAlī al-Aṣbahānī al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Aṣbahānī informed us, Ismāʿīl ibn Ibrāhīm al-Qaṭṭān narrated to us, al-Ḥasan ibn ʿĪsā informed us, Ibn al-Mubārak informed us, Sufyān narrated from Qābūs, from Abī Ẓabyān, from ʿAlī, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: \Two men came to him who had both been intimate with a woman during one period of purity. He said: 'The child is between the two of you"," and it belongs to the one of you who remains (i.e."," the one who is the true father).'\"" It has also been narrated through another chain from ʿAlī"," may Allah be pleased with him"," in a mursal (disconnected) form"," and there is question regarding its attribution to ʿAlī"," may Allah be pleased with him. [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"21294","(21288) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ, Abū ʿAbd Allāh Isḥāq ibn Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf al-Sūsī, and Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī all said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Khālid ibn Khalī al-Ḥimṣī narrated to us, Bishr ibn Shuʿayb narrated from his father, from Abī al-Zinād, from al-Aʿraj, from Abū Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \While two women were with them their two sons"," a wolf came and carried away the son of one of them. This one said to her companion: 'It has carried away your son.' The other said: 'It has carried away your son.' So they took their dispute to Dāwūd"," peace be upon him"," and he judged in favour of the elder woman. They then went out to Sulaymān ibn Dāwūd"," peace be upon him"," and informed him. He said: 'Bring me a knife so that I may split him between the two of you.' The younger woman said: 'Do not do that — may Allah have mercy upon you — he is her son.' So he judged in favour of the younger woman.\"" Abū Hurayrah"," may Allah be pleased with him"," said: \""By Allah"," I never heard the word 'sikkīn' (knife) before that day. We used only to say 'mudyah.'\"" Al-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Abī al-Yamān from Shuʿayb. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muttafaq ʿalayh]"""
"21295","(21289) Abū Ḥāzim al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū ʿAmr Ismāʿīl ibn Nujayd al-Sulamī informed us, Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-ʿAbdī narrated to us, Umayyah ibn Bisṭām narrated to us, Yazīd ibn Zuraiʿ narrated to us, Rūḥ ibn al-Qāsim narrated from Muḥammad ibn ʿAjlān, from Abī al-Zinād, from al-Aʿraj, from Abū Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: \Two women"," one of whose sons was eaten by a wolf"," came to Dāwūd"," peace be upon him"," disputing over the remaining son. He judged in favour of the elder woman. When they went out to Sulaymān"," peace be upon him"," he asked: 'How did he judge between you?' They informed him. He said: 'Bring me a knife.'\"" Abū Hurayrah"," may Allah be pleased with him"," said: \""The first time I heard anyone say 'sikkīn' was the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. We used only to call it 'mudyah.'\"" The younger woman said: 'Why?' He said: 'So that I may split him between the two of you.' She said: 'Give him to her.' The elder woman said: 'Split him between us.' So he judged in favour of the younger woman and said: 'If he were your son"," you would not consent to having him split.'\"" Muslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Umayyah ibn Bisṭām. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"21296","(21290) Abū Naṣr ibn Qatādah informed us, Abū ʿAmr ibn Maṭar and Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Sarrāj both informed us, saying: Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā ibn Sulaymān al-Marwazī narrated to us, ʿĀṣim ibn ʿAlī narrated to us, Shuʿbah narrated from ʿAmr ibn Murrah, who said: I asked Saʿīd ibn Jubayr about this verse: {And those who believed and whose offspring followed them in faith} [al-Ṭūr 21]. He said: Ibn ʿAbbās, may Allah be pleased with him, said: \The believer shall have his offspring joined with him"," so that Allah may cool his eyes through them"," even if they are below him in deeds.\"" [Ḥasan]"""
"21297","(21291) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī al-Ṣanʿānī narrated to us in Makkah, Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbbād informed us, ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us, al-Thawrī narrated from ʿAmr ibn Murrah, from Saʿīd ibn Jubayr, from Ibn ʿAbbās, may Allah be pleased with both of them, regarding the words of the Almighty: {We shall join their offspring with them and shall not diminish anything of their deeds} [al-Ṭūr 21]. He said: \Allah raises the offspring of the believer with him in his station in Paradise"," even if they are below him in deeds.\"" Then he recited: {And those who believed and whose offspring followed them in faith — We shall join their offspring with them and shall not diminish anything} — meaning: We shall not reduce anything from them. Al-Thawrī did not hear it from ʿAmr; rather"," someone else narrated it from al-Thawrī from his own hearing from ʿAmr. We have mentioned this elsewhere. The ḥadīth of Shuʿbah from ʿAmr is connected (mawṣūl). Al-Shāfiʿī"," may Allah have mercy upon him"," said"," among the things he cited as evidence: \""Islam is most deserving of authority"," for Allah"," the Most High"," has elevated Islam above all other religions"," and the highest authority is most deserving of judgment.\"" Something to this effect has also been narrated from ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb"," may Allah be pleased with him. [Ḥasan. Preceded before it]"""
"21298","(21292) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū al-Walīd narrated to us, ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad said: Abū ʿAbd Allāh — meaning Muḥammad ibn Naṣr — narrated to us, Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā informed us, Abū Muʿāwiyah narrated from Ashʿath, from al-Ḥasan, who said: ʿUmar, may Allah be pleased with him, said: \The child belongs to the Muslim parent.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"21299","(21293) He said: Abū ʿAbd Allāh narrated to us, Yaḥyā narrated from Hushaym, from Ashʿath, from al-Shaʿbī, from Sharīḥ: \A dispute was brought before him concerning a boy whose parents were Christian. He said: 'The Muslim parent has greater right to the child.'\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"21300","(21294) He said: Abū ʿAbd Allāh narrated to us, Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā informed us, Yazīd ibn Zuraiʿ narrated from Yūnus, from al-Ḥasan, regarding the minor child, he said: \He is with the Muslim one of his two parents.\"" All that has been narrated on this topic has already been mentioned in the book on the Foundling (al-Laqīṭ). [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"21301","(21295) Abū al-Qāsim ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Tājir al-Aṣbahānī in Rayy informed us that Abū al-Qāsim Ḥamzah ibn ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Aḥmad al-Mālikī informed us that Abū Ḥātim Muḥammad ibn Idrīs informed us that Abū al-Walīd Hishām ibn ʿAbd al-Malik al-Ṭayālisī and ʿAbd Allāh ibn Maslamah al-Qaʿnabī both said: Nāfiʿ ibn ʿUmar al-Jumaḥī informed us from Ibn Abī Mulaykah, who said: Ibn ʿAbbās — may Allah be pleased with them both — wrote to me that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ decreed that the oath is upon the defendant.\n\nThey both recorded it in the Ṣaḥīḥ as has been previously mentioned. And here, each one of them is a defendant with respect to what is in his hand; the statement is his statement along with his oath, in negation of what his companion claims against him.\n\nAl-Shāfiʿī — may Allah have mercy upon him — said: A man may possess the belongings of women, and a woman may possess the belongings of a man through purchase and inheritance and other means. And ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib — may Allah be pleased with them both — made Ṣalāḥ (dowry) for Fāṭimah — may Allah be pleased with them both — a suit of iron (i.e., a coat of mail), and this is the belonging of a man, while Fāṭimah — may Allah be pleased with her — at that time was the owner of the suit of iron, not ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib — may Allah be pleased with him.\n\nThe Shaykh said: This has also passed in the narration of ʿIkrimah from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: When ʿAlī married Fāṭimah — may Allah be pleased with them both — the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: \Give her something.\"" He said: \""I have nothing.\"" He said: \""Where is your Ḥuṭamī coat of mail?\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Muttafaq ʿalayh]"""
"21302","(21296) And it has been narrated from ʿAlī — may Allah be pleased with him —: Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf al-Aṣbahānī informed us that Abū Saʿīd ibn al-Aʿrābī informed us that al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad al-Zaʿfarānī informed us that Saʿīd ibn Sulaymān informed us that Muḥammad ibn Sulaymān informed us that Raqabah said: Yazīd ibn Abī Muslim came out from the presence of al-Ḥajjāj and said: \The commander has issued a ruling.\"" Al-Shaʿbī said to him: \""What is it?\"" He said: \""Whatever belongs to a man belongs to the man"," and whatever belongs to women belongs to the woman.\"" He said to al-Shaʿbī: \""It is the ruling of a man from the people of Badr.\"" He said: \""Who is he?\"" He said: \""I shall not inform you.\"" He said: \""Who is it"," upon the covenant of Allah and His pledge"," that I should not inform of him?\"" He said: \""It is ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib — may Allah be pleased with him.\"" He (Yazīd) then went to al-Ḥajjāj and informed him. Al-Ḥajjāj said: \""He has spoken the truth — woe to you! We do not seek vengeance against ʿAlī for his ruling. We know that ʿAlī was the most judicious of them (aqḍāhum).\""\n\n[Ḍaʿīf]"""
"21303","(21297) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzakkī informed us that Abū al-Ḥasan Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad, meaning al-Ṭarāʾifī, informed us that Abū Saʿīd ʿUthmān ibn Saʿīd informed us that Muḥammad ibn Kathīr al-ʿAbdī informed us that Sufyān, namely al-Thawrī, informed us from Hishām ibn ʿUrwah from his father from ʿĀʾishah — may Allah be pleased with her — that Hind said to the Prophet ﷺ: \O Messenger of Allah"," Abū Sufyān is a stingy man. Is there any sin upon me if I take from his wealth secretly?\"" He said: \""Take what suffices you and your children"," reasonably (bil-maʿrūf).\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn Kathīr.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Muttafaq ʿalayh]"""
"21304","(21298) Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī and Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq both informed us that Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us that al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us that al-Shāfiʿī informed us that Anas ibn ʿIyāḍ informed us from Hishām ibn ʿUrwah — (ḥ) and Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me that Abū al-Walīd informed us that Ibrāhīm ibn Abī Ṭālib informed us that Kurayb informed us that Wakīʿ and Ibn Numayr informed us from Hishām ibn ʿUrwah from his father from ʿĀʾishah — may Allah be pleased with her — she said: Hind came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: \O Messenger of Allah"," Abū Sufyān is a stingy man and does not spend upon me and my children what suffices me and my sons. May I take from his wealth while he is unaware?\"" He said: \""Take what suffices you and your children"," reasonably (bil-maʿrūf).\""\n\nIn the narration of Anas ibn ʿIyāḍ: \""He does not give me what suffices me and my children except what I take from him secretly while he does not know. Is there any blame upon me for that?\"" Then he mentioned it.\n\nMuslim narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Abī Kurayb"," and he extracted it from the ḥadīth of al-Zuhrī from ʿUrwah from ʿĀʾishah — may Allah be pleased with her.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Previously mentioned]"""
"21305","(21299) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us that Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us that Ibn Milḥān informed us that Yaḥyā ibn Bukayr informed us that al-Layth informed me that Yūnus informed us from Ibn Shihāb — (ḥ) and Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me that Abū Muḥammad al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Ḥalīm al-Marwazī informed us that Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr ibn al-Muwajjih informed us that ʿAbdān informed us that ʿAbd Allāh from Yūnus ibn Yazīd from al-Zuhrī, who informed me that ʿUrwah informed him from ʿĀʾishah — may Allah be pleased with her — she said: Hind bint ʿUtbah ibn Rabīʿah came and said: \O Messenger of Allah"," by Allah"," there was no household upon the surface of the earth more beloved to me than that they be humiliated from your household. And then today there is no household upon the surface of the earth more beloved to me than that they be raided from your household.\"" He said: \""And also"," by the One in whose Hand is my soul.\"" Then she said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," Abū Sufyān is a miserly man. Is there any sin upon me if I feed his dependents from what he has?\"" He said: \""No — reasonably (bil-maʿrūf).\"" And in the narration of Ibn Bukayr: \""Is there any sin upon me that I feed from what he has?\"" He said: \""Yes — reasonably (bil-maʿrūf).\""\n\nTheir meanings are the same"," and Ibn Bukayr was uncertain whether it was aḥyāʾ or khiyāb.\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Ibn Bukayr"," and in another place from ʿAbdān"," and Muslim extracted it from two other directions from Ibn Shihāb.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"21306","(21300) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us that Abū Bakr al-Qaṭṭān informed us that ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥasan informed us that Abū Jābir Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Malik informed us that Shuʿbah informed us from Abī al-Jūdī, who said: I heard Saʿīd ibn al-Muhājir say that he heard al-Miqdām say that he heard the Prophet ﷺ say: \Any Muslim who is a guest of a people"," and the guest is left deprived"," it is a right upon every Muslim to support him"," so that he may take from his (the host's) wealth and his crops the equivalent of his hospitality.\""\n\n[Ḍaʿīf]"""
"21307","(21301) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us that Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣaghānī informed us that Abū Salamah Manṣūr ibn Salamah al-Khuzāʿī informed us that Layth ibn Saʿd informed us from Yazīd ibn Abī Ḥabīb from Abī al-Khayr from ʿUqbah ibn ʿĀmir, who said: I said: \O Messenger of Allah"," you send us forth and we arrive among a people who do not host us. What do you see in that?\"" The Prophet ﷺ said: \""If you arrive among a people and they are commanded with what is befitting for a guest"," then accept it. And if they do not do so"," then take from them the right of the guest that is befitting for them.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf and others from al-Layth"," and Muslim narrated it from Qutaybah from al-Layth.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Muttafaq ʿalayh]"""
"21308","(21302) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us that Muḥammad ibn Bakr informed us that Abū Dāwūd informed us that Abū Kāmil informed us that Yazīd ibn Zurayʿ informed them, who said: Ḥumayd al-Ṭawīl informed us from Yūsuf ibn Māhik al-Makkī, who said: I used to write the expenditure of certain orphans for a man who was their guardian, and he cheated me out of one thousand dirhams. Then he (the guardian) paid it back to them, and I found their wealth to be the same (amount). He said: I said: \Take the one thousand that they took from you.\"" He said: \""No. My father informed me that he heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'Render back the trust to the one who entrusted you"," and do not betray the one who betrayed you.'\""\n\n[Ḍaʿīf]"""
"21309","(21303) And Abū al-Ḥusayn ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Bishrān in Baghdad informed us that Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr al-Razzāz informed us that ʿAbbās ibn Muḥammad informed us that Ṭalq ibn Ghanām al-Nakhaʿī informed us that Sharīk and Qays informed us from Abī Ḥuṣayn from Abī Ṣāliḥ from Abī Hurayrah that the Prophet ﷺ said: \Render back the trust to the one who entrusted you"," and do not betray the one who betrayed you.\"" Abū al-Faḍl said: I said to Ṭalq: \""Should I write down Sharīk and omit Qays?\"" He said: \""You are more knowledgeable of the ḥadīth.\"" The first ḥadīth is in the ruling of the munqaṭiʿ (disconnected chain)"," since Yūsuf ibn Māhik did not mention the name of the one who narrated to him"," nor the name of the one who narrated from the one who narrated to him. And the ḥadīth of Abī Ḥuṣayn was singularly transmitted from him by Sharīk al-Qāḍī and Qays ibn al-Rabīʿ. And Qays is ḍaʿīf"," and Sharīk was not used as a proof by most scholars of ḥadīth; Muslim ibn al-Ḥajjāj only mentioned him in the shawāhid (supporting narrations).\n\nAnd it has been narrated from Abī Ḥafṣ al-Dimashqī from Maḥkūl from Abī Umāmah from the Prophet ﷺ"," and this is ḍaʿīf"," because Maḥkūl did not hear anything from Abī Umāmah"," and Abī Ḥafṣ al-Dimashqī is majhūl (unknown).\n\nAnd it has been narrated from al-Ḥasan from the Prophet ﷺ"," and it is munqaṭiʿ (disconnected).\n\n[Ḍaʿīf]"""
"21310","(21304) And Ayyūb ibn Suwayd — who is ḍaʿīf — narrated it from Ibn Shawdhāb from Abī al-Tayyāḥ from Anas, marfūʿ (elevated). Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-ʿAṭṭār al-Ḥayrī informed us that Abū Saʿīd al-Rāzī informed us that Aḥmad ibn ʿUmayr informed us that Sulaymān al-Khassāf informed us that Ayyūb ibn Suwayd informed them, and he mentioned it.\n\n[Ḍaʿīf]"
"21311","(21305) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us that Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm narrated to us that al-Rabīʿ said: al-Shāfiʿī, may Allah have mercy upon him, said regarding this hadith: \It is not established (thābit) among the scholars of hadith among you. And even if it were established"," it would not constitute a proof (ḥujjah) against us.\"" Then he continued speaking until he said: \""When the Sunnah and the consensus (ijmāʿ) of many scholars of knowledge indicate that a man may take what is rightfully his secretly from the one who owes it"," then it is established that this is not betrayal (khiyānah). Bettaking is taking what is not lawful to take. If someone betrays me regarding one dirham and I say"," 'He has made my betrayal lawful for himself","' it would not be permissible for me to take ten dirams from him in requital for his betrayal of me. Rather"," I may take one diram"," and I would not thereby be a betrayer or wrongdoer"," just as you would be a betrayer and wrongdoer by taking nine dirams along with my diram"," because you did not betray those.\"""""
"21312","(21306) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq narrated to us that al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn Ziyād said that Aḥmad ibn Yūnus narrated to us that ʿĀṣim ibn Muḥammad narrated to us that Wāqid ibn Muḥammad narrated to me that Saʿīd ibn Marjānah, the companion of ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥusayn, narrated to me that he said: Abū Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Any Muslim man who frees a Muslim man"," Allah will ransom him for every limb of the freed person"," a limb of his own from the Fire.\""\n\nSaʿīd ibn Marjānah said: I heard the hadith and went with it to ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥusayn"," who then set free a slave for whom ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar had given ten thousand dirams or one thousand dinars.\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Aḥmad ibn Yūnus"," and Muslim narrated it from another route from ʿĀṣim. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"21313","(21307) ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us that Aḥmad ibn ʔUbayd al-Ṣaffār narrated us that Ibn Milḥān narrated to us that Ibn Bukayr narrated to us that al-Layth narrated from Ibn al-Hād from ʿUmar ibn ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥusayn from Saʿīd ibn Marjānah, who heard him narrate from Abū Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \Whoever frees a believing slave"," Allah will free for every limb of that slave a limb of his own from the Fire"," until He frees his private parts for his private parts.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Qutaybah from al-Layth. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muttafaq ʿalayh]"""
"21314","(21308) Abū Naṣr Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Shīrāzī al-Faqīh informed us that Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn Nuʿaym and Aḥmad ibn Sahl said that Dāwūd ibn Rushayd narrated to us that al-Walīd ibn Muslim narrated from Muḥammad ibn Muṭarrif, Abū Ghassān, from Zayd ibn Aslam from ʿAlī ibn Ḥusayn from Saʿīd ibn Marjānah from Abū Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, who said: \Whoever frees a slave"," Allah will free for every limb of that slave a limb of his own from the Fire"," even his private parts for his private parts.\"" Muslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Dāwūd ibn Rushayd"," and al-Bukhārī narrated it from Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥīm from Dāwūd ibn Rushayd. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muttafaq ʿalayh]"""
"21315","(21309) Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Fūrak informed us that ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us that Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb narrated to us that Abū Dāwūd narrated to us that Shuʿbah narrated from ʿAmr ibn Murrah, who said: I heard Sālim ibn Abī al-Jaʿd narrate from Shuraḥbīl ibn al-Simṭ, who said: It was said to Kaʿb ibn Murrah — or Murrah ibn Kaʿb — al-Bahzī: \Narrate to us a hadith you heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. May your father be sacrificed for Allah"," and beware (of falsehood).\"" He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \""Any Muslim man who frees a Muslim man shall be his ransom from the Fire; he will be recompensed for every bone of his bones with a bone of his own. And any Muslim man who frees two Muslim women shall be their ransom from the Fire; he will be recompensed for every two bones of their bones with a bone of his own. And any Muslim woman who frees a Muslim woman shall be her ransom from the Fire; she will be recompensed for every bone of her bones with a bone of her own.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"21316","(21310) Abū ʿUthmān Saʿīd ibn Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdān al-Naysābūrī informed us that Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Muʾammal narrated to us that al-Faḍl ibn Muḥammad al-Shaʿrānī narrated to us that Abū Ṣāliḥ narrated to me that Muʿāwiyah ibn Ṣāliḥ said: I heard Asad ibn Wādiʿah al-Ṭāʾī say: Shuraḥbīl ibn al-Simṭ, who was the governor of Ḥimṣ, said to ʿAmr ibn ʿAbasah al-Salamī, a companion of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: \O Abā Najīḥ"," narrate to us a hadith you heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ"," without any addition or omission.\"" He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \""Whoever frees a believing slave"," Allah will free for every limb of that slave a limb of his own from the Fire. And whoever shoots an arrow in the cause of Allah and it reaches the enemy and strikes"," it is for him equivalent to freeing a slave. And whoever grows grey-haired in the cause of Allah"," it will be for him a light on the Day of Resurrection.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"21317","(21311) Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Fūrak informed us that ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us that Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb narrated to us that Abū Dāwūd narrated to us that Hishām narrated from Qatādah from Sālim ibn Abī al-Jaʿd from Maʿdān ibn Abī Ṭalḥah al-Yaʿmurī from Abū Najīḥ al-Sulamī, who said: We besieged the fortress of al-Ṭāʾif with the Prophet ﷺ, and I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \Whoever shoots an arrow in the cause of Allah"," it is for him equivalent to freeing a slave.\"" I shot sixteen arrows that day. And I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \""Whoever shoots an arrow in the cause of Allah"," it is for him a degree in Paradise. And whoever grows grey-haired in Islam"," it will be for him a light on the Day of Resurrection. And any Muslim man who frees a Muslim man"," Allah will make for every bone of his bones a bone of his own"," freed from the Fire. And any Muslim woman who frees a Muslim woman"," Allah"," Mighty and Majestic"," will make for every bone of her bones a bone of her own"," freed from the Fire.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"21318","(21312) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that ʿAlī ibn Ḥamshādh al-ʿAdl narrated to us that Ibrāhīm ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn Dayzīl narrated to us that Ādam ibn Abī Iyās al-ʿAsqalānī, ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Zubayr al-Ḥumaydī, and Ibrāhīm ibn Bashshār al-Ramādī said: Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah narrated to me that a shaykh from the people of Kūfah, called Shuʿbah, said: We were with Abū Burdah ibn Abī Mūsā, and his sons were with him. He said: \Shall I not narrate to you a hadith that my father narrated to me?\"" They said: \""Yes"," father"," narrate to us.\"" He said: My father narrated to me that he heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \""Whoever frees a slave or a bondsman shall be his ransom from the Fire"," limb for limb.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ in other than this chain]"""
"21319","(21313) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us that Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn ʿUmar ibn Ḥafṣ al-Zāhid narrated to us that al-Sarī ibn Khuzaymah narrated to us that Abū Nuʿaym narrated to us — (ḥ) And Abū Bakr ibn Fūrak informed us that ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us that Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb narrated to us that Abū Dāwūd narrated to us — both said: ʿĪsā ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān narrated from Ṭalḥah al-Yāmī from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAwsajah from al-Barāʾ, who said: A Bedouin came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: \O Messenger of Allah"," tell me of a deed that will admit me into Paradise.\"" He said: \""Even though you have shortened the sermon"," you have made the question lengthy. Free a soul (nasamah) and ransom a slave (raqabah).\"" He said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," are they the same?\"" He said: \""No. Freeing a soul is when you do it alone"," and ransoming a slave is when you assist in its price. And the gift is a milking animal"," and maintaining ties of kinship with an oppressive relative.\"" He said: \""Who has the capacity for that?\"" He said: \""Then feed the hungry and give drink to the thirsty.\"" He said: \""What if I am unable to do that?\"" He said: \""Enjoin what is good and forbid what is evil.\"" He said: \""Who has the capacity for that?\"" He said: \""Then restrain your tongue except for good.\"" This is the wording of the hadith of Abū Dāwūd. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"21320","(21314) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf al-Aṣbahānī informed us that Abū Muḥammad al-Ḥasan ibn ʿImrān al-Qāḍī al-Harawī narrated to us that Abū Ḥātim ʿAbd al-Jalīl ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān narrated to us that ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Mūsā narrated to us that Hishām ibn ʿUrwah narrated from his father from Abū Murāwigh al-Ghifārī from Abū Dharr, who said: I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: \Which deed is best?\"" He said: \""Faith in Allah and striving in His cause.\"" I said: \""Which slaves are best?\"" He said: \""Those most expensive in price and most precious to their families.\"" He said: I said: \""What if I cannot do that?\"" He said: \""Then help a craftsman or make something for one who is helpless.\"" He said: I said: \""What if I cannot do that?\"" He said: \""Then leave people from harm"," for it is a charity that you give upon yourself.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Mūsā. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muttafaq ʿalayh]"""
"21321","(21315) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, that Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣaghānī narrated to us, that Abū Nuʿaym narrated to us, that Sufyān narrated from Abū Isḥāq, from Abū Ḥabīb al-Ṭāʾī, who said: I met Abū al-Dardāʾ and said, \A brother of mine died and bequeathed to me a portion of his wealth. In what should I place it — among the poor"," the mujāhidīn"," or for the freeing of necks?\"" He said: \""By Allah"," if I were in such a position"," I would not consider anyone equal to the mujāhidīn"," for the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: 'The likeness of the one who frees a slave at the point of death is like the one of gives a gift after he has already eaten his fill.'\"" [Weak]"""
"21322","(21316) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us that Muḥammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, that Abū Dāwūd narrated to us, that Abū al-Walīd al-Ṭayālisī narrated to us, that Hammām narrated.\n\n(Ḥ) And Muḥammad ibn Kathīr al-Maʿnī narrated to us that Hammām narrated from Qatādah, from Abū al-Malīḥ — and Abū al-Walīd said from his father — that a man freed his share of a slave. He mentioned this to the Prophet (ﷺ), who said: \Allah has no partner.\""\n\nIbn Kathīr added in his version: \""And the Prophet (ﷺ) validated his act of emancipation.\""\n\nThe Shaykh (may Allah have mercy on him) said: It is possible that this refers to a man who freed his share of a slave jointly owned between him and another"," and it is also possible that it refers to something else. [Authentic]"""
"21323","(21317) Abū Jaʿfar Kāmil ibn Aḥmad al-Mustamlī informed us that Bishr ibn Aḥmad al-Isfarāʾīnī narrated to us, that Dāwūd ibn al-Ḥusayn al-Bayhaqī narrated to us, that Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā informed us that ʿAbbād ibn al-ʿAwwām narrated from Saʿīd, from Qatādah, from Abū al-Malīḥ, that a man from his people freed one-third of his slave. This was raised to the Prophet (ﷺ), who said: \He is entirely free. Allah has no partner.\""\n\nThis is more apparent in terms of what we have placed this chapter upon"," and Allah knows best. [Authentic; previously cited]"""
"21324","(21318) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us that Abū Bakr al-Qaṭṭān narrated to us, that Aḥmad ibn Yūsuf al-Sulamī narrated to us, that Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf said: Sufyān mentioned from Khālid ibn Salamah al-Makhzūmī, who said: A man came to ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) at ʿArafah and said, \I have freed my share of this slave.\"" He said: \""Free him entirely. Allah has no partner.\""\n\nThus I found it in my book"," and in the Jāmiʿ it is the narration of ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Walīd al-ʿAdanī from Sufyān"," who said: ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: \""He is entirely free. There is no compulsion in it.\"" [Weak]"""
"21325","(21319) As for the hadith that Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, that Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Bālawayh narrated to us from the original of his book, that ʿAbd Allāh ibn Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal narrated to me, that my father narrated to me, that ʿAbd al-Razzāq narrated to us, that ʿUmar ibn Ḥawshab narrated to me, that Ismāʿīl ibn Umayyah narrated from his father, from his grandfather, who said: They had a slave called Ṭahmān or Dhakwān. His grandfather freed half of him. The slave came to the Prophet (ﷺ) and informed him. The Prophet (ﷺ) said: \Whatever portion of him has been freed is free"," and whatever remains remains in bondage.\"" So he continued to serve his master until he (the remaining share) was freed.\n\nThis is narrated uniquely by ʿUmar ibn Ḥawshab"," and Ismāʿīl is Ibn Umayyah ibn ʿAmr ibn Saʿīd ibn al-ʿĀṣ. And ʿAmr ibn Saʿīd did not have companionship (ṣuḥbah). [Weak]"""
"21326","(21320) As for the hadith that Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, that Abū al-Walīd narrated to us, that al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān narrated to us, that ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Salām narrated to us, that Khalīfah ibn Khayyāṭ narrated to us, that ʿAbd al-Wāḥid ibn Wāṣil narrated to us, that Muḥammad ibn Faḍāʾ narrated from his father, from ʿAlqamah ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Muzanī, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \A man may free from his slave as much as he wishes — if he wishes"," a third; if he wishes"," a quarter; if he wishes"," a fifth. There is no compulsion between him and Allah.\"" And he said in another place: \""no injustice.\""\n\nThe Ustādh Abū al-Walīd said: Our companions said: This refers to the one who frees a third of this one and a quarter of that one"," and if one dies or bequeaths half the emancipation of this one and half the emancipation of that one"," neither invalidates the other"," and from each one the portion that was freed is freed.\n\nThe Shaykh (may Allah have mercy on him) said: This is a good interpretation. However"," Muḥammad ibn Faḍāʾ is weak and cannot be used as a proof. Yaḥyā ibn Maʿīn"," Sulaymān ibn Ḥarb"," and Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Nasāʾī (may Allah have mercy on them) all spoke critically of him. [Weak]"""
"21327","(21321) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū al-Walīd narrated to us, that al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān narrated to us, that Ḥabbān narrated from Ibn al-Mubārak, from Sufyān, from al-Ashʿath, from al-Ḥakam, from ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: \If a man has a slave and frees half of him"," only that which he freed is freed from him.\"" This is munqaṭiʿ (disconnected). [Weak]"""
"21328","(21322) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ, Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzakkī, and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us that al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us that al-Shāfiʿī informed us that Mālik informed us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlāʾ ibn Muḥammad ibn Abī Saʿīd al-Isfarāʾīnī narrated to us from there, that Abū Sahl Bishr ibn Aḥmad narrated to us, that Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAlī al-Dhuhlī narrated to us, that Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us. I said to Mālik ibn Anas: Nāfiʿ narrated to you from Ibn ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Whoever frees his share in a slave and he has wealth sufficient to cover the price of the slave"," a fair valuation shall be placed upon him"," his partners shall be given their shares"," and the slave shall be emancipated upon him. Otherwise"," only that which he freed is freed from him.\"" He said: Yes.\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf"," and Muslim narrated it from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā"," both from Mālik.\n\n[Authentic; agreed upon]"""
"21329","(21323) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us that al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān narrated to us that Shuʿayb ibn al-Layth narrated to us that al-Layth ibn Saʿd narrated from Nāfiʿ, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say: \Any slave who is jointly owned by partners"," and one of them frees his share"," a fair valuation shall be assessed upon the wealth of the one who freed him"," and he shall be emancipated if his wealth suffices for that.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Qutaybah and others from al-Layth"," and al-Bukhārī cited it as corroborating evidence"," saying: \""And al-Layth narrated it.\""\n\n[Authentic; Muslim 1501]"""
"21330","(21324) Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn Dāwūd al-ʿAlawī informed us that ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn al-Sharqī narrated to us that ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Bishr ibn al-Ḥakam narrated to us that ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us that Ibn Jurayj informed me that Ismāʿīl ibn Umayyah narrated from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him), that he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Whoever frees his share in a slave"," a valuation shall be assessed upon the wealth of the one who freed him"," its price shall be paid to his partners"," and he shall be emancipated from the wealth of the one who freed him.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn Rāfiʿ from ʿAbd al-Razzāq"," and al-Bukhārī said: \""And Ismāʿīl ibn Umayyah narrated it.\""\n\n[Authentic; agreed upon]"""
"21331","(21325) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Ismāʿīl ibn Aḥmad al-Jurjānī narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Qutaybah narrated to us: Ḥarmalah ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us: Ibn Wahb informed us: Usāmah ibn Zayd informed us, from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with them both), that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Whoever frees his share in a slave"," a fair valuation shall be placed upon him. His co-owners shall be given their respective shares"," and the slave shall be freed upon him.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Hārūn ibn Saʿīd"," from Ibn Wahb. [Ṣaḥīḥ — agreed upon]"""
"21332","(21326) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū Aḥmad — meaning al-Ḥāfiẓ — informed me: Abū al-Ḥusayn Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Ghāzī narrated to us: Abū al-Ashʿath narrated to us: al-Fuḍayl ibn Sulaymān narrated to us: Mūsā ibn ʿUqbah informed us: Nāfiʿ informed me, from Ibn ʿUmar, who used to issue fatwā regarding a slave or a slave-girl who was jointly owned and one of his co-owners freed his share. He would say: \The emancipation of the entire slave has become obligatory upon him"," provided he has sufficient wealth by which the slave may be valued at a fair price. The co-owners shall be given their respective shares"," and the emancipated slave shall be set free.\"" Ibn ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with them both) attributed this to the Prophet (ﷺ).\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Abī al-Ashʿath. [Ṣaḥīḥ — agreed upon]"""
"21333","(21327) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us: Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-Qaṭṭān narrated to us: Ibrāhīm ibn al-Ḥārith al-Baghdādī narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Abī Bukayr narrated to us: Ibn Abī Dhiʾb narrated to us, from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar, from the Prophet (ﷺ), who said: \Whoever frees his share of a possessed slave"," and the one who freed him possesses the means to cover its price"," he shall be liable for the share of his partner.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī said: Ibn Abī Dhiʾb narrated it"," and Muslim narrated it through another chain from Ibn Abī Dhiʾb. [Ṣaḥīḥ — agreed upon]"""
"21334","(21328) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, among the last narrations, they said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us: al-Shāfiʿī informed us: Sufyān narrated to us, from ʿAmr ibn Dīnār, from Sālim ibn ʿAbd Allāh, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Any slave who is owned by two persons and one of them frees his share — if he is affluent"," he shall be valued at the highest price or at a fair valuation"," without depreciation or excess — then he shall pay to the other his share.\""\n\nThus al-Shāfiʿī narrated it in the book *Ikhtilāf al-Aḥādīth*. And he narrated it in the book *al-Qurʿah*"," saying: \""At the highest price"," and he shall be freed.\"" And sometimes he said: \""A valuation in which there is neither depreciation nor excess.\""\n\nAl-Ḥumaydī narrated it from Sufyān"," similar to the first narration from al-Shāfiʿī"," adding: \""then he shall be freed.\"" And he added: Sufyān said: \""ʿAmr used to have doubt in it"," thus.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ — agreed upon]"""
"21335","(21329) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me: ʿAlī ibn Sakhṭawayh narrated to us: Bishr ibn Mūsā narrated to us: al-Ḥumaydī narrated to us: Sufyān narrated to us: ʿAmr ibn Dīnār narrated, and he mentioned it.\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd Allāh, from Sufyān, without these two phrases. [Ṣaḥīḥ — agreed upon]"
"21336","(21330) Abū ʿAmr al-Adīb informed us: Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī narrated to us: Hārūn ibn Yūsuf narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā ibn Abī ʿUmar narrated to us: Sufyān narrated to us, from ʿAmr, from Sālim, from his father, that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \Whoever frees a slave jointly owned between himself and another"," a fair valuation shall be placed upon him from his wealth — without depreciation nor excess — and he shall be freed from his wealth"," if he is affluent.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Ibn Abī ʿUmar. [Ṣaḥīḥ — agreed upon]"""
"21337","(21331) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us: Muḥammad ibn Bakr narrated to us: Abū Dāwūd narrated to us: al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us: Maʿmar informed us, from al-Zuhrī, from Sālim, from Ibn ʿUmar, that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \Whoever frees his share in a slave"," the remainder shall be freed from his wealth"," provided he has wealth sufficient to cover the price of the slave.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbd ibn Ḥumayd"," from ʿAbd al-Razzāq. [Ṣaḥīḥ — agreed upon]"""
"21338","(21332) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbd Allāh narrated to us: Yazīd ibn Hārūn informed us: Shuʿbah informed us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Bakr ibn Fūrak informed us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us: Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb narrated to us: Abū Dāwūd al-Ṭayālisī narrated to us: Shuʿbah narrated to us, from Qatādah, from al-Naḍr ibn Anas, from Bashīr ibn Nahīk, from Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \When a man frees his portion of a possessed slave"," he is free.\"" This is the wording of al-Ṭayālisī's ḥadīth.\n\nAnd in the narration of Yazīd"," from the Prophet (ﷺ): \""Regarding a slave owned by two men"," one of whom frees his share","\"" he said: \""He shall be liable.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from the ḥadīth of Ghundar"," from Shuʿbah"," thus in the manner of Yazīd's narration"," and from the ḥadīth of Muʿādh ibn Muʿādh"," in the manner of al-Ṭayālisī's narration"," adding: \""He is free from his wealth.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ — Muslim 1502]"""
"21339","(21333) Abū Aḥmad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Mihrajānī informed us: Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥasan — meaning al-Dārajirdī — narrated to us: Azhar ibn al-Qāsim narrated to us: Hishām al-Dastuwāʾī narrated to us, from Qatādah, from Bashīr ibn Nahīk, from Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Whoever frees his share in a possessed slave"," he shall be freed from his wealth"," if he has wealth.\"" Some of the narrators from Hishām did not mention al-Naḍr ibn Anas in his chain"," while some of them did mention him.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ — as previously cited]"""
"21340","(21334) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed it to us: Abū ʿAlī al-Ḥusayn ibn ʿAlī al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: Ibrāhīm ibn Abī Ṭālib narrated to us: Abū Qudāmah narrated to us: Muʿādh ibn Hishām narrated to us: My father narrated to me, from Qatādah, from al-Naḍr ibn Anas, from Bashīr ibn Nahīk, from Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Whoever frees a portion of a possessed slave"," his emancipation is incumbent upon him from his wealth"," if he has wealth — for Allah has no partner.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ — as previously cited]"""
"21341","(21335) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us that Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us that Tamtām narrated to us that Abū Salamah narrated to us that Hammām narrated to us that Qatādah narrated from al-Naḍr ibn Anas from Bashīr ibn Nahīk from Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) that a man freed his share in a slave boy, so the Prophet (peace be upon him) validated his emancipation and required him to pay the remainder of the price. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Preceded it.]"
"21342","(21336) Abū Saʿd al-Mālinī informed us that Abū Aḥmad ibn ʿAdī al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān narrated to us that Ṣafwān ibn Ṣāliḥ narrated to us that al-Walīd ibn Muslim narrated to us that Abū Muʿayd narrated from Sulaymān ibn Mūsā from Nāʿif from Ibn ʿUmar and from ʿAṭāʾ from Jābir that the Prophet (peace be upon him) —\n\nAbū Aḥmad said: and Ṣāliḥ ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Hāshimī narrated to us that Maḥmūd ibn Khālid narrated to us that al-Walīd ibn Muslim narrated, and Abū Muʿayd narrated, and Sulaymān narrated from Nāʿif from Ibn ʿUmar and from ʿAṭāʾ from Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: \Whoever frees a share he has in a slave"," and he has in him a portion"," and he has the means to pay"," then he is free"," and he guarantees the share of his partners at a fair value for what he has wronged them in their partnership"," and there is nothing upon the slave.\""\n\nAbū Aḥmad said: His statement \""and there is nothing upon the slave\"" is not narrated by anyone other than Abū Muʿayd"," who is Ḥafṣ ibn Ghaylān"," from Sulaymān ibn Mūsā. [Ḥasan]"""
"21343","(21337) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū al-Walīd al-Faqīh narrated to us that al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān narrated to us that Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah narrated to us that Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah narrated from Ibn Abī Laylā from Ismāʿīl from Abī Mijlaz that a slave belonged to two men, and one of them freed his share, so the Prophet (peace be upon him) detained him until he sold a sheep he had.\n\nThis is munqaṭiʿ (disrupted). And al-Thawrī narrated it from Ibn Abī Laylā from al-Qāsim ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān from Abī Mijlaz with its meaning. And it was narrated from another route from al-Qāsim from his father from his grandfather ʿAbd Allāh ibn Masʿūd, and it is ḍaʿīf (weak). [Ḍaʿīf]"
"21344","(21338) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū al-Walīd narrated to us that al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān narrated to us that Abū Bakr narrated to us that Azhar al-Sammān narrated from Ibn ʿAwn from Muḥammad who said: A slave belonged to two men, and one of them freed his share, so his partner rode to ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him), and he wrote that he should be valued at the highest price. [Ḍaʿīf]"
"21345","(21339) And with his chain of narration, Abū Bakr narrated to us that Yaḥyā ibn Ādam narrated from Mughīrah from Ibrāhīm and al-Shaʿbī regarding a slave who belongs to two men and one of them frees his share: they said: He guarantees his price to his partner at a fair value on the day he freed him. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"21346","(21340) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq informed us that Mūsā ibn al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAbbād narrated to us that ʿĀrim ibn al-Faḍl narrated to us that Ḥammād ibn Zayd narrated from Ayyūb from Nāʿif from Ibn ʿUmar from the Prophet (peace be upon him) who said: \Whoever frees his share in a slave or a portion of a slave"," and he has wealth sufficient to cover the remainder of the slave's price"," then he has been emancipated.\""\n\nNāʿif said: \""Otherwise"," then what he freed has been emancipated from him.\"" Ayyūb said: \""I do not know whether Nāʿif said this on his own or it is in the hadith.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Agreed upon (muttafaq ʿalayh).]"""
"21347","(21341) And Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Muqriʾ informed us that al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us that Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us that Abū al-Rabīʿ narrated to us that Ḥammād ibn Zayd narrated to us that Ayyūb narrated it with its chain and its meaning and said: \So he is free (ʿatīq).\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿĀrim"," and Muslim narrated it from Abū al-Rabīʿ. And al-Bukhārī said in his narration: \""So he is free (ʿatīq).\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Preceded it.]"""
"21348","(21342) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq informed us that Abū al-Muthannā narrated to us that Musaddad narrated to us that Bishr ibn al-Mufaḍḍal narrated to us that ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿUmar narrated from Nāʿif from Ibn ʿUmar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: \Whoever frees a share he has in a slave"," then all of him has been emancipated.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Musaddad. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"21349","(21343) And others narrated it from Bishr: \Whoever frees a share in a slave"," then all of him has been emancipated"," if the one who freed his share has wealth sufficient to cover his price; he values him at a fair value and pays his partners their shares and sets him free.\""\n\nAbū ʿAmr al-Adīb informed us that Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī informed us that Yaḥyā ibn Muḥammad al-Ḥinnāʾī narrated to us that ʿUbayd Allāh"," who is Ibn Muʿādh"," narrated to us that Bishr narrated it with its chain.\n\nAnd with its meaning"," Yaḥyā al-Qaṭṭān narrated from ʿUbayd Allāh. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Preceded it.]"""
"21350","(21344) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us that Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb al-Shaybānī narrated to us by dictation that Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Saʿdī informed us that Yazīd ibn Hārūn informed us that Ibn Abī Dhiʾb narrated from Nāʿif from Ibn ʿUmar that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: \Whoever frees a share he has in a slave"," and the one who emancipates his share has the means to cover his price"," then all of him has been emancipated.\""\n\nThey both (al-Bukhārī and Muslim) recorded it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Preceded it.]"""
"21351","(21345) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Salmān al-Faqīh narrated to us; al-Ḥasan ibn Mukram narrated to us; Yazīd ibn Hārūn narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd informed us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Aḥmad al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me — and the wording is his — ʿAbd Allāh ibn Sulaymān ibn al-Ashʿath informed us; ʿAmr ibn ʿAlī narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Wahhāb al-Thaqafī narrated to us; he said: I heard Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd say: I heard Nāfiʿ narrating from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say: \Whoever frees his share in a slave"," he is obligated to free what remains"," and he shall set him free.\"" Nāfiʿ used to say: Yaḥyā said"," \""I do not know whether this was something he said on his own or whether it is part of the hadith. If he did not have the means"," then what he has done is sufficient.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn al-Muthannā from ʿAbd al-Wahhāb. [Ṣaḥīḥ — agreed upon]"""
"21352","(21346) Abū Naṣr ibn Qatādah informed us; Abū al-Faḍl ibn Khamīruwayh informed us; Aḥmad ibn Najdah narrated to us; Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr narrated to us; Hushaym narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd informed us from Ibn ʿUmar that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Any man who has a share in a slave and frees his share"," it is incumbent upon him to complete his emancipation at a fair valuation.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ — agreed upon]"""
"21353","(21347) ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us; Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us; ʿUthmān ibn ʿUmar al-Dabbī narrated to us; Musaddad narrated to us; Juwayriyah ibn Asmāʾ narrated to us; from Nāfiʿ from Ibn ʿUmar that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \Whoever frees a share in a slave"," it becomes obligatory upon him to free what remains"," if he has sufficient wealth to cover its price. A fair valuation shall be assigned"," his partners shall be given their shares"," and the emancipated one shall be set free.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Musaddad. [Ṣaḥīḥ — agreed upon]"""
"21354","(21348) Abū al-Qāsim ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿUbayd Allāh al-Ḥurfī in Baghdād informed us; Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Shāfiʿī narrated to us; Bishr ibn Mūsā narrated to us; Khallād ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us; Hishām ibn Saʿd narrated to us; Nāfiʿ narrated to me from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Whoever frees a share in a slave"," it is incumbent upon him to free what remains.\""\n\nIn the other narrations we have cited"," there is evidence supporting this view"," and in them there is also evidence supporting the first view. It appears that they did not give consideration to this; rather"," they were concerned with the occurrence of emancipation in general"," without the obligation of compensation if the person is solvent. And Allah knows best.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ — agreed upon]"""
"21355","(21349) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ, Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī, and Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī informed us; they said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; Abū Umayyah narrated to us; Abū al-Jumāhir narrated to us; Ismāʿīl narrated to us; from Layṭ from Ṭāwūs from Ibn ʿAbbās from the Prophet (ﷺ), who said: \Whoever frees a share in a slave belonging to him"," he guarantees his emancipation. The slave shall be valued and then set free.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"21356","(21350) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-Walīd informed us; al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān narrated to us; Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah narrated to us; Abū Muʿāwiyah narrated to us; from al-Aʿmash from Ibrāhīm from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Yazīd, who said: Between myself, al-Aswad, and our mother there was a shared slave who had witnessed the Battle of al-Qādisiyyah and distinguished himself therein. They intended to emancipate him, but I was young at the time. Al-Aswad mentioned this to ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him), and ʿUmar said: \You all emancipate him"," and ʿAbd al-Raḥmān shall retain his share until he desires the same as you have desired"," or he may take his share.\""\n\nIt may be that by \""his share\"" he meant his share of the valuation. We have narrated from ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) what indicates this.\n\nA mursal hadith has been narrated with a similar meaning. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"21357","(21351) Abū Naṣr ibn Qatādah informed us; Abū al-Faḍl ibn Khamīruwayh informed us; Aḥmad ibn Najdah narrated to us; Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr narrated to us; Sufyān narrated to us; from ʿAmr ibn Dīnār from Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr ibn Saʿīd: that the Banū Saʿīd ibn al-ʿĀṣ had a slave, and all of them emancipated him except one man. The slave went to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) seeking his intercession with the man. The man then gifted his share to the Prophet (ﷺ), and he emancipated him. The slave used to say: \I am the freedman of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ).\"" The man was known as Rāfiʿ"," Abū al-Bahī.\n\nThis indicates"," if it is authentic"," that he did not emancipate by explicit declaration. It is also possible that they were insolvent. The hadith is munqaṭiʿ (disconnected).\n\nWe have narrated from Ismāʿīl ibn Umayyah from ʿAmr ibn Saʿīd ibn al-ʿĀṣ from his father from his grandfather another account of this story that contradicts this version. The ruling has already been discussed in the preceding section. And Allah knows best. [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"21358","(21352) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ, Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī, and Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Mazzī informed us; they said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥakam informed us; Ibn Wahb informed us; Mālik ibn Anas informed me.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Jaʿfar Kāmil ibn Aḥmad al-Mustamlī informed us; Abū Sahl Bishr ibn Aḥmad al-Isfarāyīnī narrated to us; Dāwūd ibn al-Ḥusayn al-Bayhaqī narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us; he said: I said to Mālik: Did Nāfiʿ narrate to you from Ibn ʿUmar that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Whoever frees a share he has in a slave"," and he has wealth sufficient to cover the price of the slave"," a fair valuation shall be assigned to him"," his partners shall be given their shares"," and the slave shall be emancipated upon him; otherwise"," only what he has freed shall be freed of him\""? He said: Yes.\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf from Mālik"," and Muslim narrated it from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ — agreed upon]"""
"21359","(21353) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; al-Rabīʿ narrated to us; he said: al-Shāfiʿī said to one of those who debated with him — or he said, \Is there any room for debate?\"" — given the established Sunnah of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) regarding the abandonment of istisʿāʾ (compelling the slave to earn his freedom) in the hadith of Nāfiʿ and ʿImrān? He said: We say that Ayyūb said — and sometimes Nāfiʿ said — \""only what he has freed shall be freed of him","\"" and sometimes he did not say it. He said: \""And my strongest assumption is that it was something Nāfiʿ said based on his own opinion.\"" Al-Shāfiʿī (may Allah have mercy on him) said: I said to him"," \""I do not think any scholar of hadith and its narrators would doubt that Mālik is more precise in his narration of Nāfiʿ's hadith than Ayyūb"," because he was more devoted to him than Ayyūb. And Mālik has a superior faculty of preservation regarding the hadiths of his companions in particular. Even if they were equal in preservation"," and one of them expressed doubt about something about which his companion did not express doubt"," there would be no room in this case for the one who did not doubt to be mistaken. Rather"," a man is only contradicted by one who is more precise than him"," or he brings something in the hadith in which he is joined by one who did not preserve what he preserved — they are many"," while he is alone.\"" Others agreed with Mālik in adding \""otherwise"," only what he has freed shall be freed of him","\"" meaning someone else. And some of them added: \""and he shall remain enslaved in what remains enslaved.\""\n\nThe Shaykh (may Allah have mercy on him) said: As for the hadith of Ayyūb"," we have already mentioned it in what has preceded. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"21360","(21354) Abū ʿAmr al-Adīb informed us; Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī informed us; Abū Yaʿlā narrated to us; Abū al-Rabīʿ narrated to us; Ḥammād narrated to us; Ayyūb narrated to us; from Nāfiʿ from Ibn ʿUmar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Whoever frees a share or a portion he has in a slave"," and he has wealth sufficient to cover its price at a fair valuation"," then he is fully emancipated.\"" He (the narrator) said: \""I do not know whether this is from the hadith of the Prophet (ﷺ) or something Nāfiʿ said. Otherwise"," only what he has freed shall be freed of him.\""\n\nBoth al-Bukhārī and Muslim narrated it in their Ṣaḥīḥ in this manner"," and in it there is clear evidence that he (Ayyūb) was doubtful about it. And Mālik ibn Anas (may Allah have mercy on him) affirmed it as being from the hadith of the Prophet (ﷺ)"," so the ruling is his"," not the other's. As for the superiority of Mālik's preservation"," it is recognized among the scholars of hadith"," as al-Shāfiʿī (may Allah have mercy on him) stated.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ — agreed upon]"""
"21361","(21355) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq informed us that Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq informed us that ʿAlī ibn al-Madīnī said: ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Mahdī used not to place anyone above Mālik. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"21362","(21356) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, saying: I heard Abū al-Ḥasan al-ʿAnazī say: I heard ʿUthmān ibn Saʿīd al-Dārimī say: I said to Yaḥyā ibn Maʿīn, \Who is more beloved to you regarding the ḥadīth of Nāfiʿ — Mālik or ʿUbaydullāh ibn ʿUmar?\"" He said: \""Mālik.\"" I said: \""And Ayyūb al-Sakhtiyānī?\"" He said: \""Mālik.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"21363","(21357) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū Muḥammad ibn Ukht Abī ʿAwānah informed us, my paternal uncle narrated to me, who said: al-Maymūnī informed us, saying: I heard Yaḥyā ibn Maʿīn and Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal both say: \Mālik was among the most precise of people in his ḥadīth.\"" Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal said: \""O Abū al-Ḥasan"," do not concern yourself with asking about any man from whom Mālik narrated"," especially if he is a Medinan.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"21364","(21358) Abū ʿAbdillāh informed us, saying: I heard Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad al-Ḥīrī say: I heard al-Ḥusayn ibn Muḥammad al-Qabbānī say: I heard ʿUbaydullāh ibn ʿUmar al-Qawārīrī say: I heard Ḥammād ibn Zayd say: I heard Ayyūb al-Sakhtiyānī say: \Mālik indeed had a ḥalaqah during the lifetime of Nāfiʿ.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"21365","(21359) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān informed us in Baghdad, saying: ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar informed us that Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān informed us that Muḥammad ibn Abī Rukayn informed us that Ibn Wahb informed us that Mālik narrated to me, saying: Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd said to me: \Write for me one hundred aḥādīth from the ḥadīth of Ibn Shihāb"," selected for me"," and I shall give you an old"," yellowed chest.\"" Mālik said: \""So I wrote those aḥādīth for him until I filled it and clarified it for him.\"" Mālik said: \""And rarely was there a man from whom I used to learn who died before he would come to me and seek a fatwā from me.\""\n\nAs for the agreement of those who agreed with Mālik on this additional wording"," it is in what follows. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"21366","(21360) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us that Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-Qaṭṭān informed us that Muḥammad ibn Yazīd al-Sulamī informed us that Muḥammad ibn ʿUbayd informed us that ʿUbaydullāh ibn ʿUmar narrated from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar — may Allah be pleased with both of them — who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Whoever frees his share in a slave"," it is incumbent upon him to free him entirely"," if he has wealth sufficient to cover his price. And if he does not have wealth"," then he has freed of him only what he freed.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muttafaq ʿalayh]"""
"21367","(21361) Abū ʿAmr Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Adīb informed us that Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī informed us that Abū al-Qāsim al-Manīʿī informed us that Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah informed us that Abū Usāmah and Ibn Numayr narrated —\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Bakr said: ʿImrān ibn Mūsā informed us that ʿUthmān informed us that Abū Usāmah and Ibn Numayr narrated —\n\n(Ḥ) And al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān informed us that Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn Numayr informed us that my father narrated — both saying: ʿUbaydullāh narrated from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar — may Allah be pleased with both of them — who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Whoever frees his share in a slave"," it is incumbent upon him to free him entirely"," if he has wealth sufficient to cover his price. And if he does not have wealth"," then he has freed of him only what he freed.\""\n\nThis is the wording of Ibn Numayr. And in the ḥadīth of Abū Bakr and ʿUthmān: \""It is incumbent upon him to free him entirely"," if he has wealth sufficient to cover his price. And if he does not have wealth"," he shall be appraised a fair price\"" — meaning"," on the one who freed"," he freed of him only what he freed.\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿUbayd ibn Ismāʿīl from Abū Usāmah"," and Muslim narrated it from Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn Numayr. Likewise"," Khālid ibn al-Ḥārith narrated it from ʿUbaydullāh with the meaning of Ibn Numayr. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Preceded before it]"""
"21368","(21362) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that ʿAbdullāh ibn Muḥammad al-Kaʿbī informed us that Muḥammad ibn Ayyūb informed us that Shaybān ibn Farrūkh informed us that Jarīr ibn Ḥāzim informed us that Nāfiʿ, the mawlā of ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar, narrated from Ibn ʿUmar — may Allah be pleased with both of them — who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Whoever frees his portion in a slave"," and he has wealth to the extent of its value"," a fair price shall be appraised upon him; otherwise"," he has freed of him only what he freed.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Shaybān. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muttafaq ʿalayh]"""
"21369","(21363) Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥārith al-Aṣbahānī al-Faqīh informed us that ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū Bakr al-Naysābūrī informed us that Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥakam informed us that Ismāʿīl ibn Marzūq al-Kaʿbī informed us that Yaḥyā ibn Ayyūb narrated from ʿUbaydullāh ibn ʿUmar, Ismāʿīl ibn Umayyah, and Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd, from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar — may Allah be pleased with both of them — that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Whoever frees his share in a slave"," a fair price shall be appraised upon him"," and his partners shall be given their shares"," and the slave shall be freed upon him"," if he is affluent. Otherwise"," he has freed of him only what he freed"," and the remainder remains enslaved.\""\n\nAs for the ḥadīth of ʿImrān ibn Ḥuṣayn regarding the invalidation of seeking the slave's labour (al-istisʿāʾ): [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muttafaq ʿalayh]"""
"21370","(21364) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that ʿAbdullāh ibn Muḥammad al-Kaʿbī informed us that Ismāʿīl ibn Qutaybah informed us that Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah informed us that Ismāʿīl — meaning Ibn ʿUlayyah — narrated from Ayyūb, from Abū Qilābah, from Abū al-Muhallab, from ʿImrān ibn Ḥuṣayn, that a man freed six slaves upon his death, and he had no wealth other than them. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ called them and divided them into thirds, then drew lots among them. He freed two and kept four as slaves, and he spoke to him a severe word.\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 1668]"
"21371","(21365) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us that Abu al-Walid al-Faqih informed us that al-Hasan ibn Sufyan narrated to us that Habban narrated from Ibn al-Mubarak from Ibn Lahī'a from Yazīd ibn Qusayt from Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Thawbān: that a man asked Ibn 'Umar about a slave whose half had been set free. He said: The rulings pertaining to slaves shall apply to him until he is entirely freed. [Da'īf]"
"21372","(21366) Abu 'Abd Allah informed us that Abu al-Walid narrated to us that al-Hasan ibn Sufyan narrated to us that Habban narrated from Ibn al-Mubarak from Ma'mar from Ibn Tāwūs from his father, regarding a man who died while half of him was free: He said: It is between them as two halves — half for the one who freed him and half for the one who did not free him. And from Ibn al-Mubarak from Ma'mar from Jābir from al-Sha'bī, regarding a slave who belonged to two men, one of whom contracted a mukātab agreement with him and the other freed him, then the mukātab died before he could pay: He said: His wealth is divided into two halves — half for the one who freed him and half for the one who contracted the mukātab, he placed it between them."
"21373","(21367) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us that Abu al-Walid al-Faqih narrated to us that al-Hasan ibn Sufyan narrated to us that Habban narrated from Ibn al-Mubarak from Ma'mar from al-Zuhrī, and from a man from al-Hasan, regarding a man who said to his slave woman: \You are free"," except what is in your womb.\"" They both said: She and what is in her womb are free"," and his exception is not valid. And Ma'mar said: The one who asked al-Hakam narrated to me"," and he said the same. [Sahīh"," exclusively for al-Dhahabī]"""
"21374","(21368) Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn 'Alī informed us that Ibrāhīm ibn 'Abd Allah al-Aṣbahānī informed us that Ismā'īl ibn Ibrāhīm al-Qaṭṭān narrated to us that al-Hasan ibn 'Īsá narrated to us that Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us that Ibn Jurayj said: I said to 'Aṭā': A free man married a slave woman of mine and she conceived from him, and I freed her child in her womb — to whom does its walā' belong? He said: To the one who freed it, but its inheritance is to its father. (Q) And that is because the nasab takes precedence over the mawlā in matters of inheritance. [Sahīh]"
"21375","(21369) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz and Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Ishāq al-Muzakkī and Abū Bakr Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Adīb said: Muhammad ibn Ya'qūb al-Hafiz narrated to us that Ibrāhīm ibn 'Abd Allah narrated to us that Yazīd ibn Hārūn narrated to us that Sa'īd ibn Abī 'Arūbah narrated from Qatādah from al-Naḍr ibn Anas from Bashīr ibn Nahīk from Abū Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, who said: Whoever has a partner in a slave and frees him, then it is incumbent upon him to secure his full liberation from his wealth, if he possesses wealth. And if he does not possess wealth, the slave shall be required to labor for the price of his neck, without being subjected to hardship. Al-Bukhārī and Muslim narrated it in the Sahīh from various chains from Sa'īd ibn Abī 'Arūbah. [Sahīh, agreed upon (muttafaq 'alayh)]"
"21376","(21370) And Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us that Abū 'Alī al-Husayn ibn 'Alī al-Hafiz narrated to us that Ibrāhīm ibn Abī Tālib and 'Abd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Azdī both narrated to us that Ishāq ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us that 'Īsá ibn Yūnus narrated from Sa'īd, who mentioned it with his chain: that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: Whoever frees a share in a slave, it is incumbent upon him to secure his full liberation from his wealth, if he possesses wealth. And if he does not possess wealth, the slave shall be appraised at a just value, and then required to labor for the share of his companion who did not free him, without being subjected to hardship. Muslim narrated it in the Sahīh from Ishāq and others. [Sahīh, agreed upon (muttafaq 'alayh)]"
"21377","(21371) Abū Tāhir al-Faqih informed us that Abū Bakr Muhammad ibn al-Husayn al-Qaṭṭān narrated to us that Ibrāhīm ibn al-Hārith al-Baghdādī narrated to us that Yahyá ibn Abī Bukayr narrated to us that Jarīr ibn Hāzim narrated to us, and he said: I heard Qatādah saying: al-Naḍr ibn Anas narrated to me from Bashīr ibn Nahīk, who said: I heard Abū Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, saying: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, was asked about a slave who belongs to two men, one of whom frees his share. He said: The slave has been freed; he shall be appraised at a just value in his owner's wealth. If he does not possess wealth, the slave shall be required to labor, without being subjected to hardship. [Sahīh]"
"21378","(21372) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz narrated to us that Abu 'Abd Allah Muhammad ibn Ya'qūb al-Hafiz, through dictation, narrated to us that 'Alī ibn al-Hasan ibn Abī 'Īsá narrated to us that Abū al-Nu'mān Muhammad ibn al-Faḍl narrated to us that Jarīr ibn Hāzim narrated to us that Qatādah narrated from al-Naḍr ibn Anas from Bashīr ibn Nahīk from Abū Hurayrah from the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, who said: Whoever frees a share he holds in a slave, and he possesses wealth sufficient to cover its value, he shall free him from his wealth. And if he does not possess wealth, the slave shall be required to labor, without being subjected to hardship. Al-Bukhārī narrated it in the Sahīh from Abū al-Nu'mān, and Muslim narrated it from another chain from Jarīr ibn Hāzim, and both reported it from Abū Hurayrah. Likewise, al-Hajjāj ibn al-Hajjāj and Abān ibn Yazīd al-'Aṭṭār and Mūsá ibn Khalaf al-'Ammī narrated from Qatādah — they mentioned the istis'ā' (requiring the slave to labor) as incorporated within the hadith. Al-Bukhārī used their narration as corroborating evidence. As for al-Shāfi'ī, may Allah have mercy on him, he weakened the matter of the si'āyah (labor requirement) in it on several grounds, among them that Shu'bah ibn al-Hajjāj and Hishām al-Dastawā'ī narrated this hadith from Qatādah without any mention of istis'ā', and they are the more precise in memorization. The Shaykh, may Allah have mercy on him, said: And we have previously presented their narration. [Sahīh, agreed upon (muttafaq 'alayh)]"
"21379","(21373) Abū Bakr ibn al-Hārith al-Faqih said: Abū al-Hasan al-Dāraquṭnī al-Hafiz said: Shu'bah and Hishām are more precise in memorization than those who narrated from Qatādah and did not mention the istisā' in it. And among the reasons is that al-Shāfi'ī heard some people of critical reflection and deep contemplation, and knowledge of hadith, saying: Were it not that the hadith of Sa'īd ibn Abī 'Arūbah regarding the istisā' is singular and unopposed by anyone else, it would not have been established. The Shaykh, may Allah have mercy on him, said: Perhaps he said that because the hadith of Bashīr ibn Nahīk from Abū Hurayrah is said to be from a written document, and it has been narrated from Bashīr that he read what was written for Abū Hurayrah, and there is nothing in it that undermines his hadith. And it is possible that he said it because Sa'īd is singular in reporting it, and the huffāz (master hadith scholars) are cautious about establishing what Sa'īd reports singularly, due to his confusion (ikhtilāt) in the latter part of his life, even though others agreed with him in narrating the istisā'. Or he said it because his chain of narration is disputed. And most of them narrated it from Qatādah from al-Naḍr ibn Anas from Bashīr ibn Nahīk from Abū Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him. And Ma'mar and Sa'īd ibn Bashīr narrated it from Qatādah from Bashīr, without any mention of al-Naḍr ibn Anas, and such is the case in one of the two narrations from Hishām. And it has been said: from Qatādah from Mūsá ibn Anas from Bashīr, and it has been said: from Bashīr from Jābir ibn 'Abd Allah — and all of that is erroneous, and the position of the majority is what we have stated. And what weakens the matter of the si'āyah in it is the narration of Hammām ibn Yahyá from Qatādah, where he attributed the istisā' to the statement of Qatādah and separated it from the words of the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him. [Sahīh]"
"21380","(21374) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us of it in the Book of Ma'rifat al-Hadīth, and he said: Abu 'Abd Allah Muhammad ibn Ya'qūb al-Hafiz narrated to us that 'Alī ibn al-Hasan al-Darābjirdī narrated to us that 'Abd Allah ibn Yazīd al-Muqri' narrated to us that Hammām narrated from Qatādah from al-Naḍr ibn Anas from Bashīr ibn Nahīk from Abū Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him: that a man freed a share he held in a slave, and the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, imposed upon him the payment of his price. Hammām said: And Qatādah used to say: If he does not possess wealth, then the slave shall be required to labor. [Sahīh; narrated one hadith before this]"
"21381","(21375) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū ʿAlī al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me, Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Ḥurayth narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yazīd al-Muqriʾ narrated to me, my father narrated to me.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Aṣbahānī informed us, ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, Abū Bakr al-Naysābūrī narrated to us, ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Abī ʿĪsā narrated to us, ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yazīd al-Muqriʾ narrated to us, Hammām narrated from Qatādah, from al-Naḍr ibn Anas, from Bashīr ibn Nahīk, from Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) that a man freed his share of a slave. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) validated his emancipation and required him to pay the remainder of the price. Qatādah said: \If he does not have wealth"," the slave shall be made to work (to earn the remainder) without being burdened (unduly).\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. It was mentioned before.]"""
"21382","(21376) Abū Bakr informed us, ʿAlī said: \I heard al-Naysābūrī say: 'How excellent is what Hammām narrated; he preserved it precisely and distinguished between the statement of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) and the statement of Qatādah.' And from what has reached me from Abū Sulaymān al-Khaṭṭābī"," from al-Ḥasan ibn Yaḥyā"," from Ibn al-Mundhir"," the author of the *Khilāfiyyāt*"," he said: 'This statement is from the legal opinion (fatwā) of Qatādah and is not part of the text of the hadith.' Then he mentioned the hadith of ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥasan from al-Muqriʾ from Hammām"," and then he said: 'Hammām has made it clear that the mention of *siʿāyah* (making the slave work) is from the statement of Qatādah"," whereas Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿArūbah"," whom Hammām distinguished from Qatādah"," joined it to the hadith as if it were part of it.'\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"21383","(21377) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū ʿAlī al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me, Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Ḥurayth narrated to us, Abū Mūsā said: \I heard ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Mahdī say: 'The hadiths of Hammām from Qatādah are more authentic than the hadiths of anyone else"," because he wrote them down from dictation.'\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"21384","(21378) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, he said: \I heard Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Kāmil al-Qāḍī say: 'I heard Abū Qilābah al-Raqāshī say: 'I heard ʿAlī ibn al-Madīnī say: 'I heard Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd say: 'Shuʿbah is the most knowledgeable of people regarding the hadith of Qatādah—what he heard from him and what he did not hear. And Hishām is the most precise in memorization"," and Saʿīd is the most prolific in narration.'\""\n\nThe Shaykh (may Allah have mercy on him) said: \""Shuʿbah combined the excellence of his memorization and his knowledge of what he heard from Qatādah and what he did not hear; Hishām combined the excellence of his memorization; and Hammām combined the soundness of his written record and his additional knowledge of what is not part of the hadith—in contrast to Ibn Abī ʿArūbah and those who agreed with him in incorporating the mention of *siʿāyah* into the hadith. And in this there is a difficulty regarding the establishment of *istisʿāʾ* (making the slave work to earn his freedom) in this hadith.\""\n\nAnd that which indicates that the mention of *istisʿāʾ* in this hadith is from the legal opinion of Qatādah. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"21385","(21379) Abū ʿAbd Allāh informed us, Isḥāq ibn Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf al-Sūsī narrated to us, Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, al-ʿAbbāb ibn al-Walīd ibn Mazīd informed us, ʿUqbah ibn ʿAlqamah informed us, he said: \al-Awzāʿī was asked about a slave jointly owned by three persons"," one of whom contracted him for manumission (*mukātabah*)"," then another freed his share"," and the third withheld his share. He said: 'It has been reported from Qatādah that he said: 'For the one who withheld his share"," his portion is incumbent upon the one who freed (his share)"," if he is of means"," in respect of his share. And if he does not have wealth"," the slave shall be made to work for one-third of his value. And the walāʾ (clientage) is between the one who freed and the one who contracted for manumission: two-thirds for the one who freed and one-third for the one who contracted.'\""\n\nAnd from this is that al-Shāfiʿī (may Allah have mercy on him) said: \""It was said to those present among the people of hadith: 'If Nāfiʿ from Ibn ʿUmar from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) alone differs"," and this isnād—which of the two is more firmly established?' They said: 'Nāfiʿ from Ibn ʿUmar from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him).'\""\n\nal-Shāfiʿī (may Allah have mercy on him) said: \""I said: 'And upon us is that we turn to the more firmly established of the two hadiths.' He said: 'Yes.'\""\n\nThe Shaykh said: \""Alongside Nāfiʿ is the hadith of ʿImrān ibn Ḥuṣayn"," which invalidates *istisʿāʾ*.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"21386","(21380) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Sulaymān said: \I heard Muḥammad ibn Ismāʿīl al-Bukhārī say: 'The most authentic of all chains of narration is Mālik from Nāfiʿ from Ibn ʿUmar.'\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"21387","(21381) And Manṣūr ibn ʿAbd al-Wahhāb al-Ṣūfī informed us, Abū ʿAmr ibn Ḥamdān said: \I heard Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Thaqafī say: 'I asked Muḥammad ibn Ismāʿīl al-Bukhārī about the most authentic chains of narration"," and he said: 'Mālik from Nāfiʿ from Ibn ʿUmar.'\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"21388","(21382) As for the hadith which Abū Jaʿfar Kāmil ibn Aḥmad al-Mustamlī informed us, Bishr ibn Aḥmad al-Isfarāʾīnī narrated to us, Dāwūd ibn al-Ḥusayn al-Bayhaqī narrated to us, Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā informed us, Hushaym narrated from Khālid, from Abū Qilābah, from a man of Banī ʿAdhrah—among them was one who freed a slave of his at the time of his death, and he had no other wealth—the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) freed one-third of him and commanded that he (the slave) work for the remaining two-thirds.\n\nThis was mentioned to al-Shāfiʿī (may Allah have mercy on him), and he said: \The one who was present (at the narration) said: 'It is a mursal hadith"," and even if it were connected"," it would be from an unnamed man who is not known"," and his hadith is not established.'\""\n\nal-Shāfiʿī (may Allah have mercy on him) said: \""Then one of them opposed us with another hadith concerning *istisʿāʾ*"," and some of his companions refuted it and said: 'No one who knows the hadith mentions a hadith like this"," due to its weakness.'\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"21389","(21383) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me with all of this speech and what I have transmitted in this chapter from his words. He narrated to us, Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm narrated to us, al-Rabīʿ informed us, al-Shāfiʿī narrated it, and I do not know which hadith was opposed with it. [Ḍaʿīf]"
"21390","(21384) Perhaps it was opposed by what Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū al-Walīd narrated to us, al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān narrated to us, Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah narrated to us, Ḥafṣ ibn Ghiyāth narrated from al-Ḥajjāj, from al-ʿAlāʾ ibn Badr, from Abū Yaḥyā al-Aʿraj, who said: \The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) was asked about a slave whose master freed him at the time of his death"," and he had no other wealth"," and upon whom there was a debt. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) commanded that he work to pay off the debt.\""\n\nAnd this hadith is munqaṭiʿ (discontinuous). Its narrator is al-Ḥajjāj ibn Arṭāh"," and he is not used as a basis for argument (in establishing rulings). [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"21391","(21385) Or it was narrated through what Abū Muḥammad al-Sukkarī informed us in Baghdād, that Ismāʿīl al-Ṣaffār informed us, that Saʿdān ibn Naṣr narrated to us, that Abū Muʿāwiya narrated from al-Ḥajjāj ibn Arṭāʾ from ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb from Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyab, who said: \Thirty of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) used to say: 'When a man frees a slave who is jointly owned between him and another man"," he is liable (to compensate the co-owner) if he is affluent; and if he is impoverished"," the co-owner shall employ the slave to work for half of his value"," without burdening him.'\""\n\nAnd this narration is also weak. Al-Ḥajjāj ibn Arṭāʾ is not used as a basis for legal argument. It has also been narrated from al-Ḥajjāj ibn Arṭāʾ from Nāfiʿ from Ibn ʿUmar regarding the matter of siʿāyah (compulsory labor of the slave)"," and it is utterly rejected. [Weak]"""
"21392","(21386) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Aḥmad ibn Yaʿqūb al-Thaqafī informed me that Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad al-Tirmidhī narrated to us that Abū Khaythama Zuhayr ibn Ḥarb narrated to us, saying: \I and Khalaf ibn Hishām mentioned al-Ḥajjāj ibn Arṭāʾ to ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Mahdī"," and his disagreement with the trustworthy narrators and the ḥuffāẓ (those with strong memory). We discussed many hadiths of this nature. Then we mentioned to ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Mahdī the hadith of al-Ḥajjāj from Nāfiʿ from Ibn ʿUmar: 'That the Prophet (ﷺ) ruled that when a slave is owned by two men and one of them frees his share"," the one who did not free (his share) has the option: if he wishes"," he may hold the one who freed (his share) liable for the value; and if he does not have (the means)"," the slave shall be made to work (to earn the remaining value)"," without being burdened.'\""\n\nʿAbd al-Raḥmān said: \""This too is among the greatest fabrications! How can this be"," as al-Ḥajjāj narrated it from Nāfiʿ from Ibn ʿUmar"," when ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿUmar narrated it — and there was none in the family of ʿUmar more precise"," more reliable"," more trustworthy"," or more eminent in the science of hadith in his time? It was said that he was unparalleled in memory in his era. Then Mālik ibn Anas followed him in its narration"," and he was not inferior to him in memory; rather"," in our view"," he was equal to him or even more comprehensive in many respects. And Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd al-Anṣārī also narrated it"," and he was among the most precise and most accurate narrators of Madinah. All of them narrated it from Nāfiʿ from Ibn ʿUmar from the Prophet (ﷺ)"," that he said: 'Whoever frees a share or a portion of a slave"," he is obligated to free the remainder if he has wealth; and if he does not have wealth"," then only that portion of the slave which he freed shall be freed.'\""\n\nThe jurist (may Allah have mercy on him) said: \""The matter of siʿāyah (compulsory labor)"," if it is established in the hadith of Bashīr ibn Nahīk from Abū Hurayra (may Allah be pleased with him) from the Prophet (ﷺ)"," then in it is evidence that the choice is from the side of the slave"," for he said 'without being burdened.' And in compelling him"," while he refuses"," there is great hardship upon him. If it is by his choice"," then there is no contradiction between it and the other narrations. And with Allah is the granting of success.\""\n\nSome people have interpreted it"," saying: \""The meaning of siʿāyah is that the slave is made to work for his master"," i.e."," he is employed for his owner. That is why he said 'without being burdened","' meaning he is not required to perform service beyond what is incumbent upon him according to the share of his remaining enslavement.\"" [Authentic]"""
"21393","(21387) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us that Muḥammad ibn Bakr narrated to us that Abū Dāwūd narrated to us that Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us that Shuʿba narrated from Khālid from Abū Bishr al-ʿAnbarī from Ibn al-Thalab from his father: \That a man freed his share of a slave"," and the Prophet (ﷺ) did not hold him liable (for the co-owner's share).\""\n\nAḥmad ibn Ḥanbal said: \""It is with tāʾ (i.e."," al-Talab)"," for Shuʿba was unclear in his speech and did not distinguish the tāʾ from the thāʾ.\""\n\nThe Shaykh (may Allah have mercy on him) said: \""This does not contradict the hadiths that have preceded. Rather"," it pertains to the case of the impoverished person: when he frees his share of a slave"," the remainder is not guaranteed (by him). And Allah knows best.\"" [Weak]"""
"21394","(21388) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū al-Walīd narrated to us that al-Sirāj narrated to us that Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad al-Birtī narrated to us that Abū Ḥudhayfa narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn Muslim narrated from Ayyūb ibn Mūsā, who informed me that Nāfiʿ informed him from Ibn ʿUmar from the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ), who said: \When a man has a share in a slave and then frees his share while the slave is alive"," a fair valuation shall be established against him from his wealth"," and then he shall be freed.\""\n\nAbū al-Walīd al-Faqīh said: \""Our companions said: His statement (ﷺ) 'while the slave is alive' — i.e."," at the time the valuation is established upon him — indicates that the valuation is not to be established after death.\""\n\nThe Shaykh (may Allah have mercy on him) said: \""Thus he narrated it from Muḥammad ibn Muslim.\"" [Authentic. Al-Nasāʾī narrated it in al-Kubrā"," 4927.]"""
"21395","(21389) It was narrated on the authority of Zāhir ibn Aḥmad al-Faqīh that Abū al-Qāsim al-Baghawī informed us that Dāwūd ibn ʿAmr al-Ḍabbī narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn Muslim al-Ṭāʾifī narrated from ʿAmr ibn Dīnār from Ibn ʿUmar, who said: \The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) ruled: 'Any slave in which there is a partnership"," and a man frees his share — the valuation shall be established on the day of emancipation"," and not at the time of death.'\""\n\nThe Shaykh Zāhir (may Allah have mercy on him) said: \""And this wording is not found in every hadith.\"" [Authentic]"""
"21396","(21390) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzakkī and Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī and others narrated to us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us that al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us that al-Shāfiʿī informed us that ʿAbd al-Wahhāb informed us from Ayyūb from Abū Qilāba from Abū al-Muhallab from ʿImrān ibn Ḥuṣayn: \That a man from the Anṣār made a bequest at the time of his death and freed six slaves"," and he had no wealth other than them — or he said: he freed at the time of his death six slaves belonging to him"," and he had nothing other than them. This reached the Prophet (ﷺ)"," and he spoke severely concerning it. Then he called for them and divided them into three parts. He then drew lots among them and freed two and kept four as slaves.\"" [Authentic. Muslim"," 1668.]"""
"21397","(21391) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū ʿAmr ibn Abī Jaʿfar informed me that ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad narrated to us that Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm and Muḥammad ibn al-Muthannā narrated to us, saying: ʿAbd al-Wahhāb al-Thaqafī narrated to us. He mentioned it with its chain and its meaning, except that in the narration of Isḥāq it says: \That a man from the Anṣār freed six slaves belonging to him at the time of his death.\"" And in the narration of Muḥammad ibn al-Muthannā it says: \""A man from the Anṣār made a bequest at the time of his death and freed six slaves belonging to him"," and he had nothing other than them.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm and Ibn Abī ʿUmar"," with the wording of the hadith of Muḥammad ibn al-Muthannā. [Authentic]"""
"21398","(21392) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Aḥmad ibn Jaʿfar informed us that ʿAbd Allāh ibn Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal narrated to me that my father narrated to me.\n\n(Ḥ) And he said: Abū Aḥmad al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me that Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq informed us that ʿAlī ibn Ḥujr and Ziyād ibn Ayyūb narrated to us, saying: Ismāʿīl — that is, Ibn ʿUlayya — narrated from Ayyūb from Abū Qilāba from Abū al-Muhallab from ʿImrān ibn Ḥuṣayn: \That a man freed six slaves at the time of his death"," and he had no wealth other than them. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) called for them and divided them into thirds. He then drew lots among them and freed two and kept four as slaves"," and he spoke to him severely.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAlī ibn Ḥujr and others. [Authentic. It was narrated before.]"""
"21399","(21393) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me that Abū al-Walīd narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn Nuʿaym narrated to us that Qutayba narrated to us that Ḥammād ibn Zayd narrated from Ayyūb. He mentioned it with the chain of Ibn ʿUlayya and its meaning.\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Qutayba. [Authentic. It was narrated before.]"
"21400","(21394) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Aḥmad ibn Salmān al-Faqīh informed us that Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn al-Minhāl narrated to us that Yazīd ibn Zuraiʿ narrated to us that Hishām ibn Ḥassān narrated from Muḥammad ibn Sīrīn from ʿImrān ibn Ḥuṣayn: \That a man had six slaves and had no wealth other than them. He freed them at the time of his death. This was brought to the attention of the Prophet (ﷺ)"," and he disapproved of it. Then he divided them into — I think he said — three parts. He then drew lots among them and freed two and kept four as slaves.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn al-Minhāl and others. [Authentic. It was narrated before.]"""
"21401","(21395) Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān — Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-Sulamī — narrated to us from his origin. Abū al-ʿAbbās — Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb — narrated to us. Muḥammad ibn Sinān narrated to us. Musaddad narrated to us. Ḥammād, who is ibn Zayd, narrated to us, from Yaḥyā ibn ʿAtīq and Ayyūb.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū al-Ḥasan — ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Muqriʾ — informed us. Al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad narrated to us. Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb al-Qāḍī narrated to us. Abū al-Rabīʿ narrated to us. Ḥammād ibn Zayd narrated to us. Ayyūb and Yaḥyā ibn ʿAtīq and Hishām narrated, from Muḥammad ibn Sīrīn, from ʿImrān ibn Ḥuṣayn, that a man freed six slaves of his at the time of his death, and he had no other wealth besides them. This reached the Prophet (ﷺ), so he drew lots among them and freed two and kept four in bondage.\n\nYaḥyā said: Muḥammad said: \Had this not reached me from the Prophet (ﷺ)"," my own opinion would have been [the same].\"" The wording is that of the ḥadīth of Musaddad. [Ṣaḥīh. Preceded before it.]"""
"21402","(21396) Abū al-Ḥasan — ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān — informed us. Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us. Al-Ḥulwānī — Aḥmad ibn Yaḥyā — narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Manṣūr — Aḥmad ibn ʿAlī al-Dāmaghānī — and Abū al-Ḥasan — ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Khusrajirdī — both said: Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī informed us. Abū Bakr — Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī ibn ʿAmr al-Ḥaffār — narrated to us. Both said: ʿAbd al-Aʿlā ibn Ḥammād narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us. Abū al-Walīd narrated to us. The son of the daughter of Aḥmad ibn Manīʿ narrated to us. ʿAbd al-Aʿlā narrated to us. Ḥammād ibn Salamah narrated to us, from ʿAṭāʾ al-Khurāsānī, from Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyab, and Ayyūb, from Muḥammad ibn Sīrīn, from ʿImrān ibn Ḥuṣayn, and Simāk, from al-Ḥasan, from ʿImrān ibn Ḥuṣayn. And in the narration of al-Ḥulwānī and al-Ḥaffār: Qatādah and Ḥumayd and Simāk ibn Ḥarb narrated, from al-Ḥasan, from ʿImrān ibn Ḥuṣayn, that a man freed six slaves of his at the time of his death, and he had no wealth other than them. So the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) drew lots among them and freed two and returned four to bondage. [Ṣaḥīh. Preceded before it.]"
"21403","(21397) And Abū al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAbdān informed us. Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd narrated to us. Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣaffār and Yaḥyā ibn Muḥammad al-Ḥinnāʾī both said: ʿAbd al-Aʿlā ibn Ḥammād narrated to us. He mentioned the ḥadīth with the same wording as the ḥadīth of al-Ḥulwānī and its chain of narration, except that he said: \from ʿAṭāʾ ibn al-Sāʾib\"" instead of \""ʿAṭāʾ al-Khurāsānī","\"" and this is an error. [Ṣaḥīh. Preceded before it.]"""
"21404","(21398) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us. Abū al-ʿAbbās, who is al-Aṣamm, narrated to us. Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad ibn Shākir narrated to us. ʿAmr, meaning ibn Ḥammād al-Qannād, narrated to us. Asbāṭ narrated to us, from Simāk, from al-Ḥasan al-Baṣrī, from ʿImrān ibn Ḥuṣayn, that a man died and left six men [slaves] and freed them at the time of his death. His heirs came and mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ). He said: \Had we known"," we would not have prayed over him.\"" And he said: \""Call them to me.\"" So they were called"," and he drew lots among them and freed two and returned four to bondage. [Ṣaḥīh. Preceded.]"""
"21405","(21399) Abū al-Ḥasan — Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn Dāwūd al-ʿAlawī — narrated to us by dictation. Abū Ḥāmid — Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Ḥāfiẓ — narrated to us. Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā al-Dhuhlī and Aḥmad ibn Yūsuf al-Sulamī both said: ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Mūsā informed us. Isrāʾīl narrated to us, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Mukhtār, from Muḥammad ibn Ziyād, from Abū Hurayrah, that a man freed six slaves at the time of his death, and he had no wealth other than them, during the time of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ). So the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) divided them into portions and freed two and kept four in bondage. [Ṣaḥīh.]"
"21406","(21400) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzakkī informed us. Abū al-ʿAbbās — Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb — informed us. Al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us. Al-Shāfiʿī informed us. ʿAbd al-Majīd informed us, from Ibn Jurayj. Qays ibn Saʿd informed me that he heard Makḥūl saying: \I heard Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyab saying: 'A woman or a man freed six slaves of theirs"," and they had no wealth other than them.' The Prophet (ﷺ) was approached concerning that"," so he drew lots among them and freed one-third of them.\""\n\nAl-Shāfiʿī said: \""That was during the illness of the emancipator in which he died.\"" [Ṣaḥīh. For other than him.]"""
"21407","(21401) Abū Naṣr ibn Qatādah informed us. Abū ʿAmr ibn Najayd narrated to us. Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us. Ibn Bukayr narrated to us. Mālik narrated to us, from Rabīʿah ibn Abī ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, that during the time of Abān ibn ʿUthmān, a man freed all his slaves. Abān ibn ʿUthmān ordered those slaves to be divided into three groups, and he drew lots among them to determine which group the share of the deceased would fall upon, and they would be freed. The lot of the deceased fell upon one of the three groups, so they were freed.\n\nMālik said: \And that is the best of what I have heard.\"" [Ṣaḥīh. Mālik narrated it.]"""
"21408","(21402) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us. Abū Aḥmad — Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣaffār — narrated to us. Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Naṣr al-Labbād narrated to us. ʿAmr ibn Ṭalḥah narrated to us. Asbāṭ ibn Naṣr narrated to us, from al-Suddī, from Abī Mālik and Abī Ṣāliḥ, from Ibn ʿAbbās, and from Murrah, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Masʿūd, from some of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ). He mentioned the tafsīr and said in the story of Maryam (peace be upon her): \Indeed"," those who used to write the Torah — when a person was brought to them to be tested"," they would draw lots among themselves as to who would take him and teach him. And Zakariyyā was the best of them that day"," and he was their prophet. And the sister of Maryam was under his care. So when they brought her"," Zakariyyā said to them: 'I am most deserving of her"," for her sister is under my care.' But they refused. So they went out to the river al-Urdun and cast their pens with which they used to write"," [to see] whose pen would stand and thus take custody of her. The pens floated"," and the pen of Zakariyyā stood upright on its tip"," as though it were in clay. So he took the girl.\"" [Ḥasan.]"""
"21409","(21403) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī informed us. Ibrāhīm ibn al-Ḥusayn narrated to us. Ādam ibn Abī Iyās narrated to us. Warqāʾ narrated to us, from Ibn Abī Najīḥ, from Mujāhid, regarding His statement {And Zakariyyā took care of her} [Āl ʿImrān 37], he said: \He cast lots with his pen and prevailed over them"," meaning he took care of her.\"" And in His statement {So he cast lots and was among those who lost}"," he says: \""He was among those who were overcome by the lot.\"" [Ḍaʿīf.]"""
"21410","(21404) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq informed us. Abū al-Ḥasan al-Ṭarāʾifī informed us. ʿUthmān ibn Saʿīd informed us. ʿAbd Allāh ibn Ṣāliḥ narrated to us, from Muʿāwiyah ibn Ṣāliḥ, from ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭalḥah, from Ibn ʿAbbās, regarding His statement {So he cast lots}, he says: \So he drew lots.\"" {And was among those who lost}"," he says: \""Among those who were overcome by the lot.\"" [Ḍaʿīf.]"""
"21411","(21405) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr narrated to us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, saying: Muḥammad ibn ʿUbayd Allāh ibn al-Munādī narrated to us, saying: Yūnus ibn Muḥammad narrated to us, saying: Shaybān narrated from Qatādah regarding His statement — \So he cast lots and was among the defeated\"" [al-Ṣāffāt 141] — that he said: \""The Prophet of Allāh Yūnus"," peace be upon him"," cast lots and was defeated.\"" He said: \""The ship was held back"," and the people knew it was held back on account of some offence committed by one of them. So they cast lots"," and Yūnus — ﷺ — was defeated"," so he cast himself into the sea. 'And the whale swallowed him while he was blameworthy' [al-Ṣāffāt 142].\"" He said: \""He was reproaching himself for what he had done. 'Had he not been of those who glorify Allāh' [al-Ṣāffāt 143].\"" He said: \""He was one who prayed abundantly during times of ease"," and so He saved him.\""\n\nAl-Shāfiʿī"," may Allāh have mercy on him"," said: \""The Prophet's ﷺ drawing of lots in every situation in which he cast lots"," in a sense similar to those who drew lots over the guardianship of Maryam"," is consistent and not contradictory.\"" He elaborated on this and cited what has been narrated to us in the ḥadīth of ʿImrān ibn Ḥuṣayn from the Prophet ﷺ regarding slaves. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"21412","(21406) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān al-ʿAdl narrated to us in Baghdād, saying: Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr ibn al-Razzāz narrated to us, saying: Muḥammad ibn Dāwūd al-Qūmisī narrated to us, saying: Yaḥyā ibn Bukayr narrated to us, saying: al-Layth narrated from Jarīr ibn Ḥāzim from Ayyūb al-Sakhtiyānī from Muḥammad ibn Sīrīn from ʿImrān ibn Ḥuṣayn.\n\nHe said: And al-Layth narrated to me from Jarīr ibn Ḥāzim from Abī Qilābah from Abī al-Muhallab from ʿImrān ibn Ḥuṣayn, who said: \A man from the Anṣār died and left behind six slaves"," having no other wealth besides them. He manumitted all of them at the time of his death. This matter was raised to the Prophet ﷺ"," so he divided them into three portions"," then cast lots among them. He manumitted one-third and kept two-thirds as slaves.\""\n\nMuḥammad ibn Sīrīn said: \""Had this not reached me from the Prophet ﷺ"," it would have been my own opinion.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim]"""
"21413","(21407) He said: And al-Layth narrated to me from Jarīr from al-Ḥasan, who said: \I do not know except from Abū Hurayrah"," may Allāh be pleased with him"," something similar to that.\"" He added: And Khālid al-Ḥaddāʾ narrated from Abī Qilābah something that Ayyūb did not understand"," so I do not know whether he did not memorise it or concealed it. Jarīr said: Khālid al-Ḥaddāʾ narrated to me from Abī Qilābah just as Ayyūb had said"," except that he added: ʿImrān ibn Ḥuṣayn said: \""The Messenger of Allāh ﷺ said when his matter was mentioned to him: 'Had I known what he did"," I would not have prayed over him.'\"" This is in the narration of Jarīr ibn Ḥāzim: \""He manumitted one-third and kept two-thirds as slaves.\"" And the narration of the group whom we mentioned earlier states: \""He manumitted two and kept four as slaves.\"" This is what Jarīr intended by what he narrated"," and it is the narration that is more consistent with the division and the casting of lots. And in Allāh lies all success. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Preceded earlier]"""
"21414","(21408) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī narrated to us, saying: Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār narrated to us, saying: ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Khalaf narrated to us, saying: Ḥajjāj ibn Minhāl narrated to us, saying: ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar al-Numayrī narrated to us, saying: Yūnus ibn Yazīd narrated to us, saying: I heard al-Zuhrī say: I heard —\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, saying: Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq al-Faqīh narrated to us, saying: Aḥmad ibn Ibrāhīm ibn Milḥān narrated to us, saying: Yaḥyā ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Bukayr narrated to us, saying: al-Layth ibn Saʿd narrated from Yūnus ibn Yazīd from Ibn Shihāb that he said: ʿUrwah ibn al-Zubayr, Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyib, ʿAlqamah ibn Waqqāṣ, and ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUtbah narrated to me from the ḥadīth of ʿĀʾishah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ — they claimed that ʿĀʾishah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, said: \When the Messenger of Allāh ﷺ intended to travel"," he would cast lots among his wives. Whosever lot came out"," the Messenger of Allāh ﷺ would take her with him.\"" ʿĀʾishah said: \""He cast lots among us during a battle he fought"," and my lot came out"," so I went out with the Messenger of Allāh ﷺ.\"" And she mentioned the ḥadīth.\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Ibn Bukayr and from Ḥajjāj ibn Minhāl"," and Muslim narrated it from another route from Yūnus. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Agreed upon]"""
"21415","(21409) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yaḥyā ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār al-Sukkarī narrated to us in Baghdād, saying: Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār narrated to us, saying: Aḥmad ibn Manṣūr al-Ramādī narrated to us, saying: ʿAbd al-Razzāq narrated to us, saying: Mālik narrated —\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, saying: Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, saying: Muḥammad ibn Naṣr al-Marwazī and Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad narrated to us, saying: Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us, saying: I read to Mālik from Sumayy, the freedman of Abī Bakr, from Abī Ṣāliḥ al-Sammān, from Abū Hurayrah, may Allāh be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allāh ﷺ said: \If people knew what is in the call to prayer and the first row"," and then found no way to attain it except by drawing lots"," they would draw lots for it. And if they knew what is in hastening to the prayer at midday"," they would race to it. And if they knew what is in the ʿIshāʾ and Fajr prayers"," they would attend them even if they had to crawl on their knees.\"" This is the wording of the ḥadīth of Yaḥyā. He said: I said to him: \""Do you dislike saying al-ʿAtamah?\"" He said: \""Thus said the one who narrated it to me.\""\n\nʿAbd al-Razzāq said: And Maʿmar used to narrate it from Mālik.\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Ibn Abī Uways from Mālik"," and Muslim narrated it from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Agreed upon]"""
"21416","(21410) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh narrated to us, saying: Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Saʿīd al-Rāzī narrated to us, saying: Muḥammad ibn Muslim ibn Wārah narrated to us, saying: Abū Nuʿaym narrated —\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, saying: Abū Manṣūr Muḥammad ibn al-Qāsim al-ʿAtakī narrated to us, saying: Aḥmad ibn Naṣr narrated to us, saying: Abū Nuʿaym narrated to us, saying: Zakariyyā narrated to us, saying: I heard ʿĀmir say: I heard al-Nuʿmān ibn Bashīr say: The Messenger of Allāh ﷺ said: \The example of those who uphold the limits of Allāh and those who transgress them is like a people who drew lots for places on a ship. Some of them got the upper part and some the lower part. When those in the lower part wanted to draw water"," they had to pass by those above them"," causing them harm. So they said: 'If we bore a hole in our own portion"," we could draw water without troubling those above us.' If they are left to do what they intend"," all will perish; but if they are prevented"," all will be saved.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Abī Nuʿaym. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 2493]"""
"21417","(21411) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh narrated to us, saying: Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-Qaṭṭān narrated to us, saying: Aḥmad ibn Yūsuf al-Sulamī narrated to us, saying: ʿAbd al-Razzāq narrated to us, saying: Maʿmar narrated from al-Zuhrī from Khārijah ibn Zayd ibn Thābit, who said: Umm al-ʿAlāʾ al-Anṣāriyyah used to say: \When the Muhājirūn arrived in Madīnah"," the Anṣār drew lots for hosting them. She said: 'The lot fell to us for ʿUthmān ibn Maẓʿūn's lodging.'\"" And she mentioned the ḥadīth. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Preceded earlier]"""
"21418","(21412) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, saying: al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Ḥalīm narrated to us in Marw, saying: Abū al-Muwajjih narrated to us, saying: ʿAbdān narrated to us, saying: ʿAbd Allāh narrated to us, saying: Maʿmar narrated from al-Zuhrī from Khārijah ibn Zayd ibn Thābit from Umm al-ʿAlāʾ — and she was a woman from among their women who had pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allāh ﷺ — who said: \The lot fell to us for ʿUthmān ibn Maẓʿūn's lodging when the Anṣār drew lots for the lodging of the Muhājirūn. He fell ill"," and we nursed him until he passed away. Then we placed him in his garments. She said: The Messenger of Allāh ﷺ came to us"," and I said: 'May Allāh's mercy be upon you"," Abū al-Sāʾib! My testimony is that Allāh has honoured you.' The Prophet ﷺ said: 'How do you know?' She said: 'By Allāh"," I do not know"," O Messenger of Allāh.' He said: 'As for him"," certainty has come to him"," and I hope for good for him from Allāh. By Allāh"," I do not know — and I am the Messenger of Allāh — what will be done to him or to you.'\"" Umm al-ʿAlāʾ said: \""By Allāh"," I never declared anyone righteous again.\"" She said: \""I saw ʿUthmān in a dream with a flowing stream. I came to the Messenger of Allāh ﷺ and mentioned it to him"," and he said: 'That is his deed"," flowing for him.'\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbdān. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 1243]"""
"21419","(21413) Abū al-Qāsim ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿUbayd Allāh al-Ḥurfī narrated to us in Baghdād, saying: Ḥamzah ibn Muḥammad ibn al-ʿAbbās narrated to us, saying: al-Ḥārith ibn Muḥammad narrated to us, saying: Abū al-Naḍr narrated to us, saying: al-Layth narrated to us, saying: ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUbayd Allāh, meaning Ibn Abī Maysarah, narrated from al-Miswar ibn Makhramah, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allāh ﷺ say while he was on the pulpit: \The Banū Hishām ibn al-Mughīrah asked my permission to marry their daughter to ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib. I will not permit it"," then I will not permit it. My daughter is a part of me. What troubles her troubles me"," and what harms her harms me.\""\n\nBoth al-Bukhārī and Muslim narrated it in their Ṣaḥīḥ collections from Qutaybah from al-Layth. He informed that one's offspring is a part of oneself"," and when a slave frees himself by fulfilling the payment of his kitābah or by purchasing himself"," he is emancipated. Likewise"," when a free person owns his child"," he owns a part of himself"," and when he owns his parent"," he owns one who is a part of himself"," and thus emancipation is obligatory. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Agreed upon]"""
"21420","(21414) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh narrated to us, saying: Ḥājib ibn Aḥmad al-Ṭūsī narrated to us, saying: ʿAbd al-Raḥīm ibn Munīb narrated to us, saying: Jarīr ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥamīd narrated to us, saying: Suhayl ibn Abī Ṣāliḥ narrated —\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh narrated to us, saying: Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn narrated to us, saying: Aḥmad ibn Yūsuf al-Sulamī narrated to us, saying: Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf narrated to us, saying: Sufyān mentioned from Suhayl ibn Abī Ṣāliḥ from his father from Abū Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allāh ﷺ said: \A child cannot repay his parent unless he finds him enslaved"," purchases him"," and then manumits him.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Abī Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah and others from Jarīr"," and he narrated it through other routes from Sufyān al-Thawrī.\n\nHis statement \""purchases him and then manumits him\"" may mean that he manumits him through the act of purchasing"," and Allāh knows best. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Agreed upon]"""
"21421","(21415) Abū Ḥāẓim al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Isḥāq Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us; Ismāʿīl ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us; Isḥāq ibn Manṣūr informed us; Muḥammad ibn Bakr al-Bursānī narrated to us; Ḥammād ibn Salamah narrated from ʿĀṣim al-Aḥwal and Qatādah, from al-Ḥasan, from Samurah ibn Jundub, from the Prophet ﷺ, who said: \Whoever possesses a maḥram relative among his kin"," that person is free.\"""""
"21422","(21416) Abū ʿAlī al-Ḥusayn ibn Muḥammad al-Rūdhbārī informed us; Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Bakr narrated to us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; Muslim ibn Ibrāhīm and Mūsā ibn Ismāʿīl both said: Ḥammād ibn Salamah narrated to us from Qatādah, from al-Ḥasan, from Samurah, from the Prophet ﷺ. Mūsā said in another place, from Samurah, according to what Ḥammād thought: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Whoever possesses a maḥram relative"," that person is free.\""\n\nAbū Dāwūd said: No one narrated this ḥadīth except Ḥammād ibn Salamah"," and he was doubtful in it. Aḥmad said"," and Abū ʿĪsā al-Tirmidhī said — as it reached me — \""I asked al-Bukhārī about this ḥadīth"," and he did not know it from al-Ḥasan from Samurah except through the ḥadīth of Ḥammād ibn Salamah.\""\n\nThe Shaykh"," may Allah have mercy on him"," said: Ḥammād was doubtful regarding the mention of Samurah in its isnād"," as we have previously noted from Mūsā ibn Ismāʿīl. And other than Ḥammād narrate it from Qatādah from ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb"," may Allah be pleased with him"," and from Qatādah from al-Ḥasan as his own statement."""
"21423","(21417) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us; Muḥammad ibn Bakr narrated to us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Sulaymān al-Anbārī narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Wahhāb narrated from Saʿīd, from Qatādah, that ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb, may Allah be pleased with him, said: \Whoever possesses a maḥram relative"," that person is free.\"""""
"21424","(21418) Abū ʿAlī informed us; Muḥammad ibn Bakr narrated to us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah narrated to us; Abū Usāmah narrated from Saʿīd, from Qatādah, from Jābir ibn Zayd and al-Ḥasan, similarly.\n\nAbū Dāwūd said: Saʿīd is more precise than Ḥammād, Aḥmad said. And it was narrated through another isnād in which the narrator made an error."
"21425","(21419) ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us; Sulaymān ibn Aḥmad al-Lakhmī narrated to us; ʿAbdān ibn Aḥmad and al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī al-Maʿmarī both said: Abū ʿUmayr ibn al-Nuḥḥās narrated to us; Ḍamrah ibn Rabīʿah narrated from al-Thawrī, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Dīnār, from Ibn ʿUmar, from the Prophet ﷺ, who said: \Whoever possesses a maḥram relative"," that person is free (ʿatīq).\""\n\nSulaymān said: No one narrated this ḥadīth from Sufyān except Ḍamrah. The Shaykh"," may Allah have mercy on him"," said: The preserved narration through this isnād is the ḥadīth prohibiting the selling of walāʾ and its gifting. Abū ʿUmayr narrated it from Ḍamrah from al-Thawrī along with the first ḥadīth."""
"21426","(21420) Abū Naṣr ibn Qatādah informed us with both ḥadīths together; Abū ʿAmr ibn Maṭar narrated to us; Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad ibn Yūnus Abū Isḥāq narrated to us; Abū ʿUmayr ʿĪsā ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Naḥḥās narrated both of them together. And Allah knows best."
"21427","(21421) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us; ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Nūḥ al-Jundaysābūrī narrated to us; ʿAlī ibn Ḥarb al-Jundaysābūrī narrated to us; Ashʿath ibn ʬAṭṭāf narrated to us; al-ʿArzamī narrated from Abū al-Naḍr, from Abū Ṣāliḥ, from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: A man called Ṣāliḥ came with his brother and said, \O Messenger of Allah"," I wish to free this brother of mine.\"" He ﷺ said: \""Indeed Allah freed him when you came to possess him.\""\n\nʿAlī al-Dāraquṭnī"," may Allah have mercy on him"," said: al-ʿArzamī was abandoned by Ibn al-Mubārak"," Yaḥyā al-Qaṭṭān"," and Ibn Mahdī. Abū al-Naḍr is Muḥammad ibn al-Sāʾib al-Kalbī"," who is abandoned (matrūk)"," and he is the one who said: \""Everything I narrated from Abū Ṣāliḥ is a lie.\""\n\nThe Shaykh said: It was narrated from Ḥafṣ ibn Abī Dāwūd"," from Muḥammad ibn Abī Laylā"," from ʬAṭāʾ"," from Ibn ʿAbbās"," with something similar. This is a weak isnād. Ḥafṣ is Ibn Sulaymān al-Qāriʾ"," who was declared weak by Shuʿbah"," Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal"," Yaḥyā ibn Maʿīn"," and others."""
"21428","(21422) Abū Naṣr ibn Qatādah informed us; Abū ʿAmr Ismāʿīl ibn Nujayd informed us; Abū Muslim al-Kajjī narrated to us; Abū ʿĀṣim informed us; Abū ʿAwanah narrated from al-Ḥakam, from Ibrāhīm, from al-Aswad, who said: ʿUmar, may Allah be pleased with him, said: \Whoever possesses a maḥram relative"," that person is free.\"""""
"21429","(21423) Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī informed us; Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn Maḥmūd al-Faqīh narrated to us; Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us; Abū Mūsā Muḥammad ibn al-Muthannā narrated to us; al-Ḍaḥḥāk narrated from Abū ʿAwanah, from al-Ḥakam, from Ibrāhīm, from al-Aswad, from ʿUmar, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: \Whoever possesses a maḥram relative"," that person is free\"" — or \""a maḥram\"" — al-Ḍaḥḥāk was doubtful.\n\nAbū Mūsā said: I heard Abū al-Walīd say"," \""I read in the book of Abū ʿAwanah"," from al-Ḥakam"," from Ibrāhīm"," from al-Aswad"," from ʿUmar"," may Allah be pleased with him"," who said: 'A person with kinship ties cannot be enslaved.'\"""""
"21430","(21424) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Jarrāḥī in Marw informed us; Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī narrated to us; Khalaf ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz narrated to me; my father narrated from my grandfather, from Shuʿbah, from Sufyān al-Thawrī and Ghaylān, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from al-Mustawrid, that a man came to Ibn Masʿūd and said, \My uncle has married me to his slave-girl"," and he wishes to enslave my child.\"" ʿAbd Allāh said"," \""That is not permissible for him.\""\n\nIt was narrated from Rūḥ"," from Shuʿbah"," from Sufyān"," from Salamah.\n\nAnd ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Mahdī narrated it from Sufyān"," and it is from ʿUmar and Ibn Masʿūd"," may Allah be pleased with both of them. It is ḥasan"," and some of our companions held this opinion."""
"21431","(21425) Abū al-Ḥasan al-Raffāʾ informed us that ʿUthmān ibn Muḥammad ibn Bashr narrated to us that Ismāʿīl al-Qāḍī narrated to us that Ibn Abī Uways narrated to us that ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī al-Zinād narrated from his father, from the jurists whose opinion was relied upon among the people of Madīnah, that they used to say: \If a child owns his parent"," the parent is freed; and if a parent owns his child"," the child is freed. As for other relations besides that"," they differed concerning it.\""\n\nAl-Qāḍī said: And ʿĪsā ibn Mīnāʾ narrated from Ibn Abī al-Zinād that the people differed concerning it. Ibn Abī Uways narrated from Ibn Abī al-Zinād from his father from them"," and they used to say: \""If a man purchases a share of his father or his mother"," that share is freed"," and the remainder is valued against him"," so that the entirety is freed upon him. But if he inherits a share of him and does not purchase it"," the share is freed"," and the remainder is not valued against him.\"" [Weak]"""
"21432","(21426) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū Aḥmad Bakr ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣayrafī in Marw narrated to us that Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿĪsā narrated to us that Abū Maʿmar narrated to us that ʿAbd al-Wārith ibn Saʿīd narrated to us that Saʿīd ibn Jumḥān narrated to me that Safīnah said: Umm Salamah said to me: \I will free you on the condition that you serve the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) for as long as you live.\"" He said: I said: \""Even if you had not stipulated that upon me"," I would not have parted from the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) for as long as I live.\"" He said: So she freed me and stipulated upon me that I serve the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) for as long as I live.\n\nAbū Dāwūd narrated it in the book of Sunan from Musaddad from ʿAbd al-Wārith. [Good]"""
"21433","(21427) And Ḥammād ibn Salamah narrated it from Saʿīd, as Abū Manṣūr al-Ẓafar ibn Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad al-ʿAlawī, may Allah have mercy on him, informed us that Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī ibn Duḥaym narrated to us that Aḥmad ibn Ḥāzim narrated to us that ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Mūsā informed us that Ḥammād ibn Salamah narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Bakr ibn Fūrak informed us that ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us that Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb narrated to us that Abū Dāwūd narrated to us that Ḥammād ibn Salamah narrated from Saʿīd ibn Jumḥān that Safīnah, the freed slave of Umm Salamah, informed me and said: \Umm Salamah"," may Allah be pleased with her"," freed me and stipulated upon me that I serve the Prophet (peace be upon him) for as long as he lives.\"" This is the wording of the ḥadīth of Abū Dāwūd. [Good]"""
"21434","(21428) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzzakī and Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥakam informed us that Ibn Wahb informed me that Yaʿqūb ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān and Ḥafṣ ibn Mayṣarah narrated from Mūsā ibn ʿUqbah from Nāfiʿ that ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar freed a slave of his and then stipulated upon him that he would work for him for some years, so he tended for him for some of those years.\n\nAnd in the narration of al-Qāḍī: \for some of a year","\"" then he came to him"," either during Ḥajj or during ʿUmrah"," and ʿAbd Allah said to him: \""I have relinquished what I stipulated upon you"," and you are free"," and there is no work upon you.\""\n\nThus I found it: \""then he stipulated upon him","\"" and it is: \""and he stipulated upon him.\"" [Authentic]"""
"21435","(21429) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us that Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us that Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib narrated to us that Ḥammād ibn Masʿadah narrated to us that Ibn ʿAwn narrated that Nāfiʿ said: \Ibn ʿUmar sent me on an errand. He said: I returned from it"," and he said to me: 'You are free"," if you wish to stay with us"," and we are those you know.' He said: I said: 'Where shall I go"," or to whom shall I go?'\"" [Good]"""
"21436","(21430) Abū Naṣr Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Faqīh al-Shīrāzī and Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzzakī both said: Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb al-Shaybānī al-Akhr narrated to us that al-Sarī ibn Khuzaymah narrated to us that Abū Nuʿaym narrated to us that Sufyān, that is al-Thawrī, narrated from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Dīnār from Ibn ʿUmar, who said: \The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) forbade the selling of walāʾ (clientage) and the gifting of it.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Abī Nuʿaym"," and Muslim narrated it from another route from Sufyān al-Thawrī. [Authentic. Agreed upon]"""
"21437","(21431) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us that Abū Ḥāmid Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā ibn Bilāl narrated to us that Yaḥyā ibn al-Rabīʿ al-Makkī narrated to us that Sufyān, that is Ibn ʿUyaynah, narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī and others said: Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm informed us that al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us that al-Shāfiʿī informed us that Mālik and Ibn ʿUyaynah narrated from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Dīnār from Ibn ʿUmar that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) forbade the selling of walāʾ and the gifting of it.\n\nThe wording of both their ḥadīths is the same. Muslim narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Abī Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah and others from Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah. [Authentic. Previously mentioned]"
"21438","(21432) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq informed us that ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz narrated to us that Abū al-Walīd narrated to us that Shuʿbah narrated from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Dīnār, who said: I heard Ibn ʿUmar say: \The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) forbade the selling of walāʾ and the gifting of it.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Abī al-Walīd"," and Muslim narrated it from another route from Shuʿbah.\n\nAnd likewise ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿAmr"," Ismāʿīl ibn Jaʿfar"," Sulaymān ibn Bilāl"," al-Ḍaḥḥāk ibn ʿUthmān"," and others narrated it from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Dīnār. [Authentic. Previously mentioned]"""
"21439","(21433) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us that al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us that al-Shāfiʿī informed us that Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan narrated from Yaʿqūb ibn Ibrāhīm from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Dīnār from Ibn ʿUmar that the Prophet (peace be upon him) said: \Walāʾ (clientage) is a bond like the bond of lineage; it is neither sold nor gifted.\""\n\nThus Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Faqīh narrated it from Yaʿqūb Abī Yūsuf al-Qāḍī from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Dīnār. [Weak]"""
"21440","(21434) And Abū Ḥāmid Aḥmad ibn ʿAlī al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Zāhir ibn Aḥmad al-Sarakhshī narrated to us, who said: Abū Bakr ibn Ziyād al-Naysābūrī said after this ḥadīth: \This is an error"," because the trustworthy narrators did not narrate it in this manner. Rather"," al-Ḥasan narrated it as a mursal (disconnected) narration.\"" [Authentic]"""
"21441","(21435) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr narrated to us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib narrated to us: Yazīd ibn Hārūn informed us: Hishām ibn Ḥassān informed us, from al-Ḥasan, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Walāʾ (clientage) is a bond like the bond of lineage; it cannot be sold nor gifted.\""\n\nThe Shaykh (may Allah have mercy on him) said: It has been narrated through other chains"," all of which are weak. [Weak]"""
"21442","(21436) ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us: Sulaymān ibn Aḥmad al-Lakhmī narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn ʿAbd al-Bāqī al-Adhanī narrated to us: Abū ʿUmayr ibn al-Naḥḥās narrated to us: Ḍamrah narrated, from Sufyān, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Dīnār, from Ibn ʿUmar, from the Prophet (ﷺ), who said: \Walāʾ (clientage) is a bond like the bond of lineage; it cannot be sold nor gifted.\""\n\nSulaymān said: No one narrated this ḥadīth from Sufyān except Ḍamrah.\n\nThe Shaykh (may Allah have mercy on him) said: Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf al-Firyābī narrated it from Ḍamrah"," just as the group narrated it — the prohibition of selling walāʾ and gifting it. Thus"," the error appears to have come from someone other than him. And Allah knows best. [Weak]"""
"21443","(21437) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-Walīd narrated to us: Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Nuʿaym narrated to us: Yaʿqūb ibn Ḥumayd ibn Kāsib informed us: Yaḥyā ibn Sulaym narrated, from ʿUbayd Allāh, from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar, that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \Walāʾ (clientage) is a bond like the bond of lineage; it cannot be sold nor gifted.\""\n\nThis is an error on the part of Yaḥyā ibn Sulaym or from someone below him"," in both the isnād and the matn.\n\nFor the ḥuffāẓ only narrated it from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿUmar"," from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Dīnār"," from Ibn ʿUmar"," from the Prophet (ﷺ)"," that he prohibited the selling of walāʾ and the gifting of it. [Weak]"""
"21444","(21438) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed him: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us by dictation: Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣaghānī narrated to us: Shujāʿ ibn al-Walīd narrated to us: ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿUmar narrated — and he mentioned it.\n\nMuslim extracted it through another chain from ʿUbayd Allāh, regarding the sale (of walāʾ). And Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Malik ibn Abī al-Shawārib narrated it from Yaḥyā ibn Sulaym, with the error in its isnād but not in its matn.\n\nAbū ʿĪsā said — as it reached me — \I asked al-Bukhārī about it"," and he said: 'Yaḥyā ibn Sulaym made an error in his ḥadīth. It is only from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Dīnār"," from Ibn ʿUmar.' And ʿAbd Allāh ibn Dīnār is the one who is alone in this ḥadīth"," meaning with the well-known wording.\""\n\nAnd Abū Ḥassān al-Ziyādī narrated it from Yaḥyā ibn Sulaym"," from Ismāʿīl ibn Umayyah"," from Nāfiʿ"," from Ibn ʿUmar"," from the Prophet (ﷺ)"," that he said: \""Walāʾ (clientage) is a bond like lineage.\"" [Weak]"""
"21445","(21439) The Imam Abū ʿUthmān informed him: Abū Ṭāhir Muḥammad ibn al-Faḍl ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq ibn Khuzaymah narrated to us: My grandfather narrated to us: al-Ziyādī narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Sulaym narrated — and he mentioned it.\n\nThis is a third discrepancy from Yaḥyā ibn Sulaym, and he was of poor memory and frequent in error. And Allah knows best.\n\nThe Shaykh (may Allah have mercy on him) said: It has been narrated regarding that from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Nāfiʿ through two chains, and he erred in both, and there was disagreement regarding it from Yaḥyā ibn Abī Unaysah, from al-Zuhrī, from Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyab, from Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), as a marfūʿ narration, but al-Zuhrī has no basis for it. And Yaḥyā ibn Abī Unaysah is weak, to say the least. This wording is only narrated as a mursal narration, as we have previously mentioned, and it is narrated from someone other than the Prophet (ﷺ)."
"21446","(21440) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib narrated to us: Yazīd ibn Hārūn informed us: Abū al-ʿAlāʾ Ayyūb ibn Miskīn narrated, from Qatādah, who said: Indeed, ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him) said: \Walāʾ (clientage) is like lineage; it cannot be sold nor gifted.\""\n\nAnd Ḥammād narrated it from Dāwūd and Qatādah"," from Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyab"," that ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him) said — and he mentioned it. [Weak]"""
"21447","(21441) Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās informed us: al-Rabīʿ informed us: al-Shāfiʿī informed us: Sufyān narrated, from Ibn Abī Najīḥ, from Mujāhid, that ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) said: \Walāʾ (clientage) holds the status of an alliance (ḥilf); I affirm it wherever Allah has placed it.\"" [Weak]"""
"21448","(21442) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-Walīd narrated to us: al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān narrated to us: ʿAbbās ibn al-Walīd al-Narsī narrated to us: Sufyān narrated, from Ibn Abī Najīḥ, from Mujāhid, from ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Walāʾ (clientage) holds the status of lineage; it cannot be sold nor gifted. I affirm it wherever Allah has placed it.\"" [Weak]"""
"21449","(21443) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr narrated to us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās — al-Aṣamm — narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib narrated to us: Yazīd ibn Hārūn informed us: Sufyān al-Thawrī and Sharīk narrated, from ʿImrān ibn Muslim ibn Rabbāḥ, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Maʿqil, who said: I heard ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) say: \Walāʾ (clientage) is a branch of lineage.\"" [Ḥasan]"""
"21450","(21444) He said: And Yazīd informed us, from ʿAbd al-Malik ibn al-Ḥusayn, from ʿImrān ibn Muslim, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Maʿqil, who said: ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) was asked about the selling of walāʾ, so he said: \Does a man sell his lineage?\"" [Weak]"""
"21451","(21445) He narrated: Yazid informed us, ʿAbd al-Malik ibn Abī Sulaymān informed us, from ʿAṭāʾ, from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: \Walāʾ (clientage) shall not be sold"," and walāʾ shall not be given as a gift. The walāʾ belongs to the one who manumitted.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"21452","(21446) Abū ʿAbd Allāh informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās narrated to us, Yaḥyā narrated to us, Yazid informed us, Ḥammād ibn Zayd informed us, from Abī Hāshim, that Ibn Masʿūd, may Allah be pleased with him, said: \Walāʾ shall not be sold.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"21453","(21447) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad al-Muqriʾ informed us, Aḥmad ibn Salmān narrated to us, Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad ibn Shākir narrated to us, Abū Nuʿaym narrated to us, Ḥasan ibn Ṣāliḥ informed us, from Ibn Abī Najīḥ, from Mujāhid, from ʿAlī, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: \He forbade the sale of walāʾ and the gifting of it.\""\n\nIn my copy"," it is stated with the alif (i.e."," he forbade)"," and upon this the text is sound. Its apparent meaning is that ʿAlī"," may Allah be pleased with him"," forbade the sale of walāʾ and the gifting of it. [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"21454","(21448) Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us, al-Shāfiʿī informed us, Mālik informed us, from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar, from ʿĀʾishah, may Allah be pleased with her, that she wished to purchase a slave-girl in order to manumit her. Her owners said: \We shall sell her to you on the condition that her walāʾ shall be for us.\"" She mentioned this to the Messenger of Allah"," peace and blessings be upon him. He said: \""Let that not prevent you"," for indeed the walāʾ belongs to the one who manumits.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muttafaq ʿalayh]"""
"21455","(21449) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad and Muʿammad ibn ʿAbd al-Salām said: Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us. He said: I read it before Mālik, and he mentioned it similarly.\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Ibn Abī Uways, from Mālik, and Muslim narrated it from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"21456","(21450) Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us, al-Shāfiʿī informed us, Mālik informed us, from Hishām ibn ʿUrwah, from his father, from ʿĀʾishah, may Allah be pleased with her, who said: \Barīrah came to me and said: 'I have contracted a mukātabah (manumission contract) with my masters for nine awāq"," one uqiyyah per year. So help me.' ʿĀʾishah said to her: 'If your masters wish"," I will pay it to them in full"," and your walāʾ shall be for me.' Barīrah went to her masters and told them this"," but they refused. She came back from her masters while the Messenger of Allah"," peace and blessings be upon him"," was sitting"," and said: 'I offered them that"," but they refused unless the walāʾ remains for them.' The Messenger of Allah"," peace and blessings be upon him"," heard this and asked her about it. ʿĀʾishah"," may Allah be pleased with her"," informed him. The Messenger of Allah"," peace and blessings be upon him"," said: 'Purchase her and stipulate the walāʾ for them"," for indeed the walāʾ belongs to the one who manumits.' ʿĀʾishah"," may Allah be pleased with her"," did so. Then the Messenger of Allah"," peace and blessings be upon him"," stood among the people and praised Allah"," then said: 'As for what comes after"," what is the matter with men who stipulate conditions that are not in the Book of Allah? Any condition that is not in the Book of Allah is false"," even if it be a hundred conditions. The decree of Allah is more deserving"," and His condition is more binding. Indeed"," the walāʾ belongs to the one who manumits.'\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf and others"," from Mālik. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muttafaq ʿalayh]"""
"21457","(21451) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn al-Naḍr informed us, Muʿāwiyah ibn ʿAmr narrated to us, Zāʾidah informed us, from Simāk, from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Qāsim, from his father, from ʿĀʾishah, may Allah be pleased with her, that she purchased Barīrah from a group of the Anṣār, and they stipulated the walāʾ. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: \The walāʾ belongs to the one who bestowed the favour (of manumission).\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from the ḥadīth of Zāʾidah. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Preceded before it]"""
"21458","(21452) Abū ʿAmr al-Adīb informed us, Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī narrated to us, ʿImrān — that is, ibn Mūsā — narrated to us, ʿUthmān — that is, ibn Abī Shaybah — narrated to us, Wakīʿ informed us, from Sufyān, from Manṣūr, from Ibrāhīm, from al-Aswad, from ʿĀʾishah, may Allah be pleased with her, that she wished to purchase Barīrah, and they stipulated the walāʾ. The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: \Purchase her"," for indeed the walāʾ belongs to the one who paid the price and bestowed the favour (of manumission).\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn Salām"," from Wakīʿ.\n\nAl-Shāfiʿī"," may Allah have mercy upon him"," also cited as evidence in this matter that lineage (nasab) is analogous to walāʾ"," and walāʾ is analogous to lineage. Were a man whose father is unknown to ask another man to attribute him to himself"," and that man agreed"," it would never be permissible for him to be considered his son forever. Rather"," the Messenger of Allah"," peace and blessings be upon him"," said: \""The child belongs to the bed (i.e."," the husband of the mother).\"" Likewise"," if a man does not manumit another"," it is not permissible for the latter to be attributed to him through walāʾ"," thereby wronging his ʿāqilah (tribe of the patron) by burdening them with the payment of blood-wit on his behalf"," and attributing to himself the walāʾ of one he did not manumit. Rather"," the Messenger of Allah"," peace and blessings be upon him"," said: \""The walāʾ belongs to the one who manumits.\"" He said: And His statement"," peace and blessings be upon him"," \""Indeed"," the walāʾ belongs to the one who manumits\"" makes clear that walāʾ belongs exclusively to the one who manumits. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Preceded]"""
"21459","(21453) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Ismāʿīl ibn Aḥmad al-Jurjānī informed us, Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn Mukram narrated to us, ʿUthmān ibn Abī Shaybah narrated to us, Abū Usāmah narrated to us, Idrīs al-Awdī narrated to us, Ṭalḥah ibn Muṣarrif informed us, from Saʿīd ibn Jubayr, from Ibn ʿAbbās, may Allah be pleased with them both, regarding the words of the Almighty: {And those with whom your right hands have made a covenant — give them their share} [al-Nisāʾ 33]. He said: \When the Muhājirūn arrived in Madīnah"," they used to bequeath inheritance to the Anṣār to the exclusion of their blood relatives"," on account of the brotherhood that the Prophet"," peace and blessings be upon him"," established between them. Then this verse was revealed: {And for all"," We have made heirs from what the parents and nearest relatives leave behind} [al-Nisāʾ 33]. That was abrogated. Then He said: {And those with whom your right hands have made a covenant — give them their share} [al-Nisāʾ 33] — from support"," counsel"," and assistance"," and one may bequeath to them"," but the inheritance has ceased.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from al-Ṣalt ibn Muḥammad and others"," from Abū Usāmah.\n\nAnd it has been narrated to us from ʿIkrimah"," from Ibn ʿAbbās"," may Allah be pleased with them both"," who said: {And those with whom your right hands have made a covenant — give them their share} [al-Nisāʾ 33] — \""A man would enter into a pact of alliance (ḥilf) with another man between whom there was no blood relationship"," and one would inherit from the other. Then al-Anfāl abrogated that"," and He said: {And the possessors of kinship are nearer to one another}.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 22922]"""
"21460","(21454) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib narrated to us, Yazid ibn Hārūn informed us, Muḥammad ibn Ṭalḥah ibn Muṣarrif informed us, from Muʿāwiyah ibn Isḥāq, who said: \A man came to the Prophet"," peace and blessings be upon him"," and said: 'So-and-so embraced Islam at my hand.' He said: 'He is your mawlā (client). When you die"," bequeath for him.'\""\n\nThis is a mursal ḥadīth"," and therein is confirmation of the statement of Ibn ʿAbbās regarding the abrogation of the verse of muʿāqadah (covenant) in matters of inheritance. However"," one may bequeath for him and treat him kindly. And Allah knows best. [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"21461","(21455) Abū al-Qāsim ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Muḥammad ibn Shaybān al-ʿAṭṭār informed us in Baghdād: Abū ʿAmr ʿUthmān ibn Aḥmad al-Daqqāq narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn ʿUbayd Allāh ibn al-Munādī narrated to us: Abū Badr narrated to us: ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz narrated to me — from one I do not suspect — from Tamīm al-Dārī, who said: \I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about a man from among the people of disbelief who accepts Islam at the hands of a Muslim man — what is the Sunnah regarding him?\"" He ﷺ said: \""He is the most entitled of all people to him"," in his life and in his death.\"" [Weak]"""
"21462","(21456) He said: And ʿUthmān narrated to us: al-Ḥasan ibn Salām narrated to us: Abū Nuʿaym narrated to us: ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz narrated from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Mawhab, from Tamīm al-Dārī, from the Prophet ﷺ, with a similar meaning. [Weak; it was mentioned before it.]"
"21463","(21457) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān informed us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar informed us: Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān narrated to me: Abū Nuʿaym narrated to us: ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz narrated from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Mawhab, who said: \I heard Tamīm al-Dārī.\""\n\n(Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān said: \""This is an error on the part of Ibn Mawhab; he did not hear from Tamīm"," nor did he meet him.\"") [Error]"""
"21464","(21458) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān informed us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar informed us: Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān narrated to us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Ḥamzah narrated from ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Mawhab, from Qabīṣah ibn Dhūʾayb, from Tamīm al-Dārī, who said: \I asked the Prophet ﷺ: 'What is the Sunnah regarding a man from among the people of disbelief who accepts Islam at the hands of a Muslim man?'\"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \""He is the most entitled of all people to his life and his death.\"" [Weak]"""
"21465","(21459) Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Fārisī informed us: Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Aṣbahānī informed us: Muḥammad ibn Sulaymān ibn Fāris narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Ismāʿīl al-Bukhārī said: Hishām ibn ʿAmmār said to us: Yaḥyā ibn Ḥamzah narrated to us, and he mentioned this hadith with its meaning. Then Muḥammad said: \And some of them said: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Mawhab heard from Tamīm al-Dārī — but this is not correct"," due to the saying of the Prophet ﷺ: 'Indeed"," walāʾ (clientage) belongs only to the one who sets free.'\""\n\n(The Shaykh"," may Allah have mercy on him"," said: And Yazīd ibn Khālid ibn Mawhab al-Ramlī also narrated it from Yaḥyā ibn Ḥamzah.) [Authentic; as reported by al-Bukhārī]"""
"21466","(21460) As Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us: Muḥammad ibn Bakr informed us: Abū Dāwūd narrated to us: Yazīd ibn Khālid ibn Mawhab al-Ramlī and Hishām ibn ʿAmmār narrated to us, both saying: Yaḥyā — meaning Ibn Ḥamzah — narrated from ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn ʿUmar, who said: \I heard ʿAbd Allāh ibn Mawhab narrating to ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz from Qabīṣah ibn Dhūʾayb.\"" Hishām said: \""From Tamīm al-Dārī"," that he said: 'O Messenger of Allah!'\"" And Yazīd said: \""Indeed"," Tamīm said: 'O Messenger of Allah! What is the Sunnah regarding a man who accepts Islam at the hands of a Muslim man?'\"" He ﷺ said: \""He is the most entitled of all people to his life and his death.\""\n\n(The Shaykh"," may Allah have mercy on him"," said: Thus the hadith reverts"," with the mention of Qabīṣah in it"," to being mursal [disconnected].) [Weak]"""
"21467","(21461) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣaghānī informed us: Abū Bakr al-Ḥanafī narrated to us: Yūnus ibn Abī Isḥāq narrated from his father, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Wahb, from Tamīm al-Dārī, that he said: \O Messenger of Allah! A man from among the polytheists accepts Islam at the hands of a Muslim man?\"" He ﷺ said: \""He is the most entitled to him in his life and in his death.\"" That is what Ibn Wahb said. [Weak]"""
"21468","(21462) And Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl informed us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar informed us: Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn al-Muthannā narrated to us: Abū Bakr al-Ḥanafī narrated to us, and he mentioned it, and he said: \ʿAbd Allāh ibn Mawhab.\"""""
"21469","(21463) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm informed us: al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān said: al-Shāfiʿī, may Allah have mercy on him, said regarding this hadith: \It is not established (thābit). It is only narrated by ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn ʿUmar from Ibn Mawhab from Tamīm al-Dārī"," and Ibn Mawhab is not known to us"," and we do not know that he met Tamīm. And something like this is not established according to us"," nor according to you"," because he is majhūl [unknown]"," and I do not know it to be muttaṣil [connected].\"""""
"21470","(21464) Abū Saʿd al-Mālinī informed us: Abū Aḥmad ibn ʿAdī al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: al-Faḍl ibn al-Ḥubāb informed us: Musaddad narrated to us: ʿĪsā ibn Yūnus narrated from Jaʿfar ibn al-Zubayr, from al-Qāsim, from Abī Umāmah, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Whoever accepts Islam at the hands of a man"," his walāʾ (clientage) belongs to him.\""\n\n(Abū Aḥmad said: \""I heard Ibn Ḥammād say: al-Bukhārī said: 'Jaʿfar ibn al-Zubayr al-Shāmī"," from al-Qāsim — he is matrūk al-ḥadīth [abandoned in hadith]; they abandoned him.'\"")\n\n(The Shaykh"," may Allah have mercy on him"," said: And Muʿāwiyah ibn Yaḥyā al-Ṣadafī also narrated it from al-Qāsim"," and Muʿāwiyah ibn Yaḥyā is also weak; no proof is established by him.) [Weak]"""
"21471","(21465) Abu Sa'd al-Malini informed us that Abu Ahmad ibn 'Adiyy informed us that al-Hasan ibn Sufyan narrated to us that Hisham ibn 'Ammar narrated to us that 'Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us that Mu'iyah ibn Yahya narrated on the authority of al-Qasim Abu 'Abd al-Rahmani al-Shami, and he mentioned it. [Da'if]"
"21472","(21466) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us that Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub informed us that Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah ibn 'Abd al-Hakam informed us that Ibn Wahb informed us that Malik ibn Anas narrated on the authority of Nafi', on the authority of 'Abd Allah ibn 'Umar, that 'A'ishah, the wife of the Prophet (peace be upon him), wished to purchase a slave-girl and set her free. Her family said: \We shall sell her to you on the condition that her wala' (clientage) shall remain ours.\"" She mentioned this to the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him)"," and he said: \""Let not that prevent you"," for the wala' belongs only to the one who sets free.\"" Both al-Bukhari and Muslim recorded it in their Sahih collections from the hadith of Malik. [Sahih — Agreed upon]"""
"21473","(21467) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us that Abu al-'Abbas narrated to us that Yahya ibn Abi Talib informed us that Yazid informed us that Hisham narrated on the authority of al-Hasan, who said: \The foundling belongs to the Muslims — his inheritance is theirs and his blood-money is upon them. The one who found him has nothing from him except the reward (of the good deed).\"" [Hasan]"""
"21474","(21468) 'Abd Allah ibn Yusuf informed us that Abu Sa'id ibn al-A'rabi informed us. And Abu al-Husayn ibn Bishran al-'Adl in Baghdad informed us that Isma'il ibn Muhammad al-Saffar informed us — both said: Sa'dan ibn Nasr narrated to us that Sufyan narrated on the authority of al-Zuhri that he heard Sinan, Abu Jamilah, narrating that Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib said: \I found an abandoned child during the time of 'Umar (may Allah be pleased with him). My overseer mentioned it to 'Umar"," so he sent for me. He called me while the overseer was present. When he saw me approaching"," he said: 'Is this he?' — 'Perhaps al-Ghuwayr will bring trouble.' The overseer said: 'O Commander of the Faithful"," he is not under suspicion.' He said: 'Why did you take this child?' He said: 'I found a lost soul"," and I wished that Allah would reward me for it.' He said: 'He is free"," and his wala' is yours"," and his maintenance is upon us.'\""\n\nAl-Shafi'i (may Allah have mercy on him) responded to this by saying: \""This is not something that can be established by such a report"," for it comes from a man who is not well-known — meaning Abu Jamilah. Then he continued his discourse until he said: 'The established Sunnah has come that the wala' belongs only to the one who sets free"," and it is possible that a hadith from the Prophet (peace be upon him) was unknown to some of his Companions"," and no one — even if they were numerous alongside the Prophet (peace be upon him) — constitutes an independent proof.'\"" [Da'if]"""
"21475","(21469) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us that Abu 'Abd Allah Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us that Yahya ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us that Abu 'Umar narrated to us that Shu'bah narrated on the authority of al-Hakam, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of al-Aswad, on the authority of 'A'ishah (may Allah be pleased with her), regarding the story of Barirah, that she said: \The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: 'Buy her and set her free"," for the wala' belongs to the one who sets free.'\""\n\nAl-Bukhari recorded it in his Sahih from Abu 'Umar.\n\nAl-Shafi'i (may Allah have mercy on him) said: \""The Prophet (peace be upon him) did not single out one of them over the other. And if the freed person dies"," his mawla (the one who freed him) does not inherit from him if the two differ in religion.\"" [Sahih — Agreed upon]"""
"21476","(21470) He cited as evidence what Abu 'Ali al-Rudhbari and Abu al-Husayn ibn Bishran al-'Adl informed us — both said: Isma'il ibn Muhammad al-Saffar narrated to us that Sa'dan ibn Nasr narrated to us that Sufyan narrated on the authority of al-Zuhri, on the authority of 'Ali ibn Husayn, on the authority of 'Amr ibn 'Uthman, on the authority of Usamah ibn Zayd, that it reached the Prophet (peace be upon him) that he said: \A Muslim does not inherit from a disbeliever"," and a disbeliever does not inherit from a Muslim.\""\n\nMuslim recorded it in his Sahih from Yahya ibn Yahya and others"," from Sufyan. And al-Bukhari recorded it through another chain from al-Zuhri. [Sahih — Agreed upon]"""
"21477","(21471) Abu Nasr ibn Qatadah informed us that Abu 'Amr ibn Najid narrated to us that Muhammad ibn Ibrahim narrated to us that Ibn Bukayr narrated to us that Malik narrated on the authority of Yahya ibn Sa'id, on the authority of Isma'il ibn Abi Hakim, that 'Umar ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz freed a Christian slave of his, and the slave died. Isma'il said: \'Umar ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz ordered me to take his inheritance and place it in the Bayt al-Mal (public treasury).\"" [Sahih — Recorded by Malik]"""
"21478","(21472) 'Ali ibn Ahmad ibn 'Abdan informed us that Ahmad ibn 'Ubaid al-Saffar narrated to us that 'Ubayd ibn Sharik and Ibn Milhan both narrated to us that Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated to us that al-Layth narrated. And Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us that Abu 'Abd Allah Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us that Muhammad ibn Shadhan and Ahmad ibn Salamah both narrated to us that Qutaybah narrated to us that al-Layth ibn Sa'd narrated on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of 'Urwah, that 'A'ishah (may Allah be pleased with her) informed him that Barirah came to 'A'ishah seeking her help regarding her kitabah (contract of manumission), and she had not yet paid anything of her kitabah. 'A'ishah said to her: \Return to your family. If they wish that I pay your kitabah on your behalf and that the wala' be mine"," I shall do so.\"" Barirah mentioned this to her family"," but they refused and said: \""If she wishes to seek reward for herself"," let her do so"," but the wala' shall be ours.\"" She mentioned this to the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him)"," and the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said to her: \""Buy her and set her free"," for the wala' belongs only to the one who sets free.\"" Then the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) stood up and said: \""What is the matter with people who stipulate conditions that are not in the Book of Allah? Whoever stipulates a condition that is not in the Book of Allah"," it is not valid for him"," even if he stipulates a hundred conditions. The conditions of Allah are more deserving of being fulfilled and more binding.\""\n\nAl-Bukhari and Muslim both recorded it in their Sahih collections from Qutaybah ibn Sa'id. [Sahih — Agreed upon]"""
"21479","(21473) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz and Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr both narrated to us that Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us that Yahya ibn Abi Talib informed us that Yazid ibn Harun informed us that Sufyan ibn Sa'id narrated on the authority of Abu Qays, on the authority of Huzayl ibn Shurahbil, who said: \A man came to 'Abd Allah — meaning Ibn Mas'ud — and said: 'I freed my slave and made him a saibah (one set free without designated clientage). He died and left behind wealth.' 'Abd Allah said: 'The people of Islam do not set slaves as saibah; rather"," it was the people of the Jahiliyyah who used to do so. You are his heir and the one entitled to his wala'. If you feel any scruple about something"," then bring it and we shall place it in the Bayt al-Mal.'\""\n\nAl-Bukhari recorded it in his Sahih in an abridged form from Qabisah"," from Sufyan. And al-Sha'bi"," al-Nakha'i"," and others narrated it from 'Abd Allah ibn Mas'ud in a mursal (disconnected) and abridged form. It was also narrated from 'Alqamah"," from 'Abd Allah"," in a musnad (connected) form"," and in his version he said: \""If you refuse"," then here are many heirs","\"" and he placed it in the Bayt al-Mal. [Sahih — Bukhari 6753]"""
"21480","(21474) And in what Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz permitted me to narrate from him, he narrated to us that Abu al-'Abbas informed us that al-Rabi' informed us that al-Shafi'i informed us that Sufyan informed me that Abu Tawalah 'Abd Allah ibn 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Ma'mar said: \Salim"," the mawla of Abu Hudhayfah"," was the mawla of a woman from the Ansar called 'Amrah ibn Ya'far"," who had freed him as a saibah. He was killed on the day of al-Yamamah. His inheritance was brought to Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him)"," and he said: 'Give it to 'Amrah.' But she refused to accept it.\"" [Da'if]"""
"21481","(21475) Abu 'Abd Allah, the hafiz, informed us that Abu al-Walid related to us that 'Abd Allah ibn Muhammad and Ja'far ibn Ahmad both related to us that 'Amr ibn Zurarah related to us from Isma'il ibn Ayyub and Salamah ibn 'Alqamah from Muhammad ibn Sirin, who said: I was informed that Salim, the freedman of Abu Hudhayfah, was emancipated by a woman of the Ansar who said, \Go and attach yourself as a patron (wala') to whomever you wish.\"" So Salim took Abu Hudhayfah as his patron. When he was struck down (i.e."," died as a martyr)"," they disputed over his inheritance"," and so his inheritance was assigned to the Ansar. [Da'if]"""
"21482","(21476) Abu al-Husayn ibn al-Fadd al-Qattan informed us in Baghdad that 'Abd Allah ibn Ja'far related to us that Ya'qub ibn Sufyan related to us that Muhammad ibn Mansur related to us that Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim ibn Sa'd related to us that his father related to us from Ibn Ishaq — 'Abd Allah ibn Abi Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn 'Amr ibn Hazm related to me that 'Abd Allah ibn Wuday'ah ibn Khidam ibn Khalid, the brother of Banu 'Amr ibn 'Awf, said: Salim, the freedman of Abu Hudhayfah, was in fact the freedman of a woman from among us named Salmayah bint Ya'ar. She had emancipated him as a sa'ibah (a freed slave set at large) during the pre-Islamic period (Jahiliyyah). When he was struck down at al-Yamamah, 'Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, was brought his inheritance. He summoned Wuday'ah ibn Khidam and said, \This is the inheritance of your freedman; you have the greatest right to it.\"" Wuday'ah said"," \""O Commander of the Faithful"," Allah has rendered us independent of it. Our companion emancipated him as a sa'ibah"," and we have no desire to derive any benefit from his affair\"" — or he said"," \""to receive any share.\"" So 'Umar"," may Allah be pleased with him"," placed it in the public treasury (Bayt al-Mal). [Da'if]"""
"21483","(21477) Abu Tahir al-Faqih informed us that Abu Hamid ibn Bilal related to us that Abu al-Azhar related to us that Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim ibn Sa'd mentioned it with its chain of transmission and its meaning in elevated form, and said at the end of it: \And he called for Wuday'ah ibn Khidam"," who was the heir of Salmayah bint Ya'ar"," and said"," 'This is the inheritance of your freedman; take it.' Wuday'ah said"," 'O Commander of the Faithful"," our companion emancipated him as a sa'ibah for her parents"," and Allah has rendered us independent of it. We have no need of it.'\"" He said: \""So 'Umar"," may Allah be pleased with him"," placed it in the treasury of the Muslims (Bayt Mal al-Muslimin).\""\n\nAnd Abu Bakr ibn Abi al-Jahm narrated it with the same meaning from 'Urwah ibn al-Zubayr. [Da'if; previously referenced]"""
"21484","(21478) Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn al-Hasan related to us that Abu al-'Abbas al-Aṣamm informed us that al-Rabi' informed us that al-Shafi'i informed us that Sufyan ibn 'Uyaynah related to us from Ibn Jurayj from 'Ata' ibn Abi Rabah that Tariq ibn al-Muratta' emancipated an entire household as sa'ibah (slaves set at large). Their inheritance was brought before 'Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, and he said, \Give it to the heirs of Tariq.\"" But they refused to accept it. So 'Umar said"," \""Then distribute it among people of similar status.\"" [Da'if]"""
"21485","(21479) And Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr related to us that Abu al-'Abbas informed us that al-Rabi' informed us that al-Shafi'i informed us that Muslim and Sa'id ibn Salim related to us from Ibn Jurayj from 'Ata' that Tariq ibn al-Muratta' emancipated entire households from the people of Yemen as sa'ibah, and they separated from some ten thousand (i.e., a large number of people). This was mentioned to 'Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, and he ordered that it be given to Tariq or to the heirs of Tariq.\n\nAl-Shafi'i, may Allah have mercy on him, said: I have doubt regarding this hadith in this manner. [Da'if; previously referenced]"
"21486","(21480) And Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz and Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr both related to us that Abu al-'Abbas — Muhammad ibn Ya'qub — related to us that Yahya ibn Abi Talib informed us that Yazid ibn Harun informed us that 'Uqbah ibn 'Abd Allah al-Aṣamm related to us from 'Ata' ibn Abi Rabah that Tariq emancipated a man as a sa'ibah. The sa'ibah died and left behind wealth, and his wealth was brought to the governor of Makkah. He sent word to Tariq and offered his wealth to him, but Tariq refused to accept it. So the governor of Makkah wrote to 'Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, and 'Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, wrote back: \Gather the wealth and offer it to Tariq. If he accepts it"," give it to him. If he does not accept it"," then purchase slaves with it and emancipate them.\"" He said: \""So it was offered to Tariq"," and he did not accept it. So he purchased with it fifteen or sixteen slaves and emancipated them.\"" 'Uqbah said: \""It was as though I could see 'Ata' counting on his fingers — fifteen or sixteen.\""\n\nAnd Qatadah and Qays ibn Sa'd narrated from 'Ata' regarding it that Ya'li ibn Munyah wrote to 'Umar ibn al-Khattab"," may Allah be pleased with him"," and 'Umar ibn al-Khattab"," may Allah be pleased with him"," wrote that he (Tariq) had the greatest right to his inheritance.\n\nAl-Shafi'i"," may Allah have mercy on him"," said: It is as though 'Ata' heard it directly from Tariq. And if he did not hear it from him"," then the hadith of Sulayman ibn Yasar is mursal (disconnected).\n\nThe Shaykh"," may Allah have mercy on him"," said — meaning regarding what was narrated by those who differed from him on this issue from Sulayman ibn Yasar — that a sa'ibah was emancipated by a man among the pilgrims"," and a slave from Banu Makhzum fatally struck him. 'Umar"," may Allah be pleased with him"," ruled that the blood money (diyah) was upon them. [The narrator] said: \""What if he had struck my son?\"" He said: \""Then nothing would be upon him.\"" He said: \""He is then like al-Arqam: if he is thrown"," he devours; and if he is killed"," he is avenged.\"" 'Umar"," may Allah be pleased with him"," said: \""Then he is"," by Allah"," like al-Arqam.\"" [Da'if; previously referenced]"""
"21487","(21481) Abu Tahir al-Faqih informed us that Abu Hamid ibn Bilal related to us that Abu al-Azhar related to us that Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim ibn Sa'd related to us that his father related to us from Ibn Ishaq — Abu al-Zinad 'Abd Allah ibn Dhakwan related to me that Sulayman ibn Yasar said: 'Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, arrived in Makkah while he was caliph, and a case was brought before him: a man had emancipated a sa'ibah, and the sa'ibah had killed the son of al-Sa'ib ibn 'A'ish ibn 'Abd Allah ibn 'Umar ibn Makhzum by mistake. The sa'ibah's master (i.e., the one who had emancipated him) sought the blood money (diyah) for his son from 'Umar ibn al-Khattab. 'Umar said: \If the sa'ibah has wealth"," let him pay the blood money for your son from his wealth"," in full.\"" The sa'ibah's master said: \""And if he has no wealth?\"" 'Umar"," may Allah be pleased with him"," said: \""Then you have nothing.\"" The sa'ibah's master said: \""What if we killed him by mistake?\"" He said: \""Then"," by Allah"," you shall pay the blood money.\"" He said: \""So if he is killed"," the blood money is paid; but if he kills"," the blood money is not paid on his behalf?\"" 'Umar"," may Allah be pleased with him"," said: \""Yes.\"" He said: \""Then he is like al-Arqam: if something is thrown at him"," he swallows it; and if he is killed"," he is avenged.\"" 'Umar"," may Allah be pleased with him"," said: \""Then he is"," by Allah"," exactly that.\"" So he was not given anything.\n\nAl-Shafi'i"," may Allah have mercy on him"," said: This"," according to our position"," if it is established"," is ambiguous (ashbah)"," for if he had seen the wala' as belonging to the Muslims"," he would have seen the blood money upon them. But it is ambiguous that the blood money was upon his mawali (freed slaves)"," and since they were not identifiable"," he did not see any blood money until his mawali could be identified.\n\nThe Shaykh"," may Allah have mercy on him"," said: What indicates the soundness of this interpretation is… [Da'if]"""
"21488","(21482) Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn 'Ali al-Aṣbahani al-Hafiz informed us that Ibrahim ibn 'Abd Allah al-Aṣbahani informed us that Isma'il ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Harith al-Qattan informed us that al-Hasan ibn 'Isa informed us that Ibn al-Mubarak informed us that 'Abd Allah ibn 'Uqbah related to us from 'Abd Allah ibn Hubayrah from Qabisah ibn Dhubayb, who said: When a man would emancipate a sa'ibah, he would not inherit from him; and if the sa'ibah committed an offense, the blood money would be upon the one who emancipated him. So they came to 'Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, and said: \O Commander of the Faithful"," grant us justice — either the blood money is upon you and the inheritance is yours"," or the inheritance is ours and the blood money is upon us.\"" So 'Umar"," may Allah be pleased with him"," ruled that the inheritance was for them.\n\nAl-Shafi'i said: And the hadith of Sulayman ibn Yasar from 'Umar"," may Allah be pleased with him"," is munqati' (disconnected). [Da'if]"""
"21489","(21483) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz and Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr both related to us that Abu al-'Abbas — Muhammad ibn Ya'qub — related to us that Yahya ibn Abi Talib informed us that Yazid ibn Harun informed us that Sulayman al-Taymi informed us that Abu 'Uthman al-Nahdi said: 'Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, said: \Sadaqah (charity) and sa'ibah (emancipation) are for the Day of theirs\"" — i.e."," the Day of Judgment. [Sahih]"""
"21490","(21484) Abu 'Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami informed us that Abu al-Hasan al-Karizi informed us that 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz said: Abu 'Ubayd said — meaning by his statement \for the Day of theirs\"" — the Day of Resurrection"," the day on which he emancipated his sa'ibah and gave his sadaqah"," saying: \""He shall not return to derive any benefit from either of them thereafter in this world.\"" This is like the man who emancipates his slave as a sa'ibah"," and then the emancipated slave dies and leaves behind wealth and has no heir except the one who emancipated him. He says: \""It is not fitting for him to receive anything from his inheritance"," nor to receive anything from the inheritance of the sa'ibah"," except that he should put it in a similar cause.\""\n\nAnd similarly it is narrated from Ibn 'Umar. And this from them is by way of virtue (fadl) and reward (thawab)"," not by way of it being forbidden (haram). [Sahih]"""
"21491","(21485) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr narrated to us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās narrated to us, saying: Yaḥyā narrated to us, saying: Yazīd informed us, saying: Sulaymān al-Taymī informed us from Bakr ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Muzanī, that the estate of a freed slave belonging to Ibn ʿUmar was brought to him. He said: \We only set him free as a *sāʾiba* (one released without ties of *walāʾ*).\"" He then ordered that slaves be purchased with that wealth and freed on his behalf"," i.e."," that they be manumitted. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"21492","(21486) Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn ʿAlī al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, saying: Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Aṣbahānī informed us, saying: Ismāʿīl ibn Ibrāhīm al-Qaṭṭān narrated to us, saying: al-Ḥasan ibn ʿĪsā narrated to us, saying: Ibn al-Mubārak informed us, saying: ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUqbah informed us from Ibn Hubayrah, from Ziyād ibn Nuʿaym, who informed him: He was sitting with Ibn ʿUmar when a man came to him with a purse of silver. They said: \So-and-so"," your father's freed slave"," has passed away"," and he instructed me to deliver this to you.\"" Ibn ʿUmar said: \""Woe to him! Why did he not spend it in the cause of Allah?\"" Then the messenger of ʿĀṣim ibn ʿUmar came"," saying: \""Send me the inheritance from your father's freed slave.\"" So he sent the entirety of it to him. Ibn ʿUmar did not inherit from a *sāʾiba*"," and ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) had freed that slave as a *sāʾiba*.\n\nThe Shaykh (may Allah have mercy on him) said: \""If this is authentic"," it indicates that he did not consider it unlawful (*ḥarām*)"," for had he considered it unlawful"," he would have prevented his brother ʿĀṣim from it"," just as he abstained from it himself. However"," he preferred to keep away from it"," and Allah knows best.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"21493","(21487) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yaḥyā ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār al-Sukkarī informed us in Baghdad, saying: Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār narrated to us, saying: ʿAbbās ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Tarqafī narrated to us, saying: Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Muqriʾ narrated to us, saying: Shuʿbah narrated to us from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Abū ʿAmr al-Shaybānī, who said: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Masʿūd said: \The *sāʾiba* may dispose of his wealth wherever he wishes.\""\n\nShuʿbah said: \""No one other than me heard this from Salamah.\""\n\nThe Shaykh (may Allah have mercy on him) said: \""It is possible that he meant that he may dispose of it during his lifetime wherever he wishes"," because his former master would refrain from taking his wealth after his death. And Allah knows best.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"21494","(21488) Abū ʿAmr al-Adīb informed us, saying: Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī informed us, saying: Ibn Nājiʿah informed me, saying: Muḥammad ibn ʿUthmān ibn Karāmah and Aḥmad ibn ʿUthmān ibn Ḥakīm both narrated to us, saying: ʿUbayd Allāh — meaning Ibn Mūsā — narrated to us, from Isrāʾīl, from Abū Ḥuṣayn, from Abū Ṣāliḥ, from Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \I am closer to the believers than their own selves. Whoever dies and leaves behind wealth"," it belongs to his heirs (*mawālī al-ʿaṣabah*)"," and whoever leaves behind debt or dependents"," then I am his guardian"," and I will provide for him.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in *al-Ṣaḥīḥ* from Maḥmūd"," from ʿUbayd Allāh. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muttafaq ʿalayh]"""
"21495","(21489) Others narrated from ʿUbayd Allāh: \Whoever leaves behind wealth"," it belongs for his heirs (*mawālihi*).\"" Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us"," saying: Abū al-Walīd narrated to us"," saying: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad narrated to us"," saying: Isḥāq — meaning al-Ḥanẓalī — informed us"," saying: ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Mūsā informed us"," and he mentioned it. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Preceded before it]"""
"21496","(21490) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr narrated to us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, saying: Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib informed us, saying: Yazīd ibn Hārūn informed us, saying: Sufyān narrated to us from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Shaddād, that the daughter of Ḥamzah ibn ʿAbd al-Muṭṭalib had a freed slave whom she manumitted. The freed slave died, leaving behind a daughter and his freedwoman — the daughter of Ḥamzah. This matter was raised to the Prophet (ﷺ), and he gave the daughter half and gave the freedwoman — the daughter of Ḥamzah — half.\n\nThis is a *mursal* narration. It has been narrated through other chains as *mursal*, some of which corroborate others. Its evidences have preceded along with the statements of ʿAlī and Zayd (may Allah be pleased with them both) on the matter in the book of *al-Farāʾiḍ*. [Ḍaʿīf]"
"21497","(21491) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzakkī informed us, saying: Abū ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, saying: Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Wahhāb informed us, saying: Jaʿfar ibn ʿAwn informed us, saying: Misʿar narrated to us from ʿImrān ibn Riyāḥ, from Ibn Maʿqil, who said: ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) said: \Walāʾ is a branch of bondage. Whoever secures walāʾ has secured inheritance.\"" [Ḥasan]"""
"21498","(21492) Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī narrated to us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, saying: al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us, saying: al-Shāfiʿī informed us, saying: Mālik informed us from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Abī Bakr, from ʿAbd al-Malik ibn Abī Bakr ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Ḥārith ibn Hishām, from his father, who informed him: al-ʿĀṣ ibn Hishām died and left behind three sons — two from one mother and one from another. One of the two sons from the same mother died, leaving behind wealth and freed slaves. His full brother (from both mother and father) inherited his wealth and the walāʾ of his freed slaves. Then the one who had inherited the wealth and the walāʾ of the freed slaves died, leaving behind a son and his brother (from his father). The son said: \I have secured what my father secured of the wealth and the walāʾ of the freed slaves.\"" His brother said: \""It is not so. You have only secured the wealth. As for the walāʾ of the freed slaves"," I do not think so — if my brother were to die today"," would I not inherit from him?\"" They took their dispute to ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān (may Allah be pleased with him)"," and he ruled in favor of his brother regarding the walāʾ of the freed slaves. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Mālik]"""
"21499","(21493) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, saying: Abū al-Walīd narrated to us, saying: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad narrated to us, saying: Bundār narrated to us, saying: Abū Aḥmad al-Zubayrī narrated to us, from Sufyān, from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd, from Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyab, that ʿUmar and ʿUthmān (may Allah be pleased with them both) said: \Walāʾ belongs to the eldest.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"21500","(21494) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, saying: Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib informed us, saying: Yazīd ibn Hārūn informed us, saying: al-Ashʿath ibn Sawwār informed us, from al-Shaʿbī, who said: ʿUmar, ʿAlī, and Zayd ibn Thābit (may Allah be pleased with them) — and I think he also mentioned ʿAbd Allāh (may Allah be pleased with him) — used to say: \Walāʾ belongs to the eldest (*al-akbar*).\"" He said: \""By *al-akbar*"," he means the closest of them in lineage.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"21501","(21495) Abu 'Abd Allah narrated to us, Abu al-'Abbas narrated to us, Yahya narrated to us, Yazid narrated to us, Sufyan al-Thawri narrated from Mansur, from Ibrahim, who said: 'Umar, 'Abd Allah, and Zayd (may Allah be pleased with them) said: \Al-wala' belongs to the elder.\"" [Sahih]"""
"21502","(21496) And Yazid narrated to us, Shu'bah ibn al-Hajjaj narrated from al-Mughirah, from Ibrahim, that 'Ali, 'Abd Allah, and Zayd (may Allah be pleased with them) said: \Al-wala' belongs to the elder.\""\n\nIt is also narrated from Zayd ibn Wahb"," from 'Ali"," 'Abd Allah"," and Zayd (may Allah be pleased with them). [Sahih. Previously cited.]"""
"21503","(21497) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz narrated to us, Abu al-Walid narrated to us, 'Abd Allah ibn Muhammad narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn 'Isa narrated from Ibn al-Mubarak, from Ma'mar, from Abu Hashim, from al-Nakha'i, that 'Ali and Zayd (may Allah be pleased with them both) said regarding a man who left a full brother (a brother from his father and mother) and a paternal half-brother: they assigned the wala' to his full brother (from his father and mother). If the paternal half-brother were to die, the wala' would revert to the sons of the full brother (from the father and mother). [Sahih. Previously cited.]"
"21504","(21498) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz narrated to us, Abu al-'Abbas narrated to us, Yahya narrated to us, Yazid narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Salim narrated from al-Sha'bi, that 'Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) said: \When a woman frees a male or female slave"," and she dies leaving a male child"," the wala' of that freed slave belongs to her children"," so long as they are males. When the males cease"," the wala' reverts to her patrons (awliya').\""\n\nAnd Shurayh said: \""The wala' proceeds in its course"," just as inheritance proceeds"," but the wala' is not inherited by a female except for something she herself freed.\"" [Da'if]"""
"21505","(21499) Abu Nasr ibn Qatadah narrated to us, Abu 'Amr ibn Nujayd narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Ibn Bukayr narrated to us, Malik narrated from 'Abd Allah ibn Abi Bakr, that his father informed him: He was sitting with Aban ibn 'Uthman ibn 'Affan when a group from Juhaynah and a group from Banu al-Harith ibn al-Khazraj came to him with a dispute. A woman from Juhaynah had been married to a man from Banu al-Harith ibn al-Khazraj, called Ibrahim ibn Kulayb. The woman died, leaving wealth and freed slaves (mawali). Her son and her husband inherited from her. Then her son died. The heirs of her son said: \The wala' of the freed slaves belongs to us"," for her son had secured it.\"" The Juhaynites said: \""It is not so. Rather"," they are the freed slaves of our companion. When her son dies"," their wala' belongs to us"," and we inherit from them.\"" So Aban ibn 'Uthman ruled in favor of the Juhaynites regarding the wala' of the freed slaves. [Sahih]"""
"21506","(21500) And with his chain of narration, Malik narrated that it reached him that Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab said regarding a man who died and left three sons and freed slaves whom he had manumitted, then two of his sons died, leaving children: Sa'id said: \The remaining one of the three inherits the freed slaves. When he dies"," his children and the children of his brothers are equal partners in the freed slaves (by right of the wala').\"" A mursal hadith has been narrated concerning this which confirms the preceding narrations. [Da'if]"""
"21507","(21501) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz narrated to us, Abu al-Walid narrated to us, 'Abd Allah ibn Muhammad narrated to us. He said: Abu 'Abd Allah, meaning Muhammad ibn Nasr, narrated to us, Mahmud ibn Adam narrated to us, Bishr ibn al-Sari narrated to us, Sa'id ibn 'Abd al-Rahman al-Jumahi narrated from Yunus, from al-Zuhri, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: \The freed slave (mawla) is a brother in faith and a blessing. The most deserving of people regarding his inheritance is the one closest to the one who freed him.\"" [Da'if]"""
"21508","(21502) Abu 'Ali al-Rawdhbari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, Abu Dawud narrated to us, 'Abd Allah ibn 'Amr ibn Abi al-Hajjaj, Abu Ma'mar, narrated to us, al-Warith narrated to us, Husayn al-Mu'allim narrated from 'Amr ibn Shu'ayb, from his father, from his grandfather, that Riyab ibn Hudhayfah married a woman who bore him three boys. Their mother died, and they inherited her estates and the wala' of her freed slaves. 'Amr ibn al-'As was the 'asabah (agnatic heir) of her sons. He took them to Syria, where they died. Then 'Amr ibn al-'As came, and a freed slave of hers died, leaving wealth. Her brothers brought a claim against him before 'Umar ibn al-Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him). 'Umar said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: \Whatever a child or parent secures"," it belongs to his 'asabah"," whoever it may be.\"" He (the narrator) said: \""So I wrote a document for him containing the testimony of 'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Awf"," Zayd ibn Thabit (may Allah be pleased with them both)"," and another man. When 'Abd al-Malik was appointed as caliph"," they brought their dispute before Hisham ibn Isma'il or Isma'il ibn Hisham"," and he referred it to 'Abd al-Malik. He said: 'This is a ruling that I consider sound.' So he ruled in us according to the document of 'Umar ibn al-Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him)"," and we remain upon it to this day.\""\n\n(T) The Shaykh (may Allah have mercy on him) said: \""Thus it is in this narration. We have narrated from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab"," from 'Umar ibn al-Khattab and 'Uthman ibn 'Affan (may Allah be pleased with them both)"," that they said: 'Al-wala' belongs to the elder.' And the mursal narration of Ibn al-Musayyab from 'Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) is more authentic than the narration of 'Amr ibn Shu'ayb. As for the marfu' hadith contained therein"," it does not contain the Prophet (peace be upon him) saying that specifically regarding the wala'.\"" [Hasan]"""
"21509","(21503) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz and Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr both narrated to us, saying: Abu al-'Abbas, Muhammad ibn Ya'qub, narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abi Talib narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun informed us, Sufyan al-Thawri and Sharik narrated from 'Imran ibn Muslim ibn Riyah, from 'Abd Allah ibn Ma'qil, who said: I heard 'Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) say: \Al-wala' is a branch of lineage. Whoever secures the inheritance has secured the wala'.\""\n\nThus I found it in this narration"," and it is an error. It is as though Yazid conflated the narration of al-Thawri with the narration of Sharik"," and Sharik was mistaken in it"," or Yazid was mistaken in it"," or someone below him. [Hasan]"""
"21510","(21504) Rather, the wording of the hadith is as Abu al-Husayn ibn al-Fadl al-Qattan informed us, 'Abd Allah ibn Ja'far ibn Durustawayh narrated to us, Ya'qub ibn Sufyan narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym and Qabisah narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated from 'Imran ibn Muslim ibn Riyah, from 'Abd Allah ibn Ma'qil, who said: 'Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) said: \Al-wala' is a branch of bondage (al-riqq). Whoever secures the wala' has secured the inheritance.\""\n\nThis is the correct version. Likewise"," Mis'ar narrated it from 'Imran. Its meaning is: whoever has the wala' has the inheritance through the wala'. [Hasan]"""
"21511","(21505) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz and Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr informed us, they said: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us: Yahya ibn Abi Talib informed us: Yazid ibn Harun informed us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated from Hisham ibn 'Urwah from his father, who said: Al-Zubayr ibn al-'Awwam, may Allah be pleased with him, said: The wala' (patronage) is gathered by the one who gathers the inheritance.\n\nThis may be interpreted as meaning that the one who gathers the inheritance — namely the 'asabah (residuary heir) who takes the entirety of the estate — is the one who takes the wala' to the exclusion of the ashab al-furudh (fixed-share heirs). And Allah knows best. [Hasan]"
"21512","(21506) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us: Abu al-Walid narrated to us: Ja'far ibn Ahmad narrated to us: 'Amr ibn Zurarah narrated to us: Isma'il narrated from Ayyub from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, who said: A son of 'Abd Allah ibn 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakr contested with al-Qasim ibn Muhammad before Ibn al-Zubayr regarding the inheritance of a mawla (freed slave) of 'A'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her. So Ibn al-Zubayr ruled that the inheritance belonged to the son of 'Abd Allah ibn 'Abd al-Rahman — for 'Abd al-Rahman was the full brother of 'A'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her, through her mother and her father, while Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr was her brother only through her father, not through her mother — so he awarded it to the son of 'Abd Allah ibn 'Abd al-Rahman, because 'Abd Allah died after 'A'ishah, so his son secured what his father had secured of the wala'. And whoever says that the wala' belongs to the elder, then he assigned it to al-Qasim ibn Muhammad. And it has been reported from al-Qasim that he rejected that ruling of Ibn al-Zubayr. [Sahih]"
"21513","(21507) Abu Zakariyya ibn Abi Ishaq and Abu Bakr ibn al-Hasan said: Abu al-'Abbas, that is al-Asamm, informed us: Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah ibn 'Abd al-Hakam informed us: Ibn Wahb informed me: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated from Muhammad ibn Zayd ibn al-Muhajir, who said: He was present when al-Qasim ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr and Talhah ibn 'Abd Allah ibn 'Abd al-Rahman were disputing before Ibn al-Zubayr regarding the inheritance of Abu 'Amr, a mawla of 'A'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her. And 'Abd Allah was the heir of 'A'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her, to the exclusion of al-Qasim, because her father was her brother through both her mother and her father, while Muhammad was her brother only through her father. Then 'Abd Allah died, and his son Talhah inherited him. Then Abu 'Amr died, so 'Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr ruled in favour of Talhah. He said: I heard al-Qasim ibn Muhammad saying: \Subhan Allah! The mawla is not merely abandoned wealth to be inherited by whoever inherits him; rather"," the mawla is an 'asabah (residuary heir).\""\n\nAnd Ibn Jurayj narrated from 'Ata': that Ibn al-Zubayr's inheritance of the son of 'Abd Allah ibn 'Abd al-Rahman to the exclusion of al-Qasim — 'Ata'"," may Allah have mercy upon him"," said: He used to criticise that ruling of Ibn al-Zubayr"," may Allah have mercy upon them all. [Da'if]"""
"21514","(21508) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us: Abu al-Walid narrated to us: 'Abd Allah ibn Muhammad narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Yusuf narrated to us: Sufyan narrated from Ibn Jurayj from 'Ata', regarding a man who died leaving behind his brother and his grandfather, he said: The wala' is shared between the grandfather and the brother. [Sahih]"
"21515","(21509) And Abu 'Abd Allah informed us: Abu al-Walid narrated to us: 'Abd Allah ibn Muhammad said: Abu 'Abd Allah narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us: Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us: Abu Bakr narrated to me: Makhul, Rashid, Damrah, and 'Atiyyah narrated from Zayd ibn Thabit, who said: The grandfather has a stronger right than the son of the brother and the paternal uncle, and the people act upon that. [Sahih]"
"21516","(21510) Abu 'Amr Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah al-Adib informed us: Abu Bakr al-Isma'ili narrated to us: 'Ubayd Allah ibn Musa narrated to us: 'Abd al-A'la narrated to us: Wuhib narrated from 'Abd Allah ibn Tawus from Ibn 'Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: \Assign the fixed shares to their respective recipients; whatever remains is for the nearest male residuary heir.\""\n\nAl-Bukhari narrated it in his Sahih from Muslim ibn Ibrahim and others from Wuhib"," and Muslim narrated it from 'Abd al-A'la ibn Hammad.\n\nThis indicates that the one who takes through ta'sib (residuary inheritance) is exclusively a man"," except where a specific Sunnah has designated otherwise. And he"," peace and blessings be upon him"," said regarding the manumission of Barirah by 'A'ishah: \""The wala' belongs to the one who manumits.\"" This indicates that she inherits the wala'."""
"21517","(21511) Abu Tahir al-Faqih informed us: Abu Bakr al-Qattan narrated to us: Abu al-Azhar narrated to us: Yahya ibn Isma'il narrated to us: 'Abd al-Salam narrated from al-Harith ibn Husayn from Zayd ibn Wahb from 'Ali, 'Abd Allah, and Zayd ibn Thabit, may Allah be pleased with them: They used to assign the wala' to the eldest among the 'asabah (residuary heirs) and did not make women inherit from the wala' except what they themselves manumitted, or what the one whom they had manumitted manumitted. [Sahih]"
"21518","(21512) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us: Abu al-Walid narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn 'Ali narrated to us: Yahya ibn Yahya informed us: 'Abd al-Salam narrated from al-A'mash from Ibrahim, who said: 'Umar, 'Ali, and Zayd ibn Thabit used not to make women inherit from the wala' except what they manumitted. [Da'if]"
"21519","(21513) He said: And Abu al-Walid informed us: 'Abd Allah narrated to us: Ishaq informed us: 'Abd al-Salam narrated something similar to that."
"21520","(21514) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz narrated to us: Abu al-'Abbas, that is al-Asamm, narrated to us: Yahya ibn Abi Talib narrated to us: Yazid ibn Harun informed us: Hisham ibn Hassan narrated from Muhammad ibn Sirin, who said: Women do not inherit anything from the wala' except what they have contracted through mukatabah (a contract of manumission) or what they have manumitted.\n\nYazid said: And I heard Sufyan al-Thawri saying: \Women do not inherit anything from the wala' except what they have contracted through mukatabah"," or what they have manumitted"," or what the one whom they have manumitted has manumitted"," or the one whom they have manumitted has brought his wala' to them.\"" [Hasan]"""
"21521","(21515) Abū al-Ḥasan al-Raffāʾ informed us, ʿUthmān ibn Muḥammad ibn Bashr narrated to us, Ismāʿīl al-Qāḍī narrated to us, Ibn Abī Uways and ʿĪsā ibn Mīnāʾ both said: Ibn Abī al-Zinād narrated from his father, from the jurists of the people of Madīnah, who used to say: A woman does not inherit any walāʾ from any of her relatives, and she inherits walāʾ only from those whom she herself manumitted, or from those with whom she contracted mukātabah and who were thereby freed, or the walāʾ of a slave whom she manumitted. [Weak]"
"21522","(21516) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzakkī informed us, Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Wahhāb informed us, Jaʿfar ibn ʿAwn informed us, al-Aʿmash narrated from Ibrāhīm, who said: ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: When a free woman is under a slave and bears him a child, the child is freed by the freeing of his mother, and his walāʾ belongs to the patrons of his mother. Then, when the father is manumitted, he draws the walāʾ to the patrons of his father. This is munqaṭiʿ (disconnected). It has also been narrated as mawṣūl (connected) from ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him). [Authentic]"
"21523","(21517) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū al-Walīd al-Faqīh narrated to us, ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad narrated to us, Isḥāq informed us, ʿĪsā ibn Yūnus narrated from al-Aʿmash, from Ibrāhīm, from al-Aswad, from ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: When a slave marries a free woman and she bears children, they are freed by her freeing, and their walāʾ belongs to the patron of their mother. Then, when the father is manumitted, he draws the walāʾ. [Authentic]"
"21524","(21518) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū al-Walīd narrated to us, ʿAbd Allāh narrated to us, Abū Qudāmah narrated from Sufyān, from Hishām ibn ʿUrwah, from his father: that al-Zubayr and Rāfiʿ ibn Khadīj brought a dispute to ʿUthmān (may Allah be pleased with them) concerning a female slave belonging to Rāfiʿ ibn Khadīj who was under a slave and bore him children. Al-Zubayr purchased the slave and manumitted him. ʿUthmān (may Allah be pleased with him) judged the walāʾ in favour of al-Zubayr (may Allah be pleased with him). [Authentic]"
"21525","(21519) Likewise, al-Thawrī narrated it from Hishām ibn ʿUrwah, from ʿUrwah. Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn ʿAlī al-Aṣbahānī informed us, Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Aṣbahānī informed us, Ismāʿīl ibn Ibrāhīm al-Qaṭṭān narrated to us, al-Ḥasan ibn ʿĪsā informed us, Ibn al-Mubārak informed us, Sufyān narrated from Hishām ibn ʿUrwah, from his father: that they both brought a dispute to ʿUthmān (may Allah be pleased with him), and he judged it in favour of al-Zubayr in this matter.\n\nLikewise, Rabīʿah ibn Abī ʿAbd al-Raḥmān and Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Taymī narrated it from ʿUthmān and al-Zubayr (may Allah be pleased with them both) as mursal (with a missing link in the chain). [Authentic]"
"21526","(21520) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr both informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib informed us, Yazīd ibn Hārūn informed us, Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr narrated from Yaḥyā ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Ḥāṭib: that al-Zubayr ibn al-ʿAwwām (may Allah be pleased with him) came to Khaybar and saw some handsome, witty young men. He was impressed by their wit and asked about them. He was told: They are freedmen of Rāfiʿ ibn Khadīj; their mother is a free woman, a freedwoman of Rāfiʿ ibn Khadīj, and their father is a slave of Ashjaʿ, belonging to some of the Ḥuraqah. Al-Zubayr (may Allah be pleased with him) sent for their father, purchased him, and manumitted him. Then he said to the young men: Attribute yourselves to me, for you are my freedmen. Rāfiʿ said: Rather, they are my freedmen; they were born while their mother was free and their father was a slave. They both brought the dispute to ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān (may Allah be pleased with him), and he judged their walāʾ in favour of al-Zubayr.\n\nThis is the well-known narration from ʿUthmān (may Allah be pleased with him). It has also been narrated from al-Zuhrī from ʿUthmān (may Allah be pleased with him) as munqaṭiʿ (disconnected), contradicting it. [Weak]"
"21527","(21521) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbāṣ al-Aṣamm narrated to us, Yaḥyā informed us, Yazīd informed us, Ibn Abī Dhiʾb narrated from al-Zuhrī: that al-Zubayr (may Allah be pleased with him) came to Khaybar and saw some young men whose condition impressed him. He asked about them and was told: They are freedmen of Banī Ḥārithah; their mother is a free woman, a freedwoman of Banī Ḥārithah, and their father is a slave. He sent for their father, purchased him, and manumitted him. He and Banī Ḥārithah then brought a dispute to ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān (may Allah be pleased with him) regarding the walāʾ. ʿUthmān (may Allah be pleased with him) judged the walāʾ in favour of Banī Ḥārithah. ʿUthmān (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Walāʾ is not drawn (transferred). Thus he said. The first narration from ʿUthmān (may Allah be pleased with him) is more authentic due to its supporting evidences, and the mursal narrations of al-Zuhrī are weak. [Weak]"
"21528","(21522) Aḥmad ibn ʿAlī al-Aṣbahānī al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Aṣbahānī informed us, Ismāʿīl ibn Ibrāhīm al-Qaṭṭān narrated to us, al-Ḥasan ibn ʿĪsā informed us, Ibn al-Mubārak informed us, Ibn Lahīʿah narrated from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Hubayrah: that ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) judged regarding a slave who had a free woman under him and she bore children. They were freed by the freeing of their mother. Then their father was manumitted afterwards. He said: Their walāʾ belongs to the ʿaṣabah (agnatic heirs) of their father. [Weak]"
"21529","(21523) He said: Ibn al-Mubārak informed us, Maʿmar narrated from Yazīd al-Rishk: that ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) used to draw (transfer) the walāʾ. [Weak]"
"21530","(21524) He said: Ibn al-Mubārak informed us, Sufyān narrated from Jābir, from al-Shaʿbī, from al-Aswad ibn Yazīd, from Ibn Masʿūd, who said: A slave draws the walāʾ of his children when he is manumitted. He said: Shurayḥ used to judge that the walāʾ of the child belonged to the patrons of the mother, until al-Aswad informed him of the statement of Ibn Masʿūd, whereupon Shurayḥ judged accordingly. Thus said Jābir al-Juʿfī from al-Shaʿbī from al-Aswad. [Weak]"
"21531","(21525) Al-Sharīf Abū al-Fatḥ al-ʿUmarī informed us, ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Shurayḥ informed us, Abū al-Qāsim al-Baghawī informed us, ʿAlī ibn al-Jaʿd informed us, Shuʿbah narrated from al-Ḥakam, from Ibrāhīm, who said: Shurayḥ would hardly ever retract a judgment he had passed until al-Aswad ibn Yazīd narrated to him from ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāy (may Allah be pleased with him) that he said regarding a free woman who is married to a slave and bears him children, and then their father is freed: their walāʾ (clientage) shall revert to the mawālī (freedmen) of their father. So Shurayḥ adopted this ruling. This is a ṣaḥīḥ (authentic) chain of narration, and it is possible that al-Aswad narrated it from both ʿUmar and Ibn Masʿūd together. And Allah knows best. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"21532","(21526) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib informed us, Yazīd ibn Hārūn informed us, al-Ḥajjāj ibn Arṭāh narrated from Wabrah, who said: Shurayḥ used to judge that if a slave married a free woman and she bore him children, the walāʾ belonged to their mother. It was said to him: Indeed, ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) judged that if the father were freed, he would pull the walāʾ (to himself). So Shurayḥ abandoned that (earlier ruling). [Ḍaʿīf]"
"21533","(21527) Through his chain, Yazīd informed us, Ashʿath ibn Sawwār narrated from Muḥammad ibn Sīrīn: A free woman was married to a slave and bore him children; then the slave was freed. So Shurayḥ judged that the walāʾ would be pulled (to the father's patrons). [Ḍaʿīf]"
"21534","(21528) Through his chain, Yazīd informed us, Zakariyyā ibn Abī Zāʾidah narrated from al-Shaʿbī: He was asked about a slave who had children by a free woman, and the slave had a free father. It was said: To whom does the walāʾ of his children belong? He said: To the mawālī (freedmen) of the grandfather. [Ḍaʿīf]"
"21535","(21529) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū al-Walīd al-Faqīh informed us, Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAlī informed us, Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā informed us, Ibn Lahīʿah narrated from Yazīd ibn Abī Ḥabīb, from ʿUrwah, from Ghaylān ibn Salamah: That Rāfīʾ, Abū al-Sāʾib, was a slave of Ghaylān. He fled to the Prophet (ﷺ), and the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) freed him. Then Ghaylān embraced Islam, so the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) returned his walāʾ to Ghaylān. [Ḍaʿīf]"
"21536","(21530) He said: And Ibrāhīm narrated to us, Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā informed us, Ibn Lahīʿah narrated from Yazīd ibn Abī Ḥabīb: When the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) besieged a fortress and one of the slaves came to him, he would free him. Then, when the slave's master embraced Islam, he would return the walāʾ to him.\n\nThis chain is munqaṭiʿ (discontinued), and Ibn Lahīʿah is alone in narrating it. And Allah knows best.\n\nMuḥammad ibn Isḥāq ibn Ysār narrated it from ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Mukaddam al-Thaqafī, from the Prophet (ﷺ), regarding those slaves of the people of al-Ṭāʾif who came out to him. Then the people of al-Ṭāʾif came as a delegation and embraced Islam. They said: \O Messenger of Allah"," return to us our slaves who came to you.\"" He said: \""They are the freedmen of Allah.\"" And he returned the walāʾ of each man's slave to him. This chain is also munqaṭiʿ (discontinued)"," and it has already been mentioned in the book of al-Jizyah. [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"21537","(21531) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us, Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us, Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq al-Qāḍī informed us, ʿĀrim, Sulaymān ibn Ḥarb, and Musaddad said: Ḥammād ibn Zayd narrated from ʿAmr ibn Dīnār, from Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh: A man from the Anṣār freed a slave of his as a mudabbar (to be freed upon the master's death), and he had no other property. This reached the Prophet (ﷺ), so he said: \Who will buy him?\"" So Nuʿaym ibn ʿAbd Allāh bought him for eight hundred dirhams and paid the price to him. I heard Jābir say: \""He was a Coptic slave who died in the first year.\"" The wording is that of ʿĀrim. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muttafaq ʿalayh]"""
"21538","(21532) Abū ʿAmr Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Adīb informed us, Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī informed me, Abū Yaʿlā informed us, Abū al-Rabīʿ al-Zahrānī informed us, Ḥammād ibn Zayd narrated with his chain, similar to it, except that he said: \He freed a slave of his as a mudabbar (to be freed upon the master's death).\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Abī al-Nuʿmān ʿĀrim"," and Muslim narrated it from Abī al-Rabīʿ. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Preceded before it]"""
"21539","(21533) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me, ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī informed us, Ibrāhīm ibn al-Ḥusayn informed us, Ādam informed us, Shuʿbah informed us, ʿAmr ibn Dīnār said: I heard Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Anṣārī say: A man from among us freed a slave of his as a mudabbar. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) called for him and sold him. Jābir said: \The boy died in the first year.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Ādam. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muttafaq ʿalayh]"""
"21540","(21534) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf al-Aṣbahānī informed us, Abū Saʿīd Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Ziyād al-Baṣrī informed us in Makkah, al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ṣabbāḥ al-Zaʿfarānī informed us, Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah said: ʿAmr ibn Dīnār heard Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh say: A man from the Anṣār freed a slave of his as a mudabbar, and he had no other property. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) sold him. Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh said: Ibn al-Naḥḥām bought him — a Coptic slave who died in the year of Ibn al-Zubayr.\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Qutaybah, and Muslim narrated it from Abī Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah and Isḥāq ibn Rāhawayh, all from Sufyān. Likewise, Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal, ʿAlī ibn al-Madīnī, and al-Ḥumaydī narrated it from Sufyān. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muttafaq ʿalayh]"
"21541","(21535) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzakkī and Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī narrated to us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān narrated to us: al-Shāfiʿī narrated to us: Ibn ʿUyaynah narrated to us from ʿAmr ibn Dīnār and from Abū al-Zubayr, both of whom heard Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh say: A man among us made his slave a mudabbar (one who is to be freed upon the master's death), and he had no other wealth besides him. So the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \Who will purchase him from me?\"" So Nuʿaym al-Naḥḥām bought him. ʿAmr said: I heard Jābir say: He was a Coptic slave who died in the first year"," during the governorship of Ibn al-Zubayr. Abū al-Zubayr added: He was called Yaʿqūb.\n\nAl-Shāfiʿī said: Thus I heard it from him throughout most of my life"," then I found in my book: \""A man among us made his slave a mudabbar"," and he died.\"" It may be an error from my book or an error from Sufyān. If it is from Sufyān"," then Ibn Jurayj is more precise in the ḥadīth of Abū al-Zubayr than Sufyān"," and with Ibn Jurayj is the ḥadīth of al-Layth and others. And Abū al-Zubayr narrates the ḥadīth with precision"," mentioning the life of the one who made him a mudabbar. And Ḥammād ibn Zayd"," along with Ḥammād ibn Salamah and others"," is more precise in the ḥadīth of ʿAmr than Sufyān alone. The precision of a ḥadīth may be inferred from its errors by less than what I have found. More than one person who met Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah in the past informed me that he did not include \""he died\"" in his ḥadīth. Some of them were astonished when I informed them that I found \""he died\"" in my book"," and said: \""Perhaps this is an error from him or a slip from him that you preserved from him.\""\n\nThe Shaykh"," may Allah have mercy on him"," said: As for the ḥadīth of Ḥammād ibn Zayd from ʿAmr ibn Dīnār"," we have mentioned it along with the ḥadīth of Shuʿbah from ʿAmr. And as for the ḥadīth of Ḥammād ibn Salamah from ʿAmr… [Ṣaḥīḥ. It was mentioned before.]"""
"21542","(21536) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan narrated to us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān narrated to us: al-Shāfiʿī narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Ḥassān narrated to us from Ḥammād ibn Salamah from ʿAmr ibn Dīnār from Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh from the Prophet (ﷺ), similar to the ḥadīth of Ḥammād ibn Zayd from ʿAmr.\n\nAnd as for the ḥadīth of Ibn Jurayj from Abū al-Zubayr…"
"21543","(21537) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan narrated to us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās — he is al-Aṣamm — narrated to us: al-Rabīʿ narrated to us: al-Shāfiʿī narrated to us: Muslim ibn Khālid and ʿAbd al-Majīd narrated to us from Ibn Jurayj: Abū al-Zubayr informed me that he heard Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh say: Abū Madhkūr, a man from Banī ʿUdhrah, had a Coptic slave whom he freed as a mudabbar (to be freed after the master's death). The Prophet (ﷺ) heard about that slave, so he sold the slave and said: \When one of you is poor"," let him begin with himself. If there is surplus"," let him provide for those he supports. Then if there is surplus after that"," let him give in charity to others.\""\n\nAnd as for the ḥadīth of al-Layth ibn Saʿd from Abū al-Zubayr… [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"21544","(21538) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn Yūnus narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Muḥammad ibn Shādhān and Aḥmad ibn Salamah narrated to us, saying: Qutaybah ibn Saʿīd narrated to us: al-Layth narrated to us from Abū al-Zubayr from Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh, who said: A man from Banī ʿUdhrah freed a slave of his as a mudabbar. This reached the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ), and he said: \Do you have any wealth besides him?\"" He said: \""No.\"" He said: \""Who will purchase him from me?\"" So Nuʿaym ibn ʿAbd Allād al-ʿAdawī bought him for eight hundred dirhams. He brought the price to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"," who handed it over to him (the owner)"," and then said: \""Begin with yourself and give charity on its behalf. If anything remains"," then for your family. If anything remains beyond your family"," then for your relatives. If anything remains beyond your relatives"," then thus and thus\"" — meaning: in front of you"," to your right"," and to your left.\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Qutaybah and Muḥammad ibn Rumḥ.\n\nLikewise"," Ayyūb ibn Abī Tamīmah al-Sakhtiyānī narrated it from Abū al-Zubayr. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Agreed upon.]"""
"21545","(21539) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Bakr narrated to us: Abū Dāwūd narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal narrated to us: Ismāʿīl ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us: Ayyūb narrated to us from Abū al-Zubayr from Jābir: A man from the Anṣār, called Abū Madhkūr, freed a slave of his called Yaʿqūb as a mudabbar, and he had no other wealth besides him. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) called for him and said: \Who will purchase him?\"" Nuʿaym ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Naḥḥām bought him for eight hundred dirhams and handed the price to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ). He said: \""When one of you is poor"," let him begin with himself. If there is surplus in it"," then upon his dependents. If there is surplus"," then upon his relatives or his kin. If there is surplus"," then here and here.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. It was mentioned before.]"""
"21546","(21540) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us: Yaʿqūb and Aḥmad narrated to us: Ibrāhīm al-Dawraqī narrated to us, saying: Ismāʿīl ibn ʿUlayyah narrated to us from Ayyūb, and he mentioned it.\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Yaʿqūb al-Dawraqī."
"21547","(21541) As for the ḥadīth of Ḥammād ibn Salamah from Abū al-Zubayr: Abū Bakr ibn Fūrak narrated to us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us: Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb narrated to us: Abū Dāwūd al-Ṭayālisī narrated to us: Ḥammād ibn Salamah narrated to us from…\n\n(Ḥ) And ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us: Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq narrated to us: Ḥajjāj ibn Minhāl narrated to us: Ḥammād ibn Salamah narrated to us: Abū al-Zubayr narrated to us from Jābir: A man from his people freed a slave of his as a mudabbar. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Do you have anything besides him?\"" He said: \""No.\"" The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \""Who will purchase him from me?\"" Nuʿaym ibn ʿAbd Allāh bought him for eight hundred dirhams. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) handed the price over to him and said: \""Spend on yourself. If there is surplus"," then on your family. If there is surplus"," then on your relatives. If there is surplus"," then here and here.\""\n\nThe wording is that of Ḥajjāj. In the narration of Abū Dāwūd: \""A man freed a slave of his as a mudabbar"," and this reached the Prophet (ﷺ)"," and he said: 'Do you have anything besides him?'\"" The rest is similar. Yūnus said: Abū Dāwūd gestured with his hand — in front of him"," to his right"," and to his left.\n\nLikewise"," Zuhayr ibn Muʿāwiyah and others narrated it from Abū al-Zubayr. It is also confirmed in that from ʿAṭāʾ from Jābir. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Agreed upon.]"""
"21548","(21542) Abū al-Ḥusayn ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Bishrān narrated to us in Baghdad: Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Miṣrī narrated to us: Mālik ibn Yaḥyā Abū Ghassān narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Wahhāb al-Khaffāf narrated to us: Ḥusayn al-Muʿallim narrated to us from ʿAṭāʾ from Jābir: A man freed a slave of his as a mudabbar, and then he fell into need. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) took him and said: \Who will purchase him from me?\"" Nuʿaym ibn ʿAbd Allāh bought him from him for eight hundred dirhams and handed over his price. [Ṣaḥīḥ. It was mentioned before.]"""
"21549","(21543) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad al-Kaʿbī informed me: Muḥammad ibn Ayyūb narrated to us: ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥasan narrated to us: Ibn al-Mubārak narrated to us from Ḥusayn ibn al-Mukattib.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Muqriʾ narrated to us: al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us: Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Abī Bakr narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd narrated to us from Ḥusayn al-Muʿallim, and he mentioned the ḥadīth with the same isnād and text as that of al-Khaffāf.\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Bishr ibn Muḥammad from Ibn al-Mubārak, and Muslim narrated it from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Hāshim from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd al-Qaṭṭān."
"21550","(21544) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad ibn Nuṣayr al-Khuldī narrated to us: Mūsā ibn Hārūn narrated to us: Qutaybah ibn Saʿīd narrated to us: al-Mughīrah ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān narrated to us from ʿAbd al-Majīd ibn Suhayl from ʿAṭāʾ ibn Abī Rabāḥ from Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh: A man from the Anṣār freed a slave of his as a mudabbar, and he was in need. This was mentioned to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ), so he called him and said: \Did you free your slave?\"" He said: \""Yes.\"" The Prophet (ﷺ) said: \""You are more in need of him.\"" Then he said: \""Who will purchase him?\"" Nuʿaym ibn ʿAbd Allāh said: \""I will.\"" So he bought him"," and the Prophet (ﷺ) took his price and handed it over to its owner.\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Qutaybah ibn Saʿīd. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Agreed upon.]"""
"21551","(21545) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū ʿAmr ʿUthmān ibn Aḥmad ibn al-Sammāk narrated to us that Yaḥyā ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn ʿUbayd narrated to us that Ismāʿīl ibn Abī Khālid narrated from Salamah ibn Kuhayl from ʿAṭāʾ from Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh that a man from among the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ emancipated a slave as a mudabbar (a slave to be freed upon the master's death), and he had no other wealth besides him. So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sold him for eight hundred dirhams and handed the price over to his master.\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from two other routes from Ismāʿīl. [Sound. Previously mentioned.]"
"21552","(21546) ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us that Aḥmad ibn ʢUbayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us that Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq narrated to us that Musaddad narrated to us that Hushaym narrated from ʿAbd al-Malik ibn Abī Sulaymān from ʿAṭāʾ and Ismāʿīl ibn Abī Khālid from Salamah ibn Kuhayl from ʿAṭāʾ from Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh that a man emancipated a slave as a mudabbar, and he had no other wealth besides him. So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded, and he was sold for nine hundred dirhams or for seven hundred dirhams. This is the correct version.\n\nSharīk ibn ʿAbd Allāh narrated it from Salamah ibn Kuhayl from ʿAṭāʾ and Abū al-Zubayr from Jābir that a man died and left behind a mudabbar and a debt. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded them to sell him for his debt, so they sold him for eight hundred. [Sound. Previously mentioned.]"
"21553","(21547) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Aṣbahānī informed us that ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us that Abū Bakr al-Naysābūrī narrated to us that Aḥmad ibn Yūsuf al-Sulamī, al-ʿAbbās ibn Muḥammad, and Ibrāhīm ibn Hāniʾ said: Abū Nuʿaym narrated to us that Sharīk narrated it.\n\nAbū Bakr al-Naysābūrī said: Sharīk's statement that \a man died\"" is an error on his part"," because in the ḥadīth of al-Aʿmash from Salamah ibn Kuhayl"," it is mentioned that he ﷺ returned its price to him and said: \""Pay off your debt.\""\n\nʿAmr ibn Dīnār and Abū al-Zubayr narrated from Jābir that the master of the mudabbar was alive on the day the mudabbar was sold.\n\nThe Shaykh"," may Allah have mercy on him"," said: The scholars of ḥadīth do not doubt the error of Sharīk in this. This error occurred to him and to others because of that. [Sound. Previously mentioned.]"""
"21554","(21548) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Salmān ibn al-Ḥasan al-Faqīh narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn Ghālib ibn Ḥarb narrated to us that Abū Ghassān al-Mismaʿī narrated to us that Muʿādh ibn Hishām narrated to me; my father narrated to me from Maṭar from ʿAṭāʾ ibn Abī Rabāḥ and Abū al-Zubayr and ʿAmr ibn Dīnār that Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh narrated to them that a man from the Anṣār emancipated his slave on the condition that if any death-claim befell him, he would be freed. Then he died. So the Prophet ﷺ called for him and sold him to Nuʿaym ibn ʿAbd Allāh, one of Banū ʿAdī ibn Kaʿb.\n\nMuslim narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū Ghassān, except that he did not cite its text (matn) and referred instead to the narration of Ḥammād ibn Zayd. His statement \if any death-claim befell him"," then he died\"" is part of the condition of emancipation and is not a report about the death of the emancipator. It is from here that the error occurred for some narrators in mentioning the death of the man at the time of the sale. In fact"," he mentioned his death as part of the condition of emancipation on the day of the tadbīr. What indicates this is the narration of the majority. [Sound. Previously mentioned.]"""
"21555","(21549) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ, Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī, Abū al-Qāsim al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Ḥabīb al-Mufassir from his original, and Abū ʿAbd Allāh Isḥāq ibn Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf al-Sūsī informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us that al-ʿAbbās ibn al-Walīd ibn Yazīd narrated to me; my father narrated to me that al-Awzāʿī narrated to me that ʿAṭāʾ ibn Abī Rabāḥ said: I heard Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh say: A man granted his slave freedom after his death, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sold him, then handed its price over to him and said: \You are more in need of its price"," and Allah is free of need of it.\""\n\nBishr ibn Bakr likewise narrated it from al-Awzāʿī"," mentioning in it that al-Awzāʿī heard it directly from ʿAṭāʾ.\n\nAl-Walīd ibn Yazīd narrated it afterwards"," saying: al-Awzāʿī narrated to me that Abū ʿAmmār narrated from ʿAṭāʾ from Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh"," who said: A man emancipated a slave of his"," and he had no other wealth besides him"," so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sold him"," then handed its price over to him and said: \""You are more in need of its price"," and Allah is free of need of it.\"" [Sound. Previously mentioned.]"""
"21556","(21550) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ, Abū Bakr al-Qāḍī, and Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Sūsī narrated it to us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās narrated to us that al-ʿAbbās narrated to me; my father narrated it, as though al-Awzāʿī dropped from it his words \and he had no other wealth besides him","\"" and he narrated it from Abū ʿAmmār from ʿAṭāʾ. [Sound. Previously mentioned.]"""
"21557","(21551) Muḥammad ibn Ṭarīf narrated it from Ibn Fuḍayl from ʿAbd al-Malik ibn Abī Sulaymān from ʿAṭāʾ from Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \There is no harm in selling the service of a mudabbar if one is in need.\""\n\nAbū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū al-Walīd narrated to us that Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn Zurayḥ al-ʿUkbariyy narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn Ṭarīf narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn Fuḍayl narrated to us that ʿAbd al-Malik narrated it. This is an error on the part of Ibn Ṭarīf."""
"21558","(21552) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us that Abū al-Ḥasan al-Dāraquṭnī al-Ḥāfiẓ said: After this ḥadīth, \This is an error on the part of Ibn Ṭarīf"," and the correct version is from ʿAbd al-Malik from Abī Jaʿfar"," as a mursal narration.\""\n\nThe Shaykh"," may Allah have mercy on him"," said: Muḥammad ibn Ṭarīf"," may Allah have mercy on him and on us"," had one ḥadīth mixed into another ḥadīth. This is because the trustworthy narrators only narrated from ʿAbd al-Malik ibn Abī Sulaymān from ʿAṭāʾ from Jābir that a man emancipated a slave as a mudabbar and he had no other wealth besides him"," so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded regarding him"," and he was sold for nine hundred or seven hundred dirhams. [Denounced (Munkar).]"""
"21559","(21553) ʿAbd al-Malik ibn Abī Sulaymān narrated from Abī Jaʿfar that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sold the service of a mudabbar.\n\nAbū al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAbdān informed us that Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd narrated to us that Ziyād ibn al-Khalīl narrated to us that Musaddad narrated to us that Hushaym narrated from ʿAbd al-Malik from ʿAṭāʾ, and he mentioned the ḥadīth.\n\nAbū Dāwūd likewise narrated it in the Sunan from Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal from Hushaym from ʿAbd al-Malik from ʿAṭāʾ. Muslim ibn al-Ḥajjāj said: The narration of Ibn Fuḍayl from ʿAbd al-Malik from ʿAṭāʾ contains a mistake in both the isnād and the matn."
"21560","(21554) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū al-Walīd narrated to us that Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAlī narrated to us that Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā informed us that Hushaym narrated from ʿAbd al-Malik from Abī Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī from the Prophet ﷺ: \He only sold the service of the mudabbar.\""\n\nYazīd ibn Hārūn narrated something to that effect from ʿAbd al-Malik. [Weak.]"""
"21561","(21555) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū al-Walīd narrated to us, that al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān narrated to us, that Abū Bakr narrated to us, that Abū Khālid al-Aḥmar narrated from Shuʿbah, from al-Ḥakam, from Abū Jaʿfar, who said: \The Prophet (ﷺ) sold the service of a mudabbar (a slave granted manumission upon the master's death).\""\n\nJābir al-Juʿfī also narrated it from Abū Jaʿfar"," thus as a mursal hadith. And al-Shāfiʿī mentioned it in al-Qadīm from Ḥajjāj"," meaning Ibn Arṭāh"," from Abū Jaʿfar.\n\nAnd he responded to it in al-Jadīd with what follows. [Weak]"""
"21562","(21556) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr narrated to us that Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm narrated to us that al-Rabīʿ said: al-Shāfiʿī said: \Someone said: 'We have narrated from Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī that the Prophet (ﷺ) only sold the service of a mudabbar.' So I said to him: 'I do not know of anyone from whom this hadith has been narrated from Abū Jaʿfar whose hadith is established (as reliable). And even if it were narrated by one whose hadith is established"," there would be no proof in it from several aspects.' He said: 'What are they?' I said: 'You yourself do not accept a munqaṭiʿ (disconnected) hadith when it is not contradicted by anyone else"," so how can you accept a munqaṭiʿ hadith when it is contradicted by a muttaṣil (connected)"," established hadith"," if indeed it is contradicted?' He said: 'Is it contradicted?' I said: 'It is not a hadith (i.e."," not strong enough)"," so I would not need to mention it.' He said: 'Then mention it"," despite its weakness in your estimation.' I said: 'If it were established"," it would be permissible for me to say that the Prophet (ﷺ) sold the neck of a mudabbar"," as Jābir narrated"," and the service of a mudabbar"," as Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī narrated.' He then spoke at length in response to it.\""\n\nAnd ʿAbd al-Ghaffār ibn al-Qāsim connected it from Abū Jaʿfar"," from Jābir — and this ʿAbd al-Ghaffār was accused of fabrication (waḍʿ) by ʿAlī ibn al-Madīnī. And Abū Shaybah Ibrāhīm ibn ʿUthmān also connected it from ʿUthmān ibn ʿUmayr"," from Abū Jaʿfar"," from Jābir — and Abū Shaybah is weak"," and one cannot use the likes of him as proof. And it has also been narrated from Mujāhid and Muḥammad ibn al-Munkadar"," from Jābir"," similar to the narration of ʿAṭāʾ"," ʿAmr"," and Abū al-Zubayr from Jābir."""
"21563","(21557) As for the hadith of Mujāhid: Abū Ṭāhir al-Imām informed us that Abū Ḥāmid Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us that Abū al-Azhar narrated to us that Yaʿqūb ibn Ibrāhīm ibn Saʿd narrated to us that his father narrated to us from Abū Isḥāq, who said: \And ʿAbd Allāh ibn Abī Najīḥ and Abān ibn Ṣāliḥ narrated to me from Mujāhid"," Abū al-Ḥajjāj"," from Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Anṣārī"," who said: 'There was a man from Banī ʿUdhrah in the mosque of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"," called Abū al-Madhkūr"," and he had a Coptic slave. He granted him manumission upon his death (dabbirahu)"," then he fell into need. So the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \""When one of you is in need"," let him begin with himself.\"" So he sold him to Nuʿaym ibn ʿAbd Allāh"," the brother of Banī ʿAdī ibn Kaʿb"," for eight hundred"," and he benefited from the price.'\""\n\nMujāhid and the jurists of the people of Makkah held the view that tadbīr (granting manumission upon the master's death) is a bequest"," and its owner retains the option regarding it for as long as he lives — he may act upon it as he wishes or retract from it as he wishes. [Sound. Agreed upon (muttafaq ʿalayh)]"""
"21564","(21558) As for the hadith of Ibn al-Munkadar from Jābir: Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq informed us that ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz narrated to us that ʿĀṣim ibn ʿAlī narrated to us that Ibn Abī Dhiʾb narrated from Muḥammad ibn al-Munkadar, from Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh, that a man freed a slave of his who had no other property besides him, so the Prophet (ﷺ) returned him to him (into slavery), and then Nuʿaym ibn al-Naḥḥām bought him.\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿĀṣim ibn ʿAlī. [Sound]"
"21565","(21559) And Abū ʿAmr al-Adīb informed us that Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī informed us that Abū Ḥufayṣ narrated to us that ʿUqbah ibn Mukram narrated to us that Salm ibn Qutaybah narrated to us that Ibn Abī Dhiʾb narrated from Muḥammad ibn al-Munkadar, from Jābir, that a man granted tadbīr (posthumous manumission) to his slave, so the Prophet (ﷺ) commanded that he be sold, and a man called Nuʿaym bought him. [Sound. Preceded earlier]"
"21566","(21560) And Abū al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAbdān informed us that Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd narrated to us that Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn Abī Bakr narrated to us that Saʿīd ibn Salamah al-Madanī narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn al-Munkadar narrated from Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh, that a man freed a slave of his who had no other property besides him, so the Prophet (ﷺ) returned him to him (into slavery), then sold him and gave him the price.\n\nThese three narrations, taken together, convey the complete hadith. [Sound. Preceded earlier]"
"21567","(21561) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr narrated to us that Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm narrated to us that al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān narrated to us that al-Shāfiʿī narrated to us that al-Thiqah (a trustworthy narrator) narrated from Maʿmar, from Ibn Ṭāwūs, from his father, who said: \The Prophet (ﷺ) sold a mudabbar whose owner was in need of its price.\"" [Weak]"""
"21568","(21562) Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī and Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Mazzī both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us that al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān narrated to us that al-Shāfiʿī narrated to us that Mālik narrated from Abū al-Rijāl Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, from his mother ʿAmrah, that ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her) granted tadbīr to a slave-girl of hers, but the girl practiced sorcery and confessed to it. So ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her) commanded that she be sold to the Bedouins — to those who would treat their slaves poorly — and so she was sold. [Sound. Narrated by Mālik]"
"21569","(21563) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr narrated to us that Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm narrated to us that al-Rabīʿ narrated to us that al-Shāfiʿī narrated to us that Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah narrated from Ibn Abī Najīḥ, from Mujāhid, who said: \The mudabbar is a bequest; its owner may retract it whenever he wishes.\"" [Sound]"""
"21570","(21564) And with his chain of narration: al-Shāfiʿī informed us that al-Thiqah (a trustworthy narrator) narrated from Maʿmar, from Ayyūb, that ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz sold a mudabbar on account of his owner's debt. [Weak]"
"21571","(21565) And with its isnad: al-Shāfiʿī informed us, the trustworthy one informed us, from Maʿmar, from ʿAmr ibn Muslim, from Ṭāwūs, who said: \A man may revoke [his decision] regarding his mudabbar slave.\"" [Weak]"""
"21572","(21566) And with its isnad, he said: al-Shāfiʿī informed us, the trustworthy one informed us, from Maʿmar, from Ibn Ṭāwūs, who said: \Ibn al-Munkadir asked me: 'What did your father say about the mudabbar — may its owner sell it?' He said: I said: 'He would sell it when he was in need of its price.' Ibn al-Munkadir said: 'And may he sell it even when he is not in need?'\"" [Weak]"""
"21573","(21567) Abū ʿAbd Allāh the ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-Walīd the faqīh informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān narrated to us: Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah narrated to us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Idrīs narrated to us, from Layth, from Mujāhid, who said: ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: \Whatever a man frees of his slaves during his illness"," it is a bequest; if he wishes"," he may revoke it.\"" [Weak]"""
"21574","(21568) Abū ʿAbd Allāh informed us: Abū al-Walīd informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān narrated to us: Abū Bakr narrated to us: al-Ḍaḥḥākh ibn Mukhlid narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from ʿAmr ibn Dīnār, from Ṭāwūs: \That he saw no harm in a man revoking his act of manumission.\"" [Sound]"""
"21575","(21569) He said: And Abū Bakr narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Aʿlá narrated to us, from Hishām, from al-Ḥasan, who said: \When a man makes a bequest"," he may alter his will as he wishes.\"" It was said: \""Even manumission?\"" He said: \""Manumission and other than manumission.\"" [Sound]"""
"21576","(21570) Abū ʿAbd Allāh the ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-Walīd the faqīh informed us: Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAlī narrated to us: Yaḥyá ibn Yaḥyá informed us: Ḥafṣ ibn Ghiyāth narrated to us, from al-Ḥajjāj, from al-Ḥasan, from Zayd ibn Thābit (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: \The mudabbar shall not be sold.\"" [Weak]"""
"21577","(21571) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh informed us: Abū al-Walīd informed us: Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAlī narrated to us: Yaḥyá ibn Yaḥyá informed us: Ḥammād narrated to us, from Ayyūb, from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar, who said: \The mudabbar shall not be sold.\""\n\nThis is sound from Ibn ʿUmar as his own statement"," stopped (mawqūf). It has also been narrated as marfūʿ (attributed to the Prophet ﷺ) with a weak isnad. [Sound]"""
"21578","(21572) Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith the faqīh informed us, saying: ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar the ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn ʿUbayd Allāh ibn al-ʿAlāʾ the scribe, and Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Abī Bakr, and a group, said: ʿAlī ibn Ḥarb narrated to us: ʿAmr ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār, Abū Muʿāwiyah al-Jazarī, narrated to us, from his uncle ʿUbaydah ibn Ḥassān, from Ayyūb, from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar, that the Prophet ﷺ said: \The mudabbar shall not be sold and shall not be given as a gift; it is free from the third (of the estate).\""\n\nʿAlī said: \""No one narrated it with a complete chain (asnadahū) other than ʿUbaydah ibn Ḥassān"," and he is weak. It is [in fact] from Ibn ʿUmar as a stopped statement (mawqūf)"," and it is not established as marfūʿ.\"" [Weak]"""
"21579","(21573) Abū ʿAbd Allāh the ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us: al-Shāfiʿī informed us: ʿAlī ibn Ẓabyān narrated to us, from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿUmar, from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar, who said: \The mudabbar is from the third (of the estate).\""\n\nAl-Shāfiʿī (may Allah have mercy on him) said: \""ʿAlī ibn Ẓabyān said to me: 'I used to narrate it as marfūʿ (attributed to the Prophet ﷺ)"," but my companions said to me: \""It is not marfūʿ; it is stopped (mawqūf) upon Ibn ʿUmar.\""' So I stopped [narrating it as marfūʿ]. And the ḥuffāẓ (master narrators) stop it at Ibn ʿUmar.\"" [Weak]"""
"21580","(21574) Abū ʿAbd Allāh the ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb the ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: My father narrated to us: ʿAlī ibn Salamah al-Labqī narrated to us: ʿAlī ibn Ẓabyān narrated to us, from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿUmar, from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \The mudabbar is from the third (of the estate).\""\n\nAnd similarly ʿUthmān ibn Abī Shaybah"," ʿAlī ibn Muslim"," Sufyān ibn Wakīʿ"," and others narrated it from ʿAlī ibn Ẓabyān as marfūʿ. But the sound narration is mawqūf (stopped)"," as narrated by al-Shāfiʿī (may Allah have mercy on him). And that has also been narrated through another route as mursal (with a broken chain) from the Prophet ﷺ. [Weak]"""
"21581","(21575) Abū Ḥāmid Aḥmad ibn ʿAlī al-Isfarāʾinī informed us, that Zāhir ibn Aḥmad informed us, that Abū Bakr ibn Ziyād al-Naysābūrī narrated to us, that Ḥājib ibn Sulaymān narrated to us, that Muʾammal narrated to us, that Sufyān narrated from Khālid from Abū Qilābah: that a man freed his mudabbar (a slave promised freedom upon the master's death), and the Prophet ﷺ placed it (the emancipation) within the third (of the estate). [Weak]"
"21582","(21576) And Abū Ḥāzim Aḥmad ibn ʿAlī informed us, that Zāhir ibn Aḥmad informed us, that Abū Bakr al-Naysābūrī narrated to us, that Aḥmad ibn Yūsuf and al-Ghazzī both said: Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf narrated to us, that Sufyān narrated from Ashʿath from al-Shaʿbī from ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib, may Allah be pleased with him: that he used to consider it (the mudabbar) as part of the third. [Weak]"
"21583","(21577) Abū ʿAbd Allāh the Ḥāfiẓ informed us, that Abū al-Walīd informed us, that Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Zuhayr narrated to us, that ʿAbd Allāh ibn Hāshim narrated from Wakīʿ from Hishām al-Dastawāʾī from Qatādah from al-Ḥasan from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Masʿūd, who said: \He is freed from his third.\""\n\nAnd we have narrated the same from Sharīḥ and Ibrāhīm. [Weak]"""
"21584","(21578) Abū ʿAbd Allāh the Ḥāfiẓ informed us, that Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, that Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣaghānī narrated to us, that Muḥammad ibn Ṭarīf al-Bajalī narrated to us, that ʿAbd Allāh ibn Idrīs narrated from his father from Ḥabīb ibn Abī Thābit from ʬāʾ from Jābir: that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sold a mudabbar (slave promised freedom upon the master's death) for a debt. [Denounced (Munkar)]"
"21585","(21579) Abū ʿAbd Allāh the Ḥāfiẓ informed us, that Abū al-Walīd informed us, that Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAlī narrated to us, that Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā informed us, that Wakīʿ narrated from Ibn Abī Dhiʾb from Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Taymī from his father from al-Salūlī al-Aʿwar from Muʿādh ibn Jabal from Abū ʿUbaydah, who said: \The offense (blood-money) of the mudabbar falls upon his master.\"" [Weak]"""
"21586","(21580) Abū ʿAbd Allāh the Ḥāfiẓ informed us, that Abū al-Walīd informed us, that Ibrāhīm ibn Isḥāq informed us, that al-Ḥasan ibn ʿĪsā narrated from Ibn al-Mubārak from Abū Ḥamzah al-Sukkārī from Yazīd al-Naḥwī from Mujāhid from Abū Hurayrah, who said: \A woman from Quraysh made her servant a mudabbar"," then she wished to enter into a mukātabah (contract of emancipation) with him"," so she wrote to Abū Hurayrah. He said: 'Enter into the mukātabah with him. If he pays his mukātabah"," then that is that. And if she dies (before that)"," he is freed.' And I think he said: 'She has no claim to anything from his mukātabah.'\"" [Authentic (Ṣaḥīḥ)]"""
"21587","(21581) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr narrated to us, that Abū al-ʿAbbāṣ al-Aṣamm informed us, that al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us, that al-Shāfiʿī informed us, that Mālik narrated from Nāfiʿ from Ibn ʿUmar: that he had made two of his slave-girls mudabbar, and he used to cohabit with them while they were mudabbarāt. [Authentic (Ṣaḥīḥ)]"
"21588","(21582) And Abū Bakr al-Qāḍī and Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq both informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbāṣ, that is al-Aṣamm, informed us, that Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥakam informed us, that Ibn Wahb informed me, that ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar and Mālik ibn Anas and Usāmah ibn Zayd al-Laythī and Yūnus ibn Yazīd narrated from Nāfiʿ: that ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar mentioned it similarly. [Authentic (Ṣaḥīḥ)]"
"21589","(21583) Abū Ḥāmid Aḥmad ibn ʿAlī al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, that Zāhir ibn Aḥmad informed us, that Abū Bakr ibn Ziyād al-Naysābūrī narrated to me, that Yūsuf ibn Saʿīd narrated to us, that Ḥajjāj narrated to us, that Layth narrated from Yazīd from Abū al-Naḍr from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Yaʿqūb, a client of al-Ḥaraqah, a clan of the Juhaynah, who said: \The master of my grandmother married her to a slave of his"," then he freed her as a mudabbar (promising her freedom upon his death). She had already borne children after her tadbīr (being made mudabbar). Then her master died"," and she brought a dispute to ʿUthmān"," may Allah be pleased with him"," and he ruled that whatever children she bore before she was made mudabbar are slaves"," and whatever children she bore after the tadbīr are freed by her emancipation.\"" [Weak]"""
"21590","(21584) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān informed us in Baghdād, that Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār informed us, that al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn ʿAffān narrated to us, that Ibn Numayr narrated from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿUmar from Nāfiʿ from Ibn ʿUmar, that he used to say: \The children of the mudabbarah are in her status; they are freed by her emancipation and remain enslaved by her enslavement.\"" [Good (Ḥasan)]"""
"21591","(21585) Sufyān al-Thawrī narrated from ʿUbayd Allāh, who said in the hadith: \The children of a mudabbarah (a slave woman promised freedom upon her master's death) shall be of the same status as their mother"," provided she gave birth while she was a mudabbarah.\""\n\nIt was relayed to us by Aḥmad ibn ʿAlī al-Isfarāyīnī"," who reported to us from Zāhir ibn Aḥmad"," who narrated to us from Abū Bakr al-Naysābūrī"," who narrated to us from Aḥmad ibn Yūsuf al-Sulamī and ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿUmar al-Ghazzī"," who both said: Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf narrated to us"," Sufyān narrated to us"," and he mentioned it.\n\n[Hasan]"""
"21592","(21586) And Aḥmad informed us, Zāhir narrated to us, Abū Bakr narrated to us, Abū al-Azhar narrated to us, Rūḥ narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, Abū al-Zubayr informed me that he heard Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh saying: \I do not consider the children of a mudabbarah to be other than of the same status as their mother.\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"21593","(21587) And Aḥmad informed us, Zāhir reported to us, Abū Bakr narrated to us, Yazīd ibn Sinān narrated to us, Abū Dāwūd al-Ṭayālisī narrated to us, ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Ibn Abī Najīḥ, from ʿAṭāʾ, Ṭāwūs, Mujāhid, and Saʿīd ibn Jubayr, that they said: \The children of a mudabbarah are of the same status as their mother.\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"21594","(21588) And Aḥmad informed us, Zāhir reported to us, Abū Bakr narrated to us, Aḥmad ibn Yūsuf and ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad al-Ghazzī both said: Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf narrated to us, Sufyān narrated to us, from Dāwūd ibn Abī Hind, from al-Shaʿbī, regarding the mudabbarah and the umm al-walad (a slave woman who bears her master a child): \Their children are of the same status as they are.\""\n\nAnd it has been narrated from Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyab"," Abū Salamah ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān"," al-Zuhrī"," and al-Nakhaʿī.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"21595","(21589) Abū Aḥmad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Mihrajānī informed us, Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar al-Muzzakī narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Būshanjī narrated to us, Ibn Bukayr narrated to us, Mālik narrated to us, from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd, that he heard Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyab saying: \When a man makes a tadbīr (promise of freedom upon his death) for his slave woman"," he retains the right to cohabit with her"," but he does not have the right to sell her or gift her away. Her children are of the same status as she is.\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"21596","(21590) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū al-Walīd reported to us, Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAlī narrated to us, Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā reported to us, Ibn Lahīʿah informed us, from Bukayr, that Ibn al-Musayyab and Abū Salamah — that is, Ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān — both said: \The children of a mudabbarah are of the same status as their mother.\""\n\nAl-Shāfiʿī"," may Allāh have mercy on him"," said: \""And the second opinion is that they are slaves (mamlūkūn).\"" He said: \""And this has been stated by more than one scholar of the people of knowledge.\""\n\n[Ḍaʿīf]"""
"21597","(21591) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr narrated to us, Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm reported to us, al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān reported to us, al-Shāfiʿī reported to us, Ibn ʿUyaynah narrated to us, from ʿAmr ibn Dīnār, from Abū al-Shaʿthāʾ, who said: \The children of a mudabbarah are slaves.\""\n\nAl-Shāfiʿī"," may Allāh have mercy on him"," said: \""And this was also stated by others besides Abū al-Shaʿthāʾ among the people of knowledge.\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"21598","(21592) Abū Ḥāmid Aḥmad ibn ʿAlī al-Isfarāyīnī informed us, Zāhir ibn Aḥmad reported to us, Abū Bakr al-Naysābūrī narrated to us, Abū al-Azhar narrated to us, Rūḥ ibn ʿUbādah narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, ʿAṭāʾ informed me that Abū al-Shaʿthāʾ used to say regarding the mudabbarah: \Her children are slaves"," like a garden which you have given in charity upon your death — its fruit belongs to you as long as you live.\"" And ʿAṭāʾ used to say: \""And like camels which you give in charity upon your death — their young and their milk belong to you as long as you live.\"" And it has been narrated from Makḥūl.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. It was mentioned before it.]"""
"21599","(21593) And Abū Ḥāmid Aḥmad ibn ʿAlī informed us, Zāhir reported to us, Abū Bakr al-Naysābūrī narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us, ʿAbd al-Razzāq reported to us, Maʿmar narrated to us, from Ayyūb, from ʿIkrimah ibn Khālid, who said: \I was present with ʿAbd al-Malik ibn Marwān when a dispute concerning the children of a mudabbarah was brought before him. He consulted those around him. A man said: 'Her children may be sold"," for a man gives a date-palm in charity yet eats from its fruit.' Another man spoke"," contradicting what his companion had said"," stating: 'The children of a mudabbarah are of the same status as their mother. A man may offer a she-camel (badanah) as a sacrifice"," and if it gives birth"," its young is sacrificed along with it.'\"" ʿIkrimah said: \""He stood up and did not pass any judgment concerning them.\""\n\nAnd something indicating this opinion has been narrated from Zayd ibn Thābit.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. ʿAbd al-Razzāq narrated it.]"""
"21600","(21594) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū al-Walīd al-Faqīh reported to us, al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān narrated to us, Ḥabbān narrated to us, from Ibn al-Mubārak, from ʿUthmān ibn Ḥakīm, from Sulaymān ibn Yasār, that a man came to Zayd ibn Thābit and said: \My paternal aunt made a tadbīr for her slave woman"," and she has no other property besides her.\"" He said: \""Let her (the aunt) derive benefit from her (the slave woman) as long as she is alive.\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"21601","(21595) Abū ʿAbdullāh informed us that Abū al-Walīd narrated to us that al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān narrated to us that Ḥabbān narrated from Ibn al-Mubārak from Ibn Jurayj that Abū al-Zubayr informed him that he heard Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh say regarding the children of a *mudabbarah* (a slave woman granted emancipation upon her master's death): \When the master dies"," we consider them nothing but free.\""\n\nHe said: And ʿAṭāʾ said: \""The children of a *mudabbarah* are slaves"," unless she was pregnant on the day she was designated as *mudabbarah*.\""\n\nAbū al-Walīd said: Our companions said: This is the position of Zayd ibn Thābit"," who made her child an heir. Jābir suspended the ruling on this matter"," and ʿAṭāʾ and Jābir ibn Zayd (Abū al-Shaʿthāʾ) were explicit about it. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"21602","(21596) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān informed us in Baghdād that Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār narrated to us that Aḥmad ibn Manṣūr al-Ramādī narrated to us that ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us that Maʿmar narrated from al-Zuhrī from ʿUrwah ibn al-Zubayr from Ḥakīm ibn Ḥizām, who said: I said: \O Messenger of Allah"," what is your view of matters I used to perform during the Jāhiliyyah — such as freeing slaves and maintaining ties of kinship — is there any reward for me in them?\"" The Prophet ﷺ said: \""You have embraced Islam upon the good that preceded you.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his *Ṣaḥīḥ* from Isḥāq ibn Rāhawayh and ʿAbd from ʿAbd al-Razzāq"," and al-Bukhārī narrated it through another chain from Maʿmar. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Agreed upon]"""
"21603","(21597) Abū Ṣāliḥ ibn Abī Ṭāhir al-ʿAnbarī informed us that my grandfather Yaḥyā ibn Manṣūr al-Qāḍī narrated to us that Aḥmad ibn Salamah narrated to us that Hannād ibn al-Sarī narrated to us that Abū Muʿāwiyah narrated from Hishām ibn ʿUrwah from his father from Ḥakīm ibn Ḥizām, who said: I said: \O Messenger of Allah"," what is your view of something I used to do during the Jāhiliyyah?\"" Hishām said: i.e."," I used to seek righteousness through it. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \""You have embraced Islam upon the righteous good that preceded you.\"" He said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," I shall not leave anything I did for the sake of Allah during the Jāhiliyyah except that I shall do the same for the sake of Allah in Islam.\"" He said: \""So he had freed one hundred slaves during the Jāhiliyyah"," and he freed the like of that — one hundred slaves — in Islam"," and he had offered one hundred *badanah* (camels) in sacrifice during the Jāhiliyyah"," and he offered one hundred *badanah* in sacrifice in Islam.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his *Ṣaḥīḥ* from the ḥadīth of Abī Muʿāwiyah and Ibn Numayr from Hishām"," and al-Bukhārī narrated it from the ḥadīth of Abī Usāmah from Hishām. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Agreed upon]"""
"21604","(21598) Abū Naṣr ibn Qatādah informed us that Abū ʿAmr ibn Nujayd narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us that Ibn Bukayr narrated to us that Mālik narrated from ʿAbdullāh ibn Abī Bakr from his father that ʿAmr ibn Sulaym al-Zuraqī informed him that it was said to ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him): \There is here a young boy from Ghassān who has not yet reached puberty"," and his heir is in al-Shām. He possesses wealth"," and he has no heir here except a paternal cousin.\"" ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him) said: \""Then let him bequeath for her.\"" So he bequeathed for her a property known as Biʾr Jusham. ʿAmr ibn Sulaym said: \""I sold that property for thirty thousand"," and the paternal cousin for whom he bequeathed is Umm ʿAmr ibn Sulaym.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Ibn Mālik]"""
"21605","(21599) And Abū Naṣr informed us that Abū ʿAmr narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us that Ibn Bukayr narrated to us that Mālik narrated from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd from Abī Bakr ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr ibn Ḥazm that a slave boy from Ghassān was on the verge of death in Madīnah, and his heir was in al-Shām. That was mentioned to ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him), and it was said to him: \So-and-so is dying; should he make a bequest?\"" ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him) said: \""Yes"," let him bequeath.\"" Abū Bakr ibn Muḥammad said: \""The boy was ten or twelve years of age.\"" So he bequeathed a property known as Biʾr Jusham"," and his family sold it for thirty thousand dirhams. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"21606","(21600) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū al-Walīd narrated to us that al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn Abān narrated to us that Ḥammād ibn Salamah narrated from Ḥammād from Ibrāhīm from al-Aswad from ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her) that the Prophet ﷺ said: \The pen has been lifted from three: the sleeper until he awakens"," the insane until he regains his senses"," and the child until he reaches puberty.\""\n\nAnd it has been narrated previously from ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) from the Prophet ﷺ. [Ṣaḥīḥ through other chains]"""
"21607","(21601) Abū Dāwūd narrated in his *Marāsīl* from al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī from Abī ʿĀṣim from ʿIkrimah ibn ʿAmmār from Yaḥyā ibn Abī Kathīr, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said regarding His words: **\And give them writing (of emancipation) if you know any good in them\""** [al-Nūr 33]: \""If you know in them a skill or craft"," and do not send them as dependents upon the people.\""\n\nAbū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad informed us that Abū al-Ḥusayn al-Fasawī narrated to us that Abū ʿAlī al-Luʾluʾī narrated to us that Abū Dāwūd narrated it. [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"21608","(21602) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī both said that Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥakam informed us that Ibn Wahb informed me that Yaḥyā ibn Ayyūb narrated from Yazīd ibn Abī Ḥabīb that ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbbās used to say regarding **\And give them writing (of emancipation) if you know any good in them\""** [al-Nūr 33]: \""If you know that your *mukātab* (slave contracted for emancipation) will fulfill his payment to you.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"21609","(21603) And Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq informed us that Abū al-Ḥasan al-Ṭarāʾifī narrated to us that ʿUthmān ibn Saʿīd narrated to us that ʿAbdullāh ibn Ṣāliḥ narrated from Muʿāwiyah ibn Ṣāliḥ from ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭalḥah from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: \If you know in them any resourcefulness"," do not place their burden upon the Muslims.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"21610","(21604) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū al-Walīd narrated to us that Aḥmad ibn Naṣr ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn Mirdās narrated to us that Yaḥyā ibn Abī Rawq narrated to us that my father narrated from al-Ḍaḥḥāk from Ibn ʿAbbās regarding His words: **\And give them writing (of emancipation) if you know any good in them\""** [al-Nūr 33]. He said: \""Trustworthiness and faithfulness.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"21611","(21605) Abu 'Abd Allah and Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr narrated to us, saying: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us: Yahya ibn Abi Talib narrated to us: Yazid ibn Harun informed us: Sufyan al-Thawri informed us, from 'Abd al-Karim, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, that he used to disapprove of concluding a mukataba (contract of manumission) with a slave who had no craft or trade, and he would say: \You will feed me from the refuse of people.\"" [Sahih]"""
"21612","(21606) Abu Bakr ibn al-Hasan and Abu Zakariyya ibn Abi Ishaq narrated to us, saying: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub informed us: Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah ibn 'Abd al-Hakam informed us: Ibn Wahb informed us: Ibn Sam'an informed us, from Mujahid, from Ibn 'Abbas, that he said regarding the words of Allah, the Mighty and Majestic: {Then write (a contract of manumission) for them, if you know any good in them} [al-Nur 33]: \If you know they possess a craft or trade"," or wealth.\"" [Da'if]"""
"21613","(21607) Abu Zakariyya and Abu Bakr narrated to us, saying: Abu al-'Abbas informed us: Muhammad informed us: Ibn Wahb informed me: Muhammad ibn 'Amr al-Yafi'i informed us, from Ibn Jurayj, that 'Ata' ibn Abi Rabah used to say: \We do not understand 'al-khayr' (good) except to mean wealth.\"" He then recited: {Prescribed for you"," when death approaches one of you"," if he leaves behind any good"," is the bequest} [al-Baqarah 180]. 'Ata' said: \""Al-khayr"," as we understand it"," is wealth.\"" And Ibn 'Abbas said regarding {If you know any good in them} [al-Nur 33] and {And indeed"," he is"," in love of wealth (khayr)"," intense} [al-'Adiyat 8]: \""Al-khayr means wealth.\"" And {If he leaves behind any good} [al-Baqarah 180]: \""Al-khayr means wealth.\"" [Da'if]"""
"21614","(21608) Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr narrated to us: Abu al-'Abbas informed us: al-Rabi' informed us: al-Shafi'i informed us: 'Abd Allah ibn al-Harith ibn 'Abd al-Malik informed us, from Ibn Jurayj, that he said to 'Ata': \What is al-khayr — wealth"," righteousness"," or all of that?\"" He said: \""We do not understand it except to mean wealth.\"" I said: \""What if he has no wealth but is an honest man?\"" He said: \""I do not consider 'good' to be anything other than wealth and righteousness.\"" Mujahid said regarding {If you know any good in them} [al-Nur 33]: \""Wealth — whatever their morals and faiths may be.\"" [Sahih]\n\nAl-Shafi'i"," may Allah have mercy on him"," said: \""Al-khayr is a word whose intended meaning is understood from the context in which it is used. Allah"," the Most High"," said: {Indeed"," those who believe and do righteous deeds — they are the best of creatures} [al-Bayyinah 7]. So we understood that they are the best of creatures by virtue of faith and righteous deeds"," not by virtue of wealth. And Allah"," the Most High"," said: {And the sacrificial camels — We have made them for you among the symbols of Allah; for you therein is good} [al-Hajj 36]. So we understood that the 'good' refers to the benefit of reward"," not that there is wealth in the sacrificial camels for them. And the Mighty and Majestic said: {When death approaches one of you"," if he leaves behind any good} [al-Baqarah 180]. So we understood that this refers to wealth"," because wealth is what is left behind"," and by His words: {The bequest is for parents and near relatives} [al-Baqarah 180]. Then when Allah"," the Most High"," said: {Then write (a contract of manumission) for them"," if you know any good in them} [al-Nur 33]"," the most apparent meaning of it"," by the evidence of what we have derived from the Book"," is strength in earning wealth and trustworthiness — for a slave may be strong and earn"," but if he is not trustworthy and honest"," he will not fulfill (the contract); and he may not be strong in earning"," and so will not fulfill (it).\""\n\nAl-Shafi'i"," may Allah have mercy on him"," said: \""The apparent meaning of the statement is not that 'good' in your slave refers to two meanings"," one of which is that wealth is not something inherent in him but rather something he possesses. Rather"," what is in him is the earning capacity that produces wealth. The second meaning is that the wealth in his possession belongs to his master.\"" He said: \""And perhaps those who went to the view that al-khayr means wealth did so because he (the slave) earned wealth for his master by his labor"," and so it is inferred that he will earn wealth by which he will be freed"," just as he earned (wealth) initially.\"""""
"21615","(21609) Abu Nasr ibn Qatadah informed us: Abu Mansur al-'Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Harawi narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Najdah narrated to us: Sa'id ibn Mansur narrated to us: Isma'il ibn Ibrahim informed us, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Mujahid and Tawus, regarding His words {If you know any good in them} [al-Nur 33]: \He said: Wealth and trustworthiness.\""\n\nSa'id narrated to us: Isma'il ibn Ibrahim informed us"," from Yunus"," from al-Hasan"," who said: \""Honesty"," fulfillment of obligations"," and trustworthiness.\""\n\nSa'id narrated to us: Hushaym informed us"," from Mughirah"," from Ibrahim"," who said: \""Honesty and fulfillment (of obligations).\"" [Sahih]"""
"21616","(21610) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz and Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr narrated to us, saying: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us: Ahmad ibn 'Abd al-Jabbar narrated to us: Abu Mu'awiyah informed us, from Isma'il, from Abu Salih, regarding His words {If you know any good in them} [al-Nur 33]: \He said: Fulfillment (of obligations) and trustworthiness.\"" [Da'if]"""
"21617","(21611) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz and Abu Bakr al-Qadi narrated to us, saying: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad informed us: al-'Abbas ibn al-Walid informed us: My father said: I heard al-Awza'i say: \It has reached me that Makhul used to say regarding this verse {If you know any good in them} [al-Nur 33]: 'Earning (a livelihood).'\"" [Da'if]"""
"21618","(21612) Abu Sa'id al-Zahid and Abu al-Hasan Muhammad ibn Abi al-Ma'ruf al-Faqih narrated to us, saying: Abu 'Amr Isma'il ibn Nujayd al-Sulami informed us: Abu Muslim al-Kajji narrated to us: Abu 'Asim informed us, from Muhammad ibn 'Ajlan, from al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurayradh, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Three persons — it is a right upon Allah to help them: the one who strives in the cause of Allah"," the one who marries seeking chastity"," and the one who enters into a mukataba (contract of manumission) seeking to fulfill (its obligations).\"" [Hasan. Previously cited under number 7/1345]"""
"21619","(21613) Abu Tahir al-Faqih informed us: 'Ali ibn Ibrahim ibn Mu'awiyah al-Naysaburi narrated to us: Muslim ibn Muslim ibn Warah narrated to me: 'Amr ibn 'Asim ibn 'Ubayd Allah ibn al-Wazi' narrated to me: My grandfather 'Ubayd Allah ibn al-Wazi' informed me, from Ayyub al-Sakhtiyani, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir ibn 'Abd Allah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Three (types of people) — whoever does them with trust in Allah and in expectation of reward"," it is a right upon Allah to help him and to bless him for him: whoever strives for the emancipation of his own neck (i.e."," seeks to free himself) with trust in Allah and in expectation of reward"," it is a right upon Allah to help him and to bless him for him; and whoever marries with trust in Allah and in expectation of reward"," it is a right upon Allah to help him and to bless him for him; and whoever revives a dead (barren) land with trust in Allah and in expectation of reward"," it is a right upon Allah to help him and to bless him for him.\"" [Da'if]"""
"21620","(21614) Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Isbahani informed us: Abu Nasr al-'Iraqi narrated to us: Sufyan ibn Muhammad informed us: 'Ali ibn al-Hasan informed us: 'Abd Allah ibn al-Walid informed us: Sufyan informed us: Abu Ja'far al-Farra' informed us, from Abu Layla al-Kindi, that Salman al-Farisi, may Allah be pleased with him, was requested by one of his slaves to conclude a mukataba (contract of manumission) with him. He said: \Do you have anything?\"" He said: \""No.\"" He said: \""From where will you (obtain it)?\"" He said: \""I will ask people (for charity).\"" So he refused to conclude the mukataba with him and said: \""You will feed me from the dirty wash-water of people.\"" [Hasan]"""
"21621","(21615) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz narrated to us, Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qubu narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abi Talib narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun informed us, Sa'id ibn Abi 'Arubah informed us, from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: Sirin desired to enter into a mukatabah (contract of emancipation) with me, but I refused. So he went to 'Umar ibn al-Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) and mentioned that to him. 'Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) then came toward me with his whip and said: \Enter into the mukatabah with him.\"" [Hasan]"""
"21622","(21616) Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr narrated to us, Abu al-'Abbas al-Asamm informed us, al-Rabi' informed us, al-Shafi'i informed us, 'Abd Allah ibn al-Harith ibn 'Abd al-Malik narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, who said: I said to 'Ata': \Is it obligatory upon me"," if I know that he (the slave) possesses some wealth"," to enter into a mukatabah with him?\"" He said: \""I do not consider it anything but obligatory.\"" 'Amr ibn Dinar also said the same. I said to 'Ata': \""Do you narrate this from anyone?\"" He said: \""No.\"" [Sahih]"""
"21623","(21617) Abu Nasr ibn Qatadah informed us, Abu Mansur al-Nadrawi narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Najdah narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Mansur narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, from one of his companions, from al-Hasan, who said: \It is not binding (obligatory); if he wishes"," he may enter into a mukatabah"," and if he wishes"," he may not.\""\n\nAnd we have narrated something similar from al-Sha'bi. [Da'if]"""
"21624","(21618) And in what 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Yahya narrated from Hibban ibn Abi Jabalah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \Every one has a greater right to his own wealth than his parents"," his children"," and all the people combined.\""\n\nAbu Bakr ibn al-Harith al-Isbahani informed us of it"," 'Ali ibn 'Umar al-Hafiz narrated to us"," Ahmad ibn al-Husayn ibn Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Junayd narrated to us"," al-Hasan ibn 'Arafah narrated to us"," Hushaym narrated to us"," from 'Abd al-Rahman"," and he mentioned it. This is a mursal hadith. Hibban ibn Abi Jabalah al-Qurashi was among the Tabi'in. [Da'if]"""
"21625","(21619) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz narrated to us, Abu al-Walid informed us, Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Zuhayr narrated to us, 'Abd Allah ibn Hashim narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, from Thawr, from Yunus ibn Sayf, from Harim ibn Hakim, who said: 'Umar ibn al-Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) wrote to 'Umayr ibn Sa'd (may Allah be pleased with him): \To proceed: forbid the Muslims under your authority from entering into mukatabah (contracts of emancipation) with their slaves on the condition of asking people for charity.\"" [Da'if]"""
"21626","(21620) Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Isbahani informed us, Abu Nasr al-'Iraqi narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Muhammad al-Jawhari narrated to us, 'Ali ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, 'Abd Allah ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu Ja'far al-Farra', Ja'far ibn Abi Tharwan al-Harithi narrated to me, from Ibn al-Nabah, who said: He came to 'Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) and said: \I wish to enter into a mukatabah.\"" He said: \""Do you have anything?\"" He said: \""No.\"" So 'Ali ibn Abi Talib gathered the people and said: \""Help your brother.\"" So they collected (wealth) for him. He said: There remained a remainder of his mukatabah (payment). He said: He then came to 'Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) and asked him about the remainder. He said: \""Place him among the mukatabeen (those under emancipation contracts).\"" This indicates that the mukatab (one under an emancipation contract) is given from the sadaqat (charitable funds) from the share of al-riqab (emancipation of slaves)"," that which is between him and his being freed. [Da'if]"""
"21627","(21621) Abu Tahir al-Faqih informed us by recitation, and Abu Muhammad 'Abd Allah ibn Yusuf al-Isbahani by dictation, both said: Abu Bakr al-Qattan informed us, Ibrahim ibn al-Harith narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to us, Zuhayr ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from 'Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn 'Uqayl.\n\n(And) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz narrated to us, Abu 'Abd Allah Muhammad ibn Ya'qub al-Hafiz narrated to us, Yahya ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, Abu al-Walid Hisham ibn 'Abd al-Malik narrated to us, 'Amr ibn Thabit narrated to us, 'Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn 'Uqayl narrated to us, from 'Abd Allah ibn Sahl ibn Hunayf, that Sahl narrated to him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \Whoever helps a mujahid in the cause of Allah"," or one in debt in his hardship"," or a mukatab (one under an emancipation contract) in purchasing his freedom"," Allah will shade him under His Throne on the Day when there shall be no shade except His shade.\"" The wording of both their hadiths is the same. 'Amr ibn Thabit added: \""or a warrior (ghazi).\"" [Da'if]"""
"21628","(21622) Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us, Abu 'Abd Allah Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Abu Usamah narrated to us, Hisham ibn 'Urwah informed us, my father informed me, from 'A'ishah (may Allah be pleased with her), who said: Barirah came and said: \My masters have contracted a mukatabah with me for nine uqiyyah over nine years"," one uqiyyah each year. So help me.\"" And she mentioned the hadith.\n\nBoth (al-Bukhari and Muslim) recorded it in the Sahih. And we have narrated in the authentic hadith from Abu Hurayrah that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) prohibited bay' al-gharar (transaction involving uncertainty/deception). And in the immediate mukatabah there is considerable gharar (uncertainty). [Sahih. Agreed upon.]"""
"21629","(21623) Abu al-Husayn ibn al-Fadl al-Qattan informed us in Baghdad, 'Abd Allah ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Ya'qub ibn Sufyan narrated to me, Abu Bishr narrated to us, Sa'id ibn 'Amir narrated to us, Juwayriyah ibn Asma' narrated to us, from Muslim ibn Abi Maryam, from a man, who said: I was a slave of 'Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him). He said: 'Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him) sent me on a trade mission. I returned to him and he praised my conduct. He said: I stood before him one day and said: \O Commander of the Faithful"," I ask you for a mukatabah (emancipation contract).\"" He frowned and said: \""Yes"," were it not for a verse in the Book of Allah"," I would not do it. I will enter into a mukatabah with you for one hundred thousand"," to be paid by me in installments over two periods. By Allah"," I will not diminish a single dirham of it for you.\"" He said: I left his presence and met al-Zubayr ibn al-'Awwam (may Allah be pleased with him). He said: \""What do I see in you?\"" I said: \""The Commander of the Faithful sent me on a trade mission. I returned to him and he praised my conduct. I stood before him and said: 'O Commander of the Faithful"," I ask you for a mukatabah.' He frowned and said: 'Yes"," were it not for a verse in the Book of Allah"," I would not do it. I will enter into a mukatabah with you for one hundred thousand"," to be paid by me in installments over two periods. By Allah"," I will not diminish a single dirham of it for you.'\"" He said: \""Go.\"" He said: He brought me back to him. I stood before him and he said: \""O Commander of the Faithful"," so-and-so — you have contracted a mukatabah with him.\"" He frowned and said: \""Yes"," were it not for a verse in the Book of Allah"," I would not do it. I will enter into a mukatabah with him for one hundred thousand"," to be paid by me in installments over two periods. By Allah"," I will not diminish a single dirham of it for him.\"" He said: Al-Zubayr became angry and said: \""By Allah"," I will set forth before you examples"," for I am only requesting of you a need that you are preventing with an oath.\"" He said: He struck — I do not know — he said: \""my shoulder\"" or he said: \""my upper arm.\"" Then he said: \""Enter into the mukatabah with him.\"" He said: So I entered into the mukatabah with him. Al-Zubayr took me to his family and gave me one hundred thousand. Then he said: \""Go and seek from the bounty of Allah through it. If a matter overcomes you"," then pay 'Uthman what is due to him from it.\"" He said: I went and sought from the bounty of Allah through it"," and I paid 'Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him) his wealth and al-Zubayr (may Allah be pleased with him) his wealth"," and there remained in my hand eighty thousand.\"" [Da'if]"""
"21630","(21624) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz (may Allah have mercy on him) informed me, Abu al-Qasim 'Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Hasan al-Qadi in Hamadan narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Husayn narrated to us, 'Affan ibn Muslim narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from 'Asim ibn Sulayman and 'Ali ibn Zayd, from Abu 'Uthman, from Salman, who said: \I contracted a mukatabah with my masters that I would plant for them five hundred date-palm saplings"," and when they bore fruit"," I would be free. I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) and mentioned that to him. He said: 'Plant and stipulate the condition for them. And when you wish to plant"," inform me.' So I informed him"," and he came and began to plant them — all except one sapling"," which I planted with my own hand. They all bore fruit except the one.\"" [Da'if]"""
"21631","(21625) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq informed us that Mūsā ibn Isḥāq al-Qāḍī narrated to us that ʿAbd Allāh ibn Abī Shaybah narrated to us that Zayd ibn al-Ḥubāb narrated from al-Ḥusayn ibn Wāqid who narrated to me that ʿAbd Allāh ibn Buraydah narrated from his father that Salmān (may Allah be pleased with him) came to Madīnah and brought a gift to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), placing it on a platter before him. He asked, \What is this"," O Salmān?\"" He replied"," \""It is charity (ṣadaqah) for you and your Companions.\"" He said"," \""I do not eat charity.\"" So he took it away. Then he came the next day with something similar and placed it before him. He asked"," \""What is this?\"" He replied"," \""It is a gift for you.\"" The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) then said to his Companions"," \""Eat.\"" He asked"," \""Who are you?\"" He said"," \""I am a slave of a people.\"" He said"," \""Seek from them that they enter into a mukātabah (contract of manumission) with you.\"" He said"," \""So they contracted a mukātabah with me for such and such number of date palms that I would plant for them"," and Salmān would tend them until they bore fruit.\"" He said"," \""They did so.\"" He said"," \""Then the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) came and planted all the date palms except one"," which ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) planted. All the date palms bore fruit that year except that one palm. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) asked"," 'Who planted it?' They said"," 'ʿUmar.' So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) planted it with his own hand"," and it bore fruit that same year.\"" [Ḥasan]"""
"21632","(21626) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Bakr al-Ḥīrī both informed us, saying that Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us that Aḥmad ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār narrated to us that Yūnus ibn Bukayr narrated from Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq who narrated to me that ʿĀṣim ibn ʿUmar ibn Qatādah narrated from Maḥmūd ibn Labīd who narrated from Ibn ʿAbbās who said: Salmān al-Fārisī narrated to me, and he mentioned the hadith at length regarding the story of his conversion to Islam. In it he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said, \Enter into a mukātabah"," O Salmān.\"" So I contracted a mukātabah with my masters for three hundred date palms that I would bring to life and forty awqiyyahs (of gold/silver). The Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) assisted me with the date palm saplings — thirty small saplings"," twenty small saplings"," and ten"," each man according to what he had. He mentioned the hadith regarding the digging. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) went out with me until he came to them"," and we would carry the small saplings to him and he would place them with his own hand and level the earth over them. By the One Who sent him with truth"," not a single one of those small saplings died. The dirhams"," however"," remained outstanding upon me. Then a man from one of the mines came to him with an amount of gold the size of an egg. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said"," \""Where is the Muslim Fārisī mukātab (one contracted for manumission)?\"" So I was called to him and he said"," \""Take this"," O Salmān"," and discharge what is upon you.\"" I said"," \""O Messenger of Allah"," how can this possibly cover what is upon me?\"" He said"," \""Allah will discharge your debt through it.\"" By the One in Whose hand is the soul of Salmān"," I weighed out for them forty awqiyyahs from it and paid it to them. And Salmān was set free (may Allah be pleased with him).\n\nThe Shaykh (may Allah have mercy on him) said: In the first narration there is an increase in the number of saplings"," and in it there is the stipulation of freedom"," and that one of them did not bear fruit — that being the one the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) did not plant. In the third narration there is a decrease in the number of saplings and an increase of forty awqiyyahs. In both of them"," along with the second narration"," that was upon the condition of ʿallūq (bearing fruit) or ṭiʿām (producing food)"," and the contract was with disbelievers"," and the objective was the attainment of manumission. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) permitted the stipulation by his words"," \""Stipulate for them","\"" because it is a valid condition for the attainment of manumission through it"," even though the contract of mukātabah would be vitiated by it. [Ḥasan]"""
"21633","(21627) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us that Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib narrated to us that ʿAlī ibn ʿĀṣim informed us that Ḥātim ibn Abī Ṣaghīrah narrated from Simāk ibn Ḥarb who narrated from Zayd ibn Ṣūḥān who narrated from Salmān, in the story of his conversion to Islam, that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, \To whom do you belong?\"" I said"," \""To a woman of the Anṣār who has placed me in her garden.\"" He said"," \""O Abū Bakr!\"" He said"," \""At your service.\"" He said"," \""Purchase him.\"" So Abū Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) purchased me and set me free.\n\nThis contradicts the narrations before it. It is possible that his manumission did not take effect because not a single one of the saplings had borne fruit until the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) replanted it with his own hand and it bore fruit that same year"," and that Abū Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) purchased him during that interval and set him free. And other explanations are possible"," and Allah knows best. There is some question regarding the authenticity of some of these narrations. [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"21634","(21628) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq and Abū Bakr al-Ḥīrī both informed us, saying that Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us that Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥakam informed us that Ibn Wahb informed us that Jarīr ibn Ḥāzim narrated from Ayyūb al-Sakhtiyānī who narrated from Nāfiʿ that Ḥafṣah, the wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), entered into a mukātabah with a slave of hers for a quantity of fine cloth. Nāfiʿ said: \I came across three such people who had paid in their mukātabah contracts.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"21635","(21629) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū al-Walīd narrated to us that al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān narrated to us that Abū Bakr — meaning Ibn Abī Shaybah — narrated to us that ʿAbbād ibn al-ʿAwwām narrated from Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq who narrated from Nāfiʿ who narrated from Ibn ʿUmar that he saw no harm in a mukātabah (contract of manumission) based upon the description of good qualities (waṣfāʾ). [Ḍaʿīf]"
"21636","(21630) He said, and Abū Bakr narrated to us that Wakīʿ narrated from Ḥammād ibn Zayd who narrated from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Abī Bakr ibn Anas who said: \This is the mukātabah of Sīrīn in our possession. This is what Anas ibn Mālik contracted with his slave Sīrīn — he contracted with him for such and such thousands"," and for two slave boys who would perform work similar to his.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"21637","(21631) Abū Zakariyyā and Abū Bakr both informed us, saying that Abū al-ʿAbbās informed us that Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh informed us that Ibn Wahb informed us that Maslamah ibn ʿAlī and others narrated that al-Awzāʿī narrated to them that ʿAṭāʾ ibn Abī Rabāḥ said: Ibn ʿAbbās said regarding a man who entered into a mukātabah with his slave for three described qualities (waṣfāʾ): \There is no harm in that.\"" Al-Awzāʿī said: And Ibn Shihāb said the same. [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"21638","(21632) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr narrated to us that Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us that al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us that al-Shāfiʿī informed us that ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Ḥārith narrated from Ibn Jurayj who said: ʿAṭāʾ said: \If you enter into a mukātabah with your slave and he has sons at that time"," and he contracts with you for himself and for them"," then their father dies or one of them dies"," his value on the day he dies shall be deducted from the mukātabah. And if you set him free or some of his sons"," then it is likewise.\"" ʿAmr ibn Dīnār said the same.\n\nAl-Shāfiʿī (may Allah have mercy on him) said: \""This"," if Allah wills"," is as ʿAṭāʾ and ʿAmr ibn Dīnār said: if the sons are adults and their father contracted on their behalf by their command"," then upon each one of them is his share of the mukātabah according to his value. Whichever of them dies or is set free"," that share of the mukātabah shall be lifted from the rest.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"21639","(21633) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr narrated to us that Abū al-ʿAbbās informed us that al-Rabīʿ informed us that al-Shāfiʿī informed us that ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Ḥārith narrated from Ibn Jurayj who said: I said to ʿAṭāʾ: \I have written over two men in a sale: 'The living among you is responsible for the deceased among you"," and the solvent among you is responsible for the insolvent among you.'\"" He said: \""It is permissible.\"" ʿAmr ibn Dīnār and Sulaymān ibn Mūsā said the same. Zaʿāmah said: \""That is ḥamālah (mutual guarantee).\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"21640","(21634) Abū Saʿīd informed us that Abū al-ʿAbbās informed us that al-Rabīʿ informed us that al-Shāfiʿī informed us that ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Ḥārith narrated from Ibn Jurayj who said: I said to ʿAṭāʾ: \I have entered into a mukātabah with two of my slaves and I have written that obligation upon both of them.\"" He said: \""It is not permissible regarding your two slaves.\"" Sulaymān ibn Mūsā said the same. Ibn Jurayj said: I said to ʿAṭāʾ"," \""Why is it not permissible?\"" He said: \""Because if one of them becomes insolvent"," the other reverts to being a slave who owns nothing from you.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"21641","(21635) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us that Abu al-Walid informed us that al-Hasan ibn Sufyan informed us that Habban narrated from Ibn al-Mubarak from Ma'mar from Qatadah, and from Ibn Jurayj from 'Ata': regarding a man who enters into a mukataba (contract of manumission) with two slaves jointly, stipulating that \your living one is responsible for your dead one"," and your destitute one is responsible for your solvent one\"" — they both said: \""It is not permissible.\"""""
"21642","(21636) Abu al-Hasan 'Ali ibn Ahmad ibn 'Abdan informed us that Ahmad ibn 'Ubaid al-Saffar informed us that 'Abbas ibn al-Fadl informed us that Abu al-Walid informed us that Hammam narrated from al-'Ala' al-Jazari from 'Amr ibn Shu'aib.\n\n(And) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us that Maymun ibn Ishaq al-Hashimi in Baghdad informed us that al-'Abbas ibn Muhammad al-Dawri informed us that 'Amr ibn 'Asim al-Kalabi informed us that Hammam narrated from 'Abbas al-Jurayri, who said: 'Amr ibn Shu'aib narrated from his father from his grandfather that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Any mukatab (slave under a contract of manumission) who has been contracted for a thousand awqiyyah and pays all but ten awqiyyah remains a slave; and any mukatab who has been contracted for a hundred dinars and pays all but ten dinars remains a slave.\""\n\nThe wording is that of the hadith of 'Amr ibn 'Asim. In the narration of Abu al-Walid: \""Any slave who enters into a mukataba for a hundred dinars and pays all but ten dinars remains a slave; and any slave who enters into a mukataba for a hundred awqiyyah and pays all but ten awqiyyah remains a slave.\"" 'Abd al-Samad ibn 'Abd al-Warith also narrated it from Hammam from 'Abbas al-Jurayri. [Sahih li-ghayrihi]"""
"21643","(21637) Abu 'Ali al-Rudhbari informed us that Muhammad ibn Bakr informed us that Abu Dawud informed us that Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna informed me that 'Abd al-Samad informed us that Hammam informed us that 'Abbas al-Jurayri narrated it, saying: \A hundred awqiyyah.\"" [Hasan]"""
"21644","(21638) Abu 'Ali al-Rudhbari informed us that Muhammad ibn Bakr informed us that Abu Dawud informed us that Harun ibn 'Abd Allah informed us that Abu Badr informed me that Abu 'Utbah Isma'il ibn 'Ayyash informed me that Sulayman ibn Sulaym narrated from 'Amr ibn Shu'aib from his father from his grandfather from the Prophet (ﷺ), who said: \The mukatab remains a slave so long as a single dirham of his mukataba remains upon him.\"" [Hasan]"""
"21645","(21639) Abu Hazim al-Hafiz informed us that Abu al-Fadl ibn Khamirawayh informed us that Ahmad ibn Najdah informed us that Sa'id ibn Mansur informed us that Hushaym narrated from Hajjaj from 'Amr ibn Shu'aib from his father from his grandfather that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) delivered a sermon and said: \Any man who enters into a mukataba with his slave for a hundred awqiyyah"," and the slave is unable to pay ten awqiyyah"," he remains a slave.\""\n\nAl-Shafi'i (may Allah have mercy upon him) said in al-Qadim: \""I do not know of anyone who narrated this from the Prophet (ﷺ) except 'Amr ibn Shu'aib"," and upon this is the fatwa of the muftis.\"" [Hasan]"""
"21646","(21640) 'Ali ibn Ahmad ibn 'Abdan informed us that Ahmad ibn 'Ubaid al-Saffar informed us that Ziyad ibn al-Khalil al-Tustari informed us that Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir informed me that Hisham ibn Sulaymakh al-Makhzumi informed us that Ibn Jurayj narrated from 'Abd Allah ibn 'Amr ibn al-'As, who said: \O Messenger of Allah"," we hear from you"," so permit me to write it down.\"" He said: \""Yes.\"" The first thing he wrote on behalf of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) to the people of Makkah was: \""Two conditions in a single sale are not permissible; a sale and a loan combined are not permissible; and the sale of that which is not guaranteed is not permissible. And whoever enters into a mukataba for a hundred dirhams and pays all but ten dirhams"," he remains a slave; or for a hundred awqiyyah and pays all but one awqiyyah"," he remains a slave.\""\n\nThus I found it"," and I do not consider it preserved (as a continuous chain). [Sahih]"""
"21647","(21641) Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr informed us that al-'Abbas — Muhammad ibn Ya'qub — informed us that al-Rabi' ibn Sulayman informed us that al-Shafi'i informed us that Sufyan ibn 'Uyaynah narrated from Ibn Abi Najih from Mujahid that Zayd ibn Thabit said regarding the mukatab: \He is a slave so long as a dirham remains upon him.\"" [Sahih]"""
"21648","(21642) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz and Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr said: al-'Abbas — Muhammad ibn Ya'qub — informed us that Yahya ibn Abi Talib informed us that Yazid ibn Harun informed us that Sufyan al-Thawri narrated from 'Abd Allah ibn Abi Najih from Mujahid, who said: \Zayd used to say: 'The mukatab is a slave so long as anything of his mukataba remains upon him.' And Jabir ibn 'Abd Allah used to say: 'Their conditions are permissible among them.'\"" [Hasan]"""
"21649","(21643) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us that al-'Abbas informed us that Yahya informed us that Yazid informed us that Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid narrated from al-Sha'bi from Zayd ibn Thabit, who said: \The mukatab is a slave so long as a dirham remains upon him.\"" Al-Sha'bi said to him: \""Indeed"," Shurayh used to rule in such cases that what remained of the mukataba upon the mukatab"," if he died"," was to be paid to his patrons (mawali)"," and what remained of his estate went to his heirs.\"" Shurayh said: \""He ruled in it according to the ruling of 'Abd Allah.\"" [Da'if]"""
"21650","(21644) Abu al-Husayn ibn Bishran al-'Adl in Baghdad informed us that Isma'il ibn Muhammad al-Saffar informed us that al-Hasan ibn 'Ali ibn 'Affan informed us that Ibn Numayr narrated from 'Ubayd Allah ibn 'Umar from Nafi' from Ibn 'Umar that he used to say: \The mukatab is a slave so long as a dirham remains upon him.\"" [Hasan]"""
"21651","(21645) Abū ʿAliyy al-Rūdhbārī — may Allah have mercy upon him — informed us: Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār narrated to us: Saʿdān ibn Naṣr narrated to us: Abū Muʿāwiyah Muḥammad ibn Khāzi al-Ḍarīr narrated from ʿAmr ibn Maymūn ibn Mihrān, from Sulaymān ibn Yasār, from ʿĀʾishah — may Allah be pleased with her — who said: \I sought permission to enter upon her"," and she said"," 'Who is this?' I said"," 'Sulaymān.' She said"," 'How much remains upon you of your mukātabah (contract of manumission)?' He said: 'I said"," 'Ten awāq.' She said: 'Enter"," for you are still a slave so long as a single dirham remains upon you.'\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"21652","(21646) Abū Bakr al-Qāḍī and Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzakkī both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʤ al-Ḥakam narrated to us: Ibn Wahb informed me: Saʿīd ibn Muslim al-Madanī narrated to me, saying: I heard Sālim Sabalān, the mawlā of al-Naṣrāniyyīn, mention that he used to hire out his services to ʿĀʾishah, Umm al-Muʾminīn — may Allah be pleased with her — for Ḥajj and ʿUmrah. He said: \Then I entered into a mukātabah (contract of manumission)"," and I came and stood at the door and sought permission in a manner in which I had not previously sought permission. She disapproved of that and said"," 'O my son"," why do you not enter?' He said: 'I said"," 'O Umm al-Muʾminīn"," I have entered into a mukātabah.' She said: 'Come in to me; so long as a single dirham remains upon you"," you remain a slave"," for as long as a single dirham of your mukātabah remains upon you.'\"" [Ḥasan]"""
"21653","(21647) He said: Ibn Wahb informed me: ʿUmar ibn Qays narrated from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Qāsim, from his father, who said: \Indeed"," the Ummahāt al-Muʾminīn (Mothers of the Believers) used to lower the veil for a mukātab (a slave under a contract of manumission) so long as a single dirham remained upon him. When he paid it"," they drew the veil before him.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"21654","(21648) Abū Ḥāzi al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-Faḍl ibn Khamīruwayh narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn Najdah narrated to us: Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr narrated to us: Hushaym narrated from Khālid, from Abū Qilābah, who said: \The wives of the Messenger of Allah — ﷺ — used not to observe hijāb (veiling) from a mukātab so long as a dīnār remained upon him.\""\n\nThe narrations differ regarding ʿUmar — may Allah be pleased with him — and it has been reported from him as follows: [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"21655","(21649) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib informed us: Yazīd ibn Hārūn informed us: Ibn Abī ʿArūbah narrated from Qatādah, from Maʿbad al-Juhanī, from ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb — may Allah be pleased with him — who said: \The mukātab is a slave so long as a single dirham remains upon him.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"21656","(21650) It has been reported from him as follows: Abū al-Qāsim ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿUbayd Allāh al-Ḥurfī in Baghdād informed us: Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Sulaymān ibn al-Ḥārith narrated to us: Qabīṣah ibn ʿUqbah al-Suwāʾī narrated to us: Sufyān narrated from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Masʿūdī, from al-Qāsim ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, from Jābir ibn Samurah, from ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb — may Allah be pleased with him: \When the mukātab pays half"," he is not to be treated as a slave (i.e."," he is not to be re-enslaved).\"" Al-Qāsim ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān's hearing (samāʿ) from Jābir ibn Samurah is not established. If this narration is sound"," it is as though he intended that the mukātab has drawn close to emancipation"," and it is more appropriate that he be given time to earn what remains"," and that he not be returned to slavery due to inability to pay the remainder. And Allah knows best. [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"21657","(21651) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-Walīd narrated to us: al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān narrated to us: Ḥibbān narrated from Ibn al-Mubārak, from Maʿmar, from al-Zuhrī, from Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyab, who said: \A mukātab divorced his wife during the time of ʿUthmān — may Allah be pleased with him — and he (ʿUthmān) treated him in the status of a slave.\""\n\nAnd from Ibn al-Mubārak"," from Yaḥyā ibn Abī Kathīr"," from ʿIkrimah"," from Ibn ʿAbbās"," who said: \""No ḥadd (prescribed punishment) is carried out upon the mukābat except the ḥadd of a slave.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"21658","(21652) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib informed us: Yazīd ibn Hārūn informed us: Ḥammād ibn Salamah narrated from Ayyūb, from ʿIkrimah, from Ibn ʿAbbās — may Allah be pleased with both of them — from the Prophet — ﷺ — who said: \When the mukātab is subject to a ḥadd (prescribed punishment) or an inheritance"," he inherits according to the proportion of him that has been freed"," and the ḥadd is carried out upon him according to the proportion of him that has been freed.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"21659","(21653) With this chain of narration (isnad), from ʿIkrimah, from Ibn ʿAbbās, from the Prophet — ﷺ — who said: \The mukātab pays the diyah (blood money) in proportion to what he has paid (toward his freedom) at the rate of a free man"," and the remainder at the rate of a slave.\""\n\nAbū ʿĪsā said — as it has reached me — that I asked al-Bukhārī about this hadith"," and he said: \""Some of them narrated this hadith from Ayyūb"," from ʿIkrimah"," from ʿAlī — may Allah be pleased with him.\""\n\nThe Shaykh — may Allah have mercy upon him — said: He means by this the second hadith. As for the first"," it is from the individual narrations (afrād) of Ḥammād. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"21660","(21654) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf al-Aṣbahānī informed him: Abū Saʿīd ibn al-Aʿrābī narrated to us: al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad al-Zaʿfarānī narrated to us: ʿAffān narrated to us: Wuhayb narrated to us: Ayyūb narrated from ʿIkrimah, from ʿAlī — may Allah be pleased with him — who said: The Messenger of Allah — ﷺ — said: \The mukātab pays according to the proportion of what he has paid (toward his freedom).\""\n\nThe Shaykh — may Allah have mercy upon him — said: The narration of ʿIkrimah from ʿAlī is mursal (disconnected). And Ḥammād ibn Zayd and Ismāʿīl ibn Ibrāhīm narrated it from Ayyūb"," from ʿIkrimah"," from the Prophet — ﷺ — as a mursal narration"," and Ismāʿīl made it the statement (qawl) of ʿIkrimah. Al-Bukhārī — may Allah have mercy upon him — said: And Yaḥyā ibn Abī Kathīr narrated this hadith from ʿIkrimah"," from Ibn ʿAbbās"," from the Prophet — ﷺ.\n\nThe Shaykh said: There is a difference of opinion regarding its being raised (marfūʿ) to the Prophet. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"21661","(21655) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān and Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Ḥasan al-Ghaḍāʾirī informed us in Baghdad, they both said: Abū Jaʿfar ʿAmr al-Razzāz narrated to us: al-Ḥasan ibn Thawāb al-Taghlabī narrated to us: Yazīd ibn Hārūn informed us: Hishām —\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Bakr ibn Fūrak, may Allah have mercy on him, informed us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us: Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb narrated to us: Abū Dāwūd narrated to us: Hishām, from Yaḥyā ibn Abī Kathīr, from ʿIkrimah, from Ibn ʿAbbās, that the Prophet ﷺ said: *The mukātab (a slave contracted for emancipation) shall pay the diyah (blood-money) of a free man in proportion to the portion of him that has been emancipated, and the diyah of a slave in proportion to the portion of him that remains in bondage.*\n\nAbū Dāwūd added in his narration: He said, and ʿAlī, may Allah be pleased with him, and Marwān used to say that. Abū ʿAlī al-Taghlabī said: I asked Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal about this hadith, and he said: I incline toward the hadith of Barīrah that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded regarding her purchase — meaning that she remained under the ruling of slavery until he commanded her purchase.\n\nAnd a group narrated it from Hishām al-Dastawāʾī. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"21662","(21656) Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar narrated it from Hishām, from Yaḥyā, from ʿIkrimah, from Ibn ʿAbbās, similar to it, but he did not raise it (to the Prophet). Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Muqriʾ informed him: al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us: Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Abī Bakr narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar, from Hishām, and he mentioned it, and he said: Yaḥyā said: ʿAlī, may Allah be pleased with him, and Marwān used to say that.\n\nAnd Ḥajjāj al-Ṣawwāf, Muʿāwiya ibn Salām, and Abān ibn Yazīd narrated it from Yaḥyā ibn Abī Kathīr, raised (marfūʿan). [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"21663","(21657) ʿAlī ibn al-Mubārak narrated it from Yaḥyā, raised (marfūʿan), and he added in it from Ibn ʿAbbās, from his statement: *That which contradicts the raised hadith in qiyās (analogical reasoning) and contradicts what Ḥammād ibn Salamah narrated in the explicit text (naṣṣ).* Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed him: Aḥmad ibn Sulaymān ibn al-Ḥasan al-Faqīh narrated to us: al-Ḥasan ibn Mukram narrated to us: ʿUthmān ibn ʿUmar narrated to us: ʿAlī ibn al-Mubārak, from Yaḥyā ibn Abī Kathīr, from ʿIkrimah, from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ decreed regarding a mukātab who is killed: he is to be compensated with the diyah of a free man in proportion to what he has paid (toward his emancipation).\n\nYaḥyā said: ʿIkrimah said, from Ibn ʿAbbās: *The ḥadd (prescribed punishment) of the slave is to be carried out upon him.* The hadith of ʿIkrimah — when there is disagreement regarding it, suspension (tawqīf) is obligatory. And this position is only narrated from ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib, may Allah be pleased with him, namely that he is emancipated in proportion to what he has paid. As for its authenticity from the Prophet ﷺ, there is consideration. And Allah knows best. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"21664","(21658) Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm informed us: Abū Naṣr al-ʿIrāqī narrated to us: Sufyān ibn Muḥammad al-Jawharī narrated to us: ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥasan narrated to us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Walīd narrated to us: Sufyān, from Ṭāriq ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, who said: I heard al-Shaʿbī saying: Zayd ibn Thābit used to say: *The mukātab remains a slave as long as a single dirham remains upon him.* And ʿAlī, may Allah be pleased with him, used to say: *He is emancipated in proportion to what he has paid.*\n\nAnd from Ṭāriq, from al-Shaʿbī, from ʿAlī, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: *The mukātab inherits in proportion to what he has paid.* [Ḍaʿīf]"
"21665","(21659) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib informed us: Yazīd ibn Hārūn narrated to us: Sufyān, from al-Mughīrah, from Ibrāhīm, who said: ʿAbd Allāh said: *When the mukātab pays the price of his neck, he is free (gharīm).* [Ḥasan]"
"21666","(21660) And with his isnād, he said: Sufyān informed us, from Manṣūr, from Ibrāhīm, who said: ʿAbd Allāh said: *When the mukātab pays a third or a quarter, he is free (gharīm).* [Ḥasan]"
"21667","(21661) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Sulaymān al-Mawṣilī narrated to us: ʿAlī ibn Ḥarb narrated to us: Sufyān, from al-Zuhrī, from Nahbān, a mukātab of Umm Salamah, who said: I heard Umm Salamah saying: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: *If any of you has a mukātab and he possesses the means to pay, let her observe ḥijāb (veiling) from him.* [Ḥasan]"
"21668","(21662) And Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us: Muḥammad ibn Bakr narrated to us: Abū Dāwūd narrated to us: Musaddad ibn Musarhad narrated to us: Sufyān, and he mentioned it with its like. [Ḥasan]"
"21669","(21663) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī al-Ṣanʿānī in Makkah narrated to us: Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm informed us: ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us: Maʿmar, from al-Zuhrī — Nahbān, a mukātab of Umm Salamah, narrated to me. He said: I used to lead her by the desert or by the mountain passes. She said: Who is this? I said: I am Nahbān. She said: I have left the remainder of your kitābah (emancipation contract) with your nephew, Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Abī Umayyah — I had assisted him with it for his marriage. He said: I said: No, by Allah, I shall never pay it to him. She said: If your only concern is that you should enter upon me or see me, then by Allah, you shall never see me. I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying: *When the mukātab possesses the means to pay, observe ḥijāb from him.*\n\nAnd al-Shāfiʿī, may Allah have mercy on him, narrated in his older work from Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah, and he said: I did not preserve from Sufyān that al-Zuhrī heard it from Nahbān, and I have not seen anyone among the people of knowledge whose approval I accept who authenticates either of these two hadiths. And Allah knows best — he means the hadith of Nahbān and the hadith of ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb, that the Prophet ﷺ said: *Whoever contracts his slave for a hundred awāq and he pays them except ten awāq, he remains a slave.*\n\nAl-Shāfiʿī, may Allah have mercy on him, only narrated the hadith of ʿAmr with a disconnected chain (munqaṭiʿ). And we have narrated it through other routes from ʿAmr, from his father, from his grandfather, from the Prophet ﷺ. As for the hadith of Nahbān, Maʿmar mentioned in it that al-Zuhrī heard it from Nahbān, except that al-Bukhārī and Muslim, the authors of the Ṣaḥīḥ, did not include his hadith in the Ṣaḥīḥ, as though his ʿadālah (trustworthiness) was not established to them, or he did not emerge from the level of jāhiliyyah (ignorance) through the narration of a trustworthy narrator from him. And other than al-Zuhrī narrated from him — if it is preserved — and that is what Qabīṣah narrated from Sufyān, from Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, mawlā of the family of Ṭalḥah, from a mukātab of Uamm Salamah called Nahbān, and he mentioned this hadith accordingly. Ibn Khuzaymah mentioned it from Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣaghānī from Qabīṣah. And Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā al-Dhuhlī mentioned that Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, mawlā of the family of Ṭalḥah, narrated from al-Zuhrī, who said: Umm Salamah had a mukātab called Nahbān. And it was narrated from Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf, from Sufyān, from him, so the hadith reverts to the narration of al-Zuhrī. Al-Shāfiʿī, may Allah have mercy on him, said: And it is possible that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded Umm Salamah — if he commanded her — to observe ḥijāb from her mukātab when he possessed the means to pay, by virtue of what Allah has magnified for the wives of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, the Mothers of the Believers, may Allah have mercy on them, and by what He specified for them and distinguished them from other women, provided they remain dutiful. Then he recited the verses concerning their specification, that He imposed upon them ḥijāb from the believers, and they are the Mothers of the Believers, and He did not impose upon any woman other than them to veil herself from one whom marriage to her is forbidden. And in his statement ﷺ, \If\"" — he said it meaning \""If any of you\"" — referring specifically to his wives. Then he continued the speech until he said: And along with this"," a woman's veiling herself from one who may see her is expansive for her. And the Prophet ﷺ commanded — meaning Sawdah — to veil herself from a man"," and that was her brother"," and this resembles a matter of iḥtiyāṭ (precaution). And veiling from one who may see her is permissible. And Abū al-ʿAbbās ibn Surayj said regarding its meaning: The ḥijāb of the wives from him is to urge him toward prompt payment and toward emancipation"," and not to leave that on account of his entering upon them. [Ḥasan]"""
"21670","(21664) Abū Bakr al-Qāḍī and Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʤAbd al-Ḥakam informed us: Ibn Wahb informed me: Ibn Samʿān informed me, from Ibn Shihāb, that Umm Salamah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, sold Nahbān, her mukātab, and she said: Pay what remains of your kitābah to your nephew, ʿAbd Allāh ibn Abī Umayyah, for I have assisted him with it, and do not speak to me except from behind a ḥijāb. Nahbān wept. Umm Salamah, may Allah be pleased with her, said: Indeed, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to us: *When one of you contracts her slave in emancipation, and there remains anything of his kitābah, let him see her. When he pays it, let none of you speak except from behind a ḥijāb.*\n\nThus did ʿAbd Allāh ibn Ziyād ibn Samʿān narrate it, and he is weak (ḍaʿīf). The narration of the trustworthy narrators from al-Zuhrī contradicts it. [Ḍaʿīf]"
"21671","(21665) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʤAbd al-Ḥakam informed us; Ibn Wahb informed us; Mālik ibn Anas reported to me from Rabīʿah, from al-Qāsim ibn Muḥammad, from ʿĀʾishah, the wife of the Prophet (peace be upon him), that she said: \In the matter of Barīrah"," there three established practices: she was given the choice regarding her husband when she was emancipated; and some meat was given to her as charity. The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) came to me while the pot was on the fire"," and he called for food. He was brought bread and some stew from the house's stew"," and he said: 'Did I not see a pot on the fire containing meat?' They said: 'Yes"," O Messenger of Allah"," that is meat that was given in charity to Barīrah"," and we disliked that we should feed you from it.' He said: 'For her it is charity"," and from her it is a gift for us.' And the Prophet (peace be upon him) said regarding her: 'Indeed"," the walāʾ (right of clientage) belongs to the one who emancipates.'\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbd Allās ibn Yūsuf and others from Mālik"," and Muslim narrated it from Abī al-Ṭāhir from Ibn Wahb. [Weak"," but agreed upon]"""
"21672","(21666) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-Walīd al-Faqīh informed us; Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Zuhayr narrated to us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Hāshim narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān narrated to us; Abū Bakr narrated to us; both said: Wakīʿ narrated to us; Jaʿfar ibn Burqān narrated to us from Maymūn ibn Mihrān, who said: \Ibn ʿUmar contracted a mukātabah (deed of emancipation) with a slave of his. The slave came with his instalment when it became due"," and Ibn ʿUmar said: 'Where is this from?' He said: 'I used to beg and work.' He said: 'Do you wish to feed me the refuse of people? You are free"," and your instalment is yours.'\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"21673","(21667) Abū Ḥāmid Aḥmad ibn ʿAlī al-Isfarāʾinī informed us; Zāhir ibn Aḥmad informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Ziyād al-Naysābūrī narrated to us; Yūsuf ibn Saʿīd narrated to us; Ḥajjāj narrated to us; Ibn Jurayj narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Zakariyyā al-ʿAnbarī informed us; Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Salām narrated to us; Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm informed us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Saʿd Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad al-Mālinī informed us; Abū Aḥmad ibn ʿAdī al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān narrated to us; Isḥāq al-Ḥanẓalī informed us; ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us; Ibn Jurayj informed us; ʿAṭāʾ ibn al-Sāʾib reported to me that ʿAbd Allāh ibn Ḥabīb informed him — and in the narration of Ḥajjāj, it is from Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ʿAbd Allāh ibn Ḥabīb — from ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Prophet (peace be upon him), regarding the verse: \And give them from the wealth of Allah which He has given you\"" (al-Qurʾān 24:33) — he said: \""One quarter of the mukātabah.\"" And in the narration of Abū ʿAbd Allāh"," he said: \""He leaves one quarter for the mukātab.\""\n\nḤajjāj ibn Muḥammad added: Ibn Jurayj said: \""Someone other than one person from those who heard this ḥadīth from ʿAṭāʾ ibn al-Sāʾib informed me that he did not raise it to the Prophet (peace be upon him).\"" Ibn Jurayj said: \""And he raised it for me.\"" [Weak]"""
"21674","(21668) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us; Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-Qaṭṭān informed us; Abū al-Azhar narrated to us; Rūḥ narrated to us; Ibn Jurayj and Hishām ibn Abī ʿAbd Allāh both informed us; ʿAṭāʾ ibn al-Sāʾib informed us from Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī, from ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him), regarding the verse: \And give them from the wealth of Allah which He has given you\"" — he said: \""One quarter of the kitābah (deed of emancipation).\"" This is the correct version"," and it is mawqūf (stopped at the companion).\n\nLikewise"," Warqāʾ ibn ʿAmr"," Khālid ibn ʿAbd Allāh"," and Asbāṭ ibn Muḥammad narrated it from ʿAṭāʾ ibn al-Sāʾib as mawqūf. And likewise"," others narrated it from Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ʿAbd Allāh ibn Ḥabīb al-Sulamī"," from ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him)"," as mawqūf. [Weak]"""
"21675","(21669) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us; Abū Ḥāmid ibn Bilāl informed us; Abū al-Azhar narrated to us; Rūḥ narrated to us; Shuʿbah and al-Thawrī narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Naṣr ibn Qatādah informed us; Abū Manṣūr al-ʿAbbās ibn al-Faḍl al-Naḍrawī informed us; Aḥmad ibn Najdah narrated to us; Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr narrated to us; Abū ʿAwanah narrated to us — all of them from ʿAbd al-Aʿlā, from Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī, from ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him), regarding the verse: \And give them from the wealth of Allah which He has given you\"" — he said: \""One quarter.\""\n\nAnd in the narration of Abū ʿAwanah: \""One quarter of his mukātabah.\"" [Weak]"""
"21676","(21670) And Abū Bakr al-Ardistānī informed us; Abū Naṣr al-ʿIrāqī informed us; Sufyān ibn Muḥammad narrated to us; ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥasan narrated to us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Walīd narrated to us; Sufyān narrated to us from ʿAbd al-Aʿlā, who said: \I witnessed Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī contract a mukātabah with a slave of his for four thousand"," and he stipulated upon him that if he fell short"," he would be returned to slavery"," and whatever I have taken would be mine. He waived one thousand of the four thousand and said: 'Indeed"," I heard your intimate friend ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) say regarding the verse: \""And give them from the wealth of Allah which He has given you\"" — one quarter.'\"" [Weak]"""
"21677","(21671) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār narrated to us; Wakīʿ narrated to us from Abī Shaybah, from ʿIkrimah, from Ibn ʿAbbās, that ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) contracted a mukātabah with a slave of his, known as Abū Umayyah. The slave came with his instalment when it became due, and ʿUmar said: \Go and use it towards your mukātabah.\"" He said: \""O Commander of the Faithful"," if you were to leave it until the next instalment.\"" He said: \""I fear that I may not live to see that.\"" Then he recited: \""And give them from the wealth of Allah which He has given you.\"" ʿIkrimah said: \""And it was the first instalment ever paid in Islam.\"" [Weak]"""
"21678","(21672) Abū Bakr al-Ardistānī informed us; Abū Naṣr al-ʿIrāqī informed us; Sufyān ibn Muḥammad al-Jawharī narrated to us; ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥasan narrated to us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Walīd narrated to us; Sufyān narrated to us from ʿAbd al-Malik ibn Abī Bashīr; Faḍālah ibn Abī Umayyah narrated to me from his father, that ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him) contracted a mukātabah with him, and he (ʿUmar) borrowed two hundred from Ḥafṣah for his stipend and helped him with it. He (the narrator) said: \I mentioned that to ʿIkrimah"," and he said: 'It is the word of Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic: \""And give them from the wealth of Allah which He has given you.\""'\"" [Weak]"""
"21679","(21673) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr narrated to us; Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm informed us; al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us; al-Shāfiʿī informed us; al-Thiqah informed us from Ayyūb.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us; Abū al-Walīd narrated to us; Jaʿfar ibn Aḥmad narrated to us; ʿAmr ibn Zurārah narrated to us; Ismāʿīl — that is, Ibn ʿUlayyah — narrated to us from Ayyūb, from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar, that he contracted a mukātabah with a slave of his for thirty-five thousand, and he waived five thousand from him — I think he said: \From his last instalments.\"" The wording of both their narrations is the same. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"21680","(21674) And Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥakam informed us; Ibn Wahb informed us; Mukhramah ibn Bukayr reported to me from his father, from Nāfiʿ, who said: \ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar contracted a mukātabah with a slave of his called Sharaf for thirty-five thousand dirhams"," and he waived for him five thousand dirhams from the end of his kitābah.\"" Nāfiʿ did not mention that he gave him anything other than what he waived for him. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"21681","Abu Zakariyya ibn Abi Ishaq narrated to us — Abu al-Hasan al-Tarā'ifī narrated to us — ʿUthmān ibn Saʿīd narrated to us — ʿAbd Allāh ibn Ṣāliḥ narrated from Muʿāwiya ibn Ṣāliḥ from ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭalḥa from Ibn ʿAbbās regarding the words of Allah, **\And give them from the wealth of Allah which He has given you\""** — he said: \""Reduce from their mukātabah (contract of manumission).\"" [Weak]"""
"21682","Abu Ṭāhir al-Faqīh narrated to us — Abu Bakr al-Qaṭṭān narrated to us — Abu al-Azhar narrated to us — Rūḥ narrated to us — Ḥammād narrated from al-Jurayrī from Abū Naḍra from Abū Saʿīd, the freedman of Abī Usayd, that he contracted a mukātabah with one of his freedmen for one thousand two hundred dirhams. He said: \I brought him my mukābatī (the amount of my contract)"," and he returned two hundred dirhams to me.\"" [Authentic]"""
"21683","Abu Naṣr ibn Qatāda narrated to us — Abu Manṣūr al-Naḍrawī narrated to us — Aḥmad ibn Najda narrated to us — Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr narrated to us — Hushaym narrated from Muḥammad ibn Sālim from al-Shaʿbī, who said: \Ibn ʿUmar used to like that whatever remained from the last instalment of his mukātabah (be waived).\"" [Weak]"""
"21684","He said: And Hushaym narrated to us from Ibn ʿAwn from Ibn Sīrīn, the same. [Weak]"
"21685","Abu ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us — Abu al-Walīd narrated to us — al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān narrated to us — Ḥabbān narrated from Ibn al-Mubārak from al-Ḥakam ibn ʿAṭiyya from Muḥammad ibn Sīrīn regarding the words of Allah, **\And give them from the wealth of Allah which He has given you\""** — he said: \""It pleased them that a man should leave (i.e."," waive) a portion of his mukātabah for his mukātab (slave under contract of manumission).\""\n\nAnd from Ibn al-Mubārak from Ibn Abī Najīḥ from Mujāhid regarding the words of Allah"," **\""And give them from the wealth of Allah which He has given you\""** — he said: \""He should leave a portion of the mukātabah.\"" [Weak]"""
"21686","Abu Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr narrated to us — Abu al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm narrated to us — al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān narrated to us — al-Shāfiʿī narrated to us — ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Ḥārith narrated from Ibn Jurayj, who said: \I asked him — meaning ʿAṭāʾ — about a mukātab who dies and leaves free children and leaves more wealth than what remains of his kitābah (contract).\"" He said: \""What remains of his kitābah shall be paid on his behalf"," and whatever surplus remains goes to his children.\"" I asked: \""Did you hear this from anyone?\"" He said: \""They claim that ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṣālib"," may Allah be pleased with him"," used to judge according to this.\"" [Authentic]"""
"21687","And with his chain of narration, he said: al-Shāfiʿī narrated to us — ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Ḥārith narrated from Ibn Jurayj — Ibn Ṭāwūs informed me from his father that he used to say: \What is owed upon him shall be paid"," and what remains goes to his children.\"" And ʿAmr ibn Dīnār said: \""I do not think it goes to his children.\""\n\nAl-Shāfiʿī"," may Allah have mercy on him"," said — meaning that it (the surplus) goes to his master"," and Allah knows best. And with this statement of ʿAmr ibn Dīnār we concur"," and it is the view of Zayd ibn Thābit. As for what is narrated from ʿAṭāʾ that he heard it from ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib"," may Allah be pleased with him — it is narrated from him that he used to say regarding the mukātab: \""He is freed in proportion to what has been paid.\"" And I do not know whether this is authentically established from him or not. We only follow the statement of Zayd in this matter. [Authentic]"""
"21688","Abu Ḥāzim al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us — Abu al-Faḍl ibn Khamīruwayh narrated to us — Aḥmad ibn Najda narrated to us — Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr narrated to us — Sufyān narrated from Ibn Abī Najīḥ from Mujāhid from Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh regarding the mukātabūn (slaves under contract of manumission), who said: \Their conditions (stipulated between them) are valid.\"" And Zayd ibn Thābit said: \""He remains a slave so long as a single dirham remains upon him.\"" And ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib"," may Allah be pleased with him"," said: \""He is freed in proportion to what he has paid.\"" [Authentic]"""
"21689","And Abu ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us — Abu al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us — Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib narrated to us — Yazīd ibn Hārūn narrated to us — Muḥammad ibn Sālim narrated from al-Shaʿbī, who said: \Zayd ibn Thābit"," may Allah be pleased with him"," used to say: 'The mukātab is a slave so long as a single dirham remains upon him; he neither inherits nor is inherited from.' And ʿAlī"," may Allah be pleased with him"," used to say: 'When the mukātab dies and leaves wealth"," what he left is divided according to what has been paid and what remains. Whatever corresponds to what has been paid goes to the heirs"," and whatever corresponds to what remains goes to his mawālī (those who contracted his manumission).' And ʿAbd Allāh"," may Allah be pleased with him"," used to say: 'What remains of his mukātabah is paid to his mawālī"," and what remains (of the estate) goes to his heirs.'\"" [Weak]"""
"21690","Abu ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us — Abu al-Walīd narrated to us — Ibrāhīm ibn Abī Ṭālib narrated to us — al-Ḥasan ibn ʿĪsā narrated to us — Ibn al-Mubārak narrated from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿUmar from Nāfiʿ from Ibn ʿUmar, who said: \When the mukātab dies having paid a portion of his kitābah and leaves wealth that is greater than his mukātabah"," his wealth and whatever he leaves belongs to his master; his heirs receive nothing from his wealth.\"" [Authentic]"""
"21691","(21685) Abu 'Abdillah al-Hafiz informed us; Abu al-Walid narrated to us; Ibrahim ibn Abi Talib narrated to us; al-Hasan ibn 'Isa narrated to us from Ibn al-Mubarak from 'Ubaydullah from Nafi' from Ibn 'Umar: that he had a mukatab (a slave contracted for emancipation), and his mukatab had a child by a slave-girl of his. The mukatab had paid fifteen thousand from his kitabah (contract of emancipation), then he died. Ibn 'Umar seized all of his wealth and gave nothing to his child; he enslaved his child and seized his wealth as well. [Sahih]"
"21692","(21686) Abu 'Abdillah al-Hafiz informed us; Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us; Yahya ibn Abi Talib narrated to us; Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us; Ibn Abi 'Arubah narrated to us from Qatadah, who said: 'Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, said: \When a mukatab dies and leaves wealth"," it belongs to his mawali (those who contracted his emancipation)"," and his heirs receive nothing.\"" [Da'if]"""
"21693","(21687) Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ibrahim informed us; Abu Nasr al-'Iraqi narrated to us; Sufyan ibn Muhammad al-Jawhari narrated to us; 'Ali ibn al-Hasan narrated to us; 'Abdullah ibn al-Walid narrated to us; Sufyan narrated to us from Sulayman al-Taymi from a man from Ma'bad al-Juhani that Mu'awiyah, may Allah be pleased with him, used to say: \When a mukatab dies and leaves sufficient wealth to fulfill his contract"," his mawali receive what is owed to them"," and the remainder goes to his heirs.\"" And 'Umar"," may Allah be pleased with him"," used to say: \""He remains a slave so long as a single dirham remains upon him.\"" [Da'if]"""
"21694","(21688) Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr narrated to us; Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us; al-Rabi' ibn Sulayman narrated to us; al-Shafi'i narrated to us; 'Abdullah ibn al-Harith narrated to us from Ibn Jurayj, who said: I said to him — meaning 'Ata' — \My mukatab has become insolvent and has left wealth"," and the people have debts upon him"," but he has not left enough to fulfill his contract. Shall I give precedence to the rights of the people over my kitabah?\"" He said: Yes. And 'Amr ibn Dinar also said the same to me.\n\nIbn Jurayj said: I said to 'Ata': \""Shall I apportion to them a share from the installments of his contract that have become due"," since he earned his labor during the year?\"" He said: No.\n\nAl-Shafi'i"," may Allah have mercy upon him"," said: \""This is what we follow. When a mukatab dies and debts are upon him"," the debts of the people are given precedence"," because he died as a slave"," the kitabah is void"," the master has no claim of debt upon him"," and whatever wealth remains belongs to the master.\"" [Sahih]"""
"21695","(21689) Abu 'Abdillah al-Hafiz informed us; Abu al-Walid narrated to us; al-Hasan ibn Sufyan narrated to us; Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us; 'Abdullah ibn Idris narrated to us from Sa'id from Qatadah from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab from Zayd ibn Thabit, who said: \Precedence is given to the debt.\"" [Da'if]"""
"21696","(21690) Abu Nasr ibn Qatadah informed us; Abu 'Amr ibn Matar and Abu al-Hasan al-Sarraj both narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Sulayman al-Marwazi narrated to us; 'Asim ibn 'Ali narrated to us; Shu'bah narrated to us. Qatadah informed me, saying: I said to Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab: \Shurayh used to say that precedence is given to the kitabah over the debt\"" — or he said"," \""they are shared between them\"" — Shu'bah was uncertain. Ibn al-Musayyab said: \""Shurayh was mistaken"," even though he was a judge. Zayd ibn Thabit said: Precedence is given to the debt.\""\n\nThe Shaykh"," may Allah have mercy upon him"," said: \""It has also been narrated from Shurayh that he said: Precedence is given to the debt.\"" [Hasan]"""
"21697","(21691) Abu 'Abdillah al-Hafiz informed us; al-Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn Halim narrated to us; Abu al-Muwajjah informed us; 'Abdan informed us; Shu'bah narrated to us from al-Hakam from Shurayh regarding a mukatab who dies and upon whom there is a debt. He said: \Precedence is given to his debt.\"" [Da'if]"""
"21698","(21692) Abu 'Abdillah al-Hafiz informed us; Abu al-Walid narrated to us; al-Hasan ibn Sufyan narrated to us; Habban narrated to us; Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us from Ya'qub ibn al-Qa'qa' from Matar from al-Hasan regarding a slave jointly owned by partners: \None of them may contract a kitabah with him without the permission of his co-owners. If he does so"," what he has received shall be taken and divided among them"," and the slave remains among them as a shared property.\"" [Da'if]"""
"21699","(21693) Abu 'Abdillah al-Hafiz informed us; Abu al-Walid narrated to us; al-Hasan ibn Sufyan narrated to us; Abu Bakr — meaning Ibn Abi Shaybah — narrated to us; Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us from Ya'qub from Matar from al-Hasan regarding a slave jointly owned by three persons, one of whom contracted a kitabah with him. He said: \What he received shall be taken from him and divided among his co-owners"," and the slave remains among them; his kitabah is not valid.\"" He said: \""'Ata' used to say: The portion of emancipation corresponding to the share that was freed shall be enforced.\"" [Da'if]"""
"21700","(21694) He said: And Abu Bakr narrated to us; Hushaym narrated to us from Yunus from al-Hasan regarding a slave jointly owned by two men. He said: \It is disliked for one of them to contract a kitabah with him without the permission of his partner. If he does so"," it shall be divided between them.\"" [Da'if]"""
"21701","(21695) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū al-Walīd narrated to us that Abū al-ʿAbbās ibn Surayj narrated to us that Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq narrated to us that ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAbd al-Wahhāb al-Ḥajabī narrated on the authority of ʿAbd al-Wāḥid ibn Ziyād, on the authority of Abī al-Jaḥm Ṣubayḥ ibn al-Qāsim, who said: \I contracted a mukātabah (deed of manumission) for twenty thousand on the condition that I would not leave al-Kūfah. So I asked Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyib"," and he said: 'They have imposed twenty thousand upon you and constrained the land for you — go forth (travel).' He said: 'And I asked Saʿīd ibn Jubayr"," and he said the same.'\"" [Weak]"""
"21702","(21696) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū al-Walīd narrated to us that Jaʿfar ibn Aḥmad narrated to us that Jubārah narrated on the authority of Qays ibn al-Rabīʿ, on the authority of Ṣubayḥ, who said: \I contracted a mukātabah for ten thousand"," and it was stipulated upon me that I would not travel. He (my master) took me to Sharīḥ (the judge)"," and he said: 'You wish to constrain the world upon yourself — travel (nevertheless).'\"" [Weak]"""
"21703","(21697) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh informed us that Abū al-Walīd narrated to us that al-Sarrāj narrated to us that Ziyād ibn Ayyūb narrated to us that Hushaym narrated on the authority of Yūnus, on the authority of al-Ḥasan, who said: \Such a condition is a false condition. He may go forth if he wishes.\"" And we have narrated it from al-Shaʿbī. [Weak]"""
"21704","(21698) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr narrated to us that Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us that al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us that al-Shāfiʿī informed us that ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Ḥārith narrated on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, who said: \I said to ʿAṭāʾ: 'A mukātab (slave under a manumission contract) belongs to a group of people"," and some of them wish to settle (their share of the contract) with him?' He said: 'No"," unless there is for him (the mukātab) an amount of wealth equivalent to what these (partners) settled upon.'\""\n\nAl-Shāfiʿī"," raḥimahu Allāh"," said: \""And this is what we adhere to: none of the partners in a mukātabah may take anything from the mukātab without his co-owner's consent.\"" [Weak]"""
"21705","(21699) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū al-Walīd narrated to us that al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān narrated to us that Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah narrated to us that Ḥafṣ ibn Ghiyāth narrated on the authority of Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad, on the authority of his father, on the authority of ʿAlī, raḍiya Allāh ʿanhu, who said: \Her child is in her status\"" — meaning the child of a mukātabah. [Weak]"""
"21706","(21700) Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm informed us that Abū Naṣr al-ʿIrāqī narrated to us that Sufyān ibn Muḥammad narrated to us that ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥasan narrated to us that ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Walīd narrated to us that Sufyān narrated on the authority of Ayyūb al-Sakhtiyānī, on the authority of Ibn Sīrīn, on the authority of Sharīḥ, that he was asked about the sale of the child of a mukātabah. He said: \Her children are from her: if she is manumitted"," they are manumitted; and if she remains enslaved"," they remain enslaved.\"" [Fair]"""
"21707","(21701) He (Ibn Sīrīn) said: \And Sufyān narrated to us on the authority of al-Mughīrah"," on the authority of Ibrāhīm"," who said: 'Her child may be sold for the purpose of manumission"," so that the mother may thereby assist herself in her mukātabah.' But the statement of Sharīḥ is more beloved to Sufyān.\"" [Fair]"""
"21708","(21702) Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan and Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥakam informed us that Ibn Wahb informed us that Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr narrated on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, who said: \I said to ʿAṭāʾ: 'A mukātab does not stipulate that whatever children she bears will be included in my kitābah (manumission contract)"," and then she gives birth.' He said: 'They are included in his kitābah.' And ʿAmr ibn Dīnār said the same.\"" [Weak]"""
"21709","(21703) Ibn Jurayj said: \And Ibn Abī Mulaykah informed me that her mother had contracted a mukābat"," then she bore two children"," and then she died. So I asked ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Zubayr about her"," and he said: 'If they were present at the time of their mother's kitābah"," then they are subject to its ruling. If they fulfill it"," they are manumitted.' And ʿAmr ibn Dīnār said the same.\"" [Authentic]"""
"21710","(21704) Ibn Jurayj said: \And ʿAṭāʾ ibn Abī Rabāḥ said: 'If a mukātab contracts a mukābat and has no children"," and then he has children from a concubine of his"," and their father dies"," nothing shall be reduced from (the amount owed)"," and they shall remain upon their father's kitābah. If they wish"," they may fulfill it; and if they wish"," the kitābah of their father may be annulled"," and they shall be slaves for him.' Thus they said.\n\nAnd we say: If the mukātab or the mukābatah dies before paying the sum of the kitābah"," they die as slaves"," and their children are slaves — by analogy to what has been established regarding the mukātab: he remains a slave so long as a single dirham remains upon him.\"" [Weak]"""
"21711","(21705) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm narrated to us, al-Rabīʿ informed us, al-Shāfiʿī informed us, ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Ḥārith reported from Ibn Jurayj, who said: I said to ʿAṭāʾ: A man contracted a mukātabah (deed of manumission) with his slave and then settled the payment, but the slave concealed from him wealth and slaves and other property besides that. He said: It belongs to the master. ʿAmr ibn Dīnār and Sulaymān ibn Mūsā also said the same. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"21712","(21706) And with his chain of narration, he said: al-Shāfiʿī informed us, ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Ḥārith reported from Ibn Jurayj, who said: I said to ʿAṭāʾ: If the master asked him about his wealth and he concealed it, he said: It belongs to his master. Ibn Jurayj said: I said to ʿAṭāʾ: What if he concealed a child born to him from his umm walad (slave concubine), or the master did not ask him about it? He said: It belongs to his master. ʿAmr ibn Dīnār and Sulaymān ibn Mūsā also said the same. Ibn Jurayj said: I said to him: What if the master knew of the slave's child but neither the master nor the slave mentioned it at the time of the mukātabah? He said: He is not included in his mukātabah; he is the property of their master. ʿAmr ibn Dīnār also said the same. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"21713","(21707) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad ibn Ismāʿīl al-Muqrīʾ informed me, Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us, Saʿīd ibn Yaḥyā al-Qarāṭīsī narrated to us, Muʿādh ibn Muʿādh narrated to us, ʿAlī ibn Suwayd ibn Manjūf narrated to us, Anas ibn Sīrīn narrated from his father, who said: Anas ibn Mālik contracted a mukātabah with me for twenty thousand dirhams. I was among those who conquered Tustar. I purchased some goods and profited from them. I brought Anas ibn Mālik the amount of my mukātabah, but he refused to accept it from me except in instalments. So I went to ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāh, may Allah be pleased with him, and mentioned that to him. He said: Anas wants the inheritance. And he wrote to Anas: Accept it from the man. So he accepted it. [Ḍaʿīf]"
"21714","(21708) Abū Ḥāmid Aḥmad ibn ʿAlī al-Isfarāʾīnī narrated to us, Zāhir ibn Aḥmad narrated to us, Abū Bakr ibn Ziyād al-Naysābūrī narrated to us, Abū al-Zinbāʿ Rūḥ ibn al-Faraj narrated to us, Yaḥyā ibn Bukayr narrated to me, ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz al-Laythī reported from Saʿīd ibn Abī Saʿīd al-Maqburī, who reported from his father, who said: A woman from Banū Layth purchased me at the market of Dhū al-Majāz for seven hundred dirhams. Then I came to Madīnah, and she contracted a mukātabah with me for forty thousand dirhams. I paid her the bulk of that. Then I carried the remainder to her and said: This is your wealth; take it. She said: No, by Allah, I shall not take it from you except month by month and year by year. So I went out with it to ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāh, may Allah be pleased with him, and mentioned that to him. ʿUmar, may Allah be pleased with him, said: Deposit it in the Bayt al-Māl (public treasury). Then he sent for her and said: Your wealth is in the Bayt al-Māl, and Abū Saʿīd has been freed. If you wish, take it month by month and year by year. He said: She then sent and collected it. Abū Bakr al-Naysābūrī said: This is a ḥasan hadith. [Ḍaʿīf]"
"21715","(21709) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū al-Walīd narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Zuhayr narrated to us, ʿAbdullāh ibn Hāshim narrated to us, Wakīʿ reported from Isrāʾīl, from ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Rufayʿ, from Abū Bakr, that a man contracted a mukātabah with his slave and stipulated instalments for him. The slave brought the entire amount of his mukātabah, but the master refused to accept it except in instalments. The mukātab (slave under contract) went to ʿUmar, may Allah be pleased with him. ʿUmar, may Allah be pleased with him, sent for his master, who came. He presented the matter to him, but he refused to accept it. ʿUmar, may Allah be pleased with him, said: Then I shall deposit it in the Bayt al-Māl. And he said to the master: Take it in instalments. And he said to the mukātab: Go wherever you wish. [Ḍaʿīf]"
"21716","(21710) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū al-Walīd narrated to us, al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān narrated to us, Ḥibbān ibn Mūsā narrated to us, Ibn al-Mubārak reported from Ibn ʿAwn, from Muḥammad, that a mukātab said to his master: Take your mukātabah payment from me. He said: No, except in instalments. So he went to ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān, may Allah be pleased with him, and mentioned that to him. He summoned the master and said: Take your mukātabah payment. He said: No, except in instalments. He said to him: Bring the wealth. He brought it, and he wrote his manumission for him and said: Cast it into the Bayt al-Māl, and I shall pay it to you in instalments. When he saw that, he took it. Ibn al-Mubārak said: Saʿīd narrated to us, from Qatādah, from ʿUthmān, may Allah be pleased with him, something similar to that. Thus said ʿUthmān, may Allah be pleased with him. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"21717","(21711) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bushrān informed us, Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār narrated to us, al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn ʿAffān narrated to us, Ibn Numayr reported from ʿUbaydullāh ibn ʿUmar, from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar, that he used to say regarding a man who contracts a mukātabah with his slave in gold or silver, stipulating instalments for him: He used to dislike that the slave say: \Pay me in advance such and such of it"," and the remainder is yours.\"" [Ḥasan]"""
"21718","(21712) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū al-Walīd narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Zuhayr narrated to us, ʿAbdullāh ibn Hāshim narrated to us, Wakīʿ ibn al-Jarrāḥ reported from al-Rabīʿ, from al-Ḥasan and Ibn Sīrīn, that they both disliked in the case of a mukātab that he say: \Pay me in advance and I shall reduce your payment.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"21719","(21713) And Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū al-Walīd narrated to us, al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān narrated to us, Abū Bakr narrated to us, Wakīʿ reported from Sufyān, from Jābir, from ʿAṭāʾ, from Ibn ʿAbbās, regarding a man who says to his mukātab: \Pay me in advance and I shall reduce your payment\"" — there is nothing wrong with that. The Shaykh Abū al-Walīd said: Our companions said its meaning is: \""Pay me in advance whatever you wish"," and I shall free you upon it"," and I shall reduce your mukātabah payment\"" — so there is nothing wrong with that. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"21720","(21714) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū al-Walīd narrated to us, al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān narrated to us, Ḥibbān ibn Mūsā narrated to us, Ibn al-Mubārak reported from Usāmah ibn Zayd, who said: al-Qāsim ibn Muḥammad informed me that ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāh, may Allah be pleased with him, used to dislike the muqāṭaʿah (lump-sum settlement) of a mukātab upon whom gold and silver were owed, and then he would settle with him for a third or a quarter of it or whatever it may be. And he would say: Make that in goods, whatever you wish. Al-Qāsim said: And ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz, may Allah have mercy on him, wrote accordingly to Abū Bakr ibn Muḥammad. The Shaykh Abū al-Walīd said: Our companions said: We did not permit the master to accept in exchange for dirhams less than their value, because that is ribā (usury). [Ḍaʿīf]"
"21721","(21715) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us that Abu al-Walid narrated to us, that al-Hasan ibn Sufyan narrated to us, that Abu Bakr narrated to us, that Waqi' narrated to us, that Sufyan narrated from 'Asim ibn Sulayman, from Bakr al-Muzani, from Ibn 'Umar (may Allah be pleased with both of them), who said: There is no harm in a master taking commodities from his mukatab (a slave contracted for emancipation). [Da'if]"
"21722","(21716) He said, and Waqi' narrated to us from Sufyan, from Jabir, from 'Ata', from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with both of them), who said: There is no harm in a master taking commodities from his mukatab. [Da'if]"
"21723","(21717) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us that Abu al-Walid al-Faqih narrated to us, that al-Hasan ibn Sufyan narrated to us, that Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated from Ibn al-Mubarak.\n\n(Reference) He said, and Abu al-Walid informed us, that Ibrahim ibn Abi Talib narrated to us, that al-Hasan ibn 'Isa narrated from Ibn al-Mubarak, from Salih ibn Khawwat, from 'Abd Allah ibn Abi Bakr: that 'Umar ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz wrote to me that a mukatab may not make a bequest nor a gift except with the permission of his master. [Da'if]"
"21724","(21718) And Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us that Abu al-Walid narrated to us, that al-Hasan ibn Sufyan narrated to us, that Abu Bakr narrated to us, that Ibn Abi 'Adiyy narrated from Ash'ath, from al-Hasan, who said: A mukatab may not emancipate nor give a gift except with the permission of his master. Muhammad ibn Abi 'Adiyy said in this hadith: They used to say that a mukatab may not emancipate nor give a gift except with the permission of his master. [Sahih]"
"21725","(21719) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us that Abu al-Walid narrated to us, that al-Hasan ibn Sufyan narrated to us, that Habban narrated from Ibn al-Mubarak, from Ibn Jurayj, who said: I said to 'Ata': A mukatab had a slave, and he contracted him for emancipation (mukatabah), then the slave died — to whom does his inheritance go? He said: Those before you used to say that it belongs to the one who contracted him for emancipation, and he may use it to assist him in fulfilling his own contract of emancipation. [Sahih]"
"21726","(21720) And Abu 'Abd Allah informed us that Abu al-Walid narrated to us, that al-Hasan ibn Sufyan narrated to us, that Habban narrated from Ibn al-Mubarak, from Ibn Luha'ah, from Khalid ibn Abi 'Imran, who said: I asked al-Qasim and Salim about a mukatab who has paid half of his contract of emancipation, and then the mukatab contracts his own slave for emancipation. They both strive, and the slave of the mukatab completes his contract of emancipation, but then the first of them (the original mukatab) becomes unable to pay. Is he returned to slavery, or is his emancipation valid based on what he has already paid to his master? They both said: If his first master had given him permission to contract the slave for emancipation, then there is no objection upon him; otherwise, he is in the same position as his slave. [Da'if]"
"21727","(21721) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us that Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us, that al-Rabi' ibn Sulayman narrated to us, that al-Shafi'i narrated to us, that Malik narrated to us.\n\n(Reference) And Abu 'Abd Allah informed us that Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Salman al-Faqih narrated to us, that Isma'il ibn Ishaq narrated to us, that Ibn Abi Uways narrated to us, that Malik narrated from Hisham ibn 'Urwah, from his father, from 'A'ishah (may Allah be pleased with her), who said: Barirah came and said, \I have contracted my family for emancipation for nine uqiyyahs"," one uqiyyah per year. Help me.\"" 'A'ishah said"," \""If your family wish"," I will pay it to them in a single payment"," and your loyalty (wala') will be for me.\"" Barirah went to her family and told them this"," but they refused. She came back from her family while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) was sitting"," and said"," \""I offered them that"," but they refused unless the wala' remains for them.\"" The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) heard this and asked her about it. 'A'ishah informed him. He said"," \""Take her and stipulate the wala' for them"," for indeed the wala' belongs only to the one who emancipates.\"" 'A'ishah did so. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) stood among the people"," praised Allah"," and extolled Him"," then said: \""What is the matter with men who stipulate conditions that are not in the Book of Allah? Any condition that is not in the Book of Allah is invalid"," even if it be a hundred conditions. The decree of Allah is more deserving of fulfillment"," and the condition of Allah is more binding. Indeed"," the wala' belongs only to the one who emancipates.\""\n\nAl-Bukhari narrated it in al-Sahih from Isma'il ibn Abi Uways"," and Muslim and al-Bukhari narrated it through other chains from Hisham ibn 'Urwah. Al-Shafi'i (may Allah have mercy on him) said: If her family agrees to the sale and the mukatabah agrees to the sale"," then that constitutes a termination of the contract of emancipation. [Sahih. Agreed upon]"""
"21728","(21722) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us among the last narrators, who said: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us, that al-Rabi' ibn Sulayman narrated to us, that al-Shafi'i narrated to us, that Malik narrated to us, that Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to me, from 'Amrah bint 'Abd al-Rahman: that Barirah came seeking the help of 'A'ishah (may Allah be pleased with her). 'A'ishah said, \If your family wish"," I will pay your price to them in a single payment and emancipate you.\"" Barirah mentioned this to her family"," and they said"," \""No"," unless the wala' is for us.\"" Malik said: Yahya said that 'Amrah claimed that 'A'ishah (may Allah be pleased with her) mentioned this to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)"," and he said: \""Let that not prevent you. Buy her and emancipate her"," for indeed the wala' belongs only to the one who emancipates.\""\n\nAl-Bukhari narrated it in al-Sahih from 'Abd Allah ibn Yusuf from Malik. Malik sent it as a mursal narration in most of the reports from him. [Sahih. Agreed upon]"""
"21729","(21723) And Muttarif ibn 'Abd Allah narrated it from him. Abu 'Amr Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah al-Adib informed us that Abu Bakr al-Isma'ili informed us that Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn 'Uqbah al-Shaybani al-Kufi narrated to me that Abu Sabrah al-Qurashi narrated to us that Muttarif ibn 'Abd Allah narrated from Malik ibn Anas, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from 'Amrah bint 'Abd al-Rahman, from 'A'ishah (may Allah be pleased with her): that Barirah came to her seeking her help, and he mentioned the hadith. [Sahih. Previously narrated]"
"21730","(21724) And al-Shafi'i narrated it from Sufyan ibn 'Uyaynah, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from 'Amrah, from 'A'ishah (may Allah be pleased with her). Abu Ishaq Ibrahim ibn Muhammad al-Faqih informed us that Shafi' ibn Muhammad informed us that Abu Ja'far al-Tahawi narrated to us that al-Muzani narrated to us that al-Shafi'i narrated from Sufyan, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from 'Amrah, from 'A'ishah (may Allah be pleased with her), who said: I intended to purchase Barirah and emancipate her, but her masters stipulated upon me that I emancipate her and that the wala' would be for them. 'A'ishah (may Allah be pleased with her) said: I mentioned this to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), and he said: \Buy her and emancipate her"," for indeed the wala' belongs only to the one who emancipates.\"" Then he addressed the people and said: \""What is the matter with people who stipulate conditions that are not in the Book of Allah? Whoever stipulates a condition that is not in the Book of Allah"," it is not for him"," even if he stipulates it a hundred times.\"" [Sahih. Agreed upon]"""
"21731","(21725) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us that al-Rabīʿ informed us that al-Shāfiʿī said: The ḥadīth of Yaḥyā from ʿAmrah from ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her) is more firmly established than the ḥadīth of Hishām, and I consider his statement \and stipulate for them the walāʾ\"" to be an error. And I reckon the ḥadīth of ʿAmrah is that ʿĀʾishah had stipulated that for them without the command of the Prophet (peace be upon him)"," and she considered that permissible. So the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) informed her that if she freed her"," the walāʾ would be hers. He said: \""Let not your prior stipulation prevent you.\"" And I do not think her matter was that she stipulated for them what is not permissible.\n\nThe Shaykh (may Allah have mercy on him) said: The ḥadīth of ʿAmrah from ʿĀʾishah is a firmly established ḥadīth"," for a group narrated it from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd in a connected (mawṣūl) chain. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"21732","(21726) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzakkī informed us that Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūh al-Shaybānī narrated to us that Abū Aḥmad Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Wahhāb narrated to us that Jaʿfar ibn ʿAwn narrated to us that Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd narrated from ʿAmrah from ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her) who said: Barīrah came to ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her) seeking her assistance in her kitābah (contract of manumission). She said to her: \If your masters wish"," I can pay your price to them in a single payment and free you.\"" Barīrah mentioned that to her masters"," but they refused unless she stipulated the walāʾ for them. She mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him)"," and he said: \""Purchase her"," for indeed the walāʾ belongs to the one who frees.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muttafaq ʿalayh]"""
"21733","(21727) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū al-Walīd al-Faqīh narrated to us that Qāsim al-Muṭarriz narrated to us that Yūsuf ibn Mūsā narrated to us that Jaʿfar ibn ʿAwn narrated from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd who said: I heard ʿAmrah narrate from ʿĀʾishah who said: Barīrah came to me seeking my assistance in her kitābah — and he mentioned the ḥadīth. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Preceded before it]"
"21734","(21728) He said: And Qāsim al-Muṭarriz narrated to us that Bundār narrated to us that Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd narrated from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd from ʿAmrah, and he mentioned something similar to it. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Preceded before it]"
"21735","(21729) He said: And Qāsim al-Muṭarriz narrated to us that Bundār narrated to us that ʿAbd al-Wahhāb narrated from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd with its like. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Preceded before it]"
"21736","(21730) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us that Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us that al-Rabīʿ narrated to us that al-Shāfiʿī narrated to us that Mālik narrated from Nāfiʿ from Ibn ʿUmar from ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her) that she intended to —\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAmr al-Adīb informed us that Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī informed us that al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān narrated to us that Qutaybah narrated from Mālik from Nāfiʿ from Ibn ʿUmar that ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her) intended to purchase a slave-girl to free her, but her family said: \We will sell her to you only on the condition that her walāʾ remains ours.\"" ʿĀʾishah mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him)"," and he said: \""Let not that prevent you"," for indeed the walāʾ belongs to the one who frees.\"" Al-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Qutaybah and others"," and Muslim narrated it from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā from Mālik. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muttafaq ʿalayh]"""
"21737","(21731) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr narrated to us that Abū al-ʿAbbās narrated to us that al-Rabīʿ narrated to us that al-Shāfiʿī said: I consider the ḥadīth of Nāfiʿ to be the most firmly established of all, because it is musnad (fully connected), and it is more likely. And it is as though ʿĀʾishah, in the ḥadīth of Nāfiʿ, had stipulated the walāʾ for them, so the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) informed her that if she freed her, the walāʾ would be hers. If it was thus, then she did not stipulate the walāʾ for them by the command of the Prophet (peace be upon him). And perhaps Hishām or ʿUrwah, when he heard that the Prophet (peace be upon him) said \Let not that prevent you","\"" thought that he had commanded her to stipulate the walāʾ for them"," and his memory did not preserve what Ibn ʿUmar preserved. And Allah knows best.\n\nThe Shaykh (may Allah have mercy on him) said: And for the meaning of the ḥadīth of Ibn ʿUmar there are corroborating narrations. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"21738","(21732) Among them is what Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, that Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq narrated to us by dictation, that Mūsā ibn Isḥāq al-Qāḍī narrated to us that ʿAbd Allāh ibn Abī Shaybah narrated to us that Khālid ibn Makhlad narrated to us that Sulaymān ibn Bilāl narrated to us that Suhayl ibn Abī Ṣāliḥ narrated from his father from Abū Hurayrah who said: ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her) intended to purchase a slave-girl to free her, but her family refused unless the walāʾ would be theirs. She mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him), and he said: \Let not that prevent you"," for indeed the walāʾ belongs to the one who frees.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 1505]"""
"21739","(21733) And among them is what Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, that Abū al-Faḍl ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us that Aḥmad ibn Salamah narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn Bashshār narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us that Shuʿbah said: I heard ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Qāsim say: I heard al-Qāsim narrate from ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her) that she intended to purchase Barīrah for the purpose of freeing her, and that they stipulated her walāʾ. She mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him), and he said: \Purchase her and free her"," for indeed the walāʾ belongs to the one who frees.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn Mathannā from Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muttafaq ʿalayh]"""
"21740","(21734) In this meaning, al-Zuhrī narrated from ʿUrwah from ʿĀʾishah. Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us that Muḥammad ibn Bakr narrated to us that Abū Dāwūd narrated to us that Qutaybah ibn Saʿīd and ʿAbd Allāh ibn Maslamah both narrated to us that al-Layth narrated from Ibn Shihāb from ʿUrwah that ʿĀʾishah informed him that Barīrah came to ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her) seeking her assistance in her kitābah, and she had not yet paid anything of her kitābah. ʿĀʾishah said to her: \Return to your family. If they wish that I pay your kitābah on your behalf and that your walāʾ be mine"," I will do so.\"" Barīrah mentioned that to her family"," but they refused and said: \""If she wishes to do a favour for you"," let her do so"," but your walāʾ will be ours.\"" She mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him)"," and the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said to her: \""Purchase and free"," for indeed the walāʾ belongs to the one who frees.\"" Then the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) stood up and said: \""What is the matter with people who stipulate conditions that are not in the Book of Allah? Whoever stipulates a condition that is not in the Book of Allah"," it is not valid for him"," even if he stipulates it a hundred times. The condition of Allah is more deserving and more binding.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Qutaybah and from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Maslamah"," and Muslim narrated it from Qutaybah. And in its meaning"," al-Aswad narrated from ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her). [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muttafaq ʿalayh]"""
"21741","(21735) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Ibrāhīm ibn Ayyūb al-Mattūthī narrated to us: Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Sulaymān ibn Ḥarb narrated to us: Shuʿbah narrated from al-Ḥakam, from Ibrāhīm, from al-Aswad, from ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her) that she wished to purchase Barīrah, and her family stipulated the condition of walāʾ (clientage) for themselves. She mentioned this to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ), and the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Purchase her"," for walāʾ belongs to the one who sets free.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Sulaymān ibn Ḥarb. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muttafaq ʿalayh]"""
"21742","(21736) Abū ʿAmr al-Adīb narrated to us: Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī narrated to us: ʿImrān ibn Mūsā narrated to us: ʿUthmān — who is Ibn Abī Shaybah — narrated to us: Jarīr narrated from Manṣūr, from Ibrāhīm, from al-Aswad, from ʿĀʾishah, who said: \I purchased Barīrah"," and her family stipulated the condition of walāʾ. I mentioned this to the Prophet (ﷺ)"," and he said: 'Set her free"," for walāʾ belongs to the one who paid the price (al-wariq).'\"" She said: \""So I set her free.\"" She said: \""Then the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) called her and gave her the choice regarding her husband. She said: 'Were he to give me such and such"," I would not remain with him.' So she chose herself"," and her husband was a free man.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿUthmān ibn Abī Shaybah"," without the statement \""and her husband was a free man.\"" We have clarified in the Book of Marriage that this is a statement of al-Aswad"," which Abū ʿAwānah distinguished from Manṣūr's narration"," attributing it to al-Aswad.\n\nAl-Bukhārī said: \""The statement of al-Aswad is munqaṭiʿ (disconnected)"," and the statement of Ibn ʿAbbās — 'I saw him as a slave' — is more correct.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muttafaq ʿalayh]"""
"21743","(21737) The Shaykh (may Allah have mercy on him) said: Ayman narrated from ʿĀʾishah, as Abū ʿAlī al-Ḥusayn ibn Muḥammad al-Rūdhbārī narrated to us: Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn Sakhtawayh al-ʿAdl narrated to us: Isḥāq ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Maymūn narrated to us: Abū Nuʿaym narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Wāḥid ibn Ayman narrated to us: Ayman narrated to me.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Naṣr ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn ʿUmar ibn Qatādah narrated to us: Abū Muḥammad Aḥmad ibn Isḥāq al-Baghdādī al-Harwī narrated to us there: Muʿādh ibn Najdah narrated to us: Khallād ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Wāḥid ibn Ayman al-Makkī narrated from his father, who said: \I entered upon ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her) and said: 'O Mother of the Believers"," I was a slave of ʿUtbah ibn Abī Lahab. ʿUtbah died"," and his sons inherited me"," and they sold me to ʿAbd Allāh ibn Abī ʿAmr al-Makhzūmī. Ibn Abī ʿAmr set me free"," but they stipulated my walāʾ. So whose mawlā am I?'\""\n\nIn the narration of Abū Nuʿaym"," he said: \""I entered upon ʿĀʾishah"," and I had been a slave of ʿUtbah ibn Abī Lahab. ʿUtbah died"," and his sons inherited him"," and Ibn Abī ʿAmr purchased him and set him free. But the sons of ʿUtbah stipulated the walāʾ. So he entered upon ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her) and mentioned this to her.\""\n\nʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her) said: \""I entered upon Barīrah while she was a mukātabah (a slave contracted to purchase her freedom)"," and she said: 'Purchase me"," O Mother of the Believers"," for my family wishes to sell me"," so set me free.'\"" In the narration of Abū Nuʿaym: \""Purchase me and set me free.\"" I said: \""Yes.\"" She said: \""My family will not sell me unless they stipulate my walāʾ.\"" ʿĀʾishah said: \""I have no need of you.\"" The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) heard of this"," or it was conveyed to him"," and he said: \""What is the matter with Barīrah?\"" So she informed him. In the narration of Abū Nuʿaym: \""He mentioned this to ʿĀʾishah"," and ʿĀʾishah mentioned what she had said to her.\"" He said: \""Purchase her and set her free"," and let them stipulate whatever they wish.\"" In the narration of Abū Nuʿaym: \""Call them"," and let them stipulate whatever they wish.\""\n\nʿĀʾishah said: \""So I set her free"," and her family stipulated the walāʾ.\"" In the narration of Abū Nuʿaym: \""So ʿĀʾishah purchased her and set her free"," and her family stipulated the walāʾ.\"" Then the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \""Walāʾ belongs to the one who sets free"," even if they stipulate a hundred conditions.\"" Khallād added in his narration: \""You are the mawlā of Ibn Abī ʿAmr.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū Nuʿaym and from Khallād ibn Yaḥyā. This narration is close to the narration of Hishām ibn ʿUrwah"," and the multiple narrations through preservation are stronger than the single narration. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muttafaq ʿalayh]"""
"21744","(21738) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān narrated to us, and he said: al-Shāfiʿī (may Allah have mercy on him) said: \When her family consents to the sale and the mukātabah consents to the sale"," that constitutes a relinquishment of the mukātabah (contract).\""\n\nAl-Shāfiʿī said: \""Some people said to me: 'What is the meaning of the Prophet's (ﷺ) invalidation of ʿĀʾishah's condition imposed by Barīrah's family?' I replied: 'We have clarified — and Allah knows best — in the hadith itself that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) had already informed them that Allah has decreed that walāʾ belongs to the one who sets free.' And He said: 'Call them by their fathers' names; that is more just in the sight of Allah. And if you do not know their fathers"," then they are your brothers in religion and your mawlās.' (al-Aḥzāb 5) He attributed them to their mawlās just as He attributed them to their fathers. So just as it is not permissible to divert them from their fathers"," likewise it is not permissible to divert them from their mawlās who were the source of their emancipation. And Allah the Most High said: 'And when you said to the one whom Allah had favored and you had favored: \""Keep your wife to yourself.\""' (al-Aḥzāb 37) And the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: 'Walāʾ belongs to the one who sets free.' And he prohibited the sale of walāʾ and its gifting. It is narrated from him that he said: 'Walāʾ is a bond like the bond of lineage. Lineage is neither sold nor gifted.' When this reached them"," whoever stipulated something contrary to what Allah and His Messenger (ﷺ) had decreed was a transgressor. And for transgressions there are prescribed punishments and disciplinary measures. So among the disciplinary measures for transgressors is that their conditions be nullified"," so that they may desist from the like of it"," or others may take warning thereby. And this is among the finest forms of discipline.\""\n\nAl-Zaʿfarānī narrated from al-Shāfiʿī the meaning of this"," and more clearly than it. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"21745","(21739) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to me: Abū Aḥmad ibn Abī al-Ḥasan narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Raḥmān — meaning Ibn Abī Ḥātim al-Rāzī — narrated to us: My father narrated to us: Ḥarmalah narrated to us, and he said: \I heard al-Shāfiʿī say regarding the Prophet's (ﷺ) hadith where he said to her: 'Stipulate the walāʾ for them' — its meaning is: 'Stipulate the walāʾ against them.' Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic"," said: 'Those — for them is the curse' (meaning: upon them is the curse).\""\n\nThe Shaykh (may Allah have mercy on him) said: \""The first answer is more correct"," and there is room for consideration regarding the authenticity of this wording. And Allah knows best.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"21746","(21740) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: Abū al-Walīd al-Faqīh narrated to us: al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān narrated to us: Abū Bakr narrated to us: al-Ḍaḥḥāk ibn Makhlad narrated from Ibn Jurayj, from ʬAṭāʾ, from Ibn Masʿūd: \He used to dislike the sale of a mukātab (a slave under a contract of manumission).\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"21747","(21741) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār narrated to us: Yūnus ibn Bukayr narrated from Ibn Isḥāq, from ʿĀṣim ibn ʿUmar ibn Qatādah, from Maḥmūd ibn Labīd, from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: \Salmān al-Fārisī narrated to me.\"" He mentioned his story and said in it: \""A man from Banī Qurayẓah"," a Jew"," came to Wādī al-Qurā and purchased me from the master I was with. He brought me to me to al-Madīnah.\"" He mentioned the hadith and that he related his account to the Prophet (ﷺ). When he finished"," the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \""Enter into a mukātabah contract"," O Salmān.\"" So I entered into a mukātabah contract. [Ḥasan]"""
"21748","(21742) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: Abū al-Walīd narrated to us: al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān narrated to us: Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah narrated to us: Hushaym narrated from Yūnus, from al-Ḥasan, who said: \The criminal liability of a mukātab (a slave under a contract of manumission) is upon his own person; it begins with him.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"21749","(21743) And with his chain of narration: Abū Bakr narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Sawāʾ narrated from ʿAbbād ibn Manṣūr, from Ḥammād, from Ibrāhīm, from Sharīḥ, who said: \The wounding (compensation for injury) of a mukātab is like the wounding of a slave.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"21750","(21744) He said: And Abū Bakr narrated to us from Muḥammad ibn Sawāʾ, from Saʿīd, from Qatādah, from ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: \The wounding (compensation for injury) of a mukātab is like the wounding of a slave.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"21751","(21745) Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr informed us — Abu al-'Abbas al-Amm narrated to us — al-Rabi' narrated to us — al-Shafi'i narrated to us — 'Abd Allah ibn al-Harith narrated from Ibn Jurayj, who said: 'Ata' said: \When a mukatab (a slave contracted for emancipation) is wounded"," his blood-money is due.\"" And 'Amr ibn Dinar said it as well. Ibn Jurayj said: \""It is because he is"," as it were"," from his own property — he guards him just as he guards his own property.\"" He said: \""Yes.\""\n\nAl-Shafi'i"," may Allah have mercy on him"," said: \""As 'Ata' and 'Amr ibn Dinar said — the crime committed against him constitutes a financial liability from his own property"," which his master has no right to seize under any circumstance"," unless he dies before fulfilling [the contract].\"" [Sahih]"""
"21752","(21746) Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr informed us — Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us — al-Rabi' ibn Sulayman narrated to us — al-Shafi'i narrated to us — 'Abd Allah ibn al-Harith narrated from Ibn Jurayj, who said: \We said to Ibn Tawus: 'How did your father rule regarding a man who contracts a mukatab"," then dies"," and his daughter inherits that mukatab"," who then fulfills his kitabah (contract of emancipation)"," is set free"," and then dies?' He said: 'He used to say: his wala' (patronage) belongs to her. And I do not think anyone among the people would disagree with that.' And he was amazed at their saying: 'She has no wala'.'\"" [Sahih]"""
"21753","(21747) And with his chain of narration, al-Shafi'i informed us — 'Abd Allah ibn al-Harith narrated from Ibn Jurayj, who said: \I said to 'Ata': 'A man died and left two sons and a mukatab"," and the mukatab fell to the share of one of them. He then fulfilled his kitabah through the one to whom it had passed in the inheritance"," and then the mukatab died — who inherits him?' He said: 'Both of them inherit him together.' And 'Amr ibn Dinar said the same. 'Ata' said: 'His wala' reverts to the one who originally contracted him.' I raised the matter with him again"," and he said it more than once.\""\n\nAl-Shafi'i"," may Allah have mercy on him"," said: \""And we hold the view of 'Ata' and 'Amr ibn Dinar — that regarding a mukatab whom a man contracts"," then the master dies"," and then the mukatab fulfills his contract and is emancipated by the kitabah — his wala' belongs to the one who originally contracted his kitabah.\""\n\nThe Shaykh"," may Allah have mercy on him"," said: \""He did not hold his view regarding the division of the mukatab"," because division constitutes a sale"," and the sale of a mukatab is not permissible.\"" [Sahih]"""
"21754","(21748) Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn 'Ali al-Hafiz informed us — Ibrahim ibn Allah al-Isfahani narrated to us — Isma'il ibn Ibrahim al-Qattan narrated to us — al-Hasan ibn 'Isa narrated to us — Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us — 'Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Sulayman narrated from 'Ata', regarding a man who died and had a mukatab slave, and the deceased had sons and daughters: He said: \They inherit — the women and the men — from what is upon his back (i.e."," from the outstanding installments). But the women inherit nothing of the wala' except what they have contracted for or set free.\"" [Sahih]"""
"21755","(21749) He said, and Ibn al-Mubarak informed us — Ma'mar narrated from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir — from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib and Abu Salamah ibn 'Abd al-Rahman, who both said regarding a man who contracts his slave in mukatabah, then dies, and leaves male and female children, and the mukatab fulfills his kitabah to them: They said: \The wala' belongs to the men"," not to the women.\"" And Ibn Shihab used to say that as well. [Sahih]"""
"21756","(21750) He said, and Ibn al-Mubarak informed us — Sufyan narrated from Mansur — from Ibrahim, regarding a man who contracted his slave in mukatabah, then the man who contracted him died and left men and women: He said: \The women have nothing of the mukatab's wala'"," and the inheritance is between them — meaning the men and the women.\"" [Sahih]"""
"21757","(21751) He said, and Ibn al-Mubarak informed us — 'Ammar ibn Ruzayq narrated from al-Mughirah, who said: \I asked Ibrahim about a man who died and left a mukatab"," and the heirs set the mukatab free with what he would receive of the inheritance — to whom does the wala' belong?\"" He said: \""To the deceased mukatab (i.e."," the mukatab's own wala' reverts to the heirs of the one who set him free).\"" [Sahih]"""
"21758","(21752) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us — Abu al-Walid al-Faqih narrated to us — al-Hasan ibn Sufyan narrated to us — Hibban narrated — from Ibn al-Mubarak — from Aban ibn 'Abd Allah al-Bajali — 'Ata' ibn Abi Rabah narrated that Ibn 'Umar had a mukatab who paid nine hundred (dinars) and one hundred dinars remained, but he fell short, so he returned him to slavery. [Hasan]"
"21759","(21753) He said, and al-Hasan ibn Sufyan narrated to us — Abu Bakr narrated to us — Ibn Abi Zaidah narrated from Muhammad ibn Ishaq — from Nafi' — from Ibn 'Umar, that his mukatab fell short, so he returned him as a slave and kept what he had already taken from him. [Hasan]"
"21760","(21754) Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr informed us — Abu al-'Abbas al-Amm narrated to us — al-Rabi' narrated to us — al-Shafi'i narrated to us — 'Abd Allah ibn al-Harith narrated from Ibn Jurayj — from Isma'il ibn Umayyah — that Nafi' informed him that 'Abd Allah ibn 'Umar contracted a slave of his for thirty thousand, and then the slave came to him and said: \I have fallen short.\"" He said: \""Then erase your kitabah.\"" He said: \""I have fallen short — erase it yourself.\"" Nafi' said: \""So I gestured to him to erase it"," while the slave was hoping to be set free.\"" So the slave erased it. He had two sons"," or one son. Ibn 'Umar said: \""Keep away from my slave woman.\"" Then Ibn 'Umar set his son free afterwards. [Sahih]"""
"21761","(21755) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū al-Walīd narrated to us that al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān narrated to us that Ḥibbān ibn Mūsā narrated to us, from Ibn al-Mubārak, from Ibn ʿAwn, from Nāfiʿ, that Ibn ʿUmar contracted a mukātabah (deed of manumission) with his slave, who had a child and an umm walad. The slave came to Ibn ʿUmar and said: \I have become unable to pay; accept my kitābah (deed of manumission).\"" Ibn ʿUmar said: \""I will not accept it from you until you bring them to me.\"" So he brought them to him"," and he returned them to bondage. Then"," after that — either one day or three days later — he set them all free. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"21762","(21756) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan and Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq both informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh ibn ʤAbd al-Ḥakam narrated to us that Ibn Wahb narrated to me that ʿUmar ibn Muḥammad ibn Zayd ibn ʿAbdillāh ibn ʿUmar informed me that his father narrated to him that ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar contracted a mukātabah with his slave, whose name was Sharaf, for forty thousand. The slave went to Kūfah and worked on donkeys belonging to him until he had paid fifteen thousand. Then a man came to him and said: \You are mad! You are here tormenting yourself"," while ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar buys slaves left and right and then sets them free. Go back to him and tell him: 'I have become unable to pay.'\"" So he came to him with his ṣaḥīfah (deed) and said: \""O Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān"," I have become unable to pay"," and here is my deed — erase it.\"" He said: \""No"," but you may erase it if you wish.\"" So he erased it"," and the eyes of ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar filled with tears. He said: \""Go"," you are free.\"" The slave said: \""May Allah set you right — be kind to my two sons.\"" He said: \""They are both free.\"" He said: \""May Allah set you right — be kind to the mother of my children.\"" She is also free.\"" So he set all five of them free"," sitting in one place. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"21763","(21757) Abū Ḥāzim al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū al-Faḍl ibn Khamīruwayh informed us that Aḥmad ibn Najdah narrated to us that Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr narrated to us that Abū ʿAwānah narrated to us, from Isḥāq, the mawlā of ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar, that his father contracted a mukātabah with ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar for thirty thousand. He became unable to pay, so he was returned to bondage, having paid half or nearly half. He requested of him that he set free his children, who had been born during the period of his mukātabah. So he set him free and set his children free, and returned to him one thousand five hundred dirhams. [Ḍaʿīf]"
"21764","(21758) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū al-Walīd narrated to us that al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān narrated to us that Ḥibbān ibn Mūsā narrated to us, from Ibn al-Mubārak, from Ibn Jurayj, from Abū al-Zubayr, that he heard Jābir ibn ʿAbdillāh say regarding the mukātab (one who has contracted a deed of manumission): \He pays the first instalment of his kitābah and then becomes unable to pay — is he returned to being a slave?\"" He said: \""His master has the greater right to the condition he stipulated.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"21765","(21759) He said: And al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān narrated to us that Abū Bakr narrated to us that Ḥafṣ narrated to us, from al-Ashʿath, from Abū al-Zubayr, from Jābir, who said: \Whatever they have taken from him — meaning"," if he does not complete the payment"," he is returned to bondage"," and whatever has been taken remains his (the master's).\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"21766","(21760) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū al-Walīd narrated to us that al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān narrated to us that Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah narrated to us that ʿAbbād ibn al-ʿAwwām narrated to us, from al-Ḥajjāj, from Ḥuṣayn, from al-Shaʿbī, from al-Ḥārith, from ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: \If two consecutive instalments become due upon the mukātab and he does not pay his instalments"," he is returned to bondage.\"" And he said in another narration: \""If it occurs in the second year\"" — or he said — \""in the third year.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"21767","(21761) And Abū ʿAbdillāh informed us that Abū al-Walīd narrated to us that al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān narrated to us that Ḥibbān narrated to us, from Ibn al-Mubārak, from Saʿīd, from Qatādah, from Khilās, from ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: \If the mukātab becomes unable to pay"," he shall be made to work for two years. If he pays"," [he is free]; otherwise"," he is returned to bondage.\""\n\nThe first isnād from ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) is weak"," and the narration of Khilās from ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) is not considered authentic by the scholars of hadith. If it is authentic"," it is understood as an act of kindness on the part of the master. If he does not grant respite"," the mukātab is returned to bondage. And Allah knows best. [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"21768","(21762) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr narrated to us that Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm narrated to us that al-Rabīʿ narrated to us that al-Shāfiʿī narrated to us that Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah narrated to us, from Shabīb, from Gharqadah, who said: \I witnessed Shurayḥ return a mukātab who had become unable to pay back into bondage.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"21769","(21763) Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan and Abū Zakariyyā Yaḥyā ibn Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā both informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥakam informed us that Ibn Wahb informed me that ʿUmar ibn Muḥammad, ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar, Mālik ibn Anas, and others informed me that Nāfiʿ informed them, from ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar, that ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him) said: \Any umm walad who bears a child for her master — he shall not sell her"," nor give her away as a gift"," nor bequeath her. He may enjoy her as long as he wishes. When he dies"," she is free.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"21770","(21764) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿUmar ibn Ḥafṣ, Ibn al-Ḥammāmī al-Muqriʾ (may Allah have mercy on him), narrated to us that Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Salmān al-Najjād narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn al-Haytham al-Qāḍī narrated to us that Saʿīd ibn Kathīr narrated to me that Sulaymān ibn Bilāl narrated to me, from ʿAbdullāh ibn Dīnār, from Ibn ʿUmar, who said: \ʿUmar forbade the selling of ummahāt al-awlād (mothers of children). He said: 'She shall not be sold"," nor given away as a gift"," nor bequeathed. Her master may enjoy her as long as he wishes. When he dies"," she is free.'\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"21771","(21765) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad al-Muqriʾ informed us: Aḥmad ibn Salmān narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Ghālib narrated to us: Abū Ḥudhayfah narrated to us: Sufyān narrated from ʿAbdullāh ibn Dīnār, who said: Two men came to Ibn ʿUmar, and he said, \From where have you come?\"" They said"," \""From Ibn al-Zubayr"," and he has permitted for us certain things that were forbidden to us.\"" He said"," \""What has he permitted for you that was forbidden to you?\"" They said"," \""He has permitted for us the sale of the *ummahāt al-awlād* (mothers of children).\"" He said"," \""Do you know Abū Ḥafṣ ʿUmar"," may Allah be pleased with him?\"" They said"," \""Yes.\"" He said"," \""Indeed"," ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb"," may Allah be pleased with him"," forbade that they be sold"," gifted"," or inherited. One may enjoy her company as long as he is alive"," and when he dies"," she is free.\""\n\nSuch is the narration of the group from ʿAbdullāh ibn Dīnār. And some narrators erred in it on the authority of ʿAbdullāh ibn Dīnār by raising it to the Prophet ﷺ"," and it is an error that is not permissible to mention. [Weak]"""
"21772","(21766) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbdullāh ibn Yūsuf al-Aṣbahānī informed us: Abū Saʿīd ibn al-Aʿrābī narrated to us: al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad al-Zaʿfarānī narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn ʿUbayd narrated to us: Ismāʿīl ibn Abī Khālid narrated from ʿĀmir from ʿUbaydah al-Salmānī, who said: ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib, may Allah be pleased with him, said: \ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb"," may Allah be pleased with him"," consulted me regarding the sale of the *ummahāt al-awlād*"," and I held the opinion that they were free. ʿUmar passed judgment accordingly during his lifetime"," and ʿUthmān"," may Allah be pleased with them both"," did so after him. Then when I assumed authority"," I held the opinion that I should enslave them.\"" He said: \""Muḥammad ibn Sīrīn informed me that he asked ʿUbaydah about that"," and he said"," 'Which of the two opinions is more beloved to me?' He said"," 'The opinion of ʿUmar and ʿAlī"," may Allah be pleased with them both"," together is more beloved to me than the opinion of ʿAlī"," may Allah be pleased with him"," alone when he encountered the disagreement.'\"" [Authentic]"""
"21773","(21767) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān in Baghdād informed us: Abū ʿAmr ibn al-Sammāk narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn ʿĪsā ibn al-Sakan al-Wāsiṭī narrated to us: ʿAmr ibn ʿUthmān narrated to us: Hushaym narrated from Ismāʿīl ibn Abī Khālid from al-Shaʿbī from ʿUbaydah, who said: ʿAlī, may Allah be pleased with him, said: \ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb"," may Allah be pleased with him"," debated with me regarding the sale of the *ummahāt al-awlād*. I said"," 'They may be sold","' and he said"," 'They may not be sold.' ʿAlī said: \""ʿUmar kept returning to the matter with me until I said what he said. He passed judgment accordingly during his lifetime. Then when the matter came to me"," I held the opinion that they may be sold.\""\n\nAl-Shaʿbī said: \""And Muḥammad ibn Sīrīn narrated to me from ʿUbaydah"," who said: 'I said to ʿAlī"," \""Your opinion and the opinion of ʿUmar together is more beloved to me than your opinion alone in times of division.\""'\""\n\nHe said: \""And Muḥammad ibn ʿĪsā narrated to us: Sulaymān ibn Ḥarb narrated to us: Ḥammād ibn Zayd narrated from Ayyūb from Muḥammad ibn Sīrīn from ʿUbaydah from ʿAlī"," may Allah be pleased with him"," with the like of it.\"" [Weak]"""
"21774","(21768) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us: Abū ʿUthmān al-Baṣrī and Abū al-Faḍl al-ʿAbbās ibn Muḥammad ibn Qūhyār both said: Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Wahhāb informed us: Yaʿlā ibn ʿUbayd narrated to us: Sufyān narrated from Salamah ibn Kuhayl from Zayd ibn Wahb, who said: \ʿUmar"," may Allah be pleased with him"," sold the *ummahāt al-awlād*"," then retracted.\"" [Weak]"""
"21775","(21769) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān in Baghdād informed us: ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us: Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān narrated to me: Saʿīd ibn ʿUfayr narrated to me: ʬAṭṭāf ibn Khālid narrated from ʿAbd al-Aʿlā ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn Abī Farwah from Ibn Shihāb, who mentioned a narration. Ibn Shihāb said: \I said to ʿAbd al-Malik"," meaning Marwān"," 'I heard Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyib mention that ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb"," may Allah be pleased with him"," ordered that the *ummahāt al-awlād* be appraised at a fair value and then be freed. He remained upon that during the early part of his caliphate. Then a man from Quraysh died who had a son by an *umm walad*"," and ʿUmar"," may Allah be pleased with him"," used to admire that boy. That boy passed by ʿUmar"," may Allah be pleased with him"," in the mosque a few nights after his father's death"," and ʿUmar"," may Allah be pleased with him"," said to him"," 'What have you done"," O brother of mine"," regarding your mother?' He said"," 'I did"," O Commander of the Faithful"," when my brothers gave me the choice between keeping my mother as a slave or being expelled from my inheritance from my father. My inheritance from my father was easier upon me than my mother being enslaved.' ʿUmar said"," 'Did I not order in this matter a fair appraisal? What do you think of my opinion or any command I give"," and you say about it?' Then he stood and sat upon the pulpit. The people gathered to him"," and when he was satisfied with their assembly"," he said"," 'O people"," I had given an order regarding the *ummahāt al-awlād* that you know of. Then an opinion other than that occurred to me. Any man who has an *umm walad* — she is his property by his right hand as long as he lives"," and when he dies"," she is free"," and there is no way over her.'\"" [Authentic]"""
"21776","(21770) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Dāwūd ibn Sulaymān al-Zāhid narrated to us: ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Junayd al-Mālikī narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn Ṣāliḥ narrated to us: ʿAnbasah narrated to me: Yūnus narrated from Ibn Shihāb, who said: \I arrived in Damascus while ʿAbd al-Malik was occupied with his affairs. I sat in a gathering where I did not know the people. A man came and they made room for him. He said"," 'What do you think about something the Commander of the Faithful mentioned just now? A message came to him from Madīnah regarding the *ummahāt al-awlād* — should they be enslaved or freed?' I said"," 'Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyib mentioned that a man from Quraysh"," whose intellect and eloquence were admired"," died and left wealth and his mother was an *umm walad*. They set his mother up for sale and outbid him for his mother until they expelled him from his inheritance. He passed by ʿUmar"," may Allah be pleased with him"," who called him and asked him what had become of his inheritance from his father. He said"," \""I was expelled from my inheritance from my father by my mother.\"" ʿUmar said"," \""By Allah"," I shall certainly say a word about this by which I will deter the people from it.\"" He stood and addressed the people"," then said"," \""O people"," any free man who leaves behind an *umm walad* who bore from him — she is free.\""'\""\n\nHe said: \""Then he took my hand"," and lo"," it was Qabīṣah ibn Dhūʾayb"," until he brought me to ʿAbd al-Malik ibn Marwān. And ʿAbd al-Malik mentioned to Qabīṣah that Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyib had not confirmed it. So I was brought in to him"," and he said"," 'This is the ḥadīth you told me about.' He began and asked me about my lineage. When I reached my father"," he said"," 'Your father was indeed a firebrand in the fitnah. What is the ḥadīth of Saʿīd that Qabīṣah told me about on your authority?' I informed him with the same as I had informed Qabīṣah. He ordered that and it was carried out. He said"," 'No man like you has ever died.'\"" [Authentic. It was mentioned before it.]"""
"21777","(21771) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzakkī informed us: Abū ʿAbdullāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Wahhāb informed us: Jaʿfar ibn ʿAwn informed us: ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Ziyād narrated from Muslim ibn Yasār from Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyib, who said: \The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered the freeing of the *ummahāt al-awlād*"," and that they not be placed in the one-third (of the estate)"," and he ordered that they not be sold for debt.\""\n\nJaʿfar said: \""No one narrated this ḥadīth other than him.\"" And Sufyān al-Thawrī narrated it in *al-Jāmiʿ* from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Ziyād ibn Anʿum from Muslim ibn Yasār"," who said: \""I asked Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyib about freeing the *ummahāt al-awlād*"," and he said"," 'The people say that the first to order the freeing of the *ummahāt al-awlād* was ʿUmar"," may Allah be pleased with him"," but that is not so. Rather"," the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was the first to free them"," and they should not be placed in one-third"," nor sold for debt.'\"" [Weak]"""
"21778","(21772) Abū Bakr al-Aṣbahānī informed us: Abū Naṣr al-ʿIrāqī narrated to us: Sufyān ibn Muḥammad narrated to us: ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥasan narrated to us: ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Walīd narrated to us: Sufyān narrated it.\n\nAnd Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: Abū al-Walīd al-Faqīh informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān narrated to us: Muṣarrif ibn ʿAmr narrated to us: Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah narrated from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Ifrīqī from Muslim ibn Yasār from Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyib, that ʿUmar, may Allah be pleased with him, freed the *ummahāt al-awlād* and said: \The Messenger of Allah ﷺ freed them.\""\n\nAl-Ifrīqī was alone in raising it to the Prophet ﷺ"," and he is weak. [Weak]"""
"21779","(21773) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar ibn Durustawayh al-Fārisī narrated to us: Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān al-Fārisī narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Yaʿlā ibn al-Ḥārith narrated to us: My father narrated to us: Ghaylān ibn Jāmiʿ narrated from Ibrāhīm ibn Ḥarb from ʿAbdullāh ibn Buraydah from his father, who said: \I was sitting with ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb"," may Allah be pleased with him"," when he heard a scream. He said"," 'O Yarfāʾ"," see what this voice is!' He went and looked"," then came back and said"," 'A slave-girl from Quraysh is being sold along with her mother.' ʿUmar said"," 'Call — or he said"," \""Bring me — the Muhājirūn and the Anṣār.'\"" He said: \""He did not wait but an hour before the house and the chamber were filled.\"" He said: \""ʿUmar praised Allah and extolled Him"," then said"," 'To proceed: Do you know of any severing of kinship ties that Muḥammad ﷺ brought?' They said"," 'No.' He said"," 'Indeed"," it has become widespread among you.' Then he recited: *{Perhaps"," if you turn away"," you will cause corruption in the earth and sever your ties of kinship}* [Muḥammad: 22]. Then he said"," 'What severing of kinship ties is worse than the mother of a man among you being sold"," when Allah has expanded provision for you?' They said"," 'Do as you wish"," or do what you will.' So he wrote to the outlying regions that the mother of a free man should not be sold"," for it is a severing of kinship ties and it is not permissible.'\"" [Good]"""
"21780","(21774) Abū Muḥammad Janāḥ ibn Nadhīr al-Qāḍī in al-Kūfah narrated to us: Abū Jaʿfar ibn Duḥaym narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn Ḥāzim informed us: ʿAbd al-Ḥamīd ibn Ṣāliḥ narrated to us: Abū Bakr al-Nahshalī narrated from ʿAbdullāh ibn Saʿīd from his grandfather, that he heard ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb, may Allah be pleased with him, say upon the pulpit of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: \O assembly of Muslims"," Allah has granted you as booty from the lands of the non-Arabs their women and their children"," such as was not granted to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ nor to Abū Bakr"," may Allah be pleased with him. And I know that men have intercourse with women. Any man whose wife from among the non-Arab women bears a child for him — do not sell your *ummahāt al-awlād*"," for if you do so"," it is likely that a man will approach his own Ḥarīm (close female relative) while he is unaware.\"" [Weak]"""
"21781","(21775) ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us, Aḥmad ibn ʢbayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us, ʿUthmān ibn ʿUmar al-Ḍabbī narrated to us, Hudbah narrated to us, al-Qāsim ibn al-Faḍl narrated from Muḥammad ibn Ziyād, who said: My grandmother was an *umm walad* of ʿUthmān ibn Maẓʿūn. After the death of her master, a son of ʿUthmān wished to sell her. She came to ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her) and said: \O Mother of the Believers"," the son of ʿUthmān ibn Maẓʿūn wishes to sell me"," whereas I bore a child to his father. If you could speak to him and place me in a good position.\"" ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her) said to her: \""Did you bear a child to his father?\"" She said: \""Yes.\"" She said: \""Go to the Commander of the Believers"," ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him)"," and he will emancipate you.\"" So she came to ʿUmar and informed him that she had borne a child to ʿUthmān and that his son wished to sell her. ʿUmar sent for the son of ʿUthmān ibn Maẓʿūn and said: \""Did you intend that?\"" He said: \""Yes.\"" He said: \""That is not for you\"" — I think he said — \""she is free.\"" My grandmother said: \""O Commander of the Believers"," who emancipated me?\"" He said: \""Your child by ʿUthmān.\"" She said: \""He inflicted this wound upon me after the death of his father.\"" So ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him) said to him: \""Give her the compensation (*arsh*) for what you did to her.\"" [Weak]"""
"21782","(21776) Abū ʿAbd Allāh the Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū al-Walīd narrated to us, al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān narrated to us, Ḥibbān narrated from Ibn al-Mubārak, from Saʿīd, from Qatādah, that both ʿUmar — meaning ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him) — and ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz (may Allah have mercy on him) used to emancipate *ummahāt al-awlād* (mothers of children), as did the caliphs who came between them.\n\nIt has also been narrated from the Prophet (peace be upon him) reports concerning that. [Weak]"
"21783","(21777) Among them is what Abū ʿAbd Allāh the Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan the Qāḍī both informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣaghānī narrated to us, Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm al-Rāzī, the son-in-law of Salamah ibn al-Faḍl, narrated to us, Salamah narrated to me, Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated from al-Khiṭṭāb ibn Ṣāliḥ, from his mother, who said: Salamah ibnat Maʿqil narrated to me, saying: I was a slave woman of al-Ḥubbāb ibn ʿAmr. He died, and I had a boy by him. His wife said: \Now you will be sold to settle his debts.\"" I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) and mentioned that to him. The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: \""Who is the heir of the estate of al-Ḥubbāb ibn ʿAmr?\"" They said: \""His brother"," Abū al-Yasr Kaʿb ibn ʿAmr.\"" The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) summoned him and said: \""Do not sell her; rather"," emancipate her. And if you hear of a slave who has come to me"," come to me so that I may compensate you with him.\"" They did so. After the death of the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him)"," they differed among themselves. Some said: \""The *umm walad* is a slave woman; were it not so"," the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) would not have compensated them with her.\"" And some of them said: \""Rather"," she is free; the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) emancipated her.\"" Thus the difference arose concerning this.\n\nAbū Dāwūd narrated it in the *Kitāb al-Sunan* from al-Nufaylī"," from Muḥammad ibn Salamah"," from Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq"," with its meaning"," without what is at the end of it regarding the difference. [Weak]"""
"21784","(21778) Abū ʿAbd Allāh the Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū al-Walīd al-Faqīh narrated to us, al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān narrated to us, Ḥumayd ibn Qutaybah and ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Salām both said: Ibn Abī Maryam narrated to us, from Ibn Lahīʿah, from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Abī Jaʿfar, from Yaʿqūb ibn ʿAbd Allāh, from Busr ibn Saʿīd, from Khawwāt ibn Jubayr, that a man among the Anṣār made a bequest to him. Among what he left behind was his *umm walad* and a free woman. There was some matter between the free woman and the *umm walad*, so the free woman sent word to her: \You will certainly be sold"," O you wretched woman!\"" Khawwāt went back to the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him)"," and the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: \""She shall not be sold.\"" And he ordered regarding her"," so she was emancipated. [Weak]"""
"21785","(21779) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us, ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Ismāʿīl al-Fārisī narrated to us, Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥājjāj ibn Rashdīn narrated to us, Yūnus ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥīm al-ʿAsqalānī narrated to us — and Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal heard it from me — Rashdīn ibn Saʿd al-Mahrī narrated to me, Ṭalḥah ibn Abī Saʿīd narrated to us, from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Abī Jaʿfar, from Yaʿqūb ibn al-Ashajj, from Busr ibn Saʿīd, from Khawwāt ibn Jubayr, that a man made a bequest to him, and he mentioned the hadith similarly.\n\nHe said: And Rashdīn narrated to me, from Ibn Lahīʿah, from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Abī Jaʿfar, from Yaʿqūb ibn al-Ashajj, from Busr ibn Saʿīd, from Khawwāt ibn Jubayr, from the Prophet (peace be upon him), the like of it. [Weak]"
"21786","(21780) Abū Bakr informed us, ʿAlī narrated to us, Muḥammad narrated to us, Aḥmad narrated to us, Saʿīd ibn Abī Maryam narrated to us, Ibn Lahīʿah narrated with his chain, similarly.\n\nIt has also been narrated from Ibn Lahīʿah, from ʿUbayd Allāh, from Bukayr instead of Yaʿqūb, and Allah knows best."
"21787","(21781) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us, Abū Ḥāmid Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā ibn Bilāl narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Ismāʿīl al-Aḥmasī narrated to us, Wakīʿ narrated, from Sharīk, from Ḥusayn ibn ʿAbd Allāh, from ʿIkrimah, from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: \Any man whose slave woman bears his child"," she is emancipated upon his death.\""\n\nḤusayn ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUbayd Allāh ibn al-ʿAbbāsh al-Hāshimī was declared weak by the majority of the scholars of hadith. [Weak]"""
"21788","(21782) Abū Bakr ibn Abī Sabrah also narrated from him, as Abū ʿAbd Allāh the Ḥāfiẓ informed me, Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn Ṣāliḥ ibn Hānīʾ narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr al-Ḥarashī narrated to us, al-Qaʿnabī narrated to us, Abū Bakr ibn Abī Sabrah al-Qurashī narrated from Ḥusayn ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿAbbās, from ʿIkrimah, from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said, regarding Umm Ibrāhīm when she gave birth: \Her child has emancipated her.\""\n\nAbū Bakr ibn Abī Sabrah is weak and is not used as proof"," except that others have narrated from Ḥusayn with this wording. [Weak]"""
"21789","(21783) Abū ʿAbd Allāh the Ḥāfiẓ informed me, Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Faḍl al-Shaʿrānī narrated to me, my grandfather narrated to us, Ismāʿīl ibn Abī Uways narrated to me, my father narrated from Ḥusayn ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿAbbās, from ʿIkrimah, from Ibn ʿAbbās, that he said: When Umm Ibrāhīm, the mother of the son of the Prophet (peace be upon him), gave birth, the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: \Her child has emancipated her.\""\n\nThus did Abū Uways narrate it from Ḥusayn"," as a *mursal* (disconnected) narration.\n\nIt has also been narrated from Abū Uways as a *mawṣūl* (connected) narration"," mentioning Ibn ʿAbbās in it"," with the meaning of the first wording. That is what ʿAbd al-Ḥamīd ibn Abī Uways and Abū Bakr ibn Abī Uways narrated from their father. And Saʿīd ibn Kulayb and ʿAbd Allāh ibn Salamah ibn Aslam narrated from Ḥusayn ibn ʿAbd Allāh as Ibn Abī Sabrah narrated. [Weak]"""
"21790","(21784) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Aṣbahānī informed us, ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, Abū ʿUbayd al-Qāsim ibn Ismāʿīl narrated to us, Ziyād ibn Ayyūb narrated to us, Saʿīd ibn Zakariyyā al-Madāʾinī narrated, from Ibn Abī Sārah, from Ibn Abī Ḥusayn, from ʿIkrimah, from Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: When Māriyah gave birth, the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: \Her child has emancipated her.\"" ʿAlī said: Ziyād ibn Ayyūb is the sole narrator of the hadith of Ibn Abī Ḥusayn. And Ziyād is trustworthy"," but the hadith of ʿIkrimah has a remarkable defect despite its sound chain from him. [Weak]"""
"21791","(21785) The Sharif Abu al-Fatḥ Nāṣir ibn al-Ḥusayn al-ʿUmarī informed us: ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Shurayḥ informed us: Abū al-Qāsim al-Baghawī informed us: ʿAlī ibn al-Jaʿd informed us: Sufyān informed me: my father informed me from ʿIkrimah, from ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: \The mother of a child (umm al-walad) is freed by her child"," even if it is a miscarriage (siqṭ).\""\n\nAnd Sharik similarly narrated it from Saʿīd ibn Masrūq"," Abū Sufyān al-Thawrī"," from ʿIkrimah"," from ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him).\n\n[Weak]\n\n---"""
"21792","(21786) And Khuṣayf al-Jazarī narrated it from ʿIkrimah, from Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him) said: \When the mother of a child (umm al-walad) gives birth from her master"," she is freed"," even if it is a miscarriage (siqṭ).\""\n\nAbū al-Ḥasan ibn Abī al-Maʿrūf al-Faqīh informed us of it: Bishr ibn Aḥmad al-Isfarāʾinī informed us: al-Ḥusayn ibn ʿAlī al-Qaṭṭān al-Baghdādī informed us: ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿUmar al-Qawārīrī informed us: ʿAbd al-Wāḥid ibn Ziyād informed us: Khuṣayf informed us"," and he mentioned it. Thus the hadith goes back to ʿUmar.\n\n[Weak]\n\n---"""
"21793","(21787) And Abū Naṣr ibn Qatādah informed us: Abū Manṣūr al-Naḍrawī informed us: Aḥmad ibn Najdah informed us: Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr informed us: Sufyān informed me: al-Ḥakam ibn Abān said: ʿIkrimah was asked about the mothers of children (ummahāt al-awlad). He said: \They are free.\"" They said to him: \""On what basis do you say this?\"" He said: \""By the Qur'an.\"" They said: \""What from the Qur'an?\"" He said: \""The words of Allah"," the Most High: {O you who believe"," obey Allah and obey the Messenger and those in authority among you} [al-Nisāʾ 59]. And ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) was among those in authority.\"" He said: \""She is freed"," even if it is a miscarriage (siqṭ).\""\n\nAnd it is narrated from al-Ḥakam ibn Abān"," from ʿIkrimah"," from Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with him)"," from the Prophet (peace be upon him): \""The mother of a child (umm al-walad) is free"," even if it is a miscarriage (siqṭ).\"" And this is weak.\n\nThe authentic narration is the hadith of Saʿīd ibn Masrūq al-Thawrī from ʿIkrimah from ʿUmar"," and the hadith of Sufyān from al-Ḥakam from ʿIkrimah from ʿUmar. And Allah knows best. It is possible that the narration of the story of Māriyah has an original basis"," and Allah knows best.\n\n[Authentic]\n\n---"""
"21794","(21788) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥakam informed us: Ibn Wahb informed me: Ibn Lahīʿah informed me from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Abī Jaʿfar that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said to Umm Ibrāhīm: \Your child has set you free.\""\n\nThis is munqaṭiʿ (disconnected). And we have narrated from ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her) that the Prophet (peace be upon him) passed away and did not leave behind any dinar or dirham"," nor any male slave or female slave. In that there is an indication that he did not leave Umm Ibrāhīm as a slave"," and that she was freed upon his death by virtue of the prior prohibition of istīlād (the status of being a mother of a child).\n\n[Weak]\n\n---"""
"21795","(21789) Our companions cited as evidence what Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Aḥmad ibn Jaʿfar al-Qaṭīʿī informed us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal informed me: my father informed me: Abū al-Yamān informed us: Shuʿayb informed us from al-Zuhrī: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥayrīz al-Jumaḥī informed me that Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī informed him: \While he was sitting with the Prophet (peace be upon him)"," a man from the Anṣār came and said: 'O Messenger of Allah"," we capture female captives and we desire the prices. What do you think about coitus interruptus (ʿazl)?' The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: 'Do you indeed do that? It is not upon you that you do not do it. For there is no soul that Allah has decreed to come into existence except that it will come into existence.'\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū al-Yamān"," and both al-Bukhārī and Muslim narrated it through various routes from al-Zuhrī. They said: Were it not that istīlād (the status of being a mother of a child) prevents the transfer of ownership"," there would have been no benefit in their desire for prices through coitus interruptus. And Allah knows best.\n\n[Authentic — Agreed upon (muttafaq ʿalayh)]\n\n---"""
"21796","(21790) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān informed us: Abū Sahl ibn Ziyād al-Qaṭṭān informed us: Abū Bakr Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib informed us: Abū Bakr al-Ḥanafī, ʿAbd al-Kabīr ibn ʿAbd al-Majīd informed us: al-Ḍaḥḥāk ibn ʿUthmān informed us: Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā ibn Ḥabbān informed us from Ibn Muḥayrīz that Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī and Abū Ṣirmah informed him: \They had captured female captives during the expedition of Banī al-Muṣṭaliq. Among those of us who wanted to take them as wives"," and among those of us who wanted to sell them. So we discussed the matter and some of us said to others: 'It is not permissible.' We mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him)"," and he said: 'It is not upon you that you do not practice coitus interruptus (ʿazl). For Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic"," has decreed what He is creating until the Day of Resurrection.'\""\n\n[Authentic — previously mentioned]\n\n---"""
"21797","(21791) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us: Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us: Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq informed us: Ḥajjāj ibn Minhāl and ʿĀrim ibn al-Faḍl both said: Ḥammād ibn Salamah informed us from Qays ibn Saʿd from ʿAṭāʾ, from Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh, who said: \We used to sell the mothers of children (ummahāt al-awlad) during the time of the Prophet (peace be upon him) and Abū Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him). Then when ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) was in charge"," he forbade us"," so we desisted.\""\n\nAbū Dāwūd narrated it in the Sunan from Mūsā ibn Ismāʿīl from Ḥammād.\n\n[Authentic]\n\n---"""
"21798","(21792) And Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us: ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū Bakr al-Naysābūrī informed us: ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Bishr informed us from ʿAbd al-Razzāq, who informed us: Ibn Jurayj informed me: Abū al-Zubayr informed me that he heard Jābir saying: \We used to sell our concubines who were mothers of children (ummahāt al-awlad) while the Prophet (peace be upon him) was alive"," and we saw no harm in that.\""\n\n[Authentic — previously mentioned]\n\n---"""
"21799","(21793) Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Fūrak informed us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar informed us: Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb informed us: Abū Dāwūd informed us: Shuʿbah informed us from Zayd al-ʿAmmī from Abī al-Ṣiddīq al-Nājī, from Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī, who said: \We used to sell the mothers of children (ummahāt al-awlad) during the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him).\""\n\nThere is nothing in any of these hadiths indicating that the Prophet (peace be upon him) knew of it and approved of them. And we have narrated what indicates the prohibition"," and Allah knows best.\n\n[Weak]\n\n---"""
"21800","(21794) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf al-Aṣbahānī informed us: Abū Saʿīd ibn al-Aʿrābī informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad al-Zaʿfarānī informed us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Bakr informed us: Hishām, meaning Ibn Ḥassān, informed us from Muḥammad, meaning Ibn Sīrīn, from ʿUbaydah, from ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: \My opinion and the opinion of ʿUmar were united on the freeing of the mothers of children (ummahāt al-awlad). Then later I considered keeping them as slaves in such and such a manner.\"" He said: \""I said to him: 'Your opinion and the opinion of ʿUmar together are more beloved to me than your opinion alone.'\""\n\n[Authentic]"""
"21801","(21795) Abu 'Abdillah al-Hafiz and Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn al-Hasan al-Qadi informed us, they said: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us: Abu Yahya Zakariyya ibn Yahya ibn Asad narrated to us in Baghdad: Sufyan narrated from 'Ubayd Allah ibn 'Umar from Nafi', who said: Two men met Ibn 'Umar on one of the roads of Madinah and said to him: \We have left this man\"" — meaning Ibn al-Zubayr — \""selling *ummahat al-awlad* (slave women who bore children to their masters).\"" He said to them: \""But do you know Abu Hafs 'Umar?\"" They said: \""Yes.\"" He said: \""He passed judgement regarding *ummahat al-awlad* that they shall not be sold"," nor given as gifts"," nor inherited. Their owner enjoys their services as long as he lives"," and when he dies"," they become free.\"" [Sahih]"""
"21802","(21796) Abu 'Abdillah al-Hafiz informed us: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us: Qabisah narrated to us: Sufyan narrated from 'Abd Allah ibn Dinar, who said: Ibn 'Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, met a caravan and said: \From where have you come?\"" They said: \""From Ibn al-Zubayr"," who has made permissible for us things that have been forbidden to us.\"" He said: \""What has he made permissible for you?\"" He said: \""He has made it permissible for us to sell *ummahat al-awlad*.\"" He said: \""Do you know Abu Hafs 'Umar?\"" They said: \""Yes.\"" He said: \""Verily"," he forbade that they be sold"," given as gifts"," or inherited. Their owner may enjoy their services as long as he lives"," and when he dies"," they become free.\"" [Hasan]"""
"21803","(21797) Abu 'Abdillah al-Hafiz informed us: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us: Yahya ibn Abi Talib narrated to us: 'Abd al-Wahhab ibn 'Ata' informed us: Sa'id narrated from al-Hakam ibn 'Utaybah from Zayd ibn Wahb, who said: I and a man set out to see Ibn Mas'ud to ask him about *umm al-walad* — could she be manumitted? He said: \She is manumitted from the share of her child.\""\n\nThe Shaykh"," may Allah have mercy on him"," said: It is as though 'Umar"," may Allah be pleased with him"," reached a ruling from the Prophet ﷺ that he judged by their emancipation upon the death of their masters by explicit text"," and he and others agreed upon the prohibition of selling them. And it is as though he and others deduced from some of what has reached us and what has been transmitted from the Prophet ﷺ that which indicates their emancipation"," and he and others agreed upon the prohibition of selling them. Therefore"," it is more appropriate for us to follow them in that upon which they agreed before the difference of opinion"," while seeking evidence from the Sunnah. And Allah knows best. [Sahih]"""
"21804","(21798) Abu 'Abdillah al-Hafiz informed us: Abu al-Walid narrated to us: Ibn bint Mani' narrated to us: Khalaf ibn Hisham narrated to us: Sharik narrated from Sa'id ibn Masruq from 'Ikrimah, who said: 'Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, said: \*Umm al-walad* is manumitted"," even if the child is a miscarriage (*siqṭ*).\"" [Da'if]"""
"21805","(21799) Abu 'Abdillah informed us: Abu al-Walid narrated to us: al-Hasan ibn Sufyan narrated to us: Hibban narrated from Ibn al-Mubarak from Hammad ibn Zayd from Kathir ibn Shindir from al-Hasan, who said: \If *umm al-walad* miscarries something that is known to be from a pregnancy"," she is manumitted by it and becomes an *umm walad*.\"" [Hasan]"""
"21806","(21800) Abu Zakariyya ibn Abi Ishaq and Abu Bakr ibn al-Hasan informed us, they said: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub informed us: Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah ibn 'Abd al-Hakam informed us: Ibn Wahb informed me: Makhrah ibn Bukayr narrated from his father from Ibn Qusayt, who heard Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Thawban, who heard 'Abd Allah ibn 'Umar saying: \When a slave woman bears a child to her master and then he marries her and she bears children"," her children are in her status — slaves — as long as her master lives. And if he dies"," they become free.\"" [Sahih]"""
"21807","(21801) Abu Hamid Ahmad ibn 'Ali al-Isfarayini informed us: Zahir ibn Ahmad narrated to us: Abu Bakr ibn Ziyad al-Naysaburi narrated to us: Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Malik narrated to us: Yazid, that is ibn Harun, narrated to us: Isma'il narrated from 'Amir, who said: \The children of a *mudabbarah* (a slave woman promised manumission upon her master's death) and *umm al-walad* are in the same position as their mothers: when they are manumitted"," they become manumitted"," when the master dies.\"" [Sahih]"""
"21808","(21802) Abu 'Abdillah al-Hafiz informed us: Abu al-Walid narrated to us: al-Hasan ibn Sufyan narrated to us: Hibban informed us: 'Abd Allah narrated from Hammad ibn Zayd from Abu Hashim from Ibrahim, who said: \The children of a *mudabbarah* and *umm al-walad* are in the same position as their mothers.\"" [Sahih]\n\nAnd from 'Abd Allah ibn Lahi'ah"," who said: Ja'far ibn Rabi'ah narrated to me that 'Umar ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz said regarding a man who married his *umm walad* to his slave and she bore a child: \""They are in the position of their mother.\"""""
"21809","(21803) Muhammad ibn Abi al-Ma'ruf informed us: Abu Sa'id al-Razi narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ayyub informed us: Muslim narrated to us: Hisham narrated to us: Qatadah narrated from al-Hasan regarding *umm al-walad* being manumitted while she had children: \She is manumitted"," and so are her children.\"" [Sahih]"""
"21810","(21804) Abu 'Abdillah al-Hafiz informed us: Abu al-Walid narrated to us: Ja'far Abu Qudamah narrated from 'Abd al-Wahhab from Yahya ibn Sa'id — (ḥ) — and he said: al-Hasan ibn Sufyan narrated to us: Hibban narrated from Ibn al-Mubarak from Yahya ibn Sa'id from Nafi', who mentioned a story: Ibn 'Umar said: \Do you know 'Umar ibn al-Khattab"," may Allah be pleased with him?\"" He said: \""Yes.\"" He said: \""Any slave woman who bears a child to her master — she is an enjoyment (*mut'ah*) to him as long as he lives"," and when he dies"," she becomes free (*ḥurrah*) after him. And whoever has intercourse with a slave woman and renders her pregnant — the child is his"," and the loss is upon him.\"" [Sahih]"""
"21811","(21805) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, Aḥmad ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥamīd al-Ḥārithī narrated to us, Abū Usāmah narrated to us from Ḥammād ibn Zayd, Fuḍayl ibn Mayṣarah Abū Muʿādh narrated to us from Abī Ḥarīz from al-Shaʿbī, who said: A case was brought before Shurayḥ concerning a man who had married a slave woman and she bore him children, and then he purchased her. Shurayḥ referred the matter to ʿUbaydah, and ʿUbaydah said: \An umm al-walad is set free only if she bore them while they were free; but if she bore them while they were enslaved"," then she is not set free.\"" [Weak]"""
"21812","(21806) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū al-Walīd narrated to us, al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān narrated to us, Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah narrated to us, Ibn ʿUlayyah narrated to us from Yūnus from al-Ḥasan regarding an umm al-walad who commits an offence: \She shall be valued against her master (i.e."," her liability falls upon her master).\"" [Authentic]"""
"21813","(21806) He said: And Abū Bakr narrated to us, ʿAbd al-Aʿlā narrated to us from Maʿmar from al-Zuhrī regarding an umm al-walad: \If she commits an offence"," then her offence falls upon her master.\"" [Authentic]"""
"21814","(21808) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh informed us, Abū al-Walīd narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Zuhayr narrated to us, ʿAbd Allāh — he is Ibn Hāshim — narrated to us from Wakīʿ from Sufyān from Khālid from Abī Maʿshār from Ibrāhīm, who said: \The offence of an umm al-walad falls upon her master.\"""""
"21815","(21809) Abū ʿAbd Allāh informed us, Abū al-Walīd narrated to us, al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān narrated to us, Abū Yaḥyā narrated to us, Ibrāhīm ibn Ṣadaqah narrated to us from Sufyān from al-Ḥakam, who said: \The offence of an umm al-walad shall not exceed her own person (i.e."," she shall not be subjected to excessive punishment on account of her offence).\"" [Weak]"""
"21816","(21810) Abū Aḥmad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Mihrānjānī informed us, Abū Bakr ibn Jaʿfar al-Muzakkī narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Būshanjī narrated to us, Ibn Bukayr narrated to us, Mālik narrated to us from Nāfiʿ from Ibn ʿUmar that he said regarding an umm al-walad whose master dies: \She shall observe an ʿiddah of one menstrual cycle.\"" And what has been narrated regarding the differences of opinion on this matter has already passed in the Book of ʿIddah. And success is through Allah. [Authentic]"""
"21817","(21811) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū al-Walīd narrated to us, al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān narrated to us, Abū Bakr narrated to us, al-Muʿtamir ibn Sulaymān narrated to us from Kathīr ibn Nubātah from Ibn Sīrīn, who said: \When a man purchases a young slave woman who has not yet reached the age of menstruation"," he shall observe an istibrāʾ (waiting period to ascertain the status of the womb) of three months.\"" [Weak]"""
"21818","(21812) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh informed us, Abū al-Walīd narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Zuhayr narrated to us, ʿAbd Allāh — he is Ibn Hāshim — narrated to us from Wakīʿ from Misʿar and Sufyān from ʿAbd al-Karīm from Mujāhid, who said: \Three months.\""\n\nAnd from Wakīʿ from Saʿīd from al-Ḥakam from Ibrāhīm"," who said: \""Three months.\""\n\nAnd we have narrated similar from ʿAṭāʾ"," Ṭāwūs"," ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz"," and Abī Qilābah — may Allah"," the Most High"," have mercy upon them."""
